/01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469/terminal/call-e3feb156-cbee-4207-b960-c47f019d7d40-10.log]\\n80408b4c72ef08be3ec628d578f8b008644c1c7e447a4cc8c5979b08212e78aa  /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/pixel-engine.js\\ngot session.js 16707\\ngot harness.html 27469\\ngot bridge.js 13624\\ngot round.js 20248\\ngot README.md 17587\\n=== CHANGELOG head ===\\n# Changelog\\n\\nWhat changed in Pixel Engine for a game built on it, newest first. The version is\\n`package.json`'s; a game reads it as `ENGINE_VERSION`, `Engine.version` or\\n`engine.state().version`. The engine kit (`npm run bundle`, docs/GUIDE.md) ships this file.\\n\\nWhen a change alters the public API (`src/bundle.ts` exports) or something a game can see,\\nbump the version (minor while it is 0.x) and add its section here; `npm test` fails when\\n`package.json`'s version has no section.\\n\\n## 0.46.0\\n\\n- **No more handoff page**: the engine's site is gone, so `manifest.json` has no `handoff` and the\\n  kit's `README.md` no longer names a page for agents. Newer kits are where they were:\\n  `latest` (the newest release's zip), `releases` and `source`.\\n\\n## 0.45.0\\n\\n- **The kit runs in Node**: `Engine.headless(game, { assets })` from `pixel-engine.js` alone, with\\n  no `node_modules`. In Node, Rapier's wasm comes from the data URL the kit inlines, and a reader\\n  (`assets`, `setAssetReader`) no longer sees the files the kit embeds (`__PIXEL_ASSETS__`: the\\n  built-in models load as they do in a page).\\n- **`node check.mjs --headless game.js`**: plays a game module in Node, no browser. It makes the game\\n  with the module's `createGame()` export, plays the `--keys` frames, replays the recording in a\\n  fresh game and writes `report.json` (`state()`, errors, the fingerprint). Exit 1 on an error or a\\n  replay that ends elsewhere, 2 for a page or a module without `createGame()`.\\n- **The starter `game.js` exports `createGame()`** and starts the engine only where there is a\\n  `document`, so it imports in Node. GUIDE.md section 8, *Play it in Node*, shows a test of your own.\\n\\n## 0.44.0\\n\\n- **Removed from the texture library: its equipment icons**: `sword-icon`, `axe-icon`,\\n  `mace-icon`, `dagger-icon`, `bow-icon`, `staff-icon`, `wand-icon`, `shield-icon`,\\n  `round-shield-icon`, `quiver-icon`, `helmet-icon`, `armor-icon`, `gloves-icon`, `boots-icon`,\\n  `belt-icon`, `ring` and `amulet`. They were a second way to draw an item next to Riftlight's own\\n  icons, which fill any item footprint (a one-cell item's box is 7 px wide), and nothing used them. A game that wants one makes its own\\n  `TextureDef` (docs/GUIDE-ASSETS.md) and adds it with `TEXTURE_LIBRARY.add(def)`. The library\\n  keeps the items Riftlight has no class for (potions, key, scroll, map, book, bomb, torch...),\\n  `gem-icon`, `gold-icon`, the skill and UI icons and the creatures.\\n\\n## 0.43.0\\n\\n- **`Game.args`**: the plain JSON a game was made with, when its name alone can't rebuild it (a\\n  lab's depth and seed, the door a room was entered by). Recordings keep it (**`Recording.args`**),\\n  so a tool can make the same game again and replay one (`npm run replay` in this repository).\\n\\n## 0.42.0\\n\\n- **`Engine.headless(game, options)`: games without a page** (docs/engine/headless.md). The same\\n  boot, game code and frames as `Engine.start`, in Node: no GPU, DOM or listeners, manual time from\\n  the start (`step()`, `input.setKey` / `send`, `replay()`), errors in `engine.errors`. Options add\\n  `viewport` (default 960×540 at DPR 1) and `assets`.\\n- **`engine.renderer` is a `View`**: what gameplay reads from a view (art resolution, framing,\\n  `viewport`, look, mode, filters, `screen`, `capture()`), the page's `PixelRenderer` or a\\n  `HeadlessView`. Direct GPU work goes through **`engine.gpu`** (the `PixelRenderer`, null\\n  headless): `engine.renderer.renderer` becomes `engine.gpu.renderer`. `BackendName` gains\\n  `'headless'`.\\n- **The GPU helpers take the view**: `swarm.update(engine.renderer, dt)` (was\\n  `engine.renderer.renderer`), `mirror.attach(engine.renderer, scene)` and\\n  `view.attach(engine.renderer, scene)` as before; headless they do nothing.\\n=== version string ===\\n1:# Pixel Engine 0.46.0\\n24:| `CHANGELOG.md` | What changed between engine versions |\\n26:| `manifest.json` | Version, build, where newer versions are (`latest`, `releases`, `source`) and every file with its size |\\n31:Newer versions: the newest release of the kit is always https://github.com/michaelcrosato/riftlight/releases/latest/download/pixel-engine.zip, and every release stays\\n1:/*! Pixel Engine 0.46.0 (build 2026-11-02 f75d4a6). One self-contained ES module: import it from game.js, see GUIDE.md. Includes three.js r186 (MIT) and Rapier 0.20 (Apache-2.0). */\\n2:var e=Object.defineProperty,t=(t,n)=>{let r={};for(var i in t)e(r,i,{get:t[i],enumerable:!0});return n||e(r,Symbol.toStringTag,{value:`Module`}),r},n=`html,body{background:#0d0e16;height:100%;margin:0;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow:hidden}#app{position:fixed;inset:0}canvas[data-engine-canvas]{image-rendering:pixelated;image-rendering:crisp-edges}.debug-ui{z-index:10;color:#f4f4f4;background:#1a1c2cd9;border:2px solid #566c86;min-width:220px;padding:8px 10px;font-size:12px;line-height:1.5;position:absolute;top:8px;left:8px}.debug-ui .row{justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;display:flex}.debug-ui span{color:#94b0c2}.debug-ui b[data-backend=webgpu]{color:#a7f070}.debug-ui .game{color:#ffcd75;margin-top:4px}.debug-ui .buttons{gap:6px;margin:6px 0 4px;display:flex}.debug-ui button{font:inherit;color:#1a1c2c;cursor:pointer;background:#94b0c2;border:0;flex:1;padding:3px 4px}.debug-ui button:hover{background:#f4f4f4}.debug-ui .keys{color:#566c86;font-size:11px}.fatal{color:#ef7d57;text-align:center;place-items:center;padding:24px;display:grid;p