r(params.get('play')) || 6000;\"},{\"line_number\":170,\"content\":\"  const limitMs = params.has('limit') ? Number(params.get('limit')) * 1000 : limitFor(metas?.minutes);\"},{\"line_number\":181,\"content\":\"  const state = { round, n, metas, mode, limitMs, seed, players, cells: [], hubEnd, status: null, record: null, hidden: false, splashUntil: performance.now() + SPLASH_MS, answers: { ready: new Set(), more: new Set() } };\"},{\"line_number\":183,\"content\":\"  log(`round ${round}: ${n} player${n > 1 ? 's' : ''}, seed ${seed}, limit ${Math.round(limitMs / 1000)} s, mode ${mode || '(from hello)'}`);\"},{\"line_number\":192,\"content\":\"    limitMs,\"},{\"line_number\":456,\"content\":\"    await until(() => state.status.phase === 'playing' || state.record, TIMINGS.countdownMs + 2000);\"},{\"line_number\":465,\"content\":\"    await randomly(Math.min(1500, playMs / 4));\"},{\"line_number\":479,\"content\":\"    await randomly(playMs / 2);\"},{\"line_number\":497,\"content\":\"    const ended = await until(() => state.record, TIMINGS.graceMs + 2000);\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"6cbc679d-bb2f-43a6-93b7-25468278bb49"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_15","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I understand the requirements and am ready to build the game.\n\nThe architecture will use a single simulation kernel with thin scenes. Activities will be pure functions in `src/core/activities.js`. Tests will import real modules and run headless scenes via `Engine.headless` to satisfy the verification requirements. A fast mode for activities is also being considered to speed up the playthrough.\n\nA fast mode is unnecessary. Headless step execution is already fast enough. A full week of activities totals roughly 42,000 frames and about five to twenty seconds of runtime. Scene loading overhead is minimal at around six seconds.\n\nThe architecture is being simplified to a single `MintDial` Game class. It will stay loaded and switch internal modes without reloading the engine scene for menus. A reusable stage with floor, lights, and an avatar pool will be built once during setup. Activities will spawn their props on this shared stage. Headless tests can then drive the entire flow from one persistent game instance.\n\nThe plan is shifting to follow the requirement of swapping scenes with `engine.loadGame`. A `Boot` scene will handle audio settings before loading `Title` or `Card`. A shared `Stage` base class will let separate scene classes access the same App state. Headless tests will instantiate a scene directly and navigate through it. `loadGame` resets `timeScale`, which needs attention.\n\nThe `App` class is being defined with shared state for the entire game session. It stores title, tunables, save data, device info, audio settings, driver skill, god mode, overlays, week state, scene ID, widget rectangles, and attract mode. This centralizes global data so scenes can share it without reloading.\n\nThe `App` class now includes pause, medley, session, ended, and debug flags. It exposes `state()`, `go(id, args)`, and `setDriver(skill)` methods. The week state object tracks version, slot, name, avatar, look, day, week, phase, age chart points, star scores, drips, unlocks, daily activities, prescription status, confession status, and total stars.\n\nThe week state now includes a questions array and a locker object for skin, hair, top, bottom, headband, and items. All menus are modeled as lists with rows, focus, and confirm callbacks. Input handling covers arrow keys, WASD, pad directions, stick repeat, Enter, Space, KeyE, PadCross, and mouse clicks for confirmation, plus Escape, Backspace, and PadCircle for back. Headless tests will simulate key presses by setting flags on the engine input system before each step. The wasPressed behavior is being verified to ensure it fires exactly on the frame a key is pressed.\n\nThe dot bot test will run 84,000 pure JavaScript steps across 40 seeds in 35 seconds. Star thresholds are mapped to the plan: idle at ring 0.30 yields zero stars, average yields one, and good yields three. The keyboard and mouse averages from the table will be used for those bots.\n\nThe bot model will use a PD controller. Only the four specified performance bands are required for testing. Each activity will define its own bot play through a `botInput` function that returns movement, breathing, step, and confirm signals.\n\nStillness will use the Dot bot targeting zero or its bias, with expert performance keeping the avatar inside the ring. For Reps, the expert bot will track a target radius using the stick, and the rep system will apply lag to the radius following input. The standard gamepad axis mapping is being verified: positive moveAxis.y corresponds to upward stick movement.\n\nThe Reps expert bot will drive the radius toward a target that cycles from 0 to 1 and back. The simulation applies a 0.10-second lag to the radius following input. With a 3.2-second tempo, the lag keeps the error small enough for expert quality above 0.9 and three stars.\n\nIdle performance on Stillness scores about 36, confirming zero stars. The gag adds two extra reps without changing the core score.\n\nFor Hoop, the expert will circle at a constant angular speed of 1.5 rev/s within the band. Score is weighted rotations in band. A full minute yields about ninety rotations. Expert gets three stars.\n\nHoop expert speed is refined to 2.0 rev/s for three stars, since 1.5 rev/s yields only two. Idle performance remains zero.\n\nStep expert will press on beat at 104 BPM with a `L.R.L.R.` chart, hitting within 20 ms for three stars. Idle scores zero.\n\nHeader expert will move to the landing x position before each object lands. The flight time is 1.4 s and the interval shrinks from 1.3 s to 0.7 s. Expert can reach any point in the lane before impact. Score scales with coconut hits and combo. Idle scores zero.\n\nHeader idle performance is being tuned to stay below the 150-point threshold. Objects will land at random positions across the lane with a seeded RNG, and the hit radius will be set to 0.28 m so that an idle avatar scores near zero.\n\nFor Slackline, the expert will walk when the avatar is within 0.45 m of center and balance using a PD controller. The target is a good finish of 28 seconds with zero falls.\n\nSlackline star thresholds are now defined: two stars for a finish under 45 seconds with at most one fall, and three stars for a finish under 32 seconds with zero falls. The expert will score three stars, while idle scores zero because it never finishes.\n\nThe Slackline physics will use the Dot bot with mass and wind gusts across a 30-meter span.\n\nFor Tray, the expert will tilt the board to guide kinematic vitamin balls toward their cups. Idle performance scores zero since the balls do not move without tilt. The expert should clear roughly eighty percent of the maximum score. The board design will be simple so the tilt-based AI can solve it reliably.\n\nJog expert will alternate left and right steps at 3 steps per second while steering toward cups. Score is 70 percent of pace plus 30 percent of cups, yielding about 100 points for three stars. Idle scores zero.\n\nPier expert will hold the dot in the tuck zone between y -0.8 and -0.4 for five seconds to build speed from 6 to 14.\n\nPier expert will press at the lip with perfect timing after building speed, keeping the flight inside the ring. Distance is speed multiplied by a pressure and ring fraction factor; maximum distance is about 42 meters for three stars. Idle scores zero because without pressing the dot stays near the starting speed of 6 m/s.\n\nLong stand expert will use the Dot bot to stay mostly inside a shrinking ring of 0.24 radius. Score scales with time spent in the ring. The expert table shows 98 percent accuracy at that size, which clears the two-star threshold.\n\nThe Long stand bot will recover from brief knockouts caused by impulses. Idle performance across varying ring sizes averages low enough to score zero stars.\n\nDrip rewards will be computed as `2 + 3*stars + floor(playSeconds/30)` plus five for prescription status. Tests will validate this formula against the result function output.\n\nTests will import `dripsFor` from the shipped module to verify activity result drips match the formula. A quick sanity check uses zero stars, twenty-nine seconds, and no bonus for two drips, or three stars, sixty seconds, and bonus for eighteen.\n\nA `lines.js` file will hold all samples plus many more lines. Every activity needs zero, one, two, and three star versions, both first time and repeat. Each line must be under fifty-two characters and contain at most three lines.\n\nEvery character in game text must have a font glyph. The font covers lowercase a-z and uppercase letters via `hud.text`.\n\nThe `say()` function renders lowercase letters from the GLYPHS sprite sheet and all other characters through `hud.text`. The engine font is a 5x7 capital bitmap, so uppercase letters, digits, and punctuation are drawn by the engine. Any character the engine font lacks will be replaced with a question mark.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ff45615e-8abc-4695-9500-74cad35370ac-24","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/types/engine/animation/font.d.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ff45615e-8abc-4695-9500-74cad35370ac-25","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"FONT|glyphs|0123456789","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/types/engine/hud.d.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ff45615e-8abc-4695-9500-74cad35370ac-26","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/types/engine/hud.d.ts","limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4626,"output_tokens":3911,"cache_read_input_tokens":91648,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"d48da764-d0c0-46b2-8c1d-b77477a0dd15"}
