{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_17","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The engine font includes uppercase letters, digits, and common punctuation.\n\nThe engine font supports letters, digits, space, and basic punctuation like periods, commas, exclamation marks, apostrophes, colons, semicolons, hyphens, parentheses, slashes, and plus signs. Em-dashes, special quotes, and stars are excluded.\n\nStars will be drawn as sprites or replaced with asterisks. Uppercase letters route through hud.text, which likely uppercases them automatically. The next step is to verify the validateClip, analyzeClip, and model() signatures before writing the implementation files.\n\nThe implementation plan covers nineteen files across data, core systems, audio, UI, and art. These include title and about screens, tunables, dot physics, drivers, score tracking, save logic, device detection, actions, voice and sound effects, font rendering, glyphs, dialogue lines, weekly content, activity definitions, simulation logic, and the main application entry point.\n\nThe file list expanded to twenty-nine files. The plan is being consolidated into a leaner architecture: a single Game shell, mode handlers, and a unified HUD module. This replaces the original scattered scene files for easier maintenance.\n\nTests will import from the core modules listed in the plan. The Game class is being designed with a BaseScene base that binds to the app context and exposes setup and fixedUpdate hooks for headless testing.\n\nBaseScene.update handles device input, attract timer, pause overlay, and scene drawing. The engine skips fixedUpdate when timeScale is zero, but update still runs. The attract timer only activates on title and menu screens, not during gameplay, pause, or hub sessions.\n\nThe attract timer's 10-second idle window is being weighed against real time versus scaled game time. The engine documentation is being checked to confirm whether update dt is affected by timeScale, since the plan requires update to keep running even when paused.\n\nThe attract timer will use the dt passed to update. Headless tests step the engine with a fixed frame delta, so the exact step size still needs verification. Menu input will be read from ctx.input.\n\nMenu input will use wasPressed for arrow keys, W, and pad up to move focus, plus Enter, Space, E, or pad cross to confirm. Stick repeat will trigger every 0.18 seconds while the vertical axis exceeds 0.5. Mouse hover will map pointer coordinates to art pixels and track widget rectangles each frame to set focus on hover and confirm on click.\n\nThe title screen will feature a 3D plaza with an Ounce model, a mat, and a sea-colored background so the capture is not blank. Model definitions will be exported from the plan and built using `buildModel` inside the scene.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5503116a-e96f-4f51-9c5c-9753385bf3ac-29","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/types/engine/audio/AudioManager.d.ts","offset":90,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5503116a-e96f-4f51-9c5c-9753385bf3ac-30","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"buildModel\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/API.md","head_limit":15}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5503116a-e96f-4f51-9c5c-9753385bf3ac-31","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/types/engine/Engine.d.ts","offset":370,"limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1099,"output_tokens":1979,"cache_read_input_tokens":100480,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"932dcd7a-6241-4ffb-b04a-26731faad699"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-5503116a-e96f-4f51-9c5c-9753385bf3ac-29","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"90→     * it yourself from a click handler if you start sound from your own UI.\\n     */\\n    unlock(): void;\\n    private target;\\n    /** Listen for the next user input (until the context is running). */\\n    private armUnlock;\\n    private disarmUnlock;\\n    /** Resume a suspended / interrupted context; stop listening for input once it runs. */\\n    private resume;\\n    /** Add or replace a sound effect (data, see SoundDef). */\\n100→    register(name: string, def: SoundDef): void;\\n    /**\\n     * Play a sound effect by name (built-in SFX, `register`ed or `load`ed) or directly from a\\n     * SoundDef. Returns false when nothing could be heard (locked, muted, no Web Audio).\\n     */\\n    play(sound: string | SoundDef, options?: PlayOptions): boolean;\\n    /**\\n     * Start a sound looping, as a voice you steer while it plays (volume, pan, muffle, pitch:\\n     * with `spatialize` it sits at a place in the world). Before the first user input, or with\\n     * no Web Audio, the voice keeps its settings silently and starts once audio unlocks.\\n110→     * Stop it when you are done (a level's `dispose`).\\n     */\\n    loop(sound: string | SoundDef, settings?: VoiceSettings): Voice;\\n    /** Voices playing or waiting to (tooling and tests). */\\n    get loops(): readonly Voice[];\\n    /** Stop every looping voice (the engine does this when a level unloads). */\\n    stopLoops(): void;\\n    /**\\n     * Load an audio file (wav/ogg/mp3…) under `name`; `play(name)` then plays it. Works\\n     * before the first user input too: the file is decoded once audio unlocks.\\n120→     */\\n    load(name: string, url: string): Promise<void>;\\n    /** Start a song (looping by default), replacing the current one. `null` stops music. */\\n    playMusic(song: Song | null, name?: string): void;\\n    stopMusic(): void;\\n    /**\\n     * Volume changes are written to storage. The engine turns this off while a replay plays: the\\n     * recording sets the volumes it set, nothing is written, and the player's come back after.\\n     */\\n    persist: boolean;\\n130→    setVolume(channel: VolumeChannel, value: number): void;\\n    setMuted(muted: boolean): void;\\n    toggleMute(): boolean;\\n    /** The default volumes, sound on (the settings panel's Reset). */\\n    resetVolumes(): void;\\n    /** Engine: once per rendered frame. Schedules the next notes of the song. */\\n    update(): void;\\n    /** Stop everything and close the AudioContext. */\\n    dispose(): void;\\n    private start;\\n140→    private bufferFor;\\n    private toBuffer;\\n    private decode;\\n    private applyVolumes;\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"90→     * it yourself from a click handler if you start sound from your own UI.\\n     */\\n    unlock(): void;\\n    private target;\\n    /** Listen for the next user input (until the context is running). */\\n    private armUnlock;\\n    private disarmUnlock;\\n    /** Resume a suspended / interrupted context; stop listening for input once it runs. */\\n    private resume;\\n    /** Add or replace a sound effect (data, see SoundDef). */\\n100→    register(name: string, def: SoundDef): void;\\n    /**\\n     * Play a sound effect by name (built-in SFX, `register`ed or `load`ed) or directly from a\\n     * SoundDef. Returns false when nothing could be heard (locked, muted, no Web Audio).\\n     */\\n    play(sound: string | SoundDef, options?: PlayOptions): boolean;\\n    /**\\n     * Start a sound looping, as a voice you steer while it plays (volume, pan, muffle, pitch:\\n     * with `spatialize` it sits at a place in the world). Before the first user input, or with\\n     * no Web Audio, the voice keeps its settings silently and starts once audio unlocks.\\n110→     * Stop it when you are done (a level's `dispose`).\\n     */\\n    loop(sound: string | SoundDef, settings?: VoiceSettings): Voice;\\n    /** Voices playing or waiting to (tooling and tests). */\\n    get loops(): readonly Voice[];\\n    /** Stop every looping voice (the engine does this when a level unloads). */\\n    stopLoops(): void;\\n    /**\\n     * Load an audio file (wav/ogg/mp3…) under `name`; `play(name)` then plays it. Works\\n     * before the first user input too: the file is decoded once audio unlocks.\\n120→     */\\n    load(name: string, url: string): Promise<void>;\\n    /** Start a song (looping by default), replacing the current one. `null` stops music. */\\n    playMusic(song: Song | null, name?: string): void;\\n    stopMusic(): void;\\n    /**\\n     * Volume changes are written to storage. The engine turns this off while a replay plays: the\\n     * recording sets the volumes it set, nothing is written, and the player's come back after.\\n     */\\n    persist: boolean;\\n130→    setVolume(channel: VolumeChannel, value: number): void;\\n    setMuted(muted: boolean): void;\\n    toggleMute(): boolean;\\n    /** The default volumes, sound on (the settings panel's Reset). */\\n    resetVolumes(): void;\\n    /** Engine: once per rendered frame. Schedules the next notes of the song. */\\n    update(): void;\\n    /** Stop everything and close the AudioContext. */\\n    dispose(): void;\\n    private start;\\n140→    private bufferFor;\\n    private toBuffer;\\n    private decode;\\n    private applyVolumes;\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/types/engine/audio/AudioManager.d.ts\",\"offset\":90,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"     * it yourself from a click handler if you start sound from your own UI.\\n     */\\n    unlock(): void;\\n    private target;\\n    /** Listen for the next user input (until the context is running). */\\n    private armUnlock;\\n    private disarmUnlock;\\n    /** Resume a suspended / interrupted context; stop listening for input once it runs. */\\n    private resume;\\n    /** Add or replace a sound effect (data, see SoundDef). */\\n    register(name: string, def: SoundDef): void;\\n    /**\\n     * Play a sound effect by name (built-in SFX, `register`ed or `load`ed) or directly from a\\n     * SoundDef. Returns false when nothing could be heard (locked, muted, no Web Audio).\\n     */\\n    play(sound: string | SoundDef, options?: PlayOptions): boolean;\\n    /**\\n     * Start a sound looping, as a voice you steer while it plays (volume, pan, muffle, pitch:\\n     * with `spatialize` it sits at a place in the world). Before the first user input, or with\\n     * no Web Audio, the voice keeps its settings silently and starts once audio unlocks.\\n     * Stop it when you are done (a level's `dispose`).\\n     */\\n    loop(sound: string | SoundDef, settings?: VoiceSettings): Voice;\\n    /** Voices playing or waiting to (tooling and tests). */\\n    get loops(): readonly Voice[];\\n    /** Stop every looping voice (the engine does this when a level unloads). */\\n    stopLoops(): void;\\n    /**\\n     * Load an audio file (wav/ogg/mp3…) under `name`; `play(name)` then plays it. Works\\n     * before the first user input too: the file is decoded once audio unlocks.\\n     */\\n    load(name: string, url: string): Promise<void>;\\n    /** Start a song (looping by default), replacing the current one. `null` stops music. */\\n    playMusic(song: Song | null, name?: string): void;\\n    stopMusic(): void;\\n    /**\\n     * Volume changes are written to storage. The engine turns this off while a replay plays: the\\n     * recording sets the volumes it set, nothing is written, and the player's come back after.\\n     */\\n    persist: boolean;\\n    setVolume(channel: VolumeChannel, value: number): void;\\n    setMuted(muted: boolean): void;\\n    toggleMute(): boolean;\\n    /** The default volumes, sound 