{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-891638a3-d7f5-497a-8966-eb030b00fc35-43","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"115→    private readonly padHeld;\\n    private readonly listeners;\\n    /** Pointer movement this frame, in CSS pixels (drag or pointer lock). */\\n    readonly mouseDelta: {\\n        x: number;\\n120→        y: number;\\n    };\\n    /**\\n     * Where the pointer last was over the canvas, in normalised device coordinates (−1..1, y up:\\n     * `camera.rayAt(pointer.x, pointer.y, …)` turns it into a ray), and whether it is over it now.\\n     * Under pointer lock it is the screen's centre (the crosshair).\\n     */\\n    readonly pointer: {\\n        x: number;\\n        y: number;\\n130→        over: boolean;\\n        touch: boolean;\\n    };\\n    /** Wheel ticks this frame (+1 = scroll down / zoom out). */\\n    wheel: number;\\n    /** This frame's button presses and releases, in order (`buttonEvents`). */\\n    private _buttonEvents;\\n    /** Commands sent since the last frame began, and this frame's (`send`, `commands`). */\\n    private outbox;\\n    private _commands;\\n140→    private lockTarget;\\n    /** When true, clicking the canvas requests pointer lock (first-person / free camera). */\\n    wantsPointerLock: boolean;\\n    /** Touch joystick, -1..1 per axis; overrides keys when active. */\\n    readonly analog: {\",\"content_concise\":\"115→    private readonly padHeld;\\n    private readonly listeners;\\n    /** Pointer movement this frame, in CSS pixels (drag or pointer lock). */\\n    readonly mouseDelta: {\\n        x: number;\\n120→        y: number;\\n    };\\n    /**\\n     * Where the pointer last was over the canvas, in normalised device coordinates (−1..1, y up:\\n     * `camera.rayAt(pointer.x, pointer.y, …)` turns it into a ray), and whether it is over it now.\\n     * Under pointer lock it is the screen's centre (the crosshair).\\n     */\\n    readonly pointer: {\\n        x: number;\\n        y: number;\\n130→        over: boolean;\\n        touch: boolean;\\n    };\\n    /** Wheel ticks this frame (+1 = scroll down / zoom out). */\\n    wheel: number;\\n    /** This frame's button presses and releases, in order (`buttonEvents`). */\\n    private _buttonEvents;\\n    /** Commands sent since the last frame began, and this frame's (`send`, `commands`). */\\n    private outbox;\\n    private _commands;\\n140→    private lockTarget;\\n    /** When true, clicking the canvas requests pointer lock (first-person / free camera). */\\n    wantsPointerLock: boolean;\\n    /** Touch joystick, -1..1 per axis; overrides keys when active. */\\n    readonly analog: {\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/types/engine/input.d.ts\",\"offset\":115,\"limit\":30,\"raw_output\":\"    private readonly padHeld;\\n    private readonly listeners;\\n    /** Pointer movement this frame, in CSS pixels (drag or pointer lock). */\\n    readonly mouseDelta: {\\n        x: number;\\n        y: number;\\n    };\\n    /**\\n     * Where the pointer last was over the canvas, in normalised device coordinates (−1..1, y up:\\n     * `camera.rayAt(pointer.x, pointer.y, …)` turns it into a ray), and whether it is over it now.\\n     * Under pointer lock it is the screen's centre (the crosshair).\\n     */\\n    readonly pointer: {\\n        x: number;\\n        y: number;\\n        over: boolean;\\n        touch: boolean;\\n    };\\n    /** Wheel ticks this frame (+1 = scroll down / zoom out). */\\n    wheel: number;\\n    /** This frame's button presses and releases, in order (`buttonEvents`). */\\n    private _buttonEvents;\\n    /** Commands sent since the last frame began, and this frame's (`send`, `commands`). */\\n    private outbox;\\n    private _commands;\\n    private lockTarget;\\n    /** When true, clicking the canvas requests pointer lock (first-person / free camera). */\\n    wantsPointerLock: boolean;\\n    /** Touch joystick, -1..1 per axis; overrides keys when active. */\\n    readonly analog: {\\n\",\"total_lines\":278}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"07f58ab7-db78-443b-95d2-d7c70e0be58e"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_24","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I have a solid plan and am starting to write code.\n\nFiles will be created in batches. Playwright is being installed in parallel. The simulation kernel design is being refined to pass star tests on the first attempt. Simulations and a node test will be written first without full 3D, then scenes will be wired up. The activity runner API is being drafted.\n\nThe runner API will expose step, result, phase, done, score, and stars. The scene will feed driver input into the simulation each frame. Headless tests will use a lightweight floor mesh with no hero for speed. A simple torso rotation may replace the full mixer if model loading is slow. The hero model will be loaded once.\n\nA headless boot will be timed after the minimal game is ready. PROGRESS.md will be added at the root, and plan checkboxes will be flipped only after actual completion. The RNG seed for the title screen will be stored in title.js. The game API design is being aligned with the week scripted test structure, with `press` routed through engine input and `state()` returning all test data.\n\nThe `state()` API payload is being defined. It will expose the title screen, current mode, menu rows and focus, day and week data, character stats, activity progress, device state, glyphs, prompt text, pause status, time scale, and tunables.\n\nThe `state()` payload is being expanded to include widgets, touch-only flags, attract mode, save version, music, medley lanes, near status, prescription, and jar unlocks. A headless test harness is being drafted with `boot`, `tap`, and `until` helpers.\n\nThe `until` helper will step the engine up to a maximum of 600 frames until a predicate passes. The name entry screen will default to \"Guest\" with the Done button focused, so tests can confirm by pressing Enter. The ferry screen will auto-advance or be skipped with Enter. The weigh-in flow is also being planned.\n\nThe weigh-in will use expert bots when the driver is set to 'expert'. Local input for the dot will be ignored in that mode, but menus will still respond to keyboard. After weigh-in, the game enters island mode. The player selects an unlocked station from a menu and focuses the pavilion to open the station activity list.\n\nThe hammock option will always end the day, but leaving early triggers a guilt trip rather than blocking progress. The test should complete at least one activity before choosing hammock to see all stations. Day 1 playthrough assertions are being drafted.\n\nThe scripted playthrough is being mapped to a concrete daily routine. Day 1 will use the tree and hoop activities. Days 2 through 7 will each attempt different activities, including a long stand and a beat against the expert. The week ends with a confession that deducts seven stars. Activity durations are being estimated to keep the test run efficient.\n\nActivity durations are being estimated to keep the scripted test efficient. Tree and hoop each take roughly 45–70 seconds, while other days average 40–60 seconds. Seven weigh-ins add about 105 seconds. The full week totals roughly 700 seconds, or about 42,000 frames at 60fps. To keep this fast, fixedUpdate will stay lightweight: a cheap matrix transform on a group will handle visuals instead of the full 3D mixer, which is only used if the hero model is loaded.\n\nHeadless mixer updates will take roughly 5.6 seconds for 42,000 frames, which is acceptable. The scripted test will include full intro, practice, countdown, play, and results screens to match the real flow; first-time practice adds about 100 seconds across activities. The results screen shows stars popping before offering Retry, Next, or Back, and the test will press Next or Back to return to the island. Activity IDs are being mapped to specific stations: tree at the pavilion, heron, warrior (breath), and chair.\n\nThe activity map is being finalized. Day 1 includes squat, hoop, and tree. Day 2 includes header and lunge. Day 3 includes step and slack. Day 4 includes tray and fold. Day 5 includes plank, jog, and pier. Day 6 uses hard versions of each activity. Day 7 uses long stand.\n\nDennis's scores are being set low so the expert can beat him on day 5. June will score around two stars.\n\nMarguerite will score near the three-star threshold so she is often unbeaten. The weekly prescription map is being drafted with daily goals and station openings. A goal-check function will validate progress against these prescriptions. The wobble age formula stores the last three T values, clamps the true age between 18 and 95, subtracts half the star count, and adds seven when the player is unconfessed.\n\nThe chart stores the shown age at each weigh-in. Confession subtracts seven from every stored point. The test will verify that all points drop by exactly seven.\n\nA separate age test will force T values to 1 and 0 to confirm the formula. It will also use idle and expert bots. With T=1 the shown age is 27. With T=0 it is 87.\n\nThe age test will compare an expert bot against an idle bot. The expert should end with a lower age than the average, while the idle bot stays high.\n\nQuestions do not affect age. Only the remark does. Day 7 asks \"Are you happy?\"\n\nA feel-age picker appears once. It is a number picker from 18 to 80 defaulting to 30. The result is used in a joke about wobble age.\n\nSaves use a versioned JSON key `mint-dial-save-v1`. They write after every activity and day. An in-memory fallback covers missing or broken localStorage.\n\nSave parsing will ignore corrupted JSON and fall back to a fresh state instead of crashing. The attract mode idle timer will count title, menu, settings, about, drop-in list, family join, slot select, name entry, records, and locker as menus. Island play, activities, weigh-in, report, ferry, and medley are considered active gameplay. After ten seconds of no input the game exits to the title screen and re-arms.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-995b5ec5-ffeb-4943-9ae0-d62f42ee2a2b-44","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"touch\\?:","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/types/engine/Engine.d.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-995b5ec5-ffeb-4943-9ae0-d62f42ee2a2b-45","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/types/engine/animation/metrics.d.ts","limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":448,"output_tokens":2905,"cache_read_input_tokens":119552,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"c3fb5e52-3fa5-414d-b0e4-37e07952182e"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-995b5ec5-ffeb-4943-9ae0-d62f42ee2a2b-44","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,49,54,48,55,95,95,120,54,57,56,49,101,51,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,49,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,49,54,48,55,95,95,120,54,57,56,49,101,51,47,119,111,114,107,47,77,105,110,116,32,68,105,97,108,45,87,105,105,32,70,105,116,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,49,54,48,55,47,116,121,112,101,115,47,101,110,103,105,110,101,47,69,110,103,105,110,101,46,100,46,116,115,10,49,57,50,58,32,32,32,32,116,111,117,99,104,63,58,32,98,111,111,108,101,97,110,59,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":1,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/types/engine/Engine.d.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":192,\"content\":\"    touch?: boolean;\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-995b5ec5-ffeb-4943-9ae0-d62f42ee2a2b-45","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→import { type AnimationClip, type Object3D, Vector3 } from 'three/webgpu';\\nimport type { ClipDef, RigSpec } from './types';\\n/**\\n * Objective checks for a clip, computed by actually posing the rig (no renderer). These\\n * are the numbers an agent can't eyeball: foot sliding, ground contact, loop seams,\\n * velocity spikes, joint limits. Thresholds are deliberately forgiving; `problems` are\\n * real defects, `warnings` are worth a look.\\n */\\nexport interface ClipReport {\\n10→    name: string;\\n    frames: number;\\n    loop: boolean;\\n    speed: number | null;\\n    /** Lowest sole point over the clip (m) and the frame it happens. Negative = through the floor. */\\n    minSoleY: number;\\n    minSoleFrame: number;\\n    /** Lowest point of any other body part (knees, hands, head...), where and when. */\\n    minBodyY: number;\\n    minBodyMesh: string;\\n20→    minBodyFrame: number;\\n    /** Frames (of grounded clips) where neither sole is within 5 cm of the floor. */\\n    floatingFrames: number;\\n    /** Mean horizontal slip of the planted foot, m/s (0 = perfectly planted). */\\n    footSlide: number;\\n    /** Largest joint-angle jump between the last and first frame of a loop, degrees. */\\n    loopSeam: number;\\n    /** Fastest joint rotation, degrees per second, and where. */\\n    maxAngularSpeed: {\\n        joint: string;\\n30→        degPerSec: number;\\n        frame: number;\\n    };\\n    limitViolations: {\\n        joint: string;\\n        axis: 'x' | 'y' | 'z';\\n        frame: number;\\n        value: number;\\n        range: [number, number];\\n    }[];\\n40→    /** Pelvis height range (m) — how much the body bobs. */\",\"content_concise\":\"1→import { type AnimationClip, type Object3D, Vector3 } from 'three/webgpu';\\nimport type { ClipDef, RigSpec } from './types';\\n/**\\n * Objective checks for a clip, computed by actually posing the rig (no renderer). These\\n * are the numbers an agent can't eyeball: foot sliding, ground contact, loop seams,\\n * velocity spikes, joint limits. Thresholds are deliberately forgiving; `problems` are\\n * real defects, `warnings` are worth a look.\\n */\\nexport interface ClipReport {\\n10→    name: string;\\n    frames: number;\\n    loop: boolean;\\n    speed: number | null;\\n    /** Lowest sole point over the clip (m) and the frame it happens. Negative = through the floor. */\\n    minSoleY: number;\\n    minSoleFrame: number;\\n    /** Lowest point of any other body part (knees, hands, head...), where and when. */\\n    minBodyY: number;\\n    minBodyMesh: string;\\n20→    minBodyFrame: number;\\n    /** Frames (of grounded clips) where neither sole is within 5 cm of the floor. */\\n    floatingFrames: number;\\n    /** Mean horizontal slip of the planted foot, m/s (0 = perfectly planted). */\\n    footSlide: number;\\n    /** Largest joint-angle jump between the last and first frame of a loop, degrees. */\\n    loopSeam: number;\\n    /** Fastest joint rotation, degrees per second, and where. */\\n    maxAngularSpeed: {\\n        joint: string;\\n30→        degPerSec: number;\\n        frame: number;\\n    };\\n    limitViolations: {\\n        joint: string;\\n        axis: 'x' | 'y' | 'z';\\n        frame: number;\\n        value: number;\\n        range: [number, number];\\n    }[];\\n40→    /** Pelvis height range (m) — how much the body bobs. */\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/types/engine/animation/metrics.d.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"import { type AnimationClip, type Object3D, Vector3 } from 'three/webgpu';\\nimport type { ClipDef, RigSpec } from './types';\\n/**\\n * Objective checks for a clip, computed by actually posing the rig (no renderer). These\\n * are the numbers an agent can't eyeball: foot sliding, ground contact, loop seams,\\n * velocity spikes, joint limits. Thresholds are deliberately forgiving; `problems` are\\n * real defects, `warnings` are worth a look.\\n */\\nexport interface ClipReport {\\n    name: string;\\n    frames: number;\\n    loop: boolean;\\n    speed: number | null;\\n    /** Lowest sole point over the clip (m) and the frame it happens. Negative = through the floor. */\\n    minSoleY: number;\\n    minSoleFrame: number;\\n    /** Lowest point of any other body part (knees, hands, head...), where and when. */\\n    minBodyY: number;\\n    minBodyMesh: string;\\n    minBodyFrame: number;\\n    /** Frames (of grounded clips) where neither sole is within 5 cm of the floor. */\\n    floatingFrames: number;\\n    /** Mean horizontal slip of the planted foot, m/s (0 = perfectly planted). */\\n    footSlide: number;\\n    /** Largest joint-angle jump between the last and first frame of a loop, degrees. */\\n    loopSeam: number;\\n    /** Fastest joint rotation, degrees per second, and where. */\\n    maxAngularSpeed: {\\n        joint: string;\\n        degPerSec: number;\\n        frame: number;\\n    };\\n    limitViolations: {\\n        joint: string;\\n        axis: 'x' | 'y' | 'z';\\n        frame: number;\\n        value: number;\\n        range: [number, number];\\n    }[];\\n    /** Pelvis height range (m) — how much the body bobs. */\\n\",\"total_lines\":68}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"22210d7e-2e3d-40bb-912e-aa6fc747b495"}
