/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/CREDITS.md\\n(node:3867286) Warning: The 'NO_COLOR' env is ignored due to the 'FORCE_COLOR' env being set.\\n(Use `node --trace-warnings ...` to show where the warning was created)\\n\\nadded 2 packages in 487ms\\npw ok\\n(node:3867315) Warning: The 'NO_COLOR' env is ignored due to the 'FORCE_COLOR' env being set.\\n(Use `node --trace-warnings ...` to show where the warning was created)\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"command\":\"DEV=\\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607\\\"\\nwc -c \\\"$DEV/CREDITS.md\\\"\\n# install playwright locally without downloading browsers\\ncd \\\"$DEV\\\"\\nnpm init -y >/dev/null 2>&1\\nnpm install --no-save --no-fund --no-audit playwright@1.63.0 2>&1 | tail -20\\nnode -e \\\"import('playwright').then(p=>console.log('pw', p.chromium ? 'ok' : 'no'))\\\"\",\"truncated\":false,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Install Playwright 1.63 and check credits size\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3%2Fwork/01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469/terminal/call-90ddf066-c486-426a-8272-4cf886291750-50.log\",\"total_bytes\":513}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"c6093d37-d980-4d7f-bbd9-f016fa8d7264"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_28","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The `npm install --no-save` command likely did not write dependencies to package.json.\n\nI will add Playwright to package.json as a devDependency and set \"type\": \"module\". I am now writing the source files directly.\n\nThe app architecture is now fully mapped. Core modules will handle dots, RNG, drivers, tunables, scoring, saving, and device state. Audio modules will cover voice synthesis, songs, and SFX. UI font utilities will manage text rendering.\n\nThe architecture now includes art and data modules for glyphs, sprites, and game content. Activity simulations, clips, models, avatars, and textures are mapped out. The main entry point, world scene, boot script, and build tools are also defined. The large app.js state machine will be split into modes.\n\nI am adding `src/game/flow.js` for week transitions and `src/game/huddraw.js` for drawing. I will keep the app.js monolithic but well-organized to ship faster.\n\nI am also flagging five bugs to watch for: engine headless import paths, missing-world setup failures, volume timing, gamepad button assignments, and headless title attract mode frame updates.\n\nI will write the full code in one pass and debug afterward rather than bootstrapping a minimal world first. I am now drafting HUD text helpers: `say`, `wrap`, and `measureSay`. I also need to verify which characters are allowed in the glyph set.\n\nLowercase letters will be drawn by the custom glyph renderer. Uppercase letters, digits, and punctuation will use the standard HUD text system. Invalid characters will be replaced with question marks.\n\nStars will be rendered as small sprites instead of unicode symbols.\n\nPrompt strings will follow a `[glyph] verb` pattern. The browser test will verify game state directly rather than inspecting pixels. State objects will expose `promptDevice`, `promptGlyph`, and `focus` to support this.\n\nThe prompt glyph set is fixed at 'playstation'. The confirm glyph will be 'cross' by default, but 'a' for Xbox, 'enter' for keyboard, and 'click' for mouse. Widgets register during draw with hover and click handlers. Input is processed against the previous frame's widget list before drawing rebuilds them.\n\nMouse lean will be calculated by subtracting the dial center from the pointer position, dividing by the radius, and clamping to a unit disc. LocalDriver will also smooth keyboard input and halve speed when Shift is held. The title scene needs visible 3D geometry—ground plane, ounce model, and sky background—to ensure the capture is substantially painted.\n\nThe title camera will be fixed on the plaza. Morning sky will be applied at 10 o'clock. High quality is kept despite possible software WebGPU slowness. The hub scene will render at medium quality in four copies. Card scenes will use light lighting.\n\nI am writing the source files in large parallel batches. The 120-line requirement will be filled by a generator of hand-authored in-voice lines. Each activity needs eight line sets: four star levels and two repeats. I have counted 17 activities total, including poses.\n\nThe line data structure will use a `LINES` object keyed by activity name. Each activity stores `first` and `repeat` sets, with each set holding arrays of 0/1/2/3 star levels. Every line is capped at 52 characters and three lines. Barks will be stored in a separate `barks` section.\n\nI am adding `ringOut`, `fall`, and `streak` barks to the line bank. A `lineFor` helper will select the correct result line from the first or repeat set based on star level. Classmate scores are being stored in a `RIVALS` object keyed by activity.\n\nDennis will score 30 for tree, below the 45-star threshold, so the expert can beat him. Marguerite at 96 may tie. Story beats will appear on the island each day. sims.js needs careful writing. Rep input mapping is separate from dot lean: the expert bot sets depth commands, while the local driver maps the stick to depth; reps scrub animation rather than scoring via the dot, though the dot remains for flavor.\n\nThe activity bot interface will be a `botAct` function returning x, y, breath, stepL, stepR, confirm, and depth. Stillness bots use BotDriver coordinates. Reps bots use a depth tracker. Hoop bots circle. The scene uses this for bot skills while LocalDriver handles human input.\n\nA GhostDriver class is being drafted for replay. It stores a target message and simulated state. Push adds a new message. Read returns default zero inputs.\n\nGhostDriver now interpolates its shown position toward the target message each frame using exponential smoothing. A Dot placed on a ghost lane will not receive step() calls because that lane runs with sim: false and its position is driven entirely by present(). The Lane class constructor is being drafted to accept a driver type, track score, and instantiate a Dot.\n\nThe `Lane.step` method will branch on `simulated`: ghost lanes call `driver.present(dt)` directly, while simulated lanes read inputs from the driver and step the event simulation. The medley sequence will run 55 seconds per event with 10-second gaps between them, followed by a podium. Scores are normalized to a 0-1000 range per event using a stars-like curve, and the total is the sum of all three events, capped at 3000.\n\nA `norm` helper will scale raw scores into 0-1000 by dividing by thresholds and clamping. Stillness maps 0–100 to 0–1000, hoop divides raw rotations by 110, and header divides raw by 800.\n\nFamily hour join screen lets up to four devices claim mats. Pads press Cross on their index; keyboard presses Enter. Keyboard-and-mouse counts as one seat, so the total cap is four.\n\nPadDriver will detect button 0 on the pad index to claim a mat, with a Node.js guard for missing getGamepads. In session mode, the medley clock will use AIHub.time()/1000 while outside it uses accumulated time. Session ghost replay will simulate one local lane and run the other three as ghosts fed by messages, sending the player's state every 100 ms. Pause will also adjust timeScale.\n\nPause freezes the engine at `timeScale = 0` and restores the previous speed on resume, including any dev slider value. The simulation reads `app.tunables` live each step so tests can mutate values like `dotInstability` and see immediate effects. Reset methods will copy defaults per tab or clone all defaults globally.\n\nThe Tools tab will expose real functions for every requested shortcut: jump to day, jump to activity, finish with n stars, give 50 drips, unlock all, autopilot, god mode, time scale, overlay, hide HUD, free camera, dialogue tester, sound test, animation viewer, and reset save. Each one will be implemented as a genuine function and verified in tests.\n\nExport JSON will print to the console or copy to the clipboard when allowed; Node.js falls back to console.log.\n\nA fingerprint method will serialize mode, score, dot state, and day into a string so that recording an activity and replaying it produces identical fingerprints, satisfying the determinism requirement.\n\nThe engine's recording and replay rely on deterministic fingerprints, so Math.random is forbidden; only ctx.random or a seeded generator may be used. Dot noise derives from sine-of-time, and bots use seeded randomness. The attract mode will loop ring ×2, god mode, and expert bots for 14 seconds each, advancing through iris transitions without waiting for the cover promise.\n\nIris transitions will fire-and-forget without blocking the simulation. Touch messages wrap at hud.width minus 24 pixels. The settings button appears only in top-right corner when touch-only mode is detected at boot via matchMedia and gamepad detection.\n\nA later-arriving pad will drop the touch-only message. Settings live in our save and override engine defaults; music volume is locked to 0.10 at boot, overwriting any engine-stored value.\n\nA package.json with type module and a simple test runner are being added. The runner prints only failures and a one-line pass count, exits with code 1 if any tests fail, and must end with an all-passed line such as `212/212 passed`. Browser tests will live inside test.mjs.\n\nThe test runner will execute node tests first, then browser tests, then the hub. Browsers will run sequentially and close after each pass. A shot.mjs script is being added for screenshots. File creation is starting now, with extra care for the large app.js. The flow state machine is being reviewed once more before drafting.\n\nThe full flow state machine is now mapped. Pause is an overlay flag that keeps the current mode active while freezing time and routing input to a menu. Attract mode replaces the current mode and always exits back to title. All other states are discrete modes: title, menu, settings, about, slots, name, ferry, feel, weighin, island, station, activity, results, report, ending, week2, dev, dropin, join, medley, podium, card, locker, records, and jar.\n\nIsland menu rows will be dynamic: unlocked stations, Sweat Jar, Locker from day two onward, Hall of Numbers, Hammock, and Back. Station menus list activities with locked ones greyed by day requirement. Drop-in mode skips drips and story, saving only best scores. Family flow runs join, medley, podium, then rematch or menu. Simulations will expose a `createSim(id, opts)` factory returning `step(dt, input)` and `snapshot()`, letting activity mode drive them frame by frame.\n\nActivity phases now compute stars and set done=true once the results phase begins. Intro timing is fixed at 2.5 seconds, practice at 8 seconds on first play, a 3-second countdown, and an outro of 1.5 seconds. The week test will wait for results mode before pressing confirm; practice delays add up to roughly 120 seconds across fifteen activities. The day minimum path is mapped: Day 1 requires stillness plus one other activity, Day 2 needs two stars, Day 3 needs step, and Day 4 requires tray, press, and fold.\n\nDay 5 requires beating Dennis at header or pier. Day 6 needs any three-star activity, such as hard tree or hoop. Day 7 is longstand. The full week path totals about ten activities and seven weigh-ins, roughly thirty-six thousand frames. Weigh-in duration is fixed at thirteen seconds of scoring plus question and reveal.\n\nHammock will advance immediately after confirmation. Report mode pauses for three seconds or until the player presses confirm; tests can skip it. Ferry waits for confirmation or eight seconds, then test asserts the ferry mode and confirms. Age picker in feel mode and name entry default to Guest. Confession is added to ending mode after longstand results. Dev tools are not required during the week playthrough.\n\nAfter the ending credits, the game advances to Week 2 with day eight and phase set to weigh-in or island. Tests will assert week equals two, ages are reduced by seven, and the mode is either weigh-in or island. The chart animates seven points for days one through seven; confession subtracts seven from each point, while Week 2 entries reflect true ages without the added offset. The shown age logic during weigh-in recording is now being implemented.\n\nThe shown age formula is now concrete: `trueAge + 7` when unconfessed, and `trueAge` after confession. Confession subtracts seven from every stored shown age. Tests will snapshot the chart before and after confession to verify each point drops by exactly seven.\n\nA dedicated weigh-in simulation unit test will validate the age formula against known T arrays, confirm that idle T produces a higher age than expert T, and check that Stillness yields ring 0.30 with the same dot measurement.\n\nThe question does not change T. The glyph font will be added exactly as specified. Models.js will include the plan's ounce, kettlebell, foam roller, jar, pavilion, and a few simpler models; checkModel will run in tests to catch issues. Clips will be copied from the plan, and validateClip will be tested directly. analyzeClip will be exercised in tests by loading the hero model headlessly.\n\nPlank and other director-verified clips will be used exactly. A new Press clip will be added using placeFeet, but it will be removed from the required set if analyzeClip fails; squat can stand in visually while the simulation remains Press. The avatar dress function and a clinic-tile texture will also be added. Files are now being written.\n\nA comprehensive test file will import real modules. Headless three.js works through pixel-engine. The Game class requires name, setup, update, fixedUpdate, status, fingerprint, and cameraTarget. Optional dispose is allowed. cameraTarget for title returns a point. If the hero model fails to load in headless mode, a simple mesh will be substituted so simulations can still run.\n\nActivity simulations will live in `src/core/sims.js` as a `Sim` class. It steps at 1/60 second intervals and tracks phase, time, score, stars, and drip count. The factory exports `createSim(id, opts)` and a `runToEnd` helper for tests. Options include tunables, seed, difficulty flags, prescription, and ring scale.\n\nThe simulation will be kept pure of input logic. The scene always passes input from its driver into `step(dt, input)`, and the bot stays outside the sim so tests can drive it the same way the real game does.\n\nThe test strategy now includes both a direct simulation loop and a headless scene run. The headless test will use Engine.headless(World) with setDriver and go() to activity, then step until results. This validates that the scene wires input correctly. The go() method is a required debug API.\n\nThe `go` method is an App-level transition that starts activities through the same `startActivity(id)` path used by menus, so tests can begin from real game states. A headless run of 17 activities across two skills at roughly 600 frames per second should take about 16 seconds, though idle and sloppy phases may add a small amount.\n\nA tiny benchmark will be written first to measure headless frame rate before the full suite runs. Files will be batched as they are written. PROGRESS.md will be placed in the workspace root. Deviations from the plan will be noted, and scene files will stay in their prescribed locations.\n\nScene modes will be grouped into `src/app.js` and `src/scenes/world.js` rather than one file per screen. This keeps the week as a single headless session. The deviation will be noted in PROGRESS.md.\n\nThe file layout is now fixed: `src/scenes/world.js` for the game shell, `src/app.js` for state and transitions, `src/core/sims.js` for activity simulations, and `src/ui/draw.js` for the HUD. A dev tool will let tests force an activity result to 0–3 stars and jump straight to results. God mode will scale the avatar back inside the ring if it drifts past 98% of the radius after a dot step. Autopilot will be wired through `setDriver`.\n\nEngine time scale will be stored and paused by setting it to zero. Free camera mode will be enabled with a preset and URL sync disabled. The HUD can be hidden by skipping the draw call. Debug text will appear in both status and HUD overlays. A dialogue tester will display a line with voice. Sound tests will play the song and sound effects. An animation viewer mode will cycle through clips by posing the hero. Reset save will clear all storage.\n\nA live slider test will exercise the game's balance code directly. A `sampleDot(tunables, frames)` helper will be shared by the game and tests. During a headless run, changing a tunable mid-step will produce a different dot path than a control run. The slider list must match the plan exactly. Gentle mode is a setting that scales rings by 1.25 and noise by 0.8. It is not a slider.\n\nThe effective ring radius is base times ringScale times 1.25 in gentle mode, and dot noise is multiplied by 0.8 in that mode. The medical disclaimer will read exactly: \"This is not medical advice. Ounce is a scale.\" Forbidden words will be checked in line text and activity names. The title \"Mint Dial\" is original and avoids Nintendo names. The output filename will use the stem Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607.html with a matching dev folder. Code will be written in a compact but readable style.\n\nThe expert strategy for the header activity will track incoming objects by land time and type. It will move toward the nearest coconut or pine and away from a flip-flop, clamping horizontal input to arrive smoothly at 4.5 speed. The slackline expert will target the dot’s x position and walk when the dot is within 0.4 meters.\n\nGusts will apply a ±1.6 horizontal force to the dot. The expert bot must counter this with PD control using tau 0.17 and kp 1.9, plus instability. It should finish the slackline activity with zero falls, matching the good bot’s 28-second run.\n\nThe expert bot will be tuned to match the measured good-bot baseline of 28 seconds and zero falls. The continuous ±1.6 m/s² gust force is integrated directly into velocity, so the impulse over one second is roughly 1.6 m/s.\n\nThe expert bot can counter the 1.6 m/s² gust with a horizontal input of roughly -0.53, so it should finish the slackline without falling. Idle and sloppy phases will not finish activities, yielding zero stars. The slackline time limit is 75 seconds; reaching that limit without finishing also gives zero stars. Walking instability is set to 4.333 and standing to 2, multiplied into the dot formula as `inst * (m.inst ?? 1)`.\n\nThe tray physics will use kinematic tilt-driven acceleration instead of Rapier gravity. This avoids headless tuning issues and keeps the simulation deterministic. The visual group tilts to match the physics rules.\n\nThe jog activity will use a simple linear path from 0 to 220 meters with fixed cup positions and lateral offsets of ±1.5, skipping the full Catmull-Rom spline for scoring.\n\nThe expert jog strategy steers toward each cup’s lateral offset. The coach moves at 3 m/s and the player speed maps 2.4–3.6 steps per second to roughly 3 m/s; staying inside the band yields full pace and cup scores for three stars. Idle yields zero score. Step chart notes will be precomputed from a string pattern at 104 BPM.\n\nThe step chart will be generated programmatically from repeated 16-character patterns rather than a single long string. Each pattern represents one bar of 16 sixteenths. The expert bot will press the foot on the exact frame nearest each note to hit the timing window.\n\nThe step chart timing window is ±55 ms, about three frames at 60 fps. The expert will press the foot on a rising edge or hold it during that window without double-counting notes. Idle never presses and scores zero.\n\nFor the breath activity, the expert will follow the pose’s breathing cycle by holding `input.breath` true during the inhale phase. The score includes a 0.2×breath term.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The kit is Pixel Engine 0.46.0 and the title draw is Mint Dial. I'll put the core systems in place and prove the balance model before building the week on top."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-cc117e5e-787f-4607-b669-27bd7222b585-51","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/package.json","new_string":"{\n  \"name\": \"mint-dial\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"description\": \"Mint Dial, a fitness week about a polite scale.\"\n}\n","old_string":""}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-cc117e5e-787f-4607-b669-27bd7222b585-52","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/data/title.js","new_string":"/** The only place the title is stored. Everything else imports this. */\nexport const TITLE = 'Mint Dial';\nexport const TAGLINE = 'Keep the dot in the circle.';\n","old_string":""}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-cc117e5e-787f-4607-b669-27bd7222b585-53","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/core/rng.js","new_string":"/** Mulberry32. Same seed, same stream. Never Math.random in gameplay. */\nexport function mulberry32(seed) {\n  let a = seed >>> 0;\n  return function rand() {\n    a |= 0;\n    a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) | 0;\n    let t = Math.imul(a ^ (a >>> 15), 1 | a);\n    t = (t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), 61 | t)) ^ t;\n    return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n  };\n}\n\nexport function hashString(s) {\n  let h = 2166136261;\n  const str = String(s);\n  for (let i = 0; i < str.length; i++) h = Math.imul(h ^ str.charCodeAt(i), 16777619);\n  return h >>> 0;\n}\n","old_string":""}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-cc117e5e-787f-4607-b669-27bd7222b585-54","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/core/dot.js","new_string":"// Pure centre-of-balance. Step at 60 Hz. p stays in -1.2..1.2.\nexport class Dot {\n  x = 0;\n  y = 0;\n  vx = 0;\n  vy = 0;\n  ux = 0;\n  uy = 0;\n  t = 0;\n  constructor(rand) {\n    this.ph = [rand(), rand(), rand(), rand()].map((r) => r * 6.283185307179586);\n  }\n  step(dt, inX, inY, T, m = {}) {\n    this.t += dt;\n    const k = Math.min(1, dt / T.dotLag);\n    this.ux += (inX - this.ux) * k;\n    this.uy += (inY - this.uy) * k;\n    const n = T.dotNoise * (m.noise ?? 1);\n    const inst = T.dotInstability * (m.inst ?? 1);\n    const auth = T.dotAuthority * (m.auth ?? 1);\n    const nx = n * (Math.sin(1.7 * this.t + this.ph[0]) + 0.6 * Math.sin(3.1 * this.t + this.ph[1]));\n    const ny = n * (Math.sin(1.3 * this.t + this.ph[2]) + 0.6 * Math.sin(2.7 * this.t + this.ph[3]));\n    this.vx += (inst * this.x + auth * this.ux - T.dotDamping * this.vx + nx + (m.bx ?? 0)) * dt;\n    this.vy += (inst * this.y + auth * this.uy - T.dotDamping * this.vy + ny + (m.by ?? 0)) * dt;\n    this.x += this.vx * dt;\n    this.y += this.vy * dt;\n    const d = Math.hypot(this.x, this.y);\n    if (d > 1.2) {\n      const s = 1.2 / d;\n      this.x *= s;\n      this.y *= s;\n      this.vx *= 0.3;\n      this.vy *= 0.3;\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nexport const DOT_DEFAULTS = {\n  dotInstability: 0.6,\n  dotAuthority: 3.0,\n  dotDamping: 3.4,\n  dotNoise: 0.8,\n  dotLag: 0.08,\n};\n","old_string":""}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-cc117e5e-787f-4607-b669-27bd7222b585-55","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/core/tunables.js","new_string":"import { DOT_DEFAULTS } from './dot.js';\n\n/** Live sliders. Read every step. Defaults match the plan. */\nexport const TUNABLE_TABS = {\n  Balance: [\n    ['dotInstability', 0.6, 0, 4, 0.05],\n    ['dotAuthority', 3, 0, 8, 0.1],\n    ['dotDamping', 3.4, 0, 8, 0.1],\n    ['dotNoise', 0.8, 0, 4, 0.05],\n    ['dotLag', 0.08, 0.01, 0.4, 0.01],\n    ['ringScale', 1, 0.5, 2, 0.05],\n    ['gustForce', 1.6, 0, 4, 0.1],\n    ['mouseLeanRadius', 70, 20, 160, 2],\n  ],\n  'Breath and reps': [\n    ['breathBonus', 0.55, 0, 1, 0.05],\n    ['repLag', 0.1, 0.02, 0.4, 0.01],\n    ['repFatigue', 0.1, 0, 0.5, 0.01],\n    ['repTempoScale', 1, 0.5, 2, 0.05],\n  ],\n  Rhythm: [\n    ['stepWindow', 1, 0.5, 2, 0.05],\n    ['stepOffsetMs', 0, -80, 80, 5],\n    ['hoopLow', 0.9, 0.2, 2, 0.05],\n    ['hoopHigh', 2.4, 1, 4, 0.05],\n    ['hoopLiftRate', 0.35, 0.05, 1, 0.05],\n  ],\n  Games: [\n    ['headerInterval', 1, 0.4, 2, 0.05],\n    ['slackWalkInst', 2.6, 0.5, 5, 0.1],\n    ['trayGravity', 9.8, 2, 24, 0.2],\n    ['trayMaxTilt', 14, 4, 30, 1],\n    ['jogTargetCadence', 3, 1.5, 5, 0.1],\n    ['pierBoost', 2.14, 1, 3, 0.02],\n  ],\n  Economy: [\n    ['dripRate', 1, 0, 3, 0.1],\n    ['starThresholdScale', 1, 0.5, 1.5, 0.05],\n    ['ageTrainingWeight', 0.5, 0, 2, 0.05],\n  ],\n};\n\nexport function defaultTunables() {\n  const t = { ...DOT_DEFAULTS };\n  for (const rows of Object.values(TUNABLE_TABS)) {\n    for (const [key, value] of rows) t[key] = value;\n  }\n  return t;\n}\n\nexport const DEFAULT_TUNABLES = defaultTunables();\n\nexport function cloneTunables(src = DEFAULT_TUNABLES) {\n  return { ...src };\n}\n\nexport function tabKeys(name) {\n  return (TUNABLE_TABS[name] || []).map((row) => row[0]);\n}\n","old_string":""}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-cc117e5e-787f-4607-b669-27bd7222b585-56","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/core/drivers.js","new_string":"import { applyDeadzone } from '../../pixel-engine.js';\n\n/** Delayed PD. Same bots for classmates, attract, and tests. */\nexport const BOT_SKILLS = {\n  sloppy: { tau: 0.42, kp: 0.7, kd: 0.12, err: 1.3 },\n  average: { tau: 0.3, kp: 1.1, kd: 0.35, err: 0.8 },\n  good: { tau: 0.22, kp: 1.5, kd: 0.55, err: 0.45 },\n  expert: { tau: 0.17, kp: 1.9, kd: 0.7, err: 0.2 },\n};\n\nexport function clampDisc(x, y) {\n  const m = Math.hypot(x, y);\n  if (m > 1) return { x: x / m, y: y / m };\n  return { x, y };\n}\n\nconst EMPTY = { x: 0, y: 0, breath: false, stepL: false, stepR: false, confirm: false, depth: 0 };\n\nexport class BotDriver {\n  constructor(skill, rand, targetFn) {\n    this.skill = skill;\n    this.rand = rand || Math.random;\n    this.targetFn = targetFn || (() => ({ x: 0, y: 0 }));\n    this.hist = [];\n    this.dx = 0;\n    this.dy = 0;\n    this.t = 0;\n    this.displayOnly = false;\n  }\n  read(dot) {\n    if (this.skill === 'idle' || !BOT_SKILLS[this.skill]) return { ...EMPTY };\n    const b = BOT_SKILLS[this.skill];\n    const dt = 1 / 60;\n    this.t += dt;\n    const p = dot || { x: 0, y: 0, vx: 0, vy: 0 };\n    this.hist.push({ t: this.t, x: p.x, y: p.y, vx: p.vx, vy: p.vy });\n    const want = this.t - b.tau;\n    let seen = this.hist[0];\n    for (const h of this.hist) if (h.t <= want + 1e-9) seen = h;\n    while (this.hist.length > 2 && this.hist[1].t < want) this.hist.shift();\n    const tgt = this.targetFn() || { x: 0, y: 0 };\n    this.dx += (this.rand() - 0.5) * b.err * dt * 6;\n    this.dy += (this.rand() - 0.5) * b.err * dt * 6;\n    this.dx *= 0.995;\n    this.dy *= 0.995;\n    let ux = -b.kp * (seen.x - (tgt.x || 0)) - b.kd * seen.vx + this.dx;\n    let uy = -b.kp * (seen.y - (tgt.y || 0)) - b.kd * seen.vy + this.dy;\n    const c = clampDisc(ux, uy);\n    return { ...EMPTY, x: c.x, y: c.y };\n  }\n}\n\n/** Keyboard attack 0.10s, release 0.06s. Shift halves the lean. */\nexport function smoothKeys(state, wishX, wishY, dt, shift) {\n  const ax = wishX === 0 ? 0.06 : 0.1;\n  const ay = wishY === 0 ? 0.06 : 0.1;\n  const kx = 1 - Math.exp(-dt / ax);\n  const ky = 1 - Math.exp(-dt / ay);\n  state.x += (wishX - state.x) * kx;\n  state.y += (wishY - state.y) * ky;\n  const scale = shift ? 0.5 : 1;\n  return clampDisc(state.x * scale, state.y * scale);\n}\n\nexport class LocalDriver {\n  constructor() {\n    this.keys = { x: 0, y: 0 };\n    this.displayOnly = false;\n  }\n  /**\n   * u from the last device's lean.\n   * stick: moveAxis. keys: WASD/arrows. mouse: offset from the dial, a force.\n   */\n  readFrom(ctx, device, dial, radius, dt) {\n    const input = ctx.input;\n    const axis = input.moveAxis();\n    const pad = Math.hypot(input.padAxis?.x || 0, input.padAxis?.y || 0) > 0.05;\n    let x = 0;\n    let y = 0;\n    if (device === 'mouse') {\n      const p = input.pointer;\n      const ax = ((p.x + 1) / 2) * ctx.hud.width;\n      const ay = ((1 - p.y) / 2) * ctx.hud.height;\n      const ox = (ax - dial.x) / radius;\n      const oy = (dial.y - ay) / radius;\n      const c = clampDisc(ox, oy);\n      x = c.x;\n      y = c.y;\n    } else if (device === 'pad' || pad) {\n      x = axis.x;\n      y = axis.y;\n    } else {\n      const wishX = (input.isDown('KeyD') || input.isDown('ArrowRight') ? 1 : 0) - (input.isDown('KeyA') || input.isDown('ArrowLeft') ? 1 : 0);\n      const wishY = (input.isDown('KeyW') || input.isDown('ArrowUp') ? 1 : 0) - (input.isDown('KeyS') || input.isDown('ArrowDown') ? 1 : 0);\n      const shift = input.isDown('ShiftLeft') || input.isDown('ShiftRight');\n      const c = smoothKeys(this.keys, wishX, wishY, dt, shift);\n      x = c.x;\n      y = c.y;\n    }\n    const breath = input.isDown('Space') || input.isDown('PadR2') || input.isDown('PadCross') || input.isDown('MouseLeft');\n    const stepL = input.isDown('KeyF') || input.isDown('ArrowLeft') || input.isDown('PadL1') || input.isDown('PadL2') || (input.mouseButtons & 1) !== 0;\n    const stepR = input.isDown('KeyJ') || input.isDown('ArrowRight') || input.isDown('PadR1') || input.isDown('PadR2') || (input.mouseButtons & 2) !== 0;\n    const confirm = input.wasPressed('Enter') || input.wasPressed('Space') || input.wasPressed('KeyE') || input.wasPressed('PadCross');\n    return { x, y, breath, stepL, stepR, confirm, depth: Math.max(0, -y) };\n  }\n}\n\n/** One physical pad, by index. The engine merges pads, so lanes read the browser themselves. */\nexport class PadDriver {\n  constructor(index) {\n    this.index = index;\n    this.displayOnly = false;\n    this.prevL = false;\n    this.prevR = false;\n  }\n  pad() {\n    const nav = globalThis.navigator;\n    if (!nav?.getGamepads) return null;\n    const list = nav.getGamepads();\n    return list?.[this.index] || null;\n  }\n  read() {\n    const pad = this.pad();\n    if (!pad) return { ...EMPTY };\n    const ax = pad.axes?.[0] || 0;\n    const ay = pad.axes?.[1] || 0;\n    const dz = applyDeadzone(ax, -ay, 0.12);\n    const b = (i) => !!(pad.buttons?.[i]?.pressed);\n    const stepL = b(4) || b(6);\n    const stepR = b(5) || b(7);\n    const out = {\n      x: dz.x,\n      y: dz.y,\n      breath: b(7) || b(0),\n      stepL,\n      stepR,\n      confirm: b(0),\n      depth: Math.max(0, -dz.y),\n      edgeL: stepL && !this.prevL,\n      edgeR: stepR && !this.prevR,\n    };\n    this.prevL = stepL;\n    this.prevR = stepR;\n    return out;\n  }\n}\n\n/** Display only. Never steps a Dot. */\nexport class GhostDriver {\n  constructor() {\n    this.displayOnly = true;\n    this.simulated = false;\n    this.target = null;\n    this.shown = { x: 0, y: 0, c: 0, t: 0, s: 0, a: 0 };\n  }\n  push(msg) {\n    if (!msg) return;\n    this.target = msg;\n  }\n  present(dt) {\n    if (!this.target) return this.shown;\n    const k = 1 - Math.exp(-Math.max(0, dt) * 12);\n    this.shown.x += ((this.target.x || 0) - this.shown.x) * k;\n    this.shown.y += ((this.target.y || 0) - this.shown.y) * k;\n    this.shown.c = this.target.c ?? this.shown.c;\n    this.shown.t = this.target.t ?? this.shown.t;\n    this.shown.s = this.target.s ?? this.shown.s;\n    this.shown.a = this.target.a ?? this.shown.a;\n    return this.shown;\n  }\n  read() {\n    return { ...EMPTY };\n  }\n}\n","old_string":""}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1045,"output_tokens":13389,"cache_read_input_tokens":144256,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"e5cb85f9-1f7d-4a34-8ead-b20ef7c90762"}
