-xhigh-20261104-221607/types/engine/clock.d.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":2,\"content\":\" * Game time from real time: a speed (`engine.timeScale`: slow motion, fast forward, 0 to\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/types/engine/audio/music.d.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":37,\"content\":\"export declare function parseSong(song: Song): ParsedSong;\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/types/engine/audio/AudioManager.d.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":123,\"content\":\"    playMusic(song: Song | null, name?: string): void;\"},{\"line_number\":130,\"content\":\"    setVolume(channel: VolumeChannel, value: number): void;\"},{\"line_number\":134,\"content\":\"    resetVolumes(): void;\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/types/engine/audio/index.d.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":3,\"content\":\"export { PLAYGROUND_SONG, noteSound, parseSong, type Instrument, type ParsedSong, type Song, type SongNote } from './music';\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-99f02aad-ea55-46fb-bd7a-02e2431e34f5-22","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→// Lantern Night: walk (WASD / arrows), push both crates onto the glowing pads (walk into a\\n// crate to push it), then leave through the gate in the north wall.\\nimport { compileClips, ContactShadow, Engine, HERO_CLIPS, HERO_MODEL, HERO_RIG, LOOK_PRESETS, mergeStaticMeshes, PALETTE, PlatformerCharacter, RAPIER, readMoveInput, setLookLayer, THREE, toonMaterial, withUrlOptions } from '../pixel-engine.js';\\n\\nconst { BoxGeometry, Color, CylinderGeometry, Mesh, Vector3 } = THREE;\\n\\nconst SONG = {\\n  bpm: 84,\\n  tracks: { lead: { wave: 'triangle', decay: 0.3, volume: 0.12 }, bass: { wave: 'square', duty: 0.125, decay: 0.25, volume: 0.05 } },\\n10→  patterns: { a: { lead: 'A4 . C5 . E5 . . . D5 . C5 . B4 . . .', bass: 'A2 . . . . . . . F2 . . . . . . .' } },\\n  order: ['a'],\\n};\\nconst PADS = [[-3, -4], [3, -4]];\\nconst CRATES = [[-3, 1], [3, 1]];\\n\\nclass LanternNight {\\n  name = 'Lantern Night';\\n  assets = [HERO_MODEL, 'assets/tree.glb'];\\n  crates = [];\\n20→  pads = [];\\n  solved = false;\\n  escaped = false;\\n  nextFirefly = 0;\\n  target = new Vector3();\\n  at = new Vector3();\\n\\n  async setup(ctx) {\\n    const { scene, physics, palette, engine } = ctx;\\n    this.sparkle = ctx.random.fork('fireflies'); // drawn per frame (cosmetic): its own stream, so gameplay's never depends on the frame rate\\n30→    // Night: dim the engine's sun and ambient light (reset for the next game on unload).\\n    engine.sun.color.setHex(PALETTE.sky);\\n    engine.sun.intensity = 1.2;\\n    engine.ambient.color.setHex(PALETTE.navy);\\n    engine.ambient.intensity = 1.4;\\n    scene.background = new Color(PALETTE.ink);\\n\\n    const parts = [];\\n    const wall = (x, z, w, d) => {\\n      physics.addStaticBox({ position: [x, 0.6, z], halfExtents: [w / 2, 0.6, d / 2] });\\n40→      const m = new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(w, 1.2, d), toonMaterial(palette.slate));\\n      m.position.set(x, 0.6, z);\\n      m.castShadow = m.receiveShadow = true;\\n      parts.push(m);\\n    };\\n    const floor = new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(30, 1, 30), toonMaterial(palette.teal));\\n    floor.position.y = -0.5;\\n    floor.receiveShadow = true;\\n    parts.push(floor);\\n    physics.addStaticBox({ position: [0, -0.5, 0], halfExtents: [15, 0.5, 15] });\\n50→    wall(-4.75, -8, 6.5, 1); // north wall, with a 3 m gap for the gate\\n    wall(4.75, -8, 6.5, 1);\\n    wall(0, 8, 17, 1);\\n    wall(-8, 0, 1, 15);\\n    wall(8, 0, 1, 15);\\n    for (const [x, z] of [[-6.5, -6.5], [6.5, -6.5], [-6.5, 6.5], [6.5, 6.5]]) {\\n      const post = new Mesh(new CylinderGeometry(0.12, 0.15, 1.6, 6), toonMaterial(palette.plum));\\n      post.position.set(x, 0.8, z);\\n      parts.push(post);\\n      ctx.lights.request({ position: [x, 1.8, z], color: 0xffa040, intensity: 7, radius: 7, flicker: 'torch' });\\n60→    }\\n    scene.add(...mergeStaticMeshes(parts));\\n\\n    // The gate: a collider we remove when the puzzle is solved.\\n    this.gate = new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(3, 1.6, 0.6), toonMaterial(palette.red));\\n    this.gate.position.set(0, 0.8, -8);\\n    scene.add(this.gate);\\n    this.gateCollider = physics.addStaticBox({ position: [0, 0.8, -8], halfExtents: [1.5, 0.8, 0.3] });\\n    physics.trigger({ box: [1.5, 1, 0.5] }, [0, 1, -9.2], { tag: 'character', once: true, onEnter: () => this.escape(ctx) });\\n\\n70→    // Pads and crates. A crate is a dynamic Rapier body the hero pushes (tag 'pushable').\\n    for (const [x, z] of PADS) {\\n      const mesh = new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(1.2, 0.06, 1.2), toonMaterial(palette.navy));\\n      mesh.position.set(x, 0.03, z);\\n      scene.add(mesh);\\n      this.pads.push({ x, z, mesh, lit: false });\\n    }\\n    for (const [x, z] of CRATES) {\\n      const mesh = new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(0.98, 0.98, 0.98), toonMaterial(palette.orange));\\n      mesh.castShadow = mesh.receiveShadow = true;\\n80→      setLookLayer(mesh, 'actors');\",\"content_concise\":\"1→// Lantern Night: walk (WASD / arrows), push both crates onto the glowing pads (walk into a\\n// crate to push it), then leave through the gate in the north wall.\\nimport { compileClips, ContactShadow, Engine, HERO_CLIPS, HERO_MODEL, HERO_RIG, LOOK_PRESETS, mergeStaticMeshes, PALETTE, PlatformerCharacter, RAPIER, readMoveInput, setLookLayer, THREE, toonMaterial, withUrlOptions } from '../pixel-engine.js';\\n\\nconst { BoxGeometry, Color, CylinderGeometry, Mesh, Vector3 } = THREE;\\n\\nconst SONG = {\\n  bpm: 84,\\n  tracks: { lead: { wave: 'triangle', decay: 0.3, volume: 0.12 }, bass: { wave: 'square', duty: 0.125, decay: 0.25, volume: 0.05 } },\\n10→  patterns: { a: { lead: 'A4 . C5 . E5 . . . D5 . C5 . B4 . . .', bass: 'A2 . . . . . . . F2 . . . . . . .' } },\\n  order: ['a'],\\n};\\nconst PADS = [[-3, -4], [3, -4]];\\nconst CRATES = [[-3, 1], [3, 1]];\\n\\nclass LanternNight {\\n  name = 'Lantern Night';\\n  assets = [HERO_MODEL, 'assets/tree.glb'];\\n  crates = [];\\n20→  pads = [];\\n  solved = false;\\n  escaped = false;\\n  nextFirefly = 0;\\n  target = new Vector3();\\n  at = new Vector3();\\n\\n  async setup(ctx) {\\n    const { scene, physics, palette, engine } = ctx;\\n    this.sparkle = ctx.random.fork('fireflies'); // drawn per frame (cosmetic): its own stream, so gameplay's never depends on the frame rate\\n30→    // Night: dim the engine's sun and ambient light (reset for the next game on unload).\\n    engine.sun.color.setHex(PALETTE.sky);\\n    engine.sun.intensity = 1.2;\\n    engine.ambient.color.setHex(PALETTE.navy);\\n    engine.ambient.intensity = 1.4;\\n    scene.background = new Color(PALETTE.ink);\\n\\n    const parts = [];\\n    const wall = (x, z, w, d) => {\\n      physics.addStaticBox({ position: [x, 0.6, z], halfExtents: [w / 2, 0.6, d / 2] });\\n40→      const m = new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(w, 1.2, d), toonMaterial(palette.slate));\\n      m.position.set(x, 0.6, z);\\n      m.castShadow = m.receiveShadow = true;\\n      parts.push(m);\\n    };\\n    const floor = new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(30, 1, 30), toonMaterial(palette.teal));\\n    floor.position.y = -0.5;\\n    floor.receiveShadow = true;\\n    parts.push(floor);\\n    physics.addStaticBox({ position: [0, -0.5, 0], halfExtents: [15, 0.5, 15] });\\n50→    wall(-4.75, -8, 6.5, 1); // north wall, with a 3 m gap for the gate\\n    wall(4.75, -8, 6.5, 1);\\n    wall(0, 8, 17, 1);\\n    wall(-8, 0, 1, 15);\\n    wall(8, 0, 1, 15);\\n    for (const [x, z] of [[-6.5, -6.5], [6.5, -6.5], [-6.5, 6.5], [6.5, 6.5]]) {\\n      const post = new Mesh(new CylinderGeometry(0.12, 0.15, 1.6, 6), toonMaterial(palette.plum));\\n      post.position.set(x, 0.8, z);\\n      parts.push(post);\\n      ctx.lights.request({ position: [x, 1.8, z], color: 0xffa040, intensity: 7, radius: 7, flicker: 'torch' });\\n60→    }\\n    scene.add(...mergeStaticMeshes(parts));\\n\\n    // The gate: a collider we remove when the puzzle is solved.\\n    this.gate = new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(3, 1.6, 0.6), toonMaterial(palette.red));\\n    this.gate.position.set(0, 0.8, -8);\\n    scene.add(this.gate);\\n    this.gateCollider = physics.addStaticBox({ position: [0, 0.8, -8], halfExtents: [1.5, 0.8, 0.3] });\\n    physics.trigger({ box: [1.5, 1, 0.5] }, [0, 1, -9.2], { tag: 'character', once: true, onEnter: () => this.escape(ctx) });\\n\\n70→    // Pads and crates. A crate is a dynamic Rapier body the hero pushes (tag 'pushable').\\n    for (const [x, z] of PADS) {\\n      const mesh = new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(1.2, 0.06, 1.2), toonMaterial(palette.navy));\\n      mesh.position.set(x, 0.03, z);\\n      scene.add(mesh);\\n      this.pads.push({ x, z, mesh, lit: false });\\n    }\\n    for (const [x, z] of CRATES) {\\n      const mesh = new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(0.98, 0.98, 0.98), toonMaterial(palette.orange));\\n      mesh.castShadow = mesh.receiveShadow = true;\\n80→      setLookLayer(mesh, 'actors');\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/examples/top-down.js\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"// Lantern Night: walk (WASD / arrows), push both crates onto the glowing pads (walk into a\\n// crate to push it), then leave through the gate in the north wall.\\nimport { compileClips, ContactShadow, Engine, HERO_CLIPS, HERO_MODEL, HERO_RIG, LOOK_PRESETS, mergeStaticMeshes, PALETTE, PlatformerCharacter, RAPIER, readMoveInput, setLookLayer, THREE, toonMaterial, withUrlOptions } from '../pixel-engine.js';\\n\\nconst { BoxGeometry, Color, CylinderGeometry, Mesh, Vector3 } = THREE;\\n\\nconst SONG = {\\n  bpm: 84,\\n  tracks: { lead: { wave: 'triangle', decay: 0.3, volume: 0.12 }, bass: { wave: 'square', duty: 0.125, decay: 0.25, volume: 0.05 } },\\n  patterns: { a: { lead: 'A4 . C5 . E5 . . . D5 . C5 . B4 . . .', bass: 'A2 . . . . . . . F2 . . . . . . .' } },\\n  order: ['a'],\\n};\\nconst PADS = [[-3, -4], [3, -4]];\\nconst CRATES = [[-3, 1], [3, 1]];\\n\\nclass LanternNight {\\n  name = 'Lantern Night';\\n  assets = [HERO_MODEL, 'assets/tree.glb'];\\n  crates = [];\\n  pads = [];\\n  solved = false;\\n  escaped = false;\\n  nextFirefly = 0;\\n  target = new Vector3();\\n  at = new Vector3();\\n\\n  async setup(ctx) {\\n    const { scene, physics, palette, engine } = ctx;\\n    this.sparkle = ctx.random.fork('fireflies'); // drawn per frame (cosmetic): its own stream, so gameplay's never depends on the frame rate\\n    // Night: dim the engine's sun and ambient light (reset for the next game on unload).\\n    engine.sun.color.setHex(PALETTE.sky);\\n    engine.sun.intensity = 1.2;\\n    engine.ambient.color.setHex(PALETTE.navy);\\n    engine.ambient.intensity = 1.4;\\n    scene.background = new Color(PALETTE.ink);\\n\\n    const parts = [];\\n    const wall = (x, z, w, d) => {\\n      physics.addStaticBox({ position: [x, 0.6, z], halfExtents: [w / 2, 0.6, d / 2] });\\n      const m = new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(w, 1.2, d), toonMaterial(palette.slate));\\n      m.position.set(x, 0.6, z);\\n      m.castShadow = m.receiveShadow = true;\\n      parts.push(m);\\n    };\\n    const floor = new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(30, 1, 30), toonMaterial(palette.teal));\\n    floor.position.y = -0.5;\\n    floor.receiveShadow = true;\\n    parts.push(floor);\\n    physics.addStaticBox({ position: [0, -0.5, 0], halfExtents: [15, 0.5, 15] });\\n    wall(-4.75, -8, 6.5, 1); // north wall, with a 3 m gap for the gate\\n    wall(4.75, -8, 6.5, 1);\\n    wall(0, 8, 17, 1);\\n    wall(-8, 0, 1, 15);\\n    wall(8, 0, 1, 15);\\n    for (const [x, z] of [[-6.5, -6.5], [6.5, -6.5], [-6.5, 6.5], [6.5, 6.5]]) {\\n      const post = new Mesh(new CylinderGeometry(0.12, 0.15, 1.6, 6), toonMaterial(palette.plum));\\n      post.position.set(x, 0.8, z);\\n      parts.push(post);\\n      ctx.lights.request({ position: [x, 1.8, z], color: 0xffa040, intensity: 7, radius: 7, flicker: 'torch' });\\n    }\\n    scene.add(...mergeStaticMeshes(parts));\\n\\n    // The gate: a collider we remove when the puzzle is solved.\\n    this.gate = new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(3, 1.6, 0.6), toonMaterial(palette.red));\\n    this.gate.position.set(0, 0.8, -8);\\n    scene.add(this.gate);\\n    this.gateCollider = physics.addStaticBox({ position: [0, 0.8, -8], halfExtents: [1.5, 0.8, 0.3] });\\n    physics.trigger({ box: [1.5, 1, 0.5] }, [0, 1, -9.2], { tag: 'character', once: true, onEnter: () => this.escape(ctx) });\\n\\n    // Pads and crates. A crate is a dynamic Rapier body the hero pushes (tag 'pushable').\\n    for (const [x, z] of PADS) {\\n      const mesh = new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(1.2, 0.06, 1.2), toonMaterial(palette.navy));\\n      mesh.position.set(x, 0.03, z);\\n      scene.add(mesh);\\n      this.pads.push({ x, z, mesh, lit: false });\\n    }\\n    for (const [x, z] of CRATES) {\\n      const mesh = new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(0.98, 0.98, 0.98), toonMaterial(palette.orange));\\n      mesh.castShadow = mesh.receiveShadow = true;\\n      setLookLayer(mesh, 'actors');\\n\",\"total_lines\":162}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"e9aaf4ee-e09a-4f92-af35-8b0c29ae1193"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_45","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to understand the Hud API, input setKey, Game interface, Song type, and model functions to write art that passes tests.\n\nI'll examine Hud.d.ts, Song type, checkModel, and Engine.headless options before writing large files. The week playthrough needs roughly 37 seconds without practice, plus an extra 8 seconds if practice defaults to first. Tests can disable practice via app or the week.\n\nDay 1 will use tree and hoop, totaling roughly 60 seconds of play plus phases. That is about 6000 frames at 60fps, which headless mode handles in about 800 milliseconds. The full week should stay within 30 to 60 seconds of node time. To speed up the playthrough test, the test can set the expert driver, navigate menus, and wait for the activity to finish. Tree and squat is a shorter alternative at roughly 38 seconds.\n\nThe week.js goal is a pair with id tree. This means the prescription requires both tree and another activity to be completed. The test can therefore use tree plus squat instead of tree plus hoop.\n\nDay 2 requires any activity at least two stars. Day 3 introduces a new activity. Day 4 needs three activities, though header, lunge, and warrior are lengthy. Day 5 is beat Dennis. Day 6 needs a three-star activity. Day 7 is Long Stand followed by confession. The playthrough test will follow the minimum path.\n\nThe test must drive real menus and run activities with bots inside, so using a dev tool to finish with three stars would violate the requirements. I am now weighing activity durations to keep the scripted week as short as possible while still satisfying all prescriptions.\n\nThe scripted week now totals roughly 308 seconds of simulated play. That equals about 18,480 frames at 60fps. Day four will use tray, press, and fold. Day five uses tray to beat Dennis. Day six uses tray for the three-star requirement.\n\nThe full week should finish in about 2.5 seconds of wall-clock time, or roughly 5 to 15 seconds even with rendering. Each activity adds about 14.4 seconds of overhead from intro, practice, countdown, and outro phases. Practice will be enabled only for the first playthrough.\n\nWeek.js sets the first flag based on existing records. The test can run for up to a minute without over-optimizing. I will implement a Menu class with rows, focus index, and per-frame actions. Input handling will use wasPressed for keyboard and pad controls, plus pointer hover and click.\n\nActivities will consume input through LocalDriver or bot auto. Pause toggles via KeyP or PadOptions during play and sets timeScale to zero, which stops fixedUpdate from running. While paused, the dev menu opens to expose live sliders that mutate the same tunables object the simulation reads. Resetting a tab or all tabs mutates those values in place so the running activity sees the new defaults immediately.\n\nAttract mode activates after ten seconds of idle time in title or menu screens. It runs expert simulations with god and ring cheats, and any input returns to the title. Touch-only mode displays a message on the title screen and runs attract without gameplay. When a session exists, the app starts directly on the card scene instead of showing the title. The card scene must stay lightweight. AIHub.ready() is triggered as soon as the card can appear, and Enter also fires it through a direct keydown listener.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c3ba2f13-91e7-4179-ac63-b8ff260447ac-23","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"^(export |  (async )?(connect|ready|answer|send|progress|result|fail|on|active))","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/vendor/hub/session.js","head_limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c3ba2f13-91e7-4179-ac63-b8ff260447ac-24","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev