{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_47","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I have a solid understanding of the requirements. I am ready to begin writing the game.\n\nThe App class will expose methods like `go`, `state`, and `setDriver` so tests can drive it directly. World will delegate update, fixed, and draw calls to the App. Headless tests will instantiate a memory-backed App and bind it to a headless engine.\n\nI am checking whether Game needs setup, update, and fixedUpdate methods. I noticed a potential issue: setting timeScale to 0 freezes the engine and drops key presses, which would break menu navigation that relies on wasPressed.\n\nThe plan claims wasPressed still works when timeScale is 0, but the type definitions say key presses are dropped. I will test this after writing the skeleton. If the engine drops keys, the pause menu approach will fail, and I will need an alternative input path.\n\nThe acceptance criteria explicitly require timeScale to be 0 for pause, so I will trust the plan author's verification and test the behavior. If key presses are indeed dropped, I may need to read input before freezing. I will examine the clock implementation comments more carefully.\n\nThe type definition clarifies that queued key presses are dropped only when the engine is paused, not when timeScale is set to zero. This makes the conflicting comment about timeScale more suspicious. I will write a quick Node script to inspect the unminified engine source and verify the actual behavior empirically.\n\nI will use ctx.time for attract timing, since it freezes at timeScale 0. The idle timer will only count elapsed time during menu modes to avoid triggering attract during gameplay.\n\nI have mapped out the core source files to write: a font utility, device abstraction, actions module, voice and song audio, SFX, and the lines data file.\n\nThe file list now includes art assets, the main app module, world scene, entry point, and build tools. Credits will be extracted from CREDITS.md at build time into a generated creditsText.js for the About screen.\n\nCREDITS.md is 41812 bytes, so it can be included directly. I need validateTexture and textureDef for the clinic tile. I also need checkModel for the models module. For headless tests, analyzeClip requires loading HERO_MODEL, which may need a GPU; I will try it anyway since the plan says it works without one.\n\nI will author the clip definitions exactly as specified in the plan, adding simple hold poses like Press, StepL, and StepR so validateClip passes. I will include the plan's verified clips plus a few extras that also pass validation. If analyzeClip flags any issues, I will fix them. I also noted the song volume requirement: the sum of all volumes must be at least 0.375.\n\nI will use 0.55 and 0.5 for the two song tracks, giving a total volume of 1.0. The step song tempo is exactly 104 BPM.\n\nThe voice syllabifier will split words into consonants and vowels, keep syllable patterns consistent across instances, raise pitch by 25% at question marks, and vary f0 and rate per speaker.\n\nClinical lines will be generated programmatically as original arrays, with at least 120 entries beyond the samples. Every character in game strings must exist in the font or HUD text set; forbidden symbols include stars, em-dashes, curly quotes, and Nintendo-related words.\n\nI will add a glyph set function to ensure every character in game strings has a font glyph. App.state() will expose mode, title, music volume, device, prompt, focus row, widget rects, touch message, attract status, family hour lanes, and score so browser tests can read the full game state.\n\nThe App.state() payload will also include device, prompt, touch flags, attract, paused, timeScale, widget rectangles, HUD dimensions, music settings, family hour lanes, activity, score, stars, day, week, confessed status, chart, and session. Widget rectangles must fit inside the HUD at 1920×1280 and scale down to 640×360. Art assets render at 480×270 for 1080p, 427×240 for 720p, or 640×360 in a small frame.\n\nAspect-fill framing means internal resolution depends on the viewport, so tests must set the viewport. Widgets must fit inside the art rectangle with a 12-pixel margin. The title scales down when the HUD width drops below 220 pixels. Touch messages wrap to fit. Family hour uses three lanes: two stub pads and a keyboard. Each lane reads its own PadDriver index or the keyboard. Headless and browser builds step medley lanes in World fixedUpdate.\n\nI will expose lane positions in App.state() during medley and join modes so browser tests can read them. The test.mjs script must demonstrate that two stub pads and a keyboard move three Family Hour lanes independently. I will write this test to satisfy the verifier's audit of committed tests.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d0dbf5a5-68d0-4430-b18f-efc7b2dd9b40-31","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/vendor/hub/session.js","offset":1,"limit":220}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d0dbf5a5-68d0-4430-b18f-efc7b2dd9b40-32","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/CREDITS.md","limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d0dbf5a5-68d0-4430-b18f-efc7b2dd9b40-33","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"export declare function (textureDef|validateTexture|loadModel|renderSheet)","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/types","glob":"*.d.ts"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4067,"output_tokens":2441,"cache_read_input_tokens":82304,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"11927e06-cf7a-4d72-814d-d20ce6efcca2"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-d0dbf5a5-68d0-4430-b18f-efc7b2dd9b40-31","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\\n(function (root) {\\n  'use strict';\\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\\n\\n  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\\n  var PROGRESS_EVERY_MS = 1000;\\n10→  /** The hub's welcome may change these; a newer hub never needs a newer copy of this file for it. */\\n  var limits = { maxBytes: 16384, ratePerS: 20, burst: 40 };\\n\\n  var framed = false;\\n  try {\\n    framed = root.parent && root.parent !== root;\\n  } catch (e) {\\n    framed = true;\\n  }\\n  var search = String(root.location && root.location.search);\\n20→  var flagged = /[?&]aihub=/.test(search);\\n  var seedArg = /[?&]aihub-seed=(\\\\d+)/.exec(search);\\n\\n  var hub = {\\n    version: VERSION,\\n    protocol: 1,\\n    /** True when the hub launched this page for a session (?aihub=1 inside a frame). */\\n    active: !!(flagged && framed),\\n    me: null,\\n    host: null,\\n30→    isHost: false,\\n    players: [],\\n    mode: null,\\n    seed: 0,\\n    limitMs: 0,\\n    round: 0,\\n    /** True when the hub shows the round's splash and collects every player's ready: call ready() once loaded, with no prompt. */\\n    splash: false,\\n    /** True when the hub seeded Math.random for this round (side by side): every copy draws the same numbers. */\\n    seeded: false,\\n40→  };\\n\\n  /** A storage that lives and dies with the page: the Storage methods, and items as properties too. */\\n  function memoryStorage() {\\n    var data = Object.create(null);\\n    var api = {\\n      getItem: function (k) {\\n        k = String(k);\\n        return k in data ? data[k] : null;\\n      },\\n50→      setItem: function (k, v) {\\n        data[String(k)] = String(v);\\n      },\\n      removeItem: function (k) {\\n        delete data[String(k)];\\n      },\\n      clear: function () {\\n        for (var k in data) delete data[k];\\n      },\\n      key: function (i) {\\n60→        var keys = Object.keys(data);\\n        return i >= 0 && i < keys.length ? keys[i] : null;\\n      },\\n    };\\n    if (typeof Proxy !== 'function') return api;\\n    return new Proxy(api, {\\n      get: function (t, k) {\\n        if (k === 'length') return Object.keys(data).length;\\n        if (typeof k === 'symbol' || k in t) return t[k];\\n        return k in data ? data[k] : undefined;\\n70→      },\\n      set: function (t, k, v) {\\n        if (typeof k !== 'symbol') data[k] = String(v);\\n        return true;\\n      },\\n      has: function (t, k) {\\n        return k in data || k in t;\\n      },\\n      deleteProperty: function (t, k) {\\n        delete data[k];\\n80→        return true;\\n      },\\n      ownKeys: function () {\\n        return Object.keys(data);\\n      },\\n      getOwnPropertyDescriptor: function (t, k) {\\n        return k in data ? { value: data[k], writable: true, enumerable: true, configurable: true } : undefined;\\n      },\\n    });\\n  }\\n90→\\n  /** mulberry32: numbers in [0, 1), the same sequence everywhere for the same 32-bit start. */\\n  function generator(a) {\\n    return function () {\\n      a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0;\\n      var t = a;\\n      t = Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1);\\n      t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61);\\n      return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\\n    };\\n100→  }\\n\\n  // A fair start: in a session the game gets an empty storage of its own, so\\n  // every round starts as a first launch (no saved unlocks, upgrades or runs),\\n  // and nothing the round saves touches the player's own saves.\\n  if (hub.active) {\\n    for (var s = 0, stores = ['localStorage', 'sessionStorage']; s < stores.length; s++) {\\n      try {\\n        Object.defineProperty(root, stores[s], { configurable: true, value: memoryStorage() });\\n      } catch (e) {\\n110→        warn('could not give the game a fresh ' + stores[s]);\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  // Side by side: before any of the game's own scripts run, Math.random becomes\\n  // a generator seeded by the hub, so every copy builds the same start.\\n  var realRandom = Math.random;\\n  var seededRandom = null;\\n  if (hub.active && seedArg) {\\n120→    Math.random = seededRandom = generator(Number(seedArg[1]) >>> 0);\\n    hub.seeded = true;\\n  }\\n\\n  // In a session the hub owns fullscreen: a game that asks for it gets the\\n  // hub's whole page, so the scoreboard and the hub's cards stay on top. The\\n  // hub says when its page goes in and out, so the game's own toggle and its\\n  // fullscreenchange listeners work as they always did.\\n  var fullscreenOn = false;\\n  if (hub.active && root.Element && root.document) {\\n130→    var asks = function (on) {\\n      return function () {\\n        post('fullscreen', { on: on });\\n        return Promise.resolve();\\n      };\\n    };\\n    var proto = root.Element.prototype;\\n    proto.requestFullscreen = proto.webkitRequestFullscreen = asks(true);\\n    root.document.exitFullscreen = root.document.webkitExitFullscreen = asks(false);\\n    var shown = function () {\\n140→      return fullscreenOn ? root.document.documentElement || null : null;\\n    };\\n    try {\\n      Object.defineProperty(root.document, 'fullscreenElement', { configurable: true, get: shown });\\n      Object.defineProperty(root.document, 'webkitFullscreenElement', { configurable: true, get: shown });\\n    } catch (e) {}\\n  }\\n\\n  /**\\n   * No hub after all: play on, with Math.random the page's own again. The\\n150→   * empty storage stays: the game has read it already, and what it writes\\n   * must never land on the player's real saves.\\n   */\\n  function standAlone() {\\n    hub.active = false;\\n    if (seededRandom && Math.random === seededRandom) Math.random = realRandom;\\n    hub.seeded = false;\\n  }\\n\\n  var origin = '*';\\n160→  var welcomed = false;\\n  var ended = false;\\n  var connecting = null;\\n  var goAt = null;\\n  var sentReady = false;\\n  var reported = false;\\n  var handlers = {};\\n  var pending = {};\\n  var tokens = limits.burst;\\n  var refilled = now();\\n170→  var probeFn = null;\\n  var lastProgress = -Infinity;\\n  var nextProgress = null;\\n  var progressTimer = null;\\n\\n  function now() {\\n    return root.performance && root.performance.now ? root.performance.now() : Date.now();\\n  }\\n\\n  function warn(text) {\\n180→    if (root.console) root.console.warn('[AIHub] ' + text);\\n  }\\n\\n  function own(o, k) {\\n    return Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(o, k);\\n  }\\n\\n  /** This client's own fields, which no welcome may overwrite. */\\n  var KEEP = { aihub: 1, type: 1, version: 1, protocol: 1, active: 1, seeded: 1 };\\n\\n190→  /** A plain JSON copy, or undefined when it is not JSON. */\\n  function json(value) {\\n    try {\\n      var text = JSON.stringify(value);\\n      return text === undefined ? undefined : JSON.parse(text);\\n    } catch (e) {\\n      return undefined;\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n200→  function post(type, fields) {\\n    var msg = { aihub: 1, type: type };\\n    for (var key in fields) if (own(fields, key)) msg[key] = fields[key];\\n    try {\\n      root.parent.postMessage(msg, origin);\\n    } catch (e) {\\n      warn('could not reach the hub: ' + e.message);\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n210→  function emit(type, args) {\\n    var list = handlers[type];\\n    if (!list || !list.length || pending[type]) {\\n      (pending[type] = pending[type] || []).push(args);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    for (var i = 0; i < list.length; i++) {\\n      try {\\n        list[i].apply(null, args);\\n      } catch (e) {\\n220→        setTimeout(function () {\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\\n(fun