{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-970c6dd8-e0fd-4d31-a9af-c0652b025f05-36","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"270→      emit('time-up', [{ graceMs: m.graceMs }]);\\n    } else if (m.type === 'end') {\\n      ended = true;\\n      if (progressTimer) clearTimeout(progressTimer);\\n      emit('end', [{ reason: m.reason, standings: m.standings || null }]);\\n    } else {\\n      // An event this client has never heard of: hand it on as it came.\\n      var detail = {};\\n      for (var k in m) if (own(m, k) && k !== 'aihub' && k !== 'type') detail[k] = m[k];\\n      emit(m.type, [detail]);\\n280→    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function info() {\\n    var out = {};\\n    for (var key in hub) if (own(hub, key) && typeof hub[key] !== 'function' && !KEEP[key]) out[key] = hub[key];\\n    out.players = hub.players.slice();\\n    return out;\\n  }\\n\\n290→  /** Join the session. Resolves with the round's info, or null when there is no hub: play normally. */\\n  hub.connect = function (opts) {\\n    if (connecting) return connecting.promise;\\n    var done;\\n    var promise = new Promise(function (resolve) {\\n      done = resolve;\\n    });\\n    connecting = { promise: promise, resolve: done };\\n    if (!hub.active) {\\n      done(null);\\n300→      return promise;\\n    }\\n    opts = opts || {};\\n    root.addEventListener('message', onMessage);\\n    var started = now();\\n    var hello = function () {\\n      if (welcomed) return;\\n      if (now() - started > HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS) {\\n        standAlone();\\n        warn('no hub answered; playing normally');\\n310→        done(null);\\n        return;\\n      }\\n      post('hello', { v: 1, client: VERSION, mode: opts.mode || null, seats: opts.seats || null, card: opts.card === true });\\n      setTimeout(hello, HELLO_EVERY_MS);\\n    };\\n    hello();\\n    return promise;\\n  };\\n\\n320→  /** Everything is loaded: at once when info.splash, otherwise from the player's ready gesture. */\\n  hub.ready = function () {\\n    if (!welcomed || sentReady || ended) return;\\n    sentReady = true;\\n    post('ready', {});\\n  };\\n\\n  /** On the game's own card (connect({ card: true })): this player is 'ready', or asks for 'more' time (again takes it back). */\\n  hub.answer = function (what) {\\n    if (!welcomed || ended || goAt !== null) return;\\n330→    if (what !== 'ready' && what !== 'more') return warn('answer is ready or more');\\n    post('answer', { answer: what });\\n  };\\n\\n  hub.on = function (type, fn) {\\n    (handlers[type] = handlers[type] || []).push(fn);\\n    if (pending[type] && !pending[type].flushing) {\\n      pending[type].flushing = true;\\n      setTimeout(function () {\\n        var queued = pending[type];\\n340→        delete pending[type];\\n        for (var i = 0; i < queued.length; i++) emit(type, queued[i]);\\n      });\\n    }\\n    return function () {\\n      var list = handlers[type] || [];\\n      var at = list.indexOf(fn);\\n      if (at !== -1) list.splice(at, 1);\\n    };\\n  };\",\"content_concise\":\"270→      emit('time-up', [{ graceMs: m.graceMs }]);\\n    } else if (m.type === 'end') {\\n      ended = true;\\n      if (progressTimer) clearTimeout(progressTimer);\\n      emit('end', [{ reason: m.reason, standings: m.standings || null }]);\\n    } else {\\n      // An event this client has never heard of: hand it on as it came.\\n      var detail = {};\\n      for (var k in m) if (own(m, k) && k !== 'aihub' && k !== 'type') detail[k] = m[k];\\n      emit(m.type, [detail]);\\n280→    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function info() {\\n    var out = {};\\n    for (var key in hub) if (own(hub, key) && typeof hub[key] !== 'function' && !KEEP[key]) out[key] = hub[key];\\n    out.players = hub.players.slice();\\n    return out;\\n  }\\n\\n290→  /** Join the session. Resolves with the round's info, or null when there is no hub: play normally. */\\n  hub.connect = function (opts) {\\n    if (connecting) return connecting.promise;\\n    var done;\\n    var promise = new Promise(function (resolve) {\\n      done = resolve;\\n    });\\n    connecting = { promise: promise, resolve: done };\\n    if (!hub.active) {\\n      done(null);\\n300→      return promise;\\n    }\\n    opts = opts || {};\\n    root.addEventListener('message', onMessage);\\n    var started = now();\\n    var hello = function () {\\n      if (welcomed) return;\\n      if (now() - started > HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS) {\\n        standAlone();\\n        warn('no hub answered; playing normally');\\n310→        done(null);\\n        return;\\n      }\\n      post('hello', { v: 1, client: VERSION, mode: opts.mode || null, seats: opts.seats || null, card: opts.card === true });\\n      setTimeout(hello, HELLO_EVERY_MS);\\n    };\\n    hello();\\n    return promise;\\n  };\\n\\n320→  /** Everything is loaded: at once when info.splash, otherwise from the player's ready gesture. */\\n  hub.ready = function () {\\n    if (!welcomed || sentReady || ended) return;\\n    sentReady = true;\\n    post('ready', {});\\n  };\\n\\n  /** On the game's own card (connect({ card: true })): this player is 'ready', or asks for 'more' time (again takes it back). */\\n  hub.answer = function (what) {\\n    if (!welcomed || ended || goAt !== null) return;\\n330→    if (what !== 'ready' && what !== 'more') return warn('answer is ready or more');\\n    post('answer', { answer: what });\\n  };\\n\\n  hub.on = function (type, fn) {\\n    (handlers[type] = handlers[type] || []).push(fn);\\n    if (pending[type] && !pending[type].flushing) {\\n      pending[type].flushing = true;\\n      setTimeout(function () {\\n        var queued = pending[type];\\n340→        delete pending[type];\\n        for (var i = 0; i < queued.length; i++) emit(type, queued[i]);\\n      });\\n    }\\n    return function () {\\n      var list = handlers[type] || [];\\n      var at = list.indexOf(fn);\\n      if (at !== -1) list.splice(at, 1);\\n    };\\n  };\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/vendor/hub/session.js\",\"offset\":270,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"      emit('time-up', [{ graceMs: m.graceMs }]);\\n    } else if (m.type === 'end') {\\n      ended = true;\\n      if (progressTimer) clearTimeout(progressTimer);\\n      emit('end', [{ reason: m.reason, standings: m.standings || null }]);\\n    } else {\\n      // An event this client has never heard of: hand it on as it came.\\n      var detail = {};\\n      for (var k in m) if (own(m, k) && k !== 'aihub' && k !== 'type') detail[k] = m[k];\\n      emit(m.type, [detail]);\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function info() {\\n    var out = {};\\n    for (var key in hub) if (own(hub, key) && typeof hub[key] !== 'function' && !KEEP[key]) out[key] = hub[key];\\n    out.players = hub.players.slice();\\n    return out;\\n  }\\n\\n  /** Join the session. Resolves with the round's info, or null when there is no hub: play normally. */\\n  hub.connect = function (opts) {\\n    if (connecting) return connecting.promise;\\n    var done;\\n    var promise = new Promise(function (resolve) {\\n      done = resolve;\\n    });\\n    connecting = { promise: promise, resolve: done };\\n    if (!hub.active) {\\n      done(null);\\n      return promise;\\n    }\\n    opts = opts || {};\\n    root.addEventListener('message', onMessage);\\n    var started = now();\\n    var hello = function () {\\n      if (welcomed) return;\\n      if (now() - started > HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS) {\\n        standAlone();\\n        warn('no hub answered; playing normally');\\n        done(null);\\n        return;\\n      }\\n      post('hello', { v: 1, client: VERSION, mode: opts.mode || null, seats: opts.seats || null, card: opts.card === true });\\n      setTimeout(hello, HELLO_EVERY_MS);\\n    };\\n    hello();\\n    return promise;\\n  };\\n\\n  /** Everything is loaded: at once when info.splash, otherwise from the player's ready gesture. */\\n  hub.ready = function () {\\n    if (!welcomed || sentReady || ended) return;\\n    sentReady = true;\\n    post('ready', {});\\n  };\\n\\n  /** On the game's own card (connect({ card: true })): this player is 'ready', or asks for 'more' time (again takes it back). */\\n  hub.answer = function (what) {\\n    if (!welcomed || ended || goAt !== null) return;\\n    if (what !== 'ready' && what !== 'more') return warn('answer is ready or more');\\n    post('answer', { answer: what });\\n  };\\n\\n  hub.on = function (type, fn) {\\n    (handlers[type] = handlers[type] || []).push(fn);\\n    if (pending[type] && !pending[type].flushing) {\\n      pending[type].flushing = true;\\n      setTimeout(function () {\\n        var queued = pending[type];\\n        delete pending[type];\\n        for (var i = 0; i < queued.length; i++) emit(type, queued[i]);\\n      });\\n    }\\n    return function () {\\n      var list = handlers[type] || [];\\n      var at = list.indexOf(fn);\\n      if (at !== -1) list.splice(at, 1);\\n    };\\n  };\\n\",\"total_lines\":488}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-970c6dd8-e0fd-4d31-a9af-c0652b025f05-37","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,49,54,48,55,95,95,120,54,57,56,49,101,51,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,49,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,49,54,48,55,95,95,120,54,57,56,49,101,51,47,119,111,114,107,47,77,105,110,116,32,68,105,97,108,45,87,105,105,32,70,105,116,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,49,54,48,55,47,116,121,112,101,115,47,101,110,103,105,110,101,47,97,117,100,105,111,47,65,117,100,105,111,77,97,110,97,103,101,114,46,100,46,116,115,10,49,48,48,58,32,32,32,32,114,101,103,105,115,116,101,114,40,110,97,109,101,58,32,115,116,114,105,110,103,44,32,100,101,102,58,32,83,111,117,110,100,68,101,102,41,58,32,118,111,105,100,59,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":1,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/types/engine/audio/AudioManager.d.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":100,\"content\":\"    register(name: string, def: SoundDef): void;\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-970c6dd8-e0fd-4d31-a9af-c0652b025f05-38","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * Built-in retro sound effects, as data. Tweak numbers here (or register your own with\\n * `ctx.audio.register(name, def)`) and every `ctx.audio.play(name)` picks them up.\\n * See docs/engine/audio.md for the SoundDef fields.\\n */\\nexport declare const SFX: {\\n    /** Short rising square chirp. */\\n    jump: {\\n        wave: \\\"square\\\";\\n10→        duty: number;\\n        freq: number;\\n        freqEnd: number;\\n        attack: number;\\n        sustain: number;\\n        decay: number;\\n        volume: number;\\n    };\\n    /** Higher, thinner chirp with a fifth on top. */\\n    doubleJump: {\\n20→        wave: \\\"square\\\";\\n        duty: number;\\n        freq: number;\\n        freqEnd: number;\\n        arp: number[];\\n        arpRate: number;\\n        attack: number;\\n        sustain: number;\\n        decay: number;\\n        volume: number;\\n30→    };\\n    /** Soft thud: a falling triangle under a short noise puff. */\\n    land: {\\n        wave: \\\"triangle\\\";\\n        freq: number;\\n        freqEnd: number;\\n        attack: number;\\n        decay: number;\\n        volume: number;\\n        layers: {\\n40→            wave: \\\"noise\\\";\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * Built-in retro sound effects, as data. Tweak numbers here (or register your own with\\n * `ctx.audio.register(name, def)`) and every `ctx.audio.play(name)` picks them up.\\n * See docs/engine/audio.md for the SoundDef fields.\\n */\\nexport declare const SFX: {\\n    /** Short rising square chirp. */\\n    jump: {\\n        wave: \\\"square\\\";\\n10→        duty: number;\\n        freq: number;\\n        freqEnd: number;\\n        attack: number;\\n        sustain: number;\\n        decay: number;\\n        volume: number;\\n    };\\n    /** Higher, thinner chirp with a fifth on top. */\\n    doubleJump: {\\n20→        wave: \\\"square\\\";\\n        duty: number;\\n        freq: number;\\n        freqEnd: number;\\n        arp: number[];\\n        arpRate: number;\\n        attack: number;\\n        sustain: number;\\n        decay: number;\\n        volume: number;\\n30→    };\\n    /** Soft thud: a falling triangle under a short noise puff. */\\n    land: {\\n        wave: \\\"triangle\\\";\\n        freq: number;\\n        freqEnd: number;\\n        attack: number;\\n        decay: number;\\n        volume: number;\\n        layers: {\\n40→            wave: \\\"noise\\\";\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/types/engine/audio/sfx.d.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * Built-in retro sound effects, as data. Tweak numbers here (or register your own with\\n * `ctx.audio.register(name, def)`) and every `ctx.audio.play(name)` picks them up.\\n * See docs/engine/audio.md for the SoundDef fields.\\n */\\nexport declare const SFX: {\\n    /** Short rising square chirp. */\\n    jump: {\\n        wave: \\\"square\\\";\\n        duty: number;\\n        freq: number;\\n        freqEnd: number;\\n        attack: number;\\n        sustain: number;\\n        decay: number;\\n        volume: number;\\n    };\\n    /** Higher, thinner chirp with a fifth on top. */\\n    doubleJump: {\\n        wave: \\\"square\\\";\\n        duty: number;\\n        freq: number;\\n        freqEnd: number;\\n        arp: number[];\\n        arpRate: number;\\n        attack: number;\\n        sustain: number;\\n        decay: number;\\n        volume: number;\\n    };\\n    /** Soft thud: a falling triangle under a short noise puff. */\\n    land: {\\n        wave: \\\"triangle\\\";\\n        freq: number;\\n        freqEnd: number;\\n        attack: number;\\n        decay: number;\\n        volume: number;\\n        layers: {\\n            wave: \\\"noise\\\";\\n\",\"total_lines\":167}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"b945b5c3-40b4-439f-b823-7d6cdf81d953"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_50","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I have enough information to write the game.\n\nPlanning the game's menu structure. Attract idle modes include title, menu, slots, name, settings, about, dropin, station, hall, locker, jar, and results. Island, activity play, pause, and session are excluded from attract mode.\n\nClarified that Report, Question, and Reveal are menus. Ferry is a cutscene and Weigh is play. The 10-second attract idle rule excludes play, pause, and hub sessions. Island is free-roam, not a menu, so it cannot trigger attract mode.\n\nFerry is skippable and menu-like, but attract mode will not start there. I am explicitly listing all MENU_MODES. The menu system will process one input action per frame. I am also drafting a tap helper for test navigation.\n\nThe tap helper presses a key for one frame then releases it to trigger wasPressed. Navigation will use ArrowDown to reach a target row and Enter to select. The name screen defaults to \"Guest\" and confirms on Enter. Slots display Continue or New; empty slots route to the name screen. After naming, the ferry cutscene appears with Continue or skip options.\n\nsetDriver must be called before the week begins so activities and weigh-in use bots. The weigh-in lasts 14 seconds, then the question menu appears; tests will select the first answer and confirm through reveal to reach the island. Island navigation splits into two pages: page one lists stations and a More button, and page two lists jar, locker, hall, hammock, and longstand.\n\nStation menus list unlocked activities plus Back. Starting an activity creates a simulation using the driver skill or 'local'. The mode becomes 'activity' and returns to 'results' with stars and drips. Results rows are Retry, Next, and Back. Next returns to the island or station. Back returns to the station. Hammock ends the day after one activity. Otherwise it shows a guilt line.\n\nHammock is always available. Leaving early triggers a guilt line but never blocks the player.\n\nThe Report screen displays drips, stars, a chart, and concern. Confirming it advances to the next morning weigh-in. If day seven includes a longstand activity, confession appears before the report.\n\nConfession follows the longstand goal on day seven.\n\nThe confession subtracts seven from every chart point shown on the report, marks the player as confessed, and then runs credits before the next morning. Each weigh-in stores both true age and shown age. After an activity or day ends, the slot saves to disk. The save object tracks name, look, day, week, drips, stars, totalStars, a chart array, a confessed flag, and a played map recording each activity's best score, stars, and times.\n\nThe save object now includes today's activities, unlocked items, a hard flag for day six and beyond, and feltAge. A prescription check function evaluates daily goals against the current session: pair completion, star threshold, fresh play, activity count, or beating a character.\n\nThe prescription check now includes an ID-based goal. A +5 drip bonus applies once per day when an activity completes the prescription. The pause menu will include a Dev Tools tab with Balance, Breath, Rhythm, Games, Economy, and Tools tabs. Sliders adjust values by step and update live because the tunables object is shared. Reset buttons are available in the Tools tab.\n\nThe Dev Tools tab will include tools to jump to a day, finish 0–3 activities, give 50 drips, unlock all items, toggle autopilot, god mode, time scale, overlays, hide HUD, free camera, dialogue tester, sound test, animation viewer, and reset save.\n\nTests will verify that slider changes update the simulation live and that resetting restores defaults. Each tool will be tested to confirm it alters state. A pause freeze test will record elapsed time, pause the game, step many frames, assert the simulation stays frozen, then resume and confirm it advances.\n\nAttract mode runs a playlist of real simulations using expert skill, god mode, and doubled ring scale. Each activity lasts about fourteen seconds. The playlist covers every family: still, hoop, header, step, slack, tray, pier, jog, long, and hub walk. A full loop of ten activities takes roughly one second to fast-forward through. Family hour medley joins up to four pads plus keyboard.\n\nA ghost lane will use GhostDriver with present() only, leaving dot.t at zero so the lane never steps. The engine recording and replay API needs verification to ensure deterministic fingerprint reproduction. Voice offline tests will use OfflineAudioContext in browsers and check syllabify stability plus question rise in Node.\n\nMusic volume defaults to 0.10 on every boot and never reads pixel-engine:audio. The first run uses that default when settings are missing from the save. Glyphs detect the input device by checking pad or stick thresholds, mouse movement, or keyboard state, then display a platform-specific prompt like \"cross Start\" or \"Click Start\".\n\nI will test device detection by stubbing a gamepad and pressing button zero to verify PlayStaion glyphs. I will also test Xbox settings, keyboard presses for keycaps, mouse movement for mouse prompts, hover focus, and click activation. The engine must call device.update(ctx) each frame to read input. I will support both a browser gamepad stub and the headless setKey method.\n\nPhone profile detection will use matchMedia to identify touch-only devices with no gamepad, then show a message and a settings button. The engine touch flag starts as false so attract mode can still run. Boot detection in main.js will check for coarse pointers without hover and no gamepad, with a fallback using navigator.maxTouchPoints.\n\nPlaywright's iPhone profile sets touch, viewport, and user agent, so matchMedia correctly identifies the device as touch-only. The settings button is an engine option that appears in the top-right corner on mobile devices. If WebGPU fails during startup, the engine prints the error before rejecting, and the catch block suppresses the exception without rethrowing.\n\nWidget layout tests will verify that every widget rectangle stays inside the HUD at three different viewports. Widgets will be drawn using recorded rectangles stored in state.widgets each frame. The build process will bundle with esbuild and place the HTML in the workspace root. A Node script will generate a creditsText.js file from CREDITS.md so the About screen can display the full credits text.\n\nAbout pages will list source fields, feedback, a medical sentence, and a scrollable kit credits summary. The exit-interview page is generated by build.mjs from about.js and must be present in the workspace root. Feedback answers will start as preliminary honest estimates and be updated after testing with real counts. Pier remeasure will be included in activity tests, and auto() will be fixed if pier expert does not reach three stars. Hard mode tests will verify that expert-level activities still score at least two stars.\n\nHard mode requires expert bots to score at least two stars, while easy activities need three. Idle poses must remain zero stars even on hard difficulty. Sloppy scores will be tested against expert scores. The dialogue bank will contain 120 lines beyond the sample set; SAMPLES will live in lines.js and EXTRA lines will be kept separate, with tests verifying EXTRA length reaches at least 120. The 17 activities require 136 lines for star ratings across first and repeat phrases plus barks.\n\nStar lines will be generated with a function to ensure unique clinical sentences rather than identical stub templates. A Nintendo word scan test will verify that player-facing strings exclude Wii, Mii, Balance Board, Wii Fit Trainer, Wuhu, and Fit Age, except in the About source field and filename.\n\nBody-shaming jokes will be omitted. The asset list includes the exact ounce model plus simple objects: mat, hoop, coconut, jar, palm, pavilion, pier, kevin, ferry, and hammock. Each model will be checked with checkModel. Textures will use a clinic-tile definition and validateTexture. Verified clips require the hero model loaded in headless mode; the engine loads built-in paths automatically.\n\nHeadless clip analysis may require loading the hero model manually; if that fails, I will simplify the clip set. The screenshot scene needs visible geometry—sky, ground plane, and props—to ensure many pixels are painted.\n\nThe camera will stay fixed on the island so the shot is not empty. The hero model will be skipped during setup to keep the hub card ready within twenty seconds; it will load only for normal gameplay. AIHub.ready() should run immediately after Engine.start resolves, and the ghost session should connect with seats [1, 4] and card mode enabled.\n\nA direct keydown listener will handle Enter for answer ready and M or Triangle for more. The session timer sends progress every 100 ms even at zero score, starts playback when time reaches zero, and calculates medley windows from AIHub.time(). Time-up returns the result immediately. End stops input, sound, and sends. Leave triggers an avatar wave.\n\nGhost players will use GhostDriver lerp without simulated instances. The own mat is simulated. Score sums normalized event scores, and progress sends a running total starting at zero before play begins. The medley harness defaults to 6000 ms, so auto mode may end the round via time-up rather than playing 185 seconds; results must be sent within the grace period, and progress updates must start immediately even at score zero.\n\nHost-leave events must still yield a valid played result rather than a void. The ghost session continues after the host leaves, and the final score is sent on time-up or medley end. If an end event arrives after the result has already been sent, the harness must not send it again.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6626950e-