{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_54","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The Torus is a Vec3, likely representing radius, tube, and bounding dimensions.\n\nThe Torus handle will use dimensions like [0.8, 0.8, 0.12]. I'm now writing the core App structure and a defaultSettings object with audio, glyphs, and input settings.\n\nThe default settings now include pixelSize and fullscreen. Glyphs will switch to key or mouse prompts when those devices are last used, otherwise it stays pad-based. Widget IDs for the layout are title, tagline, rows, prompt, dial, and message. Title scale is 4 when width is at least 220, otherwise 2. Row scale is 2 when width is at least 200, otherwise 1. Row height derives from the 6px grid scaled by the current factor.\n\nMenu rows will be roughly 16 to 18 times the scale factor. A 12-pixel safe margin is set. Each line is capped at 52 characters across three lines, with a wrap helper. Story beats may use an optional typewriter effect. The island walk needs both a station carousel menu and real mouse or walk triggers, plus a PlatformerCharacter on the island.\n\nThe World will build a lightweight island of boxes by default. The hero character loads only when entering the island mode and is not present during headless week tests. Proximity triggers to stations will still appear for real interaction, but menus remain the primary path for tests.\n\nPlatformerCharacter will be lazy-created on the island. It may be instantiated even if the test never triggers a walk, but any errors during that creation or fixedUpdate will be caught to avoid breaking the scripted path.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8de5b990-718e-43c2-b19b-f7b6b5c011a8-46","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/types/engine/character/PlatformerCharacter.d.ts","limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8de5b990-718e-43c2-b19b-f7b6b5c011a8-47","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/core/dot.js","limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":587,"output_tokens":1000,"cache_read_input_tokens":112640,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"9161ae71-cd25-4dd6-ba87-5d205bc6bf81"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-8de5b990-718e-43c2-b19b-f7b6b5c011a8-46","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→import { type AnimationClip, type Object3D, Vector3 } from 'three/webgpu';\\nimport type { FootPlacementState } from '../animation/footPlacement';\\nimport type { RigSpec } from '../animation/types';\\nimport { type Physics, RAPIER } from '../physics/Physics';\\nimport { type AnimRequest } from './animator';\\nimport { type MoveState } from './states';\\n/**\\n * Mario-64-style third-person platformer character (and then some), built on Rapier's\\n * kinematic character controller. Physics positions are continuous; pixel alignment is\\n10→ * presentation-only. Expects the hero rig clips from src/game/hero/clips/.\\n *\\n * Moves: walk / tiptoe / run / skid-turn / bonk · crouch / crouch-walk / crouch-slide ·\\n * prone / crawl / get-up · lie down / sleep / get-up · sit · jump / jump-up / double /\\n * triple / backflip / side-flip / long jump / wall kick · dive → belly slide · ground\\n * pound · fall / land / hard landing · ledge hang / shimmy / pull-up / drop · climb\\n * (tagged 'climbable') and climb over the top · push / grab / pull (tagged 'pushable'\\n * or 'grabbable') · slope slide ('slippery' or steep) · teeter at edges · step up /\\n * step down · punch-punch-kick combo, sweep kick, jump kick · wave, victory.\\n *\\n20→ * Layout: this file is the core (body, collider, physics sweep, probes, ledge detection,\\n * stance, animation playback); every state's rules live in one table in states.ts, and\\n * every tuning number in tuning.ts.\\n */\\nexport type { MoveState } from './states';\\nexport type JumpKind = 'Jump' | 'JumpUp' | 'DoubleJump' | 'TripleJump' | 'Backflip' | 'SideFlip' | 'LongJump' | 'WallKick' | 'JumpKick';\\nexport interface MoveInput {\\n    /** Desired horizontal direction in world space, length 0..1. */\\n    move: Vector3;\\n    /** Walk / tiptoe modifier. */\\n30→    walk?: boolean;\\n    jump: boolean;\\n    jumpHeld: boolean;\\n    /** Crouch (held). */\\n    crouch: boolean;\\n    /** Crouch pressed this step (in the air: ground pound). */\\n    crouchPressed?: boolean;\\n    /** Toggle prone (pressed). */\\n    prone?: boolean;\\n    /** Toggle lying on the back (pressed). */\\n40→    lie?: boolean;\\n    /** Grab / pull (held). */\\n    grab?: boolean;\\n    attack?: boolean;\\n    wave?: boolean;\\n    sit?: boolean;\\n    /** First person: always face this direction and strafe. */\\n    face?: Vector3 | null;\\n}\\nexport interface PlatformerOptions {\\n50→    position: [number, number, number];\\n    /** Side-scroller: keep the character on its starting Z lane. */\\n    lockDepth?: boolean;\\n    runSpeed?: number;\\n}\\nexport type Stance = 'stand' | 'crouch' | 'prone';\\nexport interface Ledge {\\n    y: number;\\n    normal: Vector3;\\n    point: Vector3;\\n60→}\\nexport declare class PlatformerCharacter {\\n    readonly body: RAPIER.RigidBody;\\n    readonly collider: RAPIER.Collider;\\n    readonly kcc: RAPIER.KinematicCharacterController;\\n    state: MoveState;\\n    stateTime: number;\\n    jumpKind: JumpKind;\\n    /** Yaw in radians (0 = facing +Z). */\\n    facing: number;\\n70→    /** Horizontal velocity (world). */\\n    readonly hvel: Vector3;\\n    vy: number;\\n    grounded: boolean;\\n    stance: Stance;\\n    /** Last animation clip requested (for tests / debug UI). */\\n    anim: string;\\n    /** Counters for tests/tooling. */\\n    readonly stats: {\\n        jumps: number;\\n80→        landings: number;\",\"content_concise\":\"1→import { type AnimationClip, type Object3D, Vector3 } from 'three/webgpu';\\nimport type { FootPlacementState } from '../animation/footPlacement';\\nimport type { RigSpec } from '../animation/types';\\nimport { type Physics, RAPIER } from '../physics/Physics';\\nimport { type AnimRequest } from './animator';\\nimport { type MoveState } from './states';\\n/**\\n * Mario-64-style third-person platformer character (and then some), built on Rapier's\\n * kinematic character controller. Physics positions are continuous; pixel alignment is\\n10→ * presentation-only. Expects the hero rig clips from src/game/hero/clips/.\\n *\\n * Moves: walk / tiptoe / run / skid-turn / bonk · crouch / crouch-walk / crouch-slide ·\\n * prone / crawl / get-up · lie down / sleep / get-up · sit · jump / jump-up / double /\\n * triple / backflip / side-flip / long jump / wall kick · dive → belly slide · ground\\n * pound · fall / land / hard landing · ledge hang / shimmy / pull-up / drop · climb\\n * (tagged 'climbable') and climb over the top · push / grab / pull (tagged 'pushable'\\n * or 'grabbable') · slope slide ('slippery' or steep) · teeter at edges · step up /\\n * step down · punch-punch-kick combo, sweep kick, jump kick · wave, victory.\\n *\\n20→ * Layout: this file is the core (body, collider, physics sweep, probes, ledge detection,\\n * stance, animation playback); every state's rules live in one table in states.ts, and\\n * every tuning number in tuning.ts.\\n */\\nexport type { MoveState } from './states';\\nexport type JumpKind = 'Jump' | 'JumpUp' | 'DoubleJump' | 'TripleJump' | 'Backflip' | 'SideFlip' | 'LongJump' | 'WallKick' | 'JumpKick';\\nexport interface MoveInput {\\n    /** Desired horizontal direction in world space, length 0..1. */\\n    move: Vector3;\\n    /** Walk / tiptoe modifier. */\\n30→    walk?: boolean;\\n    jump: boolean;\\n    jumpHeld: boolean;\\n    /** Crouch (held). */\\n    crouch: boolean;\\n    /** Crouch pressed this step (in the air: ground pound). */\\n    crouchPressed?: boolean;\\n    /** Toggle prone (pressed). */\\n    prone?: boolean;\\n    /** Toggle lying on the back (pressed). */\\n40→    lie?: boolean;\\n    /** Grab / pull (held). */\\n    grab?: boolean;\\n    attack?: boolean;\\n    wave?: boolean;\\n    sit?: boolean;\\n    /** First person: always face this direction and strafe. */\\n    face?: Vector3 | null;\\n}\\nexport interface PlatformerOptions {\\n50→    position: [number, number, number];\\n    /** Side-scroller: keep the character on its starting Z lane. */\\n    lockDepth?: boolean;\\n    runSpeed?: number;\\n}\\nexport type Stance = 'stand' | 'crouch' | 'prone';\\nexport interface Ledge {\\n    y: number;\\n    normal: Vector3;\\n    point: Vector3;\\n60→}\\nexport declare class PlatformerCharacter {\\n    readonly body: RAPIER.RigidBody;\\n    readonly collider: RAPIER.Collider;\\n    readonly kcc: RAPIER.KinematicCharacterController;\\n    state: MoveState;\\n    stateTime: number;\\n    jumpKind: JumpKind;\\n    /** Yaw in radians (0 = facing +Z). */\\n    facing: number;\\n70→    /** Horizontal velocity (world). */\\n    readonly hvel: Vector3;\\n    vy: number;\\n    grounded: boolean;\\n    stance: Stance;\\n    /** Last animation clip requested (for tests / debug UI). */\\n    anim: string;\\n    /** Counters for tests/tooling. */\\n    readonly stats: {\\n        jumps: number;\\n80→        landings: number;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/types/engine/character/PlatformerCharacter.d.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"import { type AnimationClip, type Object3D, Vector3 } from 'three/webgpu';\\nimport type { FootPlacementState } from '../animation/footPlacement';\\nimport type { RigSpec } from '../animation/types';\\nimport { type Physics, RAPIER } from '../physics/Physics';\\nimport { type AnimRequest } from './animator';\\nimport { type MoveState } from './states';\\n/**\\n * Mario-64-style third-person platformer character (and then some), built on Rapier's\\n * kinematic character controller. Physics positions are continuous; pixel alignment is\\n * presentation-only. Expects the hero rig clips from src/game/hero/clips/.\\n *\\n * Moves: walk / tiptoe / run / skid-turn / bonk · crouch / crouch-walk / crouch-slide ·\\n * prone / crawl / get-up · lie down / sleep / get-up · sit · jump / jump-up / double /\\n * triple / backflip / side-flip / long jump / wall kick · dive → belly slide · ground\\n * pound · fall / land / hard landing · ledge hang / shimmy / pull-up / drop · climb\\n * (tagged 'climbable') and climb over the top · push / grab / pull (tagged 'pushable'\\n * or 'grabbable') · slope slide ('slippery' or steep) · teeter at edges · step up /\\n * step down · punch-punch-kick combo, sweep kick, jump kick · wave, victory.\\n *\\n * Layout: this file is the core (body, collider, physics sweep, probes, ledge detection,\\n * stance, animation playback); every state's rules live in one table in states.ts, and\\n * every tuning number in tuning.ts.\\n */\\nexport type { MoveState } from './states';\\nexport type JumpKind = 'Jump' | 'JumpUp' | 'DoubleJump' | 'TripleJump' | 'Backflip' | 'SideFlip' | 'LongJump' | 'WallKick' | 'JumpKick';\\nexport interface MoveInput {\\n    /** Desired horizontal direction in world space, length 0..1. */\\n    move: Vector3;\\n    /** Walk / tiptoe modifier. */\\n    walk?: boolean;\\n    jump: boolean;\\n    jumpHeld: boolean;\\n    /** Crouch (held). */\\n    crouch: boolean;\\n    /** Crouch pressed this step (in the air: ground pound). */\\n    crouchPressed?: boolean;\\n    /** Toggle prone (pressed). */\\n    prone?: boolean;\\n    /** Toggle lying on the back (pressed). */\\n    lie?: boolean;\\n    /** Grab / pull (held). */\\n    grab?: boolean;\\n    attack?: boolean;\\n    wave?: boolean;\\n    sit?: boolean;\\n    /** First person: always face this direction and strafe. */\\n    face?: Vector3 | null;\\n}\\nexport interface PlatformerOptions {\\n    position: [number, number, number];\\n    /** Side-scroller: keep the character on its starting Z lane. */\\n    lockDepth?: boolean;\\n    runSpeed?: number;\\n}\\nexport type Stance = 'stand' | 'crouch' | 'prone';\\nexport interface Ledge {\\n    y: number;\\n    normal: Vector3;\\n    point: Vector3;\\n}\\nexport declare class PlatformerCharacter {\\n    readonly body: RAPIER.RigidBody;\\n    readonly collider: RAPIER.Collider;\\n    readonly kcc: RAPIER.KinematicCharacterController;\\n    state: MoveState;\\n    stateTime: number;\\n    jumpKind: JumpKind;\\n    /** Yaw in radians (0 = facing +Z). */\\n    facing: number;\\n    /** Horizontal velocity (world). */\\n    readonly hvel: Vector3;\\n    vy: number;\\n    grounded: boolean;\\n    stance: Stance;\\n    /** Last animation clip requested (for tests / debug UI). */\\n    anim: string;\\n    /** Counters for tests/tooling. */\\n    readonly stats: {\\n        jumps: number;\\n        landings: number;\\n\",\"total_lines\":289}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-8de5b990-718e-43c2-b19b-f7b6b5c011a8-47","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→// Pure centre-of-balance. Step at 60 Hz. p stays in -1.2..1.2.\\nexport class Dot {\\n  x = 0;\\n  y = 0;\\n  vx = 0;\\n  vy = 0;\\n  ux = 0;\\n  uy = 0;\\n  t = 0;\\n10→  constructor(rand) {\\n    this.ph = [rand(), rand(), rand(), rand()].map((r) => r * 6.283185307179586);\\n  }\\n  step(dt, inX, inY, T, m = {}) {\\n    this.t += dt;\\n    const k = Math.min(1, dt / T.dotLag);\\n    this.ux += (inX - this.ux) * k;\\n    this.uy += (inY - this.uy) * k;\\n    const n = T.dotNoise * (m.noise ?? 1);\\n    const inst = T.dotInstability * (m.inst ?? 1);\\n20→    const auth = T.dotAuthority * (m.auth ?? 1);\\n    const nx = n * (Math.sin(1.7 * this.t + this.ph[0]) + 0.6 * Math.sin(3.1 * this.t + this.ph[1]));\\n    const ny = n * (Math.sin(1.3 * this.t + this.ph[2]) + 0.6 * Math.sin(2.7 * this.t + this.ph[3]));\\n    this.vx += (inst * this.x + auth * this.ux - T.dotDamping * this.vx + nx + (m.bx ?? 0)) * dt;\\n    this.vy += (inst * this.y + auth * this.uy - T.dotDamping * this.vy + ny + (m.by ?? 0)) * dt;\\n    this.x += this.vx * dt;\\n    this.y += this.vy * dt;\\n    const d = Math.hypot(this.x, this.y);\\n    if (d > 1.2) {\\n      const s = 1.2 / d;\\n30→      this.x *= s;\\n      this.y *= s;\\n      this.vx *= 0.3;\\n      this.vy *= 0.3;\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nexport const DOT_DEFAULTS = {\\n  dotInstability: 0.6,\\n40→  dotAuthority: 3.0,\",\"content_concise\":\"1→// Pure centre-of-balance. Step at 60 Hz. p stays in -1.2..1.2.\\nexport class Dot {\\n  x = 0;\\n  y = 0;\\n  vx = 0;\\n  vy = 0;\\n  ux = 0;\\n  uy = 0;\\n  t = 0;\\n10→  constructor(rand) {\\n    this.ph = [rand(), rand(), rand(), rand()].map((r) => r * 6.283185307179586);\\n  }\\n  step(dt, inX, inY, T, m = {}) {\\n    this.t += dt;\\n    const k = Math.min(1, dt / T.dotLag);\\n    this.ux += (inX - this.ux) * k;\\n    this.uy += (inY - this.uy) * k;\\n    const n = T.dotNoise * (m.noise ?? 1);\\n    const inst = T.dotInstability * (m.inst ?? 1);\\n20→    const auth = T.dotAuthority * (m.auth ?? 1);\\n    const nx = n * (Math.sin(1.7 * this.t + this.ph[0]) + 0.6 * Math.sin(3.1 * this.t + this.ph[1]));\\n    const ny = n * (Math.sin(1.3 * this.t + this.ph[2]) + 0.6 * Math.sin(2.7 * this.t + this.ph[3]));\\n    this.vx += (inst * this.x + auth * this.ux - T.dotDamping * this.vx + nx + (m.bx ?? 0)) * dt;\\n    this.vy += (inst * this.y + auth * this.uy - T.dotDamping * this.vy + ny + (m.by ?? 0)) * dt;\\n    this.x += this.vx * dt;\\n    this.y += this.vy * dt;\\n    const d = Math.hypot(this.x, this.y);\\n    if (d > 1.2) {\\n      const s = 1.2 / d;\\n30→      this.x *= s;\\n      this.y *= s;\\n      this.vx *= 0.3;\\n      this.vy *= 0.3;\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nexport const DOT_DEFAULTS = {\\n  dotInstability: 0.6,\\n40→  dotAuthority: 3.0,\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/core/dot.js\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"// Pure centre-of-balance. Step at 60 Hz. p stays in -1.2..1.2.\\nexport class Dot {\\n  x = 0;\\n  y = 0;\\n  vx = 0;\\n  vy = 0;\\n  ux = 0;\\n  uy = 0;\\n  t = 0;\\n  constructor(rand) {\\n    this.ph = [rand(), rand(), rand(), rand()].map((r) => r * 6.283185307179586);\\n  }\\n  step(dt, inX, inY, T, m = {}) {\\n    this.t += dt;\\n    const k = Math.min(1, dt / T.dotLag);\\n    this.ux += (inX - this.ux) * k;\\n    this.uy += (inY - this.uy) * k;\\n    const n = T.dotNoise * (m.noise ?? 1);\\n    const inst = T.dotInstability * (m.inst ?? 1);\\n    const auth = T.dotAuthority * (m.auth ?? 1);\\n    const nx = n * (Math.sin(1.7 * this.t + this.ph[0]) + 0.6 * Math.sin(3.1 * this.t + this.ph[1]));\\n    const ny = n * (Math.sin(1.3 * this.t + this.ph[2]) + 0.6 * Math.sin(2.7 * this.t + this.ph[3]));\\n    this.vx += (inst * this.x + auth * this.ux - T.dotDamping * this.vx + nx + (m.bx ?? 0)) * dt;\\n    this.vy += (inst * this.y + auth * this.uy - T.dotDamping * this.vy + ny + (m.by ?? 0)) * dt;\\n    this.x += this.vx * dt;\\n    this.y += this.vy * dt;\\n    const d = Math.hypot(this.x, this.y);\\n    if (d > 1.2) {\\n      const s = 1.2 / d;\\n      this.x *= s;\\n      this.y *= s;\\n      this.vx *= 0.3;\\n      this.vy *= 0.3;\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nexport const DOT_DEFAULTS = {\\n  dotInstability: 0.6,\\n  dotAuthority: 3.0,\\n\",\"total_lines\":44}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"8daef83f-06b5-42f1-888b-271ac4dac6ac"}
