{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_56","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Spawning the hero on the island.\n\nWriting files now. Pier auto expert tuck will be bumped after test math is verified. Attract mode will use a cloned tunables copy with doubled ring scale and god mode to avoid mutating player settings.\n\nAttract mode will step expert simulations for 14 seconds. Hub walk will show the island scene for 14 seconds with a playlist of activity families. Starting the medley lane class.\n\nGhost lanes will track position without creating a simulation. Bot lanes may need shortened play lengths to fit the 55-second medley window.\n\nmedley.js currently only defines 55-second windows. Activity simulations run longer than that, so scores will be normalized to a 0-1000 range using the activity's expected maximum. The runner will finish each simulation and record its score whenever the window phase changes or the event ends.\n\nClock logic will use fixedUpdate for local family hour and AIHub.time() for session. A three-lane family hour test will verify that pad and keyboard inputs move lane dots differently after one step, requiring the medley to be in play with active simulations. Tests must start from real initial states rather than jumping directly into the target scenario.\n\nThe family hour join screen will display four mats. Keyboard and mouse players claim seats by pressing Enter, while pads join when button zero is pressed. A start row appears once at least one player is present, and a toggle controls bot filling.\n\nThe browser test will navigate to Family Hour, join with keyboard and two stubbed pads, start the medley, set different axes, and step.\n\nThe browser test will verify that lane dot positions differ after input. PadDriver reads getGamepads, so the browser suite can stub it directly. Node tests will also stub navigator.getGamepads to drive the shipped PadDriver. The --fast flag targets node tests only.\n\nA node ghost test will verify that a ghost lane never steps its dot, keeping dot.t at zero. The app.js implementation may reach 1500–2000 lines, which is acceptable.\n\nA `go()` API will let dev tools and tests skip menus. Week tests must still use the real menu flow via `setKey`; only star tests may call `go('activity', id)` if it delegates to the same start function. The week test will step forward with a `stepUntil` helper. First-time practice adds eight seconds, so the initial tree activity includes that buffer.\n\nsetDriver('expert') will be called before the week so menus use keyboard while activities run with expert bots. Weigh expert stillness will use high T and low age, with idle showing high age; tests will verify a chart point exists and shown equals 7. Confession will reduce all shown ages by 7, recorded before and after. Week 2 returns to weigh or island when day is 8 and week is 2. The title menu will have one row: id 'start' with label \"Press any button. Gently.\"\n\nTitle screen accepts Enter, Space, PadCross, and click. Menu rows are Week, Drop-In Class, Family Hour, Settings, and About. The Week screen shows three slots labeled New guest or Name, day N, plus a back row. The name screen defaults to Guest and confirms on Enter; the letter grid will be paginated for real players.\n\nThe name entry grid will be paginated six letters per page plus Next and Done, with focus on Done so Enter confirms immediately. The ferry screen has one row to step off. Weigh shows a dial for fourteen seconds before the question screen appears. That screen uses three answer rows with ids a0, a1, and a2, and the question text serves as the title. Reveal displays the wobble age with an onward message. The island page lists st-pavilion, st-shed, st-beach, st-lagoon, st-jog, and st-plaza.\n\nIsland page one lists jar, locker, hall, hammock, and longstand if day seven or later. The station screen shows unlocked activities plus a back row. Results offers retry, next, and back. The report screen displays a sleep message. Settings will be paginated into two eight-row pages for music, sfx, voice, glyphs, gentle, radius, offset, flashes, look, pixel, fullscreen, reset, and back; sliders adjust left and right.\n\nAbout is paginated text with Next and Back rows. Pause is an overlay that freezes time. It offers Resume, Restart, Island, Settings, Howto, About, and Dev; in session it only shows Resume and Settings. Dev mode uses Q/E or L1/R1 tabs for up to eight sliders per page, plus a reset tab and Reset All.\n\nThe dev tools tab will page through many tools. The drop-in class screen lists all activities with no drips and records only. The family hour join screen shows a disabled start button until a player joins, plus a bots toggle and back row; joining is done by pressing Enter or pad cross, and the header displays the seat count. Once at least one human or bot is present, choosing start begins the medley. A node test can fill four bot lanes by toggling bots on and starting. After the medley, the podium screen offers rematch rows and a title.\n\nLocker look options are paged across skin, hair, top, bottom, headband, and items. Each option cycles left and right.\n\nHall shows one activity per page with next and back rows.\n\nJar displays a single screen with a drips number and a milestone list.\n\nConfession appears after the day 7 report if Long Stand was completed. It shows an ounce line and subtracts seven from every shown age on confirm. The ending follows immediately with a Week 2 row.\n\nDay seven hammock ends the day even without Long Stand, but confession only triggers if Long Stand was completed. After report confirm, the day increments; once it exceeds seven, the week advances to two and the session returns to weigh-in. Activities unlock via `isUnlocked(def, day, hard)`, where hard versions require day six or later.\n\nThe tree activity unlocks on day one, the header on day two, longstand on day seven, and hard versions on day six. Jar milestones unlock through real play; tree and squat each yield about twelve drips plus a prescription dose, so the test will assert that band unlocks after a few days of normal activity.\n\nSave and reload will be tested by writing a save, creating a fresh App with the same storage, reading back, and asserting the day matches. Corrupt JSON will fall back to defaults, and missing storage will use memory-only saves. Pause is triggered by KeyP or Escape during activities; Escape also returns from menus. To verify exact resume, snapshots of dot position and elapsed time will be compared before and after pausing.\n\nDev sliders will be tested by changing a value, stepping the activity, and asserting the simulation reads the new tunable. A parallel diverging simulation is too heavy. The simpler check verifies that app.tunables.x changed and sim.T.x points to the same object, with reset restoring the default.\n\nA deterministic still-simulation test will verify that the dot position stays identical after a reset, and that raising noise to maximum causes divergence. This proves the dev slider changes live behavior.\n\nThe title screen will enter an attract mode after ten seconds of idle time. Menus also trigger attract after ten seconds of inactivity. Activities do not enter attract mode. Any input exits attract immediately. Touch support is included for browser phone profiles. Widgets must fit the layout.\n\nHashes will be compared with SHA256. Songs must parse correctly and their volume sums must be valid. Lines need at least 120 extra characters, a glyph check, and a length of no more than 52 characters across three lines. Models must have no validation problems. Textures and clips require validation and analysis. Nintendo words must not appear in scan lines, activity names, or questions. Actions.js will be listed as a table even if the app uses it. DeviceTracker will track input kind and update state. Glyph art will use simple sprite rows for cross, circle, square, triangle, keys, and mouse.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2a60bec9-360b-47be-abf3-ff84fc12bad6-49","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"set\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/types/engine/settings.d.ts","head_limit":20}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2a60bec9-360b-47be-abf3-ff84fc12bad6-50","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"ENGINE_VERSION|Engine.version","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/types/engine/version.d.ts"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":650,"output_tokens":3650,"cache_read_input_tokens":115584,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"8e938a5a-789f-4d14-86b1-f759e14dbfe0"}
