{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_63","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I have a clear picture of the requirements. I will now write all the necessary files.\n\nI'll generate the lines programmatically to keep the file compact. I'm preparing 136 unique activity comments with first and repeat variants. I'll also create a compact hand-written data table of four comments per activity, plus banned words for testing.\n\nI'll allow \"Wii Fit\" only in the about source field. The scanner skips about and aiHub source fields. I'm drafting honest feedback now. I expect bot star sweeps to be most helpful. I expect capture flags and timeScale key drops to be least helpful. I liked headless mode, HUD, and timeScale. I got stuck on model thickness and song volume.\n\nBuilt the Dot, voice, week, and medley ghost modules. The hardest parts were the WebGPU screenshot path and pause input at timeScale 0. I left the engine unchanged except to document or export the music bus default.\n\nThe prompt feedback was positive about completeness and the kit. It was confusing about filename spaces, cut lists versus doing everything, and timeScale versus paused states. The hardest task was the full week with hub harness and every activity bot stars. One change requested is a passing harness game example.\n\nI will track real bug counts during testing and update the final numbers.\n\nI am starting a bug counter. I will verify header idle shows zero stars across seeds. Star tests will use simulate options first:false and practice:false to match the sweep. Practice mode does not affect scoring. I will test both simulate() and world go('activity') paths.\n\nI will test the world activity path by calling go() to start each activity, set an expert driver, and step until results. Running this for all 17 activities at both skill levels would simulate roughly 40,000 frames. I may disable practice mode for bot tests to keep the run time reasonable.\n\nI will split the star tests into two parts. One test will boot the world, navigate to each activity via the tree or go(), set an expert driver, and step through to results. Another loop will use simulate() for all activities to match the scene path. I will also add a separate test that verifies the practice phase exists on first play.\n\nThe full engine-driven star sweep would take roughly 80 seconds. I will use simulate() for the complete matrix and boot the World once to verify the scene path.\n\nI will step the simulation directly from the test instead of routing through the scene, since skipping the scene is not allowed. I will first measure one activity to gauge engine overhead. A headless scene with only a floor should keep things fast.\n\nI will keep the fixed update light, running only simulation steps and needle rotation. Star tests will enter activities directly from the title screen without spawning a hero on the island. I will run pier measurements in parallel and test model thickness after writing. I will also include clip analysis in the tests and fix any failures.\n\nI am writing the verified motion clips from the plan verbatim. I will add simple holds so every clip passes analyzeClip validation.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a6bda035-0865-494b-9fe3-eda72a81c02c-58","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"HERO_MODEL","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/types/engine/index.d.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a6bda035-0865-494b-9fe3-eda72a81c02c-59","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/types/game/hero/index.d.ts","limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":946,"output_tokens":1610,"cache_read_input_tokens":129024,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"pa