uilds its world and reacts to input.\\n */\\nexport interface Game {\\n    readonly name: string;\\n    /**\\n     * The plain JSON the game was made with, when its name alone can't rebuild it (a lab's depth\\n     * and seed, the door a room was entered by): kept in its recordings (`Recording.args`), so a\\n     * tool can make the same game again to replay one (`npm run replay`, src/games.ts).\\n     */\\n    readonly args?: unknown;\\n    /**\\n     * Models `setup` will load (`ctx.loadModel` URLs). Optional: listing them lets the\\n     * engine start downloading while the renderer and physics initialise.\\n     */\\n    readonly assets?: readonly string[];\\n    /** Build the level: load models, add colliders, spawn entities. */\\n    setup(ctx: GameContext): Promise<void> | void;\\n    /** Runs before every fixed 60 Hz physics step. Move characters/apply forces here. */\\n    fixedUpdate?(ctx: GameContext, dt: number): void;\\n    /**\\n     * Runs when the engine starts running this game: after `Engine.start` (just before\\n     * `__PIXEL_READY__` resolves) and after each `loadGame`. Install page handles for tools here\\n     * (`window.__MYGAME__`), so they never exist before the engine can step. An exception is\\n     * reported like any hook's (`engine.errors`, on screen); the game runs on.\\n     */\\n    ready?(ctx: GameContext): void;\\n    /** Runs once per rendered frame after physics (animation, pickups, UI state). */\\n    update?(ctx: GameContext, dt: number): void;\\n    /** World position the camera follows. */\\n    cameraTarget(ctx: GameContext): Vector3;\\n    /** First-person eye position (defaults to cameraTarget + 0.7 up). */\\n    eyePosition?(ctx: GameContext): Vector3;\\n    /** One-line status for the debug UI (score, lives...). */\\n    status?(ctx: GameContext): string;\\n    /**\\n     * The game's own state as a short string or hash, for `engine.fingerprint()`: what lives\\n     * outside physics and `ctx.random` (positions, life, counters, the game's own random\\n     * streams), so two runs that should match (a replay) can be compared. Only what a replay must\\n     * reproduce: no timings or measurements.\\n     */\\n    fingerprint?(ctx: GameContext): string;\\n    /**\\n     * The game's own state as plain data, between frames (`engine.snapshot()`): everything a\\n     * later frame reads that the engine does not keep (its entities, timers, random streams; the\\n     * handles of its physics bodies). With `restore`, the game has save-states.\\n     */\\n    snapshot?(ctx: GameContext): unknown;\\n    /**\\n     * Put the game back to what `snapshot` returned (`engine.restore()`): the same game, already\\n     * set up. Find physics bodies again by handle (`ctx.physics.world.getRigidBody(h)`).\\n     */\\n    restore?(ctx: GameContext, state: unknown): void | Promise<void>;\\n    /**\\n     * Optional: leave whatever mode the game is in before a restore changes anything (a mode\\n     * with a camera of its own, a dialog, a level): `engine.restore()` calls it first, then checks\\n     * the snapshot fits (the camera preset) and puts the engine's part back, then `restore`.\\n     */\\n    beforeRestore?(ctx: GameContext): void | Promise<void>;\\n    /**\\n     * Called after `engine.setCamera()` swapped the camera preset mid-game. The world,\\n     * physics and player are untouched; adjust anything that depends on the preset\\n\",\"total_lines\":613}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"dc51daa5-997a-4524-baa2-2dc2ad9b6ac2"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_66","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The game requires `name` and `cameraTarget`.\n\nWorld will implement `name` and `cameraTarget`, delegating status and fingerprint to the app. The engine fingerprint may combine game state, so tests can compare `app.fingerprint()`. A replay test would record activity and replay it with a fresh World, but this is tricky because the simulation depends on app state that starts fresh.\n\nReplay will restore the seed and load the level. The test will record an activity, save its fingerprints, replay it into a fresh world, and compare the results.\n\nA `make()` helper will construct the App and World together. The headless engine uses this factory to drive activity, record the session, and replay it into a fresh world via the same factory.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c8bf51c6-e44b-4ebf-b42f-6ffb11bcfdbd-63","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/types/engine/random.d.ts","limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2465,"output_tokens":593,"cache_read_input_tokens":132736,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"5d823457-a94c-47d4-8fed-5171094e3212"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-c8bf51c6-e44b-4ebf-b42f-6ffb11bcfdbd-63","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * Seeded randomness. Everything random in a game comes from an `Rng`, so the same seed always\\n * gives the same result (docs/DOCTRINE.md, principle 1). Each level gets one, `ctx.random`,\\n * seeded from the engine's seed and the game's name; fork it by purpose so streams stay\\n * independent of how many numbers each one drew:\\n *\\n *   const level = ctx.random.fork(`level:${n}`);\\n *   const room = level.fork(`room:${i}`);   // independent of how many numbers `level` drew\\n *\\n10→ * Never use Math.random in game or engine code (the lint refuses it).\\n */\\nexport declare class Rng {\\n    private s;\\n    constructor(seed: number | string);\\n    /** The generator's whole state: save it, and set it back to draw the same numbers again. */\\n    get state(): number;\\n    set state(s: number);\\n    /** Uniform in [0, 1). mulberry32. */\\n    next(): number;\\n20→    /** A child generator for one purpose; does not advance this one. */\\n    fork(purpose: string | number): Rng;\\n    /** Float in [min, max). */\\n    range(min: number, max: number): number;\\n    /** Integer in [min, max] (inclusive). */\\n    int(min: number, max: number): number;\\n    chance(p: number): boolean;\\n    pick<T>(items: readonly T[]): T;\\n    /** Pick by weight; entries with weight <= 0 never come up. */\\n    weighted<T>(items: readonly T[], weight: (item: T) => number): T;\\n30→    shuffle<T>(items: T[]): T[];\\n    /** Normal distribution (Box–Muller). */\\n    gaussian(mean?: number, sd?: number): number;\\n}\\n/** FNV-1a, 32-bit. */\\nexport declare function hashString(s: string): number;\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * Seeded randomness. Everything random in a game comes from an `Rng`, so the same seed always\\n * gives the same result (docs/DOCTRINE.md, principle 1). Each level gets one, `ctx.random`,\\n * seeded from the engine's seed and the game's name; fork it by purpose so streams stay\\n * independent of how many numbers each one drew:\\n *\\n *   const level = ctx.random.fork(`level:${n}`);\\n *   const room = level.fork(`room:${i}`);   // independent of how many numbers `level` drew\\n *\\n10→ * Never use Math.random in game or engine code (the lint refuses it).\\n */\\nexport declare class Rng {\\n    private s;\\n    constructor(seed: number | string);\\n    /** The generator's whole state: save it, and set it back to draw the same numbers again. */\\n    get state(): number;\\n    set state(s: number);\\n    /** Uniform in [0, 1). mulberry32. */\\n    next(): number;\\n20→    /** A child generator for one purpose; does not advance this one. */\\n    fork(purpose: string | number): Rng;\\n    /** Float in [min, max). */\\n    range(min: number, max: number): number;\\n    /** Integer in [min, max] (inclusive). */\\n    int(min: number, max: number): number;\\n    chance(p: number): boolean;\\n    pick<T>(items: readonly T[]): T;\\n    /** Pick by weight; entries with weight <= 0 never come up. */\\n    weighted<T>(items: readonly T[], weight: (item: T) => number): T;\\n30→    shuffle<T>(items: T[]): T[];\\n    /** Normal distribution (Box–Muller). */\\n    gaussian(mean?: number, sd?: number): number;\\n}\\n/** FNV-1a, 32-bit. */\\nexport declare function hashString(s: string): number;\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/types/engine/random.d.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * Seeded randomness. Everything random in a game comes from an `Rng`, so the same seed always\\n * gives the same result (docs/DOCTRINE.md, principle 1). Each level gets one, `ctx.random`,\\n * seeded from the engine's seed and the game's name; fork it by purpose so streams stay\\n * independent of how many numbers each one drew:\\n *\\n *   const level = ctx.random.fork(`level:${n}`);\\n *   const room = level.fork(`room:${i}`);   // independent of how many numbers `level` drew\\n *\\n * Never use Math.random in game or engine code (the lint refuses it).\\n */\\nexport declare class Rng {\\n    private s;\\n    constructor(seed: number | string);\\n    /** The generator's whole state: save it, and set it back to draw the same numbers again. */\\n    get state(): number;\\n    set state(s: number);\\n    /** Uniform in [0, 1). mulberry32. */\\n    next(): number;\\n    /** A child generator for one purpose; does not advance this one. */\\n    fork(purpose: string | number): Rng;\\n    /** Float in [min, max). */\\n    range(min: number, max: number): number;\\n    /** Integer in [min, max] (inclusive). */\\n    int(min: number, max: number): number;\\n    chance(p: number): boolean;\\n    pick<T>(items: readonly T[]): T;\\n    /** Pick by weight; entries with weight <= 0 never come up. */\\n    weighted<T>(items: readonly T[], weight: (item: T) => number): T;\\n    shuffle<T>(items: T[]): T[];\\n    /** Normal distribution (Box–Muller). */\\n    gaussian(mean?: number, sd?: number): number;\\n}\\n/** FNV-1a, 32-bit. */\\nexport declare function hashString(s: string): number;\\n\",\"total_lines\":35}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"5c2f17e3-91e2-4804-929e-03fb0dead171"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_67","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Bot rand and dot rand should be ctx.\n\nThe random fork will be created once per activity inside startActivity. This keeps replay stable. It will not be recreated on every frame. LocalDriver imports the full pixel-engine. That is acceptable.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2d06577c-07e2-466e-b1b0-7e897d3bfacf-64","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/types/engine/camera.d.ts","limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1061,"output_tokens":381,"cache_read_input_tokens":135168,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"eebf45d6-eed6-41ec-a0d5-b81c1e757ccb"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-2d06577c-07e2-466e-b1b0-7e897d3bfacf-64","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→import { type Camera, OrthographicCamera, PerspectiveCamera, Vector3 } from 'three/webgpu';\\nimport { type Resolution } from './framing';\\nimport type { Input } from './input';\\n/**\\n * Camera presets. A game picks ONE at startup (EngineOptions.camera / `?camera=`). For\\n * reviewing, `engine.setCamera()` swaps presets live without touching the world. `free`\\n * is an authoring tool: fly around, press Enter to fix the view, and paste the printed\\n * `fixed` config into your game.\\n */\\n10→export type CameraPreset = 'iso' | 'topdown' | 'side' | 'third' | 'first' | 'free' | 'fixed';\\nexport declare const CAMERA_PRESETS: readonly CameraPreset[];\\nexport interface CameraConfig {\\n    preset?: CameraPreset;\\n    /** Zoom factor, 1 = preset default, >1 = closer. Ignored by `first`. */\\n    zoom?: number;\\n    minZoom?: number;\\n    maxZoom?: number;\\n    /** Ortho presets: visible world height at zoom 1. */\\n    viewHeight?: number;\\n20→    /** iso: degrees below horizon / around Y. */\\n    pitch?: number;\\n    yaw?: number;\\n    /** Perspective presets: vertical field of view in degrees. */\\n    fov?: number;\\n    /** third: orbit distance at zoom 1. */\\n    distance?: number;\\n    /** fixed: camera position and look-at target. */\\n    position?: [number, number, number];\\n    target?: [number, number, number];\\n30→    /** fixed/free: projection. */\\n    projection?: 'perspective' | 'ortho';\\n    /** Follow smoothing; higher is snappier. */\\n    stiffness?: number;\\n}\\n/** What rigs may ask of the world (e.g. third-person wall avoidance). */\\nexport interface CameraWorld {\\n    /** Distance from `from` along `dir` to the first obstacle, or null. */\\n    raycast?(from: Vector3, dir: Vector3, maxDistance: number): number | null;\\n}\\n40→export interface CameraUpdate {\",\"content_concise\":\"1→import { type Camera, OrthographicCamera, PerspectiveCamera, Vector3 } from 'three/webgpu';\\nimport { type Resolution } from './framing';\\nimport type { Input } from './input';\\n/**\\n * Camera presets. A game picks ONE at startup (EngineOptions.camera / `?camera=`). For\\n * reviewing, `engine.setCamera()` swaps presets live without touching the world. `free`\\n * is an authoring tool: fly around, press Enter to fix the view, and paste the printed\\n * `fixed` config into your game.\\n */\\n10→export type CameraPreset = 'iso' | 'topdown' | 'side' | 'third' | 'first' | 'free' | 'fixed';\\nexport declare const CAMERA_PRESETS: readonly CameraPreset[];\\nexport interface CameraConfig {\\n    preset?: CameraPreset;\\n    /** Zoom factor, 1 = preset default, >1 = closer. Ignored by `first`. */\\n    zoom?: number;\\n    minZoom?: number;\\n    maxZoom?: number;\\n    /** Ortho presets: visible world height at zoom 1. */\\n    viewHeight?: number;\\n20→    /** iso: degrees below horizon / around Y. */\\n    pitch?: number;\\n    yaw?: number;\\n    /** Perspective presets: vertical field of view in degrees. */\\n    fov?: number;\\n    /** third: orbit distance at zoom 1. */\\n    distance?: number;\\n    /** fixed: camera position and look-at target. */\\n    position?: [number, number, number];\\n    target?: [number, number, number];\\n30→    /** fixed/free: projection. */\\n    projection?: 'perspective' | 'ortho';\\n    /** Follow smoothing; higher is snappier. */\\n    stiffness?: number;\\n}\\n/** What rigs may ask of the world (e.g. third-person wall avoidance). */\\nexport interface CameraWorld {\\n    /** Distance from `from` along `dir` to the first obstacle, or null. */\\n    raycast?(from: Vector3, dir: Vector3, maxDistance: number): number | null;\\n}\\n40→export interface CameraUpdate {\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/types/engine/camera.d.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"import { type Camera, OrthographicCamera, PerspectiveCamera, Vector3 } from 'three/webgpu';\\nimport { type Resolution } from './framing';\\nimport type { Input } from './input';\\n/**\\n * Camera presets. A game picks ONE at startup (EngineOptions.camera / `?camera=`). For\\n * reviewing, `engine.setCamera()` swaps presets live without touching the world. `free`\\n * is an authoring tool: fly around, press Enter to fix the view, and paste the printed\\n * `fixed` config into your game.\\n */\\nexport type CameraPreset = 'iso' | 'topdown' | 'side' | 'third' | 'first' | 'free' | 'fixed';\\nexport declare const CAMERA_PRESETS: readonly CameraPreset[];\\nexport interface CameraConfig {\\n    preset?: CameraPreset;\\n    /** Zoom factor, 1 = preset default, >1 = closer. Ignored by `first`. */\\n    zoom?: number;\\n    minZoom?: number;\\n    maxZoom?: number;\\n    /** Ortho presets: visible world height at zoom 1. */\\n    viewHeight?: number;\\n    /** iso: degrees below horizon / around Y. */\\n    pitch?: number;\\n    yaw?: number;\\n    /** Perspective presets: vertical field of view in degrees. */\\n    fov?: number;\\n    /** third: orbit distance at zoom 1. */\\n    distance?: number;\\n    /** fixed: camera position and look-at target. */\\n    position?: [number, number, number];\\n    target?: [number, number, number];\\n    /** fixed/free: projection. */\\n    projection?: 'perspective' | 'ortho';\\n    /** Follow smoothing; higher is snappier. */\\n    stiffness?: number;\\n}\\n/** What rigs may ask of the world (e.g. third-person wall avoidance). */\\nexport interface CameraWorld {\\n    /** Distance from `from` along `dir` to the first obstacle, or null. */\\n    raycast?(from: Vector3, dir: Vector3, maxDistance: number): number | null;\\n}\\nexport interface CameraUpdate {\\n\",\"total_lines\":222}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"3b2a7de5-1e1a-4021-bfcc-af8c020c1781"}
