{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_75","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Confirmed that wasPressed works at timeScale 0, while fixedUpdate does not run.\n\nAt timeScale 1, fixedUpdate runs normally. The pause menu will work.\n\nPier expert still needs 38 meters. Current best is 32.88. Speed and ring fraction are too low. Full zone speed with high ring fraction yields roughly 42 meters.\n\nThe bot spends most of the run outside the target zone. It takes about 1.5 seconds to reach y=-0.6, so zoneT accumulates during travel rather than while holding position. The dot's instability and authority also fight the PD input, keeping it from staying centered.\n\nIf the bot enters the target zone at t=1.2 and stays there, speed would reach roughly 12.08. That gives about 36.2 meters. To hit the 38-meter goal, the ring fraction must exceed 0.925.\n\nA ring fraction of 1.125 is impossible. Even with perfect ring coverage, speed 12 only yields about 36 meters. The bot must be in the target zone for roughly 4.18 seconds to reach the goal, meaning it needs to enter by about t=0.82. Currently it only spends 3.57 seconds there, so it is either entering too late or leaving early. I will add a log to pinpoint exactly when the dot first crosses into the zone.\n\nA more aggressive auto-input clamp could keep the dot inside the target zone by pushing it back whenever it overshoots or oscillates. The flight ring fraction is also very low because the dot is highly unstable.\n\nThe expert flight correction is being strengthened to fully counter the dot's instability and velocity each frame. The instability force at the ring is roughly 0.81, while the bot authority can apply -3, so the correction should be sufficient.\n\nWith stronger correction, ring fraction could rise to 0.95 or higher. If zone time increases from 3.57 to about 4.5 seconds, speed reaches roughly 13.2 and distance becomes 38.7 meters. That is just enough to hit the goal. The timer starts at zero when scoring begins, so the intro does not count.\n\nEntering the target zone at 0.4 seconds and holding there for the full run would yield roughly 13.4 speed, so ring fraction must exceed 0.93 to reach the goal.\n\nThe idle skill will remain unchanged because it already returns zero input.\n\nA similar improvement will be applied to the good skill so it can earn 2 or 3 stars, while sloppy keeps using the stock bot.\n\nThe expert and good bots now use tighter run-phase controls. They push hard to keep the dot inside a narrower vertical band around y=-0.62, and clamp horizontal input toward zero. During flight, the correction is stronger: it counteracts both position and velocity with gains of 7 and 1.5.\n\nThe flight correction now also counteracts velocity with a gain of 1.5. The expert and good bots will press the confirm button during the last second of the run. Average and sloppy bots will use a milder dive so they still jump but score lower. The zone timer only counts frames where the dot is inside the target band after the step, which means the dot must first accelerate out of its starting position before it can begin accumulating zone time.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Pause input works while the simulation is frozen. Pier Jump’s expert bot still lands short of three stars, so I’m tightening the tuck and the flight hold."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4edaf749-3f20-40f4-8b3b-c8626bbdd0cd-73","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/core/sims.js","old_string":"  auto(dt) {\n    if (this.skill === 'idle') return { ...ZERO };\n    const u = this.bot.read(this.dot, dt);\n    if (this.phaseLocal === 'run' && this.dot.y > -0.58) u.y = -1;\n    if (this.phaseLocal === 'flight' && (this.skill === 'expert' || this.skill === 'good')) {\n      u.x = clamp(u.x - this.dot.x * 2.2, -1, 1);\n      u.y = clamp(u.y - this.dot.y * 2.2, -1, 1);\n    }\n    const lip = this.phaseLocal === 'run' && this.localT >= 5 - dt - 1e-4 && this.localT < 5;\n    const cannon = this.phaseLocal === 'flight' && this.localT >= 3.5 - 0.25 && this.localT < 3.5 - 0.25 + dt;\n    const tight = this.skill === 'expert' || this.skill === 'good';\n    const press = tight && (lip || cannon);\n    return { ...ZERO, x: u.x, y: u.y, confirm: press };\n  }","new_string":"  auto(dt) {\n    if (this.skill === 'idle') return { ...ZERO };\n    const u = this.bot.read(this.dot, dt);\n    const tight = this.skill === 'expert' || this.skill === 'good';\n    if (this.phaseLocal === 'run' && tight) {\n      const y = this.dot.y;\n      if (y > -0.48) u.y = -1;\n      else if (y < -0.74) u.y = 1;\n      else u.y = clamp((-0.62 - y) * 8 - this.dot.vy * 2, -1, 1);\n      u.x = clamp(-this.dot.x * 6 - this.dot.vx, -1, 1);\n    } else if (this.phaseLocal === 'run' && this.dot.y > -0.45) {\n      u.y = Math.min(u.y, -0.85);\n    }\n    if (this.phaseLocal === 'flight' && tight) {\n      u.x = clamp(-this.dot.x * 8 - this.dot.vx * 2, -1, 1);\n      u.y = clamp(-this.dot.y * 8 - this.dot.vy * 2, -1, 1);\n    }\n    const lip = this.phaseLocal === 'run' && this.localT >= 5 - dt - 1e-4 && this.localT < 5;\n    const press = tight && lip;\n    return { ...ZERO, x: u.x, y: u.y, confirm: press };\n  }"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1052,"output_tokens":3092,"cache_read_input_tokens":149760,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"43ed9955-9bea-4eab-976e-d856b5d84e80"}
