xit-interview.json` in the exact TASK.md shape (every value filled, `\\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"`, `aiHub` block included), and one self-contained HTML file whose stem is `{Title}-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607` (`{Title}` is a playful riff on “Wii Fit”, not a Nintendo name, chosen with a real RNG and stored in one constant). A dev folder with that same stem holds the project. The page opens from `file://` with no runtime network fetches, boots on WebGPU with zero page errors, shows that title, and sets the music bus to exactly 0.10 on first run. Shipped `pixel-engine.js` is byte-identical to the downloaded kit. The in-game About/Credits screen shows every TASK.md Source Information field, Testing / Engine / Prompt Feedback, the kit credits, and the sentence “This is not medical advice. Ounce is a scale.” `exit-interview.json` is generated from that same text and re-parses as JSON.\"},{\"line_number\":13,\"content\":\"## Verification plan\"},{\"line_number\":30,\"content\":\"- Workspace root (this folder): the HTML deliverable, `exit-interview.json`, `PROGRESS.md`.\"},{\"line_number\":39,\"content\":\"## Task checklist\"},{\"line_number\":47,\"content\":\"- [ ] Write About/Credits from one data source, emit `exit-interview.json`, update `PROGRESS.md`, and capture `node tools/test.mjs`, two `file://` launches, and the hub log under `{SCRATCH}`.\"},{\"line_number\":55,\"content\":\"- Player-facing text must avoid Nintendo names, but Source Information and the filename must say Wii Fit. Those two places are the exception.\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"58d3e021-5f0a-42ba-816c-dc3cb8a44682"}
