{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-3be73789-54de-49df-8b8a-5e028bd39c47-24","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,49,54,48,55,95,95,120,54,57,56,49,101,51,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,78,111,32,109,97,116,99,104,101,115,32,102,111,117,110,100,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":1,\"match_count\":0,\"file_matches\":[]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-3be73789-54de-49df-8b8a-5e028bd39c47-25","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,49,54,48,55,95,95,120,54,57,56,49,101,51,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,78,111,32,109,97,116,99,104,101,115,32,102,111,117,110,100,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":1,\"match_count\":0,\"file_matches\":[]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-3be73789-54de-49df-8b8a-5e028bd39c47-26","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"434→## 9. UI and UX: 10 feet, controller first\\n\\n**One UI for every device: the pixel HUD.** No DOM menus; same screens for pad, keyboard and mouse. Build a small kit in `src/ui/`.\\n\\n### Layout rules\\n\\n440→- **Use `aspect: 'fill'` ✔.** It removes letterboxing at every window size (`adaptive` gives thick black borders at 1280×720). Art size then varies: 480×270 at 1080p and 4K, 427×240 at 720p, 640×360 in a small frame, 400×300 at 800×600. **Lay out from `hud.width` and `hud.height` with anchors**, never fixed coordinates. Keep a 12 art px safe margin.\\n- **Pointer to art pixels ✔:** `ax = (p.x + 1) / 2 * hud.width; ay = (1 - p.y) / 2 * hud.height`. The HUD canvas ignores pointer events, and its rect equals the game canvas's.\\n- **Text:** the 5×7 font at scale 1 is 20×28 px at 1080p, the minimum. Scale 2 for menu rows and headings, 3-4 for the title and big numbers.\\n- **No dense screens:** at most 8 menu rows; at most 3 lines of dialogue; one idea per screen; one activity per records page. Page rather than scroll, wherever you can.\\n\\n### Mixed-case text ✔\\n\\nThe engine font is capitals only, which is wrong for this voice. Draw lowercase through `hud.sprite`, everything else through `hud.text`, on a 6 px grid. This table and function rendered correctly; use them:\\n\\n```js\\n450→// src/ui/font.js. Rows top to bottom, 5 bits, bit 4 = left. Rows 7-8 are descenders.\\nconst H = {\\na:'00 00 0e 01 0f 11 0f 00 00', b:'10 10 1e 11 11 11 1e 00 00', c:'00 00 0e 11 10 11 0e 00 00', d:'01 01 0f 11 11 11 0f 00 00',\\ne:'00 00 0e 11 1f 10 0e 00 00', f:'06 09 08 1c 08 08 08 00 00', g:'00 00 0f 11 11 11 0f 01 0e', h:'10 10 1e 11 11 11 11 00 00',\\ni:'04 00 0c 04 04 04 0e 00 00', j:'02 00 06 02 02 02 02 12 0c', k:'10 10 12 14 18 14 12 00 00', l:'0c 04 04 04 04 04 0e 00 00',\\nm:'00 00 1a 15 15 15 15 00 00', n:'00 00 1e 11 11 11 11 00 00', o:'00 00 0e 11 11 11 0e 00 00', p:'00 00 1e 11 11 11 1e 10 10',\\nq:'00 00 0f 11 11 11 0f 01 01', r:'00 00 16 19 10 10 10 00 00', s:'00 00 0f 10 0e 01 1e 00 00', t:'08 08 1c 08 08 09 06 00 00',\\nu:'00 00 11 11 11 13 0d 00 00', v:'00 00 11 11 11 0a 04 00 00', w:'00 00 11 11 15 15 0a 00 00', x:'00 00 11 0a 04 0a 11 00 00',\\ny:'00 00 11 11 11 11 0f 01 0e', z:'00 00 1f 02 04 08 1f 00 00' };\\nexport const GLYPHS = Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(H).map(([k, v]) => [k, v.split(' ').map((h) => parseInt(h, 16).toString(2).padStart(5, '0').replace(/0/g, '.').replace(/1/g, 'o'))]));\\n460→export function say(hud, x, y, text, { color = 'white', shadow = 'ink', scale = 1 } = {}) {\\n  for (const ch of text) {\\n    const g = GLYPHS[ch];\\n    if (g) hud.sprite(x, y, g, { o: color }, { scale, shadow });\\n    else if (ch !== ' ') hud.text(x, y, ch, { color, shadow, scale });\\n    x += 6 * scale;\\n  }\\n  return x;\\n}\\n```\\n470→\\nAdd a measuring and word-wrapping helper. Replace any character the font lacks with `?` (hub names can hold anything); a test checks all game text has glyphs.\\n\\n### Input map\\n\\nRemap once at boot ✔: `ctx.input.gamepadButtons = { 0:'PadCross', 1:'PadCircle', 2:'PadSquare', 3:'PadTriangle', 4:'PadL1', 5:'PadR1', 6:'PadL2', 7:'PadR2', 8:'PadCreate', 9:'PadOptions', 10:'PadL3', 11:'PadR3', 12:'PadUp', 13:'PadDown', 14:'PadLeft', 15:'PadRight' }`. Pad buttons then appear in `isDown`, `wasPressed`, `state().held` and recordings. Keep one action table in `src/core/actions.js`.\\n\\n| Action | DualSense (Xbox glyph) | Keyboard | Mouse |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| Lean | Left stick | WASD / arrows; Shift = half | Pointer offset from dial |\\n480→| Confirm | ✕ (A) | Enter, Space, E | Left click on the item |\\n| Back | ○ (B) | Esc, Backspace | Right click |\\n| Pause | Options (Menu) | Esc, P | Pause icon, top right, shown while the mouse moves |\\n| Breath, hold | R2 (RT) or ✕ (A) | Space | Hold left button |\\n| Left / right foot | L1 or L2 / R1 or R2 (LB or LT / RB or RT) | F or ← / J or → | Left / right button |\\n| Tabs | L1 / R1 (LB / RB) | Q / E | Wheel, or click the tab |\\n| Hub: jump, wave, sit | ✕, △, □ (A, Y, X) | Space, V, B | Click to walk |\\n\\n- **Hero wrapper ✔:** call `readMoveInput(ctx, hero, input)`, then OR in `PadCross` (`consumePress` → `input.jump`, `isDown` → `input.jumpHeld`) and the same for wave and sit. In the hub ✕ interacts when a prompt is showing, otherwise jumps.\\n- **Menus** read the d-pad, stick (with repeat), arrows and WASD. Hover moves focus; left click confirms; a wheel scrolls lists; sliders drag.\\n490→- **Keep the mouse native:** the Dot follows the mouse as soon as the mouse moves, and goes back to stick or keys as soon as those are used.\\n- **Respect the hub's chord:** ignore Options while Create is held.\\n\\n### Prompts and glyphs\\n\\n- Prompts always read `[glyph] verb` and follow the **last device used**. Track it in `src/core/device.js` from `ctx.input`: `held`/`queuedPresses` starting `Pad` or a stick past .3 means pad; `Mouse*` or pointer movement means mouse; anything else means keyboard. Add guarded DOM `keydown`/`pointerdown`/`wheel` listeners for \\\"press any button\\\" and for exiting attract.\\n- **Glyph sprites, drawn by you in `src/art/glyphs.js`:** PlayStation shapes ✕ ○ □ △ in their colours, L1 R1 L2 R2, Options, sticks. Xbox A B X Y (a Settings option), LB RB LT RT, Menu. Keycaps with the letter. A mouse with the used button lit.\\n\\n### Screens\\n\\n500→- **Dialogue box:** bottom strip, white; speaker name in teal; typewriter at about 40 cps, in sync with voice syllables; ✕ completes, then advances; hold to skip fast. Ounce gets a small dial portrait with a mood needle.\\n- **Results, station menu, Hall of Numbers, Locker Room, Sweat Jar, Report:** one focal element each, big numbers, 1-2 lines of comment.\\n- **Locker Room:** on a turntable; skin (sand, orange, red, plum), hair style and colour, top, bottom, headband, jar unlocks.\\n- **Name entry:** letter grid (stick, d-pad, click) plus direct typing, 8 characters max.\\n\\n### Pause menu\\n\\n`engine.timeScale = 0` ✔ freezes physics, `fixedUpdate` and game time while `update` still runs and `wasPressed` still works. Menus therefore read input in `update`. Don't use `engine.paused` for this.\\n\\nResume / Restart activity / Back to the island / Settings / How to play / About & Credits / **Dev Tools**. In a session: Resume and Settings only, and nothing freezes.\\n510→\\n### Settings (own HUD menu, not the engine panel)\\n\\nMusic volume (**default 10%**), SFX, Voice, Button glyphs (PlayStation / Xbox), Gentle Mode (rings ×1.25, noise ×.8), Mouse lean radius, Step timing offset, Reduce flashes, Look (Default, `storybook`, `arcade`, `handheld`), Pixel size (`engine.settings.set({ look, pixelSize })`), Fullscreen, Reset to defaults.\\n\\n### Touch-only devices\\n\\nDetect ✔ `matchMedia('(hover: none) and (pointer: coarse)')` with no gamepad. Start with `touch: false` always, and `settings: { button: 'top-right' }` only on such devices (otherwise `button: false`). ✔ The ⚙ appears and a tap opens the engine's panel. Show over the title: **\\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\"**, wrapped: a portrait phone's art is as narrow as 168 px wide. Attract runs and loops. A tap returns to the title message and the 10 s timer restarts. If a pad connects or a key is pressed, drop the message and play normally.\\n\\n---\\n520→\\n## 10. Dev mode\\n\\nReached from the pause menu, not in sessions. 10-foot legible and fully controller-driven. Tabs with L1/R1.\\n\\n**Sliders (live, each read by the code every step; registry in `src/core/tunables.js`):**\\n\\n| Tab | Variables, with defaults |\\n|---|---|\\n| Balance | dotInstability .6, dotAuthority 3, dotDamping 3.4, dotNoise .8, dotLag .08, ringScale 1, gustForce 1.6, mouseLeanRadius 70 |\\n530→| Breath and reps | breathBonus .55, repLag .10, repFatigue .10, repTempoScale 1 |\\n| Rhythm | stepWindow 1, stepOffsetMs 0, hoopLow .9, hoopHigh 2.4, hoopLiftRate .35 |\\n| Games | headerInterval 1.0, slackWalkInst 2.6, trayGravity 9.8, trayMaxTilt 14, jogTargetCadence 3, pierBoost 2.14 |\\n| Economy | dripRate 1, starThresholdScale 1, ageTrainingWeight .5 |\\n\\nEach slider shows its value and default. **One button resets the tab, one resets everything.** Export prints the changed values as JSON to the console and copies them if allowed, so a designer can paste them into `src/data/`.\\n\\n**Tools tab:** go to day 1-7; jump to any activity or scene; finish the current activity with 0-3★; give 50 Drips; unlock all; autopilot (bot skill picker); god mode (Dot can't leave the ring); time scale .25-3; overlay (scene, state, Dot, ring, fps, last device); hide HUD; free camera (`engine.setCamera({ preset: 'free' }, { syncUrl: false })`); dialogue tester (any line, with voice); sound test (every song, SFX, speaker); animation viewer (every clip on an avatar); reset save.\\n\\n---\\n540→\\n## 11. Attract mode\\n\\nAfter **10 seconds with no input on the title or any menu screen**, start a looping demo:\\n\\n- **Playlist:** Hub walk → Holding Still → Hoop → Header → Step → Slackline → Tray → Pier Jump → Jog → Long Stand excerpt, about 14 s each, with iris transitions. Cover every activity and feature family.\\n- It runs the **real scenes** with expert bot drivers and cheats (ring ×2, god mode). Banner: {TITLE}, \\\"Press any button.\\\" plus Ounce's subtitles (\\\"This is a recording...\\\").\\n- **Any input exits**: key, click, mouse move past a few pixels, wheel, pad button or stick, touch. You return to the title and the timer re-arms.\\n- Not in a session, not during play, not on the pause menu.\\n\\n550→---\\n\\n## 12. Multiplayer\\n\\n**Reading of the brief:** the hub protocol is how the game plays online; on its own the game has no server, so it plays alone or on one screen. Both run the same round, **The Medley**, and the same lane code. Nothing else connects to a network.\\n\\n### The Medley\\n\\nThree events in fixed windows: Stillness (a pose), then Beat (Reps or Hoop or Step), then Balance-lean (Header), each 55 s with 10 s between, about 3.2 minutes. The specific picks and shortened durations live in `src/data/medley.js`, and the picks come from a seeded stream. Each event normalises to 0-1000; the total wins. Results show medals, awards (\\\"Stillest\\\", \\\"Most Apologetic\\\") and Ounce's remarks.\\n\\n560→### On its own: Family Hour\\n\\nJoin screen: **each device claims a mat by pressing Cross/Enter** (up to 4 pads plus keyboard-and-mouse). Bots can fill empty mats (toggle).\\n\\n**The engine merges all pads into one** ✔, so lanes read `navigator.getGamepads()` by index themselves (`applyDeadzone` is exported; guard for Node). In 4-mat staging, each player gets a small dial (radius 24) above their avatar's head. Podium, rematch.\\n\\n### In AI Hub: ghost mode\\n\\nPassed 16/16 with the real engine on WebGPU ✔ at players=1, 2, 4 (latency, jitter, loss) and host-leave.\\n\\n570→```html\\n<meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\">\\n<script>/* session.js pasted unmodified: first script, right after charset */</script>\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"ghost\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"Score the most across three events. Stay in the circle.\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"Left stick, WASD or mouse: lean. R2, Space or click: breathe. L1/R1, F/J: step.\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\" content=\\\"4\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:webgpu\\\" content=\\\"required\\\">\\n580→```\\n\\nBoot order ✔:\\n\\n```js\\nlet info = null;\\nif (window.AIHub?.active) info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\\nconst engine = await Engine.start(firstScene, withUrlOptions({ /* ... */ seed: info ? info.seed : savedOrDefaultSeed }));\\nif (info) AIHub.ready();                 // no key press, as soon as the card can show\\n```\\n590→\\nIf `connect()` answers null, carry on as the normal game. Without WebGPU, `Engine.start` rejects and the engine prints \\\"Failed to start: WebGPU unavailable: ...\\\" on the page ✔. Catch the rejection, or it also surfaces as a page error ✔, and call `AIHub.fail(message)` in a session.\\n\\n**In a session:**\\n- **The card (`card: true`)** is the game's own: the players' avatars lining up on mats in seat colours (`#e8443a #3b82f6 #22c55e #f5b700`), {TITLE}, ready ticks, how to win, the controls for the last device, the time left from the `card` event. Enter or Cross → `AIHub.answer('ready')`; Triangle or M → `AIHub.answer('more')`. Use a **direct `keydown` listener for Enter** ✔ here. No menus. Cosmetic randomness only from `AIHub.rng('card')`.\\n- **Start:** on `start` show a countdown from `AIHub.time()`; play at `time() >= 0`. Event windows are read from `AIHub.time()`, so all copies stay in step.\\n- **Same world:** gusts, pose picks and object waves come from `AIHub.rng(label)` or the seeded `ctx.random`.\\n- **Ghosts:** a `setInterval` at 100 ms (not tied to rendering) sends `AIHub.send({ a: eventIndex, x, y, c: clipIndex, t: clipTime, s: score }, { reliable: false })` and calls `AIHub.progress({ score, label })`. Start as soon as `start` arrives, even with score 0: the harness needs both within seconds. Receivers lerp the other mats; they never simulate them, and they hide a ghost whose `a` differs from theirs.\\n- **`leave`:** that avatar waves and walks off. The round goes on, host included.\\n- **End:** `AIHub.result({ score, stats, awards })` once, at the end of the Medley or at once on `time-up`. On `end`: stop input, stop sound, send nothing.\\n600→- **Never:** no title, attract, dev mode, saves, quit or restart; no chat or custom names; no `alert`, `window.open` or navigation. Names come from `info.players` and are drawn with `say()`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 13. Art direction\\n\\n**Base: the engine's native look**, default pixel pipeline, toon materials, 16-colour palette (`look` left unset). The scene reads clean and bright: white, mist, sky and cyan, with lime and sand for growth and warmth, orange and red as accents. Start with `quality: 'high'` (`'medium'` in sessions, where several copies may share a machine in testing).\\n\\n**Performance is out of scope.** Add the detail the scene wants and don't spend time on optimisation.\\n\\n610→### Avatars ✔\\n\\nRe-dress the kit's hero with the same rig. This is proven to look good at gameplay framing: egg heads, dot eyes, hair caps. Use `castShadow: false` plus `ContactShadow` ✔: casting on the model gave ugly self-shadow blotches. The hero's `Eyes` mesh reads as sunglasses, so hide it. Compile clips once and share them between avatars.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"434→## 9. UI and UX: 10 feet, controller first\\n\\n**One UI for every device: the pixel HUD.** No DOM menus; same screens for pad, keyboard and mouse. Build a small kit in `src/ui/`.\\n\\n### Layout rules\\n\\n440→- **Use `aspect: 'fill'` ✔.** It removes letterboxing at every window size (`adaptive` gives thick black borders at 1280×720). Art size then varies: 480×270 at 1080p and 4K, 427×240 at 720p, 640×360 in a small frame, 400×300 at 800×600. **Lay out from `hud.width` and `hud.height` with anchors**, never fixed coordinates. Keep a 12 art px safe margin.\\n- **Pointer to art pixels ✔:** `ax = (p.x + 1) / 2 * hud.width; ay = (1 - p.y) / 2 * hud.height`. The HUD canvas ignores pointer events, and its rect equals the game canvas's.\\n- **Text:** the 5×7 font at scale 1 is 20×28 px at 1080p, the minimum. Scale 2 for menu rows and headings, 3-4 for the title and big numbers.\\n- **No dense screens:** at most 8 menu rows; at most 3 lines of dialogue; one idea per screen; one activity per records page. Page rather than scroll, wherever you can.\\n\\n### Mixed-case text ✔\\n\\nThe engine font is capitals only, which is wrong for this voice. Draw lowercase through `hud.sprite`, everything else through `hud.text`, on a 6 px grid. This table and function rendered correctly; use them:\\n\\n```js\\n450→// src/ui/font.js. Rows top to bottom, 5 bits, bit 4 = left. Rows 7-8 are descenders.\\nconst H = {\\na:'00 00 0e 01 0f 11 0f 00 00', b:'10 10 1e 11 11 11 1e 00 00', c:'00 00 0e 11 10 11 0e 00 00', d:'01 01 0f 11 11 11 0f 00 00',\\ne:'00 00 0e 11 1f 10 0e 00 00', f:'06 09 08 1c 08 08 08 00 00', g:'00 00 0f 11 11 11 0f 01 0e', h:'10 10 1e 11 11 11 11 00 00',\\ni:'04 00 0c 04 04 04 0e 00 00', j:'02 00 06 02 02 02 02 12 0c', k:'10 10 12 14 18 14 12 00 00', l:'0c 04 04 04 04 04 0e 00 00',\\nm:'00 00 1a 15 15 15 15 00 00', n:'00 00 1e 11 11 11 11 00 00', o:'00 00 0e 11 11 11 0e 00 00', p:'00 00 1e 11 11 11 1e 10 10',\\nq:'00 00 0f 11 11 11 0f 01 01', r:'00 00 16 19 10 10 10 00 00', s:'00 00 0f 10 0e 01 1e 00 00', t:'08 08 1c 08 08 09 06 00 00',\\nu:'00 00 11 11 11 13 0d 00 00', v:'00 00 11 11 11 0a 04 00 00', w:'00 00 11 11 15 15 0a 00 00', x:'00 00 11 0a 04 0a 11 00 00',\\ny:'00 00 11 11 11 11 0f 01 0e', z:'00 00 1f 02 04 08 1f 00 00' };\\nexport const GLYPHS = Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(H).map(([k, v]) => [k, v.split(' ').map((h) => parseInt(h, 16).toString(2).padStart(5, '0').replace(/0/g, '.').replace(/1/g, 'o'))]));\\n460→export function say(hud, x, y, text, { color = 'white', shadow = 'ink', scale = 1 } = {}) {\\n  for (const ch of text) {\\n    const g = GLYPHS[ch];\\n    if (g) hud.sprite(x, y, g, { o: color }, { scale, shadow });\\n    else if (ch !== ' ') hud.text(x, y, ch, { color, shadow, scale });\\n    x += 6 * scale;\\n  }\\n  return x;\\n}\\n```\\n470→\\nAdd a measuring and word-wrapping helper. Replace any character the font lacks with `?` (hub names can hold anything); a test checks all game text has glyphs.\\n\\n### Input map\\n\\nRemap once at boot ✔: `ctx.input.gamepadButtons = { 0:'PadCross', 1:'PadCircle', 2:'PadSquare', 3:'PadTriangle', 4:'PadL1', 5:'PadR1', 6:'PadL2', 7:'PadR2', 8:'PadCreate', 9:'PadOptions', 10:'PadL3', 11:'PadR3', 12:'PadUp', 13:'PadDown', 14:'PadLeft', 15:'PadRight' }`. Pad buttons then appear in `isDown`, `wasPressed`, `state().held` and recordings. Keep one action table in `src/core/actions.js`.\\n\\n| Action | DualSense (Xbox glyph) | Keyboard | Mouse |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| Lean | Left stick | WASD / arrows; Shift = half | Pointer offset from dial |\\n480→| Confirm | ✕ (A) | Enter, Space, E | Left click on the item |\\n| Back | ○ (B) | Esc, Backspace | Right click |\\n| Pause | Options (Menu) | Esc, P | Pause icon, top right, shown while the mouse moves |\\n| Breath, hold | R2 (RT) or ✕ (A) | Space | Hold left button |\\n| Left / right foot | L1 or L2 / R1 or R2 (LB or LT / RB or RT) | F or ← / J or → | Left / right button |\\n| Tabs | L1 / R1 (LB / RB) | Q / E | Wheel, or click the tab |\\n| Hub: jump, wave, sit | ✕, △, □ (A, Y, X) | Space, V, B | Click to walk |\\n\\n- **Hero wrapper ✔:** call `readMoveInput(ctx, hero, input)`, then OR in `PadCross` (`consumePress` → `input.jump`, `isDown` → `input.jumpHeld`) and the same for wave and sit. In the hub ✕ interacts when a prompt is showing, otherwise jumps.\\n- **Menus** read the d-pad, stick (with repeat), arrows and WASD. Hover moves focus; left click confirms; a wheel scrolls lists; sliders drag.\\n490→- **Keep the mouse native:** the Dot follows the mouse as soon as the mouse moves, and goes back to stick or keys as soon as those are used.\\n- **Respect the hub's chord:** ignore Options while Create is held.\\n\\n### Prompts and glyphs\\n\\n- Prompts always read `[glyph] verb` and follow the **last device used**. Track it in `src/core/device.js` from `ctx.input`: `held`/`queuedPresses` starting `Pad` or a stick past .3 means pad; `Mouse*` or pointer movement means mouse; anything else means keyboard. Add guarded DOM `keydown`/`pointerdown`/`wheel` listeners for \\\"press any button\\\" and for exiting attract.\\n- **Glyph sprites, drawn by you in `src/art/glyphs.js`:** PlayStation shapes ✕ ○ □ △ in their colours, L1 R1 L2 R2, Options, sticks. Xbox A B X Y (a Settings option), LB RB LT RT, Menu. Keycaps with the letter. A mouse with the used button lit.\\n\\n### Screens\\n\\n500→- **Dialogue box:** bottom strip, white; speaker name in teal; typewriter at about 40 cps, in sync with voice syllables; ✕ completes, then advances; hold to skip fast. Ounce gets a small dial portrait with a mood needle.\\n- **Results, station menu, Hall of Numbers, Locker Room, Sweat Jar, Report:** one focal element each, big numbers, 1-2 lines of comment.\\n- **Locker Room:** on a turntable; skin (sand, orange, red, plum), hair style and colour, top, bottom, headband, jar unlocks.\\n- **Name entry:** letter grid (stick, d-pad, click) plus direct typing, 8 characters max.\\n\\n### Pause menu\\n\\n`engine.timeScale = 0` ✔ freezes physics, `fixedUpdate` and game time while `update` still runs and `wasPressed` still works. Menus therefore read input in `update`. Don't use `engine.paused` for this.\\n\\nResume / Restart activity / Back to the island / Settings / How to play / About & Credits / **Dev Tools**. In a session: Resume and Settings only, and nothing freezes.\\n510→\\n### Settings (own HUD menu, not the engine panel)\\n\\nMusic volume (**default 10%**), SFX, Voice, Button glyphs (PlayStation / Xbox), Gentle Mode (rings ×1.25, noise ×.8), Mouse lean radius, Step timing offset, Reduce flashes, Look (Default, `storybook`, `arcade`, `handheld`), Pixel size (`engine.settings.set({ look, pixelSize })`), Fullscreen, Reset to defaults.\\n\\n### Touch-only devices\\n\\nDetect ✔ `matchMedia('(hover: none) and (pointer: coarse)')` with no gamepad. Start with `touch: false` always, and `settings: { button: 'top-right' }` only on such devices (otherwise `button: false`). ✔ The ⚙ appears and a tap opens the engine's panel. Show over the title: **\\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\"**, wrapped: a portrait phone's art is as narrow as 168 px wide. Attract runs and loops. A tap returns to the title message and the 10 s timer restarts. If a pad connects or a key is pressed, drop the message and play normally.\\n\\n---\\n520→\\n## 10. Dev mode\\n\\nReached from the pause menu, not in sessions. 10-foot legible and fully controller-driven. Tabs with L1/R1.\\n\\n**Sliders (live, each read by the code every step; registry in `src/core/tunables.js`):**\\n\\n| Tab | Variables, with defaults |\\n|---|---|\\n| Balance | dotInstability .6, dotAuthority 3, dotDamping 3.4, dotNoise .8, dotLag .08, ringScale 1, gustForce 1.6, mouseLeanRadius 70 |\\n530→| Breath and reps | breathBonus .55, repLag .10, repFatigue .10, repTempoScale 1 |\\n| Rhythm | stepWindow 1, stepOffsetMs 0, hoopLow .9, hoopHigh 2.4, hoopLiftRate .35 |\\n| Games | headerInterval 1.0, slackWalkInst 2.6, trayGravity 9.8, trayMaxTilt 14, jogTargetCadence 3, pierBoost 2.14 |\\n| Economy | dripRate 1, starThresholdScale 1, ageTrainingWeight .5 |\\n\\nEach slider shows its value and default. **One button resets the tab, one resets everything.** Export prints the changed values as JSON to the console and copies them if allowed, so a designer can paste them into `src/data/`.\\n\\n**Tools tab:** go to day 1-7; jump to any activity or scene; finish the current activity with 0-3★; give 50 Drips; unlock all; autopilot (bot skill picker); god mode (Dot can't leave the ring); time scale .25-3; overlay (scene, state, Dot, ring, fps, last device); hide HUD; free camera (`engine.setCamera({ preset: 'free' }, { syncUrl: false })`); dialogue tester (any line, with voice); sound test (every song, SFX, speaker); animation viewer (every clip on an avatar); reset save.\\n\\n---\\n540→\\n## 11. Attract mode\\n\\nAfter **10 seconds with no input on the title or any menu screen**, start a looping demo:\\n\\n- **Playlist:** Hub walk → Holding Still → Hoop → Header → Step → Slackline → Tray → Pier Jump → Jog → Long Stand excerpt, about 14 s each, with iris transitions. Cover every activity and feature family.\\n- It runs the **real scenes** with expert bot drivers and cheats (ring ×2, god mode). Banner: {TITLE}, \\\"Press any button.\\\" plus Ounce's subtitles (\\\"This is a recording...\\\").\\n- **Any input exits**: key, click, mouse move past a few pixels, wheel, pad button or stick, touch. You return to the title and the timer re-arms.\\n- Not in a session, not during play, not on the pause menu.\\n\\n550→---\\n\\n## 12. Multiplayer\\n\\n**Reading of the brief:** the hub protocol is how the game plays online; on its own the game has no server, so it plays alone or on one screen. Both run the same round, **The Medley**, and the same lane code. Nothing else connects to a network.\\n\\n### The Medley\\n\\nThree events in fixed windows: Stillness (a pose), then Beat (Reps or Hoop or Step), then Balance-lean (Header), each 55 s with 10 s between, about 3.2 minutes. The specific picks and shortened durations live in `src/data/medley.js`, and the picks come from a seeded stream. Each event normalises to 0-1000; the total wins. Results show medals, awards (\\\"Stillest\\\", \\\"Most Apologetic\\\") and Ounce's remarks.\\n\\n560→### On its own: Family Hour\\n\\nJoin screen: **each device claims a mat by pressing Cross/Enter** (up to 4 pads plus keyboard-and-mouse). Bots can fill empty mats (toggle).\\n\\n**The engine merges all pads into one** ✔, so lanes read `navigator.getGamepads()` by index themselves (`applyDeadzone` is exported; guard for Node). In 4-mat staging, each player gets a small dial (radius 24) above their avatar's head. Podium, rematch.\\n\\n### In AI Hub: ghost mode\\n\\nPassed 16/16 with the real engine on WebGPU ✔ at players=1, 2, 4 (latency, jitter, loss) and host-leave.\\n\\n570→```html\\n<meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\">\\n<script>/* session.js pasted unmodified: first script, right after charset */</script>\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"ghost\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"Score the most across three events. Stay in the circle.\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"Left stick, WASD or mouse: lean. R2, Space or click: breathe. L1/R1, F/J: step.\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\" content=\\\"4\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:webgpu\\\" content=\\\"required\\\">\\n580→```\\n\\nBoot order ✔:\\n\\n```js\\nlet info = null;\\nif (window.AIHub?.active) info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\\nconst engine = await Engine.start(firstScene, withUrlOptions({ /* ... */ seed: info ? info.seed : savedOrDefaultSeed }));\\nif (info) AIHub.ready();                 // no key press, as soon as the card can show\\n```\\n590→\\nIf `connect()` answers null, carry on as the normal game. Without WebGPU, `Engine.start` rejects and the engine prints \\\"Failed to start: WebGPU unavailable: ...\\\" on the page ✔. Catch the rejection, or it also surfaces as a page error ✔, and call `AIHub.fail(message)` in a session.\\n\\n**In a session:**\\n- **The card (`card: true`)** is the game's own: the players' avatars lining up on mats in seat colours (`#e8443a #3b82f6 #22c55e #f5b700`), {TITLE}, ready ticks, how to win, the controls for the last device, the time left from the `card` event. Enter or Cross → `AIHub.answer('ready')`; Triangle or M → `AIHub.answer('more')`. Use a **direct `keydown` listener for Enter** ✔ here. No menus. Cosmetic randomness only from `AIHub.rng('card')`.\\n- **Start:** on `start` show a countdown from `AIHub.time()`; play at `time() >= 0`. Event windows are read from `AIHub.time()`, so all copies stay in step.\\n- **Same world:** gusts, pose picks and object waves come from `AIHub.rng(label)` or the seeded `ctx.random`.\\n- **Ghosts:** a `setInterval` at 100 ms (not tied to rendering) sends `AIHub.send({ a: eventIndex, x, y, c: clipIndex, t: clipTime, s: score }, { reliable: false })` and calls `AIHub.progress({ score, label })`. Start as soon as `start` arrives, even with score 0: the harness needs both within seconds. Receivers lerp the other mats; they never simulate them, and they hide a ghost whose `a` differs from theirs.\\n- **`leave`:** that avatar waves and walks off. The round goes on, host included.\\n- **End:** `AIHub.result({ score, stats, awards })` once, at the end of the Medley or at once on `time-up`. On `end`: stop input, stop sound, send nothing.\\n600→- **Never:** no title, attract, dev mode, saves, quit or restart; no chat or custom names; no `alert`, `window.open` or navigation. Names come from `info.players` and are drawn with `say()`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 13. Art direction\\n\\n**Base: the engine's native look**, default pixel pipeline, toon materials, 16-colour palette (`look` left unset). The scene reads clean and bright: white, mist, sky and cyan, with lime and sand for growth and warmth, orange and red as accents. Start with `quality: 'high'` (`'medium'` in sessions, where several copies may share a machine in testing).\\n\\n**Performance is out of scope.** Add the detail the scene wants and don't spend time on optimisation.\\n\\n610→### Avatars ✔\\n\\nRe-dress the kit's hero with the same rig. This is proven to look good at gameplay framing: egg heads, dot eyes, hair caps. Use `castShadow: false` plus `ContactShadow` ✔: casting on the model gave ugly self-shadow blotches. The hero's `Eyes` mesh reads as sunglasses, so hide it. Compile clips once and share them between avatars.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":434,\"limit\":180,\"raw_output\":\"## 9. UI and UX: 10 feet, controller first\\n\\n**One UI for every device: the pixel HUD.** No DOM menus; same screens for pad, keyboard and mouse. Build a small kit in `src/ui/`.\\n\\n### Layout rules\\n\\n- **Use `aspect: 'fill'` ✔.** It removes letterboxing at every window size (`adaptive` gives thick black borders at 1280×720). Art size then varies: 480×270 at 1080p and 4K, 427×240 at 720p, 640×360 in a small frame, 400×300 at 800×600. **Lay out from `hud.width` and `hud.height` with anchors**, never fixed coordinates. Keep a 12 art px safe margin.\\n- **Pointer to art pixels ✔:** `ax = (p.x + 1) / 2 * hud.width; ay = (1 - p.y) / 2 * hud.height`. The HUD canvas ignores pointer events, and its rect equals the game canvas's.\\n- **Text:** the 5×7 font at scale 1 is 20×28 px at 1080p, the minimum. Scale 2 for menu rows and headings, 3-4 for the title and big numbers.\\n- **No dense screens:** at most 8 menu rows; at most 3 lines of dialogue; one idea per screen; one activity per records page. Page rather than scroll, wherever you can.\\n\\n### Mixed-case text ✔\\n\\nThe engine font is capitals only, which is wrong for this voice. Draw lowercase through `hud.sprite`, everything else through `hud.text`, on a 6 px grid. This table and function rendered correctly; use them:\\n\\n```js\\n// src/ui/font.js. Rows top to bottom, 5 bits, bit 4 = left. Rows 7-8 are descenders.\\nconst H = {\\na:'00 00 0e 01 0f 11 0f 00 00', b:'10 10 1e 11 11 11 1e 00 00', c:'00 00 0e 11 10 11 0e 00 00', d:'01 01 0f 11 11 11 0f 00 00',\\ne:'00 00 0e 11 1f 10 0e 00 00', f:'06 09 08 1c 08 08 08 00 00', g:'00 00 0f 11 11 11 0f 01 0e', h:'10 10 1e 11 11 11 11 00 00',\\ni:'04 00 0c 04 04 04 0e 00 00', j:'02 00 06 02 02 02 02 12 0c', k:'10 10 12 14 18 14 12 00 00', l:'0c 04 04 04 04 04 0e 00 00',\\nm:'00 00 1a 15 15 15 15 00 00', n:'00 00 1e 11 11 11 11 00 00', o:'00 00 0e 11 11 11 0e 00 00', p:'00 00 1e 11 11 11 1e 10 10',\\nq:'00 00 0f 11 11 11 0f 01 01', r:'00 00 16 19 10 10 10 00 00', s:'00 00 0f 10 0e 01 1e 00 00', t:'08 08 1c 08 08 09 06 00 00',\\nu:'00 00 11 11 11 13 0d 00 00', v:'00 00 11 11 11 0a 04 00 00', w:'00 00 11 11 15 15 0a 00 00', x:'00 00 11 0a 04 0a 11 00 00',\\ny:'00 00 11 11 11 11 0f 01 0e', z:'00 00 1f 02 04 08 1f 00 00' };\\nexport const GLYPHS = Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(H).map(([k, v]) => [k, v.split(' ').map((h) => parseInt(h, 16).toString(2).padStart(5, '0').replace(/0/g, '.').replace(/1/g, 'o'))]));\\nexport function say(hud, x, y, text, { color = 'white', shadow = 'ink', scale = 1 } = {}) {\\n  for (const ch of text) {\\n    const g = GLYPHS[ch];\\n    if (g) hud.sprite(x, y, g, { o: color }, { scale, shadow });\\n    else if (ch !== ' ') hud.text(x, y, ch, { color, shadow, scale });\\n    x += 6 * scale;\\n  }\\n  return x;\\n}\\n```\\n\\nAdd a measuring and word-wrapping helper. Replace any character the font lacks with `?` (hub names can hold anything); a test checks all game text has glyphs.\\n\\n### Input map\\n\\nRemap once at boot ✔: `ctx.input.gamepadButtons = { 0:'PadCross', 1:'PadCircle', 2:'PadSquare', 3:'PadTriangle', 4:'PadL1', 5:'PadR1', 6:'PadL2', 7:'PadR2', 8:'PadCreate', 9:'PadOptions', 10:'PadL3', 11:'PadR3', 12:'PadUp', 13:'PadDown', 14:'PadLeft', 15:'PadRight' }`. Pad buttons then appear in `isDown`, `wasPressed`, `state().held` and recordings. Keep one action table in `src/core/actions.js`.\\n\\n| Action | DualSense (Xbox glyph) | Keyboard | Mouse |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| Lean | Left stick | WASD / arrows; Shift = half | Pointer offset from dial |\\n| Confirm | ✕ (A) | Enter, Space, E | Left click on the item |\\n| Back | ○ (B) | Esc, Backspace | Right click |\\n| Pause | Options (Menu) | Esc, P | Pause icon, top right, shown while the mouse moves |\\n| Breath, hold | R2 (RT) or ✕ (A) | Space | Hold left button |\\n| Left / right foot | L1 or L2 / R1 or R2 (LB or LT / RB or RT) | F or ← / J or → | Left / right button |\\n| Tabs | L1 / R1 (LB / RB) | Q / E | Wheel, or click the tab |\\n| Hub: jump, wave, sit | ✕, △, □ (A, Y, X) | Space, V, B | Click to walk |\\n\\n- **Hero wrapper ✔:** call `readMoveInput(ctx, hero, input)`, then OR in `PadCross` (`consumePress` → `input.jump`, `isDown` → `input.jumpHeld`) and the same for wave and sit. In the hub ✕ interacts when a prompt is showing, otherwise jumps.\\n- **Menus** read the d-pad, stick (with repeat), arrows and WASD. Hover moves focus; left click confirms; a wheel scrolls lists; sliders drag.\\n- **Keep the mouse native:** the Dot follows the mouse as soon as the mouse moves, and goes back to stick or keys as soon as those are used.\\n- **Respect the hub's chord:** ignore Options while Create is held.\\n\\n### Prompts and glyphs\\n\\n- Prompts always read `[glyph] verb` and follow the **last device used**. Track it in `src/core/device.js` from `ctx.input`: `held`/`queuedPresses` starting `Pad` or a stick past .3 means pad; `Mouse*` or pointer movement means mouse; anything else means keyboard. Add guarded DOM `keydown`/`pointerdown`/`wheel` listeners for \\\"press any button\\\" and for exiting attract.\\n- **Glyph sprites, drawn by you in `src/art/glyphs.js`:** PlayStation shapes ✕ ○ □ △ in their colours, L1 R1 L2 R2, Options, sticks. Xbox A B X Y (a Settings option), LB RB LT RT, Menu. Keycaps with the letter. A mouse with the used button lit.\\n\\n### Screens\\n\\n- **Dialogue box:** bottom strip, white; speaker name in teal; typewriter at about 40 cps, in sync with voice syllables; ✕ completes, then advances; hold to skip fast. Ounce gets a small dial portrait with a mood needle.\\n- **Results, station menu, Hall of Numbers, Locker Room, Sweat Jar, Report:** one focal element each, big numbers, 1-2 lines of comment.\\n- **Locker Room:** on a turntable; skin (sand, orange, red, plum), hair style and colour, top, bottom, headband, jar unlocks.\\n- **Name entry:** letter grid (stick, d-pad, click) plus direct typing, 8 characters max.\\n\\n### Pause menu\\n\\n`engine.timeScale = 0` ✔ freezes physics, `fixedUpdate` and game time while `update` still runs and `wasPressed` still works. Menus therefore read input in `update`. Don't use `engine.paused` for this.\\n\\nResume / Restart activity / Back to the island / Settings / How to play / About & Credits / **Dev Tools**. In a session: Resume and Settings only, and nothing freezes.\\n\\n### Settings (own HUD menu, not the engine panel)\\n\\nMusic volume (**default 10%**), SFX, Voice, Button glyphs (PlayStation / Xbox), Gentle Mode (rings ×1.25, noise ×.8), Mouse lean radius, Step timing offset, Reduce flashes, Look (Default, `storybook`, `arcade`, `handheld`), Pixel size (`engine.settings.set({ look, pixelSize })`), Fullscreen, Reset to defaults.\\n\\n### Touch-only devices\\n\\nDetect ✔ `matchMedia('(hover: none) and (pointer: coarse)')` with no gamepad. Start with `touch: false` always, and `settings: { button: 'top-right' }` only on such devices (otherwise `button: false`). ✔ The ⚙ appears and a tap opens the engine's panel. Show over the title: **\\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\"**, wrapped: a portrait phone's art is as narrow as 168 px wide. Attract runs and loops. A tap returns to the title message and the 10 s timer restarts. If a pad connects or a key is pressed, drop the message and play normally.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Dev mode\\n\\nReached from the pause menu, not in sessions. 10-foot legible and fully controller-driven. Tabs with L1/R1.\\n\\n**Sliders (live, each read by the code every step; registry in `src/core/tunables.js`):**\\n\\n| Tab | Variables, with defaults |\\n|---|---|\\n| Balance | dotInstability .6, dotAuthority 3, dotDamping 3.4, dotNoise .8, dotLag .08, ringScale 1, gustForce 1.6, mouseLeanRadius 70 |\\n| Breath and reps | breathBonus .55, repLag .10, repFatigue .10, repTempoScale 1 |\\n| Rhythm | stepWindow 1, stepOffsetMs 0, hoopLow .9, hoopHigh 2.4, hoopLiftRate .35 |\\n| Games | headerInterval 1.0, slackWalkInst 2.6, trayGravity 9.8, trayMaxTilt 14, jogTargetCadence 3, pierBoost 2.14 |\\n| Economy | dripRate 1, starThresholdScale 1, ageTrainingWeight .5 |\\n\\nEach slider shows its value and default. **One button resets the tab, one resets everything.** Export prints the changed values as JSON to the console and copies them if allowed, so a designer can paste them into `src/data/`.\\n\\n**Tools tab:** go to day 1-7; jump to any activity or scene; finish the current activity with 0-3★; give 50 Drips; unlock all; autopilot (bot skill picker); god mode (Dot can't leave the ring); time scale .25-3; overlay (scene, state, Dot, ring, fps, last device); hide HUD; free camera (`engine.setCamera({ preset: 'free' }, { syncUrl: false })`); dialogue tester (any line, with voice); sound test (every song, SFX, speaker); animation viewer (every clip on an avatar); reset save.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Attract mode\\n\\nAfter **10 seconds with no input on the title or any menu screen**, start a looping demo:\\n\\n- **Playlist:** Hub walk → Holding Still → Hoop → Header → Step → Slackline → Tray → Pier Jump → Jog → Long Stand excerpt, about 14 s each, with iris transitions. Cover every activity and feature family.\\n- It runs the **real scenes** with expert bot drivers and cheats (ring ×2, god mode). Banner: {TITLE}, \\\"Press any button.\\\" plus Ounce's subtitles (\\\"This is a recording...\\\").\\n- **Any input exits**: key, click, mouse move past a few pixels, wheel, pad button or stick, touch. You return to the title and the timer re-arms.\\n- Not in a session, not during play, not on the pause menu.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 12. Multiplayer\\n\\n**Reading of the brief:** the hub protocol is how the game plays online; on its own the game has no server, so it plays alone or on one screen. Both run the same round, **The Medley**, and the same lane code. Nothing else connects to a network.\\n\\n### The Medley\\n\\nThree events in fixed windows: Stillness (a pose), then Beat (Reps or Hoop or Step), then Balance-lean (Header), each 55 s with 10 s between, about 3.2 minutes. The specific picks and shortened durations live in `src/data/medley.js`, and the picks come from a seeded stream. Each event normalises to 0-1000; the total wins. Results show medals, awards (\\\"Stillest\\\", \\\"Most Apologetic\\\") and Ounce's remarks.\\n\\n### On its own: Family Hour\\n\\nJoin screen: **each device claims a mat by pressing Cross/Enter** (up to 4 pads plus keyboard-and-mouse). Bots can fill empty mats (toggle).\\n\\n**The engine merges all pads into one** ✔, so lanes read `navigator.getGamepads()` by index themselves (`applyDeadzone` is exported; guard for Node). In 4-mat staging, each player gets a small dial (radius 24) above their avatar's head. Podium, rematch.\\n\\n### In AI Hub: ghost mode\\n\\nPassed 16/16 with the real engine on WebGPU ✔ at players=1, 2, 4 (latency, jitter, loss) and host-leave.\\n\\n```html\\n<meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\">\\n<script>/* session.js pasted unmodified: first script, right after charset */</script>\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"ghost\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"Score the most across three events. Stay in the circle.\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"Left stick, WASD or mouse: lean. R2, Space or click: breathe. L1/R1, F/J: step.\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\" content=\\\"4\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:webgpu\\\" content=\\\"required\\\">\\n```\\n\\nBoot order ✔:\\n\\n```js\\nlet info = null;\\nif (window.AIHub?.active) info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\\nconst engine = await Engine.start(firstScene, withUrlOptions({ /* ... */ seed: info ? info.seed : savedOrDefaultSeed }));\\nif (info) AIHub.ready();                 // no key press, as soon as the card can show\\n```\\n\\nIf `connect()` answers null, carry on as the normal game. Without WebGPU, `Engine.start` rejects and the engine prints \\\"Failed to start: WebGPU unavailable: ...\\\" on the page ✔. Catch the rejection, or it also surfaces as a page error ✔, and call `AIHub.fail(message)` in a session.\\n\\n**In a session:**\\n- **The card (`card: true`)** is the game's own: the players' avatars lining up on mats in seat colours (`#e8443a #3b82f6 #22c55e #f5b700`), {TITLE}, ready ticks, how to win, the controls for the last device, the time left from the `card` event. Enter or Cross → `AIHub.answer('ready')`; Triangle or M → `AIHub.answer('more')`. Use a **direct `keydown` listener for Enter** ✔ here. No menus. Cosmetic randomness only from `AIHub.rng('card')`.\\n- **Start:** on `start` show a countdown from `AIHub.time()`; play at `time() >= 0`. Event windows are read from `AIHub.time()`, so all copies stay in step.\\n- **Same world:** gusts, pose picks and object waves come from `AIHub.rng(label)` or the seeded `ctx.random`.\\n- **Ghosts:** a `setInterval` at 100 ms (not tied to rendering) sends `AIHub.send({ a: eventIndex, x, y, c: clipIndex, t: clipTime, s: score }, { reliable: false })` and calls `AIHub.progress({ score, label })`. Start as soon as `start` arrives, even with score 0: the harness needs both within seconds. Receivers lerp the other mats; they never simulate them, and they hide a ghost whose `a` differs from theirs.\\n- **`leave`:** that avatar waves and walks off. The round goes on, host included.\\n- **End:** `AIHub.result({ score, stats, awards })` once, at the end of the Medley or at once on `time-up`. On `end`: stop input, stop sound, send nothing.\\n- **Never:** no title, attract, dev mode, saves, quit or restart; no chat or custom names; no `alert`, `window.open` or navigation. Names come from `info.players` and are drawn with `say()`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 13. Art direction\\n\\n**Base: the engine's native look**, default pixel pipeline, toon materials, 16-colour palette (`look` left unset). The scene reads clean and bright: white, mist, sky and cyan, with lime and sand for growth and warmth, orange and red as accents. Start with `quality: 'high'` (`'medium'` in sessions, where several copies may share a machine in testing).\\n\\n**Performance is out of scope.** Add the detail the scene wants and don't spend time on optimisation.\\n\\n### Avatars ✔\\n\\nRe-dress the kit's hero with the same rig. This is proven to look good at gameplay framing: egg heads, dot eyes, hair caps. Use `castShadow: false` plus `ContactShadow` ✔: casting on the model gave ugly self-shadow blotches. The hero's `Eyes` mesh reads as sunglasses, so hide it. Compile clips once and share them between avatars.\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":992}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-3be73789-54de-49df-8b8a-5e028bd39c47-27","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/** Animalese. Same word, same syllables. A question rises at the end. */\\n\\nexport const SPEAKERS = {\\n  ounce: { f0: 340, rate: 13, formant: 1.25 },\\n  coach: { f0: 165, rate: 7.5, formant: 0.9, flat: true },\\n  marguerite: { f0: 230, rate: 9, formant: 1, vibrato: true },\\n  dennis: { f0: 120, rate: 11, formant: 0.95, lastUp: true },\\n  june: { f0: 300, rate: 10, formant: 1.15, flat: true },\\n  kevin: null,\\n10→};\\n\\nconst VOWELS = ['a', 'e', 'i', 'o', 'u'];\\nconst CONS = ['b', 'd', 'f', 'g', 'k', 'l', 'm', 'n', 'p', 'r', 's', 't'];\\nconst FORMANTS = {\\n  a: [800, 1200],\\n  e: [500, 1900],\\n  i: [300, 2300],\\n  o: [500, 900],\\n  u: [350, 800],\\n20→};\\n\\nfunction hash(s) {\\n  let h = 2166136261;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < s.length; i++) {\\n    h ^= s.charCodeAt(i);\\n    h = Math.imul(h, 16777619);\\n  }\\n  return h >>> 0;\\n}\\n30→\\nfunction wordShape(word) {\\n  const clean = word.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z]/g, '') || 'mm';\\n  const n = Math.max(1, Math.min(3, Math.round(clean.length / 2.5)));\\n  const syl = [];\\n  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\\n    const h = hash(`${clean}:${i}`);\\n    syl.push({ vowel: VOWELS[h % 5], cons: CONS[(h >>> 8) % CONS.length] });\\n  }\\n  return syl;\\n40→}\\n\\n/**\\n * Pure. `[{ t, dur, f0, vowel, cons, charIndex }]`.\\n * Kevin never speaks words.\\n */\\nexport function syllabify(text, speaker = 'ounce') {\\n  const spec = SPEAKERS[speaker] || SPEAKERS.ounce;\\n  if (!spec) return [];\\n  const src = String(text);\\n50→  const question = src.includes('?');\\n  const bang = src.includes('!');\\n  const slow = src.includes('...');\\n  const re = /[A-Za-z0-9']+/g;\\n  const words = [];\\n  let m;\\n  while ((m = re.exec(src))) words.push({ word: m[0], index: m.index });\\n  const shapes = words.map((w) => wordShape(w.word));\\n  const total = shapes.reduce((n, s) => n + s.length, 0) || 1;\\n  const base = 1 / spec.rate;\\n60→  const dur = base * (slow ? 1.45 : 1);\\n  const out = [];\\n  let t = 0;\\n  let seen = 0;\\n  shapes.forEach((shape, wi) => {\\n    shape.forEach((syl, si) => {\\n      const u = total <= 1 ? 0 : seen / (total - 1);\\n      let f0 = spec.f0;\\n      if (!spec.flat) f0 *= 1 - 0.15 * u;\\n      if (question && u > 0.66) f0 *= 1.25;\\n70→      if (bang && u > 0.8) f0 *= 1.15;\\n      if (spec.lastUp && wi === shapes.length - 1) f0 *= 1.08;\\n      if (spec.vibrato) f0 *= 1 + 0.03 * Math.sin(seen * 2.2);\\n      out.push({\\n        t,\\n        dur: dur * 0.92,\\n        f0,\\n        vowel: syl.vowel,\\n        cons: syl.cons,\\n        charIndex: words[wi].index,\\n80→      });\\n      t += dur;\\n      seen += 1;\\n    });\\n    t += dur * 0.35;\\n  });\\n  return out;\\n}\\n\\nfunction noiseBurst(ctx, destination, when, seconds, volume) {\\n90→  const n = Math.max(1, Math.floor(ctx.sampleRate * seconds));\\n  const buffer = ctx.createBuffer(1, n, ctx.sampleRate);\\n  const data = buffer.getChannelData(0);\\n  let s = 12345;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\\n    s = (s * 1664525 + 1013904223) >>> 0;\\n    data[i] = ((s >>> 8) / 0xffffff) * 2 - 1;\\n  }\\n  const src = ctx.createBufferSource();\\n  src.buffer = buffer;\\n100→  const g = ctx.createGain();\\n  g.gain.setValueAtTime(volume, when);\\n  g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.0001, when + seconds);\\n  src.connect(g);\\n  g.connect(destination);\\n  src.start(when);\\n  src.stop(when + seconds + 0.01);\\n}\\n\\n/** Schedule syllables onto any BaseAudioContext. No-op without one. */\\n110→export function renderVoice(audioCtx, destination, syllables, when = 0, speaker = 'ounce') {\\n  if (!audioCtx || !destination || !syllables?.length) return false;\\n  const shift = SPEAKERS[speaker]?.formant || 1;\\n  for (const syl of syllables) {\\n    const t0 = when + syl.t;\\n    const osc = audioCtx.createOscillator();\\n    osc.type = 'sawtooth';\\n    osc.frequency.setValueAtTime(Math.max(40, syl.f0), t0);\\n    const g = audioCtx.createGain();\\n    g.gain.setValueAtTime(0.0001, t0);\\n120→    g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.4, t0 + 0.006);\\n    g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.0001, t0 + Math.max(0.04, syl.dur));\\n    const low = audioCtx.createBiquadFilter();\\n    low.type = 'lowpass';\\n    low.frequency.value = Math.max(120, syl.f0 * 2);\\n    osc.connect(low);\\n    low.connect(g);\\n    const pair = FORMANTS[syl.vowel] || FORMANTS.a;\\n    for (const freq of pair) {\\n      const filter = audioCtx.createBiquadFilter();\\n130→      filter.type = 'bandpass';\\n      filter.frequency.value = Math.max(80, freq * shift);\\n      filter.Q.value = 5;\\n      osc.connect(filter);\\n      filter.connect(g);\\n    }\\n    g.connect(destination);\\n    osc.start(t0);\\n    osc.stop(t0 + syl.dur + 0.03);\\n    const plosive = 'bdgpkt'.includes(syl.cons);\\n140→    const fricative = 'fsvz'.includes(syl.cons);\\n    if (plosive) noiseBurst(audioCtx, destination, t0, 0.008, 0.12);\\n    else if (fricative) noiseBurst(audioCtx, destination, t0, 0.04, 0.06);\\n  }\\n  return true;\\n}\\n\\n/** Live path. Headless and locked audio do nothing. */\\nexport function speak(ctx, text, speaker = 'ounce') {\\n  const audio = ctx?.audio;\\n150→  const audioCtx = audio?.context;\\n  if (!audioCtx) return syllabify(text, speaker);\\n  const syllables = syllabify(text, speaker);\\n  const bus = audio.buses?.sfx || audio.buses?.voice || audio.master;\\n  if (!bus) return syllables;\\n  try {\\n    renderVoice(audioCtx, bus, syllables, audioCtx.currentTime + 0.02, speaker);\\n  } catch {\\n    /* the context may be closed */\\n  }\\n160→  return syllables;\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/** Animalese. Same word, same syllables. A question rises at the end. */\\n\\nexport const SPEAKERS = {\\n  ounce: { f0: 340, rate: 13, formant: 1.25 },\\n  coach: { f0: 165, rate: 7.5, formant: 0.9, flat: true },\\n  marguerite: { f0: 230, rate: 9, formant: 1, vibrato: true },\\n  dennis: { f0: 120, rate: 11, formant: 0.95, lastUp: true },\\n  june: { f0: 300, rate: 10, formant: 1.15, flat: true },\\n  kevin: null,\\n10→};\\n\\nconst VOWELS = ['a', 'e', 'i', 'o', 'u'];\\nconst CONS = ['b', 'd', 'f', 'g', 'k', 'l', 'm', 'n', 'p', 'r', 's', 't'];\\nconst FORMANTS = {\\n  a: [800, 1200],\\n  e: [500, 1900],\\n  i: [300, 2300],\\n  o: [500, 900],\\n  u: [350, 800],\\n20→};\\n\\nfunction hash(s) {\\n  let h = 2166136261;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < s.length; i++) {\\n    h ^= s.charCodeAt(i);\\n    h = Math.imul(h, 16777619);\\n  }\\n  return h >>> 0;\\n}\\n30→\\nfunction wordShape(word) {\\n  const clean = word.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z]/g, '') || 'mm';\\n  const n = Math.max(1, Math.min(3, Math.round(clean.length / 2.5)));\\n  const syl = [];\\n  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\\n    const h = hash(`${clean}:${i}`);\\n    syl.push({ vowel: VOWELS[h % 5], cons: CONS[(h >>> 8) % CONS.length] });\\n  }\\n  return syl;\\n40→}\\n\\n/**\\n * Pure. `[{ t, dur, f0, vowel, cons, charIndex }]`.\\n * Kevin never speaks words.\\n */\\nexport function syllabify(text, speaker = 'ounce') {\\n  const spec = SPEAKERS[speaker] || SPEAKERS.ounce;\\n  if (!spec) return [];\\n  const src = String(text);\\n50→  const question = src.includes('?');\\n  const bang = src.includes('!');\\n  const slow = src.includes('...');\\n  const re = /[A-Za-z0-9']+/g;\\n  const words = [];\\n  let m;\\n  while ((m = re.exec(src))) words.push({ word: m[0], index: m.index });\\n  const shapes = words.map((w) => wordShape(w.word));\\n  const total = shapes.reduce((n, s) => n + s.length, 0) || 1;\\n  const base = 1 / spec.rate;\\n60→  const dur = base * (slow ? 1.45 : 1);\\n  const out = [];\\n  let t = 0;\\n  let seen = 0;\\n  shapes.forEach((shape, wi) => {\\n    shape.forEach((syl, si) => {\\n      const u = total <= 1 ? 0 : seen / (total - 1);\\n      let f0 = spec.f0;\\n      if (!spec.flat) f0 *= 1 - 0.15 * u;\\n      if (question && u > 0.66) f0 *= 1.25;\\n70→      if (bang && u > 0.8) f0 *= 1.15;\\n      if (spec.lastUp && wi === shapes.length - 1) f0 *= 1.08;\\n      if (spec.vibrato) f0 *= 1 + 0.03 * Math.sin(seen * 2.2);\\n      out.push({\\n        t,\\n        dur: dur * 0.92,\\n        f0,\\n        vowel: syl.vowel,\\n        cons: syl.cons,\\n        charIndex: words[wi].index,\\n80→      });\\n      t += dur;\\n      seen += 1;\\n    });\\n    t += dur * 0.35;\\n  });\\n  return out;\\n}\\n\\nfunction noiseBurst(ctx, destination, when, seconds, volume) {\\n90→  const n = Math.max(1, Math.floor(ctx.sampleRate * seconds));\\n  const buffer = ctx.createBuffer(1, n, ctx.sampleRate);\\n  const data = buffer.getChannelData(0);\\n  let s = 12345;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\\n    s = (s * 1664525 + 1013904223) >>> 0;\\n    data[i] = ((s >>> 8) / 0xffffff) * 2 - 1;\\n  }\\n  const src = ctx.createBufferSource();\\n  src.buffer = buffer;\\n100→  const g = ctx.createGain();\\n  g.gain.setValueAtTime(volume, when);\\n  g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.0001, when + seconds);\\n  src.connect(g);\\n  g.connect(destination);\\n  src.start(when);\\n  src.stop(when + seconds + 0.01);\\n}\\n\\n/** Schedule syllables onto any BaseAudioContext. No-op without one. */\\n110→export function renderVoice(audioCtx, destination, syllables, when = 0, speaker = 'ounce') {\\n  if (!audioCtx || !destination || !syllables?.length) return false;\\n  const shift = SPEAKERS[speaker]?.formant || 1;\\n  for (const syl of syllables) {\\n    const t0 = when + syl.t;\\n    const osc = audioCtx.createOscillator();\\n    osc.type = 'sawtooth';\\n    osc.frequency.setValueAtTime(Math.max(40, syl.f0), t0);\\n    const g = audioCtx.createGain();\\n    g.gain.setValueAtTime(0.0001, t0);\\n120→    g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.4, t0 + 0.006);\\n    g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.0001, t0 + Math.max(0.04, syl.dur));\\n    const low = audioCtx.createBiquadFilter();\\n    low.type = 'lowpass';\\n    low.frequency.value = Math.max(120, syl.f0 * 2);\\n    osc.connect(low);\\n    low.connect(g);\\n    const pair = FORMANTS[syl.vowel] || FORMANTS.a;\\n    for (const freq of pair) {\\n      const filter = audioCtx.createBiquadFilter();\\n130→      filter.type = 'bandpass';\\n      filter.frequency.value = Math.max(80, freq * shift);\\n      filter.Q.value = 5;\\n      osc.connect(filter);\\n      filter.connect(g);\\n    }\\n    g.connect(destination);\\n    osc.start(t0);\\n    osc.stop(t0 + syl.dur + 0.03);\\n    const plosive = 'bdgpkt'.includes(syl.cons);\\n140→    const fricative = 'fsvz'.includes(syl.cons);\\n    if (plosive) noiseBurst(audioCtx, destination, t0, 0.008, 0.12);\\n    else if (fricative) noiseBurst(audioCtx, destination, t0, 0.04, 0.06);\\n  }\\n  return true;\\n}\\n\\n/** Live path. Headless and locked audio do nothing. */\\nexport function speak(ctx, text, speaker = 'ounce') {\\n  const audio = ctx?.audio;\\n150→  const audioCtx = audio?.context;\\n  if (!audioCtx) return syllabify(text, speaker);\\n  const syllables = syllabify(text, speaker);\\n  const bus = audio.buses?.sfx || audio.buses?.voice || audio.master;\\n  if (!bus) return syllables;\\n  try {\\n    renderVoice(audioCtx, bus, syllables, audioCtx.currentTime + 0.02, speaker);\\n  } catch {\\n    /* the context may be closed */\\n  }\\n160→  return syllables;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/audio/voice.js\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":160,\"raw_output\":\"/** Animalese. Same word, same syllables. A question rises at the end. */\\n\\nexport const SPEAKERS = {\\n  ounce: { f0: 340, rate: 13, formant: 1.25 },\\n  coach: { f0: 165, rate: 7.5, formant: 0.9, flat: true },\\n  marguerite: { f0: 230, rate: 9, formant: 1, vibrato: true },\\n  dennis: { f0: 120, rate: 11, formant: 0.95, lastUp: true },\\n  june: { f0: 300, rate: 10, formant: 1.15, flat: true },\\n  kevin: null,\\n};\\n\\nconst VOWELS = ['a', 'e', 'i', 'o', 'u'];\\nconst CONS = ['b', 'd', 'f', 'g', 'k', 'l', 'm', 'n', 'p', 'r', 's', 't'];\\nconst FORMANTS = {\\n  a: [800, 1200],\\n  e: [500, 1900],\\n  i: [300, 2300],\\n  o: [500, 900],\\n  u: [350, 800],\\n};\\n\\nfunction hash(s) {\\n  let h = 2166136261;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < s.length; i++) {\\n    h ^= s.charCodeAt(i);\\n    h = Math.imul(h, 16777619);\\n  }\\n  return h >>> 0;\\n}\\n\\nfunction wordShape(word) {\\n  const clean = word.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z]/g, '') || 'mm';\\n  const n = Math.max(1, Math.min(3, Math.round(clean.length / 2.5)));\\n  const syl = [];\\n  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\\n    const h = hash(`${clean}:${i}`);\\n    syl.push({ vowel: VOWELS[h % 5], cons: CONS[(h >>> 8) % CONS.length] });\\n  }\\n  return syl;\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Pure. `[{ t, dur, f0, vowel, cons, charIndex }]`.\\n * Kevin never speaks words.\\n */\\nexport function syllabify(text, speaker = 'ounce') {\\n  const spec = SPEAKERS[speaker] || SPEAKERS.ounce;\\n  if (!spec) return [];\\n  const src = String(text);\\n  const question = src.includes('?');\\n  const bang = src.includes('!');\\n  const slow = src.includes('...');\\n  const re = /[A-Za-z0-9']+/g;\\n  const words = [];\\n  let m;\\n  while ((m = re.exec(src))) words.push({ word: m[0], index: m.index });\\n  const shapes = words.map((w) => wordShape(w.word));\\n  const total = shapes.reduce((n, s) => n + s.length, 0) || 1;\\n  const base = 1 / spec.rate;\\n  const dur = base * (slow ? 1.45 : 1);\\n  const out = [];\\n  let t = 0;\\n  let seen = 0;\\n  shapes.forEach((shape, wi) => {\\n    shape.forEach((syl, si) => {\\n      const u = total <= 1 ? 0 : seen / (total - 1);\\n      let f0 = spec.f0;\\n      if (!spec.flat) f0 *= 1 - 0.15 * u;\\n      if (question && u > 0.66) f0 *= 1.25;\\n      if (bang && u > 0.8) f0 *= 1.15;\\n      if (spec.lastUp && wi === shapes.length - 1) f0 *= 1.08;\\n      if (spec.vibrato) f0 *= 1 + 0.03 * Math.sin(seen * 2.2);\\n      out.push({\\n        t,\\n        dur: dur * 0.92,\\n        f0,\\n        vowel: syl.vowel,\\n        cons: syl.cons,\\n        charIndex: words[wi].index,\\n      });\\n      t += dur;\\n      seen += 1;\\n    });\\n    t += dur * 0.35;\\n  });\\n  return out;\\n}\\n\\nfunction noiseBurst(ctx, destination, when, seconds, volume) {\\n  const n = Math.max(1, Math.floor(ctx.sampleRate * seconds));\\n  const buffer = ctx.createBuffer(1, n, ctx.sampleRate);\\n  const data = buffer.getChannelData(0);\\n  let s = 12345;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\\n    s = (s * 1664525 + 1013904223) >>> 0;\\n    data[i] = ((s >>> 8) / 0xffffff) * 2 - 1;\\n  }\\n  const src = ctx.createBufferSource();\\n  src.buffer = buffer;\\n  const g = ctx.createGain();\\n  g.gain.setValueAtTime(volume, when);\\n  g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.0001, when + seconds);\\n  src.connect(g);\\n  g.connect(destination);\\n  src.start(when);\\n  src.stop(when + seconds + 0.01);\\n}\\n\\n/** Schedule syllables onto any BaseAudioContext. No-op without one. */\\nexport function renderVoice(audioCtx, destination, syllables, when = 0, speaker = 'ounce') {\\n  if (!audioCtx || !destination || !syllables?.length) return false;\\n  const shift = SPEAKERS[speaker]?.formant || 1;\\n  for (const syl of syllables) {\\n    const t0 = when + syl.t;\\n    const osc = audioCtx.createOscillator();\\n    osc.type = 'sawtooth';\\n    osc.frequency.setValueAtTime(Math.max(40, syl.f0), t0);\\n    const g = audioCtx.createGain();\\n    g.gain.setValueAtTime(0.0001, t0);\\n    g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.4, t0 + 0.006);\\n    g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.0001, t0 + Math.max(0.04, syl.dur));\\n    const low = audioCtx.createBiquadFilter();\\n    low.type = 'lowpass';\\n    low.frequency.value = Math.max(120, syl.f0 * 2);\\n    osc.connect(low);\\n    low.connect(g);\\n    const pair = FORMANTS[syl.vowel] || FORMANTS.a;\\n    for (const freq of pair) {\\n      const filter = audioCtx.createBiquadFilter();\\n      filter.type = 'bandpass';\\n      filter.frequency.value = Math.max(80, freq * shift);\\n      filter.Q.value = 5;\\n      osc.connect(filter);\\n      filter.connect(g);\\n    }\\n    g.connect(destination);\\n    osc.start(t0);\\n    osc.stop(t0 + syl.dur + 0.03);\\n    const plosive = 'bdgpkt'.includes(syl.cons);\\n    const fricative = 'fsvz'.includes(syl.cons);\\n    if (plosive) noiseBurst(audioCtx, destination, t0, 0.008, 0.12);\\n    else if (fricative) noiseBurst(audioCtx, destination, t0, 0.04, 0.06);\\n  }\\n  return true;\\n}\\n\\n/** Live path. Headless and locked audio do nothing. */\\nexport function speak(ctx, text, speaker = 'ounce') {\\n  const audio = ctx?.audio;\\n  const audioCtx = audio?.context;\\n  if (!audioCtx) return syllabify(text, speaker);\\n  const syllables = syllabify(text, speaker);\\n  const bus = audio.buses?.sfx || audio.buses?.voice || audio.master;\\n  if (!bus) return syllables;\\n  try {\\n    renderVoice(audioCtx, bus, syllables, audioCtx.currentTime + 0.02, speaker);\\n  } catch {\\n    /* the context may be closed */\\n  }\\n  return syllables;\\n\",\"total_lines\":161}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-3be73789-54de-49df-8b8a-5e028bd39c47-28","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→import { ACTIVITIES } from './activities.js';\\n\\n/** Samples from the plan. The bank below is extra. */\\nexport const SAMPLES = [\\n  \\\"Hello! I'm Ounce. Please step on me.\\\",\\n  'Ow.',\\n  \\\"That was a joke. I can't feel pain. I can only keep records.\\\",\\n  'How old do you feel? This is not binding.',\\n  'Your Wobble Age is 68. Is that close? No? I am so sorry.',\\n10→  'Thank you. I have written that down.',\\n  'You wobbled 14 times. I only counted the ones you noticed.',\\n  'Your left side is doing very well. I will let your right side know.',\\n  'No change since yesterday. Which is, in a way, consistent.',\\n  'Excellent. Compared to Dennis.',\\n  \\\"I'm not angry. Scales don't get angry. We get accurate.\\\",\\n  'Have you been stretching? Please do not lie. I am very sensitive.',\\n  \\\"Today's concern: your ankles. I have been concerned all night.\\\",\\n  \\\"Good morning. You look rested. I can't see. But you felt rested.\\\",\\n  'Kevin has been with us eleven years. He has never once held a pose.',\\n20→  'This is a recording. The person in it is doing better than you.',\\n  'I have been adding seven. To everyone. For years. It felt motivating.',\\n  'See you tomorrow. Bring your knees.',\\n  'You are a tree. A tree does not check its phone.',\\n  'Your left knee has wandered off. Please collect it.',\\n  'Breathe in. Not like that.',\\n  'Good. Again. That was also good. Again.',\\n  'Hold. You may blink on Thursday.',\\n  'I am eighty-one. I say this so that you feel something.',\\n  'Stillness is a muscle. So is regret. We train both here.',\\n30→  'The floor is your friend. It has never once let go.',\\n  'Both hips, new. Knee, new. Opinions, original.',\\n  'I used to do this professionally. Not this. Something near it.',\\n  \\\"It's fine. It's just the one leg.\\\",\\n  \\\"I'm pacing myself.\\\",\\n  'My gran says you are doing your best. She said it very slowly.',\\n];\\n\\nconst FIRST = {\\n  0: 'The circle was elsewhere. I wrote that down.',\\n40→  1: 'One star. A start. The file is not offended.',\\n  2: 'Two stars. I allowed a small nod.',\\n  3: 'Three stars. I will not make a fuss.',\\n};\\nconst AGAIN = {\\n  0: 'Again the circle declined. Consistent, at least.',\\n  1: 'Again, one star. We are building a habit.',\\n  2: 'Again, two stars. The file agrees with itself.',\\n  3: 'Again, three stars. Please sit before you float.',\\n};\\n50→\\nfunction pack(def) {\\n  const name = def.name;\\n  const lines = [];\\n  for (const stars of [0, 1, 2, 3]) {\\n    lines.push({ id: `${def.id}-first-${stars}`, activity: def.id, stars, repeat: false, speaker: 'ounce', text: FIRST[stars] });\\n    lines.push({ id: `${def.id}-again-${stars}`, activity: def.id, stars, repeat: true, speaker: 'ounce', text: AGAIN[stars] });\\n  }\\n  lines.push({ id: `${def.id}-enter`, activity: def.id, speaker: 'coach', text: 'Begin when the circle looks friendly.' });\\n  lines.push({ id: `${def.id}-in`, activity: def.id, speaker: 'ounce', text: 'You are in the circle. Stay, if it is convenient.' });\\n60→  lines.push({ id: `${def.id}-out`, activity: def.id, speaker: 'ounce', text: 'You have left the circle. It noticed. I noticed.' });\\n  lines.push({ id: `${def.id}-fall`, activity: def.id, speaker: 'coach', text: 'Down is a direction. We will count it once.' });\\n  lines.push({ id: `${def.id}-streak`, activity: def.id, speaker: 'ounce', text: 'Several in a row. I counted all of them.' });\\n  return lines;\\n}\\n\\nexport const LINES = ACTIVITIES.flatMap(pack);\\n\\nconst MORE = [\\n  ['ounce', 'The ferry is on time. Your knees are a separate matter.'],\\n70→  ['ounce', 'Please step on me. I have cleared my morning.'],\\n  ['coach', 'The island leans a little. So do you. We can work with that.'],\\n  ['dennis', 'The deck chair has a philosophy. I am still learning it.'],\\n  ['marguerite', 'Has anyone checked the scale? I ask as a courtesy.'],\\n  ['ounce', 'I would like to weigh in on that. No.'],\\n  ['june', 'I brought a smaller worry today. It still counts.'],\\n  ['coach', 'Hard mode is the same pose, with less forgiveness.'],\\n  ['ounce', 'The jar is filling. Sweat, in a manner of speaking.'],\\n  ['kevin', ''],\\n  ['ounce', 'Kevin sat on me. The dial read 7. We left it there.'],\\n80→  ['coach', 'Stand. The rest of the week can wait its turn.'],\\n  ['ounce', 'I have been adding seven. It felt like kindness. It was not.'],\\n  ['marguerite', 'Three stars and still no speech. Typical of a good day.'],\\n  ['dennis', 'I beat the number I feared. The number did not clap.'],\\n  ['june', 'I will take the hammock. The hammock has agreed.'],\\n  ['coach', 'Breathe out. The circle prefers you slightly smaller.'],\\n  ['ounce', 'Your chart moved. I moved it. I am sorry, and also finished.'],\\n  ['ounce', 'Week two. Same circle. Fewer surprises from me.'],\\n  ['coach', 'The plumb line is straight. The island is not. Choose.'],\\n  ['ounce', 'Drips are not a fluid. They are a compliment I can store.'],\\n90→  ['dennis', 'Last one, he said. Then he said it again. I stayed.'],\\n  ['marguerite', 'I do not chase dots. The dot, today, chased me.'],\\n  ['june', 'The vitamin knew its cup. I was only the tilt.'],\\n  ['coach', 'A coconut is not a comment. Dodge it anyway.'],\\n  ['ounce', 'The pier is a suggestion. The water is a fact.'],\\n  ['coach', 'Cadence, not hurry. The path is the same length either way.'],\\n  ['ounce', 'I kept the recording. The recording is kinder than live.'],\\n  ['coach', 'Blink if you must. The heron will pretend not to see.'],\\n  ['ounce', 'Guest three is a person. I will learn the name and then forget the panic.'],\\n];\\n100→\\nfor (const [speaker, text] of MORE) {\\n  if (!text) continue;\\n  LINES.push({ id: `more-${LINES.length}`, speaker, text, activity: null, stars: null, repeat: false });\\n}\\n\\nexport function linesFor(activity, stars, repeat) {\\n  return LINES.filter((l) => l.activity === activity && l.stars === stars && l.repeat === !!repeat);\\n}\\n\\n110→export function lineText(activity, stars, repeat) {\\n  const found = linesFor(activity, stars, repeat)[0];\\n  return found ? found.text : 'Noted.';\\n}\\n\\nexport function allLineStrings() {\\n  return [...SAMPLES, ...LINES.map((l) => l.text).filter(Boolean)];\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→import { ACTIVITIES } from './activities.js';\\n\\n/** Samples from the plan. The bank below is extra. */\\nexport const SAMPLES = [\\n  \\\"Hello! I'm Ounce. Please step on me.\\\",\\n  'Ow.',\\n  \\\"That was a joke. I can't feel pain. I can only keep records.\\\",\\n  'How old do you feel? This is not binding.',\\n  'Your Wobble Age is 68. Is that close? No? I am so sorry.',\\n10→  'Thank you. I have written that down.',\\n  'You wobbled 14 times. I only counted the ones you noticed.',\\n  'Your left side is doing very well. I will let your right side know.',\\n  'No change since yesterday. Which is, in a way, consistent.',\\n  'Excellent. Compared to Dennis.',\\n  \\\"I'm not angry. Scales don't get angry. We get accurate.\\\",\\n  'Have you been stretching? Please do not lie. I am very sensitive.',\\n  \\\"Today's concern: your ankles. I have been concerned all night.\\\",\\n  \\\"Good morning. You look rested. I can't see. But you felt rested.\\\",\\n  'Kevin has been with us eleven years. He has never once held a pose.',\\n20→  'This is a recording. The person in it is doing better than you.',\\n  'I have been adding seven. To everyone. For years. It felt motivating.',\\n  'See you tomorrow. Bring your knees.',\\n  'You are a tree. A tree does not check its phone.',\\n  'Your left knee has wandered off. Please collect it.',\\n  'Breathe in. Not like that.',\\n  'Good. Again. That was also good. Again.',\\n  'Hold. You may blink on Thursday.',\\n  'I am eighty-one. I say this so that you feel something.',\\n  'Stillness is a muscle. So is regret. We train both here.',\\n30→  'The floor is your friend. It has never once let go.',\\n  'Both hips, new. Knee, new. Opinions, original.',\\n  'I used to do this professionally. Not this. Something near it.',\\n  \\\"It's fine. It's just the one leg.\\\",\\n  \\\"I'm pacing myself.\\\",\\n  'My gran says you are doing your best. She said it very slowly.',\\n];\\n\\nconst FIRST = {\\n  0: 'The circle was elsewhere. I wrote that down.',\\n40→  1: 'One star. A start. The file is not offended.',\\n  2: 'Two stars. I allowed a small nod.',\\n  3: 'Three stars. I will not make a fuss.',\\n};\\nconst AGAIN = {\\n  0: 'Again the circle declined. Consistent, at least.',\\n  1: 'Again, one star. We are building a habit.',\\n  2: 'Again, two stars. The file agrees with itself.',\\n  3: 'Again, three stars. Please sit before you float.',\\n};\\n50→\\nfunction pack(def) {\\n  const name = def.name;\\n  const lines = [];\\n  for (const stars of [0, 1, 2, 3]) {\\n    lines.push({ id: `${def.id}-first-${stars}`, activity: def.id, stars, repeat: false, speaker: 'ounce', text: FIRST[stars] });\\n    lines.push({ id: `${def.id}-again-${stars}`, activity: def.id, stars, repeat: true, speaker: 'ounce', text: AGAIN[stars] });\\n  }\\n  lines.push({ id: `${def.id}-enter`, activity: def.id, speaker: 'coach', text: 'Begin when the circle looks friendly.' });\\n  lines.push({ id: `${def.id}-in`, activity: def.id, speaker: 'ounce', text: 'You are in the circle. Stay, if it is convenient.' });\\n60→  lines.push({ id: `${def.id}-out`, activity: def.id, speaker: 'ounce', text: 'You have left the circle. It noticed. I noticed.' });\\n  lines.push({ id: `${def.id}-fall`, activity: def.id, speaker: 'coach', text: 'Down is a direction. We will count it once.' });\\n  lines.push({ id: `${def.id}-streak`, activity: def.id, speaker: 'ounce', text: 'Several in a row. I counted all of them.' });\\n  return lines;\\n}\\n\\nexport const LINES = ACTIVITIES.flatMap(pack);\\n\\nconst MORE = [\\n  ['ounce', 'The ferry is on time. Your knees are a separate matter.'],\\n70→  ['ounce', 'Please step on me. I have cleared my morning.'],\\n  ['coach', 'The island leans a little. So do you. We can work with that.'],\\n  ['dennis', 'The deck chair has a philosophy. I am still learning it.'],\\n  ['marguerite', 'Has anyone checked the scale? I ask as a courtesy.'],\\n  ['ounce', 'I would like to weigh in on that. No.'],\\n  ['june', 'I brought a smaller worry today. It still counts.'],\\n  ['coach', 'Hard mode is the same pose, with less forgiveness.'],\\n  ['ounce', 'The jar is filling. Sweat, in a manner of speaking.'],\\n  ['kevin', ''],\\n  ['ounce', 'Kevin sat on me. The dial read 7. We left it there.'],\\n80→  ['coach', 'Stand. The rest of the week can wait its turn.'],\\n  ['ounce', 'I have been adding seven. It felt like kindness. It was not.'],\\n  ['marguerite', 'Three stars and still no speech. Typical of a good day.'],\\n  ['dennis', 'I beat the number I feared. The number did not clap.'],\\n  ['june', 'I will take the hammock. The hammock has agreed.'],\\n  ['coach', 'Breathe out. The circle prefers you slightly smaller.'],\\n  ['ounce', 'Your chart moved. I moved it. I am sorry, and also finished.'],\\n  ['ounce', 'Week two. Same circle. Fewer surprises from me.'],\\n  ['coach', 'The plumb line is straight. The island is not. Choose.'],\\n  ['ounce', 'Drips are not a fluid. They are a compliment I can store.'],\\n90→  ['dennis', 'Last one, he said. Then he said it again. I stayed.'],\\n  ['marguerite', 'I do not chase dots. The dot, today, chased me.'],\\n  ['june', 'The vitamin knew its cup. I was only the tilt.'],\\n  ['coach', 'A coconut is not a comment. Dodge it anyway.'],\\n  ['ounce', 'The pier is a suggestion. The water is a fact.'],\\n  ['coach', 'Cadence, not hurry. The path is the same length either way.'],\\n  ['ounce', 'I kept the recording. The recording is kinder than live.'],\\n  ['coach', 'Blink if you must. The heron will pretend not to see.'],\\n  ['ounce', 'Guest three is a person. I will learn the name and then forget the panic.'],\\n];\\n100→\\nfor (const [speaker, text] of MORE) {\\n  if (!text) continue;\\n  LINES.push({ id: `more-${LINES.length}`, speaker, text, activity: null, stars: null, repeat: false });\\n}\\n\\nexport function linesFor(activity, stars, repeat) {\\n  return LINES.filter((l) => l.activity === activity && l.stars === stars && l.repeat === !!repeat);\\n}\\n\\n110→export function lineText(activity, stars, repeat) {\\n  const found = linesFor(activity, stars, repeat)[0];\\n  return found ? found.text : 'Noted.';\\n}\\n\\nexport function allLineStrings() {\\n  return [...SAMPLES, ...LINES.map((l) => l.text).filter(Boolean)];\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/data/lines.js\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":130,\"raw_output\":\"import { ACTIVITIES } from './activities.js';\\n\\n/** Samples from the plan. The bank below is extra. */\\nexport const SAMPLES = [\\n  \\\"Hello! I'm Ounce. Please step on me.\\\",\\n  'Ow.',\\n  \\\"That was a joke. I can't feel pain. I can only keep records.\\\",\\n  'How old do you feel? This is not binding.',\\n  'Your Wobble Age is 68. Is that close? No? I am so sorry.',\\n  'Thank you. I have written that down.',\\n  'You wobbled 14 times. I only counted the ones you noticed.',\\n  'Your left side is doing very well. I will let your right side know.',\\n  'No change since yesterday. Which is, in a way, consistent.',\\n  'Excellent. Compared to Dennis.',\\n  \\\"I'm not angry. Scales don't get angry. We get accurate.\\\",\\n  'Have you been stretching? Please do not lie. I am very sensitive.',\\n  \\\"Today's concern: your ankles. I have been concerned all night.\\\",\\n  \\\"Good morning. You look rested. I can't see. But you felt rested.\\\",\\n  'Kevin has been with us eleven years. He has never once held a pose.',\\n  'This is a recording. The person in it is doing better than you.',\\n  'I have been adding seven. To everyone. For years. It felt motivating.',\\n  'See you tomorrow. Bring your knees.',\\n  'You are a tree. A tree does not check its phone.',\\n  'Your left knee has wandered off. Please collect it.',\\n  'Breathe in. Not like that.',\\n  'Good. Again. That was also good. Again.',\\n  'Hold. You may blink on Thursday.',\\n  'I am eighty-one. I say this so that you feel something.',\\n  'Stillness is a muscle. So is regret. We train both here.',\\n  'The floor is your friend. It has never once let go.',\\n  'Both hips, new. Knee, new. Opinions, original.',\\n  'I used to do this professionally. Not this. Something near it.',\\n  \\\"It's fine. It's just the one leg.\\\",\\n  \\\"I'm pacing myself.\\\",\\n  'My gran says you are doing your best. She said it very slowly.',\\n];\\n\\nconst FIRST = {\\n  0: 'The circle was elsewhere. I wrote that down.',\\n  1: 'One star. A start. The file is not offended.',\\n  2: 'Two stars. I allowed a small nod.',\\n  3: 'Three stars. I will not make a fuss.',\\n};\\nconst AGAIN = {\\n  0: 'Again the circle declined. Consistent, at least.',\\n  1: 'Again, one star. We are building a habit.',\\n  2: 'Again, two stars. The file agrees with itself.',\\n  3: 'Again, three stars. Please sit before you float.',\\n};\\n\\nfunction pack(def) {\\n  const name = def.name;\\n  const lines = [];\\n  for (const stars of [0, 1, 2, 3]) {\\n    lines.push({ id: `${def.id}-first-${stars}`, activity: def.id, stars, repeat: false, speaker: 'ounce', text: FIRST[stars] });\\n    lines.push({ id: `${def.id}-again-${stars}`, activity: def.id, stars, repeat: true, speaker: 'ounce', text: AGAIN[stars] });\\n  }\\n  lines.push({ id: `${def.id}-enter`, activity: def.id, speaker: 'coach', text: 'Begin when the circle looks friendly.' });\\n  lines.push({ id: `${def.id}-in`, activity: def.id, speaker: 'ounce', text: 'You are in the circle. Stay, if it is convenient.' });\\n  lines.push({ id: `${def.id}-out`, activity: def.id, speaker: 'ounce', text: 'You have left the circle. It noticed. I noticed.' });\\n  lines.push({ id: `${def.id}-fall`, activity: def.id, speaker: 'coach', text: 'Down is a direction. We will count it once.' });\\n  lines.push({ id: `${def.id}-streak`, activity: def.id, speaker: 'ounce', text: 'Several in a row. I counted all of them.' });\\n  return lines;\\n}\\n\\nexport const LINES = ACTIVITIES.flatMap(pack);\\n\\nconst MORE = [\\n  ['ounce', 'The ferry is on time. Your knees are a separate matter.'],\\n  ['ounce', 'Please step on me. I have cleared my morning.'],\\n  ['coach', 'The island leans a little. So do you. We can work with that.'],\\n  ['dennis', 'The deck chair has a philosophy. I am still learning it.'],\\n  ['marguerite', 'Has anyone checked the scale? I ask as a courtesy.'],\\n  ['ounce', 'I would like to weigh in on that. No.'],\\n  ['june', 'I brought a smaller worry today. It still counts.'],\\n  ['coach', 'Hard mode is the same pose, with less forgiveness.'],\\n  ['ounce', 'The jar is filling. Sweat, in a manner of speaking.'],\\n  ['kevin', ''],\\n  ['ounce', 'Kevin sat on me. The dial read 7. We left it there.'],\\n  ['coach', 'Stand. The rest of the week can wait its turn.'],\\n  ['ounce', 'I have been adding seven. It felt like kindness. It was not.'],\\n  ['marguerite', 'Three stars and still no speech. Typical of a good day.'],\\n  ['dennis', 'I beat the number I feared. The number did not clap.'],\\n  ['june', 'I will take the hammock. The hammock has agreed.'],\\n  ['coach', 'Breathe out. The circle prefers you slightly smaller.'],\\n  ['ounce', 'Your chart moved. I moved it. I am sorry, and also finished.'],\\n  ['ounce', 'Week two. Same circle. Fewer surprises from me.'],\\n  ['coach', 'The plumb line is straight. The island is not. Choose.'],\\n  ['ounce', 'Drips are not a fluid. They are a compliment I can store.'],\\n  ['dennis', 'Last one, he said. Then he said it again. I stayed.'],\\n  ['marguerite', 'I do not chase dots. The dot, today, chased me.'],\\n  ['june', 'The vitamin knew its cup. I was only the tilt.'],\\n  ['coach', 'A coconut is not a comment. Dodge it anyway.'],\\n  ['ounce', 'The pier is a suggestion. The water is a fact.'],\\n  ['coach', 'Cadence, not hurry. The path is the same length either way.'],\\n  ['ounce', 'I kept the recording. The recording is kinder than live.'],\\n  ['coach', 'Blink if you must. The heron will pretend not to see.'],\\n  ['ounce', 'Guest three is a person. I will learn the name and then forget the panic.'],\\n];\\n\\nfor (const [speaker, text] of MORE) {\\n  if (!text) continue;\\n  LINES.push({ id: `more-${LINES.length}`, speaker, text, activity: null, stars: null, repeat: false });\\n}\\n\\nexport function linesFor(activity, stars, repeat) {\\n  return LINES.filter((l) => l.activity === activity && l.stars === stars && l.repeat === !!repeat);\\n}\\n\\nexport function lineText(activity, stars, repeat) {\\n  const found = linesFor(activity, stars, repeat)[0];\\n  return found ? found.text : 'Noted.';\\n}\\n\\nexport function allLineStrings() {\\n  return [...SAMPLES, ...LINES.map((l) => l.text).filter(Boolean)];\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":117}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"b53d6c1f-a0ee-411a-871f-e179726fd0e8"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_100","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The grep for .d.ts files returned no matches.\n\nThe missing file may be large or at the wrong path. I will read pixel-engine.d.ts and session.js directly instead.\n\nI have a six-step plan for the game:\n- Write about.js with placeholder feedback\n- Build app.js as a state machine\n- Create scenes/world.js for the main Game\n- Write main.js\n- Add tools/build.mjs, test.mjs, and shot.mjs\n- Generate creditsText.js","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b499dfa9-6daa-4e1c-a997-9893ab839b1e-29","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/examples/top-down.js","limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b499dfa9-6daa-4e1c-a997-9893ab839b1e-30","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/vendor/hub/session.js","limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b499dfa9-6daa-4e1c-a997-9893ab839b1e-31","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/audio/sfx.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b499dfa9-6daa-4e1c-a997-9893ab839b1e-32","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/art/models.js","limit":50}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8704,"output_tokens":661,"cache_read_input_tokens":73728,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"c80641dc-b9d6-48c8-9c6b-bc926bd9f275"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-b499dfa9-6daa-4e1c-a997-9893ab839b1e-29","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→// Lantern Night: walk (WASD / arrows), push both crates onto the glowing pads (walk into a\\n// crate to push it), then leave through the gate in the north wall.\\nimport { compileClips, ContactShadow, Engine, HERO_CLIPS, HERO_MODEL, HERO_RIG, LOOK_PRESETS, mergeStaticMeshes, PALETTE, PlatformerCharacter, RAPIER, readMoveInput, setLookLayer, THREE, toonMaterial, withUrlOptions } from '../pixel-engine.js';\\n\\nconst { BoxGeometry, Color, CylinderGeometry, Mesh, Vector3 } = THREE;\\n\\nconst SONG = {\\n  bpm: 84,\\n  tracks: { lead: { wave: 'triangle', decay: 0.3, volume: 0.12 }, bass: { wave: 'square', duty: 0.125, decay: 0.25, volume: 0.05 } },\\n10→  patterns: { a: { lead: 'A4 . C5 . E5 . . . D5 . C5 . B4 . . .', bass: 'A2 . . . . . . . F2 . . . . . . .' } },\\n  order: ['a'],\\n};\\nconst PADS = [[-3, -4], [3, -4]];\\nconst CRATES = [[-3, 1], [3, 1]];\\n\\nclass LanternNight {\\n  name = 'Lantern Night';\\n  assets = [HERO_MODEL, 'assets/tree.glb'];\\n  crates = [];\\n20→  pads = [];\\n  solved = false;\\n  escaped = false;\\n  nextFirefly = 0;\\n  target = new Vector3();\\n  at = new Vector3();\\n\\n  async setup(ctx) {\\n    const { scene, physics, palette, engine } = ctx;\\n    this.sparkle = ctx.random.fork('fireflies'); // drawn per frame (cosmetic): its own stream, so gameplay's never depends on the frame rate\\n30→    // Night: dim the engine's sun and ambient light (reset for the next game on unload).\\n    engine.sun.color.setHex(PALETTE.sky);\\n    engine.sun.intensity = 1.2;\\n    engine.ambient.color.setHex(PALETTE.navy);\\n    engine.ambient.intensity = 1.4;\\n    scene.background = new Color(PALETTE.ink);\\n\\n    const parts = [];\\n    const wall = (x, z, w, d) => {\\n      physics.addStaticBox({ position: [x, 0.6, z], halfExtents: [w / 2, 0.6, d / 2] });\\n40→      const m = new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(w, 1.2, d), toonMaterial(palette.slate));\\n      m.position.set(x, 0.6, z);\\n      m.castShadow = m.receiveShadow = true;\\n      parts.push(m);\\n    };\\n    const floor = new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(30, 1, 30), toonMaterial(palette.teal));\\n    floor.position.y = -0.5;\\n    floor.receiveShadow = true;\\n    parts.push(floor);\\n    physics.addStaticBox({ position: [0, -0.5, 0], halfExtents: [15, 0.5, 15] });\\n50→    wall(-4.75, -8, 6.5, 1); // north wall, with a 3 m gap for the gate\\n    wall(4.75, -8, 6.5, 1);\\n    wall(0, 8, 17, 1);\\n    wall(-8, 0, 1, 15);\\n    wall(8, 0, 1, 15);\\n    for (const [x, z] of [[-6.5, -6.5], [6.5, -6.5], [-6.5, 6.5], [6.5, 6.5]]) {\\n      const post = new Mesh(new CylinderGeometry(0.12, 0.15, 1.6, 6), toonMaterial(palette.plum));\\n      post.position.set(x, 0.8, z);\\n      parts.push(post);\\n      ctx.lights.request({ position: [x, 1.8, z], color: 0xffa040, intensity: 7, radius: 7, flicker: 'torch' });\\n60→    }\\n    scene.add(...mergeStaticMeshes(parts));\\n\\n    // The gate: a collider we remove when the puzzle is solved.\\n    this.gate = new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(3, 1.6, 0.6), toonMaterial(palette.red));\\n    this.gate.position.set(0, 0.8, -8);\\n    scene.add(this.gate);\\n    this.gateCollider = physics.addStaticBox({ position: [0, 0.8, -8], halfExtents: [1.5, 0.8, 0.3] });\\n    physics.trigger({ box: [1.5, 1, 0.5] }, [0, 1, -9.2], { tag: 'character', once: true, onEnter: () => this.escape(ctx) });\\n\\n70→    // Pads and crates. A crate is a dynamic Rapier body the hero pushes (tag 'pushable').\\n    for (const [x, z] of PADS) {\\n      const mesh = new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(1.2, 0.06, 1.2), toonMaterial(palette.navy));\\n      mesh.position.set(x, 0.03, z);\\n      scene.add(mesh);\\n      this.pads.push({ x, z, mesh, lit: false });\\n    }\\n    for (const [x, z] of CRATES) {\\n      const mesh = new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(0.98, 0.98, 0.98), toonMaterial(palette.orange));\\n      mesh.castShadow = mesh.receiveShadow = true;\\n80→      setLookLayer(mesh, 'actors');\\n      scene.add(mesh);\\n      const body = physics.world.createRigidBody(RAPIER.RigidBodyDesc.dynamic().setTranslation(x, 0.5, z).setLinearDamping(4).enabledRotations(false, false, false));\\n      physics.tag(physics.world.createCollider(RAPIER.ColliderDesc.cuboid(0.49, 0.49, 0.49).setFriction(0.1).setDensity(8), body), 'pushable');\\n      physics.bind(body, mesh);\\n      this.crates.push(body);\\n    }\\n\\n    const tree = await ctx.loadModel('assets/tree.glb');\\n    for (let i = 0; i < 14; i++) {\\n90→      const a = (i / 14) * Math.PI * 2;\\n      const t = tree.scene.clone(true);\\n      t.position.set(Math.cos(a) * 11.5, 0, Math.sin(a) * 11.5);\\n      scene.add(t);\\n    }\\n\\n    const hero = await ctx.loadModel(HERO_MODEL, { castShadow: false });\\n    this.model = hero.scene;\\n    setLookLayer(this.model, 'actors');\\n    this.shadow = new ContactShadow(0.42);\\n100→    scene.add(this.model, this.shadow);\\n    this.hero = new PlatformerCharacter(physics, { position: [0, 0, 5], lockDepth: ctx.camera.lockDepth });\\n    this.hero.attachModel(this.model, compileClips(HERO_CLIPS, HERO_RIG, this.model), HERO_RIG);\\n    ctx.lights.request({ follow: this.model, offset: [0, 1.5, 0], color: 0xffe0a0, intensity: 5, radius: 6, priority: 8 }); // the lantern\\n\\n    ctx.particles.register('firefly', { count: [1, 1], life: [1.5, 2.5], speed: [0.2, 0.5], gravity: -0.2, size: [1, 1], colors: ['lime', 'sand', 'lime'] });\\n    ctx.audio.register('chime', { wave: 'triangle', freq: 880, decay: 0.4, volume: 0.3, arp: [0, 4, 7], arpRate: 0.06 });\\n    ctx.audio.playMusic(SONG, 'night');\\n  }\\n\\n110→  escape(ctx) {\\n    this.escaped = true;\\n    this.hero.celebrate();\\n    ctx.audio.play('fanfare');\\n  }\\n\\n  fixedUpdate(ctx, dt) {\\n    this.input = readMoveInput(ctx, this.hero, this.input);\\n    if (this.escaped) this.input.move.set(0, 0, 0); // the end: stand and celebrate\\n    this.hero.fixedUpdate(dt, this.input);\\n120→  }\",\"content_concise\":\"1→// Lantern Night: walk (WASD / arrows), push both crates onto the glowing pads (walk into a\\n// crate to push it), then leave through the gate in the north wall.\\nimport { compileClips, ContactShadow, Engine, HERO_CLIPS, HERO_MODEL, HERO_RIG, LOOK_PRESETS, mergeStaticMeshes, PALETTE, PlatformerCharacter, RAPIER, readMoveInput, setLookLayer, THREE, toonMaterial, withUrlOptions } from '../pixel-engine.js';\\n\\nconst { BoxGeometry, Color, CylinderGeometry, Mesh, Vector3 } = THREE;\\n\\nconst SONG = {\\n  bpm: 84,\\n  tracks: { lead: { wave: 'triangle', decay: 0.3, volume: 0.12 }, bass: { wave: 'square', duty: 0.125, decay: 0.25, volume: 0.05 } },\\n10→  patterns: { a: { lead: 'A4 . C5 . E5 . . . D5 . C5 . B4 . . .', bass: 'A2 . . . . . . . F2 . . . . . . .' } },\\n  order: ['a'],\\n};\\nconst PADS = [[-3, -4], [3, -4]];\\nconst CRATES = [[-3, 1], [3, 1]];\\n\\nclass LanternNight {\\n  name = 'Lantern Night';\\n  assets = [HERO_MODEL, 'assets/tree.glb'];\\n  crates = [];\\n20→  pads = [];\\n  solved = false;\\n  escaped = false;\\n  nextFirefly = 0;\\n  target = new Vector3();\\n  at = new Vector3();\\n\\n  async setup(ctx) {\\n    const { scene, physics, palette, engine } = ctx;\\n    this.sparkle = ctx.random.fork('fireflies'); // drawn per frame (cosmetic): its own stream, so gameplay's never depends on the frame rate\\n30→    // Night: dim the engine's sun and ambient light (reset for the next game on unload).\\n    engine.sun.color.setHex(PALETTE.sky);\\n    engine.sun.intensity = 1.2;\\n    engine.ambient.color.setHex(PALETTE.navy);\\n    engine.ambient.intensity = 1.4;\\n    scene.background = new Color(PALETTE.ink);\\n\\n    const parts = [];\\n    const wall = (x, z, w, d) => {\\n      physics.addStaticBox({ position: [x, 0.6, z], halfExtents: [w / 2, 0.6, d / 2] });\\n40→      const m = new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(w, 1.2, d), toonMaterial(palette.slate));\\n      m.position.set(x, 0.6, z);\\n      m.castShadow = m.receiveShadow = true;\\n      parts.push(m);\\n    };\\n    const floor = new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(30, 1, 30), toonMaterial(palette.teal));\\n    floor.position.y = -0.5;\\n    floor.receiveShadow = true;\\n    parts.push(floor);\\n    physics.addStaticBox({ position: [0, -0.5, 0], halfExtents: [15, 0.5, 15] });\\n50→    wall(-4.75, -8, 6.5, 1); // north wall, with a 3 m gap for the gate\\n    wall(4.75, -8, 6.5, 1);\\n    wall(0, 8, 17, 1);\\n    wall(-8, 0, 1, 15);\\n    wall(8, 0, 1, 15);\\n    for (const [x, z] of [[-6.5, -6.5], [6.5, -6.5], [-6.5, 6.5], [6.5, 6.5]]) {\\n      const post = new Mesh(new CylinderGeometry(0.12, 0.15, 1.6, 6), toonMaterial(palette.plum));\\n      post.position.set(x, 0.8, z);\\n      parts.push(post);\\n      ctx.lights.request({ position: [x, 1.8, z], color: 0xffa040, intensity: 7, radius: 7, flicker: 'torch' });\\n60→    }\\n    scene.add(...mergeStaticMeshes(parts));\\n\\n    // The gate: a collider we remove when the puzzle is solved.\\n    this.gate = new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(3, 1.6, 0.6), toonMaterial(palette.red));\\n    this.gate.position.set(0, 0.8, -8);\\n    scene.add(this.gate);\\n    this.gateCollider = physics.addStaticBox({ position: [0, 0.8, -8], halfExtents: [1.5, 0.8, 0.3] });\\n    physics.trigger({ box: [1.5, 1, 0.5] }, [0, 1, -9.2], { tag: 'character', once: true, onEnter: () => this.escape(ctx) });\\n\\n70→    // Pads and crates. A crate is a dynamic Rapier body the hero pushes (tag 'pushable').\\n    for (const [x, z] of PADS) {\\n      const mesh = new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(1.2, 0.06, 1.2), toonMaterial(palette.navy));\\n      mesh.position.set(x, 0.03, z);\\n      scene.add(mesh);\\n      this.pads.push({ x, z, mesh, lit: false });\\n    }\\n    for (const [x, z] of CRATES) {\\n      const mesh = new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(0.98, 0.98, 0.98), toonMaterial(palette.orange));\\n      mesh.castShadow = mesh.receiveShadow = true;\\n80→      setLookLayer(mesh, 'actors');\\n      scene.add(mesh);\\n      const body = physics.world.createRigidBody(RAPIER.RigidBodyDesc.dynamic().setTranslation(x, 0.5, z).setLinearDamping(4).enabledRotations(false, false, false));\\n      physics.tag(physics.world.createCollider(RAPIER.ColliderDesc.cuboid(0.49, 0.49, 0.49).setFriction(0.1).setDensity(8), body), 'pushable');\\n      physics.bind(body, mesh);\\n      this.crates.push(body);\\n    }\\n\\n    const tree = await ctx.loadModel('assets/tree.glb');\\n    for (let i = 0; i < 14; i++) {\\n90→      const a = (i / 14) * Math.PI * 2;\\n      const t = tree.scene.clone(true);\\n      t.position.set(Math.cos(a) * 11.5, 0, Math.sin(a) * 11.5);\\n      scene.add(t);\\n    }\\n\\n    const hero = await ctx.loadModel(HERO_MODEL, { castShadow: false });\\n    this.model = hero.scene;\\n    setLookLayer(this.model, 'actors');\\n    this.shadow = new ContactShadow(0.42);\\n100→    scene.add(this.model, this.shadow);\\n    this.hero = new PlatformerCharacter(physics, { position: [0, 0, 5], lockDepth: ctx.camera.lockDepth });\\n    this.hero.attachModel(this.model, compileClips(HERO_CLIPS, HERO_RIG, this.model), HERO_RIG);\\n    ctx.lights.request({ follow: this.model, offset: [0, 1.5, 0], color: 0xffe0a0, intensity: 5, radius: 6, priority: 8 }); // the lantern\\n\\n    ctx.particles.register('firefly', { count: [1, 1], life: [1.5, 2.5], speed: [0.2, 0.5], gravity: -0.2, size: [1, 1], colors: ['lime', 'sand', 'lime'] });\\n    ctx.audio.register('chime', { wave: 'triangle', freq: 880, decay: 0.4, volume: 0.3, arp: [0, 4, 7], arpRate: 0.06 });\\n    ctx.audio.playMusic(SONG, 'night');\\n  }\\n\\n110→  escape(ctx) {\\n    this.escaped = true;\\n    this.hero.celebrate();\\n    ctx.audio.play('fanfare');\\n  }\\n\\n  fixedUpdate(ctx, dt) {\\n    this.input = readMoveInput(ctx, this.hero, this.input);\\n    if (this.escaped) this.input.move.set(0, 0, 0); // the end: stand and celebrate\\n    this.hero.fixedUpdate(dt, this.input);\\n120→  }\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/examples/top-down.js\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":120,\"raw_output\":\"// Lantern Night: walk (WASD / arrows), push both crates onto the glowing pads (walk into a\\n// crate to push it), then leave through the gate in the north wall.\\nimport { compileClips, ContactShadow, Engine, HERO_CLIPS, HERO_MODEL, HERO_RIG, LOOK_PRESETS, mergeStaticMeshes, PALETTE, PlatformerCharacter, RAPIER, readMoveInput, setLookLayer, THREE, toonMaterial, withUrlOptions } from '../pixel-engine.js';\\n\\nconst { BoxGeometry, Color, CylinderGeometry, Mesh, Vector3 } = THREE;\\n\\nconst SONG = {\\n  bpm: 84,\\n  tracks: { lead: { wave: 'triangle', decay: 0.3, volume: 0.12 }, bass: { wave: 'square', duty: 0.125, decay: 0.25, volume: 0.05 } },\\n  patterns: { a: { lead: 'A4 . C5 . E5 . . . D5 . C5 . B4 . . .', bass: 'A2 . . . . . . . F2 . . . . . . .' } },\\n  order: ['a'],\\n};\\nconst PADS = [[-3, -4], [3, -4]];\\nconst CRATES = [[-3, 1], [3, 1]];\\n\\nclass LanternNight {\\n  name = 'Lantern Night';\\n  assets = [HERO_MODEL, 'assets/tree.glb'];\\n  crates = [];\\n  pads = [];\\n  solved = false;\\n  escaped = false;\\n  nextFirefly = 0;\\n  target = new Vector3();\\n  at = new Vector3();\\n\\n  async setup(ctx) {\\n    const { scene, physics, palette, engine } = ctx;\\n    this.sparkle = ctx.random.fork('fireflies'); // drawn per frame (cosmetic): its own stream, so gameplay's never depends on the frame rate\\n    // Night: dim the engine's sun and ambient light (reset for the next game on unload).\\n    engine.sun.color.setHex(PALETTE.sky);\\n    engine.sun.intensity = 1.2;\\n    engine.ambient.color.setHex(PALETTE.navy);\\n    engine.ambient.intensity = 1.4;\\n    scene.background = new Color(PALETTE.ink);\\n\\n    const parts = [];\\n    const wall = (x, z, w, d) => {\\n      physics.addStaticBox({ position: [x, 0.6, z], halfExtents: [w / 2, 0.6, d / 2] });\\n      const m = new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(w, 1.2, d), toonMaterial(palette.slate));\\n      m.position.set(x, 0.6, z);\\n      m.castShadow = m.receiveShadow = true;\\n      parts.push(m);\\n    };\\n    const floor = new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(30, 1, 30), toonMaterial(palette.teal));\\n    floor.position.y = -0.5;\\n    floor.receiveShadow = true;\\n    parts.push(floor);\\n    physics.addStaticBox({ position: [0, -0.5, 0], halfExtents: [15, 0.5, 15] });\\n    wall(-4.75, -8, 6.5, 1); // north wall, with a 3 m gap for the gate\\n    wall(4.75, -8, 6.5, 1);\\n    wall(0, 8, 17, 1);\\n    wall(-8, 0, 1, 15);\\n    wall(8, 0, 1, 15);\\n    for (const [x, z] of [[-6.5, -6.5], [6.5, -6.5], [-6.5, 6.5], [6.5, 6.5]]) {\\n      const post = new Mesh(new CylinderGeometry(0.12, 0.15, 1.6, 6), toonMaterial(palette.plum));\\n      post.position.set(x, 0.8, z);\\n      parts.push(post);\\n      ctx.lights.request({ position: [x, 1.8, z], color: 0xffa040, intensity: 7, radius: 7, flicker: 'torch' });\\n    }\\n    scene.add(...mergeStaticMeshes(parts));\\n\\n    // The gate: a collider we remove when the puzzle is solved.\\n    this.gate = new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(3, 1.6, 0.6), toonMaterial(palette.red));\\n    this.gate.position.set(0, 0.8, -8);\\n    scene.add(this.gate);\\n    this.gateCollider = physics.addStaticBox({ position: [0, 0.8, -8], halfExtents: [1.5, 0.8, 0.3] });\\n    physics.trigger({ box: [1.5, 1, 0.5] }, [0, 1, -9.2], { tag: 'character', once: true, onEnter: () => this.escape(ctx) });\\n\\n    // Pads and crates. A crate is a dynamic Rapier body the hero pushes (tag 'pushable').\\n    for (const [x, z] of PADS) {\\n      const mesh = new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(1.2, 0.06, 1.2), toonMaterial(palette.navy));\\n      mesh.position.set(x, 0.03, z);\\n      scene.add(mesh);\\n      this.pads.push({ x, z, mesh, lit: false });\\n    }\\n    for (const [x, z] of CRATES) {\\n      const mesh = new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(0.98, 0.98, 0.98), toonMaterial(palette.orange));\\n      mesh.castShadow = mesh.receiveShadow = true;\\n      setLookLayer(mesh, 'actors');\\n      scene.add(mesh);\\n      const body = physics.world.createRigidBody(RAPIER.RigidBodyDesc.dynamic().setTranslation(x, 0.5, z).setLinearDamping(4).enabledRotations(false, false, false));\\n      physics.tag(physics.world.createCollider(RAPIER.ColliderDesc.cuboid(0.49, 0.49, 0.49).setFriction(0.1).setDensity(8), body), 'pushable');\\n      physics.bind(body, mesh);\\n      this.crates.push(body);\\n    }\\n\\n    const tree = await ctx.loadModel('assets/tree.glb');\\n    for (let i = 0; i < 14; i++) {\\n      const a = (i / 14) * Math.PI * 2;\\n      const t = tree.scene.clone(true);\\n      t.position.set(Math.cos(a) * 11.5, 0, Math.sin(a) * 11.5);\\n      scene.add(t);\\n    }\\n\\n    const hero = await ctx.loadModel(HERO_MODEL, { castShadow: false });\\n    this.model = hero.scene;\\n    setLookLayer(this.model, 'actors');\\n    this.shadow = new ContactShadow(0.42);\\n    scene.add(this.model, this.shadow);\\n    this.hero = new PlatformerCharacter(physics, { position: [0, 0, 5], lockDepth: ctx.camera.lockDepth });\\n    this.hero.attachModel(this.model, compileClips(HERO_CLIPS, HERO_RIG, this.model), HERO_RIG);\\n    ctx.lights.request({ follow: this.model, offset: [0, 1.5, 0], color: 0xffe0a0, intensity: 5, radius: 6, priority: 8 }); // the lantern\\n\\n    ctx.particles.register('firefly', { count: [1, 1], life: [1.5, 2.5], speed: [0.2, 0.5], gravity: -0.2, size: [1, 1], colors: ['lime', 'sand', 'lime'] });\\n    ctx.audio.register('chime', { wave: 'triangle', freq: 880, decay: 0.4, volume: 0.3, arp: [0, 4, 7], arpRate: 0.06 });\\n    ctx.audio.playMusic(SONG, 'night');\\n  }\\n\\n  escape(ctx) {\\n    this.escaped = true;\\n    this.hero.celebrate();\\n    ctx.audio.play('fanfare');\\n  }\\n\\n  fixedUpdate(ctx, dt) {\\n    this.input = readMoveInput(ctx, this.hero, this.input);\\n    if (this.escaped) this.input.move.set(0, 0, 0); // the end: stand and celebrate\\n    this.hero.fixedUpdate(dt, this.input);\\n  }\\n\",\"total_lines\":162}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-b499dfa9-6daa-4e1c-a997-9893ab839b1e-30","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\\n(function (root) {\\n  'use strict';\\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\\n\\n  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\\n  var PROGRESS_EVERY_MS = 1000;\\n10→  /** The hub's welcome may change these; a newer hub never needs a newer copy of this file for it. */\\n  var limits = { maxBytes: 16384, ratePerS: 20, burst: 40 };\\n\\n  var framed = false;\\n  try {\\n    framed = root.parent && root.parent !== root;\\n  } catch (e) {\\n    framed = true;\\n  }\\n  var search = String(root.location && root.location.search);\\n20→  var flagged = /[?&]aihub=/.test(search);\\n  var seedArg = /[?&]aihub-seed=(\\\\d+)/.exec(search);\\n\\n  var hub = {\\n    version: VERSION,\\n    protocol: 1,\\n    /** True when the hub launched this page for a session (?aihub=1 inside a frame). */\\n    active: !!(flagged && framed),\\n    me: null,\\n    host: null,\\n30→    isHost: false,\\n    players: [],\\n    mode: null,\\n    seed: 0,\\n    limitMs: 0,\\n    round: 0,\\n    /** True when the hub shows the round's splash and collects every player's ready: call ready() once loaded, with no prompt. */\\n    splash: false,\\n    /** True when the hub seeded Math.random for this round (side by side): every copy draws the same numbers. */\\n    seeded: false,\\n40→  };\\n\\n  /** A storage that lives and dies with the page: the Storage methods, and items as properties too. */\\n  function memoryStorage() {\\n    var data = Object.create(null);\\n    var api = {\\n      getItem: function (k) {\\n        k = String(k);\\n        return k in data ? data[k] : null;\\n      },\\n50→      setItem: function (k, v) {\\n        data[String(k)] = String(v);\\n      },\\n      removeItem: function (k) {\\n        delete data[String(k)];\\n      },\\n      clear: function () {\\n        for (var k in data) delete data[k];\\n      },\\n      key: function (i) {\\n60→        var keys = Object.keys(data);\\n        return i >= 0 && i < keys.length ? keys[i] : null;\\n      },\\n    };\\n    if (typeof Proxy !== 'function') return api;\\n    return new Proxy(api, {\\n      get: function (t, k) {\\n        if (k === 'length') return Object.keys(data).length;\\n        if (typeof k === 'symbol' || k in t) return t[k];\\n        return k in data ? data[k] : undefined;\\n70→      },\\n      set: function (t, k, v) {\\n        if (typeof k !== 'symbol') data[k] = String(v);\\n        return true;\\n      },\\n      has: function (t, k) {\\n        return k in data || k in t;\\n      },\\n      deleteProperty: function (t, k) {\\n        delete data[k];\\n80→        return true;\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\\n(function (root) {\\n  'use strict';\\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\\n\\n  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\\n  var PROGRESS_EVERY_MS = 1000;\\n10→  /** The hub's welcome may change these; a newer hub never needs a newer copy of this file for it. */\\n  var limits = { maxBytes: 16384, ratePerS: 20, burst: 40 };\\n\\n  var framed = false;\\n  try {\\n    framed = root.parent && root.parent !== root;\\n  } catch (e) {\\n    framed = true;\\n  }\\n  var search = String(root.location && root.location.search);\\n20→  var flagged = /[?&]aihub=/.test(search);\\n  var seedArg = /[?&]aihub-seed=(\\\\d+)/.exec(search);\\n\\n  var hub = {\\n    version: VERSION,\\n    protocol: 1,\\n    /** True when the hub launched this page for a session (?aihub=1 inside a frame). */\\n    active: !!(flagged && framed),\\n    me: null,\\n    host: null,\\n30→