{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_107","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Audio settings are saved to localStorage.\n\nThe game will read its own volume settings on boot and call setVolume to override any shared engine values. If no game-specific save exists, music defaults to 0.10.\n\nValidation will run in parallel with writing code. A script will validate model, clip, and song assets. Tree, heron, and plank clips lack placeFeet but were already verified. analyzeClip needs a loaded hero model and Engine.headless setup. A node script will generate creditsText.js.\n\napp.js will contain the main game logic, while draw logic stays in world.js. Menu input will use wasPressed to ensure one action per frame and avoid double-firing.\n\nKeyE will not be used as a menu confirm key during name entry to avoid typing the letter 'e'. Only Enter, Space, PadCross, and MouseLeft will confirm selections.\n\nMenu rows will be tracked as widgets with IDs like `row-${id}`. Pointer position will be mapped to art pixels to detect hover over a row. Clicking a hovered row confirms that selection.\n\nMouse movement will only register when the pointer delta exceeds two pixels.\n\nBrowser tests will move the mouse to test hover. Headless hover tests run in the browser suite.\n\nClicking a focused row with MouseLeft activates it.\n\nThe prompt text changes based on input method. PadCross shows PlayStation glyphs and \"Cross Confirm\". Xbox glyphs show \"A Confirm\". Key presses show \"Enter\". Mouse movement shows \"Click\".\n\nPhone mode will be detected at boot via a touch-only check passed to App. The engine runs in manual step mode during tests, so the browser suite can advance time with `__PIXEL_ENGINE__.step(700)` after loading. Family hour mode will use two stub pads plus a keyboard, with three lanes moving simultaneously.\n\nGamepad stubs will provide two pads in the browser and Node tests. The join screen requires pressing button 0 on each pad or Enter for the keyboard, then Start, followed by axes.\n\nFor the three-lane movement, lane.x will track each character's lean position updated each frame from input.x. After several frames with different inputs, the lanes will diverge from one another. The header and medley will use a simulation dot or position field.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-fe863941-99f5-4da6-8dfd-62a3c9424ad8-51","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"__hubCheck|ready\\(|progress|time-up|dataset.complete|fail\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/vendor/hub","glob":"*.{js,html,md}"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-fe863941-99f5-4da6-8dfd-62a3c9424ad8-52","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/types/engine/audio/AudioManager.d.ts","offset":1,"limit":90}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2168,"output_tokens":1338,"cache_read_input_tokens":117632,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"bfac3c7a-d2ec-410d-b6ab-2065c8c7482f"}
