plitFilters,Mge as springPad,Rme as spriteSheet,NY as storeSettings,Y6 as swayMaterial,vve as swayObject,Y as textureDef,n4 as textureMap,Cge as textureSheet,WG as toonGradient,XG as toonMaterial,$G as toonify,ive as turtle,Zye as twoBoneIK,PY as urlSettings,wye as validateClip,b3 as validateModel,B3 as validateTexture,_G as variantName,g6 as waterHeight,sde as withUrlOptions,W_e as woodMaterial};\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"command\":\"cd \\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607\\\" && rg -n \\\"step\\\\(n\\\" pixel-engine.js | head -5 && rg -n \\\"step\\\\(n = 1|dt = 1 / 60|1 / 60\\\" pixel-engine.js | head -20\",\"truncated\":true,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Find Engine.step default frame dt\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3%2Fwork/01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469/terminal/call-f28e8cbd-82b2-4e53-b4d2-94fb949d97da-68.log\",\"total_bytes\":3577238}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"99542bbd-ca33-4bb6-9257-efe55d2daff0"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_118","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"FIXED_DT is exported. The default step likely uses it.\n\nI'll trust 1/60 as the step rate. I'm writing app.js, world.js, and main.js now. I'm also planning a credits node one-liner and structuring about.js for build.mjs.\n\nAbout.js will stay free of engine imports so Node can import it. Credits text is separate and read by the about screen. The build script writes exit-interview.json to the workspace root. App.go takes mode and arg. A timeout guard will print mode and simulation phase for week tests. Rep keyboard input is unnecessary for bot tests.\n\nHard mode expert on tree will be tested separately from easy mode. Pier idle 0 expert 3 is already tuned and will not be retuned. Tray tests may use a board option, but the default remains straight. Ghost medley tests will create a medley with one ghost lane plus bot lanes. Family hour tests require three moving lanes.\n\nGhost lanes are added on top of existing ones. The `startMedley` method will accept a `lanes` spec. For the Node family test, I'm stubbing gamepads and polling button 0 for rising edges to claim pads.\n\nThe join screen will also claim keyboard input on Enter. The start row is disabled when no seats remain, so tests must fill or claim a seat first. After entering the medley, each lane receives input from its driver, bot simulator, or local reader, then steps forward and updates position.\n\nHeader simulation uses sim.x for position. Lane.pos will be set directly from input.x so tests see movement before integration. Medley's first event is stillness, which uses the dot. Pad axis +1 moves the dot. Keyboard lanes use LocalDriver and readFrom keys. Three lanes—pad0, pad1, and key—each run separate Dots; after frames their dot.x values differ.\n\nGhost lanes will use a Dot that is never stepped. The test will assert that the lane remains simulated but has zero steps and a dot at x=0, since the acceptance criteria require a ghost lane that does not simulate.\n\nA steps counter on the lane will confirm the ghost dot was never stepped. GhostDriver.simulated will be false. Hub ghosts are created from messages by finding or creating a lane for `from`, pushing data, and calling present during update.\n\nGhost lanes will never call createSim. The local medley test will use four bot lanes, stepping through the full 185-second sequence to verify scores stay in range and each window is respected. Skipping frames by jumping time would be cheating, so the entire simulation will run.\n\nMedley simulations use skipIntro so dots move during the first frames. Activities inside a 55-second window may finish early or get cut off by the next window. The score is snapshotted at the window boundary even if the simulation is not yet done.\n\nNormalise will use thresholds[2] as its maximum so expert scores approach 1000. After the medley, the game enters a podium mode that ranks players by total score. I am ready to write the files and will add src/data/creditsText.js via shell. World draw must remain safe if HUD methods differ, and say() uses hud.sprite for lowercase text.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3de280cc-0a05-4302-989a-5d709ec104d1-69","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/core/dot.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3de280cc-0a05-4302-989a-5d709ec104d1-70","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/art/avatar.js","limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":16187,"output_tokens":1873,"cache_read_input_tokens":145664,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-