1,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":4,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/types/engine/random.d.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":7,\"content\":\" *   const level = ctx.random.fork(`level:${n}`);\"},{\"line_number\":8,\"content\":\" *   const room = level.fork(`room:${i}`);   // independent of how many numbers `level` drew\"},{\"line_number\":19,\"content\":\"    next(): number;\"},{\"line_number\":21,\"content\":\"    fork(purpose: string | number): Rng;\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"2a8a4717-7875-4a28-881e-06a9869c12c4"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_120","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Confirmed that `rand` for `Dot` must be a function.\n\nPreparing to write all files. Reviewing settings for look and pixelSize. Handling fullscreen, HUD visibility, overlay text, export logging, and animation viewer clip assignment.\n\nMapping out the remaining tool behaviors. Animation playback will only run if a hero exists. Sound tests verify chime and music counts increase. The dialogue tester sets text via speak(). Reset save clears storage and resets mode. Day navigation updates guest day and week. Jump activity exits dev mode with timeScale at 1.\n\nDev tools will be invoked via `app.tool(name)` when confirming a row. A compact `check` helper will collect test failures and exit with a pass count. Browser tests will be skipped in fast mode.\n\nThe scratch directory is set to a temporary build path. Test output will be captured in `test.log` via tee. The test runner will remain silent on success and only report failures and the final count.\n\nFixing engine error handling so world and step exceptions propagate correctly. Preparing to write the code and generate credits.\n\nThe exit interview is built from about.js at build time, so issue counts must be accurate. The plan is to write about with placeholder counts first, build and test, then update real counts and rebuild so HTML and interview match. Tests may be re-run after that.\n\nAbout screen tests will verify that required fields and headings exist rather than checking exact issue counts. The source fields must match TASK.md exactly: Date 2026-11-04 22:16:07, Source Wii Fit, Plan PLAN.md, Genre Sports, Perspective isometric island with fixed cameras per activity.\n\nAbout screen source fields are now fully defined. Tech stack includes Pixel Engine 0.46.0, three.js r186, Rapier 0.20, and esbuild 0.28.2. Art direction uses native pixel look with a Sweetie-like palette and new models for scale and stations. Animation relies on ClipDefs and AnimationMixer. Audio uses Song and SoundDef with Web Audio formant voice and 10% music volume. Online features include AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, own card, Family Hour local. Testing runs via node tools/test.mjs with Playwright 1.63 Chromium plus WebKit and Firefox for failure paths, using headless engine.\n\nResearch covered the director's plan, PLAN.md, GUIDE sections, hub README, and the Dot table. No extra Wii Fit research was done. The environment is Grok CLI on Linux with model grok-4.7 and reasoning effort xhigh. Usage was added on import. Genre and perspective will remain separate JSON fields.\n\nThe about screen JSON will include a `sourceInformation` object with all required fields. Genre will be \"Sports\" and perspective will be \"Isometric island, fixed camera per activity\". Kit credits will also appear on the about screen.\n\nAbout screen credits will cite Kenney CC0, three.js MIT, Rapier Apache-2.0, and Sweetie 16. The text will be fully paged. Pixel Engine version 0.46.0 will be read from the exported constant at runtime. An unused variable in lines.js will be left as-is to avoid unnecessary churn. A complete world implementation is planned.\n\nWrapping `compileClips` and `dress()` in try/catch to handle potential mesh name mismatches. Confirming `setLookLayer`, `ContactShadow`, and `applySky` are exported and valid. Setting the fixed camera at [9, 7, 11] aimed at [0, 1, 0]. Activity targets will shift slightly to keep the dot in frame.\n\nThe dot mesh will be a small sphere at (dot.x, 0.4, dot.y) on the origin mat. A 40-meter lime ground plane will ensure the capture shows painted pixels even if the camera is slightly off. The scene background will be set to the bright sky color so empty areas do not render as black.\n\nThe pause menu will use `wasPressed` to detect input while the engine drops keys at zero timeScale. If that fails, a tiny timeScale workaround will be used instead.\n\nA custom `pressed` helper will detect key edges by tracking held keys with a Set. This avoids relying on `wasPressed`, which may be swallowed when timeScale is zero, and prevents double-fires.\n\nReconsidered the custom key edge detector. `wasPressed` will be used first since it was already verified at zero timeScale, with the custom helper as a fallback only if the pause test fails. Menu repeat is unnecessary. Focus wrapping will be handled.\n\nThe app will be organized into logical sections within a single file. Medley lane simulation IDs will be drawn from the still, beat, and lean activity picks. Scores will normalize when a window exits its play phase. The local clock resets to zero at the start of a medley, including during countdown; the hub waits until time reaches zero before stepping simulations, but still reports zero progress during that countdown.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4671bd3f-5933-48df-b08a-1c60316d1de3-72","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"hub.time =","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/vendor/hub/session.js","-A":12}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":623,"output_tokens":2550,"cache_read_input_tokens":164608,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"20c4b4dd-a809-47d8-bb44-ef3cb513c0c8"}
