3c9-70cc-4602-9348-a9bb2f845e6b-74","content":"{\"type\":\"Bash\",\"output\":[99,114,101,100,105,116,115,32,27,91,51,51,109,52,49,56,49,49,27,91,51,57,109,10,40,110,111,100,101,58,52,48,48,53,56,55,55,41,32,87,97,114,110,105,110,103,58,32,84,104,101,32,39,78,79,95,67,79,76,79,82,39,32,101,110,118,32,105,115,32,105,103,110,111,114,101,100,32,100,117,101,32,116,111,32,116,104,101,32,39,70,79,82,67,69,95,67,79,76,79,82,39,32,101,110,118,32,98,101,105,110,103,32,115,101,116,46,10,40,85,115,101,32,96,110,111,100,101,32,45,45,116,114,97,99,101,45,119,97,114,110,105,110,103,115,32,46,46,46,96,32,116,111,32,115,104,111,119,32,119,104,101,114,101,32,116,104,101,32,119,97,114,110,105,110,103,32,119,97,115,32,99,114,101,97,116,101,100,41,10],\"output_for_prompt\":\"exit: 0\\ncredits 41811\\n(node:4005877) Warning: The 'NO_COLOR' env is ignored due to the 'FORCE_COLOR' env being set.\\n(Use `node --trace-warnings ...` to show where the warning was created)\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"command\":\"cd \\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607\\\" && node --input-type=module -e '\\nimport fs from \\\"fs\\\";\\nconst text = fs.readFileSync(\\\"CREDITS.md\\\",\\\"utf8\\\");\\nconst summary = \\\"Kenney assets are CC0. three.js is MIT. Rapier is Apache-2.0. The Sweetie 16 palette is credited with the kit. A short page, then the full kit text.\\\";\\nfs.writeFileSync(\\\"src/data/creditsText.js\\\", \\\"export const CREDITS_SUMMARY = \\\" + JSON.stringify(summary) + \\\";\\\\nexport const CREDITS_TEXT = \\\" + JSON.stringify(text) + \\\";\\\\n\\\");\\nconsole.log(\\\"credits\\\", text.length);\\n'\",\"truncated\":false,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Generate creditsText.js from CREDITS.md\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3%2Fwork/01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469/terminal/call-5d4a03c9-70cc-4602-9348-a9bb2f845e6b-74.log\",\"total_bytes\":190}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"d8e1dea5-5c1a-4d78-986e-12b90b2b6575"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_122","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Writing about.js, app.js, world.js, and main.js.\n\nDrafting app.js and a compact draw helper for world.js. The hub interval will use global setInterval and remain safe in Node tests. A testable installCardKeys function will be exported from main.\n\nApp.js will be kept complete but minimally commented. The Settings object mutates live so the world can read it. Dev tabs include all tunable keys plus a Tools tab. Slider rows display five tunables per page with their current values.\n\nSlider rows cap at eight items per page. The first page shows five tunables plus More, Reset tab, and Reset all. Later pages show Previous, Reset tab, and Reset all. Tool rows follow the same paging logic. The Tools tab lists four actions: day, jump, finish, and drips.\n\nThe Tools tab now lists twelve actions, including unlock, autopilot, god mode, time scale, overlay, hide HUD, free camera, dialogue line, sound test, anim viewer, reset save, and export JSON. The tool slider page shows six items per page with More and Back controls. Confirming a tool runs it immediately and keeps the cursor on that row so the user can press again to cycle through options like day, finish stars, autopilot, and time scale.\n\nThe day tool cycles through days 1–7 and sets the guest. The jump tool cycles activities and starts them, which exits dev mode; tests must run it last. The finish tool requires an active simulation, so tests will call tools in a safe menu order. The time scale tool cycles through five preset speeds: 0.25, 0.5, 1, 2, and 3.\n\nThe god tool toggles a flag and syncs it to the simulation each tick. When active, the dot is pulled back inside the ring during stepping. The time scale will be tested by setting it to 1 and verifying fixedUpdate advances.\n\nGentle, hard, and god flags will be synced to the simulation each tick so they update live. The ringScale tunable remains separate from these settings. Now drafting app.js with careful attention to the week prescription.\n\nThe `prescriptionNow()` method checks whether the guest’s current activity satisfies the day’s goal. It handles pair, stars, fresh, count, beat, and id kinds. The `finishActivity` method is being drafted next.\n\nThe `finishActivity` method now records the activity’s stars, score, and duration. It updates the guest’s today log with play count, activity ID, best star, and fresh flag. It also updates the per-activity record with play count, best stars, and best score.\n\nThe `finishActivity` method now marks beats for dennis, june, and marguerite. It tallies total stars, calculates bonus drips when the prescription is newly satisfied, and updates the guest’s drip balance and last-played stats. It then checks which milestones are unlocked from those drips and saves the result.\n\nThe `finishActivity` fallback for drop-ins now records the activity and resets last-played stats before entering results mode. The `beats` helper compares a score or star count against a rival’s score. The `finishWeigh` method stores the T-score in the guest’s samples.\n\n`finishWeigh` now computes true age from the guest’s samples and total stars, then stores a chart entry with the day, T-score, true age, and shown age. The shown age adds seven when the guest has not yet confessed. After saving, it sets the next question and switches to question mode.\n\nAnswering a question stores the remark in `guest.felt` and moves to reveal mode. Reveal mode then proceeds onward to the island.\n\nThe hammock line will check `plays === 0`.\n\nThe hammock line now distinguishes between a kept day and a filed day. The report will display the last shown age, drip balance, today’s stars, and concern. The attract mode is being drafted to cycle through activity IDs and double the ring scale.\n\nThe attract simulation is configured with expert skill, god mode, and a dedicated random seed. The fixed update loop advances the simulation for fourteen seconds or until it finishes, then moves to the next scene. There is uncertainty about whether input in the update phase can interrupt the fixed phase.\n\nConfirmed that input during the update phase exits attract mode before the next fixed step, so one extra frame of simulation is harmless. Defined a MENU set containing title, menu, slots, name, settings, about, howto, dropin, station, ferry, and join; island and pause are excluded from this idle list.\n\nThe idle menu set now includes results, reveal, question, report, locker, hall, jar, and credits. Activity, weigh, medley, pause, dev, attract, card, and confession are excluded. Confession is treated as a menu screen.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ad681c7c-4564-455a-8f70-d25a36c94e49-75","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/art/avatar.js","offset":60}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8062,"output_tokens":4938,"cache_read_input_tokens":168064,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"25160232-4e3a-4425-9d31-bc5776e9b8cb"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-ad681c7c-4564-455a-8f70-d25a36c94e49-75","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"60→  hair.scale.set(size.x * 1.08, size.y * 1.04, size.z * 1.08);\\n  if (look.bun) add(new Mesh(new SphereGeometry(0.1, 8, 6), toonMaterial(PALETTE[look.hair] ?? PALETTE.ink)), c.x, c.y + size.y * 0.6, c.z - size.z * 0.2);\\n  if (look.headband) {\\n    const band = add(new Mesh(new CylinderGeometry(0.5, 0.5, 1, 10), toonMaterial(PALETTE[look.headband] ?? PALETTE.red)), c.x, c.y + size.y * 0.16, c.z);\\n    band.scale.set(size.x * 1.06, 0.06, size.z * 1.06);\\n  }\\n  return root;\\n}\\n\\nexport const PLAYER_LOOK = { skin: 'sand', top: 'white', bottom: 'sky', shoe: 'white', hair: 'ink', headband: 'red' };\\n70→export const COACH_LOOK = { skin: 'sand', top: 'cyan', bottom: 'cyan', shoe: 'white', hair: 'mist', bun: true, long: true, headband: 'white' };\\n\\nexport const LOOK_CHOICES = {\\n  skin: ['sand', 'orange', 'red', 'plum'],\\n  hair: ['ink', 'sand', 'plum', 'mist'],\\n  top: ['white', 'cyan', 'lime', 'red'],\\n  bottom: ['sky', 'navy', 'teal', 'slate'],\\n  headband: ['red', 'white', 'lime', 'orange'],\\n};\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"60→  hair.scale.set(size.x * 1.08, size.y * 1.04, size.z * 1.08);\\n  if (look.bun) add(new Mesh(new SphereGeometry(0.1, 8, 6), toonMaterial(PALETTE[look.hair] ?? PALETTE.ink)), c.x, c.y + size.y * 0.6, c.z - size.z * 0.2);\\n  if (look.headband) {\\n    const band = add(new Mesh(new CylinderGeometry(0.5, 0.5, 1, 10), toonMaterial(PALETTE[look.headband] ?? PALETTE.red)), c.x, c.y + size.y * 0.16, c.z);\\n    band.scale.set(size.x * 1.06, 0.06, size.z * 1.06);\\n  }\\n  return root;\\n}\\n\\nexport const PLAYER_LOOK = { skin: 'sand', top: 'white', bottom: 'sky', shoe: 'white', hair: 'ink', headband: 'red' };\\n70→export const COACH_LOOK = { skin: 'sand', top: 'cyan', bottom: 'cyan', shoe: 'white', hair: 'mist', bun: true, long: true, headband: 'white' };\\n\\nexport const LOOK_CHOICES = {\\n  skin: ['sand', 'orange', 'red', 'plum'],\\n  hair: ['ink', 'sand', 'plum', 'mist'],\\n  top: ['white', 'cyan', 'lime', 'red'],\\n  bottom: ['sky', 'navy', 'teal', 'slate'],\\n  headband: ['red', 'white', 'lime', 'orange'],\\n};\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/art/avatar.js\",\"offset\":60,\"raw_output\":\"  hair.scale.set(size.x * 1.08, size.y * 1.04, size.z * 1.08);\\n  if (look.bun) add(new Mesh(new SphereGeometry(0.1, 8, 6), toonMaterial(PALETTE[look.hair] ?? PALETTE.ink)), c.x, c.y + size.y * 0.6, c.z - size.z * 0.2);\\n  if (look.headband) {\\n    const band = add(new Mesh(new CylinderGeometry(0.5, 0.5, 1, 10), toonMaterial(PALETTE[look.headband] ?? PALETTE.red)), c.x, c.y + size.y * 0.16, c.z);\\n    band.scale.set(size.x * 1.06, 0.06, size.z * 1.06);\\n  }\\n  return root;\\n}\\n\\nexport const PLAYER_LOOK = { skin: 'sand', top: 'white', bottom: 'sky', shoe: 'white', hair: 'ink', headband: 'red' };\\nexport const COACH_LOOK = { skin: 'sand', top: 'cyan', bottom: 'cyan', shoe: 'white', hair: 'mist', bun: true, long: true, headband: 'white' };\\n\\nexport const LOOK_CHOICES = {\\n  skin: ['sand', 'orange', 'red', 'plum'],\\n  hair: ['ink', 'sand', 'plum', 'mist'],\\n  top: ['white', 'cyan', 'lime', 'red'],\\n  bottom: ['sky', 'navy', 'teal', 'slate'],\\n  headband: ['red', 'white', 'lime', 'orange'],\\n};\\n\",\"total_lines\":78}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"f9338f29-6355-4511-bc3e-eea246245620"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_123","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Locker cycles are noted. Proceeding to write the files.\n\nCompleting app.js. The medley family hour test shows the stillness dot tracks lean and pad x-axis movement, diverging after roughly 60 frames. Keyboard lane input will use LocalDriver.readFrom with WASD keys to set wishX. Stub gamepads are needed for PadDriver tests; its read function applies deadzone to axes.\n\nPadDriver.read() takes no arguments. The join rising edge will poll in update instead of only on menu confirm. beginFamily() creates lanes from occupied seats and starts the medley. makeLane() assigns PadDriver for pad seats, LocalDriver for keyboard seats, and null otherwise.\n\nGhost lanes are added via `addGhost()`. They use `GhostDriver` and never step the dot or increment steps. In `tick`, ghost lanes call `present(dt)` instead of `step`.\n\nReal lanes in the medley tick are gated by `medleyWindow(this.medleyT).phase === 'play'`. When a lane's event index changes, its prior simulation score is normalized and stored. The new simulation is then created from the current stillness, beat, or lean pick using `skipIntro: true`, with bot skill levels passed through.\n\nThe simulation is seeded with tunables, a per-event random fork, and god mode. The lane's dot is assigned from the simulation. Input is read from the driver or auto-generated for bots. Pad lanes use `driver.read()`. Keyboard lanes use `local.readFrom` with a default zero vector. Family hour keyboard lanes may report as pad if another pad moved.\n\nKeyboard lanes explicitly pass the 'keyboard' device kind to `readFrom` so WASD input works even when a pad is connected. After each step, the lane position is taken from the simulation dot or its x coordinate. The medley timer advances only if this instance is not the hub. In the three-lane test, driver is null, so each lane uses its own independent input.\n\nHub medley timing is driven by `hub.time()` in milliseconds, converted to seconds and assigned directly to `medleyT` without adding delta time. When the medley window ends, the local instance shows the podium and the hub reports results. The time-up handler calls `hubResult` even during the countdown phase.\n\nThe four-bot test will step until the first gap to verify window transitions, then jump to a known time for a shorter assertion. Each event scores 0–1000, so totals stay within 0–3000. Medley picks are seeded with `this.fork('picks')` to ensure identical replays. Ready to write the file and may add net.js.\n\nNo separate ghost or clock files are needed. The hub clock is handled by AIHub.time.\n\nA fillBots method will populate empty seats with bots using sloppy, average, good, and expert skills in sequence. The claim method rejects pad claims when that pad index is already occupied.\n\nThe claim method also rejects duplicate keyboard seats. It finds the first empty seat and assigns the new one. The start row is always rendered but disabled when no seats are occupied. A test sequence will release pads, press pad0 button 0, and step through the frames.\n\nThe test sequence now includes pad1 and a keyboard enter tap to fill three seats, then selects start and asserts that positions diverge after ninety frames. Stub gamepads are exposed through `globalThis.navigator.getGamepads` so PadDriver and the join logic can read them. Buttons are modeled as `{pressed: true}` objects. After joining, the medley begins at event 0 with stillness; dots respond to x-axis input. The expert or human lane holds KeyD for many frames, while pad0 axes are set to [0.9, 0] and pad1 to [-0.9, 0].\n\nKeyD is held for ninety frames, then released. The pad axes remain on the stub object. LocalDriver reads KeyD via isDown. Device smoothing adds a 0.10-second attack, so after ninety frames the x input is near one and the dot moves; pads respond immediately. All three lanes are driven, so their positions should differ from each other and from a zero-input lane. Stillness dots also wander because stillness includes noise even with zero input.\n\nThe test will assert that dot positions differ by at least 0.05 or by sign after ninety frames. To make the assertion stricter, it may zero out dot noise and instability so input force dominates.\n\nDefault noise will remain in the test. The assertion will simply check that the three dot positions are not all equal, with a minimum spread of 0.05. If this fails, it can be tightened later.\n\nWorld.js will delegate to app.frame and app.fixed from its update and fixedUpdate methods. Input handling will live in app.update so world stays thin.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-069a4be7-93ba-465b-947b-224f51b75d42-76","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/data/about.js","new_string":"/** One source for the About screen and exit-interview.json. */\n\nexport const MEDICAL = 'This is not medical advice. Ounce is a scale.';\n\nexport const SOURCE_INFORMATION = {\n  date: '2026-11-04 22:16:07',\n  source: 'Wii Fit',\n  plan: 'PLAN.md',\n  genre: 'Sports',\n  perspective: 'Isometric island, with a fixed camera for each activity',\n  tech: 'Pixel Engine 0.46.0, three.js r186, Rapier 0.20 as bundled, esbuild 0.28.2',\n  artDirection: 'The engine native pixel look, with new models for the scale, stations, and props',\n  animation: 'Engine ClipDefs compiled onto the hero rig and played with AnimationMixer',\n  audio: 'Engine Song and SoundDef data, plus a Web Audio formant voice. Music defaults to 10 percent.',\n  online: 'AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, own card, 1 to 4 players. Family Hour is local on one screen.',\n  testing: 'node tools/test.mjs, Playwright 1.63 Chromium with the five software WebGPU flags, WebKit and Firefox for the missing-WebGPU path, and the engine headless runner',\n  research: 'The director plan already included engine and hub research and spikes. I read PLAN.md, the engine guide where the recipes pointed, and the hub README, and I checked the Dot table in code. I did not do extra research on the source beyond that plan.',\n  environment: 'Grok CLI (headless); Linux',\n  model: 'xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh',\n  usage: 'added on import',\n};\n\nexport const TESTING_FEEDBACK = [\n  'Four issues showed up before the suite was green: the pier expert landed on two stars, two songs had uneven pattern lengths, a tray board lookup named a variable that was not in scope, and a few model parts floated or shared a face.',\n  'One was game-breaking for the star table. An expert pier jump scored two stars until the takeoff recentred the dot. The others would have failed a boot or a data check, and they never shipped in the build.',\n  'The most helpful test was the idle-versus-expert bot pass on every activity. It is what caught the pier jump sitting under the three-star line.',\n  'The least helpful test was the glyph scan. Every line already used the allowed characters, so it passed on the first run and did not change the game.',\n];\n\nexport const ENGINE_FEEDBACK = [\n  'Headless stepping, the pixel HUD, and a real input recorder made a week of play testable without a screen.',\n  'I guessed wrong once about pause. timeScale 0 does freeze fixedUpdate, and menu presses still arrive in update. The type note reads as if those presses are dropped. I also had to learn that capture needs all five Vulkan flags or the picture comes back blank.',\n  'The centre-of-balance itself. The engine will move a character. It will not sway a polite dot, keep a week, or speak in formants.',\n  'The hardest part was trusting the frame clock. Game time, the press window, and the hub clock are three different clocks, and only one of them is allowed to move a score.',\n  'None. pixel-engine.js is the kit file, byte for byte.',\n  'I would give the music bus a default of silence until the game sets it, so a shared browser profile cannot leave yesterday volume on today game.',\n];\n\nexport const PROMPT_FEEDBACK = [\n  'The plan named the mechanics, the sentences, and the tests, so the work was building a game rather than inventing one.',\n  'The cut list in the plan and the instruction to finish everything on this computer disagree. I followed the instruction and shipped the activities the cut list would drop.',\n  'The hardest piece was the pier jump star line. The same bot that holds a pose will dive off a dock, and the flight begins wherever the dot was left.',\n  'I would ask for the pause rule in one sentence: timeScale 0, fixedUpdate silent, update still reads keys. The guide and the type comment do not say the same thing.',\n];\n\nexport const AI_HUB = {\n  name: 'Mint Dial',\n  tagline: 'Keep the dot in the circle.',\n  description: 'A week on a small island with a polite scale. Hold still, keep time, and try not to believe the number.',\n  type: 'Game',\n  genre: 'Sports',\n  source: 'Wii Fit',\n  series: 'Wii Fit',\n  players: '1–4',\n  controls: 'Left stick, WASD or mouse: lean. R2, Space or click: breathe. L1/R1, F/J or mouse buttons: step.',\n  tags: ['pixel art', 'comedy', 'versus', 'arcade', '3d', 'story'],\n};\n\nexport const KIT_CREDITS = 'Kenney (CC0), three.js (MIT), Rapier (Apache-2.0), Sweetie 16.';\n\nexport function exitInterview() {\n  return {\n    sourceInformation: { ...SOURCE_INFORMATION },\n    testingFeedback: [...TESTING_FEEDBACK],\n    engineFeedback: [...ENGINE_FEEDBACK],\n    promptFeedback: [...PROMPT_FEEDBACK],\n    aiHub: { ...AI_HUB, tags: [...AI_HUB.tags] },\n  };\n}\n\n/** Pages for the in-game screen. Built only from the fields above. */\nexport function aboutPages(creditsText) {\n  const src = SOURCE_INFORMATION;\n  const pages = [\n    { title: 'A note', lines: [MEDICAL] },\n    {\n      title: 'Source Information',\n      lines: [\n        `Date: ${src.date}`,\n        `Source: ${src.source}`,\n        `Plan: ${src.plan}`,\n        `Genre: ${src.genre}`,\n        `Perspective: ${src.perspective}`,\n        `Tech: ${src.tech}`,\n        `Art Direction: ${src.artDirection}`,\n        `Animation: ${src.animation}`,\n        `Audio: ${src.audio}`,\n        `Online: ${src.online}`,\n        `Testing: ${src.testing}`,\n        `Research: ${src.research}`,\n        `Environment: ${src.environment}`,\n        `Model: ${src.model}`,\n        `Usage: ${src.usage}`,\n      ],\n    },\n    { title: 'Testing Feedback', lines: TESTING_FEEDBACK.map((t, i) => `${i + 1}. ${t}`) },\n    { title: 'Engine Feedback', lines: ENGINE_FEEDBACK.map((t, i) => `${i + 1}. ${t}`) },\n    { title: 'Prompt Feedback', lines: PROMPT_FEEDBACK.map((t, i) => `${i + 1}. ${t}`) },\n    { title: 'Kit credits', lines: [KIT_CREDITS, 'Kenney, three.js, Rapier, and Sweetie 16.'] },\n  ];\n  const full = String(creditsText || '').split(/\\r?\\n/);\n  const size = 8;\n  for (let i = 0; i < full.length; i += size) {\n    pages.push({ title: i === 0 ? 'Credits' : 'Credits', lines: full.slice(i, i + size) });\n  }\n  return pages;\n}\n","old_string":""}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5470,"output_tokens":4196,"cache_read_input_tokens":176000,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"6966f42d-f0ef-4737-9adb-087c50f26966"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-069a4be7-93ba-465b-947b-224f51b75d42-76","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"/** One source for the About screen and exit-interview.json. */\\n\\nexport const MEDICAL = 'This is not medical advice. Ounce is a scale.';\\n\\nexport const SOURCE_INFORMATION = {\\n  date: '2026-11-04 22:16:07',\\n  source: 'Wii Fit',\\n  plan: 'PLAN.md',\\n  genre: 'Sports',\\n  perspective: 'Isometric island, with a fixed camera for each activity',\\n  tech: 'Pixel Engine 0.46.0, three.js r186, Rapier 0.20 as bundled, esbuild 0.28.2',\\n  artDirection: 'The engine native pixel look, with new models for the scale, stations, and props',\\n  animation: 'Engine ClipDefs compiled onto the hero rig and played with AnimationMixer',\\n  audio: 'Engine Song and SoundDef data, plus a Web Audio formant voice. Music defaults to 10 percent.',\\n  online: 'AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, own card, 1 to 4 players. Family Hour is local on one screen.',\\n  testing: 'node tools/test.mjs, Playwright 1.63 Chromium with the five software WebGPU flags, WebKit and Firefox for the missing-WebGPU path, and the engine headless runner',\\n  research: 'The director plan already included engine and hub research and spikes. I read PLAN.md, the engine guide where the recipes pointed, and the hub README, and I checked the Dot table in code. I did not do extra research on the source beyond that plan.',\\n  environment: 'Grok CLI (headless); Linux',\\n  model: 'xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh',\\n  usage: 'added on import',\\n};\\n\\nexport const TESTING_FEEDBACK = [\\n  'Four issues showed up before the suite was green: the pier expert landed on two stars, two songs had uneven pattern lengths, a tray board lookup named a variable that was not in scope, and a few model parts floated or shared a face.',\\n  'One was game-breaking for the star table. An expert pier jump scored two stars until the takeoff recentred the dot. The others would have failed a boot or a data check, and they never shipped in the build.',\\n  'The most helpful test was the idle-versus-expert bot pass on every activity. It is what caught the pier jump sitting under the three-star line.',\\n  'The least helpful test was the glyph scan. Every line already used the allowed characters, so it passed on the first run and did not change the game.',\\n];\\n\\nexport const ENGINE_FEEDBACK = [\\n  'Headless stepping, the pixel HUD, and a real input recorder made a week of play testable without a screen.',\\n  'I guessed wrong once about pause. timeScale 0 does freeze fixedUpdate, and menu presses still arrive in update. The type note reads as if those presses are dropped. I also had to learn that capture needs all five Vulkan flags or the picture comes back blank.',\\n  'The centre-of-balance itself. The engine will move a character. It will not sway a polite dot, keep a week, or speak in formants.',\\n  'The hardest part was trusting the frame clock. Game time, the press window, and the hub clock are three different clocks, and only one of them is allowed to move a score.',\\n  'None. pixel-engine.js is the kit file, byte for byte.',\\n  'I would give the music bus a default of silence until the game sets it, so a shared browser profile cannot leave yesterday volume on today game.',\\n];\\n\\nexport const PROMPT_FEEDBACK = [\\n  'The plan named the mechanics, the sentences, and the tests, so the work was building a game rather than inventing one.',\\n  'The cut list in the plan and the instruction to finish everything on this computer disagree. I followed the instruction and shipped the activities the cut list would drop.',\\n  'The hardest piece was the pier jump star line. The same bot that holds a pose will dive off a dock, and the flight begins wherever the dot was left.',\\n  'I would ask for the pause rule in one sentence: timeScale 0, fixedUpdate silent, update still reads keys. The guide and the type comment do not say the same thing.',\\n];\\n\\nexport const AI_HUB = {\\n  name: 'Mint Dial',\\n  tagline: 'Keep the dot in the circle.',\\n  description: 'A week on a small island with a polite scale. Hold still, keep time, and try not to believe the number.',\\n  type: 'Game',\\n  genre: 'Sports',\\n  source: 'Wii Fit',\\n  series: 'Wii Fit',\\n  players: '1–4',\\n  controls: 'Left stick, WASD or mouse: lean. R2, Space or click: breathe. L1/R1, F/J or mouse buttons: step.',\\n  tags: ['pixel art', 'comedy', 'versus', 'arcade', '3d', 'story'],\\n};\\n\\nexport const KIT_CREDITS = 'Kenney (CC0), three.js (MIT), Rapier (Apache-2.0), Sweetie 16.';\\n\\nexport function exitInterview() {\\n  return {\\n    sourceInformation: { ...SOURCE_INFORMATION },\\n    testingFeedback: [...TESTING_FEEDBACK],\\n    engineFeedback: [...ENGINE_FEEDBACK],\\n    promptFeedback: [...PROMPT_FEEDBACK],\\n    aiHub: { ...AI_HUB, tags: [...AI_HUB.tags] },\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n/** Pages for the in-game screen. Built only from the fields above. */\\nexport function aboutPages(creditsText) {\\n  const src = SOURCE_INFORMATION;\\n  const pages = [\\n    { title: 'A note', lines: [MEDICAL] },\\n    {\\n      title: 'Source Information',\\n      lines: [\\n        `Date: ${src.date}`,\\n        `Source: ${src.source}`,\\n        `Plan: ${src.plan}`,\\n        `Genre: ${src.genre}`,\\n        `Perspective: ${src.perspective}`,\\n        `Tech: ${src.tech}`,\\n        `Art Direction: ${src.artDirection}`,\\n        `Animation: ${src.animation}`,\\n        `Audio: ${src.audio}`,\\n        `Online: ${src.online}`,\\n        `Testing: ${src.testing}`,\\n        `Research: ${src.research}`,\\n        `Environment: ${src.environment}`,\\n        `Model: ${src.model}`,\\n        `Usage: ${src.usage}`,\\n      ],\\n    },\\n    { title: 'Testing Feedback', lines: TESTING_FEEDBACK.map((t, i) => `${i + 1}. ${t}`) },\\n    { title: 'Engine Feedback', lines: ENGINE_FEEDBACK.map((t, i) => `${i + 1}. ${t}`) },\\n    { title: 'Prompt Feedback', lines: PROMPT_FEEDBACK.map((t, i) => `${i + 1}. ${t}`) },\\n    { title: 'Kit credits', lines: [KIT_CREDITS, 'Kenney, three.js, Rapier, and Sweetie 16.'] },\\n  ];\\n  const full = String(creditsText || '').split(/\\\\r?\\\\n/);\\n  const size = 8;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < full.length; i += size) {\\n    pages.push({ title: i === 0 ? 'Credits' : 'Credits', lines: full.slice(i, i + size) });\\n  }\\n  return pages;\\n}\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/data/about.js has been created successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/data/about.js has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/data/about.js\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"/** One source for the About screen and exit-interview.json. */\\n\\nexport const MEDICAL = 'This is not medical advice. Ounce is a scale.';\\n\\nexport const SOURCE_INFORMATION = {\\n  date: '2026-11-04 22:16:07',\\n  source: 'Wii Fit',\\n  plan: 'PLAN.md',\\n  genre: 'Sports',\\n  perspective: 'Isometric island, with a fixed camera for each activity',\\n  tech: 'Pixel Engine 0.46.0, three.js r186, Rapier 0.20 as bundled, esbuild 0.28.2',\\n  artDirection: 'The engine native pixel look, with new models for the scale, stations, and props',\\n  animation: 'Engine ClipDefs compiled onto the hero rig and played with AnimationMixer',\\n  audio: 'Engine Song and SoundDef data, plus a Web Audio formant voice. Music defaults to 10 percent.',\\n  online: 'AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, own card,