{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_135","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The island page contains 7 rows: 6 stations plus one additional row.\n\nThe 7-day plan is mapped out. Day 1 pairs tree with another activity. Day 2 unlocks stars and lunge. Day 3 introduces a fresh activity like heron. Days 4 through 7 require three plays, three stars, and longstand on day 7.\n\nConfession triggers after longstand on day 7. The week then advances to day 8 with a weigh-in. Week testing requires expert mode before the week starts so activities auto-complete. Menus use setKey. Island is not in MENU_IDLE, but Settings and Station are.\n\nsetDriver during menus skips intros and plays activities fast, including weigh-in. The exact weigh duration still needs checking. Station rows are verified: pavilion holds all six poses by day five, and lagoon holds five activities by day five. isOpen uses isUnlocked with hard mode disabled, so hard toggle is handled separately.\n\nKeyboard input via setKey will drive the real menus rather than app.activate. Navigation helpers like tap, confirm, and down are being drafted. The setKey signature still needs verification. Menus run every step regardless of timeScale.\n\nActivity logic runs in fixedUpdate, so timeScale must stay at 1. The default is 1. Pausing drops it to 0 and stops fixedUpdate while update still runs.\n\nAttract mode needs timeScale 1 because beginAttract starts an activity in fixedUpdate. Any key press exits attract. A 700-frame pause keeps the mode as activity. The full attract loop lasts about one second.\n\nMedley 4 bots will take roughly two to four seconds. The full activity sweep spans about seven minutes, or roughly twenty-five thousand frames. Pose holds last thirty to forty seconds each. Repetition activities total about four minutes. Hoop, step, header, slack, tray, and jog each add another minute or two.\n\nThe full simulation should finish in about twelve seconds. The week itself adds roughly five hundred sixty seconds of activity plus menus. One hard-mode test will verify that tree still scores at least two stars.\n\nHard mode will be enabled by creating a fresh guest, setting `guest.hard` to true, and calling `app.go('activity', ...)` directly. The star sweep will test plank, press, longstand, and pier in expert hard.\n\nThe Drips formula needs verification against the actual `dripsFor` implementation and how many seconds the simulator reports. An idle bot must finish with zero stars and no exception. For the Dot bands test, the real `Dot` simulation should be driven directly via `BotDriver`, not through `StillSim`; it must keep the bot inside the ring for roughly thirty-five seconds.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-122ac9a4-4642-4871-900b-3edeca6303b4-46","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/core/score.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-122ac9a4-4642-4871-900b-3edeca6303b4-47","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/core/tunables.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-122ac9a4-4642-4871-900b-3edeca6303b4-48","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/core/dot.js","limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-122ac9a4-4642-4871-900b-3edeca6303b4-49","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/core/drivers.js","limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-122ac9a4-4642-4871-900b-3edeca6303b4-50","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/core/save.js","limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-122ac9a4-4642-4871-900b-3edeca6303b4-51","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"active|connect\\(|ready\\(|\\.fail","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/vendor/hub/README.md","head_limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-122ac9a4-4642-4871-900b-3edeca6303b4-52","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"setKey\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/types/engine/input.d.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-122ac9a4-4642-4871-900b-3edeca6303b4-53","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"step\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/types/engine/Engine.d.ts"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4964,"output_tokens":2309,"cache_read_input_tokens":83328,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"c8d5e726-f582-48b3-a164-7c939d24499f"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-122ac9a4-4642-4871-900b-3edeca6303b4-46","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/** Stars from a 0..100-style score and three rising thresholds. */\\nexport function starsFor(score, thresholds, scale = 1) {\\n  const t = thresholds.map((n) => n * scale);\\n  let stars = 0;\\n  if (score >= t[0]) stars = 1;\\n  if (score >= t[1]) stars = 2;\\n  if (score >= t[2]) stars = 3;\\n  return stars;\\n}\\n10→\\n/** Drips: 2 + 3×stars + floor(playSeconds/30), plus 5 for the day's prescription. */\\nexport function dripsFor(stars, playSeconds, prescription, dripRate = 1) {\\n  const base = 2 + 3 * stars + Math.floor(Math.max(0, playSeconds) / 30);\\n  return Math.round((base + (prescription ? 5 : 0)) * dripRate);\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * true  = round(20 + 60 × (1 - mean(last 3 T))) - min(20, totalStars × weight)\\n * shown = true + 7 until the confession.\\n20→ */\\nexport function wobbleAge(samples, totalStars, weight = 0.5) {\\n  const last = samples.slice(-3);\\n  const mean = last.length ? last.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0) / last.length : 0;\\n  const raw = Math.round(20 + 60 * (1 - mean)) - Math.min(20, totalStars * weight);\\n  const trueAge = Math.max(18, Math.min(95, raw));\\n  return trueAge;\\n}\\n\\nexport const JAR_MILESTONES = [10, 25, 45, 70, 100, 135, 175];\\n30→\\nexport const JAR_ITEMS = [\\n  { at: 10, id: 'band', name: 'Second headband' },\\n  { at: 25, id: 'towel', name: 'Towel cape' },\\n  { at: 45, id: 'confidence', name: 'Confidence: no visible effect' },\\n  { at: 70, id: 'wrist', name: 'Wrist note: breathe' },\\n  { at: 100, id: 'socks', name: 'Clinic socks' },\\n  { at: 135, id: 'whistle', name: 'Quiet whistle' },\\n  { at: 175, id: 'crown', name: 'Paper crown' },\\n];\\n40→\\nexport function milestonesReached(drips) {\\n  return JAR_ITEMS.filter((item) => drips >= item.at);\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/** Stars from a 0..100-style score and three rising thresholds. */\\nexport function starsFor(score, thresholds, scale = 1) {\\n  const t = thresholds.map((n) => n * scale);\\n  let stars = 0;\\n  if (score >= t[0]) stars = 1;\\n  if (score >= t[1]) stars = 2;\\n  if (score >= t[2]) stars = 3;\\n  return stars;\\n}\\n10→\\n/** Drips: 2 + 3×stars + floor(playSeconds/30), plus 5 for the day's prescription. */\\nexport function dripsFor(stars, playSeconds, prescription, dripRate = 1) {\\n  const base = 2 + 3 * stars + Math.floor(Math.max(0, playSeconds) / 30);\\n  return Math.round((base + (prescription ? 5 : 0)) * dripRate);\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * true  = round(20 + 60 × (1 - mean(last 3 T))) - min(20, totalStars × weight)\\n * shown = true + 7 until the confession.\\n20→ */\\nexport function wobbleAge(samples, totalStars, weight = 0.5) {\\n  const last = samples.slice(-3);\\n  const mean = last.length ? last.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0) / last.length : 0;\\n  const raw = Math.round(20 + 60 * (1 - mean)) - Math.min(20, totalStars * weight);\\n  const trueAge = Math.max(18, Math.min(95, raw));\\n  return trueAge;\\n}\\n\\nexport const JAR_MILESTONES = [10, 25, 45, 70, 100, 135, 175];\\n30→\\nexport const JAR_ITEMS = [\\n  { at: 10, id: 'band', name: 'Second headband' },\\n  { at: 25, id: 'towel', name: 'Towel cape' },\\n  { at: 45, id: 'confidence', name: 'Confidence: no visible effect' },\\n  { at: 70, id: 'wrist', name: 'Wrist note: breathe' },\\n  { at: 100, id: 'socks', name: 'Clinic socks' },\\n  { at: 135, id: 'whistle', name: 'Quiet whistle' },\\n  { at: 175, id: 'crown', name: 'Paper crown' },\\n];\\n40→\\nexport function milestonesReached(drips) {\\n  return JAR_ITEMS.filter((item) => drips >= item.at);\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/core/score.js\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"/** Stars from a 0..100-style score and three rising thresholds. */\\nexport function starsFor(score, thresholds, scale = 1) {\\n  const t = thresholds.map((n) => n * scale);\\n  let stars = 0;\\n  if (score >= t[0]) stars = 1;\\n  if (score >= t[1]) stars = 2;\\n  if (score >= t[2]) stars = 3;\\n  return stars;\\n}\\n\\n/** Drips: 2 + 3×stars + floor(playSeconds/30), plus 5 for the day's prescription. */\\nexport function dripsFor(stars, playSeconds, prescription, dripRate = 1) {\\n  const base = 2 + 3 * stars + Math.floor(Math.max(0, playSeconds) / 30);\\n  return Math.round((base + (prescription ? 5 : 0)) * dripRate);\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * true  = round(20 + 60 × (1 - mean(last 3 T))) - min(20, totalStars × weight)\\n * shown = true + 7 until the confession.\\n */\\nexport function wobbleAge(samples, totalStars, weight = 0.5) {\\n  const last = samples.slice(-3);\\n  const mean = last.length ? last.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0) / last.length : 0;\\n  const raw = Math.round(20 + 60 * (1 - mean)) - Math.min(20, totalStars * weight);\\n  const trueAge = Math.max(18, Math.min(95, raw));\\n  return trueAge;\\n}\\n\\nexport const JAR_MILESTONES = [10, 25, 45, 70, 100, 135, 175];\\n\\nexport const JAR_ITEMS = [\\n  { at: 10, id: 'band', name: 'Second headband' },\\n  { at: 25, id: 'towel', name: 'Towel cape' },\\n  { at: 45, id: 'confidence', name: 'Confidence: no visible effect' },\\n  { at: 70, id: 'wrist', name: 'Wrist note: breathe' },\\n  { at: 100, id: 'socks', name: 'Clinic socks' },\\n  { at: 135, id: 'whistle', name: 'Quiet whistle' },\\n  { at: 175, id: 'crown', name: 'Paper crown' },\\n];\\n\\nexport function milestonesReached(drips) {\\n  return JAR_ITEMS.filter((item) => drips >= item.at);\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":43}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-122ac9a4-4642-4871-900b-3edeca6303b4-47","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→import { DOT_DEFAULTS } from './dot.js';\\n\\n/** Live sliders. Read every step. Defaults match the plan. */\\nexport const TUNABLE_TABS = {\\n  Balance: [\\n    ['dotInstability', 0.6, 0, 4, 0.05],\\n    ['dotAuthority', 3, 0, 8, 0.1],\\n    ['dotDamping', 3.4, 0, 8, 0.1],\\n    ['dotNoise', 0.8, 0, 4, 0.05],\\n10→    ['dotLag', 0.08, 0.01, 0.4, 0.01],\\n    ['ringScale', 1, 0.5, 2, 0.05],\\n    ['gustForce', 1.6, 0, 4, 0.1],\\n    ['mouseLeanRadius', 70, 20, 160, 2],\\n  ],\\n  'Breath and reps': [\\n    ['breathBonus', 0.55, 0, 1, 0.05],\\n    ['repLag', 0.1, 0.02, 0.4, 0.01],\\n    ['repFatigue', 0.1, 0, 0.5, 0.01],\\n    ['repTempoScale', 1, 0.5, 2, 0.05],\\n20→  ],\\n  Rhythm: [\\n    ['stepWindow', 1, 0.5, 2, 0.05],\\n    ['stepOffsetMs', 0, -80, 80, 5],\\n    ['hoopLow', 0.9, 0.2, 2, 0.05],\\n    ['hoopHigh', 2.4, 1, 4, 0.05],\\n    ['hoopLiftRate', 0.35, 0.05, 1, 0.05],\\n  ],\\n  Games: [\\n    ['headerInterval', 1, 0.4, 2, 0.05],\\n30→    ['slackWalkInst', 2.6, 0.5, 5, 0.1],\\n    ['trayGravity', 9.8, 2, 24, 0.2],\\n    ['trayMaxTilt', 14, 4, 30, 1],\\n    ['jogTargetCadence', 3, 1.5, 5, 0.1],\\n    ['pierBoost', 2.14, 1, 3, 0.02],\\n  ],\\n  Economy: [\\n    ['dripRate', 1, 0, 3, 0.1],\\n    ['starThresholdScale', 1, 0.5, 1.5, 0.05],\\n    ['ageTrainingWeight', 0.5, 0, 2, 0.05],\\n40→  ],\\n};\\n\\nexport function defaultTunables() {\\n  const t = { ...DOT_DEFAULTS };\\n  for (const rows of Object.values(TUNABLE_TABS)) {\\n    for (const [key, value] of rows) t[key] = value;\\n  }\\n  return t;\\n}\\n50→\\nexport const DEFAULT_TUNABLES = defaultTunables();\\n\\nexport function cloneTunables(src = DEFAULT_TUNABLES) {\\n  return { ...src };\\n}\\n\\nexport function tabKeys(name) {\\n  return (TUNABLE_TABS[name] || []).map((row) => row[0]);\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→import { DOT_DEFAULTS } from './dot.js';\\n\\n/** Live sliders. Read every step. Defaults match the plan. */\\nexport const TUNABLE_TABS = {\\n  Balance: [\\n    ['dotInstability', 0.6, 0, 4, 0.05],\\n    ['dotAuthority', 3, 0, 8, 0.1],\\n    ['dotDamping', 3.4, 0, 8, 0.1],\\n    ['dotNoise', 0.8, 0, 4, 0.05],\\n10→    ['dotLag', 0.08, 0.01, 0.4, 0.01],\\n    ['ringScale', 1, 0.5, 2, 0.05],\\n    ['gustForce', 1.6, 0, 4, 0.1],\\n    ['mouseLeanRadius', 70, 20, 160, 2],\\n  ],\\n  'Breath and reps': [\\n    ['breathBonus', 0.55, 0, 1, 0.05],\\n    ['repLag', 0.1, 0.02, 0.4, 0.01],\\n    ['repFatigue', 0.1, 0, 0.5, 0.01],\\n    ['repTempoScale', 1, 0.5, 2, 0.05],\\n20→  ],\\n  Rhythm: [\\n    ['stepWindow', 1, 0.5, 2, 0.05],\\n    ['stepOffsetMs', 0, -80, 80, 5],\\n    ['hoopLow', 0.9, 0.2, 2, 0.05],\\n    ['hoopHigh', 2.4, 1, 4, 0.05],\\n    ['hoopLiftRate', 0.35, 0.05, 1, 0.05],\\n  ],\\n  Games: [\\n    ['headerInterval', 1, 0.4, 2, 0.05],\\n30→    ['slackWalkInst', 2.6, 0.5, 5, 0.1],\\n    ['trayGravity', 9.8, 2, 24, 0.2],\\n    ['trayMaxTilt', 14, 4, 30, 1],\\n    ['jogTargetCadence', 3, 1.5, 5, 0.1],\\n    ['pierBoost', 2.14, 1, 3, 0.02],\\n  ],\\n  Economy: [\\n    ['dripRate', 1, 0, 3, 0.1],\\n    ['starThresholdScale', 1, 0.5, 1.5, 0.05],\\n    ['ageTrainingWeight', 0.5, 0, 2, 0.05],\\n40→  ],\\n};\\n\\nexport function defaultTunables() {\\n  const t = { ...DOT_DEFAULTS };\\n  for (const rows of Object.values(TUNABLE_TABS)) {\\n    for (const [key, value] of rows) t[key] = value;\\n  }\\n  return t;\\n}\\n50→\\nexport const DEFAULT_TUNABLES = defaultTunables();\\n\\nexport function cloneTunables(src = DEFAULT_TUNABLES) {\\n  return { ...src };\\n}\\n\\nexport function tabKeys(name) {\\n  return (TUNABLE_TABS[name] || []).map((row) => row[0]);\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/core/tunables.js\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"import { DOT_DEFAULTS } from './dot.js';\\n\\n/** Live sliders. Read every step. Defaults match the plan. */\\nexport const TUNABLE_TABS = {\\n  Balance: [\\n    ['dotInstability', 0.6, 0, 4, 0.05],\\n    ['dotAuthority', 3, 0, 8, 0.1],\\n    ['dotDamping', 3.4, 0, 8, 0.1],\\n    ['dotNoise', 0.8, 0, 4, 0.05],\\n    ['dotLag', 0.08, 0.01, 0.4, 0.01],\\n    ['ringScale', 1, 0.5, 2, 0.05],\\n    ['gustForce', 1.6, 0, 4, 0.1],\\n    ['mouseLeanRadius', 70, 20, 160, 2],\\n  ],\\n  'Breath and reps': [\\n    ['breathBonus', 0.55, 0, 1, 0.05],\\n    ['repLag', 0.1, 0.02, 0.4, 0.01],\\n    ['repFatigue', 0.1, 0, 0.5, 0.01],\\n    ['repTempoScale', 1, 0.5, 2, 0.05],\\n  ],\\n  Rhythm: [\\n    ['stepWindow', 1, 0.5, 2, 0.05],\\n    ['stepOffsetMs', 0, -80, 80, 5],\\n    ['hoopLow', 0.9, 0.2, 2, 0.05],\\n    ['hoopHigh', 2.4, 1, 4, 0.05],\\n    ['hoopLiftRate', 0.35, 0.05, 1, 0.05],\\n  ],\\n  Games: [\\n    ['headerInterval', 1, 0.4, 2, 0.05],\\n    ['slackWalkInst', 2.6, 0.5, 5, 0.1],\\n    ['trayGravity', 9.8, 2, 24, 0.2],\\n    ['trayMaxTilt', 14, 4, 30, 1],\\n    ['jogTargetCadence', 3, 1.5, 5, 0.1],\\n    ['pierBoost', 2.14, 1, 3, 0.02],\\n  ],\\n  Economy: [\\n    ['dripRate', 1, 0, 3, 0.1],\\n    ['starThresholdScale', 1, 0.5, 1.5, 0.05],\\n    ['ageTrainingWeight', 0.5, 0, 2, 0.05],\\n  ],\\n};\\n\\nexport function defaultTunables() {\\n  const t = { ...DOT_DEFAULTS };\\n  for (const rows of Object.values(TUNABLE_TABS)) {\\n    for (const [key, value] of rows) t[key] = value;\\n  }\\n  return t;\\n}\\n\\nexport const DEFAULT_TUNABLES = defaultTunables();\\n\\nexport function cloneTunables(src = DEFAULT_TUNABLES) {\\n  return { ...src };\\n}\\n\\nexport function tabKeys(name) {\\n  return (TUNABLE_TABS[name] || []).map((row) => row[0]);\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":59}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-122ac9a4-4642-4871-900b-3edeca6303b4-48","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→// Pure centre-of-balance. Step at 60 Hz. p stays in -1.2..1.2.\\nexport class Dot {\\n  x = 0;\\n  y = 0;\\n  vx = 0;\\n  vy = 0;\\n  ux = 0;\\n  uy = 0;\\n  t = 0;\\n10→  constructor(rand) {\\n    this.ph = [rand(), rand(), rand(), rand()].map((r) => r * 6.283185307179586);\\n  }\\n  step(dt, inX, inY, T, m = {}) {\\n    this.t += dt;\\n    const k = Math.min(1, dt / T.dotLag);\\n    this.ux += (inX - this.ux) * k;\\n    this.uy += (inY - this.uy) * k;\\n    const n = T.dotNoise * (m.noise ?? 1);\\n    const inst = T.dotInstability * (m.inst ?? 1);\\n20→    const auth = T.dotAuthority * (m.auth ?? 1);\\n    const nx = n * (Math.sin(1.7 * this.t + this.ph[0]) + 0.6 * Math.sin(3.1 * this.t + this.ph[1]));\\n    const ny = n * (Math.sin(1.3 * this.t + this.ph[2]) + 0.6 * Math.sin(2.7 * this.t + this.ph[3]));\\n    this.vx += (inst * this.x + auth * this.ux - T.dotDamping * this.vx + nx + (m.bx ?? 0)) * dt;\\n    this.vy += (inst * this.y + auth * this.uy - T.dotDamping * this.vy + ny + (m.by ?? 0)) * dt;\\n    this.x += this.vx * dt;\\n    this.y += this.vy * dt;\\n    const d = Math.hypot(this.x, this.y);\\n    if (d > 1.2) {\\n      const s = 1.2 / d;\\n30→      this.x *= s;\\n      this.y *= s;\\n      this.vx *= 0.3;\\n      this.vy *= 0.3;\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nexport const DOT_DEFAULTS = {\\n  dotInstability: 0.6,\\n40→  dotAuthority: 3.0,\\n  dotDamping: 3.4,\\n  dotNoise: 0.8,\\n  dotLag: 0.08,\\n};\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→// Pure centre-of-balance. Step at 60 Hz. p stays in -1.2..1.2.\\nexport class Dot {\\n  x = 0;\\n  y = 0;\\n  vx = 0;\\n  vy = 0;\\n  ux = 0;\\n  uy = 0;\\n  t = 0;\\n10→  constructor(rand) {\\n    this.ph = [rand(), rand(), rand(), rand()].map((r) => r * 6.283185307179586);\\n  }\\n  step(dt, inX, inY, T, m = {}) {\\n    this.t += dt;\\n    const k = Math.min(1, dt / T.dotLag);\\n    this.ux += (inX - this.ux) * k;\\n    this.uy += (inY - this.uy) * k;\\n    const n = T.dotNoise * (m.noise ?? 1);\\n    const inst = T.dotInstability * (m.inst ?? 1);\\n20→    const auth = T.dotAuthority * (m.auth ?? 1);\\n    const nx = n * (Math.sin(1.7 * this.t + this.ph[0]) + 0.6 * Math.sin(3.1 * this.t + this.ph[1]));\\n    const ny = n * (Math.sin(1.3 * this.t + this.ph[2]) + 0.6 * Math.sin(2.7 * this.t + this.ph[3]));\\n    this.vx += (inst * this.x + auth * this.ux - T.dotDamping * this.vx + nx + (m.bx ?? 0)) * dt;\\n    this.vy += (inst * this.y + auth * this.uy - T.dotDamping * this.vy + ny + (m.by ?? 0)) * dt;\\n    this.x += this.vx * dt;\\n    this.y += this.vy * dt;\\n    const d = Math.hypot(this.x, this.y);\\n    if (d > 1.2) {\\n      const s = 1.2 / d;\\n30→      this.x *= s;\\n      this.y *= s;\\n      this.vx *= 0.3;\\n      this.vy *= 0.3;\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nexport const DOT_DEFAULTS = {\\n  dotInstability: 0.6,\\n40→  dotAuthority: 3.0,\\n  dotDamping: 3.4,\\n  dotNoise: 0.8,\\n  dotLag: 0.08,\\n};\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/core/dot.js\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"// Pure centre-of-balance. Step at 60 Hz. p stays in -1.2..1.2.\\nexport class Dot {\\n  x = 0;\\n  y = 0;\\n  vx = 0;\\n  vy = 0;\\n  ux = 0;\\n  uy = 0;\\n  t = 0;\\n  constructor(rand) {\\n    this.ph = [rand(), rand(), rand(), rand()].map((r) => r * 6.283185307179586);\\n  }\\n  step(dt, inX, inY, T, m = {}) {\\n    this.t += dt;\\n    const k = Math.min(1, dt / T.dotLag);\\n    this.ux += (inX - this.ux) * k;\\n    this.uy += (inY - this.uy) * k;\\n    const n = T.dotNoise * (m.noise ?? 1);\\n    const inst = T.dotInstability * (m.inst ?? 1);\\n    const auth = T.dotAuthority * (m.auth ?? 1);\\n    const nx = n * (Math.sin(1.7 * this.t + this.ph[0]) + 0.6 * Math.sin(3.1 * this.t + this.ph[1]));\\n    const ny = n * (Math.sin(1.3 * this.t + this.ph[2]) + 0.6 * Math.sin(2.7 * this.t + this.ph[3]));\\n    this.vx += (inst * this.x + auth * this.ux - T.dotDamping * this.vx + nx + (m.bx ?? 0)) * dt;\\n    this.vy += (inst * this.y + auth * this.uy - T.dotDamping * this.vy + ny + (m.by ?? 0)) * dt;\\n    this.x += this.vx * dt;\\n    this.y += this.vy * dt;\\n    const d = Math.hypot(this.x, this.y);\\n    if (d > 1.2) {\\n      const s = 1.2 / d;\\n      this.x *= s;\\n      this.y *= s;\\n      this.vx *= 0.3;\\n      this.vy *= 0.3;\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nexport const DOT_DEFAULTS = {\\n  dotInstability: 0.6,\\n  dotAuthority: 3.0,\\n  dotDamping: 3.4,\\n  dotNoise: 0.8,\\n  dotLag: 0.08,\\n};\\n\",\"total_lines\":44}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-122ac9a4-4642-4871-900b-3edeca6303b4-49","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→import { applyDeadzone } from '../../pixel-engine.js';\\n\\n/** Delayed PD. Same bots for classmates, attract, and tests. */\\nexport const BOT_SKILLS = {\\n  sloppy: { tau: 0.42, kp: 0.7, kd: 0.12, err: 1.3 },\\n  average: { tau: 0.3, kp: 1.1, kd: 0.35, err: 0.8 },\\n  good: { tau: 0.22, kp: 1.5, kd: 0.55, err: 0.45 },\\n  expert: { tau: 0.17, kp: 1.9, kd: 0.7, err: 0.2 },\\n};\\n10→\\nexport function clampDisc(x, y) {\\n  const m = Math.hypot(x, y);\\n  if (m > 1) return { x: x / m, y: y / m };\\n  return { x, y };\\n}\\n\\nconst EMPTY = { x: 0, y: 0, breath: false, stepL: false, stepR: false, confirm: false, depth: 0 };\\n\\nexport class BotDriver {\\n20→  constructor(skill, rand, targetFn) {\\n    this.skill = skill;\\n    this.rand = rand || Math.random;\\n    this.targetFn = targetFn || (() => ({ x: 0, y: 0 }));\\n    this.hist = [];\\n    this.dx = 0;\\n    this.dy = 0;\\n    this.t = 0;\\n    this.displayOnly = false;\\n  }\\n30→  read(dot, dt = 1 / 60) {\\n    if (this.skill === 'idle' || !BOT_SKILLS[this.skill]) return { ...EMPTY };\\n    const b = BOT_SKILLS[this.skill];\\n    this.t += dt;\\n    const p = dot || { x: 0, y: 0, vx: 0, vy: 0 };\\n    this.hist.push({ t: this.t, x: p.x, y: p.y, vx: p.vx, vy: p.vy });\\n    const want = this.t - b.tau;\\n    let seen = this.hist[0];\\n    for (const h of this.hist) if (h.t <= want + 1e-9) seen = h;\\n    while (this.hist.length > 2 && this.hist[1].t < want) this.hist.shift();\\n40→    const tgt = this.targetFn() || { x: 0, y: 0 };\\n    this.dx += (this.rand() - 0.5) * b.err * dt * 6;\\n    this.dy += (this.rand() - 0.5) * b.err * dt * 6;\\n    this.dx *= 0.995;\\n    this.dy *= 0.995;\\n    let ux = -b.kp * (seen.x - (tgt.x || 0)) - b.kd * seen.vx + this.dx;\\n    let uy = -b.kp * (seen.y - (tgt.y || 0)) - b.kd * seen.vy + this.dy;\\n    const c = clampDisc(ux, uy);\\n    return { ...EMPTY, x: c.x, y: c.y };\\n  }\\n50→}\\n\\n/** Keyboard attack 0.10s, release 0.06s. Shift halves the lean. */\\nexport function smoothKeys(state, wishX, wishY, dt, shift) {\\n  const ax = wishX === 0 ? 0.06 : 0.1;\\n  const ay = wishY === 0 ? 0.06 : 0.1;\\n  const kx = 1 - Math.exp(-dt / ax);\\n  const ky = 1 - Math.exp(-dt / ay);\\n  state.x += (wishX - state.x) * kx;\\n  state.y += (wishY - state.y) * ky;\\n60→  const scale = shift ? 0.5 : 1;\\n  return clampDisc(state.x * scale, state.y * scale);\\n}\\n\\nexport class LocalDriver {\\n  constructor() {\\n    this.keys = { x: 0, y: 0 };\\n    this.displayOnly = false;\\n  }\\n  /**\\n70→   * u from the last device's lean.\\n   * stick: moveAxis. keys: WASD/arrows. mouse: offset from the dial, a force.\\n   */\\n  readFrom(ctx, device, dial, radius, dt) {\\n    const input = ctx.input;\\n    const axis = input.moveAxis();\\n    const pad = Math.hypot(input.padAxis?.x || 0, input.padAxis?.y || 0) > 0.05;\\n    let x = 0;\\n    let y = 0;\\n    if (device === 'mouse') {\\n80→      const p = input.pointer;\\n      const ax = ((p.x + 1) / 2) * ctx.hud.width;\\n      const ay = ((1 - p.y) / 2) * ctx.hud.height;\\n      const ox = (ax - dial.x) / radius;\\n      const oy = (dial.y - ay) / radius;\\n      const c = clampDisc(ox, oy);\\n      x = c.x;\\n      y = c.y;\\n    } else if (device === 'pad' || pad) {\\n      x = axis.x;\\n90→      y = axis.y;\\n    } else {\\n      const wishX = (input.isDown('KeyD') || input.isDown('ArrowRight') ? 1 : 0) - (input.isDown('KeyA') || input.isDown('ArrowLeft') ? 1 : 0);\\n      const wishY = (input.isDown('KeyW') || input.isDown('ArrowUp') ? 1 : 0) - (input.isDown('KeyS') || input.isDown('ArrowDown') ? 1 : 0);\\n      const shift = input.isDown('ShiftLeft') || input.isDown('ShiftRight');\\n      const c = smoothKeys(this.keys, wishX, wishY, dt, shift);\\n      x = c.x;\\n      y = c.y;\\n    }\\n    const breath = input.isDown('Space') || input.isDown('PadR2') || input.isDown('PadCross') || input.isDown('MouseLeft');\\n100→    const stepL = input.isDown('KeyF') || input.isDown('ArrowLeft') || input.isDown('PadL1') || input.isDown('PadL2') || (input.mouseButtons & 1) !== 0;\\n    const stepR = input.isDown('KeyJ') || input.isDown('ArrowRight') || input.isDown('PadR1') || input.isDown('PadR2') || (input.mouseButtons & 2) !== 0;\\n    const confirm = input.wasPressed('Enter') || input.wasPressed('Space') || input.wasPressed('KeyE') || input.wasPressed('PadCross');\\n    return { x, y, breath, stepL, stepR, confirm, depth: Math.max(0, -y) };\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** One physical pad, by index. The engine merges pads, so lanes read the browser themselves. */\\nexport class PadDriver {\\n  constructor(index) {\\n110→    this.index = index;\\n    this.displayOnly = false;\\n    this.prevL = false;\\n    this.prevR = false;\\n  }\\n  pad() {\\n    const nav = globalThis.navigator;\\n    if (!nav?.getGamepads) return null;\\n    const list = nav.getGamepads();\\n    return list?.[this.index] || null;\\n120→  }\",\"content_concise\":\"1→import { applyDeadzone } from '../../pixel-engine.js';\\n\\n/** Delayed PD. Same bots for classmates, attract, and tests. */\\nexport const BOT_SKILLS = {\\n  sloppy: { tau: 0.42, kp: 0.7, kd: 0.12, err: 1.3 },\\n  average: { tau: 0.3, kp: 1.1, kd: 0.35, err: 0.8 },\\n  good: { tau: 0.22, kp: 1.5, kd: 0.55, err: 0.45 },\\n  expert: { tau: 0.17, kp: 1.9, kd: 0.7, err: 0.2 },\\n};\\n10→\\nexport function clampDisc(x, y) {\\n  const m = Math.hypot(x, y);\\n  if (m > 1) return { x: x / m, y: y / m };\\n  return { x, y };\\n}\\n\\nconst EMPTY = { x: 0, y: 0, breath: false, stepL: false, stepR: false, confirm: false, depth: 0 };\\n\\nexport class BotDriver {\\n20→  constructor(skill, rand, targetFn) {\\n    this.skill = skill;\\n    this.rand = rand || Math.random;\\n    this.targetFn = targetFn || (() => ({ x: 0, y: 0 }));\\n    this.hist = [];\\n    this.dx = 0;\\n    this.dy = 0;\\n    this.t = 0;\\n    this.displayOnly = false;\\n  }\\n30→  read(dot, dt = 1 / 60) {\\n    if (this.skill === 'idle' || !BOT_SKILLS[this.skill]) return { ...EMPTY };\\n    const b = BOT_SKILLS[this.skill];\\n    this.t += dt;\\n    const p = dot || { x: 0, y: 0, vx: 0, vy: 0 };\\n    this.hist.push({ t: this.t, x: p.x, y: p.y, vx: p.vx, vy: p.vy });\\n    const want = this.t - b.tau;\\n    let seen = this.hist[0];\\n    for (const h of this.hist) if (h.t <= want + 1e-9) seen = h;\\n    while (this.hist.length > 2 && this.hist[1].t < want) this.hist.shift();\\n40→    const tgt = this.targetFn() || { x: 0, y: 0 };\\n    this.dx += (this.rand() - 0.5) * b.err * dt * 6;\\n    this.dy += (this.rand() - 0.5) * b.err * dt * 6;\\n    this.dx *= 0.995;\\n    this.dy *= 0.995;\\n    let ux = -b.kp * (seen.x - (tgt.x || 0)) - b.kd * seen.vx + this.dx;\\n    let uy = -b.kp * (seen.y - (tgt.y || 0)) - b.kd * seen.vy + this.dy;\\n    const c = clampDisc(ux, uy);\\n    return { ...EMPTY, x: c.x, y: c.y };\\n  }\\n50→}\\n\\n/** Keyboard attack 0.10s, release 0.06s. Shift halves the lean. */\\nexport function smoothKeys(state, wishX, wishY, dt, shift) {\\n  const ax = wishX === 0 ? 0.06 : 0.1;\\n  const ay = wishY === 0 ? 0.06 : 0.1;\\n  const kx = 1 - Math.exp(-dt / ax);\\n  const ky = 1 - Math.exp(-dt / ay);\\n  state.x += (wishX - state.x) * kx;\\n  state.y += (wishY - state.y) * ky;\\n60→  const scale = shift ? 0.5 : 1;\\n  return clampDisc(state.x * scale, state.y * scale);\\n}\\n\\nexport class LocalDriver {\\n  constructor() {\\n    this.keys = { x: 0, y: 0 };\\n    this.displayOnly = false;\\n  }\\n  /**\\n70→   * u from the last device's lean.\\n   * stick: moveAxis. keys: WASD/arrows. mouse: offset from the dial, a force.\\n   */\\n  readFrom(ctx, device, dial, radius, dt) {\\n    const input = ctx.input;\\n    const axis = input.moveAxis();\\n    const pad = Math.hypot(input.padAxis?.x || 0, input.padAxis?.y || 0) > 0.05;\\n    let x = 0;\\n    let y = 0;\\n    if (device === 'mouse') {\\n80→      const p = input.pointer;\\n      const ax = ((p.x + 1) / 2) * ctx.hud.width;\\n      const ay = ((1 - p.y) / 2) * ctx.hud.height;\\n      const ox = (ax - dial.x) / radius;\\n      const oy = (dial.y - ay) / radius;\\n      const c = clampDisc(ox, oy);\\n      x = c.x;\\n      y = c.y;\\n    } else if (device === 'pad' || pad) {\\n      x = axis.x;\\n90→      y = axis.y;\\n    } else {\\n      const wishX = (input.isDown('KeyD') || input.isDown('ArrowRight') ? 1 : 0) - (input.isDown('KeyA') || input.isDown('ArrowLeft') ? 1 : 0);\\n      const wishY = (input.isDown('KeyW') || input.isDown('ArrowUp') ? 1 : 0) - (input.isDown('KeyS') || input.isDown('ArrowDown') ? 1 : 0);\\n      const shift = input.isDown('ShiftLeft') || input.isDown('ShiftRight');\\n      const c = smoothKeys(this.keys, wishX, wishY, dt, shift);\\n      x = c.x;\\n      y = c.y;\\n    }\\n    const breath = input.isDown('Space') || input.isDown('PadR2') || input.isDown('PadCross') || input.isDown('MouseLeft');\\n100→    const stepL = input.isDown('KeyF') || input.isDown('ArrowLeft') || input.isDown('PadL1') || input.isDown('PadL2') || (input.mouseButtons & 1) !== 0;\\n    const stepR = input.isDown('KeyJ') || input.isDown('ArrowRight') || input.isDown('PadR1') || input.isDown('PadR2') || (input.mouseButtons & 2) !== 0;\\n    const confirm = input.wasPressed('Enter') || input.wasPressed('Space') || input.wasPressed('KeyE') || input.wasPressed('PadCross');\\n    return { x, y, breath, stepL, stepR, confirm, depth: Math.max(0, -y) };\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** One physical pad, by index. The engine merges pads, so lanes read the browser themselves. */\\nexport class PadDriver {\\n  constructor(index) {\\n110→    this.index = index;\\n    this.displayOnly = false;\\n    this.prevL = false;\\n    this.prevR = false;\\n  }\\n  pad() {\\n    const nav = globalThis.navigator;\\n    if (!nav?.getGamepads) return null;\\n    const list = nav.getGamepads();\\n    return list?.[this.index] || null;\\n120→  }\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/core/drivers.js\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":120,\"raw_output\":\"import { applyDeadzone } from '../../pixel-engine.js';\\n\\n/** Delayed PD. Same bots for classmates, attract, and tests. */\\nexport const BOT_SKILLS = {\\n  sloppy: { tau: 0.42, kp: 0.7, kd: 0.12, err: 1.3 },\\n  average: { tau: 0.3, kp: 1.1, kd: 0.35, err: 0.8 },\\n  good: { tau: 0.22, kp: 1.5, kd: 0.55, err: 0.45 },\\n  expert: { tau: 0.17, kp: 1.9, kd: 0.7, err: 0.2 },\\n};\\n\\nexport function clampDisc(x, y) {\\n  const m = Math.hypot(x, y);\\n  if (m > 1) return { x: x / m, y: y / m };\\n  return { x, y };\\n}\\n\\nconst EMPTY = { x: 0, y: 0, breath: false, stepL: false, stepR: false, confirm: false, depth: 0 };\\n\\nexport class BotDriver {\\n  constructor(skill, rand, targetFn) {\\n    this.skill = skill;\\n    this.rand = rand || Math.random;\\n    this.targetFn = targetFn || (() => ({ x: 0, y: 0 }));\\n    this.hist = [];\\n    this.dx = 0;\\n    this.dy = 0;\\n    this.t = 0;\\n    this.displayOnly = false;\\n  }\\n  read(dot, dt = 1 / 60) {\\n    if (this.skill === 'idle' || !BOT_SKILLS[this.skill]) return { ...EMPTY };\\n    const b = BOT_SKILLS[this.skill];\\n    this.t += dt;\\n    const p = dot || { x: 0, y: 0, vx: 0, vy: 0 };\\n    this.hist.push({ t: this.t, x: p.x, y: p.y, vx: p.vx, vy: p.vy });\\n    const want = this.t - b.tau;\\n    let seen = this.hist[0];\\n    for (const h of this.hist) if (h.t <= want + 1e-9) seen = h;\\n    while (this.hist.length > 2 && this.hist[1].t < want) this.hist.shift();\\n    const tgt = this.targetFn() || { x: 0, y: 0 };\\n    this.dx += (this.rand() - 0.5) * b.err * dt * 6;\\n    this.dy += (this.rand() - 0.5) * b.err * dt * 6;\\n    this.dx *= 0.995;\\n    this.dy *= 0.995;\\n    let ux = -b.kp * (seen.x - (tgt.x || 0)) - b.kd * seen.vx + this.dx;\\n    let uy = -b.kp * (seen.y - (tgt.y || 0)) - b.kd * seen.vy + this.dy;\\n    const c = clampDisc(ux, uy);\\n    return { ...EMPTY, x: c.x, y: c.y };\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** Keyboard attack 0.10s, release 0.06s. Shift halves the lean. */\\nexport function smoothKeys(state, wishX, wishY, dt, shift) {\\n  const ax = wishX === 0 ? 0.06 : 0.1;\\n  const ay = wishY === 0 ? 0.06 : 0.1;\\n  const kx = 1 - Math.exp(-dt / ax);\\n  const ky = 1 - Math.exp(-dt / ay);\\n  state.x += (wishX - state.x) * kx;\\n  state.y += (wishY - state.y) * ky;\\n  const scale = shift ? 0.5 : 1;\\n  return clampDisc(state.x * scale, state.y * scale);\\n}\\n\\nexport class LocalDriver {\\n  constructor() {\\n    this.keys = { x: 0, y: 0 };\\n    this.displayOnly = false;\\n  }\\n  /**\\n   * u from the last device's lean.\\n   * stick: moveAxis. keys: WASD/arrows. mouse: offset from the dial, a force.\\n   */\\n  readFrom(ctx, device, dial, radius, dt) {\\n    const input = ctx.input;\\n    const axis = input.moveAxis();\\n    const pad = Math.hypot(input.padAxis?.x || 0, input.padAxis?.y || 0) > 0.05;\\n    let x = 0;\\n    let y = 0;\\n    if (device === 'mouse') {\\n      const p = input.pointer;\\n      const ax = ((p.x + 1) / 2) * ctx.hud.width;\\n      const ay = ((1 - p.y) / 2) * ctx.hud.height;\\n      const ox = (ax - dial.x) / radius;\\n      const oy = (dial.y - ay) / radius;\\n      const c = clampDisc(ox, oy);\\n      x = c.x;\\n      y = c.y;\\n    } else if (device === 'pad' || pad) {\\n      x = axis.x;\\n      y = axis.y;\\n    } else {\\n      const wishX = (input.isDown('KeyD') || input.isDown('ArrowRight') ? 1 : 0) - (input.isDown('KeyA') || input.isDown('ArrowLeft') ? 1 : 0);\\n      const wishY = (input.isDown('KeyW') || input.isDown('ArrowUp') ? 1 : 0) - (input.isDown('KeyS') || input.isDown('ArrowDown') ? 1 : 0);\\n      const shift = input.isDown('ShiftLeft') || input.isDown('ShiftRight');\\n      const c = smoothKeys(this.keys, wishX, wishY, dt, shift);\\n      x = c.x;\\n      y = c.y;\\n    }\\n    const breath = input.isDown('Space') || input.isDown('PadR2') || input.isDown('PadCross') || input.isDown('MouseLeft');\\n    const stepL = input.isDown('KeyF') || input.isDown('ArrowLeft') || input.isDown('PadL1') || input.isDown('PadL2') || (input.mouseButtons & 1) !== 0;\\n    const stepR = input.isDown('KeyJ') || input.isDown('ArrowRight') || input.isDown('PadR1') || input.isDown('PadR2') || (input.mouseButtons & 2) !== 0;\\n    const confirm = input.wasPressed('Enter') || input.wasPressed('Space') || input.wasPressed('KeyE') || input.wasPressed('PadCross');\\n    return { x, y, breath, stepL, stepR, confirm, depth: Math.max(0, -y) };\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** One physical pad, by index. The engine merges pads, so lanes read the browser themselves. */\\nexport class PadDriver {\\n  constructor(index) {\\n    this.index = index;\\n    this.displayOnly = false;\\n    this.prevL = false;\\n    this.prevR = false;\\n  }\\n  pad() {\\n    const nav = globalThis.navigator;\\n    if (!nav?.getGamepads) return null;\\n    const list = nav.getGamepads();\\n    return list?.[this.index] || null;\\n  }\\n\",\"total_lines\":173}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-122ac9a4-4642-4871-900b-3edeca6303b4-50","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→export const SAVE_VERSION = 1;\\nexport const SAVE_KEY = 'mint-dial-save-v1';\\n\\nfunction memoryStore() {\\n  const m = new Map();\\n  return {\\n    getItem: (k) => (m.has(k) ? m.get(k) : null),\\n    setItem: (k, v) => m.set(k, String(v)),\\n    removeItem: (k) => m.delete(k),\\n10→  };\\n}\\n\\nexport function defaultSave() {\\n  return {\\n    v: SAVE_VERSION,\\n    slots: [null, null, null],\\n    settings: null,\\n  };\\n}\\n20→\\n/** Versioned JSON. Missing storage uses memory. Corrupt JSON falls back to empty. */\\nexport class Save {\\n  constructor(storage) {\\n    if (storage === null) this.storage = memoryStore();\\n    else if (storage) this.storage = storage;\\n    else this.storage = pickStorage();\\n    this.memory = false;\\n    try {\\n      const k = '__mint_probe__';\\n30→      this.storage.setItem(k, '1');\\n      this.storage.removeItem(k);\\n    } catch {\\n      this.storage = memoryStore();\\n      this.memory = true;\\n    }\\n  }\\n  read() {\\n    let raw;\\n    try {\\n40→      raw = this.storage.getItem(SAVE_KEY);\\n    } catch {\\n      return defaultSave();\\n    }\\n    if (!raw) return defaultSave();\\n    try {\\n      const data = JSON.parse(raw);\\n      if (!data || data.v !== SAVE_VERSION || !Array.isArray(data.slots)) return defaultSave();\\n      while (data.slots.length < 3) data.slots.push(null);\\n      data.slots = data.slots.slice(0, 3);\\n50→      return data;\\n    } catch {\\n      return defaultSave();\\n    }\\n  }\\n  write(data) {\\n    const out = { ...data, v: SAVE_VERSION };\\n    try {\\n      this.storage.setItem(SAVE_KEY, JSON.stringify(out));\\n      return true;\\n60→    } catch {\\n      return false;\\n    }\\n  }\\n  clear() {\\n    try {\\n      this.storage.removeItem(SAVE_KEY);\\n    } catch {\\n      /* private mode */\\n    }\\n70→  }\\n}\\n\\nfunction pickStorage() {\\n  try {\\n    if (typeof localStorage !== 'undefined' && localStorage) {\\n      const k = '__mint_probe__';\\n      localStorage.setItem(k, '1');\\n      localStorage.removeItem(k);\\n      return localStorage;\\n80→    }\",\"content_concise\":\"1→export const SAVE_VERSION = 1;\\nexport const SAVE_KEY = 'mint-dial-save-v1';\\n\\nfunction memoryStore() {\\n  const m = new Map();\\n  return {\\n    getItem: (k) => (m.has(k) ? m.get(k) : null),\\n    setItem: (k, v) => m.set(k, String(v)),\\n    removeItem: (k) => m.delete(k),\\n10→  };\\n}\\n\\nexport function defaultSave() {\\n  return {\\n    v: SAVE_VERSION,\\n    slots: [null, null, null],\\n    settings