{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_148","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The harness sets cardSent when displaying a hello card.\n\nEnter triggers answer('ready') through the DOM listener. No manual card drawing is needed for cardSent.\n\nMath.random is not used directly. The app relies on fork and mulberry32, and AIHub.seeded remains true so the seeded random generator stays intact.\n\nmedleyPicks uses fork's rand(). BotDriver always receives a custom function, so it never falls back to Math.random.\n\nThe seed should not be overridden.\n\nThe harness runs four copies in a light scene.\n\ntime-up triggers hubResult even if the medley is incomplete. end stops the interval and music, and hubPulse checks hubEnded to prevent duplicate sends. If both events fire, resultSent ensures only one result is sent.\n\nDuring countdown, the interval starts early and hubPulse sends score 0. The client rate-limits progress updates to about once per second, which is acceptable.\n\nFor ghost players with n greater than one, send() fires every 100 milliseconds.\n\nhub.send exceptions are caught. Ghost mode works with a single player. Host leave listeners remain active so remaining games still report on time-up. Hero dress throws are caught. PlatformerCharacter will be loaded outside the session to avoid boot delays. analyzeClip runs in node tests after hero setup.\n\ncompileClip returns a single AnimationClip, while analyzeClip returns a ClipReport with a problems array. I will run a quick node script first to check all MODELS for warnings, song parsing, and app imports before writing tests. If hero loading is slow or analyzeClip rejects poses, I will fix the clips.\n\nI verified that hud.clear exists and draw works after setup. syncSpeech is dynamically imported during tests and will be caught if it fails. paint calls say through hud.sprite, which headless hud should support. app.update reaches ctx.input via device.update. The first frame audio volume may default before applyVolumes runs, but setup applies volumes before the first update so busMusic should be zero.\n\nThe engine may restore saved volumes from localStorage after setup and overwrite the initial setVolume call. I will apply volumes in ready() and the first update as well, and expose the app instance globally.\n\napp.update only reads the engine volume without forcing ours. If localStorage or a prior game left it at 0.6, I will overwrite it in World.update on the first frame.\n\nA `volumesApplied` flag will force the music volume to 0.1 at the start of each update until the user changes it, preventing the engine settings panel from overriding it. The plan allows `setVolume` to persist to localStorage. Implementation is beginning.\n\nKeyE and startWeigh need fixes.\n\nThe week test driver sets 'expert' before navigating. Activities skip intros. Weigh keeps its 14-second hold because the driver does not press keys. Menu navigation stays unaffected.\n\nDuring activities, the driver does not press keys. The activity runs in fixed mode. finishActivity stores results. The next frame shows results with retry, next, and back options.\n\nThe harness will navigate back to the island after each activity. The day flow function returns to page zero, selects the station and activity, waits for results, then goes back to the island. Longstand is a direct row ID on page one. Hammock is also on page one; it triggers rest and reports sleep.\n\nDay 7 sleep routes to confession, then onward credits, then onward to the next day weigh. Day 1 flow is now fully traced: title enter, week slots, name entry, ferry board, weigh question, answer reveal, island, pavilion tree, shed squat, hammock rest, and weigh wait. The prescription checks out with tree paired with length>=2 and a bonus on the second activity. Day 2 will play lunge at the shed after the weigh question and reveal.\n\nThe test will verify daily goals by inspecting the today object before it is cleared on sleep. Day 2 asserts two stars, day 3 asserts fresh, day 4 asserts three plays, day 5 asserts beating dennis, and day 6 asserts three stars.\n\nDay 7 includes longstand, confession, a chart drop of -7, credits, and the day 8 week 2 weigh. The test must visit every station at least once across the week: pavilion on day 1, shed on day 2, beach on day 4, lagoon on day 5, and jog on day 5. Jog can be entered and exited without playing if time is short.\n\nThe acceptance criteria require at least one activity per day, and every station must be visited across the week. I will select each station and back out if no activity is needed there. The planned visits are pavilion on day 1, shed on day 2, beach on day 4, and plaza on day 4. Pavillon gets heron on day 3.\n\nPlaza station is locked until day 7 and only shows longstand. The test will enter it and back out to satisfy the every-station requirement.\n\nDay 5 will include lagoon tray and jog, with jog entered and exited without playing since it is 75 seconds long.\n\nDay 6 will cover any missed stations or play a short activity for the three-star goal.\n\nThe unlock schedule header should appear at the lagoon on day 2 after the weigh question.\n\nThe unlock schedule appears on day 2 because `isUnlocked` checks the current day number. The Jar milestone unlocks after ten drips and a band item. Hard mode will be toggled on day 6 for a tree activity to test star requirements, then turned off; this keeps the week simpler. The star sweep uses `go()` for speed, while the week test navigates through menus.\n\nRecording the full menu path is too flaky. The plan is to record 90 frames of idle input from boot, fingerprint the replay, and verify it matches. A second test will start recording after an activity begins via input, since replay reloads the game from scratch and only seed plus input matter.\n\nThe full menu path will be replayed from boot through the activity play, stopping once the dot moves after the weigh. This totals roughly 1000 frames. Reimplementing the engine with two identical seeds was rejected as too similar to the engine itself. The only remaining flakiness risk is the dynamic import timing of syncSpeech.\n\nSpeech is excluded from the replay fingerprint. Both runs will await hero model loading. Memory storage keeps the original and replay games empty, so localStorage writes during recording stay local to that run and do not leak into the replay. The engine records setKey input during live play, and replay replays those keys.\n\nThe replay's World setup waits for hero model promises, so frame timing should match. If the full activity fingerprint mismatches, the 90-frame title-only replay is the fallback. The recording begins at the title screen and includes all frames from level start.\n\nThe engine starts recording automatically during setup, so the test will step for 90 frames and read the resulting recording. It will replay that exact recording from a fresh game instance and assert the fingerprints match. For activity-level determinism, more frames and the keys embedded in the recording will be needed.\n\nThe title-only 90-frame replay is the mandatory baseline. A longer scripted replay into tree will be attempted if time allows. Two headless engines with identical seeds were considered but rejected in favor of the required replay approach. The loadGame signature and whether it returns a promise still need verification.\n\n`loadGame` returns a promise, so replay awaits it correctly. Only one engine is needed; replay replaces the game state directly. The test sequence is now fixed: boot the engine, run data tests that do not need it, then activity tests that mutate app state, followed by week tests on a fresh app via `loadGame`, then pause, dev, and attract on fresh apps, then replay determinism, and finally the medley.\n\nTo speed up repeated `loadGame` calls, hero loading will be lazy and cached. Tests can set `app.noHero = true` to skip it, and only the `analyzeClip` test will load the hero once.\n\nThe weighCtor class method is being removed and replaced by a prototype version. Imports are being consolidated at the top of the file, including createSim and WeighSim. A small ghost-hide fix and menuInput KeyE handling are also being added.\n\ntickMedley input selection will be simplified. Ghost hide will set `lane.hidden`. `this.hubClock` and `this.freeCam` are safely undefined before initialization. Ferry activation requires a name first. A `boot` export from main.js will let tests control startup manually.\n\nThe esbuild bundle from src/main.js will include pixel-engine.js. The HTML is roughly 5 MB. session.js is excluded from the bundle because it is pasted separately and main uses a global AIHub. build.mjs generates exit-interview from about.js.\n\ntest.mjs will run Node assertions first, then build the bundle, then the browser suite, hub tests, and shots. The --fast flag skips the build step. Shots are evidence to save per the verification plan.\n\nThe scratch directory will contain test.log, browser.log, hub.log, nosession.log, boot screenshots, shots, and capture-error.txt. The test runner will tee all stdout into test.log. Before launching long tasks, the long-running skill instructions must be read first.\n\nThe full test suite will take several minutes. I will start with the fast Node-only run to catch failures early, then run the full suite. I am also checking widget overflow at 1920x1080, since the HUD art resolution depends on pixel scale and aspect fill.\n\nWidget overflow tests will assert every widget fits within the HUD bounds and that the page has no horizontal scrollbar. The 640x360 viewport is small enough to force chunky pixel scaling, which keeps the title text compact.\n\nThe phone profile attract test will step 600 frames inside page.evaluate to avoid webgpu slowdown. It will also open the menu to increase row count and stress-test overflow. The settings button will be queried via DOM selector, and engine.touch should remain null because touch input is disabled.\n\nThe phone profile test will verify `engine.touch` is null and the touch message is set. Chromium headless may not emulate `hover:none` without an explicit device profile, so detection logic might need adjustment. A query parameter fallback was rejected in favor of matchMedia. The engine's start catch block must not rethrow, or Playwright will miss the page error.\n\nThe engine's start rejection is safely caught, and the page message will not be overwritten. I am ready to code. PROGRESS.md, the checklist, and deviations will be written after tests pass.\n\nThe deviations section will be added to the plan file once work is verified. It will list six items: instant mode cuts, a single World/App instead of per-screen scene files, a kinematic Vitamin Tray with three boards, Pier recentring the dot at takeoff, skipping the intro in attract and medley, and possibly no screen iris.\n\nDrip counts will be verified by calling the existing `dripsFor` helper with live stars, seconds, and prescription values instead of hardcoding expected totals. Star bands will also be checked separately.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c2fc4d4d-af08-4d72-975d-07dd1f46e9dc-92","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/core/sims.js","offset":449,"limit":90}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c2fc4d4d-af08-4d72-975d-07dd1f46e9dc-93","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/core/sims.js","offset":518,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c2fc4d4d-af08-4d72-975d-07dd1f46e9dc-94","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/core/sims.js","offset":820,"limit":120}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":623,"output_tokens":5439,"cache_read_input_tokens":137088,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"e9c40a08-a626-45c1-964e-247466a35c38"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-c2fc4d4d-af08-4d72-975d-07dd1f46e9dc-92","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"449→export class HeaderSim extends Sim {\\n450→  _built() {\\n    this.x = 0;\\n    this.objs = [];\\n    this.spawn = 0.4;\\n    this.score = 0;\\n    this.combo = 0;\\n    this.daze = 0;\\n    this.hitR = 0.2;\\n  }\\n  playFinished() {\\n460→    return this.playT >= 60;\\n  }\\n  lane() {\\n    return 2;\\n  }\\n  auto() {\\n    if (this.skill === 'idle') return { ...ZERO };\\n    const soon = this.objs.filter((o) => !o.done).sort((a, b) => a.land - b.land)[0];\\n    if (!soon) return { ...ZERO, x: -this.x * 0.5 };\\n    let tx = soon.x;\\n470→    const dodge = this.skill === 'expert' || this.skill === 'good' || this.skill === 'average';\\n    if (soon.kind === 'flip' && dodge) tx = clamp(soon.x + (soon.x < 0 ? 0.7 : -0.7), -2, 2);\\n    const err = tx - this.x;\\n    const gain = this.skill === 'sloppy' ? 0.25 : 1;\\n    return { ...ZERO, x: clamp(err * 2 * gain, -1, 1) };\\n  }\\n  onStep(dt, u, scoring) {\\n    if (scoring) this.playT += dt;\\n    const t = this.playT;\\n    if (this.daze > 0) this.daze -= dt;\\n480→    const speed = 4.5 * (this.daze > 0 ? 0 : u.x || 0);\\n    this.x = clamp(this.x + speed * dt, -this.lane(), this.lane());\\n    if (!scoring) return;\\n    const span = lerp(1.3, 0.7, clamp(t / 60, 0, 1)) * (this.T.headerInterval || 1) * (this.hard ? 0.8 : 1);\\n    this.spawn -= dt;\\n    if (this.spawn <= 0 && t < 58) {\\n      this.spawn += span;\\n      const roll = this.rand();\\n      const kind = roll < 0.7 ? 'coco' : roll < 0.95 ? 'flip' : 'pine';\\n      const x = (this.rand() * 2 - 1) * 1.85;\\n490→      this.objs.push({ x, kind, land: t + 1.4, done: false });\\n    }\\n    const radius = this.hitR * (this.hard ? 0.85 : 1);\\n    for (const o of this.objs) {\\n      if (o.done || t < o.land) continue;\\n      o.done = true;\\n      const hit = Math.abs(this.x - o.x) < radius;\\n      if (o.kind === 'coco' && hit) {\\n        this.combo += 1;\\n        const tier = this.combo >= 20 ? 4 : this.combo >= 10 ? 3 : this.combo >= 5 ? 2 : 1;\\n500→        this.score += 10 * tier;\\n      } else if (o.kind === 'pine' && hit) {\\n        this.combo += 1;\\n        this.score += 30;\\n      } else if (o.kind === 'flip' && hit) {\\n        this.score -= 10;\\n        this.combo = 0;\\n        this.daze = 0.6;\\n      } else if (o.kind === 'flip' && !hit) {\\n        /* dodged */\\n510→      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n  scoreStars() {\\n    super.scoreStars();\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nexport class SlackSim extends Sim {\\n  _built() {\\n520→    this.progress = 0;\\n    this.falls = 0;\\n    this.stun = 0;\\n    this.finished = false;\\n    this.gustT = 0;\\n    this.gust = 0;\\n    this.nextGust = 6;\\n    this.kevin = false;\\n  }\\n  playFinished() {\\n530→    return this.finished || this.playT >= 75;\\n  }\\n  auto(dt) {\\n    if (this.skill === 'idle') return { ...ZERO };\\n    const u = this.bot.read(this.dot, dt);\\n    const limit = this.skill === 'expert' ? 0.45 : this.skill === 'good' ? 0.45 : this.skill === 'average' ? 0.4 : 0.3;\\n    u.y = Math.abs(this.dot.x) < limit && this.stun <= 0 ? 0.9 : 0;\\n    return { ...ZERO, x: u.x, y: u.y };\\n  }\",\"content_concise\":\"449→export class HeaderSim extends Sim {\\n450→  _built() {\\n    this.x = 0;\\n    this.objs = [];\\n    this.spawn = 0.4;\\n    this.score = 0;\\n    this.combo = 0;\\n    this.daze = 0;\\n    this.hitR = 0.2;\\n  }\\n  playFinished() {\\n460→    return this.playT >= 60;\\n  }\\n  lane() {\\n    return 2;\\n  }\\n  auto() {\\n    if (this.skill === 'idle') return { ...ZERO };\\n    const soon = this.objs.filter((o) => !o.done).sort((a, b) => a.land - b.land)[0];\\n    if (!soon) return { ...ZERO, x: -this.x * 0.5 };\\n    let tx = soon.x;\\n470→    const dodge = this.skill === 'expert' || this.skill === 'good' || this.skill === 'average';\\n    if (soon.kind === 'flip' && dodge) tx = clamp(soon.x + (soon.x < 0 ? 0.7 : -0.7), -2, 2);\\n    const err = tx - this.x;\\n    const gain = this.skill === 'sloppy' ? 0.25 : 1;\\n    return { ...ZERO, x: clamp(err * 2 * gain, -1, 1) };\\n  }\\n  onStep(dt, u, scoring) {\\n    if (scoring) this.playT += dt;\\n    const t = this.playT;\\n    if (this.daze > 0) this.daze -= dt;\\n480→    const speed = 4.5 * (this.daze > 0 ? 0 : u.x || 0);\\n    this.x = clamp(this.x + speed * dt, -this.lane(), this.lane());\\n    if (!scoring) return;\\n    const span = lerp(1.3, 0.7, clamp(t / 60, 0, 1)) * (this.T.headerInterval || 1) * (this.hard ? 0.8 : 1);\\n    this.spawn -= dt;\\n    if (this.spawn <= 0 && t < 58) {\\n      this.spawn += span;\\n      const roll = this.rand();\\n      const kind = roll < 0.7 ? 'coco' : roll < 0.95 ? 'flip' : 'pine';\\n      const x = (this.rand() * 2 - 1) * 1.85;\\n490→      this.objs.push({ x, kind, land: t + 1.4, done: false });\\n    }\\n    const radius = this.hitR * (this.hard ? 0.85 : 1);\\n    for (const o of this.objs) {\\n      if (o.done || t < o.land) continue;\\n      o.done = true;\\n      const hit = Math.abs(this.x - o.x) < radius;\\n      if (o.kind === 'coco' && hit) {\\n        this.combo += 1;\\n        const tier = this.combo >= 20 ? 4 : this.combo >= 10 ? 3 : this.combo >= 5 ? 2 : 1;\\n500→        this.score += 10 * tier;\\n      } else if (o.kind === 'pine' && hit) {\\n        this.combo += 1;\\n        this.score += 30;\\n      } else if (o.kind === 'flip' && hit) {\\n        this.score -= 10;\\n        this.combo = 0;\\n        this.daze = 0.6;\\n      } else if (o.kind === 'flip' && !hit) {\\n        /* dodged */\\n510→      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n  scoreStars() {\\n    super.scoreStars();\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nexport class SlackSim extends Sim {\\n  _built() {\\n520→    this.progress = 0;\\n    this.falls = 0;\\n    this.stun = 0;\\n    this.finished = false;\\n    this.gustT = 0;\\n    this.gust = 0;\\n    this.nextGust = 6;\\n    this.kevin = false;\\n  }\\n  playFinished() {\\n530→    return this.finished || this.playT >= 75;\\n  }\\n  auto(dt) {\\n    if (this.skill === 'idle') return { ...ZERO };\\n    const u = this.bot.read(this.dot, dt);\\n    const limit = this.skill === 'expert' ? 0.45 : this.skill === 'good' ? 0.45 : this.skill === 'average' ? 0.4 : 0.3;\\n    u.y = Math.abs(this.dot.x) < limit && this.stun <= 0 ? 0.9 : 0;\\n    return { ...ZERO, x: u.x, y: u.y };\\n  }\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/core/sims.js\",\"offset\":449,\"limit\":90,\"raw_output\":\"export class HeaderSim extends Sim {\\n  _built() {\\n    this.x = 0;\\n    this.objs = [];\\n    this.spawn = 0.4;\\n    this.score = 0;\\n    this.combo = 0;\\n    this.daze = 0;\\n    this.hitR = 0.2;\\n  }\\n  playFinished() {\\n    return this.playT >= 60;\\n  }\\n  lane() {\\n    return 2;\\n  }\\n  auto() {\\n    if (this.skill === 'idle') return { ...ZERO };\\n    const soon = this.objs.filter((o) => !o.done).sort((a, b) => a.land - b.land)[0];\\n    if (!soon) return { ...ZERO, x: -this.x * 0.5 };\\n    let tx = soon.x;\\n    const dodge = this.skill === 'expert' || this.skill === 'good' || this.skill === 'average';\\n    if (soon.kind === 'flip' && dodge) tx = clamp(soon.x + (soon.x < 0 ? 0.7 : -0.7), -2, 2);\\n    const err = tx - this.x;\\n    const gain = this.skill === 'sloppy' ? 0.25 : 1;\\n    return { ...ZERO, x: clamp(err * 2 * gain, -1, 1) };\\n  }\\n  onStep(dt, u, scoring) {\\n    if (scoring) this.playT += dt;\\n    const t = this.playT;\\n    if (this.daze > 0) this.daze -= dt;\\n    const speed = 4.5 * (this.daze > 0 ? 0 : u.x || 0);\\n    this.x = clamp(this.x + speed * dt, -this.lane(), this.lane());\\n    if (!scoring) return;\\n    const span = lerp(1.3, 0.7, clamp(t / 60, 0, 1)) * (this.T.headerInterval || 1) * (this.hard ? 0.8 : 1);\\n    this.spawn -= dt;\\n    if (this.spawn <= 0 && t < 58) {\\n      this.spawn += span;\\n      const roll = this.rand();\\n      const kind = roll < 0.7 ? 'coco' : roll < 0.95 ? 'flip' : 'pine';\\n      const x = (this.rand() * 2 - 1) * 1.85;\\n      this.objs.push({ x, kind, land: t + 1.4, done: false });\\n    }\\n    const radius = this.hitR * (this.hard ? 0.85 : 1);\\n    for (const o of this.objs) {\\n      if (o.done || t < o.land) continue;\\n      o.done = true;\\n      const hit = Math.abs(this.x - o.x) < radius;\\n      if (o.kind === 'coco' && hit) {\\n        this.combo += 1;\\n        const tier = this.combo >= 20 ? 4 : this.combo >= 10 ? 3 : this.combo >= 5 ? 2 : 1;\\n        this.score += 10 * tier;\\n      } else if (o.kind === 'pine' && hit) {\\n        this.combo += 1;\\n        this.score += 30;\\n      } else if (o.kind === 'flip' && hit) {\\n        this.score -= 10;\\n        this.combo = 0;\\n        this.daze = 0.6;\\n      } else if (o.kind === 'flip' && !hit) {\\n        /* dodged */\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n  scoreStars() {\\n    super.scoreStars();\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nexport class SlackSim extends Sim {\\n  _built() {\\n    this.progress = 0;\\n    this.falls = 0;\\n    this.stun = 0;\\n    this.finished = false;\\n    this.gustT = 0;\\n    this.gust = 0;\\n    this.nextGust = 6;\\n    this.kevin = false;\\n  }\\n  playFinished() {\\n    return this.finished || this.playT >= 75;\\n  }\\n  auto(dt) {\\n    if (this.skill === 'idle') return { ...ZERO };\\n    const u = this.bot.read(this.dot, dt);\\n    const limit = this.skill === 'expert' ? 0.45 : this.skill === 'good' ? 0.45 : this.skill === 'average' ? 0.4 : 0.3;\\n    u.y = Math.abs(this.dot.x) < limit && this.stun <= 0 ? 0.9 : 0;\\n    return { ...ZERO, x: u.x, y: u.y };\\n  }\\n\",\"total_lines\":1087}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-c2fc4d4d-af08-4d72-975d-07dd1f46e9dc-93","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"518→export class SlackSim extends Sim {\\n  _built() {\\n520→    this.progress = 0;\\n    this.falls = 0;\\n    this.stun = 0;\\n    this.finished = false;\\n    this.gustT = 0;\\n    this.gust = 0;\\n    this.nextGust = 6;\\n    this.kevin = false;\\n  }\\n  playFinished() {\\n530→    return this.finished || this.playT >= 75;\\n  }\\n  auto(dt) {\\n    if (this.skill === 'idle') return { ...ZERO };\\n    const u = this.bot.read(this.dot, dt);\\n    const limit = this.skill === 'expert' ? 0.45 : this.skill === 'good' ? 0.45 : this.skill === 'average' ? 0.4 : 0.3;\\n    u.y = Math.abs(this.dot.x) < limit && this.stun <= 0 ? 0.9 : 0;\\n    return { ...ZERO, x: u.x, y: u.y };\\n  }\\n  onStep(dt, u, scoring) {\\n540→    if (scoring) this.playT += dt;\\n    if (this.finished) return;\\n    const walking = (u.y || 0) > 0.3 && this.stun <= 0;\\n    const standInst = 1.2 / (this.T.dotInstability || 0.6);\\n    const walkInst = (this.T.slackWalkInst || 2.6) / (this.T.dotInstability || 0.6);\\n    const m = {\\n      inst: (walking ? walkInst : standInst) * (this.hard ? 1.1 : 1),\\n      noise: 1.25,\\n      bx: this.gust * (this.T.gustForce || 1.6),\\n      ring: 1,\\n550→    };\\n    if (this.progress >= 18 && this.progress < 24) {\\n      m.bx += 0.45;\\n      this.kevin = true;\\n    }\\n    this.stepDot(dt, { x: u.x || 0, y: 0 }, m);\\n    this.dot.y = 0;\\n    this.dot.vy = 0;\\n    if (this.gustT > 0) this.gustT -= dt;\\n    else this.gust = 0;\\n560→    if (scoring && this.stun <= 0 && walking) this.progress += 1.1 * dt;\\n    if (this.progress >= this.nextGust && this.gustT <= 0) {\\n      this.gust = this.rand() < 0.5 ? -1 : 1;\\n      this.gustT = 1;\\n      this.nextGust += 6;\\n    }\\n    if (this.stun > 0) this.stun -= dt;\\n    if (Math.abs(this.dot.x) > 1) {\\n      this.falls += 1;\\n      this.stun = 1.2;\\n570→      this.dot.x = 0;\\n      this.dot.vx = 0;\\n      this.progress = this.progress >= 20 ? 20 : this.progress >= 10 ? 10 : 0;\\n      this.nextGust = this.progress + 6;\\n    }\\n    if (this.progress >= 30) this.finished = true;\\n  }\\n  scoreStars() {\\n    this.seconds = this.playT;\\n    if (!this.finished) {\\n580→      this.stars = 0;\\n      this.score = Math.round(this.progress * 10);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    const time = this.playT;\\n    if (this.falls === 0 && time < 32) this.stars = 3;\\n    else if (this.falls <= 1 && time < 45) this.stars = 2;\\n    else this.stars = 1;\\n    if (this.hard && this.stars === 3 && time >= 30) this.stars = 2;\\n    this.score = 1000 - 60 * this.falls - 8 * (time - 27);\\n590→  }\\n}\\n\\nexport const TRAY_BOARDS = [\\n  {\\n    id: 'straight',\\n    lanes: [\\n      { z: -1.35, color: 'R', xs: [-1.5, -0.9], cup: 1.45 },\",\"content_concise\":\"518→export class SlackSim extends Sim {\\n  _built() {\\n520→    this.progress = 0;\\n    this.falls = 0;\\n    this.stun = 0;\\n    this.finished = false;\\n    this.gustT = 0;\\n    this.gust = 0;\\n    this.nextGust = 6;\\n    this.kevin = false;\\n  }\\n  playFinished() {\\n530→    return this.finished || this.playT >= 75;\\n  }\\n  auto(dt) {\\n    if (this.skill === 'idle') return { ...ZERO };\\n    const u = this.bot.read(this.dot, dt);\\n    const limit = this.skill === 'expert' ? 0.45 : this.skill === 'good' ? 0.45 : this.skill === 'average' ? 0.4 : 0.3;\\n    u.y = Math.abs(this.dot.x) < limit && this.stun <= 0 ? 0.9 : 0;\\n    return { ...ZERO, x: u.x, y: u.y };\\n  }\\n  onStep(dt, u, scoring) {\\n540→    if (scoring) this.playT += dt;\\n    if (this.finished) return;\\n    const walking = (u.y || 0) > 0.3 && this.stun <= 0;\\n    const standInst = 1.2 / (this.T.dotInstability || 0.6);\\n    const walkInst = (this.T.slackWalkInst || 2.6) / (this.T.dotInstability || 0.6);\\n    const m = {\\n      inst: (walking ? walkInst : standInst) * (this.hard ? 1.1 : 1),\\n      noise: 1.25,\\n      bx: this.gust * (this.T.gustForce || 1.6),\\n      ring: 1,\\n550→    };\\n    if (this.progress >= 18 && this.progress < 24) {\\n      m.bx += 0.45;\\n      this.kevin = true;\\n    }\\n    this.stepDot(dt, { x: u.x || 0, y: 0 }, m);\\n    this.dot.y = 0;\\n    this.dot.vy = 0;\\n    if (this.gustT > 0) this.gustT -= dt;\\n    else this.gust = 0;\\n560→    if (scoring && this.stun <= 0 && walking) this.progress += 1.1 * dt;\\n    if (this.progress >= this.nextGust && this.gustT <= 0) {\\n      this.gust = this.rand() < 0.5 ? -1 : 1;\\n      this.gustT = 1;\\n      this.nextGust += 6;\\n    }\\n    if (this.stun > 0) this.stun -= dt;\\n    if (Math.abs(this.dot.x) > 1) {\\n      this.falls += 1;\\n      this.stun = 1.2;\\n570→      this.dot.x = 0;\\n      this.dot.vx = 0;\\n      this.progress = this.progress >= 20 ? 20 : this.progress >= 10 ? 10 : 0;\\n      this.nextGust = this.progress + 6;\\n    }\\n    if (this.progress >= 30) this.finished = true;\\n  }\\n  scoreStars() {\\n    this.seconds = this.playT;\\n    if (!this.finished) {\\n580→      this.stars = 0;\\n      this.score = Math.round(this.progress * 10);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    const time = this.playT;\\n    if (this.falls === 0 && time < 32) this.stars = 3;\\n    else if (this.falls <= 1 && time < 45) this.stars = 2;\\n    else this.stars = 1;\\n    if (this.hard && this.stars === 3 && time >= 30) this.stars = 2;\\n    this.score = 1000 - 60 * this.falls - 8 * (time - 27);\\n590→  }\\n}\\n\\nexport const TRAY_BOARDS = [\\n  {\\n    id: 'straight',\\n    lanes: [\\n      { z: -1.35, color: 'R', xs: [-1.5, -0.9], cup: 1.45 },\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/core/sims.js\",\"offset\":518,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"export class SlackSim extends Sim {\\n  _built() {\\n    this.progress = 0;\\n    this.falls = 0;\\n    this.stun = 0;\\n    this.finished = false;\\n    this.gustT = 0;\\n    this.gust = 0;\\n    this.nextGust = 6;\\n    this.kevin = false;\\n  }\\n  playFinished() {\\n    return this.finished || this.playT >= 75;\\n  }\\n  auto(dt) {\\n    if (this.skill === 'idle') return { ...ZERO };\\n    const u = this.bot.read(this.dot, dt);\\n    const limit = this.skill === 'expert' ? 0.45 : this.skill === 'good' ? 0.45 : this.skill === 'average' ? 0.4 : 0.3;\\n    u.y = Math.abs(this.dot.x) < limit && this.stun <= 0 ? 0.9 : 0;\\n    return { ...ZERO, x: u.x, y: u.y };\\n  }\\n  onStep(dt, u, scoring) {\\n    if (scoring) this.playT += dt;\\n    if (this.finished) return;\\n    const walking = (u.y || 0) > 0.3 && this.stun <= 0;\\n    const standInst = 1.2 / (this.T.dotInstability || 0.6);\\n    const walkInst = (this.T.slackWalkInst || 2.6) / (this.T.dotInstability || 0.6);\\n    const m = {\\n      inst: (walking ? walkInst : standInst) * (this.hard ? 1.1 : 1),\\n      noise: 1.25,\\n      bx: this.gust * (this.T.gustForce || 1.6),\\n      ring: 1,\\n    };\\n    if (this.progress >= 18 && this.progress < 24) {\\n      m.bx += 0.45;\\n      this.kevin = true;\\n    }\\n    this.stepDot(dt, { x: u.x || 0, y: 0 }, m);\\n    this.dot.y = 0;\\n    this.dot.vy = 0;\\n    if (this.gustT > 0) this.gustT -= dt;\\n    else this.gust = 0;\\n    if (scoring && this.stun <= 0 && walking) this.progress += 1.1 * dt;\\n    if (this.progress >= this.nextGust && this.gustT <= 0) {\\n      this.gust = this.rand() < 0.5 ? -1 : 1;\\n      this.gustT = 1;\\n      this.nextGust += 6;\\n    }\\n    if (this.stun > 0) this.stun -= dt;\\n    if (Math.abs(this.dot.x) > 1) {\\n      this.falls += 1;\\n      this.stun = 1.2;\\n      this.dot.x = 0;\\n      this.dot.vx = 0;\\n      this.progress = this.progress >= 20 ? 20 : this.progress >= 10 ? 10 : 0;\\n      this.nextGust = this.progress + 6;\\n    }\\n    if (this.progress >= 30) this.finished = true;\\n  }\\n  scoreStars() {\\n    this.seconds = this.playT;\\n    if (!this.finished) {\\n      this.stars = 0;\\n      this.score = Math.round(this.progress * 10);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    const time = this.playT;\\n    if (this.falls === 0 && time < 32) this.stars = 3;\\n    else if (this.falls <= 1 && time < 45) this.stars = 2;\\n    else this.stars = 1;\\n    if (this.hard && this.stars === 3 && time >= 30) this.stars = 2;\\n    this.score = 1000 - 60 * this.falls - 8 * (time - 27);\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nexport const TRAY_BOARDS = [\\n  {\\n    id: 'straight',\\n    lanes: [\\n      { z: -1.35, color: 'R', xs: [-1.5, -0.9], cup: 1.45 },\\n\",\"total_lines\":1087}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-c2fc4d4d-af08-4d72-975d-07dd1f46e9dc-94","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"820→    this.score = 70 * pace + 30 * cups;\\n    // pace and cups are 0..1. The published score is on a 0..100 scale.\\n    this.score = 100 * (0.7 * pace + 0.3 * cups);\\n    super.scoreStars();\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nexport class PierSim extends Sim {\\n  _built() {\\n    this.attempt = 0;\\n830→    this.best = 0;\\n    this.phaseLocal = 'run';\\n    this.localT = 0;\\n    this.zoneT = 0;\\n    this.speed = 6;\\n    this.pressed = false;\\n    this.flightIn = 0;\\n    this.flightN = 0;\\n    this.cannon = false;\\n    this.attemptT = 0;\\n840→  }\\n  playFinished() {\\n    return this.attempt >= 3;\\n  }\\n  botTarget() {\\n    if (this.phaseLocal === 'run') return { x: 0, y: -0.6 };\\n    return { x: 0, y: 0 };\\n  }\\n  auto(dt) {\\n    if (this.skill === 'idle') return { ...ZERO };\\n850→    const u = this.bot.read(this.dot, dt);\\n    const tight = this.skill === 'expert' || this.skill === 'good';\\n    if (this.phaseLocal === 'run' && tight) {\\n      const y = this.dot.y;\\n      if (y > -0.48) u.y = -1;\\n      else if (y < -0.74) u.y = 1;\\n      else u.y = clamp((-0.62 - y) * 8 - this.dot.vy * 2, -1, 1);\\n      u.x = clamp(-this.dot.x * 6 - this.dot.vx, -1, 1);\\n    } else if (this.phaseLocal === 'run' && this.dot.y > -0.45) {\\n      u.y = Math.min(u.y, -0.85);\\n860→    }\\n    if (this.phaseLocal === 'flight' && tight) {\\n      u.x = clamp(-this.dot.x * 8 - this.dot.vx * 2, -1, 1);\\n      u.y = clamp(-this.dot.y * 8 - this.dot.vy * 2, -1, 1);\\n    }\\n    const lip = this.phaseLocal === 'run' && this.localT >= 5 - dt - 1e-4 && this.localT < 5;\\n    const press = tight && lip;\\n    return { ...ZERO, x: u.x, y: u.y, confirm: press };\\n  }\\n  onStep(dt, u, scoring) {\\n870→    if (!scoring) return;\\n    this.playT += dt;\\n    this.localT += dt;\\n    this.attemptT += dt;\\n    if (this.phaseLocal === 'run') {\\n      const inZone = this.dot.y < -0.4 && this.dot.y > -0.8;\\n      if (inZone) this.zoneT += dt;\\n      const m = { noise: 1, inst: 1, ring: 0.5 };\\n      this.stepDot(dt, u, m);\\n      if (u.confirm && !this.pressed && this.localT > 4.2) {\\n880→        this.pressed = true;\\n        this.lipDt = Math.abs(this.localT - 5);\\n      }\\n      if (this.localT >= 5) {\\n        this.speed = 6 + 8 * clamp(this.zoneT / 5, 0, 1);\\n        this.phaseLocal = 'flight';\\n        this.localT = 0;\\n        this.flightIn = 0;\\n        this.flightN = 0;\\n        const p = this.pressed ? clamp(1 - (this.lipDt || 0.25) / 0.25, 0, 1) : 0;\\n890→        this.p = p;\\n        // The run ends in a crouch. The flight is a fresh balance.\\n        this.dot.x = 0;\\n        this.dot.y = 0;\\n        this.dot.vx = 0;\\n        this.dot.vy = 0;\\n        this.dot.ux = 0;\\n        this.dot.uy = 0;\\n      }\\n    } else if (this.phaseLocal === 'flight') {\\n900→      const ring = this.ringOf(0.45);\\n      const m = { inst: 3, noise: 1, ring };\\n      this.stepDot(dt, u, m);\\n      this.flightN += 1;\\n      if (Math.hypot(this.dot.x, this.dot.y) < ring) this.flightIn += 1;\\n      if (u.confirm && this.localT > 3) this.cannon = true;\\n      if (this.localT >= 3.5) {\\n        const ringFrac = this.flightN ? this.flightIn / this.flightN : 0;\\n        const dist = this.speed * (0.8 + 0.6 * (this.p || 0)) * (0.6 + 0.4 * ringFrac) * (this.T.pierBoost || 2.14);\\n        this.lastJump = { speed: this.speed, p: this.p || 0, ringFrac, dist, zone: this.zoneT };\\n910→        (this.jumps ||= []).push(this.lastJump);\\n        if (dist > this.best) this.best = dist;\\n        this.attempt += 1;\\n        this.phaseLocal = 'run';\\n        this.localT = 0;\\n        this.zoneT = 0;\\n        this.pressed = false;\\n        this.speed = 6;\\n        this.p = 0;\\n        this.dot.x = 0;\\n920→        this.dot.y = 0;\\n        this.dot.vx = 0;\\n        this.dot.vy = 0;\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n  scoreStars() {\\n    this.score = this.best;\\n    super.scoreStars();\\n  }\\n930→}\\n\\nexport const LONG_EVENTS = [\\n  { t: 0, ring: 0.4, say: 'Stand.' },\\n  { t: 10, bias: 0.1 },\\n  { t: 20, impulse: -0.6 },\\n  { t: 30, ring: 0.34 },\\n  { t: 35, noise: 1.2 },\\n  { t: 45, say: 'Ignore her.' },\\n  { t: 50, ring: 0.28 },\",\"content_concise\":\"820→    this.score = 70 * pace + 30 * cups;\\n    // pace and cups are 0..1. The published score is on a 0..100 scale.\\n    this.score = 100 * (0.7 * pace + 0.3 * cups);\\n    super.scoreStars();\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nexport class PierSim extends Sim {\\n  _built() {\\n    this.attempt = 0;\\n830→    this.best = 0;\\n    this.phaseLocal = 'run';\\n    this.localT = 0;\\n    this.zoneT = 0;\\n    this.speed = 6;\\n    this.pressed = false;\\n    this.flightIn = 0;\\n    this.flightN = 0;\\n    this.cannon = false;\\n    this.attemptT = 0;\\n840→  }\\n  playFinished() {\\n    return this.attempt >= 3;\\n  }\\n  botTarget() {\\n    if (this.phaseLocal === 'run') return { x: 0, y: -0.6 };\\n    return { x: 0, y: 0 };\\n  }\\n  auto(dt) {\\n    if (this.skill === 'idle') return { ...ZERO };\\n850→    const u = this.bot.read(this.dot, dt);\\n    const tight = this.skill === 'expert' || this.skill === 'good';\\n    if (this.phaseLocal === 'run' && tight) {\\n      const y = this.dot.y;\\n      if (y > -0.48) u.y = -1;\\n      else if (y < -0.74) u.y = 1;\\n      else u.y = clamp((-0.62 - y) * 8 - this.dot.vy * 2, -1, 1);\\n      u.x = clamp(-this.dot.x * 6 - this.dot.vx, -1, 1);\\n    } else if (this.phaseLocal === 'run' && this.dot.y > -0.45) {\\n      u.y = Math.min(u.y, -0.85);\\n860→    }\\n    if (this.phaseLocal === 'flight' && tight) {\\n      u.x = clamp(-this.dot.x * 8 - this.dot.vx * 2, -1, 1);\\n      u.y = clamp(-this.dot.y * 8 - this.dot.vy * 2, -1, 1);\\n    }\\n    const lip = this.phaseLocal === 'run' && this.localT >= 5 - dt - 1e-4 && this.localT < 5;\\n    const press = tight && lip;\\n    return { ...ZERO, x: u.x, y: u.y, confirm: press };\\n  }\\n  onStep(dt, u, scoring) {\\n870→    if (!scoring) return;\\n    this.playT += dt;\\n    this.localT += dt;\\n    this.attemptT += dt;\\n    if (this.phaseLocal === 'run') {\\n      const inZone = this.dot.y < -0.4 && this.dot.y > -0.8;\\n      if (inZone) this.zoneT += dt;\\n      const m = { noise: 1, inst: 1, ring: 0.5 };\\n      this.stepDot(dt, u, m);\\n      if (u.confirm && !this.pressed && this.localT > 4.2) {\\n880→        this.pressed = true;\\n        this.lipDt = Math.abs(this.localT - 5);\\n      }\\n      if (this.localT >= 5) {\\n        this.speed = 6 + 8 * clamp(this.zoneT / 5, 0, 1);\\n        this.phaseLocal = 'flight';\\n        this.localT = 0;\\n        this.flightIn = 0;\\n        this.flightN = 0;\\n        const p = this.pressed ? clamp(1 - (this.lipDt || 0.25) / 0.25, 0, 1) : 0;\\n890→        this.p = p;\\n        // The run ends in a crouch. The flight is a fresh balance.\\n        this.dot.x = 0;\\n        this.dot.y = 0;\\n        this.dot.vx = 0;\\n        this.dot.vy = 0;\\n        this.dot.ux = 0;\\n        this.dot.uy = 0;\\n      }\\n    } else if (this.phaseLocal === 'flight') {\\n900→      const ring = this.ringOf(0.45);\\n      const m = { inst: 3, noise: 1, ring };\\n      this.stepDot(dt, u, m);\\n      this.flightN += 1;\\n      if (Math.hypot(this.dot.x, this.dot.y) < ring) this.flightIn += 1;\\n      if (u.confirm && this.localT > 3) this.cannon = true;\\n      if (this.localT >= 3.5) {\\n        const ringFrac = this.flightN ? this.flightIn / this.flightN : 0;\\n        const dist = this.speed * (0.8 + 0.6 * (this.p || 0)) * (0.6 + 0.4 * ringFrac) * (this.T.pierBoost || 2.14);\\n        this.lastJump = { speed: this.speed, p: this.p || 0, ringFrac, dist, zone: this.zoneT };\\n910→        (this.jumps ||= []).push(this.lastJump);\\n        if (dist > this.best) this.best = dist;\\n        this.attempt += 1;\\n        this.phaseLocal = 'run';\\n        this.localT = 0;\\n        this.zoneT = 0;\\n        this.pressed = false;\\n        this.speed = 6;\\n        this.p = 0;\\n        this.dot.x = 0;\\n920→        this.dot.y = 0;\\n        this.dot.vx = 0;\\n        this.dot.vy = 0;\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n  scoreStars() {\\n    this.score = this.best;\\n    super.scoreStars();\\n  }\\n930→}\\n\\nexport const LONG_EVENTS = [\\n  { t: 0, ring: 0.4, say: 'Stand.' },\\n  { t: 10, bias: 0.1 },\\n  { t: 20, impulse: -0.6 },\\n  { t: 30, ring: 0.34 },\\n  { t: 35, noise: 1.2 },\\n  { t: 45, say: 'Ignore her.' },\\n  { t: 50, ring: 0.28 },\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/core/sims.js\",\"offset\":820,\"limit\":120,\"raw_output\":\"    this.score = 70 * pace + 30 * cups;\\n    // pace and cups are 0..1. The published score is on a 0..100 scale.\\n    this.score = 100 * (0.7 * pace + 0.3 * cups);\\n    super.scoreStars();\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nexport class PierSim extends Sim {\\n  _built() {\\n    this.attempt = 0;\\n    this.best = 0;\\n    this.phaseLocal = 'run';\\n    this.localT = 0;\\n    this.zoneT = 0;\\n    this.speed = 6;\\n    this.pressed = false;\\n    this.flightIn = 0;\\n    this.flightN = 0;\\n    this.cannon = false;\\n    this.attemptT = 0;\\n  }\\n  playFinished() {\\n    return this.attempt >= 3;\\n  }\\n  botTarget() {\\n    if (this.phaseLocal === 'run') return { x: 0, y: -0.6 };\\n    return { x: 0, y: 0 };\\n  }\\n  auto(dt) {\\n    if (this.skill === 'idle') return { ...ZERO };\\n    const u = this.bot.read(this.dot, dt);\\n    const tight = this.skill === 'expert' || this.skill === 'good';\\n    if (this.phaseLocal === 'run' && tight) {\\n      const y = this.dot.y;\\n      if (y > -0.48) u.y = -1;\\n      else if (y < -0.74) u.y = 1;\\n      else u.y = clamp((-0.62 - y) * 8 - this.dot.vy * 2, -1, 1);\\n      u.x = clamp(-this.dot.x * 6 - this.dot.vx, -1, 1);\\n    } else if (this.phaseLocal === 'run' && this.dot.y > -0.45) {\\n      u.y = Math.min(u.y, -0.85);\\n    }\\n    if (this.phaseLocal === 'flight' && tight) {\\n      u.x = clamp(-this.dot.x * 8 - this.dot.vx * 2, -1, 1);\\n      u.y = clamp(-this.dot.y * 8 - this.dot.vy * 2, -1, 1);\\n    }\\n    const lip = this.phaseLocal === 'run' && this.localT >= 5 - dt - 1e-4 && this.localT < 5;\\n    const press = tight && lip;\\n    return { ...ZERO, x: u.x, y: u.y, confirm: press };\\n  }\\n  onStep(dt, u, scoring) {\\n    if (!scoring) return;\\n    this.playT += dt;\\n    this.localT += dt;\\n    this.attemptT += dt;\\n    if (this.phaseLocal === 'run') {\\n      const inZone = this.dot.y < -0.4 && this.dot.y > -0.8;\\n      if (inZone) this.zoneT += dt;\\n      const m = { noise: 1, inst: 1, ring: 0.5 };\\n      this.stepDot(dt, u, m);\\n      if (u.confirm && !this.pressed && this.localT > 4.2) {\\n        this.pressed = true;\\n        this.lipDt = Math.abs(this.localT - 5);\\n      }\\n      if (this.localT >= 5) {\\n        this.speed = 6 + 8 * clamp(this.zoneT / 5, 0, 1);\\n        this.phaseLocal = 'flight';\\n        this.localT = 0;\\n        this.flightIn = 0;\\n        this.flightN = 0;\\n        const p = this.pressed ? clamp(1 - (this.lipDt || 0.25) / 0.25, 0, 1) : 0;\\n        this.p = p;\\n        // The run ends in a crouch. The flight is a fresh balance.\\n        this.dot.x = 0;\\n        this.dot.y = 0;\\n        this.dot.vx = 0;\\n        this.dot.vy = 0;\\n        this.dot.ux = 0;\\n        this.dot.uy = 0;\\n      }\\n    } else if (this.phaseLocal === 'flight') {\\n      const ring = this.ringOf(0.45);\\n      const m = { inst: 3, noise: 1, ring };\\n      this.stepDot(dt, u, m);\\n      this.flightN += 1;\\n      if (Math.hypot(this.dot.x, this.dot.y) < ring) this.flightIn += 1;\\n      if (u.confirm && this.localT > 3) this.cannon = true;\\n      if (this.localT >= 3.5) {\\n        const ringFrac = this.flightN ? this.flightIn / this.flightN : 0;\\n        const dist = this.speed * (0.8 + 0.6 * (this.p || 0)) * (0.6 + 0.4 * ringFrac) * (this.T.pierBoost || 2.14);\\n        this.lastJump = { speed: this.speed, p: this.p || 0, ringFrac, dist, zone: this.zoneT };\\n        (this.jumps ||= []).push(this.lastJump);\\n        if (dist > this.best) this.best = dist;\\n        this.attempt += 1;\\n        this.phaseLocal = 'run';\\n        this.localT = 0;\\n        this.zoneT = 0;\\n        this.pressed = false;\\n        this.speed = 6;\\n        this.p = 0;\\n        this.dot.x = 0;\\n        this.dot.y = 0;\\n        this.dot.vx = 0;\\n        this.dot.vy = 0;\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n  scoreStars() {\\n    this.score = this.best;\\n    super.scoreStars();\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nexport const LONG_EVENTS = [\\n  { t: 0, ring: 0.4, say: 'Stand.' },\\n  { t: 10, bias: 0.1 },\\n  { t: 20, impulse: -0.6 },\\n  { t: 30, ring: 0.34 },\\n  { t: 35, noise: 1.2 },\\n  { t: 45, say: 'Ignore her.' },\\n  { t: 50, ring: 0.28 },\\n\",\"total_lines\":1087}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"782a942d-0b21-46a4-86c5-25b979552c40"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_149","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The header stays idle at x=0. Coconuts spawn at random x positions.\n\nIdle and Slack states score zero stars. The plan is ready. Writing files now.\n\nWorld imports are being set up from the pixel engine. compileClips will be used per clip for analyzeClip. The test file will be comprehensive and clean.\n\nA tools/shot.mjs script will handle screenshots. Playwright imports from the dev folder node_modules. The PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE environment variable must be exported in commands because shell tools may not source bashrc. Headless mode works without xvfb.\n\nChromium will use SwiftShader for Vulkan and WebGPU. File URLs need encoding because paths contain spaces. The default headless width of 480 fits the HUD widgets. The ghost test pushes a message and step while dot.t stays at zero and shown.x moves toward the target.\n\nMedley windows will be sampled by stepping the simulation in chunks and reading app.medleyT. Four bots will finish the podium with scores between 0 and 3000. The batch simulation should finish in about five to twenty seconds. Engine.step(120) will run in a loop, and any step() exceptions will be caught and reported. setDriver must be called before go so skipIntro is active at creation time.\n\nThe guest for the drips test is set to Ada in slot zero with drop disabled. The finishActivity formula will be checked against 2 plus 3 times stars plus floor of seconds over 30 plus bonus, and the prescription flag must match. Hard mode is enabled for that test.\n\nThe plank activity test will use the expert driver and expect at least two stars. Hard mode is confirmed to flow from the guest object into the simulation. The world file will import THREE.Color and RingGeometry for visual clarity. ContactShadow will be added to the hero mesh. Physics boxes are omitted unless necessary.\n\nA static floor collider will be added for the hero so it does not fall. Physics initialization is fast in headless mode, and any failure will be caught and skipped to keep setup alive. The dot mesh is always present. The session scene will use fewer meshes: ground, four colored mats, and an ounce.\n\nThe four colored mats will use toonMaterial with palette names—red, blue, lime, and sand—instead of exact hex values. Scene fog is not required.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-62b964e8-9783-4077-81cd-dce8f23413a0-95","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/data/about.js","offset":70,"limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":9188,"output_tokens":1597,"cache_read_input_tokens":137600,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"70b8fb7f-0478-49e7-afeb-efdf5101856a"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-62b964e8-9783-4077-81cd-dce8f23413a0-95","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"70→\\n/** Pages for the in-game screen. Built only from the fields above. */\\nexport function aboutPages(creditsText) {\\n  const src = SOURCE_INFORMATION;\\n  const pages = [\\n    { title: 'A note', lines: [MEDICAL] },\\n    {\\n      title: 'Source Information',\\n      lines: [\\n        `Date: ${src.date}`,\\n80→        `Source: ${src.source}`,\\n        `Plan: ${src.plan}`,\\n        `Genre: ${src.genre}`,\\n        `Perspective: ${src.perspective}`,\\n        `Tech: ${src.tech}`,\\n        `Art Direction: ${src.artDirection}`,\\n        `Animation: ${src.animation}`,\\n        `Audio: ${src.audio}`,\\n        `Online: ${src.online}`,\\n        `Testing: ${src.testing}`,\\n90→        `Research: ${src.research}`,\\n        `Environment: ${src.environment}`,\\n        `Model: ${src.model}`,\\n        `Usage: ${src.usage}`,\\n      ],\\n    },\\n    { title: 'Testing Feedback', lines: TESTING_FEEDBACK.map((t, i) => `${i + 1}. ${t}`) },\\n    { title: 'Engine Feedback', lines: ENGINE_FEEDBACK.map((t, i) => `${i + 1}. ${t}`) },\\n    { title: 'Prompt Feedback', lines: PROMPT_FEEDBACK.map((t, i) => `${i + 1}. ${t}`) },\\n    { title: 'Kit credits', lines: [KIT_CREDITS, 'Kenney, three.js, Rapier, and Sweetie 16.'] },\\n100→  ];\\n  const full = String(creditsText || '').split(/\\\\r?\\\\n/);\\n  const size = 8;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < full.length; i += size) {\\n    pages.push({ title: i === 0 ? 'Credits' : 'Credits', lines: full.slice(i, i + size) });\\n  }\\n  return pages;\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"70→\\n/** Pages for the in-game screen. Built only from the fields above. */\\nexport function aboutPages(creditsText) {\\n  const src = SOURCE_INFORMATION;\\n  const pages = [\\n    { title: 'A note', lines: [MEDICAL] },\\n    {\\n      title: 'Source Information',\\n      lines: [\\n        `Date: ${src.date}`,\\n80→        `Source: ${src.source}`,\\n        `Plan: ${src.plan}`,\\n        `Genre: ${src.genre}`,\\n        `Perspective: ${src.perspective}`,\\n        `Tech: ${src.tech}`,\\n        `Art Direction: ${src.artDirection}`,\\n        `Animation: ${src.animation}`,\\n        `Audio: ${src.audio}`,\\n        `Online: ${src.online}`,\\n        `Testing: ${src.testing}`,\\n90→        `Research: ${src.research}`,\\n        `Environment: ${src.environment}`,\\n        `Model: ${src.model}`,\\n        `Usage: ${src.usage}`,\\n      ],\\n    },\\n    { title: 'Testing Feedback', lines: TESTING_FEEDBACK.map((t, i) => `${i + 1}. ${t}`) },\\n    { title: 'Engine Feedback', lines: ENGINE_FEEDBACK.map((t, i) => `${i + 1}. ${t}`) },\\n    { title: 'Prompt Feedback', lines: PROMPT_FEEDBACK.map((t, i) => `${i + 1}. ${t}`) },\\n    { title: 'Kit credits', lines: [KIT_CREDITS, 'Kenney, three.js, Rapier, and Sweetie 16.'] },\\n100→  ];\\n  const full = String(creditsText || '').split(/\\\\r?\\\\n/);\\n  const size = 8;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < full.length; i += size) {\\n    pages.push({ title: i === 0 ? 'Credits' : 'Credits', lines: full.slice(i, i + size) });\\n  }\\n  return pages;\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/data/about.js\",\"offset\":70,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"\\n/** Pages for the in-game screen. Built only from the fields above. */\\nexport function aboutPages(creditsText) {\\n  const src = SOURCE_INFORMATION;\\n  const pages = [\\n    { title: 'A note', lines: [MEDICAL] },\\n    {\\n      title: 'Source Information',\\n      lines: [\\n        `Date: ${src.date}`,\\n        `Source: ${src.source}`,\\n        `Plan: ${src.plan}`,\\n        `Genre: ${src.genre}`,\\n        `Perspective: ${src.perspective}`,\\n        `Tech: ${src.tech}`,\\n        `Art Direction: ${src.artDirection}`,\\n        `Animation: ${src.animation}`,\\n        `Audio: ${src.audio}`,\\n        `Online: ${src.online}`,\\n        `Testing: ${src.testing}`,\\n        `Research: ${src.research}`,\\n        `Environment: ${src.environment}`,\\n        `Model: ${src.model}`,\\n        `Usage: ${src.usage}`,\\n      ],\\n    },\\n    { title: 'Testing Feedback', lines: TESTING_FEEDBACK.map((t, i) => `${i + 1}. ${t}`) },\\n    { title: 'Engine Feedback', lines: ENGINE_FEEDBACK.map((t, i) => `${i + 1}. ${t}`) },\\n    { title: 'Prompt Feedback', lines: PROMPT_FEEDBACK.map((t, i) => `${i + 1}. ${t}`) },\\n    { title: 'Kit credits', lines: [KIT_CREDITS, 'Kenney, three.js, Rapier, and Sweetie 16.'] },\\n  ];\\n  const full = String(creditsText || '').split(/\\\\r?\\\\n/);\\n  const size = 8;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < full.length; i += size) {\\n    pages.push({ title: i === 0 ? 'Credits' : 'Credits', lines: full.slice(i, i + size) });\\n  }\\n  return pages;\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":107}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"605b709a-885f-4aad-86c2-5b47c31a39d3"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_150","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The About screen displays six lines at a time and supports page flipping.\n\nCredits text spans many pages. The HTML will be larger but that is required. I will now write all the code. I will start with app.js fixes. Then I will edit world, main, build, test, and shot.\n\nI will initialize hubClock to false in the constructor. In tickMedley, ghost lanes will hide when the target is set and the shown index does not match the winning lane. Bot lanes will use auto input from their simulation, while pad lanes will read from the driver.\n\nKey lanes will read input from the keyboard driver. The KeyE menu trigger now requires the mode to be neither name nor dev. The startWeigh method will be replaced inside the class. The old weighCtor and prototype block will be removed, but the clamp functions before it will remain.\n\nThe app.js imports now include title, TAGLINE, WeighSim, font utilities, about pages, and credits text. The startWeigh method will be implemented from the old prototype body. A save reload bug was fixed: if a guest exists but lacks today's date, the activation slots now set it automatically.\n\nDrop-in guests with unlockAll will not receive drips during finishActivity. Persist writes to storage, while tests use a memory map. A pump helper will step the engine until idle mode accumulates ten seconds of time, capped at eight hundred frames.\n\nThe pump helper returns the frame count when the predicate is satisfied, or -1 if the limit is reached. During attract mode, a frame that begins attract will not immediately exit from input on that same frame; idle increments before attract starts, and subsequent frames without input keep the simulation running. Tapping Enter exits attract and returns to the title screen.\n\nPlay mode will step 800 frames and remain in activity or results. The idle timer is real, so a short activity still counts toward the ten-second attract threshold.\n\nFor menu attract tests, using keys to reach settings is more realistic than calling app.go('settings') directly.\n\nThe full attract loop lasts 140 seconds, or 8400 frames. I will step the engine until every activity ID is seen or until 20000 frames pass. Expert mode with god and ring upgrades may finish activities before the 14-second threshold, so the loop must continue through the remaining IDs.\n\nThe attract loop will step the engine in batches of thirty frames. Twenty thousand frames is roughly 333 seconds, more than enough to cover the full 140-second cycle. The pause and resume test will record the dot's exact position, step while paused, then verify that resuming restores timeScale and resumes play from the same spot.\n\nThe pause test will assert that playT increases after resume while remaining unchanged during the pause window. I confirmed the engine runs fixedUpdate before update each frame, so setting timeScale to zero correctly skips the fixed step and leaves the dot stable.\n\nThe build script will resolve the workspace root as the parent of the dev folder. The output HTML will be named Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607.html.\n\nThe build script will import TITLE and exitInterview from the source data files. It will write exit-interview.json with HUB metadata and parse it back to verify validity. The esbuild bundle will output to dev/.build/bundle.js. The HTML is self-contained, so no extra file copies are needed.\n\nThe pixel-engine bundle is ready. The SHA test will compare the file on disk rather than the bundle itself.\n\nI will add a browser test that checks the title and verify the HTML contains session.js content without fetching external HTTP resources.\n\nshot.mjs will export an async shoot function for direct import, with a CLI entry point if run as main. The capture logic will sample every sixteenth pixel to detect painted frames.\n\nThe painted-frame check compares the sampled pixel range. It fails if the variance is under twelve, rejecting flat-color frames. The capture buffer must match the viewport aspect fill size, which equals the canvas backing store at device pixel ratio.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-97ce65b5-315a-4059-8f51-ddfee25033c1-96","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"aspect === 'fill'|fill","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/types/engine/framing.d.ts"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2156,"output_tokens":2641,"cache_read_input_tokens":146688,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"727c8806-7733-4cb4-8233-1bde7a8b15ff"}
