{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-2c128193-baff-4cf2-88d4-2d9895be14d2-124","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,49,54,48,55,95,95,120,54,57,56,49,101,51,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,78,111,32,109,97,116,99,104,101,115,32,102,111,117,110,100,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":1,\"match_count\":0,\"file_matches\":[]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-2c128193-baff-4cf2-88d4-2d9895be14d2-125","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"3520→### interface VariantGroup\\n\\nOne def standing for its variants (the defs that share its `variantName`), and the others.\\n\\n- `readonly def: T`\\n- `readonly variants: readonly T[]`\\n\\n### variantName()\\n\\n```ts\\n3530→function variantName(id: string): string\\n```\\n\\nThe name a model's variants share: its id without its last part that is one letter or a\\nnumber, at the end or before the rest of the name (`kenney-nature/rock-large-a` … `-f`,\\n`crate-1` … `-3`, `tree-pine-tall-a-detailed` … `-d-detailed` → `kenney-nature/rock-large`,\\n`crate`, `tree-pine-tall-detailed`). An id without one is its own. For models: a sheet's\\nlettered tiles (`forest-a` … `-i`) are pieces of a set, not variants.\\n\\n## 12. Animation toolkit\\n3540→\\n### analyzeClip()\\n\\n```ts\\nfunction analyzeClip(model: Object3D, rig: RigSpec, def: ClipDef, clip: AnimationClip): ClipReport\\n```\\n\\n### interface ClipDef\\n\\n- `name: string`\\n3550→- `frames: number`: Length in frames at 30 fps.\\n- `loop?: boolean`\\n- `keys: readonly Key[]`\\n- `layers?: readonly Layer[]`\\n- `feet?: readonly FeetKey[]`: Feet track: foot goals interpolated between its own keys and solved with IK every frame, overriding the keyed leg rotations. Use it whenever feet touch the floor through a transition (kneel → stand, sit → lie) so they roll instead of sinking.\\n- `speed?: number`: Ground speed (m/s) the clip is authored for at playback rate 1. Locomotion clips set this; metrics then measure foot sliding against it and the runtime can scale playback.\\n- `stance?: number`: Gait cycles (gaitClip): the share of the cycle each foot is planted. The right heel strikes at phase 0, the left at 0.5, so the right foot is mid-stance at `stance / 2`.\\n- `reach?: number`: Gaits: how far ahead of the hips (m) the middle of the stance is (feet touch down `reach` + half a stance's ground ahead).\\n- `grounded?: boolean`: Grounded clip: soles should rest on y = 0 (metrics flag floating / penetration).\\n- `fast?: boolean`: Intentionally snappy (flips, punches, launches): skip the angular-speed warning.\",\"content_concise\":\"3520→### interface VariantGroup\\n\\nOne def standing for its variants (the defs that share its `variantName`), and the others.\\n\\n- `readonly def: T`\\n- `readonly variants: readonly T[]`\\n\\n### variantName()\\n\\n```ts\\n3530→function variantName(id: string): string\\n```\\n\\nThe name a model's variants share: its id without its last part that is one letter or a\\nnumber, at the end or before the rest of the name (`kenney-nature/rock-large-a` … `-f`,\\n`crate-1` … `-3`, `tree-pine-tall-a-detailed` … `-d-detailed` → `kenney-nature/rock-large`,\\n`crate`, `tree-pine-tall-detailed`). An id without one is its own. For models: a sheet's\\nlettered tiles (`forest-a` … `-i`) are pieces of a set, not variants.\\n\\n## 12. Animation toolkit\\n3540→\\n### analyzeClip()\\n\\n```ts\\nfunction analyzeClip(model: Object3D, rig: RigSpec, def: ClipDef, clip: AnimationClip): ClipReport\\n```\\n\\n### interface ClipDef\\n\\n- `name: string`\\n3550→- `frames: number`: Length in frames at 30 fps.\\n- `loop?: boolean`\\n- `keys: readonly Key[]`\\n- `layers?: readonly Layer[]`\\n- `feet?: readonly FeetKey[]`: Feet track: foot goals interpolated between its own keys and solved with IK every frame, overriding the keyed leg rotations. Use it whenever feet touch the floor through a transition (kneel → stand, sit → lie) so they roll instead of sinking.\\n- `speed?: number`: Ground speed (m/s) the clip is authored for at playback rate 1. Locomotion clips set this; metrics then measure foot sliding against it and the runtime can scale playback.\\n- `stance?: number`: Gait cycles (gaitClip): the share of the cycle each foot is planted. The right heel strikes at phase 0, the left at 0.5, so the right foot is mid-stance at `stance / 2`.\\n- `reach?: number`: Gaits: how far ahead of the hips (m) the middle of the stance is (feet touch down `reach` + half a stance's ground ahead).\\n- `grounded?: boolean`: Grounded clip: soles should rest on y = 0 (metrics flag floating / penetration).\\n- `fast?: boolean`: Intentionally snappy (flips, punches, launches): skip the angular-speed warning.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/API.md\",\"offset\":3520,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"### interface VariantGroup\\n\\nOne def standing for its variants (the defs that share its `variantName`), and the others.\\n\\n- `readonly def: T`\\n- `readonly variants: readonly T[]`\\n\\n### variantName()\\n\\n```ts\\nfunction variantName(id: string): string\\n```\\n\\nThe name a model's variants share: its id without its last part that is one letter or a\\nnumber, at the end or before the rest of the name (`kenney-nature/rock-large-a` … `-f`,\\n`crate-1` … `-3`, `tree-pine-tall-a-detailed` … `-d-detailed` → `kenney-nature/rock-large`,\\n`crate`, `tree-pine-tall-detailed`). An id without one is its own. For models: a sheet's\\nlettered tiles (`forest-a` … `-i`) are pieces of a set, not variants.\\n\\n## 12. Animation toolkit\\n\\n### analyzeClip()\\n\\n```ts\\nfunction analyzeClip(model: Object3D, rig: RigSpec, def: ClipDef, clip: AnimationClip): ClipReport\\n```\\n\\n### interface ClipDef\\n\\n- `name: string`\\n- `frames: number`: Length in frames at 30 fps.\\n- `loop?: boolean`\\n- `keys: readonly Key[]`\\n- `layers?: readonly Layer[]`\\n- `feet?: readonly FeetKey[]`: Feet track: foot goals interpolated between its own keys and solved with IK every frame, overriding the keyed leg rotations. Use it whenever feet touch the floor through a transition (kneel → stand, sit → lie) so they roll instead of sinking.\\n- `speed?: number`: Ground speed (m/s) the clip is authored for at playback rate 1. Locomotion clips set this; metrics then measure foot sliding against it and the runtime can scale playback.\\n- `stance?: number`: Gait cycles (gaitClip): the share of the cycle each foot is planted. The right heel strikes at phase 0, the left at 0.5, so the right foot is mid-stance at `stance / 2`.\\n- `reach?: number`: Gaits: how far ahead of the hips (m) the middle of the stance is (feet touch down `reach` + half a stance's ground ahead).\\n- `grounded?: boolean`: Grounded clip: soles should rest on y = 0 (metrics flag floating / penetration).\\n- `fast?: boolean`: Intentionally snappy (flips, punches, launches): skip the angular-speed warning.\\n\",\"total_lines\":5143}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"be65b605-17fa-4d5f-a219-89c22c54c855"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_165","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"restPoseOf might not be exported from the package index.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c825021d-70af-4339-935d-3d17bc965c14-126","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"cd \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607\" && node --input-type=module -e '\nimport { Engine, analyzeClip, compileClips, HERO_RIG, validateClip } from \"./pixel-engine.js\";\nimport { App } from \"./src/app.js\";\nimport { World } from \"./src/scenes/world.js\";\nimport { CLIPS } from \"./src/art/clips.js\";\nconst app = new App({ storage: null });\nconst world = new World(app);\nawait Engine.headless(world, { viewport: { width: 320, height: 180 }, camera: { preset: \"fixed\", position: [9,7,11], target: [0,1,0] } });\nconst model = world.heroModel;\nfor (const def of CLIPS) {\n  const v = validateClip(def, HERO_RIG);\n  const clip = compileClips([def], HERO_RIG, model)[0];\n  const report = analyzeClip(model, HERO_RIG, def, clip);\n  const probs = report.problems || [];\n  console.log(def.name, \"v\", v.length, \"p\", probs.length, probs.slice(0, 3).join(\" || \"));\n}\n'","description":"Re-run analyzeClip with compileClips"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":992,"output_tokens":450,"cache_read_input_tokens":192000,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"32d2e7dc-edef-4bf8-a824-82eb9332b6b1"}
