97,114,110,105,110,103,32,119,97,115,32,99,114,101,97,116,101,100,41,10],\"output_for_prompt\":\"exit: 0\\n1 idle 7.1 | sloppy 5.0 | average 42.0 | good 92.3 | expert 100.0\\n2 idle 15.0 | sloppy 21.4 | average 73.0 | good 98.5 | expert 100.0\\n7 idle 0.0 | sloppy 27.6 | average 68.8 | good 98.2 | expert 100.0\\n20 idle 6.0 | sloppy 8.0 | average 47.0 | good 92.8 | expert 100.0\\n99 idle 3.0 | sloppy 17.0 | average 61.1 | good 92.8 | expert 100.0\\n(node:4073855) Warning: The 'NO_COLOR' env is ignored due to the 'FORCE_COLOR' env being set.\\n(Use `node --trace-warnings ...` to show where the warning was created)\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"command\":\"cd \\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607\\\" && node --input-type=module -e '\\nimport { Dot, DOT_DEFAULTS } from \\\"./src/core/dot.js\\\";\\nimport { BotDriver } from \\\"./src/core/drivers.js\\\";\\nimport { mulberry32 } from \\\"./src/core/rng.js\\\";\\nfunction band(skill, seed) {\\n  const dot = new Dot(mulberry32(seed));\\n  const bot = new BotDriver(skill, mulberry32(seed + 99));\\n  const dt = 1/60;\\n  let inside = 0, n = 0;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 37*60; i++) {\\n    const u = skill === \\\"idle\\\" ? {x:0,y:0} : bot.read(dot, dt);\\n    dot.step(dt, u.x||0, u.y||0, DOT_DEFAULTS, {});\\n    if (i >= 120) { n++; if (Math.hypot(dot.x, dot.y) < 0.3) inside++; }\\n  }\\n  return inside / n;\\n}\\nfor (const seed of [1, 2, 7, 20, 99]) {\\n  const row = [\\\"idle\\\",\\\"sloppy\\\",\\\"average\\\",\\\"good\\\",\\\"expert\\\"].map(s => s+\\\" \\\"+(band(s, seed)*100).toFixed(1));\\n  console.log(seed, row.join(\\\" | \\\"));\\n}\\n'\",\"truncated\":false,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Measure Dot ring-time bands for a few seeds\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3%2Fwork/01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469/terminal/call-162d6397-da36-4fe2-bb60-cd522925fe4a-129.log\",\"total_bytes\":552}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"3682418a-5569-4151-b2e1-bedae546a8d1"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_168","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Seed 1 shows idle at 7.1, average at 42 within the target range of 35-65, and good at 92.\n\nSloppy at 5% is worse than average. I will write test.mjs and browser.mjs next. Day 1 activities are tree and squat.\n\nThe test will assert that the second activity in a pair—squat—sets `lastPrescription` to true. Day 2 will verify that `today.bestStar` reaches at least two after lunge.\n\nIf expert lunge fails, the test will fall back to warrior. Hard expert runs are added for plank, press, longstand, and pier. Easy poses need three stars; non-easy need two. A two-star easy result would indicate a simulation bug rather than a threshold issue.\n\nA progress beat will be added to every activity. Large waits will use `engine.step(30)` or `step(60)` instead of many single steps. Menu taps will keep using `step(1)`. The first headless app in `boot()` is replaced by `loadGame`, but the `engine` variable stays.\n\nThe test suite will run in this order: dot bands, data assets, hash, boot title music, activity sweep, week, save, and pause plus dev sliders and tools. Each test will call boot to reset state.\n\nThe remaining tests cover attract mode, determinism, medley and family, voice, and clips analysis. The clips test will run in a separate hero engine that is disposed immediately after, leaving the noHero engine for the rest of the suite.\n\nVoice tests will verify syllabify stability by comparing identical inputs and checking that question marks raise pitch. Node will use a small OfflineAudioContext if available, while the browser test handles RMS analysis.\n\nVoice tests will compare mean pitch between the words \"ounce\" and \"coach\" to confirm question marks raise pitch. The line count must be at least 120 original entries beyond the plan samples. Each activity needs dialogue in 0, 1, 2, or 3 lines. Every line must wrap within a 52-character width limit so it fits its box.\n\nI will assert that every line string wraps to three lines or fewer within a 52-character width. Missing glyphs must be empty. The Nintendo test will scan allLineStrings, activity names, TAGLINE, and TITLE for inappropriate content like \"Wii\", while excluding the about source. Menu strings are harder to scan so I will focus on activity names, days, concerns, beats, and questions. I will import those lists into the test. I am ready to write the files now.\n\nThe family hour test stubs two connected gamepads and taps Enter to claim them. It asserts that at least three seats are filled, the mode is medley, and lanes exist. After 120 steps it reads lane positions.\n\nThe family hour test asserts that the three lane positions differ after two seconds. Pad inputs use axes while keyboard input uses no keys, so the dots should drift apart. Simulated lanes must have positive step counts and ghosts are excluded.\n\nA single step with the pad button down is enough to trigger the rising edge and claim the pad. However, Enter in the join menu claims both the keyboard and activates the focused row. The first row is \"fill\", not \"start\", so the test must account for this double activation.\n\nPressing Enter in the join menu would claim the keyboard seat and activate the \"fill\" row, which adds bots to empty seats. To avoid this, the test should press pad buttons first so only pad seats are claimed, leaving the keyboard seat empty for later.\n\nThe family hour test will claim the keyboard seat with Enter, then activate the \"fill\" row to add a bot. After that it will arrow down to \"start\" and press Enter again. This yields four lanes total, which is acceptable as long as at least two pads and the keyboard lane move independently.\n\nThe engine polls gamepads at beginFrame before update, so pressing a pad button may also trigger the menu confirmation. This means pad input could accidentally activate the \"fill\" row in the join menu, making the Enter-based keyboard claim unreliable.\n\nPressing a pad button in the join menu triggers both claiming and the \"fill\" row, which adds bots and leaves no keyboard seat. The first row is always \"fill\", so pad input cannot cleanly claim pads without also activating fill.\n\nArrowDown to start before pressing a pad button would activate the back row and exit the menu. The claim happens in pollJoin before menuInput, so pressing a pad button claims the pad and immediately activates the current row. If focus is on start, the medley begins with only pad lanes. A keyboard seat is still needed.\n\nPressing pad buttons in the join menu claims both pads and immediately activates the \"fill\" row, which fills the remaining seats with bots. This leaves no keyboard seat available for Enter to claim. The test cannot cleanly add a keyboard lane without also triggering fill.\n\nThe join menu's update order causes a UX bug: pressing Cross to claim a pad seat also immediately activates the focused row. This is undesirable for the test, so I will modify the join logic to prevent a claim press from triggering menu confirmation in the same frame.\n\nThe join logic now checks whether a press claimed a seat. If it did, the frame returns early and skips menu confirmation. This lets the test claim pads first, then Enter to claim the keyboard without accidentally activating fill or start.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d4f68736-09ab-44eb-8ffa-7a16d53e77be-130","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/app.js","old_string":"    if (this.mode === 'card') this.cardInput(ctx);\n    if (this.mode === 'join') this.pollJoin(ctx);\n    if (this.mode === 'name') this.typeName(ctx);","new_string":"    if (this.mode === 'card') this.cardInput(ctx);\n    let claimedJoin = false;\n    if (this.mode === 'join') {\n      const before = 