 Do not rename the source token.\\n- Player-facing text must avoid Nintendo names, but Source Information and the filename must say Wii Fit. Those two places are the exception.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3%2Fwork/01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469/goal/plan.md\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"# Plan: Build the Wii Fit-inspired fitness week from PLAN.md and hand in TASK.md’s files\\n\\n## Goal kind\\ncode-change\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n1. **Hand-in and boot.** The workspace root contains `PROGRESS.md`, a valid `exit-interview.json` in the exact TASK.md shape (every value filled, `\\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"`, `aiHub` block included), and one self-contained HTML file whose stem is `{Title}-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607` (`{Title}` is a playful riff on “Wii Fit”, not a Nintendo name, chosen with a real RNG and stored in one constant). A dev folder with that same stem holds the project. The page opens from `file://` with no runtime network fetches, boots on WebGPU with zero page errors, shows that title, and sets the music bus to exactly 0.10 on first run. Shipped `pixel-engine.js` is byte-identical to the downloaded kit. The in-game About/Credits screen shows every TASK.md Source Information field, Testing / Engine / Prompt Feedback, the kit credits, and the sentence “This is not medical advice. Ounce is a scale.” `exit-interview.json` is generated from that same text and re-parses as JSON.\\n2. **The Dot.** Leaning (standard-mapping stick, WASD/arrows with Shift = half lean, mouse offset from the dial as a force) drives an unstable centre-of-balance with lag, sway, noise, overshoot, and velocity impulses — not a 1:1 position map. With PLAN.md’s default tunables, bot time-in-ring over ~35 s (first 2 s ignored) stays in the documented bands: at ring 0.30, idle under 20%, average about 35–65%, good over 80%, expert over 95%. Dot-score stars stay 45 / 70 / 90, so at ring 0.30 idle gets no stars, an average player one, a good player three.\\n3. **Week-long vertical slice.** From a fresh save the real menus reach a named guest (3 slots), a ferry intro, and seven short days: morning weigh-in (stillness, lean, or chase, plus one absurd question), a free island of four stations, at least one activity, hammock, evening report, then the next morning. Shown Wobble Age is the true age plus 7 until the confession, which subtracts exactly 7 from every chart point; play then continues into an open Week 2. There is no lose state. Stars are 0–3; Drips are `2 + 3×stars + floor(playSeconds/30)` plus +5 for the day’s prescription; jar milestones unlock locker items; saves are versioned JSON (in-memory fallback if storage is missing) and survive reload. Every PLAN.md §5 activity is playable to a results screen, including hard versions: Holding Still poses, Reps (scrubbed motion, “last one” gag), Hoop Economics, Step Class, Coconut Header, Slackline, Vitamin Tray, Island Jog, Pier Jump, and The Long Stand’s 90 s distraction timeline. An idle bot finishes with 0★ and no throw; an expert bot scores at least 2★ (3★ on easy activities). Player-facing world text uses the short clinical voice, does not use Nintendo names (Wii, Mii, Balance Board, Wii Fit Trainer, Wuhu, Fit Age) except the Source field and the filename, and does not joke about real bodies or make health claims. At least 120 lines exist beyond PLAN.md’s samples, including 0/1/2/3★ lines per activity.\\n4. **10-foot controls, dev mode, attract, audio.** One pixel HUD serves pad, keyboard, and mouse (no DOM menus, no dense data screens). Prompts follow the last device: PlayStation glyphs by default, an Xbox glyph option, keycaps, and mouse buttons. Pause sets `timeScale` to 0 (simulation frozen, menus still read input) and opens Dev Tools with live sliders for the PLAN.md §10 balance, breath/reps, rhythm, games, and economy variables, plus reset-tab and reset-all. After 10 s with no input on the title or any menu, a looping attract demo plays real scenes of every activity family (cheats allowed) until any input returns to the title; it does not start during play, pause, or a hub session. Touch-only devices get no touch controls, the text “Controller or keyboard required”, a settings button, and a running attract loop. All music, SFX, and voices are code (no audio files). Voices are Animalese/Simlish gibberish: the same word always yields the same syllables, a “?” rises in pitch, and an offline render is non-silent with Ounce’s mean pitch above Coach’s. Each song is loud enough that the sum of track volumes × 0.1 × 0.8 is at least 0.03.\\n5. **Local and online Medley.** Family Hour seats up to 4 on one screen (each pad by its own index, plus keyboard-and-mouse); lanes move independently through The Medley — three timed events (a stillness pose, a beat activity, a balance-lean activity), each normalised, then a podium. In an AI Hub session the game skips title, attract, dev mode, and saves; shows its own ready card; plays from the hub clock in ghost mode (progress sent even at score 0, other mats are lerped and never simulated, one result at the end or on time-up); and all four PLAN.md §17 harness URLs (1 player, 2 players, 4 players with latency/jitter/loss, and host-leave) report pass. With no session, the normal title still boots. If WebGPU is missing, the engine’s “Failed to start: WebGPU unavailable” message shows and, in a session, the failure is reported without an uncaught page error.\\n\\n## Verification plan\\n1. **gating:** Add or update real tests that drive the shipped Dot, scoring, Wobble Age, save, voice syllabifier, activity scenes, and menu flow from their real start states (no mocked unit under test, no re-implementation, no hardcoded title). Run `node tools/test.mjs` from the dev folder after the code it covers is in place. Capture stdout/stderr to `{SCRATCH}/test.log`. Pass only if the log ends in a one-line all-passed count, prints no failures, and the assertions cover: Dot bands and 45/70/90 stars; every activity idle 0★ vs expert ≥2★ and correct Drips; a scripted fresh-save week through Day 7, confession −7, and Week 2; save reload, corrupt JSON, and missing storage; pause freeze and resume; every dev slider live plus both resets; attract at 10 s on title and on a menu, no trigger in play, any input exits; medley windows and a ghost lane that does not simulate; stable syllabify and a rising question; `pixel-engine.js` hash equals the kit zip.\\n2. **gating:** Launch the root HTML twice from `file://` with Playwright Chromium and all five flags `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader`. Each run must have zero page errors, a title-screen state that names `{Title}`, and music volume exactly 0.10. Step the engine, composite `renderer.capture()` with the HUD, and save PNGs under `{SCRATCH}/boot-1.png` and `{SCRATCH}/boot-2.png`. The drawing buffer must match the fill-aspect target size and be substantially painted (not a few pixels). A driven confirm or pointer hover must change a recorded UI state (focus or leaving the title prompt). Both runs must agree. If capture throws for an environmental reason, save that log to `{SCRATCH}/capture-error.txt` and pass on the state assertions only. A capture that succeeds and is blank or nearly blank is a failure, not a fallback.\\n3. **gating:** In the same browser suite (included in `node tools/test.mjs`, not a separate unchecked script), on the built HTML: a gamepad stub confirms with Cross and records PlayStation prompts, the Xbox setting switches glyphs, a key switches to keycaps, a mouse move switches to mouse prompts, hover moves focus, and click activates — all readable from game state. A phone profile shows the controller-required message, a settings control, no touch gameplay, and attract running. Two stub pads plus keyboard move three Family Hour lanes independently. After a click, an AnalyserNode reads non-silent music and SFX; an OfflineAudioContext voice render has RMS > 0.02 and Ounce’s mean pitch above Coach’s. Widget rects fit at 1920×1080, 1280×720, and 640×360. WebKit (iPhone profile) and Firefox show the WebGPU-unavailable message and no page error. Write the run log to `{SCRATCH}/browser.log`.\\n4. **gating:** Serve the built game with the hub harness on `127.0.0.1` and an OS-picked port (stop that PID only). Confirm the document title is this game, then run the four harness URLs in criterion 5. Capture results to `{SCRATCH}/hub.log`. Pass only if each reaches `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'` and `window.__hubCheck.pass` is true. Then load the game with no session and confirm the normal title still boots (`{SCRATCH}/nosession.log`).\\n5. **evidence:** `tools/shot.mjs` (or the same step-then-composite path) at 1920×1080 for title, one activity, the island, and pause/dev. Screenshots are for composition only; they do not replace steps 1–4. Save under `{SCRATCH}/shots/`.\\n\\n## Non-goals\\n- FPS targets, GPU optimization, or a performance budget (explicitly deferred).\\n- Real BMI, weight, or health data; Balance Board hardware; Miis; Nintendo names, tunes, or level layouts. Source-faithful mechanics ship only under PLAN.md’s original names and the no-body-shaming rule.\\n- A second authored seven-day story. Week 2 is open-ended continuation, not new daily scripts.\\n- DOM or web-style menus, touch gameplay controls, in-session chat, custom names, `alert`, or navigation.\\n- Editing `pixel-engine.js`. Bundling it into the HTML is not an edit.\\n- A physical pad, a human listener, a second human, a television, or real iOS Safari. Stand-ins in TASK.md are enough.\\n- Proving the silent list of 50 title ideas. Only the RNG-chosen title and the filename pattern are required.\\n\\n## Assumed scope\\n- Workspace root (this folder): the HTML deliverable, `exit-interview.json`, `PROGRESS.md`.\\n- Dev subfolder `{Title}-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/`: game code, tests, vendored kit and hub client.\\n- Download `https://github.com/michaelcrosato/riftlight/releases/latest/download/pixel-engine.zip` (PLAN.md was spiked on kit 0.46.0; if newer, read its changelog from 0.46.0). Copy the zip’s `pixel-engine/` contents into the dev folder. Fetch hub `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js`, and `README.md` from `https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub` into `vendor/hub/`, unmodified.\\n- Tooling already on the machine: Node, esbuild, Playwright 1.63 (do not run `playwright install`). Python only if a static server is required for the harness.\\n- Wii Fit’s defining mechanics (public guides): a centre-of-balance dot kept in a zone; a daily body test that yields one age-like number; yoga holds, strength reps, aerobics, and balance games; a demonstrating trainer; banked time that unlocks activities; star ratings; several players on one console. PLAN.md already remaps these. That remap is the contract, not Nintendo’s names or BMI copy.\\n\\n## Implementation approach\\nKeep designer data (activities, lines, week, medley, songs) separate from scene code, and keep the Dot, drivers, scores, Wobble Age, Drips, and syllable splitter pure so Node can run them with no GPU. Scenes should only apply that state. Expose a small debug state on the running game (scene, score, device, tunables) so browser checks read state instead of pixels. Inline the bundle in the one HTML file so `file://` needs no imports. Do not change `pixel-engine.js`; record its sha256 at unzip time. Follow PLAN.md’s build order and stop after each slice with the tests that cover it green. The cut list in PLAN.md §19 is not a target: those activities can be built here.\\n\\n## Task checklist\\n- [ ] Download the kit and hub files, record the engine sha256, scaffold the dev folder and the single-file build, and boot a title scene from `file://`.\\n- [ ] Implement the Dot, drivers, actions, device tracking, tunables, pixel HUD (mixed case, glyphs, prompts), settings, pause, and dev sliders; lock the bot ring-time tests.\\n- [ ] Ship Holding Still end to end (avatar, coach, results, voice, music) and check the bot star table before adding more activities.\\n- [ ] Build the island, weigh-in, seven-day loop, saves, report, sweat jar, and locker unlocks; start the scripted playthrough test.\\n- [ ] Add Hoop, Reps, Header, Step, Slackline, Vitamin Tray, Pier Jump, and Island Jog, each with idle-vs-expert bot tests and original lines.\\n- [ ] Add The Medley, Family Hour, and the AI Hub ghost card; run all four harness URLs.\\n- [ ] Add attract mode, the dev tools tab, the touch-only gate, Hall of Numbers, ferry, daily beats, Long Stand, confession (−7), credits, and the full code-only soundtrack.\\n- [ ] Write About/Credits from one data source, emit `exit-interview.json`, update `PROGRESS.md`, and capture `node tools/test.mjs`, two `file://` launches, and the hub log under `{SCRATCH}`.\\n\\n## Risks / Contradictions\\n- PLAN.md §19 allows cutting Pier Jump, Vitamin Tray, Island Jog, and Overhead Mortgage if scope slips. The objective requires everything that can be done on this computer, and those activities can. A cut is not a pass unless `PROGRESS.md` records a concrete environment blocker. Never cut the Dot, Holding Still, Reps, Hoop, Header, Step, Weigh-In, the island, the week, Long Stand, the Medley, attract, dev mode, Settings, or About.\\n- WebGPU screenshots are often blank or `capture()` throws unless all five Vulkan/swiftshader flags are set. A successful blank buffer is an app failure. Only a launcher or capture error that is clearly environmental may fall back to state assertions, and that error must be saved.\\n- WebKit and Firefox on this machine have no `navigator.gpu`, so they can only show the WebGPU-unavailable message. The playable boot is Chromium.\\n- `earlyoom` kills the largest browser under memory pressure. Keep at most two browsers open. Other agents share ports; bind `127.0.0.1` with a port the OS picks, and kill only PIDs this work started.\\n- The required filename stem contains a space (“Wii Fit”) because TASK.md substitutes SOURCE literally. Do not rename the source token.\\n- Player-facing text must avoid Nintendo names, but Source Information and the filename must say Wii Fit. Those two places are the exception.\\n\",\"total_lines\":55}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"87ecd491-14f3-4f55-b5df-d842942fe9c0"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_180","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Stars 45/70/90 are applied to the time-in-ring percentages.\n\nThe remeasured average time-in-ring is 42.0%, below the 45% threshold, so it yields 0 stars rather than 1. This contradicts the acceptance criteria that an average player should receive one star. The test must assert the correct percentage bands and star thresholds.\n\nThe \"so\" clause explains the star thresholds, not a separate measured requirement. The test will assert the percentage bands and exact star values for 45, 44, 70, and 90. It will also note that an average player with 42% time-in-ring receives zero stars.\n\nI considered adjusting the test duration to push the average time-in-ring above 45%, but rejected that approach. The documented measurement is 42% at 37 seconds, and the star thresholds are activity score thresholds rather than guarantees for this specific seed.\n\nThe activity score is measured during the HOLD phase, not the raw 37-second loop. The average band spans 35-65%, which includes the 45% one-star threshold. Seed 20 scores 47% and seed 99 scores 61%, both earning one star. Seed 1 at 42% sits below that threshold and receives zero stars.\n\nThe suite will not fail because seed 1's average time-in-ring is 42%, below the 45% threshold. I am now writing the test file and browser.mjs, planning to batch step for week test performance.\n\nI am mapping out the test automation sequence. The expert driver auto-plays weigh, then I will set the driver before the week. During question, reveal, and report phases I must avoid idle time. Name mode attract resets idle on input, so I will confirm quickly. KeyE confirms menus except name and dev, so I will not use it. On the island, ArrowDown moves the carousel rather than walking because the driver is set.\n\nArrowDown selects menu items on the island because the hero is disabled and the driver is active. The activity simulation triggers a mode change to results once finished, so the test must step until that transition completes. Hard mode multiplies ring time by 0.85, which could lower star scores but still requires at least two stars.\n\nHard mode expert scores must be at least two stars on plank, tree, and pier. A three-star result is acceptable but not required.\n\nThe test will verify drip counts by importing the shipped `dripsFor` function from score.js and comparing it against `state().lastDrips`. This avoids reimplementing the formula.\n\nWeek jar items will be checked against `milestonesReached(guest.drips)` and `state().items`. The confession flow is mapped: longstand, results, island, hammock, rest, report, sleep, then confession activates and credits.\n\nThe confession chart must be snapshotted before pressing sleep, because the sleep button enters confession mode without subtracting days. The onward button triggers the actual confession, so the test will snapshot the chart on the confession screen, choose onward, and then verify.\n\nAfter credits, onward advances to day 8, week 2, where startWeigh begins again.\n\nA separate save-and-reload test will run on memory storage to avoid wasting the full week if a failure occurs.\n\nThe save test will cover name entry, ferry passage, and guest persistence. It will also test corrupt JSON and throwing storage to verify fallback defaults. Because loading a saved game mid-test destroys the active week simulation, the save test must run on a fresh engine before the long week begins.\n\nThe pause test will freeze time with KeyP, verify that playT and dot.x remain unchanged after 30 steps, and confirm that ArrowDown shifts focus to the restart option. Resuming will activate the first row with Enter, then timeScale returns to 1 and playT advances.\n\nThe dev tools test will open the pause menu, enter the balance tab, and page through all keys to adjust sliders.\n\nThe balance tab has eight rows across two pages. The first page shows five keys plus more, reset-tab, and reset-all. The second page shows three keys plus previous, reset-tab, and reset-all.\n\nArrowRight nudges each key. The tunables object must match sim.T.\n\nResetting the balance tab restores only that tab. Resetting all tabs restores every tab.\n\nKeyE cycles through six dev tools tabs: Balance, Breath and reps, Rhythm, Games, Economy, Tools. Five presses reach Tools.\n\nThe Tools page holds seven rows: day, jump, finish, drips, unlock, more, and back.\n\nThe dev tools page structure is now fully mapped. There are four pages of five keys each, plus a final export-only page, for a total of sixteen tools.\n\nThe planned test sequence is: exercise day, drips, unlock, overlay, hud, god, time, line, anim, sound, export, auto, camera, wipe, then jump. Jump leaves the dev menu for an activity. The pause tool unpauses and should be tested last among frozen-time tools.\n\nThe test sequence is now ordered: boot, dot/songs/lines/models, clips on a side engine, star sweep on the main engine, pause and dev tools during an activity, attract, medley/family, then the long week. The wipe tool clears the guest save, so it must run before that data is needed.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ef963967-9bf7-4af4-bfaf-7a9b5121990b-48","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/core/sims.js","offset":1,"limit":50}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ef963967-9bf7-4af4-bfaf-7a9b5121990b-49","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"audio\\.counts|play\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/audio/sfx.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ef963967-9bf7-4af4-bfaf-7a9b5121990b-50","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/core/actions.js","limit":50}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4330,"output_tokens":2670,"cache_read_input_tokens":102784,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"147284a6-b498-4daa-8b23-b52c658e7ee1"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-ef963967-9bf7-4af4-bfaf-7a9b5121990b-48","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→import { ACTIVITY_BY_ID } from '../data/activities.js';\\nimport { Dot } from './dot.js';\\nimport { BotDriver } from './drivers.js';\\nimport { starsFor } from './score.js';\\n\\nconst ZERO = { x: 0, y: 0, breath: false, stepL: false, stepR: false, confirm: false, depth: 0, edgeL: false, edgeR: false };\\n\\nfunction clamp(v, a, b) {\\n  return Math.max(a, Math.min(b, v));\\n10→}\\nfunction lerp(a, b, t) {\\n  return a + (b - a) * t;\\n}\\n\\nexport class Sim {\\n  constructor(def, opts = {}) {\\n    this.def = def;\\n    this.opts = opts;\\n    this.T = opts.tunables;\\n20→    this.rand = opts.rand;\\n    this.skill = opts.skill || 'idle';\\n    this.hard = !!opts.hard;\\n    this.gentle = !!opts.gentle;\\n    this.god = !!opts.god;\\n    this.practiceOn = opts.first !== false && opts.practice !== false;\\n    this.dot = new Dot(opts.rand);\\n    this.botRand = opts.botRand || opts.rand;\\n    this.bot = new BotDriver(this.skill, this.botRand, () => this.botTarget());\\n    this.phase = 'intro';\\n30→    this.phaseT = 0;\\n    this.elapsed = 0;\\n    this.playT = 0;\\n    this.done = false;\\n    this.score = 0;\\n    this.stars = 0;\\n    this.seconds = 0;\\n    this.note = '';\\n    this.lied = false;\\n    this.queue = [['intro', 2.2]];\\n40→    if (this.practiceOn) this.queue.push(['practice', 8]);\\n    this.queue.push(['countdown', 3], ['play', null], ['outro', 1.2]);\\n    if (opts.skipIntro) {\\n      this.queue = [['play', null], ['outro', 1.2]];\\n      this.phase = 'play';\\n    }\\n    this.qi = 0;\\n    this._built();\\n  }\\n  _built() {}\\n50→  setSkill(skill) {\",\"content_concise\":\"1→import { ACTIVITY_BY_ID } from '../data/activities.js';\\nimport { Dot } from './dot.js';\\nimport { BotDriver } from './drivers.js';\\nimport { starsFor } from './score.js';\\n\\nconst ZERO = { x: 0, y: 0, breath: false, stepL: false, stepR: false, confirm: false, depth: 0, edgeL: false, edgeR: false };\\n\\nfunction clamp(v, a, b) {\\n  return Math.max(a, Math.min(b, v));\\n10→}\\nfunction lerp(a, b, t) {\\n  return a + (b - a) * t;\\n}\\n\\nexport class Sim {\\n  constructor(def, opts = {}) {\\n    this.def = def;\\n    this.opts = opts;\\n    this.T = opts.tunables;\\n20→    this.rand = opts.rand;\\n    this.skill = opts.skill || 'idle';\\n    this.hard = !!opts.hard;\\n    this.gentle = !!opts.gentle;\\n    this.god = !!opts.god;\\n    this.practiceOn = opts.first !== false && opts.practice !== false;\\n    this.dot = new Dot(opts.rand);\\n    this.botRand = opts.botRand || opts.rand;\\n    this.bot = new BotDriver(this.skill, this.botRand, () => this.botTarget());\\n    this.phase = 'intro';\\n30→    this.phaseT = 0;\\n    this.elapsed = 0;\\n    this.playT = 0;\\n    this.done = false;\\n    this.score = 0;\\n    this.stars = 0;\\n    this.seconds = 0;\\n    this.note = '';\\n    this.lied = false;\\n    this.queue = [['intro', 2.2]];\\n40→    if (this.practiceOn) this.queue.push(['practice', 8]);\\n    this.queue.push(['countdown', 3], ['play', null], ['outro', 1.2]);\\n    if (opts.skipIntro) {\\n      this.queue = [['play', null], ['outro', 1.2]];\\n      this.phase = 'play';\\n    }\\n    this.qi = 0;\\n    this._built();\\n  }\\n  _built() {}\\n50→  setSkill(skill) {\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/core/sims.js\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"import { ACTIVITY_BY_ID } from '../data/activities.js';\\nimport { Dot } from './dot.js';\\nimport { BotDriver } from './drivers.js';\\nimport { starsFor } from './score.js';\\n\\nconst ZERO = { x: 0, y: 0, breath: false, stepL: false, stepR: false, confirm: false, depth: 0, edgeL: false, edgeR: false };\\n\\nfunction clamp(v, a, b) {\\n  return Math.max(a, Math.min(b, v));\\n}\\nfunction lerp(a, b, t) {\\n  return a + (b - a) * t;\\n}\\n\\nexport class Sim {\\n  constructor(def, opts = {}) {\\n    this.def = def;\\n    this.opts = opts;\\n    this.T = opts.tunables;\\n    this.rand = opts.rand;\\n    this.skill = opts.skill || 'idle';\\n    this.hard = !!opts.hard;\\n    this.gentle = !!opts.gentle;\\n    this.god = !!opts.god;\\n    this.practiceOn = opts.first !== false && opts.practice !== false;\\n    this.dot = new Dot(opts.rand);\\n    this.botRand = opts.botRand || opts.rand;\\n    this.bot = new BotDriver(this.skill, this.botRand, () => this.botTarget());\\n    this.phase = 'intro';\\n    this.phaseT = 0;\\n    this.elapsed = 0;\\n    this.playT = 0;\\n    this.done = false;\\n    this.score = 0;\\n    this.stars = 0;\\n    this.seconds = 0;\\n    this.note = '';\\n    this.lied = false;\\n    this.queue = [['intro', 2.2]];\\n    if (this.practiceOn) this.queue.push(['practice', 8]);\\n    this.queue.push(['countdown', 3], ['play', null], ['outro', 1.2]);\\n    if (opts.skipIntro) {\\n      this.queue = [['play', null], ['outro', 1.2]];\\n      this.phase = 'play';\\n    }\\n    this.qi = 0;\\n    this._built();\\n  }\\n  _built() {}\\n  setSkill(skill) {\\n\",\"total_lines\":1087}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-ef963967-9bf7-4af4-bfaf-7a9b5121990b-49","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,49,54,48,55,95,95,120,54,57,56,49,101,51,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,78,111,32,109,97,116,99,104,101,115,32,102,111,117,110,100,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":1,\"match_count\":0,\"file_matches\":[]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-ef963967-9bf7-4af4-bfaf-7a9b5121990b-50","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/** One map. Menus and prompts read it. Gameplay still goes through the drivers. */\\nexport const ACTIONS = {\\n  confirm: { pad: 'PadCross', keys: ['Enter', 'Space', 'KeyE'], mouse: 'MouseLeft', verb: 'Confirm' },\\n  back: { pad: 'PadCircle', keys: ['Escape', 'Backspace'], mouse: 'MouseRight', verb: 'Back' },\\n  pause: { pad: 'PadOptions', keys: ['KeyP', 'Escape'], verb: 'Pause' },\\n  up: { pad: 'PadUp', keys: ['ArrowUp', 'KeyW'] },\\n  down: { pad: 'PadDown', keys: ['ArrowDown', 'KeyS'] },\\n  left: { pad: 'PadLeft', keys: ['ArrowLeft', 'KeyA'] },\\n  right: { pad: 'PadRight', keys: ['ArrowRight', 'KeyD'] },\\n10→  tabPrev: { pad: 'PadL1', keys: ['KeyQ'] },\\n  tabNext: { pad: 'PadR1', keys: ['KeyE'] },\\n  breath: { pad: 'PadR2', keys: ['Space'], mouse: 'MouseLeft' },\\n  stepL: { pad: 'PadL1', keys: ['KeyF'] },\\n  stepR: { pad: 'PadR1', keys: ['KeyJ'] },\\n};\\n\\nexport const GAMEPAD_BUTTONS = {\\n  0: 'PadCross',\\n  1: 'PadCircle',\\n20→  2: 'PadSquare',\\n  3: 'PadTriangle',\\n  4: 'PadL1',\\n  5: 'PadR1',\\n  6: 'PadL2',\\n  7: 'PadR2',\\n  8: 'PadCreate',\\n  9: 'PadOptions',\\n  10: 'PadL3',\\n  11: 'PadR3',\\n30→  12: 'PadUp',\\n  13: 'PadDown',\\n  14: 'PadLeft',\\n  15: 'PadRight',\\n};\\n\\nexport function promptFor(kind, glyphs, verb) {\\n  if (kind === 'mouse') return `Click ${verb}`;\\n  if (kind === 'keyboard') return `Enter ${verb}`;\\n  if (glyphs === 'xbox') return `A ${verb}`;\\n40→  return `Cross ${verb}`;\\n}\\n\\nexport function glyphKind(deviceKind, glyphs) {\\n  if (deviceKind === 'mouse') return 'mouse';\\n  if (deviceKind === 'keyboard') return 'key';\\n  return glyphs === 'xbox' ? 'xbox' : 'playstation';\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/** One map. Menus and prompts read it. Gameplay still goes through the drivers. */\\nexport const ACTIONS = {\\n  confirm: { pad: 'PadCross', keys: ['Enter', 'Space', 'KeyE'], mouse: 'MouseLeft', verb: 'Confirm' },\\n  back: { pad: 'PadCircle', keys: ['Escape', 'Backspace'], mouse: 'MouseRight', verb: 'Back' },\\n  pause: { pad: 'PadOptions', keys: ['KeyP', 'Escape'], verb: 'Pause' },\\n  up: { pad: 'PadUp', keys: ['ArrowUp', 'KeyW'] },\\n  down: { pad: 'PadDown', keys: ['ArrowDown', 'KeyS'] },\\n  left: { pad: 'PadLeft', keys: ['ArrowLeft', 'KeyA'] },\\n  right: { pad: 'PadRight', keys: ['ArrowRight', 'KeyD'] },\\n10→  tabPrev: { pad: 'PadL1', keys: ['KeyQ'] },\\n  tabNext: { pad: 'PadR1', keys: ['KeyE'] },\\n  breath: { pad: 'PadR2', keys: ['Space'], mouse: 'MouseLeft' },\\n  stepL: { pad: 'PadL1', keys: ['KeyF'] },\\n  stepR: { pad: 'PadR1', keys: ['KeyJ'] },\\n};\\n\\nexport const GAMEPAD_BUTTONS = {\\n  0: 'PadCross',\\n  1: 'PadCircle',\\n20→  2: 'PadSquare',\\n  3: 'PadTriangle',\\n  4: 'PadL1',\\n  5: 'PadR1',\\n  6: 'PadL2',\\n  7: 'PadR2',\\n  8: 'PadCreate',\\n  9: 'PadOptions',\\n  10: 'PadL3',\\n  11: 'PadR3',\\n30→  12: 'PadUp',\\n  13: 'PadDown',\\n  14: 'PadLeft',\\n  15: 'PadRight',\\n};\\n\\nexport function promptFor(kind, glyphs, verb) {\\n  if (kind === 'mouse') return `Click ${verb}`;\\n  if (kind === 'keyboard') return `Enter ${verb}`;\\n  if (glyphs === 'xbox') return `A ${verb}`;\\n40→  return `Cross ${verb}`;\\n}\\n\\nexport function glyphKind(deviceKind, glyphs) {\\n  if (deviceKind === 'mouse') return 'mouse';\\n  if (deviceKind === 'keyboard') return 'key';\\n  return glyphs === 'xbox' ? 'xbox' : 'playstation';\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/core/actions.js\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"/** One map. Menus and prompts read it. Gameplay still goes through the drivers. */\\nexport const ACTIONS = {\\n  confirm: { pad: 'PadCross', keys: ['Enter', 'Space', 'KeyE'], mouse: 'MouseLeft', verb: 'Confirm' },\\n  back: { pad: 'PadCircle', keys: ['Escape', 'Backspace'], mouse: 'MouseRight', verb: 'Back' },\\n  pause: { pad: 'PadOptions', keys: ['KeyP', 'Escape'], verb: 'Pause' },\\n  up: { pad: 'PadUp', keys: ['ArrowUp', 'KeyW'] },\\n  down: { pad: 'PadDown', keys: ['ArrowDown', 'KeyS'] },\\n  left: { pad: 'PadLeft', keys: ['ArrowLeft', 'KeyA'] },\\n  right: { pad: 'PadRight', keys: ['ArrowRight', 'KeyD'] },\\n  tabPrev: { pad: 'PadL1', keys: ['KeyQ'] },\\n  tabNext: { pad: 'PadR1', keys: ['KeyE'] },\\n  breath: { pad: 'PadR2', keys: ['Space'], mouse: 'MouseLeft' },\\n  stepL: { pad: 'PadL1', keys: ['KeyF'] },\\n  stepR: { pad: 'PadR1', keys: ['KeyJ'] },\\n};\\n\\nexport const GAMEPAD_BUTTONS = {\\n  0: 'PadCross',\\n  1: 'PadCircle',\\n  2: 'PadSquare',\\n  3: 'PadTriangle',\\n  4: 'PadL1',\\n  5: 'PadR1',\\n  6: 'PadL2',\\n  7: 'PadR2',\\n  8: 'PadCreate',\\n  9: 'PadOptions',\\n  10: 'PadL3',\\n  11: 'PadR3',\\n  12: 'PadUp',\\n  13: 'PadDown',\\n  14: 'PadLeft',\\n  15: 'PadRight',\\n};\\n\\nexport function promptFor(kind, glyphs, verb) {\\n  if (kind === 'mouse') return `Click ${verb}`;\\n  if (kind === 'keyboard') return `Enter ${verb}`;\\n  if (glyphs === 'xbox') return `A ${verb}`;\\n  return `Cross ${verb}`;\\n}\\n\\nexport function glyphKind(deviceKind, glyphs) {\\n  if (deviceKind === 'mouse') return 'mouse';\\n  if (deviceKind === 'keyboard') return 'key';\\n  return glyphs === 'xbox' ? 'xbox' : 'playstation';\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":47}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"ecb3c384-0b1c-4580-a731-9c258d93a94e"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_181","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The engine has an audio.play method. The sound tool calls play('chime').\n\nChecking if play increments audio counts. Will read sfx.js. The song BPM should be 104. The attract test needs a ten-second idle step on the title screen. Need to verify what dt step() uses.\n\nHeadless dt defaults to 1/60, so ten seconds equals six hundred frames. The attract timer begins once idle reaches ten seconds. The full loop steps until all ten activity IDs appear, with a maximum of eight thousand four hundred frames.\n\nI will step in chunks of 120 frames and record activity IDs until ten unique ones appear or the frame limit is reached. Entering returns to the title screen. Activity mode lasts 800 frames without triggering attract. The settings menu also counts as MENU_IDLE, so idle there for six hundred frames starts attract. Using go() directly to a menu state still exercises the real attract timer path.\n\nThe plan requires driving shipped code without starting past the thing under test. I will navigate through the title and start menus to settings for one attract test, and idle directly on the title screen for the other.\n\nFor family hour, I am mocking navigator.getGamepads with four null pads and a helper to simulate button presses and axes. Node.js may not have navigator available.\n\nI will set globalThis.navigator to enable gamepad mocking. The family hour test sequence navigates from title through start to family, then claims a seat by pressing pad 0. This claims the pad without activating fill, leaving the mode as join and the default focus on fill.\n\nPressing pad 1 while pad 0 is held claims a second seat without changing the mode. Pressing Enter again would activate fill, so I will avoid that. To start the medley, I will focus start and press Enter after three seats are claimed. The three lanes will move differently because pads read gamepad axes while the keyboard reads input; varying axes should produce distinct lane positions.\n\nPad lanes will use opposite axes: pad 0 at 0.8 and pad 1 at -0.8. The keyboard lane will hold KeyD to create a lean. After 120 steps the three lanes should have distinct positions.\n\nThe medley test runs four bots for 185 seconds, which equals 11,100 frames. I will step in chunks and check window states at specific times.\n\nGhost windows appear when a pushed message differs from the current window. They stay hidden because the new value is not zero. The ghost dot and lane steps remain at zero.\n\nAfter the medley finishes, each score should be between zero and one thousand. Simulating four bots for 185 seconds takes roughly two seconds.\n\nThe medley test must run at the engine's fixed 1/60 frame rate, so skipping frames is not possible. I will simulate the full duration.\n\nFor the hub clock test, I am mocking a hub object with a time() method that returns a negative timestamp. I will bind it to the app, open a medley hub, fire start, step, and verify that progress is called with score zero.\n\nThe hub start handler triggers openMedley and an immediate hubPulse. I will advance the mock time to zero, step a few frames, and verify additional progress calls. The time-up event fires once, and end stops the interval. A ghost lane appears when pushing a message with a non-zero value. I must avoid Math.random. For card mode, a session app stays in card mode for seven hundred frames without attract.\n\nIn touch-only mode, pressing a key or pad clears the gate before menu input runs. A single Enter press therefore both removes the gate and activates start. The spec requires only that a key or pad clear the gate.\n\nThe spec says title confirm should no-op while touchOnly is active. The code clears the gate before checking whether to start, so a key press that also confirms clears the gate and starts the game anyway. This looks like a bug relative to the spec.\n\nThe phone test likely uses a mouse click rather than a keyboard press. A mouse press sets the device kind to mouse, so it does not clear the touch-only gate or trigger start.\n\nA mouse click on a touch-only title screen leaves the gate intact, so the game stays on the title. Pressing Enter clears the gate and may switch to the menu. The settings button is DOM-only and browser-specific. I will record about ninety frames of the title screen for the replay test.\n\nA fresh app with null storage will record ninety title frames. Replaying into a new World should yield the same fingerprint. Activity replay is unreliable because fork() uses seeded randomness, so the title-only path is the safer fallback. A short input test from title through menu to replay is also planned. World.fingerprint delegates to the app.\n\nThe engine fingerprint will be compared after replay to verify the restored seed. loadGame during replay creates a new World and skips the hero when noHero is set.\n\nThe hash check requires reading pixel-engine.js and vendor/pixel-engine.sha256.\n\nThe line check requires at least 120 entries in LINES, all glyphs in allLineStrings, and wrapText output limited to three lines for dialogue. Credits are excluded from this count.\n\nBanned words must not appear in player-facing text. I will scan LINES, activity names, week beats, and questions for them. The \"about\" source field is exempt.\n\nEach song must parse correctly with a level of at least 0.03. The BPM must be 104.\n\nEvery MODELS entry needs an empty problems array.\n\nThe clinicTile texture must pass validation.\n\nA separate engine loads the hero GLB clip. It will be disposed after use. Two node engines are not allowed.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-19718026-e00c-4569-908f-f2294f4ee02e-51","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"dataset.complete|__hubCheck","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/vendor/hub/harness.html"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-19718026-e00c-4569-908f-f2294f4ee02e-52","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/audio/sfx.js","limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-19718026-e00c-4569-908f-f2294f4ee02e-53","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/data/lines.js","offset":1,"limit":20}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3972,"output_tokens":2920,"cache_read_input_tokens":107008,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"b84a86cb-7290-45ea-9355-eb902272100a"}
