{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f70fdf32-3164-4ca4-b36a-4c224c9593b5-72","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"505→     * controllers, triggers, tags, movers, force fields, belts; gravity and the solver back to\\n     * their defaults), particles, HUD and music, and resets the scene background, fog and the\\n     * sun / ambient light to the engine defaults. Filters, render\\n     * mode, resolution, quality, volumes and the camera rig carry over; pass `camera` to\\n     * switch the preset (applied before `setup()`, so `ctx.camera` is already the new one).\\n510→     * Nothing advances while loading, and input made while loading is dropped (data sent with\\n     * `ctx.input.send` waits for the first frame that runs).\\n     */\\n    loadGame(game: Game, options?: {\\n        camera?: CameraConfig;\\n    }): Promise<void>;\\n    /**\\n     * Stop the loop and free everything: game, scene, physics, audio, input listeners, DOM,\\n     * GPU. With a `loadGame()` in flight, the world and GPU resources are freed once its\\n     * `setup()` has finished (it never runs against a freed physics world or renderer).\\n520→     */\\n    dispose(): void;\\n    /** Switch the camera preset for a level that is loading (no game hooks, no URL sync). */\\n    private useCamera;\\n    /** `Game.ready`: like any hook, an exception goes to `errors` and the screen; the game runs on. */\",\"content_concise\":\"505→     * controllers, triggers, tags, movers, force fields, belts; gravity and the solver back to\\n     * their defaults), particles, HUD and music, and resets the scene background, fog and the\\n     * sun / ambient light to the engine defaults. Filters, render\\n     * mode, resolution, quality, volumes and the camera rig carry over; pass `camera` to\\n     * switch the preset (applied before `setup()`, so `ctx.camera` is already the new one).\\n510→     * Nothing advances while loading, and input made while loading is dropped (data sent with\\n     * `ctx.input.send` waits for the first frame that runs).\\n     */\\n    loadGame(game: Game, options?: {\\n        camera?: CameraConfig;\\n    }): Promise<void>;\\n    /**\\n     * Stop the loop and free everything: game, scene, physics, audio, input listeners, DOM,\\n     * GPU. With a `loadGame()` in flight, the world and GPU resources are freed once its\\n     * `setup()` has finished (it never runs against a freed physics world or renderer).\\n520→     */\\n    dispose(): void;\\n    /** Switch the camera preset for a level that is loading (no game hooks, no URL sync). */\\n    private useCamera;\\n    /** `Game.ready`: like any hook, an exception goes to `errors` and the screen; the game runs on. */\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/types/engine/Engine.d.ts\",\"offset\":505,\"limit\":20,\"raw_output\":\"     * controllers, triggers, tags, movers, force fields, belts; gravity and the solver back to\\n     * their defaults), particles, HUD and music, and resets the scene background, fog and the\\n     * sun / ambient light to the engine defaults. Filters, render\\n     * mode, resolution, quality, volumes and the camera rig carry over; pass `camera` to\\n     * switch the preset (applied before `setup()`, so `ctx.camera` is already the new one).\\n     * Nothing advances while loading, and input made while loading is dropped (data sent with\\n     * `ctx.input.send` waits for the first frame that runs).\\n     */\\n    loadGame(game: Game, options?: {\\n        camera?: CameraConfig;\\n    }): Promise<void>;\\n    /**\\n     * Stop the loop and free everything: game, scene, physics, audio, input listeners, DOM,\\n     * GPU. With a `loadGame()` in flight, the world and GPU resources are freed once its\\n     * `setup()` has finished (it never runs against a freed physics world or renderer).\\n     */\\n    dispose(): void;\\n    /** Switch the camera preset for a level that is loading (no game hooks, no URL sync). */\\n    private useCamera;\\n    /** `Game.ready`: like any hook, an exception goes to `errors` and the screen; the game runs on. */\\n\",\"total_lines\":613}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"e14b726e-dcf3-486a-a050-43e60d40070d"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_198","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Filters, render mode, resolution, quality, volumes, and the camera rig carry over.\n\nWriting the files now. Input during loading is dropped. The test script handles focused rows and double Enter correctly.\n\nBack navigation works correctly. Day 4 plaza and jog station back buttons return to the island. Visit does not require an activity to be playable. The test script will also visit the jar, locker, and hall screens to prevent errors.\n\nThe day 2 test sequence will visit the jar first, then the locker, hall, and hammock. Entering a skin cycles it, so the script will back out instead of selecting one.\n\nThe jar back button resets focus and page correctly. The test will visit the jar only once, then use hammock every day to save taps. Sleep always opens the report since the day always has at least one activity. The lose state is skipped because it cannot be triggered. Star counts on sweep results are verified, and expert mode requires two easy completions.\n\nIf the idle hoop scores points, the simulation will be fixed rather than retuning the dot. The test file will be thorough but not overly commented. GPU flags for unsafe WebGPU and Vulkan SwiftShader are being configured.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-99cd1ff3-c1b5-4dcb-b5ea-decf7f7e2ed8-73","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/ui/font.js","offset":43,"limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":520,"output_tokens":2007,"cache_read_input_tokens":146176,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"0d891d6e-4255-4979-849a-93db2f01fc84"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-99cd1ff3-c1b5-4dcb-b5ea-decf7f7e2ed8-73","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"43→/** Wrap to a character width. Each piece is at most `cols` characters. */\\nexport function wrapText(text, cols) {\\n  const width = Math.max(1, cols | 0);\\n  const words = String(text).split(/\\\\s+/).filter(Boolean);\\n  const lines = [];\\n  let line = '';\\n  for (const word of words) {\\n50→    const next = line ? `${line} ${word}` : word;\\n    if (next.length <= width) line = next;\\n    else {\\n      if (line) lines.push(line);\\n      if (word.length <= width) line = word;\\n      else {\\n        for (let i = 0; i < word.length; i += width) lines.push(word.slice(i, i + width));\\n        line = '';\\n      }\\n    }\\n60→  }\\n  if (line) lines.push(line);\\n  return lines.length ? lines : [''];\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"43→/** Wrap to a character width. Each piece is at most `cols` characters. */\\nexport function wrapText(text, cols) {\\n  const width = Math.max(1, cols | 0);\\n  const words = String(text).split(/\\\\s+/).filter(Boolean);\\n  const lines = [];\\n  let line = '';\\n  for (const word of words) {\\n50→    const next = line ? `${line} ${word}` : word;\\n    if (next.length <= width) line = next;\\n    else {\\n      if (line) lines.push(line);\\n      if (word.length <= width) line = word;\\n      else {\\n        for (let i = 0; i < word.length; i += width) lines.push(word.slice(i, i + width));\\n        line = '';\\n      }\\n    }\\n60→  }\\n  if (line) lines.push(line);\\n  return lines.length ? lines : [''];\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/ui/font.js\",\"offset\":43,\"limit\":30,\"raw_output\":\"/** Wrap to a character width. Each piece is at most `cols` characters. */\\nexport function wrapText(text, cols) {\\n  const width = Math.max(1, cols | 0);\\n  const words = String(text).split(/\\\\s+/).filter(Boolean);\\n  const lines = [];\\n  let line = '';\\n  for (const word of words) {\\n    const next = line ? `${line} ${word}` : word;\\n    if (next.length <= width) line = next;\\n    else {\\n      if (line) lines.push(line);\\n      if (word.length <= width) line = word;\\n      else {\\n        for (let i = 0; i < word.length; i += width) lines.push(word.slice(i, i + width));\\n        line = '';\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n  if (line) lines.push(line);\\n  return lines.length ? lines : [''];\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":63}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"573abf7e-e9eb-49b7-a5e2-ed1b83903ebb"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_199","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The test should assert wrapped line lengths do not exceed 52 characters and dialogue line counts do not exceed three.\n\nThe test will verify that every wrapped piece is at most 52 characters and that displayed dialogue lines do not exceed three. If a sample produces four lines, the test will fail.\n\nThe implementation will avoid Python. Tests will run in a specific order: dot, lines, and songs first for quick failures, then the clips engine, then main. Star sweep results will log to beat.log instead of stdout. The script will exit with code 1 on failure.\n\nThe test will not import main.js to avoid booting the document-based engine. Browser errors will be returned as an array so the failure count is accurate. The test.mjs file will be written in a single pass.\n\nThe browser suite will be a single bundled test that throws a combined message of the first failures. Each check inside runBrowser will write to browser.log. The hub log will be written directly from browser.mjs. The test file is expected to be roughly 800 to 1000 lines.\n\nThe back button is confirmed to appear after activity results. Activities will keep running until they throw a status error. The driver is set before the activity starts, which prevents the first flag from being true. Drips and records accumulate across sweep activities but do not alter simulation difficulty.\n\nHard mode requires setting guest.hard before the activity starts. The sloppy and expert sweep scores will be compared on the same activity ID; because each run uses a different RNG fork, sloppy should score lower than expert. Header idle scores must stay under 150, while expert sweep scores must reach at least 400.\n\nDirect starsFor checks will be added. The week chart will verify the shown age equals trueAge plus seven before confession and matches trueAge afterward, without recomputing trueAge. T-score values from chart points will be included in the samples.\n\nChart length will increase each morning, and T-score values will be between zero and one. The test will also verify that no mode calls gameover. For the family test, navigator.getGamepads will be assigned via globalThis or Object.defineProperty to work in Node 21+, with a quick fix if it fails.\n\nThe test will press the pad before stepping so the edge is detected. Enter will be tapped by setting the key true, stepping, then false; this claims the key and skips the menu without activating fill. Pad transitions will use step(1) only to avoid stale button states. Arrow keys held during choose will be released.\n\nBrowser instances will be closed in a finally block. Screenshots will be saved to scratch/shots/ and boot images to scratch/. A widget fit function will be added. For the phone attract test, the engine will step 700 frames inside the page or wait until mode is attract; the touch-only message may still appear during that state.\n\nThe attract mode branch includes the title branch, so the touch-only message remains visible during attract mode. The settings button stays in the DOM because the engine created it at startup. I will verify that `engine.touch` is null or `touch: false` to match the plan.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f4555793-205c-4869-b50e-98da173c883b-74","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"touch:","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/types/engine/Engine.d.ts"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2228,"output_tokens":1899,"cache_read_input_tokens":146688,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"d1053e59-6fde-4658-ad0f-447c6fa65614"}
