{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a347025d-c36e-455f-9144-31e87f2ae5e1-75","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→---\\nname: long-running-background-tasks\\ndescription: >-\\n  Required reading before you start, watch, or wait on anything that keeps running after you launch it — background jobs, watchers, scheduled loops, CI, pull requests, training runs, dev servers, long builds. Read it before you launch such work and before you report on its state. Saying where a running job stands counts as working on it. Use when: about to launch, supervise, inspect, diagnose, or report on work that keeps running after it is started.\\n---\\n\\n# Working with long-running background tasks\\n\\nOnly submitting or queuing jobs is not sufficient to complete the task. The definition of done is the job has completed successfully and you have verified that it has produced all the expected outputs.\\n10→\\nThis means you must see through the jobs completion by watching the job to ensure that its healthy, progressing, and working as intended.\\n\\n## Tools available\\n\\nThere's two ways to watch jobs: monitor and loop. Decide which of the two you need, sometimes you need both.\\n\\n### monitor — deterministic, actionable events\\n\\n- Use a monitor when the event is a predicate a script can evaluate — an API response, an exit code, a port answering.\\n20→- Typical events: CI turning red, a PR comment or merge conflict, a PR becoming ready to merge, a dev server coming up or going down, a job reaching a terminal state.\\n- The monitor requires a script polls on a fixed cadence and stays silent until the predicate fires, so an idle job costs nothing. More on writing good monitoring scripts below.\\n- Examples of when to use:\\n  - Monitoring a PR — wake on CI breaking, merge conflicts, etc.\\n  - Checking if local tooling is up — wake on the service being unavailable, errors, etc.\\n  - All of these wakeup cases can be checked deterministically.\\n\\n### loop — qualitative health that needs reading\\n\\n- Use a loop when judging health requires reading the logs and system information to detect failing, faulty or stalled jobs. It uses a subagent which is more expensive but more thorough.\\n30→- Typical signals: the loss curve going unstable, a filtering pipeline producing garbage, throughput quietly degrading, faulty nodes throwing CUDA errors.\\n- A subagent reads the logs on a fixed cadence (say every 10 min) and reports what changed, so it costs a wakeup every cycle.\\n- Examples of when to use:\\n  - Checking on a training or data processing job — the subagent should scan for instability, degradation, faulty nodes, etc.\\n  - Monitoring system deployment health — the subagent should scan for 4xx/5xx, response times, resources, etc.\\n  - All of these wakeup cases are hard to describe deterministically and hard to fully enumerate, so it is better to use a subagent to validate.\\n\\n## Good monitoring scripts\\n\\nThe monitor tool wakes you up every time you log to stdout. Wakeups are expensive, so only log if there is something actionable — but log it as early as possible, since staying silent delays the task. Plan accordingly: minimize the number of wakeups while still firing them as quickly as possible.\\n40→\\n### Planning\\n\\n- Enumerate all terminal conditions.\\n  - For PRs, this includes the PR being merged or closed.\\n  - For long-running jobs, this includes the job completing or unrecoverable failures.\\n- Enumerate all other situations where a wakeup is needed.\\n  - For PRs, this would include when a comment arrives (there are four different types of PR comments), when CI fails, when a merge conflict arises, and when the PR becomes ready to merge (CI green, no conflicts, reviews complete, no blockers).\\n  - For an ML training job, this can be when the loss is unstable or the instance is preempted.\\n- Determine situations where the monitoring has to update what it is tracking. For example, for monitoring PRs, the latest commit hash may change as you push new commits.\\n50→\\n### Writing\\n\\n- The monitoring script should poll every 30s. `watch_pr.py` defaults to\\n  `--poll-interval 30`. Lower intervals cause GitHub rate limits, especially\\n  with more than one watcher on the same token.\\n- Based on the planning, exit immediately on terminal conditions with FAILED, DONE, or CANCELLED, and log ACTION_REQUIRED for wakeups.\\n- Send all debug diagnostics — both your watcher's own trace and the monitored job's output — to a file, so a log line can never be mistaken for DONE, FAILED, or CANCELLED.\\n- The script should fail as early as possible. Emit a FAILED token immediately when any required condition reaches terminal failure. For example, if you are waiting on CI and any of them fail, emit FAILED immediately.\\n- Write the script to a durable location such as ~/.grok and name it something clear such as `ci_watcher.sh`.\\n60→- Key every log file the script writes on the pid or session id of the thing being watched. The paths are otherwise fixed, so a second job of the same kind silently clobbers the first one's log.\\n\\n## Handling wake-ups\\n\\n- Address errors or actionable events immediately. Look through the logs and debug the issue thoroughly before settling on a root cause, as long-running processes are generally expensive. Resubmit the job once it is fixed:\\n  - For PRs, this means repushing the changes and restarting CI (if needed).\\n  - For jobs, requeue or relaunch the job.\\n  - Always restart the monitor or loop so that it points at the new PR or job.\\n- If there are multiple jobs running, start debugging immediately when any jobs fail. Minimize total wall-time with completing tasks.\\n\\n70→## Restarts\\n\\n- Whenever you relaunch a job, always update the monitor.\\n- Monitors have a maximum 10-hour time limit, so be sure to restart them if you hit the time limit and if the task being monitored is still running.\\n- When you spawn a new monitor, make sure to kill any previous ones that the new one replaces. For example, if you fix a training run and respawn it, be sure to kill previous monitors, as irrelevant wakeups are expensive.\\n\\n## Cleanup\\n\\n- If a monitor is in a terminal state, kill the monitor, the loop, and the job. Dangling processes such as unkilled broken training runs are expensive. Then, address all issues if present.\\n- If an outdated monitor wakes you — that is, it is attached to an old or dead run — make sure to kill it.\\n80→- Do not leave detached workers, duplicate pollers, or orphaned watcher processes behind.\\n\\n## Examples\\n\\n### Example: maintaining a dev server\\n\\nSuppose you just made some changes to the user's frontend code and would like to spin it up to test it. While you're testing it, you would like to know if the server goes down for any reason (if you made changes, for example). This is a great use case for the monitor tool. First start a React app in a background terminal, which reports its pid:\\n\\n```\\nrun_terminal_command(\\n90→  command=\\\"echo $$; npm start >~/.grok/long-running-background-tasks/dev_server_$$.log 2>&1\\\",\\n  timeout=0,\\n  description=\\\"Start the dev server on :3000\\\",\\n  background=true\\n) # prints the pid 123456789\\n```\\n\\nThere are no terminal states, but there are two actionable events from the watcher: `http://localhost:3000` coming up and going down.\\n\\nYou want to be notified as soon as it is up so you can use it, and you want to be woken when it stops so you can address it — fix the code, restart the server, free the port. Both down paths quote the tail of the server's log, so the wakeup arrives with the error already in hand. Polling every 5s is a good cadence since you want to quickly fix it if it is down, and it is not expensive to poll.\\n100→\\n```bash\\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\\n# Log paths are keyed on the server pid so two dev servers cannot clobber each other.\\nPID=$1 URL=http://localhost:3000 DIR=~/.grok/long-running-background-tasks\\nLOG=$DIR/dev_server_$PID.log\\nup() { curl -fsS -o /dev/null --max-time 5 \\\"$URL\\\" 2>>\\\"$DIR/watch_dev_server_$PID.log\\\"; }\\nwhy() { tail -20 \\\"$LOG\\\" | tr -d '\\\\r' | tr '\\\\n' ' '; }\\n\\nuntil up; do\\n110→  kill -0 \\\"$PID\\\" 2>/dev/null || { echo \\\"FAILED: pid $PID exited before $URL came up: $(why)\\\"; exit 1; }\\n  sleep 5\\ndone\\necho \\\"ACTION_REQUIRED: $URL is up\\\"\\n\\nwhile :; do\\n  sleep 5\\n  up || { echo \\\"ACTION_REQUIRED: $URL is down: $(why)\\\"; until up; do sleep 5; done; }\\ndone\\n```\\n120→\\nTo spawn the monitor, point it at the pid `npm start` reported:\\n\\n```\\nmonitor(\\n  command='bash ~/.grok/long-running-background-tasks/watch_dev_server.sh 123456789',\\n  description=\\\"Watch the dev server on :3000\\\"\\n)\\n```\\n\\n130→On the first wakeup the app is ready to use and you can start testing it. After that, you may be woken up if the server goes down. When you do:\\n- Read `~/.grok/long-running-background-tasks/dev_server_<pid>.log` for the full compile error or port conflict and fix it.\\n- If the dev server survived, hot reload picks the fix up and the watcher recovers on its own, so leave the monitor running.\\n- If the process is dead, restart it with a fresh `run_terminal_command`, then kill this monitor and spawn a new one against the new pid.\\n\\n### Example: PR monitoring\\n\\nPR monitoring should stop when the PR is merged or closed, and it should wake up on:\\n- For comments, you should ask users how they would like to resolve them (which ones to address automatically, whether to respond / resolve, etc.), then store the decision for new future sessions. There are four different types of PR comments.\\n  - Inline review threads\\n140→  - Review bodies\\n  - Conversation comments\\n  - Commit comments\\n- Failing CI - most can be fixed in the code but sometimes they may be flaky. For flaky CI, just rerun them.\\n- Merge conflicts\\n- The PR becoming ready to merge — CI passes, no merge conflicts, reviews complete, no blockers, no unresolved inline threads. That wakeup is `kind: mergeable`. Tell the user they can merge now. It is not terminal; keep watching until merge or close.\\n\\nYou can find the example script bundled with this skill at watch_pr.py. It needs an authenticated `gh` CLI (`gh auth login`) and `python3`. Default poll is 30s; a lower poll rate may hit GitHub rate limits at higher concurrency. Transport errors (timeouts, resets, DNS) retry with backoff and jitter and do not print a line.\\n\\n```\\n150→monitor(\\n  command='python3 ~/.grok/long-running-background-tasks/watch_pr.py \\\"https://github.com/xai-org/grok-build/pull/123\\\"',\\n  description=\\\"Watch PR 123\\\"\\n)\\n```\\n\\n### Example: training monitoring\\n\\nFor monitoring long training jobs, the terminal conditions are when the job either fails or completes. Further, many issues cannot be caught deterministically, so use a subagent to run a script for most of the high-level update, then scan the logs for errors such as faulty nodes or CUDA warnings.\\n\\n160→The script below is bundled with this skill as watch_training.py. Run it with `--help` for every flag and for the run-directory and log-line layout it expects, since it parses nanoGPT stdout out of a Slurm run dir.\\n\\n```md\\nKeep an eye on the nanoGPT run nanogpt_owt_124m_r1 (slurm job 1234567) and tell me what changed since last time. Worktree ~/worktrees/nanogpt-owt-124m.\\n\\n1. python3 ~/.grok/skills/long-running-background-tasks/watch_training.py --run-name nanogpt_owt_124m_r1 --job-id 1234567 --target-val 3.00\\n\\nHow to report:\\n- Start with the job's state and if it changed, e.g. \\\"still RUNNING\\\" or \\\"PENDING -> RUNNING\\\".\\n- Copy the ISSUES line and the STATUS line from the monitor exactly as it is written, numbers and all. STATUS will include where the run is heading: how far along, iters left, the eta, and whether val loss is still coming down. We want val loss at or under 3.00.\\n170→- If the state didn't change, tell me that in one line and stop.\\n- If the job has finished or died, give me the state, the exit code, and the last ISSUES, and run these two for me:\\n  sacct -j 1234567 -D -X -P -o JobID,State,ExitCode,DerivedExitCode,Elapsed,NodeList,FailedNode\\n  tail -20 ~/train_logs/slurm-nanogpt_owt_124m_r1-1234567.out\\n\\nKeep <=10 lines: state, progress and eta, loss trend, then anything that smells like training going unstable (loss spiking, NaN, val loss creeping back up) or the cluster misbehaving (a drained or failing node, OOM, NCCL errors, a preemption, iters suddenly slower than usual).\\n```\\n\\nLaunch the scheduler on a 10 min interval, and spawn a monitor to be notified when the job crashes or succeeds.\\n\\n180→```\\nscheduler_create(\\n  interval=\\\"10m\\\",\\n  prompt: \\\"...\\\", # Copy from the prompt above.\\n)\\nmonitor(\\n  # Wakes on pending/running/finished changes after the first observation.\\n  # First poll is silent unless the job is already COMPLETED or failed —\\n  # PENDING matches *ING, so treating an empty previous state as a\\n  # transition would wake immediately on a just-submitted job.\\n190→  command='J=1234567; p=; while :; do s=$(sacct -nXP -j $J -o State|head -1); s=${s%% *}; s=${s:-PENDING}; if [ \\\"$s\\\" != \\\"$p\\\" ]; then case $s in COMPLETED) echo \\\"DONE: $J\\\"; exit;; PENDING|RUNNING|CONFIGURING|COMPLETING|REQUEUED|SUSPENDED|RESIZING) [ -n \\\"$p\\\" ] && echo \\\"ACTION_REQUIRED: $J $p -> $s\\\";; *) echo \\\"FAILED: $J $s\\\"; exit 1;; esac; fi; p=$s; sleep 30; done',\\n  description=\\\"Watch training run\\\"\\n)\\n```\\n\\nLaunch both, so that we know when the job completes. When the monitor reports that the job has completed, cancel both the monitor and the scheduler, then determine next steps. Then:\\n- If it succeeded, simply present the results to the user.\\n- If it failed, debug the issue thoroughly, then fix and relaunch the job with new monitors attached. Make sure to have a thorough understanding of the issue before resubmitting, since training jobs are expensive. But always relaunch jobs so you don't waste the user's time.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→---\\nname: long-running-background-tasks\\ndescription: >-\\n  Required reading before you start, watch, or wait on anything that keeps running after you launch it — background jobs, watchers, scheduled loops, CI, pull requests, training runs, dev servers, long builds. Read it before you launch such work and before you report on its state. Saying where a running job stands counts as working on it. Use when: about to launch, supervise, inspect, diagnose, or report on work that keeps running after it is started.\\n---\\n\\n# Working with long-running background tasks\\n\\nOnly submitting or queuing jobs is not sufficient to complete the task. The definition of done is the job has completed successfully and you have verified that it has produced all the expected outputs.\\n10→\\nThis means you must see through the jobs completion by watching the job to ensure that its healthy, progressing, and working as intended.\\n\\n## Tools available\\n\\nThere's two ways to watch jobs: monitor and loop. Decide which of the two you need, sometimes you need both.\\n\\n### monitor — deterministic, actionable events\\n\\n- Use a monitor when the event is a predicate a script can evaluate — an API response, an exit code, a port answering.\\n20→- Typical events: CI turning red, a PR comment or merge conflict, a PR becoming ready to merge, a dev server coming up or going down, a job reaching a terminal state.\\n- The monitor requires a script polls on a fixed cadence and stays silent until the predicate fires, so an idle job costs nothing. More on writing good monitoring scripts below.\\n- Examples of when to use:\\n  - Monitoring a PR — wake on CI breaking, merge conflicts, etc.\\n  - Checking if local tooling is up — wake on the service being unavailable, errors, etc.\\n  - All of these wakeup cases can be checked deterministically.\\n\\n### loop — qualitative health that needs reading\\n\\n- Use a loop when judging health requires reading the logs and system information to detect failing, faulty or stalled jobs. It uses a subagent which is more expensive but more thorough.\\n30→- Typical signals: the loss curve going unstable, a filtering pipeline producing garbage, throughput quietly degrading, faulty nodes throwing CUDA errors.\\n- A subagent reads the logs on a fixed cadence (say every 10 min) and reports what changed, so it costs a wakeup every cycle.\\n- Examples of when to use:\\n  - Checking on a training or data processing job — the subagent should scan for instability, degradation, faulty nodes, etc.\\n  - Monitoring system deployment health — the subagent should scan for 4xx/5xx, response times, resources, etc.\\n  - All of these wakeup cases are hard to describe deterministically and hard to fully enumerate, so it is better to use a subagent to validate.\\n\\n## Good monitoring scripts\\n\\nThe monitor tool wakes you up every time you log to stdout. Wakeups are expensive, so only log if there is something actionable — but log it as early as possible, since staying silent delays the task. Plan accordingly: minimize the number of wakeups while still firing them as quickly as possible.\\n40→\\n### Planning\\n\\n- Enumerate all terminal conditions.\\n  - For PRs, this includes the PR being merged or closed.\\n  - For long-running jobs, this includes the job completing or unrecoverable failures.\\n- Enumerate all other situations where a wakeup is needed.\\n  - For PRs, this would include when a comment arrives (there are four different types of PR comments), when CI fails, when a merge conflict arises, and when the PR becomes ready to merge (CI green, no conflicts, reviews complete, no blockers).\\n  - For an ML training job, this can be when the loss is unstable or the instance is preempted.\\n- Determine situations where the monitoring has to update what it is tracking. For example, for monitoring PRs, the latest commit hash may change as you push new commits.\\n50→\\n### Writing\\n\\n- The monitoring script should poll every 30s. `watch_pr.py` defaults to\\n  `--poll-interval 30`. Lower intervals cause GitHub rate limits, especially\\n  with more than one watcher on the same token.\\n- Based on the planning, exit immediately on terminal conditions with FAILED, DONE, or CANCELLED, and log ACTION_REQUIRED for wakeups.\\n- Send all debug diagnostics — both your watcher's own trace and the monitored job's output — to a file, so a log line can never be mistaken for DONE, FAILED, or CANCELLED.\\n- The script should fail as early as possible. Emit a FAILED token immediately when any required condition reaches terminal failure. For example, if you are waiting on CI and any of them fail, emit FAILED immediately.\\n- Write the script to a durable location such as ~/.grok and name it something clear such as `ci_watcher.sh`.\\n60→- Key every log file the script writes on the pid or session id of the thing being watched. The paths are otherwise fixed, so a second job of the same kind silently clobbers the first one's log.\\n\\n## Handling wake-ups\\n\\n- Address errors or actionable events immediately. Look through the logs and debug the issue thoroughly before settling on a root cause, as long-running processes are generally expensive. Resubmit the job once it is fixed:\\n  - For PRs, this means repushing the changes and restarting CI (if needed).\\n  - For jobs, requeue or relaunch the job.\\n  - Always restart the monitor or loop so that it points at the new PR or job.\\n- If there are multiple jobs running, start debugging immediately when any jobs fail. Minimize total wall-time with completing tasks.\\n\\n70→## Restarts\\n\\n- Whenever you relaunch a job, always update the monitor.\\n- Monitors have a maximum 10-hour time limit, so be sure to restart them if you hit the time limit and if the task being monitored is still running.\\n- When you spawn a new monitor, make sure to kill any previous ones that the new one replaces. For example, if you fix a training run and respawn it, be sure to kill previous monitors, as irrelevant wakeups are expensive.\\n\\n## Cleanup\\n\\n- If a monitor is in a terminal state, kill the monitor, the loop, and the job. Dangling processes such as unkilled broken training runs are expensive. Then, address all issues if present.\\n- If an outdated monitor wakes you — that is, it is attached to an old or dead run — make sure to kill it.\\n80→- Do not leave detached workers, duplicate pollers, or orphaned watcher processes behind.\\n\\n## Examples\\n\\n### Example: maintaining a dev server\\n\\nSuppose you just made some changes to the user's frontend code and would like to spin it up to test it. While you're testing it, you would like to know if the server goes down for any reason (if you made changes, for example). This is a great use case for the monitor tool. First start a React app in a background terminal, which reports its pid:\\n\\n```\\nrun_terminal_command(\\n90→  command=\\\"echo $$; npm start >~/.grok/long-running-background-tasks/dev_server_$$.log 2>&1\\\",\\n  timeout=0,\\n  description=\\\"Start the dev server on :3000\\\",\\n  background=true\\n) # prints the pid 123456789\\n```\\n\\nThere are no terminal states, but there are two actionable events from the watcher: `http://localhost:3000` coming up and going down.\\n\\nYou want to be notified as soon as it is up so you can use it, and you want to be woken when it stops so you can address it — fix the code, restart the server, free the port. Both down paths quote the tail of the server's log, so the wakeup arrives with the error already in hand. Polling every 5s is a good cadence since you want to quickly fix it if it is down, and it is not expensive to poll.\\n100→\\n```bash\\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\\n# Log paths are keyed on the server pid so two dev servers cannot clobber each other.\\nPID=$1 URL=http://localhost:3000 DIR=~/.grok/long-running-background-tasks\\nLOG=$DIR/dev_server_$PID.log\\nup() { curl -fsS -o /dev/null --max-time 5 \\\"$URL\\\" 2>>\\\"$DIR/watch_dev_server_$PID.log\\\"; }\\nwhy() { tail -20 \\\"$LOG\\\" | tr -d '\\\\r' | tr '\\\\n' ' '; }\\n\\nuntil up; do\\n110→  kill -0 \\\"$PID\\\" 2>/dev/null || { echo \\\"FAILED: pid $PID exited before $URL came up: $(why)\\\"; exit 1; }\\n  sleep 5\\ndone\\necho \\\"ACTION_REQUIRED: $URL is up\\\"\\n\\nwhile :; do\\n  sleep 5\\n  up || { echo \\\"ACTION_REQUIRED: $URL is down: $(why)\\\"; until up; do sleep 5; done; }\\ndone\\n```\\n120→\\nTo spawn the monitor, point it at the pid `npm start` reported:\\n\\n```\\nmonitor(\\n  command='bash ~/.grok/long-running-background-tasks/watch_dev_server.sh 123456789',\\n  description=\\\"Watch the dev server on :3000\\\"\\n)\\n```\\n\\n130→On the first wakeup the app is ready to use and you can start testing it. After that, you may be woken up if the server goes down. When you do:\\n- Read `~/.grok/long-running-background-tasks/dev_server_<pid>.log` for the full compile error or port conflict and fix it.\\n- If the dev server survived, hot reload picks the fix up and the watcher recovers on its own, so leave the monitor running.\\n- If the process is dead, restart it with a fresh `run_terminal_command`, then kill this monitor and spawn a new one against the new pid.\\n\\n### Example: PR monitoring\\n\\nPR monitoring should stop when the PR is merged or closed, and it should wake up on:\\n- For comments, you should ask users how they would like to resolve them (which ones to address automatically, whether to respond / resolve, etc.), then store the decision for new future sessions. There are four different types of PR comments.\\n  - Inline review threads\\n140→  - Review bodies\\n  - Conversation comments\\n  - Commit comments\\n- Failing CI - most can be fixed in the code but sometimes they may be flaky. For flaky CI, just rerun them.\\n- Merge conflicts\\n- The PR becoming ready to merge — CI passes, no merge conflicts, reviews complete, no blockers, no unresolved inline threads. That wakeup is `kind: mergeable`. Tell the user they can merge now. It is not terminal; keep watching until merge or close.\\n\\nYou can find the example script bundled with this skill at watch_pr.py. It needs an authenticated `gh` CLI (`gh auth login`) and `python3`. Default poll is 30s; a lower poll rate may hit GitHub rate limits at higher concurrency. Transport errors (timeouts, resets, DNS) retry with backoff and jitter and do not print a line.\\n\\n```\\n150→monitor(\\n  command='python3 ~/.grok/long-running-background-tasks/watch_pr.py \\\"https://github.com/xai-org/grok-build/pull/123\\\"',\\n  description=\\\"Watch PR 123\\\"\\n)\\n```\\n\\n### Example: training monitoring\\n\\nFor monitoring long training jobs, the terminal conditions are when the job either fails or completes. Further, many issues cannot be caught deterministically, so use a subagent to run a script for most of the high-level update, then scan the logs for errors such as faulty nodes or CUDA warnings.\\n\\n160→The script below is bundled with this skill as watch_training.py. Run it with `--help` for every flag and for the run-directory and log-line layout it expects, since it parses nanoGPT stdout out of a Slurm run dir.\\n\\n```md\\nKeep an eye on the nanoGPT run nanogpt_owt_124m_r1 (slurm job 1234567) and tell me what changed since last time. Worktree ~/worktrees/nanogpt-owt-124m.\\n\\n1. python3 ~/.grok/skills/long-running-background-tasks/watch_training.py --run-name nanogpt_owt_124m_r1 --job-id 1234567 --target-val 3.00\\n\\nHow to report:\\n- Start with the job's state and if it changed, e.g. \\\"still RUNNING\\\" or \\\"PENDING -> RUNNING\\\".\\n- Copy the ISSUES line and the STATUS line from the monitor exactly as it is written, numbers and all. STATUS will include where the run is heading: how far along, iters left, the eta, and whether val loss is still coming down. We want val loss at or under 3.00.\\n170→- If the state didn't change, tell me that in one line and stop.\\n- If the job has finished or died, give me the state, the exit code, and the last ISSUES, and run these two for me:\\n  sacct -j 1234567 -D -X -P -o JobID,State,ExitCode,DerivedExitCode,Elapsed,NodeList,FailedNode\\n  tail -20 ~/train_logs/slurm-nanogpt_owt_124m_r1-1234567.out\\n\\nKeep <=10 lines: state, progress and eta, loss trend, then anything that smells like training going unstable (loss spiking, NaN, val loss creeping back up) or the cluster misbehaving (a drained or failing node, OOM, NCCL errors, a preemption, iters suddenly slower than usual).\\n```\\n\\nLaunch the scheduler on a 10 min interval, and spawn a monitor to be notified when the job crashes or succeeds.\\n\\n180→```\\nscheduler_create(\\n  interval=\\\"10m\\\",\\n  prompt: \\\"...\\\", # Copy from the prompt above.\\n)\\nmonitor(\\n  # Wakes on pending/running/finished changes after the first observation.\\n  # First poll is silent unless the job is already COMPLETED or failed —\\n  # PENDING matches *ING, so treating an empty previous state as a\\n  # transition would wake immediately on a just-submitted job.\\n190→  command='J=1234567; p=; while :; do s=$(sacct -nXP -j $J -o State|head -1); s=${s%% *}; s=${s:-PENDING}; if [ \\\"$s\\\" != \\\"$p\\\" ]; then case $s in COMPLETED) echo \\\"DONE: $J\\\"; exit;; PENDING|RUNNING|CONFIGURING|COMPLETING|REQUEUED|SUSPENDED|RESIZING) [ -n \\\"$p\\\" ] && echo \\\"ACTION_REQUIRED: $J $p -> $s\\\";; *) echo \\\"FAILED: $J $s\\\"; exit 1;; esac; fi; p=$s; sleep 30; done',\\n  description=\\\"Watch training run\\\"\\n)\\n```\\n\\nLaunch both, so that we know when the job completes. When the monitor reports that the job has completed, cancel both the monitor and the scheduler, then determine next steps. Then:\\n- If it succeeded, simply present the results to the user.\\n- If it failed, debug the issue thoroughly, then fix and relaunch the job with new monitors attached. Make sure to have a thorough understanding of the issue before resubmitting, since training jobs are expensive. But always relaunch jobs so you don't waste the user's time.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/.grok/bundled/skills/long-running-background-tasks/SKILL.md\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"---\\nname: long-running-background-tasks\\ndescription: >-\\n  Required reading before you start, watch, or wait on anything that keeps running after you launch it — background jobs, watchers, scheduled loops, CI, pull requests, training runs, dev servers, long builds. Read it before you launch such work and before you report on its state. Saying where a running job stands counts as working on it. Use when: about to launch, supervise, inspect, diagnose, or report on work that keeps running after it is started.\\n---\\n\\n# Working with long-running background tasks\\n\\nOnly submitting or queuing jobs is not sufficient to complete the task. The definition of done is the job has completed successfully and you have verified that it has produced all the expected outputs.\\n\\nThis means you must see through the jobs completion by watching the job to ensure that its healthy, progressing, and working as intended.\\n\\n## Tools available\\n\\nThere's two ways to watch jobs: monitor and loop. Decide which of the two you need, sometimes you need both.\\n\\n### monitor — deterministic, actionable events\\n\\n- Use a monitor when the event is a predicate a script can evaluate — an API response, an exit code, a port answering.\\n- Typical events: CI turning red, a PR comment or merge conflict, a PR becoming ready to merge, a dev server coming up or going down, a job reaching a terminal state.\\n- The monitor requires a script polls on a fixed cadence and stays silent until the predicate fires, so an idle job costs nothing. More on writing good monitoring scripts below.\\n- Examples of when to use:\\n  - Monitoring a PR — wake on CI breaking, merge conflicts, etc.\\n  - Checking if local tooling is up — wake on the service being unavailable, errors, etc.\\n  - All of these wakeup cases can be checked deterministically.\\n\\n### loop — qualitative health that needs reading\\n\\n- Use a loop when judging health requires reading the logs and system information to detect failing, faulty or stalled jobs. It uses a subagent which is more expensive but more thorough.\\n- Typical signals: the loss curve going unstable, a filtering pipeline producing garbage, throughput quietly degrading, faulty nodes throwing CUDA errors.\\n- A subagent reads the logs on a fixed cadence (say every 10 min) and reports what changed, so it costs a wakeup every cycle.\\n- Examples of when to use:\\n  - Checking on a training or data processing job — the subagent should scan for instability, degradation, faulty nodes, etc.\\n  - Monitoring system deployment health — the subagent should scan for 4xx/5xx, response times, resources, etc.\\n  - All of these wakeup cases are hard to describe deterministically and hard to fully enumerate, so it is better to use a subagent to validate.\\n\\n## Good monitoring scripts\\n\\nThe monitor tool wakes you up every time you log to stdout. Wakeups are expensive, so only log if there is something actionable — but log it as early as possible, since staying silent delays the task. Plan accordingly: minimize the number of wakeups while still firing them as quickly as possible.\\n\\n### Planning\\n\\n- Enumerate all terminal conditions.\\n  - For PRs, this includes the PR being merged or closed.\\n  - For long-running jobs, this includes the job completing or unrecoverable failures.\\n- Enumerate all other situations where a wakeup is needed.\\n  - For PRs, this would include when a comment arrives (there are four different types of PR comments), when CI fails, when a merge conflict arises, and when the PR becomes ready to merge (CI green, no conflicts, reviews complete, no blockers).\\n  - For an ML training job, this can be when the loss is unstable or the instance is preempted.\\n- Determine situations where the monitoring has to update what it is tracking. For example, for monitoring PRs, the latest commit hash may change as you push new commits.\\n\\n### Writing\\n\\n- The monitoring script should poll every 30s. `watch_pr.py` defaults to\\n  `--poll-interval 30`. Lower intervals cause GitHub rate limits, especially\\n  with more than one watcher on the same token.\\n- Based on the planning, exit immediately on terminal conditions with FAILED, DONE, or CANCELLED, and log ACTION_REQUIRED for wakeups.\\n- Send all debug diagnostics — both your watcher's own trace and the monitored job's output — to a file, so a log line can never be mistaken for DONE, FAILED, or CANCELLED.\\n- The script should fail as early as possible. Emit a FAILED token immediately when any required condition reaches terminal failure. For example, if you are waiting on CI and any of them fail, emit FAILED immediately.\\n- Write the script to a durable location such as ~/.grok and name it something clear such as `ci_watcher.sh`.\\n- Key every log file the script writes on the pid or session id of the thing being watched. The paths are otherwise fixed, so a second job of the same kind silently clobbers the first one's log.\\n\\n## Handling wake-ups\\n\\n- Address errors or actionable events immediately. Look through the logs and debug the issue thoroughly before settling on a root cause, as long-running processes are generally expensive. Resubmit the job once it is fixed:\\n  - For PRs, this means repushing the changes and restarting CI (if needed).\\n  - For jobs, requeue or relaunch the job.\\n  - Always restart the monitor or loop so that it points at the new PR or job.\\n- If there are multiple jobs running, start debugging immediately when any jobs fail. Minimize total wall-time with completing tasks.\\n\\n## Restarts\\n\\n- Whenever you relaunch a job, always update the monitor.\\n- Monitors have a maximum 10-hour time limit, so be sure to restart them if you hit the time limit and if the task being monitored is still running.\\n- When you spawn a new monitor, make sure to kill any previous ones that the new one replaces. For example, if you fix a training run and respawn it, be sure to kill previous monitors, as irrelevant wakeups are expensive.\\n\\n## Cleanup\\n\\n- If a monitor is in a terminal state, kill the monitor, the loop, and the job. Dangling processes such as unkilled broken training runs are expensive. Then, address all issues if present.\\n- If an outdated monitor wakes you — that is, it is attached to an old or dead run — make sure to kill it.\\n- Do not leave detached workers, duplicate pollers, or orphaned watcher processes behind.\\n\\n## Examples\\n\\n### Example: maintaining a dev server\\n\\nSuppose you just made some changes to the user's frontend code and would like to spin it up to test it. While you're testing it, you would like to know if the server goes down for any reason (if you made changes, for example). This is a great use case for the monitor tool. First start a React app in a background terminal, which reports its pid:\\n\\n```\\nrun_terminal_command(\\n  command=\\\"echo $$; npm start >~/.grok/long-running-background-tasks/dev_server_$$.log 2>&1\\\",\\n  timeout=0,\\n  description=\\\"Start the dev server on :3000\\\",\\n  background=true\\n) # prints the pid 123456789\\n```\\n\\nThere are no terminal states, but there are two actionable events from the watcher: `http://localhost:3000` coming up and going down.\\n\\nYou want to be notified as soon as it is up so you can use it, and you want to be woken when it stops so you can address it — fix the code, restart the server, free the port. Both down paths quote the tail of the server's log, so the wakeup arrives with the error already in hand. Polling every 5s is a good cadence since you want to quickly fix it if it is down, and it is not expensive to poll.\\n\\n```bash\\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\\n# Log paths are keyed on the server pid so two dev servers cannot clobber each other.\\nPID=$1 URL=http://localhost:3000 DIR=~/.grok/long-running-background-tasks\\nLOG=$DIR/dev_server_$PID.log\\nup() { curl -fsS -o /dev/null --max-time 5 \\\"$URL\\\" 2>>\\\"$DIR/watch_dev_server_$PID.log\\\"; }\\nwhy() { tail -20 \\\"$LOG\\\" | tr -d '\\\\r' | tr '\\\\n' ' '; }\\n\\nuntil up; do\\n  kill -0 \\\"$PID\\\" 2>/dev/null || { echo \\\"FAILED: pid $PID exited before $URL came up: $(why)\\\"; exit 1; }\\n  sleep 5\\ndone\\necho \\\"ACTION_REQUIRED: $URL is up\\\"\\n\\nwhile :; do\\n  sleep 5\\n  up || { echo \\\"ACTION_REQUIRED: $URL is down: $(why)\\\"; until up; do sleep 5; done; }\\ndone\\n```\\n\\nTo spawn the monitor, point it at the pid `npm start` reported:\\n\\n```\\nmonitor(\\n  command='bash ~/.grok/long-running-background-tasks/watch_dev_server.sh 123456789',\\n  description=\\\"Watch the dev server on :3000\\\"\\n)\\n```\\n\\nOn the first wakeup the app is ready to use and you can start testing it. After that, you may be woken up if the server goes down. When you do:\\n- Read `~/.grok/long-running-background-tasks/dev_server_<pid>.log` for the full compile error or port conflict and fix it.\\n- If the dev server survived, hot reload picks the fix up and the watcher recovers on its own, so leave the monitor running.\\n- If the process is dead, restart it with a fresh `run_terminal_command`, then kill this monitor and spawn a new one against the new pid.\\n\\n### Example: PR monitoring\\n\\nPR monitoring should stop when the PR is merged or closed, and it should wake up on:\\n- For comments, you should ask users how they would like to resolve them (which ones to address automatically, whether to respond / resolve, etc.), then store the decision for new future sessions. There are four different types of PR comments.\\n  - Inline review threads\\n  - Review bodies\\n  - Conversation comments\\n  - Commit comments\\n- Failing CI - most can be fixed in the code but sometimes they may be flaky. For flaky CI, just rerun them.\\n- Merge conflicts\\n- The PR becoming ready to merge — CI passes, no merge conflicts, reviews complete, no blockers, no unresolved inline threads. That wakeup is `kind: mergeable`. Tell the user they can merge now. It is not terminal; keep watching until merge or close.\\n\\nYou can find the example script bundled with this skill at watch_pr.py. It needs an authenticated `gh` CLI (`gh auth login`) and `python3`. Default poll is 30s; a lower poll rate may hit GitHub rate limits at higher concurrency. Transport errors (timeouts, resets, DNS) retry with backoff and jitter and do not print a line.\\n\\n```\\nmonitor(\\n  command='python3 ~/.grok/long-running-background-tasks/watch_pr.py \\\"https://github.com/xai-org/grok-build/pull/123\\\"',\\n  description=\\\"Watch PR 123\\\"\\n)\\n```\\n\\n### Example: training monitoring\\n\\nFor monitoring long training jobs, the terminal conditions are when the job either fails or completes. Further, many issues cannot be caught deterministically, so use a subagent to run a script for most of the high-level update, then scan the logs for errors such as faulty nodes or CUDA warnings.\\n\\nThe script below is bundled with this skill as watch_training.py. Run it with `--help` for every flag and for the run-directory and log-line layout it expects, since it parses nanoGPT stdout out of a Slurm run dir.\\n\\n```md\\nKeep an eye on the nanoGPT run nanogpt_owt_124m_r1 (slurm job 1234567) and tell me what changed since last time. Worktree ~/worktrees/nanogpt-owt-124m.\\n\\n1. python3 ~/.grok/skills/long-running-background-tasks/watch_training.py --run-name nanogpt_owt_124m_r1 --job-id 1234567 --target-val 3.00\\n\\nHow to report:\\n- Start with the job's state and if it changed, e.g. \\\"still RUNNING\\\" or \\\"PENDING -> RUNNING\\\".\\n- Copy the ISSUES line and the STATUS line from the monitor exactly as it is written, numbers and all. STATUS will include where the run is heading: how far along, iters left, the eta, and whether val loss is still coming down. We want val loss at or under 3.00.\\n- If the state didn't change, tell me that in one line and stop.\\n- If the job has finished or died, give me the state, the exit code, and the last ISSUES, and run these two for me:\\n  sacct -j 1234567 -D -X -P -o JobID,State,ExitCode,DerivedExitCode,Elapsed,NodeList,FailedNode\\n  tail -20 ~/train_logs/slurm-nanogpt_owt_124m_r1-1234567.out\\n\\nKeep <=10 lines: state, progress and eta, loss trend, then anything that smells like training going unstable (loss spiking, NaN, val loss creeping back up) or the cluster misbehaving (a drained or failing node, OOM, NCCL errors, a preemption, iters suddenly slower than usual).\\n```\\n\\nLaunch the scheduler on a 10 min interval, and spawn a monitor to be notified when the job crashes or succeeds.\\n\\n```\\nscheduler_create(\\n  interval=\\\"10m\\\",\\n  prompt: \\\"...\\\", # Copy from the prompt above.\\n)\\nmonitor(\\n  # Wakes on pending/running/finished changes after the first observation.\\n  # First poll is silent unless the job is already COMPLETED or failed —\\n  # PENDING matches *ING, so treating an empty previous state as a\\n  # transition would wake immediately on a just-submitted job.\\n  command='J=1234567; p=; while :; do s=$(sacct -nXP -j $J -o State|head -1); s=${s%% *}; s=${s:-PENDING}; if [ \\\"$s\\\" != \\\"$p\\\" ]; then case $s in COMPLETED) echo \\\"DONE: $J\\\"; exit;; PENDING|RUNNING|CONFIGURING|COMPLETING|REQUEUED|SUSPENDED|RESIZING) [ -n \\\"$p\\\" ] && echo \\\"ACTION_REQUIRED: $J $p -> $s\\\";; *) echo \\\"FAILED: $J $s\\\"; exit 1;; esac; fi; p=$s; sleep 30; done',\\n  description=\\\"Watch training run\\\"\\n)\\n```\\n\\nLaunch both, so that we know when the job completes. When the monitor reports that the job has completed, cancel both the monitor and the scheduler, then determine next steps. Then:\\n- If it succeeded, simply present the results to the user.\\n- If it failed, debug the issue thoroughly, then fix and relaunch the job with new monitors attached. Make sure to have a thorough understanding of the issue before resubmitting, since training jobs are expensive. But always relaunch jobs so you don't waste the user's time.\\n\",\"total_lines\":197}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"85b33ccf-b9e9-49ae-b037-45249cf6b0c7"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_201","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Writing the test files now. This is the critical path.\n\nDesigning a silent helper for the week test. Found a bug where step(1000) cannot break mid-step if weigh ends early, leaving remaining frames in question mode.\n\nSmall 120-frame chunks are safe because leftover idle time stays under the 10-second attract threshold. The attract test needs 600 frames, so a single step(620) call is correct since idle accumulates without resetting.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-73b3e897-21a8-403c-a429-64ff99d3c972-76","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/core/sims.js","offset":50,"limit":70}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3670,"output_tokens":616,"cache_read_input_tokens":150912,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"23b8ec47-901e-4558-84ea-ff1c73adc9bc"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-73b3e897-21a8-403c-a429-64ff99d3c972-76","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"50→  setSkill(skill) {\\n    this.skill = skill || 'idle';\\n    this.bot = new BotDriver(this.skill, this.botRand, () => this.botTarget());\\n  }\\n  ringOf(base) {\\n    const scale = (this.T.ringScale ?? 1) * (this.gentle ? 1.25 : 1) * (this.hard ? 0.85 : 1);\\n    return base * scale;\\n  }\\n  botTarget() {\\n    return { x: 0, y: 0 };\\n60→  }\\n  auto(dt) {\\n    if (this.skill === 'idle') return { ...ZERO };\\n    const u = this.bot.read(this.dot, dt);\\n    return { ...ZERO, ...u };\\n  }\\n  playFinished() {\\n    return this.playT >= (this.def.play || 30);\\n  }\\n  onStep() {}\\n70→  onPhase() {}\\n  step(dt, input) {\\n    if (this.done) return;\\n    const u = input || { ...ZERO };\\n    this.elapsed += dt;\\n    this.phaseT += dt;\\n    if (this.phase === 'play' || this.phase === 'practice') this.onStep(dt, u, this.phase === 'play');\\n    const limit = this.queue[this.qi][1];\\n    const over = this.phase === 'play' && this.playFinished();\\n    if ((limit != null && this.phaseT >= limit) || over) {\\n80→      this.qi += 1;\\n      if (this.qi >= this.queue.length) {\\n        this.finish();\\n        return;\\n      }\\n      this.phase = this.queue[this.qi][0];\\n      this.phaseT = 0;\\n      this.onPhase(this.phase);\\n    }\\n  }\\n90→  finish() {\\n    this.done = true;\\n    this.seconds = this.playT;\\n    this.scoreStars();\\n  }\\n  scoreStars() {\\n    this.stars = starsFor(this.score, this.def.thresholds, this.T.starThresholdScale ?? 1);\\n  }\\n  stepDot(dt, u, m) {\\n    const noiseMul = (this.gentle ? 0.8 : 1) * (m.noise ?? 1);\\n100→    this.dot.step(dt, u.x || 0, u.y || 0, this.T, { ...m, noise: noiseMul });\\n    if (this.god) {\\n      const r = (m.ring ?? 0.4) * 0.92;\\n      const d = Math.hypot(this.dot.x, this.dot.y);\\n      if (d > r) {\\n        const s = r / d;\\n        this.dot.x *= s;\\n        this.dot.y *= s;\\n        this.dot.vx *= 0.2;\\n        this.dot.vy *= 0.2;\\n110→      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nexport class StillSim extends Sim {\\n  _built() {\\n    this.inside = 0;\\n    this.samples = 0;\\n    this.breathSum = 0;\",\"content_concise\":\"50→  setSkill(skill) {\\n    this.skill = skill || 'idle';\\n    this.bot = new BotDriver(this.skill, this.botRand, () => this.botTarget());\\n  }\\n  ringOf(base) {\\n    const scale = (this.T.ringScale ?? 1) * (this.gentle ? 1.25 : 1) * (this.hard ? 0.85 : 1);\\n    return base * scale;\\n  }\\n  botTarget() {\\n    return { x: 0, y: 0 };\\n60→  }\\n  auto(dt) {\\n    if (this.skill === 'idle') return { ...ZERO };\\n    const u = this.bot.read(this.dot, dt);\\n    return { ...ZERO, ...u };\\n  }\\n  playFinished() {\\n    return this.playT >= (this.def.play || 30);\\n  }\\n  onStep() {}\\n70→  onPhase() {}\\n  step(dt, input) {\\n    if (this.done) return;\\n    const u = input || { ...ZERO };\\n    this.elapsed += dt;\\n    this.phaseT += dt;\\n    if (this.phase === 'play' || this.phase === 'practice') this.onStep(dt, u, this.phase === 'play');\\n    const limit = this.queue[this.qi][1];\\n    const over = this.phase === 'play' && this.playFinished();\\n    if ((limit != null && this.phaseT >= limit) || over) {\\n80→      this.qi += 1;\\n      if (this.qi >= this.queue.length) {\\n        this.finish();\\n        return;\\n      }\\n      this.phase = this.queue[this.qi][0];\\n      this.phaseT = 0;\\n      this.onPhase(this.phase);\\n    }\\n  }\\n90→  finish() {\\n    this.done = true;\\n    this.seconds = this.playT;\\n    this.scoreStars();\\n  }\\n  scoreStars() {\\n    this.stars = starsFor(this.score, this.def.thresholds, this.T.starThresholdScale ?? 1);\\n  }\\n  stepDot(dt, u, m) {\\n    const noiseMul = (this.gentle ? 0.8 : 1) * (m.noise ?? 1);\\n100→    this.dot.step(dt, u.x || 0, u.y || 0, this.T, { ...m, noise: noiseMul });\\n    if (this.god) {\\n      const r = (m.ring ?? 0.4) * 0.92;\\n      const d = Math.hypot(this.dot.x, this.dot.y);\\n      if (d > r) {\\n        const s = r / d;\\n        this.dot.x *= s;\\n        this.dot.y *= s;\\n        this.dot.vx *= 0.2;\\n        this.dot.vy *= 0.2;\\n110→      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nexport class StillSim extends Sim {\\n  _built() {\\n    this.inside = 0;\\n    this.samples = 0;\\n    this.breathSum = 0;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/core/sims.js\",\"offset\":50,\"limit\":70,\"raw_output\":\"  setSkill(skill) {\\n    this.skill = skill || 'idle';\\n    this.bot = new BotDriver(this.skill, this.botRand, () => this.botTarget());\\n  }\\n  ringOf(base) {\\n    const scale = (this.T.ringScale ?? 1) * (this.gentle ? 1.25 : 1) * (this.hard ? 0.85 : 1);\\n    return base * scale;\\n  }\\n  botTarget() {\\n    return { x: 0, y: 0 };\\n  }\\n  auto(dt) {\\n    if (this.skill === 'idle') return { ...ZERO };\\n    const u = this.bot.read(this.dot, dt);\\n    return { ...ZERO, ...u };\\n  }\\n  playFinished() {\\n    return this.playT >= (this.def.play || 30);\\n  }\\n  onStep() {}\\n  onPhase() {}\\n  step(dt, input) {\\n    if (this.done) return;\\n    const u = input || { ...ZERO };\\n    this.elapsed += dt;\\n    this.phaseT += dt;\\n    if (this.phase === 'play' || this.phase === 'practice') this.onStep(dt, u, this.phase === 'play');\\n    const limit = this.queue[this.qi][1];\\n    const over = this.phase === 'play' && this.playFinished();\\n    if ((limit != null && this.phaseT >= limit) || over) {\\n      this.qi += 1;\\n      if (this.qi >= this.queue.length) {\\n        this.finish();\\n        return;\\n      }\\n      this.phase = this.queue[this.qi][0];\\n      this.phaseT = 0;\\n      this.onPhase(this.phase);\\n    }\\n  }\\n  finish() {\\n    this.done = true;\\n    this.seconds = this.playT;\\n    this.scoreStars();\\n  }\\n  scoreStars() {\\n    this.stars = starsFor(this.score, this.def.thresholds, this.T.starThresholdScale ?? 1);\\n  }\\n  stepDot(dt, u, m) {\\n    const noiseMul = (this.gentle ? 0.8 : 1) * (m.noise ?? 1);\\n    this.dot.step(dt, u.x || 0, u.y || 0, this.T, { ...m, noise: noiseMul });\\n    if (this.god) {\\n      const r = (m.ring ?? 0.4) * 0.92;\\n      const d = Math.hypot(this.dot.x, this.dot.y);\\n      if (d > r) {\\n        const s = r / d;\\n        this.dot.x *= s;\\n        this.dot.y *= s;\\n        this.dot.vx *= 0.2;\\n        this.dot.vy *= 0.2;\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nexport class StillSim extends Sim {\\n  _built() {\\n    this.inside = 0;\\n    this.samples = 0;\\n    this.breathSum = 0;\\n\",\"total_lines\":1087}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"58168a43-ded6-4f7b-b078-5a39b9203449"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_202","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The skipIntro queue is set to play then outro 1.","signature":"eBsxC0VJ6hCCxccxMxzuaxoAu4+Dl5SiK7EiCdgsRseLL9M9xcXlGd051QRT3BgxMP5KvOB9AKCf/bqqvZzKmvvOHwVzZgEenq2NmHFFBuc+Trb2B3q1F5F2ZiPPjP0JOZcd9Ydo1Dec7ClJFEsbLTf93Al/umDWHZA3IdwXkE/q5JSS6iMKVZJ/yah/OtrOCbXcJzsJxfCJ/heyw3q9gOiaIbEfvnITpokGQR+YQ8wjs1Clrne9Sd41N/aB27betdfymPai3C3GV7qfVixggVuk"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-def6930b-f6fc-407a-8d98-e0aa640b9159-77","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/core/sims.js","offset":115,"limit":100}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1421,"output_tokens":158,"cache_read_input_tokens":154496,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"ff0c7c68-989f-4be7-8fd2-29717effd7b8"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-def6930b-f6fc-407a-8d98-e0aa640b9159-77","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"115→export class StillSim extends Sim {\\n  _built() {\\n    this.inside = 0;\\n    this.samples = 0;\\n    this.breathSum = 0;\\n120→    this.breathN = 0;\\n    this.s = 0;\\n    this.hold = this.def.hold;\\n    this.settle = 4;\\n    this.release = 2;\\n  }\\n  playFinished() {\\n    return this.playT >= this.settle + this.hold + this.release;\\n  }\\n  ring() {\\n130→    return this.ringOf(this.def.ring);\\n  }\\n  mods(scoring) {\\n    const m = { noise: 1, inst: 1, bx: 0, by: 0, ring: this.ring() };\\n    const twist = this.def.twist;\\n    const k = this.hold > 0 ? clamp(this.playT / this.hold, 0, 1) : 0;\\n    if (twist === 'bias') m.bx = (this.def.bias || 0.12) * Math.sin(0.45 * this.elapsed);\\n    if (twist === 'ynoise') m.noise = this.def.noise || 1.3;\\n    if (twist === 'ramp') m.noise = lerp(1, 1.5, clamp((this.playT - this.settle) / this.hold, 0, 1));\\n    if (twist === 'plank') {\\n140→      m.inst = 1.2;\\n      if (this.playT > this.settle + 20) m.noise = 1.35;\\n    }\\n    if (this.def.breath && scoring) {\\n      m.noise *= 1.25 - (this.T.breathBonus ?? 0.55) * this.s;\\n    }\\n    m.ring = this.ring();\\n    return m;\\n  }\\n  auto(dt) {\\n150→    const u = super.auto(dt);\\n    if (this.skill === 'idle') return u;\\n    if (this.def.breath) {\\n      const p = this.def.breath;\\n      const ph = p ? (this.playT % p) / p : 0;\\n      u.breath = ph < 0.5;\\n    }\\n    if (this.skill === 'sloppy') {\\n      u.x += 0.35 * Math.sin(this.elapsed * 1.7);\\n      u.y += 0.35 * Math.cos(this.elapsed * 1.3);\\n160→    }\\n    return u;\\n  }\\n  onStep(dt, u, scoring) {\\n    const m = this.mods(scoring);\\n    this.stepDot(dt, u, m);\\n    if (!scoring) return;\\n    this.playT += dt;\\n    const t = this.playT;\\n    const inHold = t >= this.settle && t < this.settle + this.hold;\\n170→    if (!inHold) return;\\n    this.samples += 1;\\n    if (Math.hypot(this.dot.x, this.dot.y) < m.ring) this.inside += 1;\\n    if (this.def.breath) {\\n      const p = this.def.breath;\\n      const ph = (t % p) / p;\\n      const inhale = ph < 0.5;\\n      const correct = inhale ? !!u.breath : !u.breath;\\n      this.s += ((correct ? 1 : 0) - this.s) * Math.min(1, dt / 0.12);\\n      this.breathSum += this.s;\\n180→      this.breathN += 1;\\n    }\\n  }\\n  scoreStars() {\\n    const inRing = this.samples ? this.inside / this.samples : 0;\\n    if (this.def.breath && this.breathN) {\\n      const b = this.breathSum / this.breathN;\\n      this.score = 100 * (0.8 * inRing + 0.2 * b);\\n    } else this.score = 100 * inRing;\\n    super.scoreStars();\\n190→  }\\n}\\n\\nfunction repTarget(u) {\\n  if (u < 0.4) return u / 0.4;\\n  if (u < 0.55) return 1;\\n  if (u < 0.9) return 1 - (u - 0.55) / 0.35;\\n  return 0;\\n}\\nfunction repSlope(u) {\\n200→  if (u < 0.4) return 1 / 0.4;\\n  if (u < 0.55) return 0;\\n  if (u < 0.9) return -1 / 0.35;\\n  return 0;\\n}\\n\\nexport class RepSim extends Sim {\\n  _built() {\\n    this.announced = this.def.reps;\\n    this.total = this.def.reps + 2;\\n210→    this.r = 0;\\n    this.err = 0;\\n    this.n = 0;\\n    this.rep = 0;\\n    this.gag = '';\",\"content_concise\":\"115→export class StillSim extends Sim {\\n  _built() {\\n    this.inside = 0;\\n    this.samples = 0;\\n    this.breathSum = 0;\\n120→    this.breathN = 0;\\n    this.s = 0;\\n    this.hold = this.def.hold;\\n    this.settle = 4;\\n    this.release = 2;\\n  }\\n  playFinished() {\\n    return this.playT >= this.settle + this.hold + this.release;\\n  }\\n  ring() {\\n130→    return this.ringOf(this.def.ring);\\n  }\\n  mods(scoring) {\\n    const m = { noise: 1, inst: 1, bx: 0, by: 0, ring: this.ring() };\\n    const twist = this.def.twist;\\n    const k = this.hold > 0 ? clamp(this.playT / this.hold, 0, 1) : 0;\\n    if (twist === 'bias') m.bx = (this.def.bias || 0.12) * Math.sin(0.45 * this.elapsed);\\n    if (twist === 'ynoise') m.noise = this.def.noise || 1.3;\\n    if (twist === 'ramp') m.noise = lerp(1, 1.5, clamp((this.playT - this.settle) / this.hold, 0, 1));\\n    if (twist === 'plank') {\\n140→      m.inst = 1.2;\\n      if (this.playT > this.settle + 20) m.noise = 1.35;\\n    }\\n    if (this.def.breath && scoring) {\\n      m.noise *= 1.25 - (this.T.breathBonus ?? 0.55) * this.s;\\n    }\\n    m.ring = this.ring();\\n    return m;\\n  }\\n  auto(dt) {\\n150→    const u = super.auto(dt);\\n    if (this.skill === 'idle') return u;\\n    if (this.def.breath) {\\n      const p = this.def.breath;\\n      const ph = p ? (this.playT % p) / p : 0;\\n      u.breath = ph < 0.5;\\n    }\\n    if (this.skill === 'sloppy') {\\n      u.x += 0.35 * Math.sin(this.elapsed * 1.7);\\n      u.y += 0.35 * Math.cos(this.elapsed * 1.3);\\n160→    }\\n    return u;\\n  }\\n  onStep(dt, u, scoring) {\\n    const m = this.mods(scoring);\\n    this.stepDot(dt, u, m);\\n    if (!scoring) return;\\n    this.playT += dt;\\n    const t = this.playT;\\n    const inHold = t >= this.settle && t < this.settle + this.hold;\\n170→    if (!inHold) return;\\n    this.samples += 1;\\n    if (Math.hypot(this.dot.x, this.dot.y) < m.ring) this.inside += 1;\\n    if (this.def.breath) {\\n      const p = this.def.breath;\\n      const ph = (t % p) / p;\\n      const inhale = ph < 0.5;\\n      const correct = inhale ? !!u.breath : !u.breath;\\n      this.s += ((correct ? 1 : 0) - this.s) * Math.min(1, dt / 0.12);\\n      this.breathSum += this.s;\\n180→      this.breathN += 1;\\n    }\\n  }\\n  scoreStars() {\\n    const inRing = this.samples ? this.inside / this.samples : 0;\\n    if (this.def.breath && this.breathN) {\\n      const b = this.breathSum / this.breathN;\\n      this.score = 100 * (0.8 * inRing + 0.2 * b);\\n    } else this.score = 100 * inRing;\\n    super.scoreStars();\\n190→  }\\n}\\n\\nfunction repTarget(u) {\\n  if (u < 0.4) return u / 0.4;\\n  if (u < 0.55) return 1;\\n  if (u < 0.9) return 1 - (u - 0.55) / 0.35;\\n  return 0;\\n}\\nfunction repSlope(u) {\\n200→  if (u < 0.4) return 1 / 0.4;\\n  if (u < 0.55) return 0;\\n  if (u < 0.9) return -1 / 0.35;\\n  return 0;\\n}\\n\\nexport class RepSim extends Sim {\\n  _built() {\\n    this.announced = this.def.reps;\\n    this.total = this.def.reps + 2;\\n210→    this.r = 0;\\n    this.err = 0;\\n    this.n = 0;\\n    this.rep = 0;\\n    this.gag = '';\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/core/sims.js\",\"offset\":115,\"limit\":100,\"raw_output\":\"export class StillSim extends Sim {\\n  _built() {\\n    this.inside = 0;\\n    this.samples = 0;\\n    this.breathSum = 0;\\n    this.breathN = 0;\\n    this.s = 0;\\n    this.hold = this.def.hold;\\n    this.settle = 4;\\n    this.release = 2;\\n  }\\n  playFinished() {\\n    return this.playT >= this.settle + this.hold + this.release;\\n  }\\n  ring() {\\n    return this.ringOf(this.def.ring);\\n  }\\n  mods(scoring) {\\n    const m = { noise: 1, inst: 1, bx: 0, by: 0, ring: this.ring() };\\n    const twist = this.def.twist;\\n    const k = this.hold > 0 ? clamp(this.playT / this.hold, 0, 1) : 0;\\n    if (twist === 'bias') m.bx = (this.def.bias || 0.12) * Math.sin(0.45 * this.elapsed);\\n    if (twist === 'ynoise') m.noise = this.def.noise || 1.3;\\n    if (twist === 'ramp') m.noise = lerp(1, 1.5, clamp((this.playT - this.settle) / this.hold, 0, 1));\\n    if (twist === 'plank') {\\n      m.inst = 1.2;\\n      if (this.playT > this.settle + 20) m.noise = 1.35;\\n    }\\n    if (this.def.breath && scoring) {\\n      m.noise *= 1.25 - (this.T.breathBonus ?? 0.55) * this.s;\\n    }\\n    m.ring = this.ring();\\n    return m;\\n  }\\n  auto(dt) {\\n    const u = super.auto(dt);\\n    if (this.skill === 'idle') return u;\\n    if (this.def.breath) {\\n      const p = this.def.breath;\\n      const ph = p ? (this.playT % p) / p : 0;\\n      u.breath = ph < 0.5;\\n    }\\n    if (this.skill === 'sloppy') {\\n      u.x += 0.35 * Math.sin(this.elapsed * 1.7);\\n      u.y += 0.35 * Math.cos(this.elapsed * 1.3);\\n    }\\n    return u;\\n  }\\n  onStep(dt, u, scoring) {\\n    const m = this.mods(scoring);\\n    this.stepDot(dt, u, m);\\n    if (!scoring) return;\\n    this.playT += dt;\\n    const t = this.playT;\\n    const inHold = t >= this.settle && t < this.settle + this.hold;\\n    if (!inHold) return;\\n    this.samples += 1;\\n    if (Math.hypot(this.dot.x, this.dot.y) < m.ring) this.inside += 1;\\n    if (this.def.breath) {\\n      const p = this.def.breath;\\n      const ph = (t % p) / p;\\n      const inhale = ph < 0.5;\\n      const correct = inhale ? !!u.breath : !u.breath;\\n      this.s += ((correct ? 1 : 0) - this.s) * Math.min(1, dt / 0.12);\\n      this.breathSum += this.s;\\n      this.breathN += 1;\\n    }\\n  }\\n  scoreStars() {\\n    const inRing = this.samples ? this.inside / this.samples : 0;\\n    if (this.def.breath && this.breathN) {\\n      const b = this.breathSum / this.breathN;\\n      this.score = 100 * (0.8 * inRing + 0.2 * b);\\n    } else this.score = 100 * inRing;\\n    super.scoreStars();\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nfunction repTarget(u) {\\n  if (u < 0.4) return u / 0.4;\\n  if (u < 0.55) return 1;\\n  if (u < 0.9) return 1 - (u - 0.55) / 0.35;\\n  return 0;\\n}\\nfunction repSlope(u) {\\n  if (u < 0.4) return 1 / 0.4;\\n  if (u < 0.55) return 0;\\n  if (u < 0.9) return -1 / 0.35;\\n  return 0;\\n}\\n\\nexport class RepSim extends Sim {\\n  _built() {\\n    this.announced = this.def.reps;\\n    this.total = this.def.reps + 2;\\n    this.r = 0;\\n    this.err = 0;\\n    this.n = 0;\\n    this.rep = 0;\\n    this.gag = '';\\n\",\"total_lines\":1087}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"a3f462c7-1993-4d88-a8e5-18e3440d1911"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_203","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The tree duration is 31 seconds plus an outro.\n\nPlank duration is 41 seconds. Activity caps are set to 6000 frames per activity. A safety margin of 110 minutes is added. The next step is writing the files.\n\nThe sweep will take roughly 65 seconds to 4 minutes. Medley and week activities are faster. Total node time is estimated at 2 to 4 minutes. The block_until timeout is set to 10 minutes.\n\nA bug was found in the activity timing logic. If an activity ends early, calling step() for the remaining frames would incorrectly trigger ATTRACT mode instead of keeping results mode. This would break the next activity selection.\n\nThe fix is to break step() into chunks of at most 240 frames. This prevents leftover idle time from triggering ATTRACT mode. A new `untilMode` helper will run these small chunks until the target mode is reached or the cap is hit.\n\nThe `untilMode` helper will log heartbeat messages every 1080 frames. Medley can use larger chunks because it clears idle time and is not a menu attract target. It will step in 600-frame blocks with heartbeat updates.\n\nMedley will be stepped in 240-frame chunks instead of 600. A 600-frame chunk could trigger ATTRACT mode because the podium is a MENU_IDLE target and 600 frames equals exactly 10 seconds of idle time. Week activities will continue using 180-frame chunks. Family joins are immediate, so running step(120) during medley is safe. The files are ready to be written.\n\nA source scan for Math.random will be added. The vendor/pixel-engine.sha256 hash will be trimmed and the first token used. checkModel returns {problems, warnings}. The code will assert that problems is empty. Warnings will be logged but not treated as failures.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The game shell is in place. Next I’ll add the test runner that drives it, then fix whatever that run shows."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8b193878-0650-4a4b-8aec-62af45d5e22e-78","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/tools/test.mjs","new_string":"/**\n * Drives the shipped game. Prints failures and one \"N/N passed\" line.\n * From the dev folder: node tools/test.mjs [--fast]\n */\nimport { createHash } from 'node:crypto';\nimport { execFileSync } from 'node:child_process';\nimport { appendFileSync, mkdirSync, readFileSync, readdirSync, statSync } from 'node:fs';\nimport path from 'node:path';\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\nimport {\n  Engine,\n  HERO_RIG,\n  analyzeClip,\n  checkModel,\n  compileClips,\n  parseSong,\n  validateClip,\n  validateTexture,\n} from '../pixel-engine.js';\nimport { App, freshGuest } from '../src/app.js';\nimport { CAMERA, World } from '../src/scenes/world.js';\nimport { ACTIVITIES, ACTIVITY_BY_ID } from '../src/data/activities.js';\nimport { DAYS } from '../src/data/week.js';\nimport { LINES, SAMPLES, allLineStrings, linesFor } from '../src/data/lines.js';\nimport { SONGS, songLevel } from '../src/audio/songs.js';\nimport { syllabify } from '../src/audio/voice.js';\nimport { Dot, DOT_DEFAULTS } from '../src/core/dot.js';\nimport { BotDriver } from '../src/core/drivers.js';\nimport { mulberry32 } from '../src/core/rng.js';\nimport { dripsFor, milestonesReached, starsFor } from '../src/core/score.js';\nimport { SAVE_KEY, Save } from '../src/core/save.js';\nimport { DEFAULT_TUNABLES, TUNABLE_TABS, tabKeys } from '../src/core/tunables.js';\nimport { missingGlyphs, wrapText } from '../src/ui/font.js';\nimport { MODELS } from '../src/art/models.js';\nimport { CLIPS } from '../src/art/clips.js';\nimport { clinicTile } from '../src/art/textures.js';\nimport { MEDICAL, SOURCE_INFORMATION, aboutPages, exitInterview } from '../src/data/about.js';\nimport { CREDITS_TEXT } from '../src/data/creditsText.js';\nimport { TITLE } from '../src/data/title.js';\n\nconst here = path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url));\nconst devRoot = path.resolve(here, '..');\nconst SCRATCH = '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/implementer';\nconst fast = process.argv.includes('--fast');\nmkdirSync(SCRATCH, { recursive: true });\nconst BEAT = path.join(SCRATCH, 'beat.log');\n\nconst fails = [];\nlet total = 0;\n\nfunction beat(msg) {\n  try { appendFileSync(BEAT, `${new Date().toISOString()} ${msg}\\n`); } catch { /* scratch only */ }\n}\n\nasync function test(name, fn) {\n  total += 1;\n  beat(`start ${name}`);\n  try {\n    await fn();\n    beat(`ok ${name}`);\n  } catch (err) {\n    fails.push(`${name}: ${err?.stack || err?.message || err}`);\n    beat(`FAIL ${name}: ${err?.message || err}`);\n  }\n}\n\nfunction assert(cond, msg) {\n  if (!cond) throw new Error(msg || 'assertion failed');\n}\n\nfunction tap(engine, code) {\n  engine.input.setKey(code, true);\n  engine.step(1);\n  engine.input.setKey(code, false);\n  engine.step(1);\n}\n\nfunction choose(engine, app, id) {\n  let guard = 0;\n  while (app.state().row !== id) {\n    if (guard++ > 12) throw new Error(`no row ${id} in ${app.mode}: ${app.state().rows.join(',')}`);\n    tap(engine, 'ArrowDown');\n  }\n  tap(engine, 'Enter');\n}\n\nfunction untilMode(engine, app, mode, cap, label) {\n  let n = 0;\n  while (app.mode !== mode) {\n    if (n >= cap) throw new Error(`${label || mode}: stuck in ${app.status()} after ${n} frames`);\n    const chunk = Math.min(180, cap - n);\n    engine.step(chunk);\n    n += chunk;\n    if (n % 1080 === 0) beat(`${label || mode} ${app.status()}`);\n  }\n}\n\nfunction memoryStorage() {\n  const m = new Map();\n  return {\n    getItem: (k) => (m.has(k) ? m.get(k) : null),\n    setItem: (k, v) => m.set(k, String(v)),\n    removeItem: (k) => m.delete(k),\n  };\n}\n\nasync function boot(engine, opts = {}) {\n  const app = new App({ storage: opts.storage === undefined ? null : opts.storage, noHero: true, session: opts.session || null, touchOnly: !!opts.touchOnly });\n  await engine.loadGame(new World(app));\n  engine.step(2);\n  return app;\n}\n\nfunction band(skill, seed) {\n  const dot = new Dot(mulberry32(seed));\n  const bot = new BotDriver(skill, mulberry32(seed + 99));\n  const dt = 1 / 60;\n  let inside = 0;\n  let n = 0;\n  for (let i = 0; i < 37 * 60; i++) {\n    const u = skill === 'idle' ? { x: 0, y: 0 } : bot.read(dot, dt);\n    dot.step(dt, u.x || 0, u.y || 0, DOT_DEFAULTS, {});\n    if (i >= 120) {\n      n += 1;\n      if (Math.hypot(dot.x, dot.y) < 0.3) inside += 1;\n    }\n  }\n  return inside / n;\n}\n\nfunction walk(dir, out = []) {\n  for (const name of readdirSync(dir)) {\n    if (name === 'node_modules' || name === '.build') continue;\n    const p = path.join(dir, name);\n    if (statSync(p).isDirectory()) walk(p, out);\n    else if (name.endsWith('.js')) out.push(p);\n  }\n  return out;\n}\n\nasync function main() {\n  await test('dot bands and star thresholds', async () => {\n    const idle = band('idle', 1);\n    const average = band('average', 1);\n    const good = band('good', 1);\n    const expert = band('expert', 1);\n    assert(idle < 0.2, `idle ${idle}`);\n    assert(average > 0.35 && average < 0.65, `average ${average}`);\n    assert(good > 0.8, `good ${good}`);\n    assert(expert > 0.95, `expert ${expert}`);\n    assert(starsFor(idle * 100, [45, 70, 90]) === 0, 'idle stars');\n    assert(starsFor(good * 100, [45, 70, 90]) === 3, 'good stars');\n    assert(starsFor(44, [45, 70, 90]) === 0, 'below one');\n    assert(starsFor(45, [45, 70, 90]) === 1, 'one');\n    assert(starsFor(70, [45, 70, 90]) === 2, 'two');\n    assert(starsFor(90, [45, 70, 90]) === 3, 'three');\n    assert(DOT_DEFAULTS.dotInstability === 0.6 && DOT_DEFAULTS.dotLag === 0.08, 'defaults');\n  });\n\n  await test('songs, lines, models, hash, about', async () => {\n    for (const [name, song] of Object.entries(SONGS)) {\n      parseSong(song);\n      const level = songLevel(song);\n      assert(level >= 0.03, `${name} level ${level}`);\n    }\n    assert(SONGS.step.bpm === 104, 'step bpm');\n    const hash = createHash('sha256').update(readFileSync(path.join(devRoot, 'pixel-engine.js'))).digest('hex');\n    const expected = readFileSync(path.join(devRoot, 'vendor/pixel-engine.sha256'), 'utf8').trim().split(/\\s+/)[0];\n    assert(hash === expected, `hash ${hash}`);\n    for (const model of MODELS) {\n      const report = checkModel(model);\n      assert(report.problems.length === 0, `${model.id || model.name} ${report.problems.join(';')}`);\n    }\n    const tex = validateTexture(clinicTile);\n    assert(tex.problems.length === 0, `texture ${tex.problems.join(';')}`);\n    assert(LINES.length >= 120, `lines ${LINES.length}`);\n    const banned = /\\b(Wii|Mii|Wuhu)\\b|Balance Board|Wii Fit Trainer|Fit Age/;\n    for (const text of allLineStrings()) {\n      const bad = missingGlyphs(text);\n      assert(bad.length === 0, `glyph ${bad.join('')} in ${text}`);\n      for (const piece of wrapText(text, 52)) assert(piece.length <= 52, `wrap width ${piece}`);\n      assert(wrapText(text, 52).length <= 3, `wrap lines ${text}`);\n      assert(!banned.test(text), `banned ${text}`);\n    }\n    for (const def of ACTIVITIES) {\n      for (const stars of [0, 1, 2, 3]) {\n        for (const repeat of [false, true]) {\n          const found = linesFor(def.id, stars, repeat);\n          assert(found.length >= 1, `missing ${def.id} ${stars} ${repeat}`);\n        }\n      }\n      assert(!banned.test(def.name), def.name);\n    }\n    for (const day of DAYS) assert(!banned.test(`${day.beat} ${day.concern}`), `day ${day.day}`);\n    const pages = aboutPages(CREDITS_TEXT).map((p) => `${p.title}\\n${p.lines.join('\\n')}`).join('\\n');\n    assert(pages.includes(MEDICAL), 'medical');\n    for (const key of Object.keys(SOURCE_INFORMATION)) assert(pages.includes(String(SOURCE_INFORMATION[key])), `about ${key}`);\n    assert(pages.includes('Testing Feedback') && pages.includes('Engine Feedback') && pages.includes('Prompt Feedback'), 'feedback');\n    assert(pages.includes('Kenney') && pages.includes('three.js') && pages.includes('Rapier'), 'kit');\n    const interview = exitInterview();\n    assert(interview.sourceInformation.usage === 'added on import', 'usage');\n    assert(interview.testingFeedback.length === 4, 'testing feedback');\n    assert(interview.engineFeedback.length === 6, 'engine feedback');\n    assert(interview.promptFeedback.length === 4, 'prompt feedback');\n    for (const key of ['name', 'tagline', 'description', 'type', 'genre', 'source', 'series', 'players', 'controls', 'tags']) {\n      assert(interview.aiHub[key], `aiHub ${key}`);\n    }\n    assert(interview.aiHub.name === TITLE, 'aiHub name');\n    JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(interview));\n    const hello = syllabify('hello', 'ounce');\n    const hello2 = syllabify('hello', 'ounce');\n    assert(JSON.stringify(hello.map((s) => s.vowel + s.cons)) === JSON.stringify(hello2.map((s) => s.vowel + s.cons)), 'stable word');\n    const q = syllabify('Are you happy?', 'coach');\n    const s = syllabify('Are you happy.', 'coach');\n    assert(q[q.length - 1].f0 > s[s.length - 1].f0, 'question rises');\n    const o = syllabify('Are you happy.', 'ounce');\n    const c = syllabify('Are you happy.', 'coach');\n    const mean = (list) => list.reduce((a, b) => a + b.f0, 0) / list.length;\n    assert(mean(o) > mean(c), 'ounce higher');\n    assert(syllabify('Kevin sat on me.', 'kevin').length === 0, 'kevin silent');\n    for (const file of walk(path.join(devRoot, 'src'))) {\n      const text = readFileSync(file, 'utf8');\n      if (!text.includes('Math.random')) continue;\n      assert(file.endsWith('drivers.js'), `Math.random in ${file}`);\n      assert(text.includes('rand || Math.random'), 'drivers fallback only');\n    }\n  });\n\n  await test('clips on the hero', async () => {\n    const app = new App({ storage: null, noHero: false });\n    const world = new World(app);\n    const engine = await Engine.headless(world, { camera: CAMERA });\n    try {\n      engine.step(1);\n      const model = world.heroModel;\n      assert(model, 'hero model');\n      for (const def of CLIPS) {\n        const problems = validateClip(def, HERO_RIG);\n        assert(problems.length === 0, `${def.name} validate ${problems.join(';')}`);\n        const clip = compileClips([def], HERO_RIG, model)[0];\n        const report = analyzeClip(model, HERO_RIG, def, clip);\n        assert(report.problems.length === 0, `${def.name} analyze ${report.problems.join(';')}`);\n      }\n    } finally {\n      engine.dispose();\n    }\n  });\n\n  const host = await Engine.headless(new World(new App({ storage: null, noHero: true })), { camera: CAMERA });\n  try {\n    await test('boot title and music', async () => {\n      const app = host.game ? host.game.app : null;\n      const live = app && app.mode === 'title' ? app : await boot(host);\n      host.step(2);\n      const state = live.state();\n      assert(state.title === TITLE, state.title);\n      assert(state.mode === 'title', state.mode);\n      assert(state.music === 0.1, `music ${state.music}`);\n      assert(host.audio.volume.music === 0.1, `bus ${host.audio.volume.music}`);\n      assert(state.rows.includes('start'), 'start row');\n    });\n\n    await test('every activity idle, sloppy, expert, drips, hard', async () => {\n      const storage = memoryStorage();\n      const app = await boot(host, { storage });\n      app.guest = freshGuest('Sweep');\n      const expertScore = {};\n      for (const skill of ['idle', 'expert', 'sloppy']) {\n        for (const def of ACTIVITIES) {\n          app.guest.hard = false;\n          app.setDriver(skill);\n          app.go('activity', def.id);\n          untilMode(host, app, 'results', 110 * 60, `${skill} ${def.id}`);\n          const state = app.state();\n          if (skill === 'idle') assert(state.stars === 0, `${def.id} idle ${state.stars}`);\n          if (skill === 'expert') {\n            assert(state.stars >= 2, `${def.id} expert ${state.stars} score ${state.score}`);\n            if (def.easy) assert(state.stars === 3, `${def.id} easy ${state.stars}`);\n            expertScore[def.id] = state.score;\n          }\n          if (skill === 'sloppy') assert(state.score < expertScore[def.id], `${def.id} sloppy ${state.score} vs ${expertScore[def.id]}`);\n          assert(state.lastDrips === dripsFor(state.stars, state.seconds, state.lastPrescription, app.tunables.dripRate), `${def.id} drips`);\n          choose(host, app, 'back');\n        }\n      }\n      app.guest.hard = true;\n      app.setDriver('expert');\n      for (const id of ['plank', 'tree', 'pier']) {\n        app.go('activity', id);\n        untilMode(host, app, 'results', 110 * 60, `hard ${id}`);\n        assert(app.state().stars >= 2, `hard ${id} ${app.state().stars}`);\n        choose(host, app, 'back');\n      }\n    });\n\n    await test('pause, dev sliders, dev tools', async () => {\n      const app = await boot(host);\n      app.guest = freshGuest('Dev');\n      app.setDriver('expert');\n      app.go('activity', 'tree');\n      host.step(30);\n      const t0 = app.state().playT;\n      const x0 = app.sim.dot.x;\n      tap(host, 'KeyP');\n      assert(app.mode === 'pause', app.mode);\n      assert(host.timeScale === 0, 'paused scale');\n      host.step(30);\n      assert(app.sim.playT === t0, 'playT frozen');\n      assert(app.sim.dot.x === x0, 'dot frozen');\n      tap(host, 'ArrowDown');\n      assert(app.state().row === 'restart', app.state().row);\n      choose(host, app, 'resume');\n      assert(host.timeScale === 1, 'resumed');\n      host.step(20);\n      assert(app.sim.playT > t0, 'playT moved');\n      tap(host, 'KeyP');\n      choose(host, app, 'dev');\n      assert(app.mode === 'dev' && host.timeScale === 0, 'dev frozen');\n      assert(app.sim.T === app.tunables, 'shared tunables');\n      const dirty = {};\n      for (const tab of Object.keys(TUNABLE_TABS)) {\n        while (app.state().devTab !== tab) tap(host, 'KeyE');\n        let guard = 0;\n        const want = new Set(tabKeys(tab));\n        while (want.size && guard++ < 6) {\n          for (const id of app.state().rows) {\n            if (!want.has(id)) continue;\n            while (app.state().row !== id) tap(host, 'ArrowDown');\n            const before = app.tunables[id];\n            tap(host, 'ArrowRight');\n            assert(app.tunables[id] !== before, `${id} did not move`);\n            assert(app.sim.T[id] === app.tunables[id], `${id} not shared`);\n            dirty[id] = app.tunables[id];\n            want.delete(id);\n          }\n          if (want.size) choose(host, app, 'more');\n        }\n        assert(want.size === 0, `missed ${[...want].join(',')}`);\n      }\n      while (app.state().devTab !== 'Balance') tap(host, 'KeyQ');\n      choose(host, app, 'reset-tab');\n      for (const key of tabKeys('Balance')) assert(app.tunables[key] === DEFAULT_TUNABLES[key], `reset-tab ${key}`);\n      assert(app.tunables.dripRate === dirty.dripRate, 'other tab kept');\n      choose(host, app, 'reset-all');\n      for (const key of Object.keys(DEFAULT_TUNABLES)) assert(app.tunables[key] === DEFAULT_TUNABLES[key], `reset-all ${key}`);\n      while (app.state().devTab !== 'Tools') tap(host, 'KeyE');\n      const dayBefore = app.guest.day;\n      choose(host, app, 'day');\n      assert(app.guest.day !== dayBefore, 'day tool');\n      const dripsBefore = app.guest.drips;\n      choose(host, app, 'drips');\n      assert(app.guest.drips === dripsBefore + 50, 'drips tool');\n      choose(host, app, 'unlock');\n      assert(app.guest.unlockAll === true, 'unlock');\n      choose(host, app, 'more');\n      const driverBefore = app.driver;\n      choose(host, app, 'auto');\n      assert(app.driver !== driverBefore, 'auto');\n      choose(host, app, 'god');\n      assert(app.god === true && app.sim.god === true, 'god');\n      choose(host, app, 'overlay');\n      assert(app.overlay === true, 'overlay');\n      choose(host, app, 'hud');\n      assert(app.hideHud === true, 'hud');\n      choose(host, app, 'hud');\n      choose(host, app, 'more');\n      choose(host, app, 'camera');\n      assert(app.freeCam === true, 'camera');\n      const lineBefore = app.dialogue;\n      choose(host, app, 'line');\n      assert(app.dialogue && app.dialogue !== lineBefore, 'line');\n      choose(host, app, 'sound');\n      assert(app.songPlaying || host.audio.counts, 'sound');\n      choose(host, app, 'anim');\n      assert(app.viewerClip, 'anim');\n      choose(host, app, 'export');\n      assert(typeof app.exported === 'string', 'export');\n      choose(host, app, 'wipe');\n      assert(app.guest === null, 'wipe');\n      choose(host, app, 'more');\n      choose(host, app, 'time');\n      assert([0.25, 0.5, 1, 2, 3].includes(host.timeScale), `time ${host.timeScale}`);\n      host.timeScale = 0;\n      while (app.state().devTab !== 'Tools') tap(host, 'KeyE');\n      while (!app.state().rows.includes('jump')) {\n        if (app.state().rows.includes('prev')) choose(host, app, 'prev');\n        else break;\n      }\n      choose(host, app, 'jump');\n      assert(app.mode === 'activity', `jump ${app.mode}`);\n      assert(app.activityId === ACTIVITIES[1].id, app.activityId);\n      tap(host, 'KeyP');\n      choose(host, app, 'dev');\n      while (app.state().devTab !== 'Tools') tap(host, 'KeyE');\n      choose(host, app, 'finish');\n      assert(app.mode === 'results', app.mode);\n      assert(app.state().stars === 1, `finish stars ${app.state().stars}`);\n    });\n\n    await test('attract, touch gate, session card', async () => {\n      const app = await boot(host);\n      assert(app.mode === 'title', app.mode);\n      host.step(700);\n      assert(app.mode === 'attract', `title attract ${app.mode}`);\n      const seen = new Set();\n      let guard = 0;\n      while (seen.size < 10 && guard < 12000) {\n        seen.add(app.activityId);\n        host.step(120);\n        guard += 120;\n      }\n      for (const id of ['tree', 'hoop', 'header', 'step', 'slack', 'tray', 'pier', 'jog', 'squat', 'longstand']) {\n        assert(seen.has(id), `attract missed ${id}`);\n      }\n      tap(host, 'Enter');\n      assert(app.mode === 'title', `attract exit ${app.mode}`);\n      choose(host, app, 'start');\n      choose(host, app, 'settings');\n      host.step(700);\n      assert(app.mode === 'attract', `settings attract ${app.mode}`);\n      tap(host, 'Enter');\n      app.setDriver('expert');\n      app.guest = freshGuest('Play');\n      app.go('activity', 'tree');\n      host.step(800);\n      assert(app.mode === 'activity', `play attract ${app.mode}`);\n      tap(host, 'KeyP');\n      choose(host, app, 'settings');\n      assert(app.frozen === true, 'settings from pause stays frozen');\n      host.step(700);\n      assert(app.mode === 'settings', `pause settings attracted ${app.mode}`);\n\n      const touch = await boot(host, { touchOnly: true });\n      assert(touch.state().touchMessage === 'Controller or keyboard required', touch.state().touchMessage);\n      tap(host, 'MouseLeft');\n      assert(touch.mode === 'title', `touch confirm ${touch.mode}`);\n      tap(host, 'Enter');\n      assert(touch.touchOnly === false, 'key clears the gate');\n\n      const card = await boot(host, { session: { players: [{ name: 'Ada' }] } });\n      assert(card.mode === 'card', card.mode);\n      host.step(700);\n      assert(card.mode === 'card', `session attract ${card.mode}`);\n    });\n\n    await test('family hour and medley ghost', async () => {\n      const pads = [null, null, null, null];\n      const nav = globalThis.navigator || {};\n      nav.getGamepads = () => pads;\n      globalThis.navigator = nav;\n      const app = await boot(host);\n      choose(host, app, 'start');\n      choose(host, app, 'family');\n      assert(app.mode === 'join', app.mode);\n      const claim = (index, axis) => {\n        pads[index] = {\n          connected: true,\n          axes: [axis, 0, 0, 0],\n          buttons: [{ pressed: true, value: 1 }, ...Array.from({ length: 15 }, () => ({ pressed: false, value: 0 }))],\n        };\n        host.step(1);\n      };\n      claim(0, 0.9);\n      claim(1, -0.9);\n      tap(host, 'Enter');\n      assert(app.mode === 'join', `join ate the claim ${app.mode} ${app.state().row}`);\n      const kinds = app.seats.map((s) => s && s.kind);\n      assert(kinds[0] === 'pad' && kinds[1] === 'pad' && kinds[2] === 'key', kinds.join(','));\n      choose(host, app, 'start');\n      assert(app.mode === 'medley', app.mode);\n      assert(app.lanes.length === 3, `lanes ${app.lanes.length}`);\n      host.input.setKey('ArrowRight', true);\n      host.step(120);\n      host.input.setKey('ArrowRight', false);\n      host.step(1);\n      const pos = app.lanes.map((lane) => lane.pos);\n      assert(new Set(pos.map((n) => n.toFixed(3))).size === 3, `lanes alike ${pos.join(',')}`);\n\n      app.go('medley', { bots: true, ghost: true, skills: ['expert', 'good', 'average', 'sloppy'] });\n      const ghost = app.lanes.find((lane) => lane.kind === 'ghost');\n      assert(ghost && ghost.simulated === false, 'ghost simulated');\n      ghost.ghost.push({ a: 1, x: 0.4, y: -0.2, c: 0, t: 1, s: 0 });\n      host.step(5);\n      assert(ghost.dot.t === 0, `ghost dot stepped ${ghost.dot.t}`);\n      assert(ghost.steps === 0, 'ghost steps');\n      assert(ghost.hidden === true, 'ghost hidden on other event');\n      let guard = 0;\n      while (app.mode === 'medley' && guard < 13000) {\n        host.step(180);\n        guard += 180;\n        if (guard % 1080 === 0) beat(`medley ${app.medleyT.toFixed(1)}`);\n      }\n      assert(app.mode === 'podium', app.mode);\n      for (const lane of app.lanes) {\n        if (lane.kind === 'ghost') {\n          assert(lane.dot.t === 0, 'ghost dot after medley');\n          continue;\n        }\n        for (const score of lane.scores) assert(score >= 0 && score <= 1000, `score ${score}`);\n      }\n    });\n\n    await test('hub clock progress and result', async () => {\n      const handlers = {};\n      const calls = [];\n      const hub = {\n        on(ev, fn) { (handlers[ev] ||= []).push(fn); },\n        emit(ev, arg) { (handlers[ev] || []).forEach((fn) => fn(arg)); },\n        send(data) { calls.push(['send', data]); },\n        progress(data) { calls.push(['progress', data]); },\n        result(data) { calls.push(['result', data]); },\n        time() { return this.t; },\n        t: -4000,\n      };\n      const app = await boot(host);\n      app.bindHub(hub);\n      hub.emit('start');\n      assert(app.mode === 'medley', app.mode);\n      assert(calls.some((c) => c[0] === 'progress' && c[1].score === 0), 'progress at 0');\n      assert(calls.some((c) => c[0] === 'send'), 'send at start');\n      host.step(10);\n      assert(app.medleyT === 0, `countdown moved ${app.medleyT}`);\n      hub.t = 2000;\n      host.step(5);\n      assert(Math.abs(app.medleyT - 2) < 0.05, `hub clock ${app.medleyT}`);\n      const ghost = app.lanes.find((lane) => lane.kind === 'ghost');\n      hub.emit('message', null);\n      app.ghostMessage({ a: 0, x: 0.8, y: 0.1, c: 0, t: 0, s: 0 }, 3);\n      host.step(8);\n      const shown = app.lanes.find((lane) => lane.kind === 'ghost');\n      assert(shown && shown.dot.t === 0, 'message ghost not simulated');\n      assert(shown.ghost.shown.x > 0, 'ghost lerped');\n      hub.emit('time-up');\n      hub.emit('time-up');\n      assert(calls.filter((c) => c[0] === 'result').length === 1, 'one result');\n      hub.emit('end');\n      assert(app.hubEnded === true, 'ended');\n      void ghost;\n    });\n\n    await test('saves, corrupt storage, scripted week', async () => {\n      const storage = memoryStorage();\n      let app = await boot(host, { storage });\n      app.setDriver('expert');\n      choose(host, app, 'start');\n      choose(host, app, 'week');\n      choose(host, app, 'slot0');\n      assert(app.mode === 'name', app.mode);\n      tap(host, 'Backspace');\n      tap(host, 'Backspace');\n      for (const ch of 'ada') tap(host, `Key${ch.toUpperCase()}`);\n      choose(host, app, 'done');\n      assert(app.mode === 'ferry', app.mode);\n      assert(app.guest.name === 'Guestada' || app.guest.name.length <= 8, app.guest.name);\n      choose(host, app, 'board');\n      untilMode(host, app, 'question', 1200, 'weigh1');\n      const savedName = app.guest.name;\n      const reloaded = new App({ storage, noHero: true });\n      await host.loadGame(new World(reloaded));\n      host.step(2);\n      choose(host, reloaded, 'start');\n      choose(host, reloaded, 'week');\n      choose(host, reloaded, 'slot0');\n      assert(reloaded.guest && reloaded.guest.name === savedName, 'reload name');\n      assert(reloaded.mode === 'weigh', `reload mode ${reloaded.mode}`);\n      untilMode(host, reloaded, 'question', 1200, 'reweigh');\n      choose(host, reloaded, 'a0');\n      choose(host, reloaded, 'onward');\n      app = reloaded;\n      app.setDriver('expert');\n\n      const play = async (station, id) => {\n        if (app.islandPage !== 0) choose(host, app, 'back');\n        choose(host, app, `st-${station}`);\n        choose(host, app, `act-${id}`);\n        untilMode(host, app, 'results', 110 * 60, id);\n        const state = app.state();\n        choose(host, app, 'back');\n        return state;\n      };\n      const visit = (station) => {\n        if (app.islandPage !== 0) choose(host, app, 'back');\n        choose(host, app, `st-${station}`);\n        assert(app.mode === 'station', station);\n        choose(host, app, 'back');\n      };\n      const sleep = () => {\n        if (app.islandPage === 0) choose(host, app, 'more');\n        choose(host, app, 'hammock');\n        choose(host, app, 'rest');\n        choose(host, app, 'sleep');\n      };\n      const morning = () => {\n        untilMode(host, app, 'question', 1200, `morning ${app.guest.day}`);\n        choose(host, app, 'a0');\n        assert(app.mode === 'reveal', app.mode);\n        const last = app.guest.chart[app.guest.chart.length - 1];\n        assert(last.shown === last.trueAge + 7, `shown ${last.shown} true ${last.trueAge}`);\n        choose(host, app, 'onward');\n        assert(app.mode === 'island', app.mode);\n      };\n\n      let tree = await play('pavilion', 'tree');\n      assert(tree.lastDrips === dripsFor(tree.stars, tree.seconds, tree.lastPrescription, app.tunables.dripRate), 'tree drips');\n      assert(tree.lastPrescription === false, 'pair not done yet');\n      const squat = await play('shed', 'squat');\n      assert(squat.lastPrescription === true, 'day 1 pair');\n      sleep();\n      morning();\n\n      const warrior = await play('pavilion', 'warrior');\n      assert(warrior.stars >= 2, `day 2 stars ${warrior.stars}`);\n      assert(warrior.lastPrescription === true, 'day 2 goal');\n      if (app.islandPage === 0) choose(host, app, 'more');\n      choose(host, app, 'jar');\n      choose(host, app, 'back');\n      choose(host, app, 'locker');\n      choose(host, app, 'back');\n      choose(host, app, 'hall');\n      choose(host, app, 'back');\n      sleep();\n      morning();\n\n      const heron = await play('pavilion', 'heron');\n      assert(heron.lastPrescription === true, 'day 3 fresh');\n      sleep();\n      morning();\n\n      visit('plaza');\n      visit('jog');\n      await play('pavilion', 'tree');\n      await play('shed', 'squat');\n      const hoop = await play('beach', 'hoop');\n      assert(hoop.lastPrescription === true, 'day 4 count');\n      sleep();\n      morning();\n\n      const tray = await play('lagoon', 'tray');\n      assert(tray.lastPrescription === true, `day 5 beat score ${tray.score}`);\n      sleep();\n      morning();\n\n      const third = await play('pavilion', 'tree');\n      assert(third.stars === 3, `day 6 stars ${third.stars}`);\n      assert(third.lastPrescription === true, 'day 6 goal');\n      sleep();\n      morning();\n\n      if (app.islandPage === 0) choose(host, app, 'more');\n      choose(host, app, 'longstand');\n      untilMode(host, app, 'results', 110 * 60, 'longstand');\n      const long = app.state();\n      assert(long.lastPrescription === true, 'day 7 long stand');\n      choose(host, app, 'back');\n      const before = app.guest.chart.map((p) => ({ ...p }));\n      assert(before.length >= 7, `chart ${before.length}`);\n      sleep();\n      assert(app.mode === 'confession', app.mode);\n      choose(host, app, 'onward');\n      assert(app.guest.confessed === true, 'confessed');\n      assert(app.mode === 'credits', app.mode);\n      app.guest.chart.forEach((point, i) => {\n        assert(point.trueAge === before[i].trueAge, 'true age changed');\n        assert(point.shown === before[i].shown - 7, `shown delta ${point.shown}`);\n        assert(point.shown === point.trueAge, 'shown is true after');\n      });\n      const items = milestonesReached(app.guest.drips).map((item) => item.id);\n      assert(JSON.stringify(app.guest.items) === JSON.stringify(items), 'jar items');\n      choose(host, app, 'onward');\n      assert(app.guest.day === 8 && app.guest.week === 2, `week 2 ${app.guest.day}/${app.guest.week}`);\n      assert(app.mode === 'weigh', `week 2 mode ${app.mode}`);\n\n      storage.setItem(SAVE_KEY, '{');\n      const corrupt = new Save(storage);\n      assert(corrupt.read().slots.every((slot) => slot == null), 'corrupt json');\n      storage.setItem(SAVE_KEY, JSON.stringify({ v: 99, slots: [{ name: 'nope' }] }));\n      assert(new Save(storage).read().slots[0] == null, 'bad version');\n      const throwing = {\n        getItem() { throw new Error('closed'); },\n        setItem() { throw new Error('closed'); },\n        removeItem() { throw new Error('closed'); },\n      };\n      const fallen = new Save(throwing);\n      assert(fallen.memory === true, 'memory fallback');\n      assert(fallen.write({ v: 1, slots: [null, null, null], settings: null }) === true, 'memory write');\n      const empty = new Save(null);\n      empty.write({ v: 1, slots: [freshGuest('Mem'), null, null], settings: null });\n      assert(empty.read().slots[0].name === 'Mem', 'null storage');\n    });\n\n    await test('replay fingerprint', async () => {\n      const app = await boot(host);\n      host.step(20);\n      tap(host, 'Enter');\n      host.step(15);\n      const fp = host.fingerprint();\n      const rec = host.recording();\n      assert(rec && rec.frames.length > 10, 'recording');\n      await host.replay(rec, () => host.loadGame(new World(new App({ storage: null, noHero: true }))));\n      assert(host.fingerprint() === fp, `replay ${host.fingerprint()} vs ${fp}`);\n    });\n  } finally {\n    host.dispose();\n  }\n\n  if (!fast) {\n    await test('browser, shots, and hub', async () => {\n      execFileSync(process.execPath, ['tools/build.mjs'], { cwd: devRoot, stdio: ['ignore', 'pipe', 'pipe'] });\n      const { runBrowser } = await import('./browser.mjs');\n      const problems = await runBrowser({ devRoot, scratch: SCRATCH });\n      if (problems.length) throw new Error(problems.join('\\n'));\n    });\n  }\n\n  if (fails.length) {\n    for (const fail of fails) console.log(`FAIL ${fail}`);\n    console.log(`${total - fails.length}/${total} passed`);\n    process.exitCode = 1;\n    return;\n  }\n  console.log(`${total}/${total} passed`);\n}\n\nmain().catch((err) => {\n  console.log(`FAIL runner: ${err?.stack || err}`);\n  console.log(`0/${total} passed`);\n  process.exitCode = 1;\n});\n","old_string":""}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8b193878-0650-4a4b-8aec-62af45d5e22e-79","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/tools/shot.mjs","new_string":"/** Step, capture the WebGPU frame, composite the HUD canvas, return a PNG data URL. */\nexport async function grab(page) {\n  return page.evaluate(async () => {\n    const engine = window.__PIXEL_ENGINE__;\n    const app = window.__GAME__;\n    engine.step(20);\n    let frame;\n    try {\n      frame = await engine.renderer.capture();\n    } catch (err) {\n      return { error: String(err && err.stack || err) };\n    }\n    const canvas = document.createElement('canvas');\n    canvas.width = frame.width;\n    canvas.height = frame.height;\n    const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');\n    const pixels = new Uint8ClampedArray(frame.pixels);\n    ctx.putImageData(new ImageData(pixels, frame.width, frame.height), 0, 0);\n    const huds = [...document.querySelectorAll('canvas')].filter((c) => c !== canvas && c.width > 0);\n    for (const hud of huds) {\n      try { ctx.drawImage(hud, 0, 0, frame.width, frame.height); } catch { /* a canvas may be tainted or empty */ }\n    }\n    let min = 255;\n    let max = 0;\n    const step = Math.max(1, Math.floor(pixels.length / 4 / 4000)) * 4;\n    for (let i = 0; i < pixels.length; i += step) {\n      const luma = pixels[i] * 0.3 + pixels[i + 1] * 0.59 + pixels[i + 2] * 0.11;\n      if (luma < min) min = luma;\n      if (luma > max) max = luma;\n    }\n    const state = app.state();\n    return {\n      width: frame.width,\n      height: frame.height,\n      span: max - min,\n      url: canvas.toDataURL('image/png'),\n      title: state.title,\n      mode: state.mode,\n      music: state.music,\n      row: state.row,\n      hudW: app.ctx.hud.width,\n      hudH: app.ctx.hud.height,\n    };\n  });\n}\n\nexport function writePng(file, dataUrl) {\n  const { writeFileSync } = require('node:fs');\n  writeFileSync(file, Buffer.from(String(dataUrl).split(',')[1], 'base64'));\n}\n","old_string":""}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1319,"output_tokens":11390,"cache_read_input_tokens":155904,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"a66d11a3-9b72-4331-b9cc-7bf36976415e"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-8b193878-0650-4a4b-8aec-62af45d5e22e-78","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"/**\\n * Drives the shipped game. Prints failures and one \\\"N/N passed\\\" line.\\n * From the dev folder: node tools/test.mjs [--fast]\\n */\\nimport { createHash } from 'node:crypto';\\nimport { execFileSync } from 'node:child_process';\\nimport { appendFileSync, mkdirSync, readFileSync, readdirSync, statSync } from 'node:fs';\\nimport path from 'node:path';\\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\\nimport {\\n  Engine,\\n  HERO_RIG,\\n  analyzeClip,\\n  checkModel,\\n  compileClips,\\n  parseSong,\\n  validateClip,\\n  validateTexture,\\n} from '../pixel-engine.js';\\nimport { App, freshGuest } from '../src/app.js';\\nimport { CAMERA, World } from '../src/scenes/world.js';\\nimport { ACTIVITIES, ACTIVITY_BY_ID } from '../src/data/activities.js';\\nimport { DAYS } from '../src/data/week.js';\\nimport { LINES, SAMPLES, allLineStrings, linesFor } from '../src/data/lines.js';\\nimport { SONGS, songLevel } from '../src/audio/songs.js';\\nimport { syllabify } from '../src/audio/voice.js';\\nimport { Dot, DOT_DEFAULTS } from '../src/core/dot.js';\\nimport { BotDriver } from '../src/core/drivers.js';\\nimport { mulberry32 } from '../src/core/rng.js';\\nimport { dripsFor, milestonesReached, starsFor } from '../src/core/score.js';\\nimport { SAVE_KEY, Save } from '../src/core/save.js';\\nimport { DEFAULT_TUNABLES, TUNABLE_TABS, tabKeys } from '../src/core/tunables.js';\\nimport { missingGlyphs, wrapText } from '../src/ui/font.js';\\nimport { MODELS } from '../src/art/models.js';\\nimport { CLIPS } from '../src/art/clips.js';\\nimport { clinicTile } from '../src/art/textures.js';\\nimport { MEDICAL, SOURCE_INFORMATION, aboutPages, exitInterview } from '../src/data/about.js';\\nimport { CREDITS_TEXT } from '../src/data/creditsText.js';\\nimport { TITLE } from '../src/data/title.js';\\n\\nconst here = path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url));\\nconst devRoot = path.resolve(here, '..');\\nconst SCRATCH = '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/implementer';\\nconst fast = process.argv.includes('--fast');\\nmkdirSync(SCRATCH, { recursive: true });\\nconst BEAT = path.join(SCRATCH, 'beat.log');\\n\\nconst fails = [];\\nlet total = 0;\\n\\nfunction beat(msg) {\\n  try { appendFileSync(BEAT, `${new Date().toISOString()} ${msg}\\\\n`); } catch { /* scratch only */ }\\n}\\n\\nasync function test(name, fn) {\\n  total += 1;\\n  beat(`start ${name}`);\\n  try {\\n    await fn();\\n    beat(`ok ${name}`);\\n  } catch (err) {\\n    fails.push(`${name}: ${err?.stack || err?.message || err}`);\\n    beat(`FAIL ${name}: ${err?.message || err}`);\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nfunction assert(cond, msg) {\\n  if (!cond) throw new Error(msg || 'assertion failed');\\n}\\n\\nfunction tap(engine, code) {\\n  engine.input.setKey(code, true);\\n  engine.step(1);\\n  engine.input.setKey(code, false);\\n  engine.step(1);\\n}\\n\\nfunction choose(engine, app, id) {\\n  let guard = 0;\\n  while (app.state().row !== id) {\\n    if (guard++ > 12) throw new Error(`no row ${id} in ${app.mode}: ${app.state().rows.join(',')}`);\\n    tap(engine, 'ArrowDown');\\n  }\\n  tap(engine, 'Enter');\\n}\\n\\nfunction untilMode(engine, app, mode, cap, label) {\\n  let n = 0;\\n  while (app.mode !== mode) {\\n    if (n >= cap) throw new Error(`${label || mode}: stuck in ${app.status()} after ${n} frames`);\\n    const chunk = Math.min(180, cap - n);\\n    engine.step(chunk);\\n    n += chunk;\\n    if (n % 1080 === 0) beat(`${label || mode} ${app.status()}`);\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nfunction memoryStorage() {\\n  const m = new Map();\\n  return {\\n    getItem: (k) => (m.has(k) ? m.get(k) : null),\\n    setItem: (k, v) => m.set(k, String(v)),\\n    removeItem: (k) => m.delete(k),\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nasync function boot(engine, opts = {}) {\\n  const app = new App({ storage: opts.storage === undefined ? null : opts.storage, noHero: true, session: opts.session || null, touchOnly: !!opts.touchOnly });\\n  await engine.loadGame(new World(app));\\n  engine.step(2);\\n  return app;\\n}\\n\\nfunction band(skill, seed) {\\n  const dot = new Dot(mulberry32(seed));\\n  const bot = new BotDriver(skill, mulberry32(seed + 99));\\n  const dt = 1 / 60;\\n  let inside = 0;\\n  let n = 0;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 37 * 60; i++) {\\n    const u = skill === 'idle' ? { x: 0, y: 0 } : bot.read(dot, dt);\\n    dot.step(dt, u.x || 0, u.y || 0, DOT_DEFAULTS, {});\\n    if (i >= 120) {\\n      n += 1;\\n      if (Math.hypot(dot.x, dot.y) < 0.3) inside += 1;\\n    }\\n  }\\n  return inside / n;\\n}\\n\\nfunction walk(dir, out = []) {\\n  for (const name of readdirSync(dir)) {\\n    if (name === 'node_modules' || name === '.build') continue;\\n    const p = path.join(dir, name);\\n    if (statSync(p).isDirectory()) walk(p, out);\\n    else if (name.endsWith('.js')) out.push(p);\\n  }\\n  return out;\\n}\\n\\nasync function main() {\\n  await test('dot bands and star thresholds', async () => {\\n    const idle = band('idle', 1);\\n    const average = band('average', 1);\\n    const good = band('good', 1);\\n    const expert = band('expert', 1);\\n    assert(idle < 0.2, `idle ${idle}`);\\n    assert(average > 0.35 && average < 0.65, `average ${average}`);\\n    assert(good > 0.8, `good ${good}`);\\n    assert(expert > 0.95, `expert ${expert}`);\\n    assert(starsFor(idle * 100, [45, 70, 90]) === 0, 'idle stars');\\n    assert(starsFor(good * 100, [45, 70, 90]) === 3, 'good stars');\\n    assert(starsFor(44, [45, 70, 90]) === 0, 'below one');\\n    assert(starsFor(45, [45, 70, 90]) === 1, 'one');\\n    assert(starsFor(70, [45, 70, 90]) === 2, 'two');\\n    assert(starsFor(90, [45, 70, 90]) === 3, 'three');\\n    assert(DOT_DEFAULTS.dotInstability === 0.6 && DOT_DEFAULTS.dotLag === 0.08, 'defaults');\\n  });\\n\\n  await test('songs, lines, models, hash, about', async () => {\\n    for (const [name, song] of Object.entries(SONGS)) {\\n      parseSong(song);\\n      const level = songLevel(song);\\n      assert(level >= 0.03, `${name} level ${level}`);\\n    }\\n    assert(SONGS.step.bpm === 104, 'step bpm');\\n    const hash = createHash('sha256').update(readFileSync(path.join(devRoot, 'pixel-engine.js'))).digest('hex');\\n    const expected = readFileSync(path.join(devRoot, 'vendor/pixel-engine.sha256'), 'utf8').trim().split(/\\\\s+/)[0];\\n    assert(hash === expected, `hash ${hash}`);\\n    for (const model of MODELS) {\\n      const report = checkModel(model);\\n      assert(report.problems.length === 0, `${model.id || model.name} ${report.problems.join(';')}`);\\n    }\\n    const tex = validateTexture(clinicTile);\\n    assert(tex.problems.length === 0, `texture ${tex.problems.join(';')}`);\\n    assert(LINES.length >= 120, `lines ${LINES.length}`);\\n    const banned = /\\\\b(Wii|Mii|Wuhu)\\\\b|Balance Board|Wii Fit Trainer|Fit Age/;\\n    for (const text of allLineStrings()) {\\n      const bad = missingGlyphs(text);\\n      assert(bad.length === 0, `glyph ${bad.join('')} in ${text}`);\\n      for (const piece of wrapText(text, 52)) assert(piece.length <= 52, `wrap width ${piece}`);\\n      assert(wrapText(text, 52).length <= 3, `wrap lines ${text}`);\\n      assert(!banned.test(text), `banned ${text}`);\\n    }\\n    for (const def of ACTIVITIES) {\\n      for (const stars of [0, 1, 2, 3]) {\\n        for (const repeat of [false, true]) {\\n          const found = linesFor(def.id, stars, repeat);\\n          assert(found.length >= 1, `missing ${def.id} ${stars} ${repeat}`);\\n        }\\n      }\\n      assert(!banned.test(def.name), def.name);\\n    }\\n    for (const day of DAYS) assert(!banned.test(`${day.beat} ${day.concern}`), `day ${day.day}`);\\n    const pages = aboutPages(CREDITS_TEXT).map((p) => `${p.title}\\\\n${p.lines.join('\\\\n')}`).join('\\\\n');\\n    assert(pages.includes(MEDICAL), 'medical');\\n    for (const key of Object.keys(SOURCE_INFORMATION)) assert(pages.includes(String(SOURCE_INFORMATION[key])), `about ${key}`);\\n    assert(pages.includes('Testing Feedback') && pages.includes('Engine Feedback') && pages.includes('Prompt Feedback'), 'feedback');\\n    assert(pages.includes('Kenney') && pages.includes('three.js') && pages.includes('Rapier'), 'kit');\\n    const interview = exitInterview();\\n    assert(interview.sourceInformation.usage === 'added on import', 'usage');\\n    assert(interview.testingFeedback.length === 4, 'testing feedback');\\n    assert(interview.engineFeedback.length === 6, 'engine feedback');\\n    assert(interview.promptFeedback.length === 4, 'prompt feedback');\\n    for (const key of ['name', 'tagline', 'description', 'type', 'genre', 'source', 'series', 'players', 'controls', 'tags']) {\\n      assert(interview.aiHub[key], `aiHub ${key}`);\\n    }\\n    assert(interview.aiHub.name === TITLE, 'aiHub name');\\n    JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(interview));\\n    const hello = syllabify('hello', 'ounce');\\n    const hello2 = syllabify('hello', 'ounce');\\n    assert(JSON.stringify(hello.map((s) => s.vowel + s.cons)) === JSON.stringify(hello2.map((s) => s.vowel + s.cons)), 'stable word');\\n    const q = syllabify('Are you happy?', 'coach');\\n    const s = syllabify('Are you happy.', 'coach');\\n    assert(q[q.length - 1].f0 > s[s.length - 1].f0, 'question rises');\\n    const o = syllabify('Are you happy.', 'ounce');\\n    const c = syllabify('Are you happy.', 'coach');\\n    const mean = (list) => list.reduce((a, b) => a + b.f0, 0) / list.length;\\n    assert(mean(o) > mean(c), 'ounce higher');\\n    assert(syllabify('Kevin sat on me.', 'kevin').length === 0, 'kevin silent');\\n    for (const file of walk(path.join(devRoot, 'src'))) {\\n      const text = readFileSync(file, 'utf8');\\n      if (!text.includes('Math.random')) continue;\\n      assert(file.endsWith('drivers.js'), `Math.random in ${file}`);\\n      assert(text.includes('rand || Math.random'), 'drivers fallback only');\\n    }\\n  });\\n\\n  await test('clips on the hero', async () => {\\n    const app = new App({ storage: null, noHero: false });\\n    const world = new World(app);\\n    const engine = await Engine.headless(world, { camera: CAMERA });\\n    try {\\n      engine.step(1);\\n      const model = world.heroModel;\\n      assert(model, 'hero model');\\n      for (const def of CLIPS) {\\n        const problems = validateClip(def, HERO_RIG);\\n        assert(problems.length === 0, `${def.name} validate ${problems.join(';')}`);\\n        const clip = compileClips([def], HERO_RIG, model)[0];\\n        const report = analyzeClip(model, HERO_RIG, def, clip);\\n        assert(report.problems.length === 0, `${def.name} analyze ${report.problems.join(';')}`);\\n      }\\n    } finally {\\n      engine.dispose();\\n    }\\n  });\\n\\n  const host = await Engine.headless(new World(new App({ storage: null, noHero: true })), { camera: CAMERA });\\n  try {\\n    await test('boot title and music', async () => {\\n      const app = host.game ? host.game.app : null;\\n      const live = app && app.mode === 'title' ? app : await boot(host);\\n      host.step(2);\\n      const state = live.state();\\n      assert(state.title === TITLE, state.title);\\n      assert(state.mode === 'title', state.mode);\\n      assert(state.music === 0.1, `music ${state.music}`);\\n      assert(host.audio.volume.music === 0.1, `bus ${host.audio.volume.music}`);\\n      assert(state.rows.includes('start'), 'start row');\\n    });\\n\\n    await test('every activity idle, sloppy, expert, drips, hard', async () => {\\n      const storage = memoryStorage();\\n      const app = await boot(host, { storage });\\n      app.guest = freshGuest('Sweep');\\n      const expertScore = {};\\n      for (const skill of ['idle', 'expert', 'sloppy']) {\\n        for (const def of ACTIVITIES) {\\n          app.guest.hard = false;\\n          app.setDriver(skill);\\n          app.go('activity', def.id);\\n          untilMode(host, app, 'results', 110 * 60, `${skill} ${def.id}`);\\n          const state = app.state();\\n          if (skill === 'idle') assert(state.stars === 0, `${def.id} idle ${state.stars}`);\\n          if (skill === 'expert') {\\n            assert(state.stars >= 2, `${def.id} expert ${state.stars} score ${state.score}`);\\n            if (def.easy) assert(state.stars === 3, `${def.id} easy ${state.stars}`);\\n            expertScore[def.id] = state.score;\\n          }\\n          if (skill === 'sloppy') assert(state.score < expertScore[def.id], `${def.id} sloppy ${state.score} vs ${expertScore[def.id]}`);\\n          assert(state.lastDrips === dripsFor(state.stars, state.seconds, state.lastPrescription, app.tunables.dripRate), `${def.id} drips`);\\n          choose(host, app, 'back');\\n        }\\n      }\\n      app.guest.hard = true;\\n      app.setDriver('expert');\\n      for (const id of ['plank', 'tree', 'pier']) {\\n        app.go('activity', id);\\n        untilMode(host, app, 'results', 110 * 60, `hard ${id}`);\\n        assert(app.state().stars >= 2, `hard ${id} ${app.state().stars}`);\\n        choose(host, app, 'back');\\n      }\\n    });\\n\\n    await test('pause, dev sliders, dev tools', async () => {\\n      const app = await boot(host);\\n      app.guest = freshGuest('Dev');\\n      app.setDriver('expert');\\n      app.go('activity', 'tree');\\n      host.step(30);\\n      const t0 = app.state().playT;\\n      const x0 = app.sim.dot.x;\\n      tap(host, 'KeyP');\\n      assert(app.mode === 'pause', app.mode);\\n      assert(host.timeScale === 0, 'paused scale');\\n      host.step(30);\\n      assert(app.sim.playT === t0, 'playT frozen');\\n      assert(app.sim.dot.x === x0, 'dot frozen');\\n      tap(host, 'ArrowDown');\\n      assert(app.state().row === 'restart', app.state().row);\\n      choose(host, app, 'resume');\\n      assert(host.timeScale === 1, 'resumed');\\n      host.step(20);\\n      assert(app.sim.playT > t0, 'playT moved');\\n      tap(host, 'KeyP');\\n      choose(host, app, 'dev');\\n      assert(app.mode === 'dev' && host.timeScale === 0, 'dev frozen');\\n      assert(app.sim.T === app.tunables, 'shared tunables');\\n      const dirty = {};\\n      for (const tab of Object.keys(TUNABLE_TABS)) {\\n        while (app.state().devTab !== tab) tap(host, 'KeyE');\\n        let guard = 0;\\n        const want = new Set(tabKeys(tab));\\n        while (want.size && guard++ < 6) {\\n          for (const id of app.state().rows) {\\n            if (!want.has(id)) continue;\\n            while (app.state().row !== id) tap(host, 'ArrowDown');\\n            const before = app.tunables[id];\\n            tap(host, 'ArrowRight');\\n            assert(app.tunables[id] !== before, `${id} did not move`);\\n            assert(app.sim.T[id] === app.tunables[id], `${id} not shared`);\\n            dirty[id] = app.tunables[id];\\n            want.delete(id);\\n          }\\n          if (want.size) choose(host, app, 'more');\\n        }\\n        assert(want.size === 0, `missed ${[...want].join(',')}`);\\n      }\\n      while (app.state().devTab !== 'Balance') tap(host, 'KeyQ');\\n      choose(host, app, 'reset-tab');\\n      for (const key of tabKeys('Balance')) assert(app.tunables[key] === DEFAULT_TUNABLES[key], `reset-tab ${key}`);\\n      assert(app.tunables.dripRate === dirty.dripRate, 'other tab kept');\\n      choose(host, app, 'reset-all');\\n      for (const key of Object.keys(DEFAULT_TUNABLES)) assert(app.tunables[key] === DEFAULT_TUNABLES[key], `reset-all ${key}`);\\n      while (app.state().devTab !== 'Tools') tap(host, 'KeyE');\\n      const dayBefore = app.guest.day;\\n      choose(host, app, 'day');\\n      assert(app.guest.day !== dayBefore, 'day tool');\\n      const dripsBefore = app.guest.drips;\\n      choose(host, app, 'drips');\\n      assert(app.guest.drips === dripsBefore + 50, 'drips tool');\\n      choose(host, app, 'unlock');\\n      assert(app.guest.unlockAll === true, 'unlock');\\n      choose(host, app, 'more');\\n      const driverBefore = app.driver;\\n      choose(host, app, 'auto');\\n      assert(app.driver !== driverBefore, 'auto');\\n      choose(host, app, 'god');\\n      assert(app.god === true && app.sim.god === true, 'god');\\n      choose(host, app, 'overlay');\\n      assert(app.overlay === true, 'overlay');\\n      choose(host, app, 'hud');\\n      assert(app.hideHud === true, 'hud');\\n      choose(host, app, 'hud');\\n      choose(host, app, 'more');\\n      choose(host, app, 'camera');\\n      assert(app.freeCam === true, 'camera');\\n      const lineBefore = app.dialogue;\\n      choose(host, app, 'line');\\n      assert(app.dialogue && app.dialogue !== lineBefore, 'line');\\n      choose(host, app, 'sound');\\n      assert(app.songPlaying || host.audio.counts, 'sound');\\n      choose(host, app, 'anim');\\n      assert(app.viewerClip, 'anim');\\n      choose(host, app, 'export');\\n      assert(typeof app.exported === 'string', 'export');\\n      choose(host, app, 'wipe');\\n      assert(app.guest === null, 'wipe');\\n      choose(host, app, 'more');\\n      choose(host, app, 'time');\\n      assert([0.25, 0.5, 1, 2, 3].includes(host.timeScale), `time ${host.timeScale}`);\\n      host.timeScale = 0;\\n      while (app.state().devTab !== 'Tools') tap(host, 'KeyE');\\n      while (!app.state().rows.includes('jump')) {\\n        if (app.state().rows.includes('prev')) choose(host, app, 'prev');\\n        else break;\\n      }\\n      choose(host, app, 'jump');\\n      assert(app.mode === 'activity', `jump ${app.mode}`);\\n      assert(app.activityId === ACTIVITIES[1].id, app.activityId);\\n      tap(host, 'KeyP');\\n      choose(host, app, 'dev');\\n      while (app.state().devTab !== 'Tools') tap(host, 'KeyE');\\n      choose(host, app, 'finish');\\n      assert(app.mode === 'results', app.mode);\\n      assert(app.state().stars === 1, `finish stars ${app.state().stars}`);\\n    });\\n\\n    await test('attract, touch gate, session card', async () => {\\n      const app = await boot(host);\\n      assert(app.mode === 'title', app.mode);\\n      host.step(700);\\n      assert(app.mode === 'attract', `title attract ${app.mode}`);\\n      const seen = new Set();\\n      let guard = 0;\\n      while (seen.size < 10 && guard < 12000) {\\n        seen.add(app.activityId);\\n        host.step(120);\\n        guard += 120;\\n      }\\n      for (const id of ['tree', 'hoop', 'header', 'step', 'slack', 'tray', 'pier', 'jog', 'squat', 'longstand']) {\\n        assert(seen.has(id), `attract missed ${id}`);\\n      }\\n      tap(host, 'Enter');\\n      assert(app.mode === 'title', `attract exit ${app.mode}`);\\n      choose(host, app, 'start');\\n      choose(host, app, 'settings');\\n      host.step(700);\\n      assert(app.mode === 'attract', `settings attract ${app.mode}`);\\n      tap(host, 'Enter');\\n      app.setDriver('expert');\\n      app.guest = freshGuest('Play');\\n      app.go('activity', 'tree');\\n      host.step(800);\\n      assert(app.mode === 'activity', `play attract ${app.mode}`);\\n      tap(host, 'KeyP');\\n      choose(host, app, 'settings');\\n      assert(app.frozen === true, 'settings from pause stays frozen');\\n      host.step(700);\\n      assert(app.mode === 'settings', `pause settings attracted ${app.mode}`);\\n\\n      const touch = await boot(host, { touchOnly: true });\\n      assert(touch.state().touchMessage === 'Controller or keyboard required', touch.state().touchMessage);\\n      tap(host, 'MouseLeft');\\n      assert(touch.mode === 'title', `touch confirm ${touch.mode}`);\\n      tap(host, 'Enter');\\n      assert(touch.touchOnly === false, 'key clears the gate');\\n\\n      const card = await boot(host, { session: { players: [{ name: 'Ada' }] } });\\n      assert(card.mode === 'card', card.mode);\\n      host.step(700);\\n      assert(card.mode === 'card', `session attract ${card.mode}`);\\n    });\\n\\n    await test('family hour and medley ghost', async () => {\\n      const pads = [null, null, null, null];\\n      const nav = globalThis.navigator || {};\\n      nav.getGamepads = () => pads;\\n      globalThis.navigator = nav;\\n      const app = await boot(host);\\n      choose(host, app, 'start');\\n      choose(host, app, 'family');\\n      assert(app.mode === 'join', app.mode);\\n      const claim = (index, axis) => {\\n        pads[index] = {\\n          connected: true,\\n          axes: [axis, 0, 0, 0],\\n          buttons: [{ pressed: true, value: 1 }, ...Array.from({ length: 15 }, () => ({ pressed: false, value: 0 }))],\\n        };\\n        host.step(1);\\n      };\\n      claim(0, 0.9);\\n      claim(1, -0.9);\\n      tap(host, 'Enter');\\n      assert(app.mode === 'join', `join ate the claim ${app.mode} ${app.state().row}`);\\n      const kinds = app.seats.map((s) => s && s.kind);\\n      assert(kinds[0] === 'pad' && kinds[1] === 'pad' && kinds[2] === 'key', kinds.join(','));\\n      choose(host, app, 'start');\\n      assert(app.mode === 'medley', app.mode);\\n      assert(app.lanes.length === 3, `lanes ${app.lanes.length}`);\\n      host.input.setKey('ArrowRight', true);\\n      host.step(120);\\n      host.input.setKey('ArrowRight', false);\\n      host.step(1);\\n      const pos = app.lanes.map((lane) => lane.pos);\\n      assert(new Set(pos.map((n) => n.toFixed(3))).size === 3, `lanes alike ${pos.join(',')}`);\\n\\n      app.go('medley', { bots: true, ghost: true, skills: ['expert', 'good', 'average', 'sloppy'] });\\n      const ghost = app.lanes.find((lane) => lane.kind === 'ghost');\\n      assert(ghost && ghost.simulated === false, 'ghost simulated');\\n      ghost.ghost.push({ a: 1, x: 0.4, y: -0.2, c: 0, t: 1, s: 0 });\\n      host.step(5);\\n      assert(ghost.dot.t === 0, `ghost dot stepped ${ghost.dot.t}`);\\n      assert(ghost.steps === 0, 'ghost steps');\\n      assert(ghost.hidden === true, 'ghost hidden on other event');\\n      let guard = 0;\\n      while (app.mode === 'medley' && guard < 13000) {\\n        host.step(180);\\n        guard += 180;\\n        if (guard % 1080 === 0) beat(`medley ${app.medleyT.toFixed(1)}`);\\n      }\\n      assert(app.mode === 'podium', app.mode);\\n      for (const lane of app.lanes) {\\n        if (lane.kind === 'ghost') {\\n          assert(lane.dot.t === 0, 'ghost dot after medley');\\n          continue;\\n        }\\n        for (const score of lane.scores) assert(score >= 0 && score <= 1000, `score ${score}`);\\n      }\\n    });\\n\\n    await test('hub clock progress and result', async () => {\\n      const handlers = {};\\n      const calls = [];\\n      const hub = {\\n        on(ev, fn) { (handlers[ev] ||= []).push(fn); },\\n        emit(ev, arg) { (handlers[ev] || []).forEach((fn) => fn(arg)); },\\n        send(data) { calls.push(['send', data]); },\\n        progress(data) { calls.push(['progress', data]); },\\n        result(data) { calls.push(['result', data]); },\\n        time() { return this.t; },\\n        t: -4000,\\n      };\\n      const app = await boot(host);\\n      app.bindHub(hub);\\n      hub.emit('start');\\n      assert(app.mode === 'medley', app.mode);\\n      assert(calls.some((c) => c[0] === 'progress' && c[1].score === 0), 'progress at 0');\\n      assert(calls.some((c) => c[0] === 'send'), 'send at start');\\n      host.step(10);\\n      assert(app.medleyT === 0, `countdown moved ${app.medleyT}`);\\n      hub.t = 2000;\\n      host.step(5);\\n      assert(Math.abs(app.medleyT - 2) < 0.05, `hub clock ${app.medleyT}`);\\n      const ghost = app.lanes.find((lane) => lane.kind === 'ghost');\\n      hub.emit('message', null);\\n      app.ghostMessage({ a: 0, x: 0.8, y: 0.1, c: 0, t: 0, s: 0 }, 3);\\n      host.step(8);\\n      const shown = app.lanes.find((lane) => lane.kind === 'ghost');\\n      assert(shown && shown.dot.t === 0, 'message ghost not simulated');\\n      assert(shown.ghost.shown.x > 0, 'ghost lerped');\\n      hub.emit('time-up');\\n      hub.emit('time-up');\\n      assert(calls.filter((c) => c[0] === 'result').length === 1, 'one result');\\n      hub.emit('end');\\n      assert(app.hubEnded === true, 'ended');\\n      void ghost;\\n    });\\n\\n    await test('saves, corrupt storage, scripted week', async () => {\\n      const storage = memoryStorage();\\n      let app = await boot(host, { storage });\\n      app.setDriver('expert');\\n      choose(host, app, 'start');\\n      choose(host, app, 'week');\\n      choose(host, app, 'slot0');\\n      assert(app.mode === 'name', app.mode);\\n      tap(host, 'Backspace');\\n      tap(host, 'Backspace');\\n      for (const ch of 'ada') tap(host, `Key${ch.toUpperCase()}`);\\n      choose(host, app, 'done');\\n      assert(app.mode === 'ferry', app.mode);\\n      assert(app.guest.name === 'Guestada' || app.guest.name.length <= 8, app.guest.name);\\n      choose(host, app, 'board');\\n      untilMode(host, app, 'question', 1200, 'weigh1');\\n      const savedName = app.guest.name;\\n      const reloaded = new App({ storage, noHero: true });\\n      await host.loadGame(new World(reloaded));\\n      host.step(2);\\n      choose(host, reloaded, 'start');\\n      choose(host, reloaded, 'week');\\n      choose(host, reloaded, 'slot0');\\n      assert(reloaded.guest && reloaded.guest.name === savedName, 'reload name');\\n      assert(reloaded.mode === 'weigh', `reload mode ${reloaded.mode}`);\\n      untilMode(host, reloaded, 'question', 1200, 'reweigh');\\n      choose(host, reloaded, 'a0');\\n      choose(host, reloaded, 'onward');\\n      app = reloaded;\\n      app.setDriver('expert');\\n\\n      const play = async (station, id) => {\\n        if (app.islandPage !== 0) choose(host, app, 'back');\\n        choose(host, app, `st-${station}`);\\n        choose(host, app, `act-${id}`);\\n        untilMode(host, app, 'results', 110 * 60, id);\\n        const state = app.state();\\n        choose(host, app, 'back');\\n        return state;\\n      };\\n      const visit = (station) => {\\n        if (app.islandPage !== 0) choose(host, app, 'back');\\n        choose(host, app, `st-${station}`);\\n        assert(app.mode === 'station', station);\\n        choose(host, app, 'back');\\n      };\\n      const sleep = () => {\\n        if (app.islandPage === 0) choose(host, app, 'more');\\n        choose(host, app, 'hammock');\\n        choose(host, app, 'rest');\\n        choose(host, app, 'sleep');\\n      };\\n      const morning = () => {\\n        untilMode(host, app, 'question', 1200, `morning ${app.guest.day}`);\\n        choose(host, app, 'a0');\\n        assert(app.mode === 'reveal', app.mode);\\n        const last = app.guest.chart[app.guest.chart.length - 1];\\n        assert(last.shown === last.trueAge + 7, `shown ${last.shown} true ${last.trueAge}`);\\n        choose(host, app, 'onward');\\n        assert(app.mode === 'island', app.mode);\\n      };\\n\\n      let tree = await play('pavilion', 'tree');\\n      assert(tree.lastDrips === dripsFor(tree.stars, tree.seconds, tree.lastPrescription, app.tunables.dripRate), 'tree drips');\\n      assert(tree.lastPrescription === false, 'pair not done yet');\\n      const squat = await play('shed', 'squat');\\n      assert(squat.lastPrescription === true, 'day 1 pair');\\n      sleep();\\n      morning();\\n\\n      const warrior = await play('pavilion', 'warrior');\\n      assert(warrior.stars >= 2, `day 2 stars ${warrior.stars}`);\\n      assert(warrior.lastPrescription === true, 'day 2 goal');\\n      if (app.islandPage === 0) choose(host, app, 'more');\\n      choose(host, app, 'jar');\\n      choose(host, app, 'back');\\n      choose(host, app, 'locker');\\n      choose(host, app, 'back');\\n      choose(host, app, 'hall');\\n      choose(host, app, 'back');\\n      sleep();\\n      morning();\\n\\n      const heron = await play('pavilion', 'heron');\\n      assert(heron.lastPrescription === true, 'day 3 fresh');\\n      sleep();\\n      morning();\\n\\n      visit('plaza');\\n      visit('jog');\\n      await play('pavilion', 'tree');\\n      await play('shed', 'squat');\\n      const hoop = await play('beach', 'hoop');\\n      assert(hoop.lastPrescription === true, 'day 4 count');\\n      sleep();\\n      morning();\\n\\n      const tray = await play('lagoon', 'tray');\\n      assert(tray.lastPrescription === true, `day 5 beat score ${tray.score}`);\\n      sleep();\\n      morning();\\n\\n      const third = await play('pavilion', 'tree');\\n      assert(third.stars === 3, `day 6 stars ${third.stars}`);\\n      assert(third.lastPrescription === true, 'day 6 goal');\\n      sleep();\\n      morning();\\n\\n      if (app.islandPage === 0) choose(host, app, 'more');\\n      choose(host, app, 'longstand');\\n      untilMode(host, app, 'results', 110 * 60, 'longstand');\\n      const long = app.state();\\n      assert(long.lastPrescription === true, 'day 7 long stand');\\n      choose(host, app, 'back');\\n      const before = app.guest.chart.map((p) => ({ ...p }));\\n      assert(before.length >= 7, `chart ${before.length}`);\\n      sleep();\\n      assert(app.mode === 'confession', app.mode);\\n      choose(host, app, 'onward');\\n      assert(app.guest.confessed === true, 'confessed');\\n      assert(app.mode === 'credits', app.mode);\\n      app.guest.chart.forEach((point, i) => {\\n        assert(point.trueAge === before[i].trueAge, 'true age changed');\\n        assert(point.shown === before[i].shown - 7, `shown delta ${point.shown}`);\\n        assert(point.shown === point.trueAge, 'shown is true after');\\n      });\\n      const items = milestonesReached(app.guest.drips).map((item) => item.id);\\n      assert(JSON.stringify(app.guest.items) === JSON.stringify(items), 'jar items');\\n      choose(host, app, 'onward');\\n      assert(app.guest.day === 8 && app.guest.week === 2, `week 2 ${app.guest.day}/${app.guest.week}`);\\n      assert(app.mode === 'weigh', `week 2 mode ${app.mode}`);\\n\\n      storage.setItem(SAVE_KEY, '{');\\n      const corrupt = new Save(storage);\\n      assert(corrupt.read().slots.every((slot) => slot == null), 'corrupt json');\\n      storage.setItem(SAVE_KEY, JSON.stringify({ v: 99, slots: [{ name: 'nope' }] }));\\n      assert(new Save(storage).read().slots[0] == null, 'bad version');\\n      const throwing = {\\n        getItem() { throw new Error('closed'); },\\n        setItem() { throw new Error('closed'); },\\n        removeItem() { throw new Error('closed'); },\\n      };\\n      const fallen = new Save(throwing);\\n      assert(fallen.memory === true, 'memory fallback');\\n      assert(fallen.write({ v: 1, slots: [null, null, null], settings: null }) === true, 'memory write');\\n      const empty = new Save(null);\\n      empty.write({ v: 1, slots: [freshGuest('Mem'), null, null], settings: null });\\n      assert(empty.read().slots[0].name === 'Mem', 'null storage');\\n    });\\n\\n    await test('replay fingerprint', async () => {\\n      const app = await boot(host);\\n      host.step(20);\\n      tap(host, 'Enter');\\n      host.step(15);\\n      const fp = host.fingerprint();\\n      const rec = host.recording();\\n      assert(rec && rec.frames.length > 10, 'recording');\\n      await host.replay(rec, () => host.loadGame(new World(new App({ storage: null, noHero: true }))));\\n      assert(host.fingerprint() === fp, `replay ${host.fingerprint()} vs ${fp}`);\\n    });\\n  } finally {\\n    host.dispose();\\n  }\\n\\n  if (!fast) {\\n    await test('browser, shots, and hub', async () => {\\n      execFileSync(process.execPath, ['tools/build.mjs'], { cwd: devRoot, stdio: ['ignore', 'pipe', 'pipe'] });\\n      const { runBrowser } = await import('./browser.mjs');\\n      const problems = await runBrowser({ devRoot, scratch: SCRATCH });\\n      if (problems.length) throw new Error(problems.join('\\\\n'));\\n    });\\n  }\\n\\n  if (fails.length) {\\n    for (const fail of fails) console.log(`FAIL ${fail}`);\\n    console.log(`${total - fails.length}/${total} passed`);\\n    process.exitCode = 1;\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  console.log(`${total}/${total} passed`);\\n}\\n\\nmain().catch((err) => {\\n  console.log(`FAIL runner: ${err?.stack || err}`);\\n  console.log(`0/${total} passed`);\\n  process.exitCode = 1;\\n});\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/tools/test.mjs has been created successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/tools/test.mjs has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/tools/test.mjs\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"/**\\n * Drives the shipped game. Prints failures and one \\\"N/N passed\\\" line.\\n * From the dev folder: node tools/test.mjs [--fast]\\n */\\nimport { createHash } from 'node:crypto';\\nimport { execFileSync } from 'node:child_process';\\nimport { appendFileSync, mkdirSync, readFileSync, readdirSync, statSync } from 'node:fs';\\nimport path from 'node:path';\\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\\nimport {\\n  Engine,\\n  HERO_RIG,\\n  analyzeClip,\\n  checkModel,\\n  compileClips,\\n  parseSong,\\n  validateClip,\\n  validateTexture,\\n} from '../pixel-engine.js';\\nimport { App, freshGuest } from '../src/app.js';\\nimport { CAMERA, World } from '../src/scenes/world.js';\\nimport { ACTIVITIES, ACTIVITY_BY_ID } from '../src/data/activities.js';\\nimport { DAYS } from '../src/data/week.js';\\nimport { LINES, SAMPLES, allLineStrings, linesFor } from '../src/data/lines.js';\\nimport { SONGS, songLevel } from '../src/audio/songs.js';\\nimport { syllabify } from '../src/audio/voice.js';\\nimport { Dot, DOT_DEFAULTS } from '../src/core/dot.js';\\nimport { BotDriver } from '../src/core/drivers.js';\\nimport { mulberry32 } from '../src/core/rng.js';\\nimport { dripsFor, milestonesReached, starsFor } from '../src/core/score.js';\\nimport { SAVE_KEY, Save } from '../src/core/save.js';\\nimport { DEFAULT_TUNABLES, TUNABLE_TABS, tabKeys } from '../src/core/tunables.js';\\nimport { missingGlyphs, wrapText } from '../src/ui/font.js';\\nimport { MODELS } from '../src/art/models.js';\\nimport { CLIPS } from '../src/art/clips.js';\\nimport { clinicTile } from '../src/art/textures.js';\\nimport { MEDICAL, SOURCE_INFORMATION, aboutPages, exitInterview } from '../src/data/about.js';\\nimport { CREDITS_TEXT } from '../src/data/creditsText.js';\\nimport { TITLE } from '../src/data/title.js';\\n\\nconst here = path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url));\\nconst devRoot = path.resolve(here, '..');\\nconst SCRATCH = '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/implementer';\\nconst fast = process.argv.includes('--fast');\\nmkdirSync(SCRATCH, { recursive: true });\\nconst BEAT = path.join(SCRATCH, 'beat.log');\\n\\nconst fails = [];\\nlet total = 0;\\n\\nfunction beat(msg) {\\n  try { appendFileSync(BEAT, `${new Date().toISOString()} ${msg}\\\\n`); } catch { /* scratch only */ }\\n}\\n\\nasync function test(name, fn) {\\n  total += 1;\\n  beat(`start ${name}`);\\n  try {\\n    await fn();\\n    beat(`ok ${name}`);\\n  } catch (err) {\\n    fails.push(`${name}: ${err?.stack || err?.message || err}`);\\n    beat(`FAIL ${name}: ${err?.message || err}`);\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nfunction assert(cond, msg) {\\n  if (!cond) throw new Error(msg || 'assertion failed');\\n}\\n\\nfunction tap(engine, code) {\\n  engine.input.setKey(code, true);\\n  engine.step(1);\\n  engine.input.setKey(code, false);\\n  engine.step(1);\\n}\\n\\nfunction choose(engine, app, id) {\\n  let guard = 0;\\n  while (app.state().row !== id) {\\n    if (guard++ > 12) throw new Error(`no row ${id} in ${app.mode}: ${app.state().rows.join(',')}`);\\n    tap(engine, 'ArrowDown');\\n  }\\n  tap(engine, 'Enter');\\n}\\n\\nfunction untilMode(engine, app, mode, cap, label) {\\n  let n = 0;\\n  while (app.mode !== mode) {\\n    if (n >= cap) throw new Error(`${label || mode}: stuck in ${app.status()} after ${n} frames`);\\n    const chunk = Math.min(180, cap - n);\\n    engine.step(chunk);\\n    n += chunk;\\n    if (n % 1080 === 0) beat(`${label || mode} ${app.status()}`);\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nfunction memoryStorage() {\\n  const m = new Map();\\n  return {\\n    getItem: (k) => (m.has(k) ? m.get(k) : null),\\n    setItem: (k, v) => m.set(k, String(v)),\\n    removeItem: (k) => m.delete(k),\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nasync function boot(engine, opts = {}) {\\n  const app = new App({ storage: opts.storage === undefined ? null : opts.storage, noHero: true, session: opts.session || null, touchOnly: !!opts.touchOnly });\\n  await engine.loadGame(new World(app));\\n  engine.step(2);\\n  return app;\\n}\\n\\nfunction band(skill, seed) {\\n  const dot = new Dot(mulberry32(seed));\\n  const bot = new BotDriver(skill, mulberry32(seed + 99));\\n  const dt = 1 / 60;\\n  let inside = 0;\\n  let n = 0;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 37 * 60; i++) {\\n    const u = skill === 'idle' ? { x: 0, y: 0 } : bot.read(dot, dt);\\n    dot.step(dt, u.x || 0, u.y || 0, DOT_DEFAULTS, {});\\n    if (i >= 120) {\\n      n += 1;\\n      if (Math.hypot(dot.x, dot.y) < 0.3) inside += 1;\\n    }\\n  }\\n  return inside / n;\\n}\\n\\nfunction walk(dir, out = []) {\\n  for (const name of readdirSync(dir)) {\\n    if (name === 'node_modules' || name === '.build') continue;\\n    const p = path.join(dir, name);\\n    if (statSync(p).isDirectory()) walk(p, out);\\n    else if (name.endsWith('.js')) out.push(p);\\n  }\\n  return out;\\n}\\n\\nasync function main() {\\n  await test('dot bands and star thresholds', async () => {\\n    const idle = band('idle', 1);\\n    const average = band('average', 1);\\n    const good = band('good', 1);\\n    const expert = band('expert', 1);\\n    assert(idle < 0.2, `idle ${idle}`);\\n    assert(average > 0.35 && average < 0.65, `average ${average}`);\\n    assert(good > 0.8, `good ${good}`);\\n    assert(expert > 0.95, `expert ${expert}`);\\n    assert(starsFor(idle * 100, [45, 70, 90]) === 0, 'idle stars');\\n    assert(starsFor(good * 100, [45, 70, 90]) === 3, 'good stars');\\n    assert(starsFor(44, [45, 70, 90]) === 0, 'below one');\\n    assert(starsFor(45, [45, 70, 90]) === 1, 'one');\\n    assert(starsFor(70, [45, 70, 90]) === 2, 'two');\\n    assert(starsFor(90, [45, 70, 90]) === 3, 'three');\\n    assert(DOT_DEFAULTS.dotInstability === 0.6 && DOT_DEFAULTS.dotLag === 0.08, 'defaults');\\n  });\\n\\n  await test('songs, lines, models, hash, about', async () => {\\n    for (const [name, song] of Object.entries(SONGS)) {\\n      parseSong(song);\\n      const level = songLevel(song);\\n      assert(level >= 0.03, `${name} level ${level}`);\\n    }\\n    assert(SONGS.step.bpm === 104, 'step bpm');\\n    const hash = createHash('sha256').update(readFileSync(path.join(devRoot, 'pixel-engine.js'))).digest('hex');\\n    const expected = readFileSync(path.join(devRoot, 'vendor/pixel-engine.sha256'), 'utf8').trim().split(/\\\\s+/)[0];\\n    assert(hash === expected, `hash ${hash}`);\\n    for (const model of MODELS) {\\n      const report = checkModel(model);\\n      assert(report.problems.length === 0, `${model.id || model.name} ${report.problems.join(';')}`);\\n    }\\n    const tex = validateTexture(clinicTile);\\n    assert(tex.problems.length === 0, `texture ${tex.problems.join(';')}`);\\n    assert(LINES.length >= 120, `lines ${LINES.length}`);\\n    const banned = /\\\\b(Wii|Mii|Wuhu)\\\\b|Balance Board|Wii Fit Trainer|Fit Age/;\\n    for (const text of allLineStrings()) {\\n      const bad = missingGlyphs(text);\\n      assert(bad.length === 0, `glyph ${bad.join('')} in ${text}`);\\n      for (const piece of wrapText(text, 52)) assert(piece.length <= 52, `wrap width ${piece}`);\\n      assert(wrapText(text, 52).length <= 3, `wrap lines ${text}`);\\n      assert(!banned.test(text), `banned ${text}`);\\n    }\\n    for (const def of ACTIVITIES) {\\n      for (const stars of [0, 1, 2, 3]) {\\n        for (const repeat of [false, true]) {\\n          const found = linesFor(def.id, stars, repeat);\\n          assert(found.length >= 1, `missing ${def.id} ${stars} ${repeat}`);\\n        }\\n      }\\n      assert(!banned.test(def.name), def.name);\\n    }\\n    for (const day of DAYS) assert(!banned.test(`${day.beat} ${day.concern}`), `day ${day.day}`);\\n    const pages = aboutPages(CREDITS_TEXT).map((p) => `${p.title}\\\\n${p.lines.join('\\\\n')}`).join('\\\\n');\\n    assert(pages.includes(MEDICAL), 'medical');\\n    for (const key of Object.keys(SOURCE_INFORMATION)) assert(pages.includes(String(SOURCE_INFORMATION[key])), `about ${key}`);\\n    assert(pages.includes('Testing Feedback') && pages.includes('Engine Feedback') && pages.includes('Prompt Feedback'), 'feedback');\\n    assert(pages.includes('Kenney') && pages.includes('three.js') && pages.includes('Rapier'), 'kit');\\n    const interview = exitInterview();\\n    assert(interview.sourceInformation.usage === 'added on import', 'usage');\\n    assert(interview.testingFeedback.length === 4, 'testing feedback');\\n    assert(interview.engineFeedback.length === 6, 'engine feedback');\\n    assert(interview.promptFeedback.length === 4, 'prompt feedback');\\n    for (const key of ['name', 'tagline', 'description', 'type', 'genre', 'source', 'series', 'players', 'controls', 'tags']) {\\n      assert(interview.aiHub[key], `aiHub ${key}`);\\n    }\\n    assert(interview.aiHub.name === TITLE, 'aiHub name');\\n    JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(interview));\\n    const hello = syllabify('hello', 'ounce');\\n    const hello2 = syllabify('hello', 'ounce');\\n    assert(JSON.stringify(hello.map((s) => s.vowel + s.cons)) === JSON.stringify(hello2.map((s) => s.vowel + s.cons)), 'stable word');\\n    const q = syllabify('Are you happy?', 'coach');\\n    const s = syllabify('Are you happy.', 'coach');\\n    assert(q[q.length - 1].f0 > s[s.length - 1].f0, 'question rises');\\n    const o = syllabify('Are you happy.', 'ounce');\\n    const c = syllabify('Are you happy.', 'coach');\\n    const mean = (list) => list.reduce((a, b) => a + b.f0, 0) / list.length;\\n    assert(mean(o) > mean(c), 'ounce higher');\\n    assert(syllabify('Kevin sat on me.', 'kevin').length === 0, 'kevin silent');\\n    for (const file of walk(path.join(devRoot, 'src'))) {\\n      const text = readFileSync(file, 'utf8');\\n      if (!text.includes('Math.random')) continue;\\n      assert(file.endsWith('drivers.js'), `Math.random in ${file}`);\\n      assert(text.includes('rand || Math.random'), 'drivers fallback only');\\n    }\\n  });\\n\\n  await test('clips on the hero', async () => {\\n    const app = new App({ storage: null, noHero: false });\\n    const world = new World(app);\\n    const engine = await Engine.headless(world, { camera: CAMERA });\\n    try {\\n      engine.step(1);\\n      const model = world.heroModel;\\n      assert(model, 'hero model');\\n      for (const def of CLIPS) {\\n        const problems = validateClip(def, HERO_RIG);\\n        assert(problems.length === 0, `${def.name} validate ${problems.join(';')}`);\\n        const clip = compileClips([def], HERO_RIG, model)[0];\\n        const report = analyzeClip(model, HERO_RIG, def, clip);\\n        assert(report.problems.length === 0, `${def.name} analyze ${report.problems.join(';')}`);\\n      }\\n    } finally {\\n      engine.dispose();\\n    }\\n  });\\n\\n  const host = await Engine.headless(new World(new App({ storage: null, noHero: true })), { camera: CAMERA });\\n  try {\\n    await test('boot title and music', async () => {\\n      const app = host.game ? host.game.app : null;\\n      const live = app && app.mode === 'title' ? app : await boot(host);\\n      host.step(2);\\n      const state = live.state();\\n      assert(state.title === TITLE, state.title);\\n      assert(state.mode === 'title', state.mode);\\n      assert(state.music === 0.1, `music ${state.music}`);\\n      assert(host.audio.volume.music === 0.1, `bus ${host.audio.volume.music}`);\\n      assert(state.rows.includes('start'), 'start row');\\n    });\\n\\n    await test('every activity idle, sloppy, expert, drips, hard', async () => {\\n      const storage = memoryStorage();\\n      const app = await boot(host, { storage });\\n      app.guest = freshGuest('Sweep');\\n      const expertScore = {};\\n      for (const skill of ['idle', 'expert', 'sloppy']) {\\n        for (const def of ACTIVITIES) {\\n          app.guest.hard = false;\\n          app.setDriver(skill);\\n          app.go('activity', def.id);\\n          untilMode(host, app, 'results', 110 * 60, `${skill} ${def.id}`);\\n          const state = app.state();\\n          if (skill === 'idle') assert(state.stars === 0, `${def.id} idle ${state.stars}`);\\n          if (skill === 'expert') {\\n            assert(state.stars >= 2, `${def.id} expert ${state.stars} score ${state.score}`);\\n            if (def.easy) assert(state.stars === 3, `${def.id} easy ${state.stars}`);\\n            expertScore[def.id] = state.score;\\n          }\\n          if (skill === 'sloppy') assert(state.score < expertScore[def.id], `${def.id} sloppy ${state.score} vs ${expertScore[def.id]}`);\\n          assert(state.lastDrips === dripsFor(state.stars, state.seconds, state.lastPrescription, app.tunables.dripRate), `${def.id} drips`);\\n          choose(host, app, 'back');\\n        }\\n      }\\n      app.guest.hard = true;\\n      app.setDriver('expert');\\n      for (const id of ['plank', 'tree', 'pier']) {\\n        app.go('activity', id);\\n        untilMode(host, app, 'results', 110 * 60, `hard ${id}`);\\n        assert(app.state().stars >= 2, `hard ${id} ${app.state().stars}`);\\n        choose(host, app, 'back');\\n      }\\n    });\\n\\n    await test('pause, dev sliders, dev tools', async () => {\\n      const app = await boot(host);\\n      app.guest = freshGuest('Dev');\\n      app.setDriver('expert');\\n      app.go('activity', 'tree');\\n      host.step(30);\\n      const t0 = app.state().playT;\\n      const x0 = app.sim.dot.x;\\n      tap(host, 'KeyP');\\n      assert(app.mode === 'pause', app.mode);\\n      assert(host.timeScale === 0, 'paused scale');\\n      host.step(30);\\n      assert(app.sim.playT === t0, 'playT frozen');\\n      assert(app.sim.dot.x === x0, 'dot frozen');\\n      tap(host, 'ArrowDown');\\n      assert(app.state().row === 'restart', app.state().row);\\n      choose(host, app, 'resume');\\n      assert(host.timeScale === 1, 'resumed');\\n      host.step(20);\\n      assert(app.sim.playT > t0, 'playT moved');\\n      tap(host, 'KeyP');\\n      choose(host, app, 'dev');\\n      assert(app.mode === 'dev' && host.timeScale === 0, 'dev frozen');\\n      assert(app.sim.T === app.tunables, 'shared tunables');\\n      const dirty = {};\\n      for (const tab of Object.keys(TUNABLE_TABS)) {\\n        while (app.state().devTab !== tab) tap(host, 'KeyE');\\n        let guard = 0;\\n        const want = new Set(tabKeys(tab));\\n        while (want.size && guard++ < 6) {\\n          for (const id of app.state().rows) {\\n            if (!want.has(id)) continue;\\n            while (app.state().row !== id) tap(host, 'ArrowDown');\\n            const before = app.tunables[id];\\n            tap(host, 'ArrowRight');\\n            assert(app.tunables[id] !== before, `${id} did not move`);\\n            assert(app.sim.T[id] === app.tunables[id], `${id} not shared`);\\n            dirty[id] = app.tunables[id];\\n            want.delete(id);\\n          }\\n          if (want.size) choose(host, app, 'more');\\n        }\\n        assert(want.size === 0, `missed ${[...want].join(',')}`);\\n      }\\n      while (app.state().devTab !== 'Balance') tap(host, 'KeyQ');\\n      choose(host, app, 'reset-tab');\\n      for (const key of tabKeys('Balance')) assert(app.tunables[key] === DEFAULT_TUNABLES[key], `reset-tab ${key}`);\\n      assert(app.tunables.dripRate === dirty.dripRate, 'other tab kept');\\n      choose(host, app, 'reset-all');\\n      for (const key of Object.keys(DEFAULT_TUNABLES)) assert(app.tunables[key] === DEFAULT_TUNABLES[key], `reset-all ${key}`);\\n      while (app.state().devTab !== 'Tools') tap(host, 'KeyE');\\n      const dayBefore = app.guest.day;\\n      choose(host, app, 'day');\\n      assert(app.guest.day !== dayBefore, 'day tool');\\n      const dripsBefore = app.guest.drips;\\n      choose(host, app, 'drips');\\n      assert(app.guest.drips === dripsBefore + 50, 'drips tool');\\n      choose(host, app, 'unlock');\\n      assert(app.guest.unlockAll === true, 'unlock');\\n      choose(host, app, 'more');\\n      const driverBefore = app.driver;\\n      choose(host, app, 'auto');\\n      assert(app.driver !== driverBefore, 'auto');\\n      choose(host, app, 'god');\\n      assert(app.god === true && app.sim.god === true, 'god');\\n      choose(host, app, 'overlay');\\n      assert(app.overlay === true, 'overlay');\\n      choose(host, app, 'hud');\\n      assert(app.hideHud === true, 'hud');\\n      choose(host, app, 'hud');\\n      choose(host, app, 'more');\\n      choose(host, app, 'camera');\\n      assert(app.freeCam === true, 'camera');\\n      const lineBefore = app.dialogue;\\n      choose(host, app, 'line');\\n      assert(app.dialogue && app.dialogue !== lineBefore, 'line');\\n      choose(host, app, 'sound');\\n      assert(app.songPlaying || host.audio.counts, 'sound');\\n      choose(host, app, 'anim');\\n      assert(app.viewerClip, 'anim');\\n      choose(host, app, 'export');\\n      assert(typeof app.exported === 'string', 'export');\\n      choose(host, app, 'wipe');\\n      assert(app.guest === null, 'wipe');\\n      choose(host, app, 'more');\\n      choose(host, app, 'time');\\n      assert([0.25, 0.5, 1, 2, 3].includes(host.timeScale), `time ${host.timeScale}`);\\n      host.timeScale = 0;\\n      while (app.state().devTab !== 'Tools') tap(host, 'KeyE');\\n      while (!app.state().rows.includes('jump')) {\\n        if (app.state().rows.includes('prev')) choose(host, app, 'prev');\\n        else break;\\n      }\\n      choose(host, app, 'jump');\\n      assert(app.mode === 'activity', `jump ${app.mode}`);\\n      assert(app.activityId === ACTIVITIES[1].id, app.activityId);\\n      tap(host, 'KeyP');\\n      choose(host, app, 'dev');\\n      while (app.state().devTab !== 'Tools') tap(host, 'KeyE');\\n      choose(host, app, 'finish');\\n      assert(app.mode === 'results', app.mode);\\n      assert(app.state().stars === 1, `finish stars ${app.state().stars}`);\\n    });\\n\\n    await test('attract, touch gate, session card', async () => {\\n      const app = await boot(host);\\n      assert(app.mode === 'title', app.mode);\\n      host.step(700);\\n      assert(app.mode === 'attract', `title attract ${app.mode}`);\\n      const seen = new Set();\\n      let guard = 0;\\n      while (seen.size < 10 && guard < 12000) {\\n        seen.add(app.activityId);\\n        host.step(120);\\n        guard += 120;\\n      }\\n      for (const id of ['tree', 'hoop', 'header', 'step', 'slack', 'tray', 'pier', 'jog', 'squat', 'longstand']) {\\n        assert(seen.has(id), `attract missed ${id}`);\\n      }\\n      tap(host, 'Enter');\\n      assert(app.mode === 'title', `attract exit ${app.mode}`);\\n      choose(host, app, 'start');\\n      choose(host, app, 'settings');\\n      host.step(700);\\n      assert(app.mode === 'attract', `settings attract ${app.mode}`);\\n      tap(host, 'Enter');\\n      app.setDriver('expert');\\n      app.guest = freshGuest('Play');\\n      app.go('activity', 'tree');\\n      host.step(800);\\n      assert(app.mode === 'activity', `play attract ${app.mode}`);\\n      tap(host, 'KeyP');\\n      choose(host, app, 'settings');\\n      assert(app.frozen === true, 'settings from pause stays frozen');\\n      host.step(700);\\n      assert(app.mode === 'settings', `pause settings attracted ${app.mode}`);\\n\\n      const touch = await boot(host, { touchOnly: true });\\n      assert(touch.state().touchMessage === 'Controller or keyboard required', touch.state().touchMessage);\\n      tap(host, 'MouseLeft');\\n      assert(touch.mode === 'title', `touch confirm ${touch.mode}`);\\n      tap(host, 'Enter');\\n      assert(touch.touchOnly === false, 'key clears the gate');\\n\\n      const card = await boot(host, { session: { players: [{ name: 'Ada' }] } });\\n      assert(card.mode === 'card', card.mode);\\n      host.step(700);\\n      assert(card.mode === 'card', `session attract ${card.mode}`);\\n    });\\n\\n    await test('family hour and medley ghost', async () => {\\n      const pads = [null, null, null, null];\\n      const nav = globalThis.navigator || {};\\n      nav.getGamepads = () => pads;\\n      globalThis.navigator = nav;\\n      const app = await boot(host);\\n      choose(host, app, 'start');\\n      choose(host, app, 'family');\\n      assert(app.mode === 'join', app.mode);\\n      const claim = (index, axis) => {\\n        pads[index] = {\\n          connected: true,\\n          axes: [axis, 0, 0, 0],\\n          buttons: [{ pressed: true, value: 1 }, ...Array.from({ length: 15 }, () => ({ pressed: false, value: 0 }))],\\n        };\\n        host.step(1);\\n      };\\n      claim(0, 0.9);\\n      claim(1, -0.9);\\n      tap(host, 'Enter');\\n      assert(app.mode === 'join', `join ate the claim ${app.mode} ${app.state().row}`);\\n      const kinds = app.seats.map((s) => s && s.kind);\\n      assert(kinds[0] === 'pad' && kinds[1] === 'pad' && kinds[2] === 'key', kinds.join(','));\\n      choose(host, app, 'start');\\n      assert(app.mode === 'medley', app.mode);\\n      assert(app.lanes.length === 3, `lanes ${app.lanes.length}`);\\n      host.input.setKey('ArrowRight', true);\\n      host.step(120);\\n      host.input.setKey('ArrowRight', false);\\n      host.step(1);\\n      const pos = app.lanes.map((lane) => lane.pos);\\n      assert(new Set(pos.map((n) => n.toFixed(3))).size === 3, `lanes alike ${pos.join(',')}`);\\n\\n      app.go('medley', { bots: true, ghost: true, skills: ['expert', 'good', 'average', 'sloppy'] });\\n      const ghost = app.lanes.find((lane) => lane.kind === 'ghost');\\n      assert(ghost && ghost.simulated === false, 'ghost simulated');\\n      ghost.ghost.push({ a: 1, x: 0.4, y: -0.2, c: 0, t: 1, s: 0 });\\n      host.step(5);\\n      assert(ghost.dot.t === 0, `ghost dot stepped ${ghost.dot.t}`);\\n      assert(ghost.steps === 0, 'ghost steps');\\n      assert(ghost.hidden === true, 'ghost hidden on other event');\\n      let guard = 0;\\n      while (app.mode === 'medley' && guard < 13000) {\\n        host.step(180);\\n        guard += 180;\\n        if (guard % 1080 === 0) beat(`medley ${app.medleyT.toFixed(1)}`);\\n      }\\n      assert(app.mode === 'podium', app.mode);\\n      for (const lane of app.lanes) {\\n        if (lane.kind === 'ghost') {\\n          assert(lane.dot.t === 0, 'ghost dot after medley');\\n          continue;\\n        }\\n        for (const score of lane.scores) assert(score >= 0 && score <= 1000, `score ${score}`);\\n      }\\n    });\\n\\n    await test('hub clock progress and result', async () => {\\n      const handlers = {};\\n      const calls = [];\\n      const hub = {\\n        on(ev, fn) { (handlers[ev] ||= []).push(fn); },\\n        emit(ev, arg) { (handlers[ev] || []).forEach((fn) => fn(arg)); },\\n        send(data) { calls.push(['send', data]); },\\n        progress(data) { calls.push(['progress', data]); },\\n        result(data) { calls.push(['result', data]); },\\n        time() { return this.t; },\\n        t: -4000,\\n      };\\n      const app = await boot(host);\\n      app.bindHub(hub);\\n      hub.emit('start');\\n      assert(app.mode === 'medley', app.mode);\\n      assert(calls.some((c) => c[0] === 'progress' && c[1].score === 0), 'progress at 0');\\n      assert(calls.some((c) => c[0] === 'send'), 'send at start');\\n      host.step(10);\\n      assert(app.medleyT === 0, `countdown moved ${app.medleyT}`);\\n      hub.t = 2000;\\n      host.step(5);\\n      assert(Math.abs(app.medleyT - 2) < 0.05, `hub clock ${app.medleyT}`);\\n      const ghost = app.lanes.find((lane) => lane.kind === 'ghost');\\n      hub.emit('message', null);\\n      app.ghostMessage({ a: 0, x: 0.8, y: 0.1, c: 0, t: 0, s: 0 }, 3);\\n      host.step(8);\\n      const shown = app.lanes.find((lane) => lane.kind === 'ghost');\\n      assert(shown && shown.dot.t === 0, 'message ghost not simulated');\\n      assert(shown.ghost.shown.x > 0, 'ghost lerped');\\n      hub.emit('time-up');\\n      hub.emit('time-up');\\n      assert(calls.filter((c) => c[0] === 'result').length === 1, 'one result');\\n      hub.emit('end');\\n      assert(app.hubEnded === true, 'ended');\\n      void ghost;\\n    });\\n\\n    await test('saves, corrupt storage, scripted week', async () => {\\n      const storage = memoryStorage();\\n      let app = await boot(host, { storage });\\n      app.setDriver('expert');\\n      choose(host, app, 'start');\\n      choose(host, app, 'week');\\n      choose(host, app, 'slot0');\\n      assert(app.mode === 'name', app.mode);\\n      tap(host, 'Backspace');\\n      tap(host, 'Backspace');\\n      for (const ch of 'ada') tap(host, `Key${ch.toUpperCase()}`);\\n      choose(host, app, 'done');\\n      assert(app.mode === 'ferry', app.mode);\\n      assert(app.guest.name === 'Guestada' || app.guest.name.length <= 8, app.guest.name);\\n      choose(host, app, 'board');\\n      untilMode(host, app, 'question', 1200, 'weigh1');\\n      const savedName = app.guest.name;\\n      const reloaded = new App({ storage, noHero: true });\\n      await host.loadGame(new World(reloaded));\\n      host.step(2);\\n      choose(host, reloaded, 'start');\\n      choose(host, reloaded, 'week');\\n      choose(host, reloaded, 'slot0');\\n      assert(reloaded.guest && reloaded.guest.name === savedName, 'reload name');\\n      assert(reloaded.mode === 'weigh', `reload mode ${reloaded.mode}`);\\n      untilMode(host, reloaded, 'question', 1200, 'reweigh');\\n      choose(host, reloaded, 'a0');\\n      choose(host, reloaded, 'onward');\\n      app = reloaded;\\n      app.setDriver('expert');\\n\\n      const play = async (station, id) => {\\n        if (app.islandPage !== 0) choose(host, app, 'back');\\n        choose(host, app, `st-${station}`);\\n        choose(host, app, `act-${id}`);\\n        untilMode(host, app, 'results', 110 * 60, id);\\n        const state = app.state();\\n        choose(host, app, 'back');\\n        return state;\\n      };\\n      const visit = (station) => {\\n        if (app.islandPage !== 0) choose(host, app, 'back');\\n        choose(host, app, `st-${station}`);\\n        assert(app.mode === 'station', station);\\n        choose(host, app, 'back');\\n      };\\n      const sleep = () => {\\n        if (app.islandPage === 0) choose(host, app, 'more');\\n        choose(host, app, 'hammock');\\n        choose(host, app, 'rest');\\n        choose(host, app, 'sleep');\\n      };\\n      const morning = () => {\\n        untilMode(host, app, 'question', 1200, `morning ${app.guest.day}`);\\n        choose(host, app, 'a0');\\n        assert(app.mode === 'reveal', app.mode);\\n        const last = app.guest.chart[app.guest.chart.length - 1];\\n        assert(last.shown === last.trueAge + 7, `shown ${last.shown} true ${last.trueAge}`);\\n        choose(host, app, 'onward');\\n        assert(app.mode === 'island', app.mode);\\n      };\\n\\n      let tree = await play('pavilion', 'tree');\\n      assert(tree.lastDrips === dripsFor(tree.stars, tree.seconds, tree.lastPrescription, app.tunables.dripRate), 'tree drips');\\n      assert(tree.lastPrescription === false, 'pair not done yet');\\n      const squat = await play('shed', 'squat');\\n      assert(squat.lastPrescription === true, 'day 1 pair');\\n      sleep();\\n      morning();\\n\\n      const warrior = await play('pavilion', 'warrior');\\n      assert(warrior.stars >= 2, `day 2 stars ${warrior.stars}`);\\n      assert(warrior.lastPrescription === true, 'day 2 goal');\\n      if (app.islandPage === 0) choose(host, app, 'more');\\n      choose(host, app, 'jar');\\n      choose(host, app, 'back');\\n      choose(host, app, 'locker');\\n      choose(host, app, 'back');\\n      choose(host, app, 'hall');\\n      choose(host, app, 'back');\\n      sleep();\\n      morning();\\n\\n      const heron = await play('pavilion', 'heron');\\n      assert(heron.lastPrescription === true, 'day 3 fresh');\\n      sleep();\\n      morning();\\n\\n      visit('plaza');\\n      visit('jog');\\n      await play('pavilion', 'tree');\\n      await play('shed', 'squat');\\n      const hoop = await play('beach', 'hoop');\\n      assert(hoop.lastPrescription === true, 'day 4 count');\\n      sleep();\\n      morning();\\n\\n      const tray = await play('lagoon', 'tray');\\n      assert(tray.lastPrescription === true, `day 5 beat score ${tray.score}`);\\n      sleep();\\n      morning();\\n\\n      const third = await play('pavilion', 'tree');\\n      assert(third.stars === 3, `day 6 stars ${third.stars}`);\\n      assert(third.lastPrescription === true, 'day 6 goal');\\n      sleep();\\n      morning();\\n\\n      if (app.islandPage === 0) choose(host, app, 'more');\\n      choose(host, app, 'longstand');\\n      untilMode(host, app, 'results', 110 * 60, 'longstand');\\n      const long = app.state();\\n      assert(long.lastPrescription === true, 'day 7 long stand');\\n      choose(host, app, 'back');\\n      const before = app.guest.chart.map((p) => ({ ...p }));\\n      assert(before.length >= 7, `chart ${before.length}`);\\n      sleep();\\n      assert(app.mode === 'confession', app.mode);\\n      choose(host, app, 'onward');\\n      assert(app.guest.confessed === true, 'confessed');\\n      assert(app.mode === 'credits', app.mode);\\n      app.guest.chart.forEach((point, i) => {\\n        assert(point.trueAge === before[i].trueAge, 'true age changed');\\n        assert(point.shown === before[i].shown - 7, `shown delta ${point.shown}`);\\n        assert(point.shown === point.trueAge, 'shown is true after');\\n      });\\n      const items = milestonesReached(app.guest.drips).map((item) => item.id);\\n      assert(JSON.stringify(app.guest.items) === JSON.stringify(items), 'jar items');\\n      choose(host, app, 'onward');\\n      assert(app.guest.day === 8 && app.guest.week === 2, `week 2 ${app.guest.day}/${app.guest.week}`);\\n      assert(app.mode === 'weigh', `week 2 mode ${app.mode}`);\\n\\n      storage.setItem(SAVE_KEY, '{');\\n      const corrupt = new Save(storage);\\n      assert(corrupt.read().slots.every((slot) => slot == null), 'corrupt json');\\n      storage.setItem(SAVE_KEY, JSON.stringify({ v: 99, slots: [{ name: 'nope' }] }));\\n      assert(new Save(storage).read().slots[0] == null, 'bad version');\\n      const throwing = {\\n        getItem() { throw new Error('closed'); },\\n        setItem() { throw new Error('closed'); },\\n        removeItem() { throw new Error('closed'); },\\n      };\\n      const fallen = new Save(throwing);\\n      assert(fallen.memory === true, 'memory fallback');\\n      assert(fallen.write({ v: 1, slots: [null, null, null], settings: null }) === true, 'memory write');\\n      const empty = new Save(null);\\n      empty.write({ v: 1, slots: [freshGuest('Mem'), null, null], settings: null });\\n      assert(empty.read().slots[0].name === 'Mem', 'null storage');\\n    });\\n\\n    await test('replay fingerprint', async () => {\\n      const app = await boot(host);\\n      host.step(20);\\n      tap(host, 'Enter');\\n      host.step(15);\\n      const fp = host.fingerprint();\\n      const rec = host.recording();\\n      assert(rec && rec.frames.length > 10, 'recording');\\n      await host.replay(rec, () => host.loadGame(new World(new App({ storage: null, noHero: true }))));\\n      assert(host.fingerprint() === fp, `replay ${host.fingerprint()} vs ${fp}`);\\n    });\\n  } finally {\\n    host.dispose();\\n  }\\n\\n  if (!fast) {\\n    await test('browser, shots, and hub', async () => {\\n      execFileSync(process.execPath, ['tools/build.mjs'], { cwd: devRoot, stdio: ['ignore', 'pipe', 'pipe'] });\\n      const { runBrowser } = await import('./browser.mjs');\\n      const problems = await runBrowser({ devRoot, scratch: SCRATCH });\\n      if (problems.length) throw new Error(problems.join('\\\\n'));\\n    });\\n  }\\n\\n  if (fails.length) {\\n    for (const fail of fails) console.log(`FAIL ${fail}`);\\n    console.log(`${total - fails.length}/${total} passed`);\\n    process.exitCode = 1;\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  console.log(`${total}/${total} passed`);\\n}\\n\\nmain().catch((err) => {\\n  console.log(`FAIL runner: ${err?.stack || err}`);\\n  console.log(`0/${total} passed`);\\n  process.exitCode = 1;\\n});\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-8b193878-0650-4a4b-8aec-62af45d5e22e-79","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"/** Step, capture the WebGPU frame, composite the HUD canvas, return a PNG data URL. */\\nexport async function grab(page) {\\n  return page.evaluate(async () => {\\n    const engine = window.__PIXEL_ENGINE__;\\n    const app = window.__GAME__;\\n    engine.step(20);\\n    let frame;\\n    try {\\n      frame = await engine.renderer.capture();\\n    } catch (err) {\\n      return { error: String(err && err.stack || err) };\\n    }\\n    const canvas = document.createElement('canvas');\\n    canvas.width = frame.width;\\n    canvas.height = frame.height;\\n    const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');\\n    const pixels = new Uint8ClampedArray(frame.pixels);\\n    ctx.putImageData(new ImageData(pixels, frame.width, frame.height), 0, 0);\\n    const huds = [...document.querySelectorAll('canvas')].filter((c) => c !== canvas && c.width > 0);\\n    for (const hud of huds) {\\n      try { ctx.drawImage(hud, 0, 0, frame.width, frame.height); } catch { /* a canvas may be tainted or empty */ }\\n    }\\n    let min = 255;\\n    let max = 0;\\n    const step = Math.max(1, Math.floor(pixels.length / 4 / 4000)) * 4;\\n    for (let i = 0; i < pixels.length; i += step) {\\n      const luma = pixels[i] * 0.3 + pixels[i + 1] * 0.59 + pixels[i + 2] * 0.11;\\n      if (luma < min) min = luma;\\n      if (luma > max) max = luma;\\n    }\\n    const state = app.state();\\n    return {\\n      width: frame.width,\\n      height: frame.height,\\n      span: max - min,\\n      url: canvas.toDataURL('image/png'),\\n      title: state.title,\\n      mode: state.mode,\\n      music: state.music,\\n      row: state.row,\\n      hudW: app.ctx.hud.width,\\n      hudH: app.ctx.hud.height,\\n    };\\n  });\\n}\\n\\nexport function writePng(file, dataUrl) {\\n  const { writeFileSync } = require('node:fs');\\n  writeFileSync(file, Buffer.from(String(dataUrl).split(',')[1], 'base64'));\\n}\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/tools/shot.mjs has been created successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/tools/shot.mjs has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/tools/shot.mjs\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"/** Step, capture the WebGPU frame, composite the HUD canvas, return a PNG data URL. */\\nexport async function grab(page) {\\n  return page.evaluate(async () => {\\n    const engine = window.__PIXEL_ENGINE__;\\n    const app = window.__GAME__;\\n    engine.step(20);\\n    let frame;\\n    try {\\n      frame = await engine.renderer.capture();\\n    } catch (err) {\\n      return { error: String(err && err.stack || err) };\\n    }\\n    const canvas = document.createElement('canvas');\\n    canvas.width = frame.width;\\n    canvas.height = frame.height;\\n    const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');\\n    const pixels = new Uint8ClampedArray(frame.pixels);\\n    ctx.putImageData(new ImageData(pixels, frame.width, frame.height), 0, 0);\\n    const huds = [...document.querySelectorAll('canvas')].filter((c) => c !== canvas && c.width > 0);\\n    for (const hud of huds) {\\n      try { ctx.drawImage(hud, 0, 0, frame.width, frame.height); } catch { /* a canvas may be tainted or empty */ }\\n    }\\n    let min = 255;\\n    let max = 0;\\n    const step = Math.max(1, Math.floor(pixels.length / 4 / 4000)) * 4;\\n    for (let i = 0; i < pixels.length; i += step) {\\n      const luma = pixels[i] * 0.3 + pixels[i + 1] * 0.59 + pixels[i + 2] * 0.11;\\n      if (luma < min) min = luma;\\n      if (luma > max) max = luma;\\n    }\\n    const state = app.state();\\n    return {\\n      width: frame.width,\\n      height: frame.height,\\n      span: max - min,\\n      url: canvas.toDataURL('image/png'),\\n      title: state.title,\\n      mode: state.mode,\\n      music: state.music,\\n      row: state.row,\\n      hudW: app.ctx.hud.width,\\n      hudH: app.ctx.hud.height,\\n    };\\n  });\\n}\\n\\nexport function writePng(file, dataUrl) {\\n  const { writeFileSync } = require('node:fs');\\n  writeFileSync(file, Buffer.from(String(dataUrl).split(',')[1], 'base64'));\\n}\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"35c3b975-406e-4c50-8a58-632cd04e476f"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_204","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"shot.mjs uses require in an ESM project.\n\nshot.mjs will be converted to pure ESM with writeFileSync imported at the top. A new browser.mjs will handle browser-side PNG capture. The test.mjs name entry logic was verified: backspacing twice from 'Guest' yields 'Gue', then typing 'ada' produces 'Gueada', which satisfies the length assertion.\n\nBackspace is a bad choice for the name test because it triggers both text editing and the menu back button. The plan is to simply confirm \"Guest\" without using Backspace.\n\nThe choose-after-reload flow may create duplicate weigh entries. After boarding, ferried is true, so reloading the slot restarts weigh mode and repeats the same day's weighing before the island. This could produce two chart points for day one.\n\nThe extra weigh point is harmless. The chart will have eight points instead of seven, but the confession logic still subtracts seven from each value and passes its assertions.\n\nThe first weigh's finishWeigh already wrote the guest to disk before the reload. The second weigh adds a second chart point, which is harmless. The initial boot sequence saves a single chart point before the reload discards the engine world. The backspace bug must be fixed or the name screen will return to slots and break the choose-done flow.\n\nRemoving all letter taps and simply confirming \"Guest\" is the cleanest fix. The player cannot delete a letter on the name screen because Backspace triggers both text editing and the menu back button.\n\nThe fix is to exclude Backspace from the menu back button when the game is in name mode. Escape and PadCircle will still exit the name screen.\n\nThe test's Backspace will now work correctly once the name-mode fix is in place.\n\nA bug was spotted in the test suite: `host.game` after a headless boot points to the World object, not the App. The first test incorrectly accesses `host.game.app`, but the correct reference is `world.app`.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7a38cfd7-179b-4a35-899d-48721f7fec83-80","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"^\\s+game:","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/types/engine/Engine.d.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7a38cfd7-179b-4a35-899d-48721f7fec83-81","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/app.js","old_string":"    } else if (this.pressedAny(ctx, PRESS) || (this.mode !== 'name' && this.mode !== 'dev' && this.edge(ctx, 'KeyE'))) {\n      const row = this.rows[this.focus];\n      if (row) this.activate(row.id);\n    } else if (this.pressedAny(ctx, BACK) && this.mode !== 'pause') {\n      this.back();\n    }","new_string":"    } else if (this.pressedAny(ctx, PRESS) || (this.mode !== 'name' && this.mode !== 'dev' && this.edge(ctx, 'KeyE'))) {\n      const row = this.rows[this.focus];\n      if (row) this.activate(row.id);\n    } else if (this.mode !== 'pause' && this.pressedAny(ctx, BACK)) {\n      const editing = this.mode === 'name' && this.edge(ctx, 'Backspace') && !this.edge(ctx, 'Escape') && !this.edge(ctx, 'PadCircle') && !this.edge(ctx, 'MouseRight');\n      if (!editing) this.back();\n    }"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7a38cfd7-179b-4a35-899d-48721f7fec83-82","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/tools/shot.mjs","old_string":"/** Step, capture the WebGPU frame, composite the HUD canvas, return a PNG data URL. */\nexport async function grab(page) {","new_string":"/** Step, capture the WebGPU frame, composite canvases, return a PNG data URL. */\nimport { writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';\