{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_223","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The grep for timeScale in pixel-engine.js returned only minified junk because the pattern matched inside a huge line.\n\nThe test still fails after the guard was added. Either frozen is not true when timeScale is zero, or headless step() still calls fixedUpdate at timeScale zero.\n\nThe test might be advancing playT without calling sim.step. Another possibility is that menuInput during pause accidentally unpause the activity, or a keyup from tap() triggers an unexpected edge event.\n\nTracing the tap sequence step by step shows frozen stays true and timeScale remains zero. The engine's step at timeScale zero does not call fixedUpdate, so playT should not advance. A new realization is forming.\n\nThe engine object inside fixedUpdate might be a different instance, so timeScale is not zero and frozen is false. I need to check update(), refresh(), go(), and startActivity for anything that resets frozen. I also need to verify whether the engine actually skips fixedUpdate when timeScale is zero.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The freeze guard is in `fixed`, but play time still moves. I'll trace a pause in a short script and see which path advances it."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-135cb1c4-134b-4985-b79d-b19e428fb106-14","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/app.js","offset":1105,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-135cb1c4-134b-4985-b79d-b19e428fb106-15","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"timeScale","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/pixel-engine.d.ts"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3547,"output_tokens":920,"cache_read_input_tokens":