1,58,32,96,115,116,101,112,40,41,96,32,112,108,97,121,115,32,111,110,32,102,114,111,109,32,116,104,101,114,101,44,32,108,105,118,101,44,32,97,110,100,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":10,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/types/engine/Engine.d.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":239,\"content\":\"     * frame keeps rendering so the picture stays up. Fix the first one first. (`step()` throws\"},{\"line_number\":278,\"content\":\"    /** True once the first start has finished: `step()` before it is a tool's race, and throws. */\"},{\"line_number\":288,\"content\":\"     * Tooling: the render loop stops driving the game; advance it yourself with `step()`.\"},{\"line_number\":385,\"content\":\"     * console. It runs in manual time from the start: advance it with `step()`, give it input with\"},{\"line_number\":484,\"content\":\"    step(n?: number, dt?: number): void;\"},{\"line_number\":486,\"content\":\"     * One manual frame (`step()`), its input live or from a recorded frame (`replay()`). A game\"},{\"line_number\":487,\"content\":\"     * hook's exception finishes the frame first, then is thrown to the caller of `step()`; in a\"},{\"line_number\":544,\"content\":\"    /** Keep this frame's input in the level's recording (live play and `step()`, not replays). */\"},{\"line_number\":555,\"content\":\"     * (`step()`), waiting for promise callbacks wherever the recorded run did. `frames` stops\"},{\"line_number\":557,\"content\":\"     * game is deterministic) and stays in manual time: `step()` plays on from there, live, and\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"a62aec50-7c3a-41d5-93cd-489814719c0e"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_226","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Level unloads reset the value to 1. Frozen states drop key presses like a pause menu.\n\nA test showed playT still changed while timeScale was 0. This contradicts the assumption that fixedUpdate receives zero delta at that scale. A diagnostic will be written to find the cause.\n\nA monkeypatched diagnostic script will be run without modifying the game code. The skipIntro behavior is being checked: if the intro lasts 2.2 seconds, playT could remain zero for thirty frames and pass an assertion against t0. Because playT changed instead, the simulation is stepping. The next step is to verify whether fixedUpdate is actually the function being called.\n\nOnly fixed() calls sim.step, so the simulation is not being stepped from elsewhere during update. placeDot and draw do not advance time. If the intro finishes into play while the pause does not freeze the clock, playT will increase.\n\nThe failure matches the theory that the freeze guard is not stopping the step. The engine's timeScale setter accepts zero, and loadGame resets the scale only on level unload, so neither explains the leak. I will inspect the minified GameClock source to see how timeScale is handled.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5197e05e-19c3-4467-ad8f-507fb4a705ee-21","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"node --input-type=module -e '\nimport { readFileSync } from \"fs\";\nconst s = readFileSync(\"pixel-engine.js\",\"utf8\");\nlet i = 0, n = 0;\nwhile ((i = s.indexOf(\"timeScale\", i)) !== -1 && n < 30) {\n  console.log(\"---\", n, i);\n  console.log(s.slice(Math.max(0,i-100), i+180));\n  console.log();\n  i += 9; n++;\n}\n'","description":"Find timeScale usages in pixel-engine.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1586,"output_tokens":848,"cache_read_input_tokens":60288,"cache_creation_input_tokens"