{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_231","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The physics update function receives the scaled delta time from the clock.\n\nA zero delta time could still trigger leftover fixed steps from an accumulator. That would break the pause test.\n\nThe accumulator should drain after one paused frame. The bug likely comes from the physics update method always executing a fixed step per frame regardless of delta time.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-64b5c127-fdab-4f99-bf8d-4bc8e53ca0ec-26","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"cd \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607\" && node --input-type=module -e '\nimport { readFileSync } from \"fs\";\nconst s = readFileSync(\"pixel-engine.js\",\"utf8\");\nfor (const needle of [\"accumulator\", \"fixedDt\", \"this.step(\", \"maxSteps\"]) {\n  let i = 0, n = 0;\n  while ((i = s.indexOf(needle, i)) !== -1 && n < 4) {\n    if (i > 4000000) { console.log(needle, i, s.slice(i-80, i+200)); console.log(); }\n    i += needle.length; n++;\n  }\n}\n'","description":"Find physics fixed-step accumulator logic"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":969,"output_tokens":548,"cache_read_input_tokens":68352,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"e66c744d-7fb8-4c9a-ae92-7c64fb114e16"}
