{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_236","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The `clearQueued` method only clears `this.queued`, not `wasPressed`.\n\nThe pause frame's fixedUpdate runs before update freezes the game, so playT advances one tick during tap(). Pause detection will move to the start of fixed() to prevent that step. Physics.update receives dt=0 when timeScale is 0, so fixedUpdate is skipped on subsequent frames; the guard in fixed() is redundant for those frames if the accumulator lacks leftover time.\n\nThe default step delta is 1/60. The pause frame adds exactly one tick before update freezes the scale, so fixedUpdate runs once on that frame. Catching pause at the start of that call prevents playT from advancing. The frozen flag handles any tiny float error that might trigger a second step.\n\nThe pause check now lives at the very start of `fixed()`. It returns immediately if the game is already frozen or timeScale is zero, so the first pause on a normal frame fires before any physics step.\n\nThe pause check stays in `update()` too. Live play can have variable frame times, so fixedUpdate might not run on a given frame even when the accumulator should step. Both paths guard against double pauses: if fixed() already opened the menu, update() sees the pause mode and skips its own call.\n\nThe pause menu refresh during fixedUpdate is harmless before update draws. The dot stays at its original x position because playT does not advance. Resuming works correctly: the menu frame runs while timeScale is zero, then update restores normal speed and the next step advances playT. Dev mode entry from the pause menu also works since update handles it when fixedUpdate is skipped. The simulation stepping is gated to prevent a step immediately after opening the pause menu.\n\nThe week test already calls `boot(host)`, which loads the game and steps the engine twice. The mode menu still appears with rows for week, dropin, family, settings, and about. This suggests the boot process may not be fully skipping the initial menu as expected.\n\nThe mode menu still appearing after boot is puzzling. loadGame might not finish replacing the old world before step(2) runs, so the engine could be stepping the previous hub session instead of the new title. But choose uses the new app's state, so that theory seems unlikely.\n\nThe new app's mode might be stuck in menu if the engine still holds the old world. The constructor should reveal the default mode when session is null. Another possibility is that the new game's initial two steps advance it from title to menu without any input.\n\nThe error confirms the new app is already in menu mode after boot. setDriver does not change mode. The initial title should survive two idle steps, so the cause of the premature menu transition is still unclear.\n\nThe error explicitly shows the main menu rows, not the title screen. If the constructor default were title, the failure would read \"no row start in title.\" This confirms the fresh app is somehow entering menu mode before the test even calls choose. The next step is to find what code sets the mode to menu.\n\nThe hub end handler was considered as a possible source of the menu mode, but it was ruled out because the old app is discarded and the new one should start in title. A loadGame replacement bug was also dismissed since that would leave the fresh app in title mode. The possibility that the week test's boot call is never reached was raised.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7051054c-35b8-4632-a1be-0e2c55aec95b-33","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/app.js","offset":100,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7051054c-35b8-4632-a1be-0e2c55aec95b-34","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"hubEnded|mode = 'menu'|go\\('menu'\\)|hubStop|case 'end'","glob":"**/{app.js,main.js,world.js}"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1291,"output_tokens":1814,"cache_read_input_tokens":77696,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"1427f955-8903-4d15-814e-64e38b5e56be"}
