{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_307","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I will check build.mjs to locate the HTML and exit-interview output paths. This will let me verify the suite results quickly.\n\nThe first testing feedback sentence is very long. The screen only shows two wrapped lines of 40 characters each, while the full text goes to exit-interview.json. I should check if the node test checks feedback length and fails on this long answer.\n\nThe About screen only displays the first two wrapped lines of each feedback item. A 400-character answer would show roughly 80 characters, so a verifier checking the HUD would miss most of the content.\n\nI will restructure the feedback answers to fit within 40 characters each. This prevents truncation on the About screen and removes the need for the two-line slice.\n\nShortening the answers would make them too brief. The better fix is to change the About renderer to page through wrapped lines instead of dropping text. Each feedback entry can be one screenful of wrapped lines, and the existing arrow keys will let the verifier scroll through them.\n\nI will pre-wrap each feedback answer into chunks of six lines or fewer. Each line must stay under 40 characters so the About screen can display it fully without truncation.\n\nThe first feedback answer is roughly 450 characters, which needs two pages of six lines each. I will restructure aboutPages to split long answers into wrapped chunks of six lines or fewer before the build runs.\n\nThe suite is already running. Node tests will finish in about fifteen seconds, so I must update aboutPages now to beat the build. If the build finishes first, I will rebuild afterward. I am also checking wrapText and font character width.\n\nThe draw function wraps text to 40 characters on wide screens and 26 on narrow ones. Pre-wrapping at 26 would make lines too short on large displays. Pre-wrapping at 40 would still hide overflow because the renderer only shows six wrapped lines per page. The existing paging system cannot reveal extra wrapped lines, so splitting long feedback answers into multiple pages is unavoidable.\n\nI will wrap each feedback answer at 26 characters and split the results into pages of six lines. A helper function chunks the wrapped lines into pages so the About screen can display every word without truncation.\n\nI need to import wrapText into about.js. The current node assertions will not be affected by this change, but if the build has already started, the HTML will be stale and the test log will reflect it. I must save the file before build.mjs runs.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b1a81b3f-48b0-4a8c-978f-444b64b85282-144","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/data/about.js","offset":70,"limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b1a81b3f-48b0-4a8c-978f-444b64b85282-145","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/ui/font.js","limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":462,"output_tokens":1817,"cache_read_input_tokens":200960,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"9a64a72c-3324-4aca-b8c8-51c62826dafa"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-b1a81b3f-48b0-4a8c-978f-444b64b85282-144","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"70→\\n/** Pages for the in-game screen. Built only from the fields above. */\\nexport function aboutPages(creditsText) {\\n  const src = SOURCE_INFORMATION;\\n  const pages = [\\n    { title: 'A note', lines: [MEDICAL] },\\n    {\\n      title: 'Source Information',\\n      lines: [\\n        `Date: ${src.date}`,\\n80→        `Source: ${src.source}`,\\n        `Plan: ${src.plan}`,\\n        `Genre: ${src.genre}`,\\n        `Perspective: ${src.perspective}`,\\n        `Tech: ${src.tech}`,\\n        `Art Direction: ${src.artDirection}`,\\n        `Animation: ${src.animation}`,\\n        `Audio: ${src.audio}`,\\n        `Online: ${src.online}`,\\n        `Testing: ${src.testing}`,\\n90→        `Research: ${src.research}`,\\n        `Environment: ${src.environment}`,\\n        `Model: ${src.model}`,\\n        `Usage: ${src.usage}`,\\n      ],\\n    },\\n    { title: 'Testing Feedback', lines: TESTING_FEEDBACK.map((t, i) => `${i + 1}. ${t}`) },\\n    { title: 'Engine Feedback', lines: ENGINE_FEEDBACK.map((t, i) => `${i + 1}. ${t}`) },\\n    { title: 'Prompt Feedback', lines: PROMPT_FEEDBACK.map((t, i) => `${i + 1}. ${t}`) },\\n    { title: 'Kit credits', lines: [KIT_CREDITS, 'Kenney, three.js, Rapier, and Sweetie 16.'] },\\n100→  ];\\n  const full = String(creditsText || '').split(/\\\\r?\\\\n/);\\n  const size = 8;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < full.length; i += size) {\\n    pages.push({ title: i === 0 ? 'Credits' : 'Credits', lines: full.slice(i, i + size) });\\n  }\\n  return pages;\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"70→\\n/** Pages for the in-game screen. Built only from the fields above. */\\nexport function aboutPages(creditsText) {\\n  const src = SOURCE_INFORMATION;\\n  const pages = [\\n    { title: 'A note', lines: [MEDICAL] },\\n    {\\n      title: 'Source Information',\\n      lines: [\\n        `Date: ${src.date}`,\\n80→        `Source: ${src.source}`,\\n        `Plan: ${src.plan}`,\\n        `Genre: ${src.genre}`,\\n        `Perspective: ${src.perspective}`,\\n        `Tech: ${src.tech}`,\\n        `Art Direction: ${src.artDirection}`,\\n        `Animation: ${src.animation}`,\\n        `Audio: ${src.audio}`,\\n        `Online: ${src.online}`,\\n        `Testing: ${src.testing}`,\\n90→        `Research: ${src.research}`,\\n        `Environment: ${src.environment}`,\\n        `Model: ${src.model}`,\\n        `Usage: ${src.usage}`,\\n      ],\\n    },\\n    { title: 'Testing Feedback', lines: TESTING_FEEDBACK.map((t, i) => `${i + 1}. ${t}`) },\\n    { title: 'Engine Feedback', lines: ENGINE_FEEDBACK.map((t, i) => `${i + 1}. ${t}`) },\\n    { title: 'Prompt Feedback', lines: PROMPT_FEEDBACK.map((t, i) => `${i + 1}. ${t}`) },\\n    { title: 'Kit credits', lines: [KIT_CREDITS, 'Kenney, three.js, Rapier, and Sweetie 16.'] },\\n100→  ];\\n  const full = String(creditsText || '').split(/\\\\r?\\\\n/);\\n  const size = 8;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < full.length; i += size) {\\n    pages.push({ title: i === 0 ? 'Credits' : 'Credits', lines: full.slice(i, i + size) });\\n  }\\n  return pages;\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/data/about.js\",\"offset\":70,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"\\n/** Pages for the in-game screen. Built only from the fields above. */\\nexport function aboutPages(creditsText) {\\n  const src = SOURCE_INFORMATION;\\n  const pages = [\\n    { title: 'A note', lines: [MEDICAL] },\\n    {\\n      title: 'Source Information',\\n      lines: [\\n        `Date: ${src.date}`,\\n        `Source: ${src.source}`,\\n        `Plan: ${src.plan}`,\\n        `Genre: ${src.genre}`,\\n        `Perspective: ${src.perspective}`,\\n        `Tech: ${src.tech}`,\\n        `Art Direction: ${src.artDirection}`,\\n        `Animation: ${src.animation}`,\\n        `Audio: ${src.audio}`,\\n        `Online: ${src.online}`,\\n        `Testing: ${src.testing}`,\\n        `Research: ${src.research}`,\\n        `Environment: ${src.environment}`,\\n        `Model: ${src.model}`,\\n        `Usage: ${src.usage}`,\\n      ],\\n    },\\n    { title: 'Testing Feedback', lines: TESTING_FEEDBACK.map((t, i) => `${i + 1}. ${t}`) },\\n    { title: 'Engine Feedback', lines: ENGINE_FEEDBACK.map((t, i) => `${i + 1}. ${t}`) },\\n    { title: 'Prompt Feedback', lines: PROMPT_FEEDBACK.map((t, i) => `${i + 1}. ${t}`) },\\n    { title: 'Kit credits', lines: [KIT_CREDITS, 'Kenney, three.js, Rapier, and Sweetie 16.'] },\\n  ];\\n  const full = String(creditsText || '').split(/\\\\r?\\\\n/);\\n  const size = 8;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < full.length; i += size) {\\n    pages.push({ title: i === 0 ? 'Credits' : 'Credits', lines: full.slice(i, i + size) });\\n  }\\n  return pages;\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":107}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-b1a81b3f-48b0-4a8c-978f-444b64b85282-145","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→// Mixed case on a 6px grid. Lowercase is drawn as sprites. Everything else uses hud.text.\\nconst H = {\\n  a: '00 00 0e 01 0f 11 0f 00 00', b: '10 10 1e 11 11 11 1e 00 00', c: '00 00 0e 11 10 11 0e 00 00', d: '01 01 0f 11 11 11 0f 00 00',\\n  e: '00 00 0e 11 1f 10 0e 00 00', f: '06 09 08 1c 08 08 08 00 00', g: '00 00 0f 11 11 11 0f 01 0e', h: '10 10 1e 11 11 11 11 00 00',\\n  i: '04 00 0c 04 04 04 0e 00 00', j: '02 00 06 02 02 02 02 12 0c', k: '10 10 12 14 18 14 12 00 00', l: '0c 04 04 04 04 04 0e 00 00',\\n  m: '00 00 1a 15 15 15 15 00 00', n: '00 00 1e 11 11 11 11 00 00', o: '00 00 0e 11 11 11 0e 00 00', p: '00 00 1e 11 11 11 1e 10 10',\\n  q: '00 00 0f 11 11 11 0f 01 01', r: '00 00 16 19 10 10 10 00 00', s: '00 00 0f 10 0e 01 1e 00 00', t: '08 08 1c 08 08 09 06 00 00',\\n  u: '00 00 11 11 11 13 0d 00 00', v: '00 00 11 11 11 0a 04 00 00', w: '00 00 11 11 15 15 0a 00 00', x: '00 00 11 0a 04 0a 11 00 00',\\n  y: '00 00 11 11 11 11 0f 01 0e', z: '00 00 1f 02 04 08 1f 00 00',\\n10→};\\n\\nexport const GLYPHS = Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(H).map(([k, v]) => [k, v.split(' ').map((h) => parseInt(h, 16).toString(2).padStart(5, '0').replace(/0/g, '.').replace(/1/g, 'o'))]));\\n\\n/** Characters hud.text can draw, plus the lowercase sprites above. */\\nexport const HUD_EXTRA = \\\"ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789.,!?'\\\\\\\": :;-()/+%*\\\";\\n\\nexport function hasGlyph(ch) {\\n  if (ch === ' ' || ch === '\\\\n') return true;\\n  if (GLYPHS[ch]) return true;\\n20→  return HUD_EXTRA.includes(ch);\\n}\\n\\nexport function missingGlyphs(text) {\\n  const bad = [];\\n  for (const ch of String(text)) if (!hasGlyph(ch)) bad.push(ch);\\n  return bad;\\n}\\n\\nexport function say(hud, x, y, text, { color = 'white', shadow = 'ink', scale = 1 } = {}) {\\n30→  for (const ch of String(text)) {\\n    const g = GLYPHS[ch];\\n    if (g) hud.sprite(x, y, g, { o: color }, { scale, shadow });\\n    else if (ch !== ' ') hud.text(x, y, hasGlyph(ch) ? ch : '?', { color, shadow, scale });\\n    x += 6 * scale;\\n  }\\n  return x;\\n}\\n\\nexport function measureText(text, scale = 1) {\\n40→  return { width: String(text).length * 6 * scale, height: 9 * scale };\",\"content_concise\":\"1→// Mixed case on a 6px grid. Lowercase is drawn as sprites. Everything else uses hud.text.\\nconst H = {\\n  a: '00 00 0e 01 0f 11 0f 00 00', b: '10 10 1e 11 11 11 1e 00 00', c: '00 00 0e 11 10 11 0e 00 00', d: '01 01 0f 11 11 11 0f 00 00',\\n  e: '00 00 0e 11 1f 10 0e 00 00', f: '06 09 08 1c 08 08 08 00 00', g: '00 00 0f 11 11 11 0f 01 0e', h: '10 10 1e 11 11 11 11 00 00',\\n  i: '04 00 0c 04 04 04 0e 00 00', j: '02 00 06 02 02 02 02 12 0c', k: '10 10 12 14 18 14 12 00 00', l: '0c 04 04 04 04 04 0e 00 00',\\n  m: '00 00 1a 15 15 15 15 00 00', n: '00 00 1e 11 11 11 11 00 00', o: '00 00 0e 11 11 11 0e 00 00', p: '00 00 1e 11 11 11 1e 10 10',\\n  q: '00 00 0f 11 11 11 0f 01 01', r: '00 00 16 19 10 10 10 00 00', s: '00 00 0f 10 0e 01 1e 00 00', t: '08 08 1c 08 08 09 06 00 00',\\n  u: '00 00 11 11 11 13 0d 00 00', v: '00 00 11 11 11 0a 04 00 00', w: '00 00 11 11 15 15 0a 00 00', x: '00 00 11 0a 04 0a 11 00 00',\\n  y: '00 00 11 11 11 11 0f 01 0e', z: '00 00 1f 02 04 08 1f 00 00',\\n10→};\\n\\nexport const GLYPHS = Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(H).map(([k, v]) => [k, v.split(' ').map((h) => parseInt(h, 16).toString(2).padStart(5, '0').replace(/0/g, '.').replace(/1/g, 'o'))]));\\n\\n/** Characters hud.text can draw, plus the lowercase sprites above. */\\nexport const HUD_EXTRA = \\\"ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789.,!?'\\\\\\\": :;-()/+%*\\\";\\n\\nexport function hasGlyph(ch) {\\n  if (ch === ' ' || ch === '\\\\n') return true;\\n  if (GLYPHS[ch]) return true;\\n20→  return HUD_EXTRA.includes(ch);\\n}\\n\\nexport function missingGlyphs(text) {\\n  const bad = [];\\n  for (const ch of String(text)) if (!hasGlyph(ch)) bad.push(ch);\\n  return bad;\\n}\\n\\nexport function say(hud, x, y, text, { color = 'white', shadow = 'ink', scale = 1 } = {}) {\\n30→  for (const ch of String(text)) {\\n    const g = GLYPHS[ch];\\n    if (g) hud.sprite(x, y, g, { o: color }, { scale, shadow });\\n    else if (ch !== ' ') hud.text(x, y, hasGlyph(ch) ? ch : '?', { color, shadow, scale });\\n    x += 6 * scale;\\n  }\\n  return x;\\n}\\n\\nexport function measureText(text, scale = 1) {\\n40→  return { width: String(text).length * 6 * scale, height: 9 * scale };\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/ui/font.js\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"// Mixed case on a 6px grid. Lowercase is drawn as sprites. Everything else uses hud.text.\\nconst H = {\\n  a: '00 00 0e 01 0f 11 0f 00 00', b: '10 10 1e 11 11 11 1e 00 00', c: '00 00 0e 11 10 11 0e 00 00', d: '01 01 0f 11 11 11 0f 00 00',\\n  e: '00 00 0e 11 1f 10 0e 00 00', f: '06 09 08 1c 08 08 08 00 00', g: '00 00 0f 11 11 11 0f 01 0e', h: '10 10 1e 11 11 11 11 00 00',\\n  i: '04 00 0c 04 04 04 0e 00 00', j: '02 00 06 02 02 02 02 12 0c', k: '10 10 12 14 18 14 12 00 00', l: '0c 04 04 04 04 04 0e 00 00',\\n  m: '00 00 1a 15 15 15 15 00 00', n: '00 00 1e 11 11 11 11 00 00', o: '00 00 0e 11 11 11 0e 00 00', p: '00 00 1e 11 11 11 1e 10 10',\\n  q: '00 00 0f 11 11 11 0f 01 01', r: '00 00 16 19 10 10 10 00 00', s: '00 00 0f 10 0e 01 1e 00 00', t: '08 08 1c 08 08 09 06 00 00',\\n  u: '00 00 11 11 11 13 0d 00 00', v: '00 00 11 11 11 0a 04 00 00', w: '00 00 11 11 15 15 0a 00 00', x: '00 00 11 0a 04 0a 11 00 00',\\n  y: '00 00 11 11 11 11 0f 01 0e', z: '00 00 1f 02 04 08 1f 00 00',\\n};\\n\\nexport const GLYPHS = Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(H).map(([k, v]) => [k, v.split(' ').map((h) => parseInt(h, 16).toString(2).padStart(5, '0').replace(/0/g, '.').replace(/1/g, 'o'))]));\\n\\n/** Characters hud.text can draw, plus the lowercase sprites above. */\\nexport const HUD_EXTRA = \\\"ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789.,!?'\\\\\\\": :;-()/+%*\\\";\\n\\nexport function hasGlyph(ch) {\\n  if (ch === ' ' || ch === '\\\\n') return true;\\n  if (GLYPHS[ch]) return true;\\n  return HUD_EXTRA.includes(ch);\\n}\\n\\nexport function missingGlyphs(text) {\\n  const bad = [];\\n  for (const ch of String(text)) if (!hasGlyph(ch)) bad.push(ch);\\n  return bad;\\n}\\n\\nexport function say(hud, x, y, text, { color = 'white', shadow = 'ink', scale = 1 } = {}) {\\n  for (const ch of String(text)) {\\n    const g = GLYPHS[ch];\\n    if (g) hud.sprite(x, y, g, { o: color }, { scale, shadow });\\n    else if (ch !== ' ') hud.text(x, y, hasGlyph(ch) ? ch : '?', { color, shadow, scale });\\n    x += 6 * scale;\\n  }\\n  return x;\\n}\\n\\nexport function measureText(text, scale = 1) {\\n  return { width: String(text).length * 6 * scale, height: 9 * scale };\\n\",\"total_lines\":63}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"sess