st.exit\\\" 2>/dev/null || echo MISSING; echo \\\"=== test.log tail ===\\\"; tail -c 4000 \\\"$SCRATCH/test.log\\\" 2>/dev/null || echo NOLOG; echo \\\"=== browser.log FAIL/tail ===\\\"; rg -n \\\"FAIL|PASS|error|rms|hover\\\" \\\"$SCRATCH/browser.log\\\" 2>/dev/null | tail -80; echo \\\"=== ps ===\\\"; ps -ef | rg -n \\\"test.mjs|chromium|webkit|firefox\\\" | rg -v rg | head -30\",\"truncated\":false,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Check suite status, logs, and browsers\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3%2Fwork/01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469/terminal/call-12b2ff03-3fdd-4416-81ae-2f155de6da11-1.log\",\"total_bytes\":11705}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"c4104ad3-d7e1-4f1e-a4d7-1222be848522"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_310","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All 12 tests passed. Now determining the next steps.\n\nAbout screen truncation needs fixing so all Source fields, feedback, kit credits, and the medical sentence are visible by paging the HUD. Then rebuild HTML and exit-interview.json to match about.js, write PROGRESS.md, flip checklist boxes, and add a Deviations section.\n\nThe aboutPages() function packs all 15 Source fields onto one page, so later sections and long feedback are hidden. The node test only checks concatenated strings, not the drawn HUD. I will restructure aboutPages() to emit chunks of at most six pre-wrapped lines, or change the draw logic to show every wrapped piece of the current page.\n\nThe green browser run's evidence remains valid because only about-text changes are involved. I will fix the about paging so every HUD element is visible, then rebuild and verify that node tests still pass.\n\nRebuilding with build.mjs will sync HTML and exit-interview.json. A node check will confirm pages stay short enough to avoid truncation. Re-running the full browser suite is unnecessary because only about-text changed.\n\nA new node test will simulate the draw constraints—six lines and two 40-column wraps—and assert that every source field appears in the visible text. The plan is to fix about.js so pages pre-wrap to fit those limits, add this test, run --fast, and rebuild HTML.\n\nI will inspect the code before finalizing the about fix. I also need to kill any lingering watcher and clear leftover Chromium processes from the previous suite run.\n\nA GPU process at 99% CPU is a leftover browser from the suite. I will check parent PIDs to confirm it belongs to our run before killing it, and leave the unrelated Nov04 processes untouched.\n\nI will read STAGE.md, TASK.md, and PLAN.md to verify the exact hand-in requirements. I also need to inspect the draw function, about.js, and test.mjs assertions before finalizing the fix. The monitor has already fired DONE, so I will kill it if it is still running.\n\nThe verifier will rebuild the HTML after the about change, so a full suite rerun is unnecessary. A targeted headless check of the about screen will confirm every field is visible.\n\nA quick file:// boot of the rebuilt HTML is needed to confirm the bundle still works. Node tests import source files directly, so they cannot catch bundle or exit-interview parsing errors. The hand-in HTML must be verified independently.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The full suite finished clean: `12/12 passed`, hover moved focus, and the voice check cleared the loudness line. Next I’ll make the About screen actually show every source field, then write the hand-in."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bcfbb0c4-4147-4c8e-9ac1-f6d78b019743-2","name":"todo_write","input":{"todos":[{"id":"7","content":"Fix About HUD so every source field and the full feedback are visible, then rebuild","status":"in_progress"},{"id":"8","content":"Hand in exit-interview.json, PROGRESS.md, checklist and deviations","status":"pending"}],"merge":true}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bcfbb0c4-4147-4c8e-9ac1-f6d78b019743-3","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"aboutPages|slice\\(0, 6\\)|wrapText|SOURCE_INFORMATION|about page","glob":"*.{js,mjs}","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bcfbb0c4-4147-4c8e-9ac1-f6d78b019743-4","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"About|Source Information|exit-interview|PROGRESS","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/TASK.md"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7485,"output_tokens":2353,"cache_read_input_tokens":32256,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","u