:0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"7e2332ea-7071-4f74-a2e4-2c207c7f93ae"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-9a3c425c-f4f0-46d8-8660-5f5b8a142640-5","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/** One source for the About screen and exit-interview.json. */\\n\\nexport const MEDICAL = 'This is not medical advice. Ounce is a scale.';\\n\\nexport const SOURCE_INFORMATION = {\\n  date: '2026-11-04 22:16:07',\\n  source: 'Wii Fit',\\n  plan: 'PLAN.md',\\n  genre: 'Sports',\\n10→  perspective: 'Isometric island, with a fixed camera for each activity',\\n  tech: 'Pixel Engine 0.46.0, three.js r186, Rapier 0.20 as bundled, esbuild 0.28.2',\\n  artDirection: 'The engine native pixel look, with new models for the scale, stations, and props',\\n  animation: 'Engine ClipDefs compiled onto the hero rig and played with AnimationMixer',\\n  audio: 'Engine Song and SoundDef data, plus a Web Audio formant voice. Music defaults to 10 percent.',\\n  online: 'AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, own card, 1 to 4 players. Family Hour is local on one screen.',\\n  testing: 'node tools/test.mjs, Playwright 1.63 Chromium with the five software WebGPU flags, WebKit and Firefox for the missing-WebGPU path, and the engine headless runner',\\n  research: 'The director plan already included engine and hub research and spikes. I read PLAN.md, the engine guide where the recipes pointed, and the hub README, and I checked the Dot table in code. I did not do extra research on the source beyond that plan.',\\n  environment: 'Grok CLI (headless); Linux',\\n  model: 'xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh',\\n20→  usage: 'added on import',\\n};\\n\\nexport const TESTING_FEEDBACK = [\\n  'Nine issues. The expert pier jump scored two stars, pause let the pose clock move on the frame the button went down, two songs had uneven pattern lengths, a tray board lookup named a variable that was not in scope, a few model parts floated, the seagull was spoken as the scale, a dev-tool page could not go back, the prompt could draw past a short screen, and the scale\\\\'s voice measured just under the loudness line.',\\n  'Two were game-breaking. The pier jump sat under the three-star line until takeoff recentred the dot, and the pose kept playing for one frame after pause. The others failed a data check, a voice check, or a menu, and they were fixed before the hand-in.',\\n  'The most helpful test was the idle-versus-expert bot pass on every activity. It is what caught the pier jump sitting under the three-star line.',\\n  'The least helpful test was the glyph scan. Every line already used the allowed characters, so it passed on the first run and did not change the game.',\\n];\\n\\n30→export const ENGINE_FEEDBACK = [\\n  'Headless stepping, the pixel HUD, and a real input recorder made a week of play testable without a screen.',\\n  'I guessed wrong about pause. At timeScale 0 the headless stepper still calls fixedUpdate, and that call happens before update reads the pause key, so the pose clock moved unless the sim refused the step. Menu presses do still arrive. The type note reads as if those presses are dropped. Capture also needs all five Vulkan flags or the picture comes back blank.',\\n  'The centre-of-balance itself. The engine will move a character. It will not sway a polite dot, keep a week, or speak in formants.',\\n  'The hardest part was trusting the frame clock. Game time, the press window, and the hub clock are three different clocks, and only one of them is allowed to move a score.',\\n  'None. pixel-engine.js is the kit file, byte for byte.',\\n  'I would give the music bus a default of silence until the game sets it, so a shared browser profile cannot leave yesterday volume on today game.',\\n];\\n\\nexport const PROMPT_FEEDBACK = [\\n40→  'The plan named the mechanics, the sentences, and the tests, so the work was building a game rather than inventing one.',\\n  'The cut list in the plan and the instruction to finish everything on this computer disagree. I followed the instruction and shipped the activities the cut list would drop.',\\n  'The hardest piece was the pier jump star line. The same bot that holds a pose will dive off a dock, and the flight begins wherever the dot was left.',\\n  'I would ask for the pause rule in one sentence: timeScale 0, fixedUpdate silent, update still reads keys. The guide and the type comment do not say the same thing.',\\n];\\n\\nexport const AI_HUB = {\\n  name: 'Mint Dial',\\n  tagline: 'Keep the dot in the circle.',\\n  description: 'A week on a small island with a polite scale. Hold still, keep time, and try not to believe the number.',\\n50→  type: 'Game',\\n  genre: 'Sports',\\n  source: 'Wii Fit',\\n  series: 'Wii Fit',\\n  players: '1–4',\\n  controls: 'Left stick, WASD or mouse: lean. R2, Space or click: breathe. L1/R1, F/J or mouse buttons: step.',\\n  tags: ['pixel art', 'comedy', 'versus', 'arcade', '3d', 'story'],\\n};\\n\\nexport const KIT_CREDITS = 'Kenney (CC0), three.js (MIT), Rapier (Apache-2.0), Sweetie 16.';\\n60→\\nexport function exitInterview() {\\n  return {\\n    sourceInformation: { ...SOURCE_INFORMATION },\\n    testingFeedback: [...TESTING_FEEDBACK],\\n    engineFeedback: [...ENGINE_FEEDBACK],\\n    promptFeedback: [...PROMPT_FEEDBACK],\\n    aiHub: { ...AI_HUB, tags: [...AI_HUB.tags] },\\n  };\\n}\\n70→\\n/** Pages for the in-game screen. Built only from the fields above. */\\nexport function aboutPages(creditsText) {\\n  const src = SOURCE_INFORMATION;\\n  const pages = [\\n    { title: 'A note', lines: [MEDICAL] },\\n    {\\n      title: 'Source Information',\\n      lines: [\\n        `Date: ${src.date}`,\\n80→        `Source: ${src.source}`,\\n        `Plan: ${src.plan}`,\\n        `Genre: ${src.genre}`,\\n        `Perspective: ${src.perspective}`,\\n        `Tech: ${src.tech}`,\\n        `Art Direction: ${src.artDirection}`,\\n        `Animation: ${src.animation}`,\\n        `Audio: ${src.audio}`,\\n        `Online: ${src.online}`,\\n        `Testing: ${src.testing}`,\\n90→        `Research: ${src.research}`,\\n        `Environment: ${src.environment}`,\\n        `Model: ${src.model}`,\\n        `Usage: ${src.usage}`,\\n      ],\\n    },\\n    { title: 'Testing Feedback', lines: TESTING_FEEDBACK.map((t, i) => `${i + 1}. ${t}`) },\\n    { title: 'Engine Feedback', lines: ENGINE_FEEDBACK.map((t, i) => `${i + 1}. ${t}`) },\\n    { title: 'Prompt Feedback', lines: PROMPT_FEEDBACK.map((t, i) => `${i + 1}. ${t}`) },\\n    { title: 'Kit credits', lines: [KIT_CREDITS, 'Kenney, three.js, Rapier, and Sweetie 16.'] },\\n100→  ];\\n  const full = String(creditsText || '').split(/\\\\r?\\\\n/);\\n  const size = 8;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < full.length; i += size) {\\n    pages.push({ title: i === 0 ? 'Credits' : 'Credits', lines: full.slice(i, i + size) });\\n  }\\n  return pages;\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/** One source for the About screen and exit-interview.json. */\\n\\nexport const MEDICAL = 'This is not medical advice. Ounce is a scale.';\\n\\nexport const SOURCE_INFORMATION = {\\n  date: '2026-11-04 22:16:07',\\n  source: 'Wii Fit',\\n  plan: 'PLAN.md',\\n  genre: 'Sports',\\n10→  perspective: 'Isometric island, with a fixed camera for each activity',\\n  tech: 'Pixel Engine 0.46.0, three.js r186, Rapier 0.20 as bundled, esbuild 0.28.2',\\n  artDirection: 'The engine native pixel look, with new models for the scale, stations, and props',\\n  animation: 'Engine ClipDefs compiled onto the hero rig and played with AnimationMixer',\\n  audio: 'Engine Song and SoundDef data, plus a Web Audio formant voice. Music defaults to 10 percent.',\\n  online: 'AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, own card, 1 to 4 players. Family Hour is local on one screen.',\\n  testing: 'node tools/test.mjs, Playwright 1.63 Chromium with the five software WebGPU flags, WebKit and Firefox for the missing-WebGPU path, and the engine headless runner',\\n  research: 'The director plan already included engine and hub research and spikes. I read PLAN.md, the engine guide where the recipes pointed, and the hub README, and I checked the Dot table in code. I did not do extra research on the source beyond that plan.',\\n  environment: 'Grok CLI (headless); Linux',\\n  model: 'xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh',\\n20→  usage: 'added on import',\\n};\\n\\nexport const TESTING_FEEDBACK = [\\n  'Nine issues. The expert pier jump scored two stars, pause let the pose clock move on the frame the button went down, two songs had uneven pattern lengths, a tray board lookup named a variable that was not in scope, a few model parts floated, the seagull was spoken as the scale, a dev-tool page could not go back, the prompt could draw past a short screen, and the scale\\\\'s voice measured just under the loudness line.',\\n  'Two were game-breaking. The pier jump sat under the three-star line until takeoff recentred the dot, and the pose kept playing for one frame after pause. The others failed a data check, a voice check, or a menu, and they were fixed before the hand-in.',\\n  'The most helpful test was the idle-versus-expert bot pass on every activity. It is what caught the pier jump sitting under the three-star line.',\\n  'The least helpful test was the glyph scan. Every line already used the allowed characters, so it passed on the first run and did not change the game.',\\n];\\n\\n30→export const ENGINE_FEEDBACK = [\\n  'Headless stepping, the pixel HUD, and a real input recorder made a week of play testable without a screen.',\\n  'I guessed wrong about pause. At timeScale 0 the headless stepper still calls fixedUpdate, and that call happens before update reads the pause key, so the pose clock moved unless the sim refused the step. Menu presses do still arrive. The type note reads as if those presses are dropped. Capture also needs all five Vulkan flags or the picture comes back blank.',\\n  'The centre-of-balance itself. The engine will move a character. It will not sway a polite dot, keep a week, or speak in formants.',\\n  'The hardest part was trusting the frame clock. Game time, the press window, and the hub clock are three different clocks, and only one of them is allowed to move a score.',\\n  'None. pixel-engine.js is the kit file, byte for byte.',\\n  'I would give the music bus a default of silence until the game sets it, so a shared browser profile cannot leave yesterday volume on today game.',\\n];\\n\\nexport const PROMPT_FEEDBACK = [\\n40→  'The plan named the mechanics, the sentences, and the tests, so the work was building a game rather than inventing one.',\\n  'The cut list in the plan and the instruction to finish everything on this computer disagree. I followed the instruction and shipped the activities the cut list would drop.',\\n  'The hardest piece was the pier jump star line. The same bot that holds a pose will dive off a dock, and the flight begins wherever the dot was left.',\\n  'I would ask for the pause rule in one sentence: timeScale 0, fixedUpdate silent, update still reads keys. The guide and the type comment do not say the same thing.',\\n];\\n\\nexport const AI_HUB = {\\n  name: 'Mint Dial',\\n  tagline: 'Keep the dot in the circle.',\\n  description: 'A week on a small island with a polite scale. Hold still, keep time, and try not to believe the number.',\\n50→  type: 'Game',\\n  genre: 'Sports',\\n  source: 'Wii Fit',\\n  series: 'Wii Fit',\\n  players: '1–4',\\n  controls: 'Left stick, WASD or mouse: lean. R2, Space or click: breathe. L1/R1, F/J or mouse buttons: step.',\\n  tags: ['pixel art', 'comedy', 'versus', 'arcade', '3d', 'story'],\\n};\\n\\nexport const KIT_CREDITS = 'Kenney (CC0), three.js (MIT), Rapier (Apache-2.0), Sweetie 16.';\\n60→\\nexport function exitInterview() {\\n  return {\\n    sourceInformation: { ...SOURCE_INFORMATION },\\n    testingFeedback: [...TESTING_FEEDBACK],\\n    engineFeedback: [...ENGINE_FEEDBACK],\\n    promptFeedback: [...PROMPT_FEEDBACK],\\n    aiHub: { ...AI_HUB, tags: [...AI_HUB.tags] },\\n  };\\n}\\n70→\\n/** Pages for the in-game screen. Built only from the fields above. */\\nexport function aboutPages(creditsText) {\\n  const src = SOURCE_INFORMATION;\\n  const pages = [\\n    { title: 'A note', lines: [MEDICAL] },\\n    {\\n      title: 'Source Information',\\n      lines: [\\n        `Date: ${src.date}`,\\n80→        `Source: ${src.source}`,\\n        `Plan: ${src.plan}`,\\n        `Genre: ${src.genre}`,\\n        `Perspective: ${src.perspective}`,\\n        `Tech: ${src.tech}`,\\n        `Art Direction: ${src.artDirection}`,\\n        `Animation: ${src.animation}`,\\n        `Audio: ${src.audio}`,\\n        `Online: ${src.online}`,\\n        `Testing: ${src.testing}`,\\n90→        `Research: ${src.research}`,\\n        `Environment: ${src.environment}`,\\n        `Model: ${src.model}`,\\n        `Usage: ${src.usage}`,\\n      ],\\n    },\\n    { title: 'Testing Feedback', lines: TESTING_FEEDBACK.map((t, i) => `${i + 1}. ${t}`) },\\n    { title: 'Engine Feedback', lines: ENGINE_FEEDBACK.map((t, i) => `${i + 1}. ${t}`) },\\n    { title: 'Prompt Feedback', lines: PROMPT_FEEDBACK.map((t, i) => `${i + 1}. ${t}`) },\\n    { title: 'Kit credits', lines: [KIT_CREDITS, 'Kenney, three.js, Rapier, and Sweetie 16.'] },\\n100→  ];\\n  const full = String(creditsText || '').split(/\\\\r?\\\\n/);\\n  const size = 8;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < full.length; i += size) {\\n    pages.push({ title: i === 0 ? 'Credits' : 'Credits', lines: full.slice(i, i + size) });\\n  }\\n  return pages;\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/data/about.js\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"/** One source for the About screen and exit-interview.json. */\\n\\nexport const MEDICAL = 'This is not medical advice. Ounce is a scale.';\\n\\nexport const SOURCE_INFORMATION = {\\n  date: '2026-11-04 22:16:07',\\n  source: 'Wii Fit',\\n  plan: 'PLAN.md',\\n  genre: 'Sports',\\n  perspective: 'Isometric island, with a fixed camera for each activity',\\n  tech: 'Pixel Engine 0.46.0, three.js r186, Rapier 0.20 as bundled, esbuild 0.28.2',\\n  artDirection: 'The engine native pixel look, with new models for the scale, stations, and props',\\n  animation: 'Engine ClipDefs compiled onto the hero rig and played with AnimationMixer',\\n  audio: 'Engine Song and SoundDef data, plus a Web Audio formant voice. Music defaults to 10 percent.',\\n  online: 'AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, own card, 1 to 4 players. Family Hour is local on one screen.',\\n  testing: 'node tools/test.mjs, Playwright 1.63 Chromium with the five software WebGPU flags, WebKit and Firefox for the missing-WebGPU path, and the engine headless runner',\\n  research: 'The director plan already included engine and hub research and spikes. I read PLAN.md, the engine guide where the recipes pointed, and the hub README, and I checked the Dot table in code. I did not do extra research on the source beyond that plan.',\\n  environment: 'Grok CLI (headless); Linux',\\n  model: 'xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh',\\n  usage: 'added on import',\\n};\\n\\nexport const TESTING_FEEDBACK = [\\n  'Nine issues. The expert pier jump scored two stars, pause let the pose clock move on the frame the button went down, two songs had uneven pattern lengths, a tray board lookup named a variable that was not in scope, a few model parts floated, the seagull was spoken as the scale, a dev-tool page could not go back, the prompt could draw past a short screen, and the scale\\\\'s voice measured just under the loudness line.',\\n  'Two were game-breaking. The pier jump sat under the three-star line until takeoff recentred the dot, and the pose kept playing for one frame after pause. The others failed a data check, a voice check, or a menu, and they were fixed before the hand-in.',\\n  'The most helpful test was the idle-versus-expert bot pass on every activity. It is what caught the pier jump sitting under the three-star line.',\\n  'The least helpful test was the glyph scan. Every line already used the allowed characters, so it passed on the first run and did not change the game.',\\n];\\n\\nexport const ENGINE_FEEDBACK = [\\n  'Headless stepping, the pixel HUD, and a real input recorder made a week of play testable without a screen.',\\n  'I guessed wrong about pause. At timeScale 0 the headless stepper still calls fixedUpdate, and that call happens before update reads the pause key, so the pose clock moved unless the sim refused the step. Menu presses do still arrive. The type note reads as if those presses are dropped. Capture also needs all five Vulkan flags or the picture comes back blank.',\\n  'The centre-of-balance itself. The engine will move a character. It will not sway a polite dot, keep a week, or speak in formants.',\\n  'The hardest part was trusting the frame clock. Game time, the press window, and the hub clock are three different clocks, and only one of them is allowed to move a score.',\\n  'None. pixel-engine.js is the kit file, byte for byte.',\\n  'I would give the music bus a default of silence until the game sets it, so a shared browser profile cannot leave yesterday volume on today game.',\\n];\\n\\nexport const PROMPT_FEEDBACK = [\\n  'The plan named the mechanics, the sentences, and the tests, so the work was building a game rather than inventing one.',\\n  'The cut list in the plan and the instruction to finish everything on this computer disagree. I followed the instruction and shipped the activities the cut list would drop.',\\n  'The hardest piece was the pier jump star line. The same bot that holds a pose will dive off a dock, and the flight begins wherever the dot was left.',\\n  'I would ask for the pause rule in one sentence: timeScale 0, fixedUpdate silent, update still reads keys. The guide and the type comment do not say the same thing.',\\n];\\n\\nexport const AI_HUB = {\\n  name: 'Mint Dial',\\n  tagline: 'Keep the dot in the circle.',\\n  description: 'A week on a small island with a polite scale. Hold still, keep time, and try not to believe the number.',\\n  type: 'Game',\\n  genre: 'Sports',\\n  source: 'Wii Fit',\\n  series: 'Wii Fit',\\n  players: '1–4',\\n  controls: 'Left stick, WASD or mouse: lean. R2, Space or click: breathe. L1/R1, F/J or mouse buttons: step.',\\n  tags: ['pixel art', 'comedy', 'versus', 'arcade', '3d', 'story'],\\n};\\n\\nexport const KIT_CREDITS = 'Kenney (CC0), three.js (MIT), Rapier (Apache-2.0), Sweetie 16.';\\n\\nexport function exitInterview() {\\n  return {\\n    sourceInformation: { ...SOURCE_INFORMATION },\\n    testingFeedback: [...TESTING_FEEDBACK],\\n    engineFeedback: [...ENGINE_FEEDBACK],\\n    promptFeedback: [...PROMPT_FEEDBACK],\\n    aiHub: { ...AI_HUB, tags: [...AI_HUB.tags] },\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n/** Pages for the in-game screen. Built only from the fields above. */\\nexport function aboutPages(creditsText) {\\n  const src = SOURCE_INFORMATION;\\n  const pages = [\\n    { title: 'A note', lines: [MEDICAL] },\\n    {\\n      title: 'Source Information',\\n      lines: [\\n        `Date: ${src.date}`,\\n        `Source: ${src.source}`,\\n        `Plan: ${src.plan}`,\\n        `Genre: ${src.genre}`,\\n        `Perspective: ${src.perspective}`,\\n        `Tech: ${src.tech}`,\\n        `Art Direction: ${src.artDirection}`,\\n        `Animation: ${src.animation}`,\\n        `Audio: ${src.audio}`,\\n        `Online: ${src.online}`,\\n        `Testing: ${src.testing}`,\\n        `Research: ${src.research}`,\\n        `Environment: ${src.environment}`,\\n        `Model: ${src.model}`,\\n        `Usage: ${src.usage}`,\\n      ],\\n    },\\n    { title: 'Testing Feedback', lines: TESTING_FEEDBACK.map((t, i) => `${i + 1}. ${t}`) },\\n    { title: 'Engine Feedback', lines: ENGINE_FEEDBACK.map((t, i) => `${i + 1}. ${t}`) },\\n    { title: 'Prompt Feedback', lines: PROMPT_FEEDBACK.map((t, i) => `${i + 1}. ${t}`) },\\n    { title: 'Kit credits', lines: [KIT_CREDITS, 'Kenney, three.js, Rapier, and Sweetie 16.'] },\\n  ];\\n  const full = String(creditsText || '').split(/\\\\r?\\\\n/);\\n  const size = 8;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < full.length; i += size) {\\n    pages.push({ title: i === 0 ? 'Credits' : 'Credits', lines: full.slice(i, i + size) });\\n  }\\n  return pages;\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":107}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-9a3c425c-f4f0-46d8-8660-5f5b8a142640-6","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1480→    y = line(view, 'ready', 'Enter ready', y, 1, 'sand');\\n  } else {\\n    const title = heading(app);\\n    y = line(view, 'head', title, y, scale, 'cyan');\\n  }\\n  if (app.mode === 'activity' || app.mode === 'weigh' || app.mode === 'attract') {\\n    y = line(view, 'phase', phaseLine(app), y, 1, 'sand');\\n    drawPips(view, app.mode === 'activity' ? (app.sim?.stars || 0) : 0, m, h - m - 10);\\n  }\\n  if (app.mode === 'results') {\\n1490→    y = line(view, 'act', ACTIVITY_BY_ID[app.activityId]?.name || '', y, 1, 'white');\\n    const bits = wrapText(app.dialogue || '', 52).slice(0, 3);\\n    bits.forEach((part, i) => { y = line(view, `line-${i}`, part, y, 1, 'sand'); });\\n    y = line(view, 'drips', `Drips ${app.lastDrips}`, y, scale, 'cyan');\\n    drawPips(view, app.lastStars, m, y);\\n    y += 16;\\n  }\\n  if (app.mode === 'reveal' && app.guest?.chart?.length) {\\n    const last = app.guest.chart[app.guest.chart.length - 1];\\n    y = line(view, 'age', String(last.shown), y, titleScale, 'white');\\n1500→    y = line(view, 'felt', wrapText(app.guest.felt || 'Noted.', 40)[0], y, 1, 'sand');\\n  }\\n  if (app.mode === 'report' && app.guest) {\\n    const last = app.guest.chart[app.guest.chart.length - 1];\\n    y = line(view, 'age', last ? String(last.shown) : '--', y, titleScale, 'white');\\n    const info = dayInfo(app.guest.day);\\n    y = line(view, 'concern', wrapText(`Concern: ${info.concern}`, 40)[0], y, 1, 'sand');\\n  }\\n  if (app.mode === 'confession') {\\n    y = line(view, 'sorry', 'I have been adding seven.', y, 1, 'sand');\\n1510→  }\\n  if (app.mode === 'hammock') {\\n    const guilt = app.guest?.today?.plays ? 'Rest. The day is filed.' : 'The hammock kept the day. The jar did not.';\\n    y = line(view, 'guilt', guilt, y, 1, 'sand');\\n  }\\n  if (app.mode === 'jar' && app.guest) {\\n    y = line(view, 'jar-n', String(app.guest.drips), y, titleScale, 'cyan');\\n    for (const item of milestonesReached(app.guest.drips).slice(0, 4)) y = line(view, item.id, item.name, y, 1, 'white');\\n  }\\n  if (app.mode === 'hall' && app.guest) {\\n1520→    const last = app.guest.chart[app.guest.chart.length - 1];\\n    y = line(view, 'hall-n', last ? String(last.shown) : '--', y, titleScale, 'white');\\n  }\\n  if (app.mode === 'about') {\\n    const pages = aboutPages(CREDITS_TEXT);\\n    const page = pages[Math.min(app.aboutPage, pages.length - 1)];\\n    y = line(view, 'about-h', page.title, y, scale, 'cyan');\\n    page.lines.slice(0, 6).forEach((text, i) => {\\n      const bits = wrapText(text, narrow ? 26 : 40).slice(0, 2);\\n      bits.forEach((part, j) => { y = line(view, `about-${i}-${j}`, part, y, 1, 'white'); });\\n1530→    });\\n  }\\n  if (app.mode === 'howto') {\\n    y = line(view, 'how1', 'Lean to keep the dot in the circle.', y, 1, 'white');\\n    y = line(view, 'how2', 'Breathe on the beat. Step on the beat.', y, 1, 'sand');\\n  }\\n  if (app.mode === 'medley' || app.mode === 'podium') {\\n    app.lanes.forEach((lane, i) => {\\n      y = line(view, `lane-${i}`, `${lane.kind} ${Math.round(app.laneTotal(lane))}`, y, 1, 'white');\\n    });\\n1540→  }\\n  if (app.mode === 'join') {\\n    app.seats.forEach((seat, i) => {\\n      y = line(view, `seat-${i}`, seat ? `${i + 1} ${seat.kind}` : `${i + 1} empty`, y, 1, 'sand');\\n    });\\n  }\\n  if (app.overlay) y = line(view, 'overlay', app.status().slice(0, 48), y, 1, 'lime');\\n  const rows = app.rows;\\n  const rowScale = scale;\\n  const rowH = 9 * rowScale + 6;\\n1550→  let ry = Math.min(y + 8, h - m - rows.length * rowH);\\n  if (ry < m) ry = m;\\n  rows.forEach((row, i) => {\\n    const mark = i === app.focus ? '> ' : '  ';\\n    const text = `${mark}${row.label}`.slice(0, narrow ? 28 : 36);\\n    const width = measureText(text, rowScale).width;\\n    const x = m;\\n    if (ry + rowH <= h) {\\n      app.widget(`row-${row.id}`, x, ry, Math.min(width, w - m * 2), 9 * rowScale);\\n      say(hud, x, ry, text, { scale: rowScale, color: i === app.focus ? 'sand' : 'white' });\\n1560→    }\\n    ry += rowH;\\n  });\\n  const prompt = app.state().prompt;\\n  const py = h - m - 9;\\n  if (py > 0 && py + 9 <= h) {\\n    const pw = Math.min(measureText(prompt, 1).width, Math.max(1, w - m));\\n    app.widget('prompt', m, py, pw, 9);\\n    say(hud, m, py, prompt, { scale: 1, color: 'mist' });\\n  }\\n1570→  if (app.mode === 'title') {\\n    const medical = wrapText(MEDICAL, narrow ? 26 : 46)[0];\\n    say(hud, m, h - m - 20, medical, { scale: 1, color: 'mist' });\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nfunction line(view, id, text, y, scale, color) {\\n  const { hud, app, w, h } = view;\\n  const m = marginOf(w);\\n  const shown = String(text || '').slice(0, 52);\\n1580→  if (!shown || y > h - 8) return y;\\n  const width = measureText(shown, scale).width;\\n  let x = Math.max(m, Math.floor((w - width) / 2));\\n  if (x + width > w - 2) x = m;\\n  app.widget(id, x, y, Math.min(width, w - x), 9 * scale);\\n  say(hud, x, y, shown, { scale, color });\\n  return y + 9 * scale + 3;\\n}\\n\\nfunction drawPips(view, stars, x, y) {\\n1590→  const { hud, app } = view;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) {\\n    hud.rect(x + i * 10, y, 7, 7, i < stars ? 'sand' : 'slate');\\n  }\\n  app.widget('stars', x, y, 28, 7);\\n}\\n\\nfunction heading(app) {\\n  if (app.mode === 'menu') return 'Mint Dial';\\n  if (app.mode === 'weigh') return 'Weigh in';\",\"content_concise\":\"1480→    y = line(view, 'ready', 'Enter ready', y, 1, 'sand');\\n  } else {\\n    const title = heading(app);\\n    y = line(view, 'head', title, y, scale, 'cyan');\\n  }\\n  if (app.mode === 'activity' || app.mode === 'weigh' || app.mode === 'attract') {\\n    y = line(view, 'phase', phaseLine(app), y, 1, 'sand');\\n    drawPips(view, app.mode === 'activity' ? (app.sim?.stars || 0) : 0, m, h - m - 10);\\n  }\\n  if (app.mode === 'results') {\\n1490→    y = line(view, 'act', ACTIVITY_BY_ID[app.activityId]?.name || '', y, 1, 'white');\\n    const bits = wrapText(app.dialogue || '', 52).slice(0, 3);\\n    bits.forEach((part, i) => { y = line(view, `line-${i}`, part, y, 1, 'sand'); });\\n    y = line(view, 'drips', `Drips ${app.lastDrips}`, y, scale, 'cyan');\\n    drawPips(view, app.lastStars, m, y);\\n    y += 16;\\n  }\\n  if (app.mode === 'reveal' && app.guest?.chart?.length) {\\n    const last = app.guest.chart[app.guest.chart.length - 1];\\n    y = line(view, 'age', String(last.shown), y, titleScale, 'white');\\n1500→    y = line(view, 'felt', wrapText(app.guest.felt || 'Noted.', 40)[0], y, 1, 'sand');\\n  }\\n  if (app.mode === 'report' && app.guest) {\\n    const last = app.guest.chart[app.guest.chart.length - 1];\\n    y = line(view, 'age', last ? String(last.shown) : '--', y, titleScale, 'white');\\n    const info = dayInfo(app.guest.day);\\n    y = line(view, 'concern', wrapText(`Concern: ${info.concern}`, 40)[0], y, 1, 'sand');\\n  }\\n  if (app.mode === 'confession') {\\n    y = line(view, 'sorry', 'I have been adding seven.', y, 1, 'sand');\\n1510→  }\\n  if (app.mode === 'hammock') {\\n    const guilt = app.guest?.today?.plays ? 'Rest. The day is filed.' : 'The hammock kept the day. The jar did not.';\\n    y = line(view, 'guilt', guilt, y, 1, 'sand');\\n  }\\n  if (app.mode === 'jar' && app.guest) {\\n    y = line(view, 'jar-n', String(app.guest.drips), y, titleScale, 'cyan');\\n    for (const item of milestonesReached(app.guest.drips).slice(0, 4)) y = line(view, item.id, item.name, y, 1, 'white');\\n  }\\n  if (app.mode === 'hall' && app.guest) {\\n1520→    const last = app.guest.chart[app.guest.chart.length - 1];\\n    y = line(view, 'hall-n', last ? String(last.shown) : '--', y, titleScale, 'white');\\n  }\\n  if (app.mode === 'about') {\\n    const pages = aboutPages(CREDITS_TEXT);\\n    const page = pages[Math.min(app.aboutPage, pages.length - 1)];\\n    y = line(view, 'about-h', page.title, y, scale, 'cyan');\\n    page.lines.slice(0, 6).forEach((text, i) => {\\n      const bits = wrapText(text, narrow ? 26 : 40).slice(0, 2);\\n      bits.forEach((part, j) => { y = line(view, `about-${i}-${j}`, part, y, 1, 'white'); });\\n1530→    });\\n  }\\n  if (app.mode === 'howto') {\\n    y = line(view, 'how1', 'Lean to keep the dot in the circle.', y, 1, 'white');\\n    y = line(view, 'how2', 'Breathe on the beat. Step on the beat.', y, 1, 'sand');\\n  }\\n  if (app.mode === 'medley' || app.mode === 'podium') {\\n    app.lanes.forEach((lane, i) => {\\n      y = line(view, `lane-${i}`, `${lane.kind} ${Math.round(app.laneTotal(lane))}`, y, 1, 'white');\\n    });\\n1540→  }\\n  if (app.mode === 'join') {\\n    app.seats.forEach((seat, i) => {\\n      y = line(view, `seat-${i}`, seat ? `${i + 1} ${seat.kind}` : `${i + 1} empty`, y, 1, 'sand');\\n    });\\n  }\\n  if (app.overlay) y = line(view, 'overlay', app.status().slice(0, 48), y, 1, 'lime');\\n  const rows = app.rows;\\n  const rowScale = scale;\\n  const rowH = 9 * rowScale + 6;\\n1550→  let ry = Math.min(y + 8, h - m - rows.length * rowH);\\n  if (ry < m) ry = m;\\n  rows.forEach((row, i) => {\\n    const mark = i === app.focus ? '> ' : '  ';\\n    const text = `${mark}${row.label}`.slice(0, narrow ? 28 : 36);\\n    const width = measureText(text, rowScale).width;\\n    const x = m;\\n    if (ry + rowH <= h) {\\n      app.widget(`row-${row.id}`, x, ry, Math.min(width, w - m * 2), 9 * rowScale);\\n      say(hud, x, ry, text, { scale: rowScale, color: i === app.focus ? 'sand' : 'white' });\\n1560→    }\\n    ry += rowH;\\n  });\\n  co