{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_315","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The credits text is enormous. It is mostly one unbroken paragraph per model pack. The current chunking logic breaks it into 8-line segments.\n\nThe full license text would span hundreds of pages and remain unreadable on the HUD. The acceptance criteria require only the TASK.md Source Information, Testing / Engine / Prompt Feedback, kit credits, and a specific sentence. Kit credits are Kenney (CC0), three.js (MIT), Rapier (Apache-2.0), and Sweetie 16.\n\nThe node test validates source fields from concatenated strings rather than rendered output. The current draw logic drops source fields after the first six lines and truncates feedback at two wrapped lines. The fix is to rewrite aboutPages to emit pages of at most N visual lines, pre-wrapped to 26 columns for the narrow HUD.\n\nThe player-facing credits should list only the kit names and GrafxKid. The full license dump is too long for the HUD. I need to check PLAN.md to confirm dropping it is not a regression. If I keep CREDITS_TEXT in the page generator, it will produce over two hundred pages at 26 columns by six lines. ArrowRight can still scroll through them.\n\nThe page order should be: the medical sentence, then all source information fields, then testing and engine feedback, then the short kit credits. The full license text can follow but must not block access to earlier sections. It also contains characters outside the available glyph set.\n\nUnknown characters will render as question marks, which is acceptable. The HUD layout at 640×360 yields a 427×240 viewport. Margins consume 12 pixels on each side. The \"About\" title scales to 30 pixels tall. \"Source Information\" scales to 21 pixels tall. Body text renders at 12 pixels per line.\n\nThe About screen layout fits six body lines inside the 427×240 HUD viewport. The title and heading scale to y=42 and y=63, leaving enough vertical space for the menu row and prompt text.\n\nThe 240-pixel viewport is safe even with the title scaled to 4. The About screen layout fits within the HUD height in both cases. Extra pages during navigation simply repeat the last page.\n\nThe About screen currently offers only a Back button. Mouse users cannot page through multi-page content without a keyboard. I will add Next and Previous rows so mouse and controller users can navigate between pages.\n\nThe Next and Previous rows will use 26-column wrapping so each line stays one row. The activate handler must be checked to ensure Next increments the page index. Three menu rows still fit within six body lines. The attract mode About screen is unchanged. A chunk function using COLS and ROWS constants is being drafted.\n\nThe chunk function wraps each paragraph to 26 columns, then groups the resulting lines into pages of six. Each page title appends its number after the first. The \"Source Information\" heading at scale 2 is 216 pixels wide, which fits comfortably inside the 427-pixel HUD viewport.\n\nPre-wrapping at 26 columns ensures every visual line stays under the 52-character draw limit. Each line wraps to exactly one piece, so nothing is dropped. Empty paragraphs still produce a single empty string.\n\nEmpty strings are falsy, so `line()` skips them and they do not consume a row. The page count would diverge from the visible rows if blank lines were emitted. The full credits file is over 50,000 characters, which would produce roughly 350 pages.\n\nThe test only checks that source fields appear in the joined pages, not that the full credits text is rendered. The About screen will show the short kit credit line and omit the lengthy license text.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e1d40a86-856a-4bce-ac5a-d7f5ab3a6b88-19","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"[Cc]redit|About","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/PLAN.md","head_limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e1d40a86-856a-4bce-ac5a-d7f5ab3a6b88-20","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/app.js","offset":1100,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e1d40a86-856a-4bce-ac5a-d7f5ab3a6b88-21","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/app.js","offset":540,"limit":100}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":15039,"output_tokens":2388,"cache_read_input_tokens":57344,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"ad586d30-71c4-4dc0-8e55-995a342307b3"}
