lse if (id === 'about') { this.aboutPage = 0; this.mode = 'about'; }\"},{\"line_number\":790,\"content\":\"    if (id === 'about') { this.aboutPage = 0; this.mode = 'about'; this.refresh(true); return; }\"},{\"line_number\":1153,\"content\":\"    if (this.mode === 'about' && (this.edge(ctx, 'ArrowRight') || this.edge(ctx, 'PadR1'))) this.aboutPage += 1;\"},{\"line_number\":1154,\"content\":\"    if (this.mode === 'about' && (this.edge(ctx, 'ArrowLeft') || this.edge(ctx, 'PadL1'))) this.aboutPage = Math.max(0, this.aboutPage - 1);\"},{\"line_number\":1224,\"content\":\"    this.widgets.forEach((w, i) => {\"},{\"line_number\":1350,\"content\":\"    this.widgets.push({ id, x, y, w, h });\"},{\"line_number\":1398,\"content\":\"      widgets: this.widgets.map((w) => ({ ...w })),\"},{\"line_number\":1433,\"content\":\"    this.widgets = [];\"},{\"line_number\":1524,\"content\":\"    const pages = aboutPages(CREDITS_TEXT);\"},{\"line_number\":1525,\"content\":\"    const page = pages[Math.min(app.aboutPage, pages.length - 1)];\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"f90a54f2-f1d8-41de-aef8-13c83c94cce6"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_318","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"CREDITS.md is very large because it contains extensive model lists and the Apache license.\n\nThe draw bug drops source fields 7-15 and truncates feedback. Reordering the pages so important content appears before the large credits dump fixes this. The pagination logic is the critical fix.\n\nPre-wrapping at 26 columns prevents line() from dropping text. Each page will contain at most six lines, so slicing to six keeps all content visible. The draw function may also stop slicing to two lines as a safety measure.\n\nRemoving the draw limit entirely would risk overflow if paging breaks. The limit stays, but pages must be guaranteed to fit. Testing that every source value appears in the simulated draw is difficult because widgets only store rectangles and not drawn text.\n\nA `visibleAbout` helper will simulate the exact draw constraints by slicing pages to six lines, wrapping to 26 columns, and truncating each line to 52 characters. Tests can then assert that every source value appears in the resulting visible text.\n\nPre-wrapping text across lines breaks simple substring checks. A value like \"I read PLAN.md\" could split into \"I read\" and \"PLAN.md\" across separate lines, so `includes` would fail on the joined wrapped string. Joining wrapped lines with spaces instead of newlines would reconstruct the original text, making the test reliable.\n\nThe visible text helper is being implemented as a flatMap chain that slices pages to six lines, wraps each line to 26 columns, truncates to two lines, and slices each fragment to 52 characters. Joining the reconstructed words with spaces preserves original spacing and word order, so substring checks remain valid. A date string is being checked for exact 26-character width.\n\nThe date string is 25 characters wide, fitting within the 26-column limit. Source, plan, and genre fields also fit easily. The wrapText function splits on whitespace and rejoins with single spaces, so joining reconstructed lines with spaces preserves the original text exactly.\n\nThe medical disclaimer wraps across two lines at 26 columns. Joining the reconstructed fragments with spaces still yields the original intact sentence.\n\nTests will verify that every page has at most six lines and each line is at most 26 characters wide. The reconstructed visible text must still contain every source field, feedback answer, and a substantial unique phrase from the full credits file.\n\nA simpler test strategy is being considered. Instead of reconstructing the full visible text, the plan is to squash both the visible output and the source strings by collapsing whitespace. Then it checks that every source value, feedback answer, and a key credits phrase like \"Kenney\" appear as contiguous substrings in the squashed visible text. This avoids slow word-order verification while still confirming all content is reachable.\n\nThe glyph issue is visual only. The font cannot draw certain symbols, so the screen renders them as question marks instead of dropping characters from the underlying strings. Verifying that the full credits text appears in the squashed visible output remains a valid acceptance check.\n\nThe font supports most ASCII characters, including letters, digits, and common punctuation. Symbols like #, `, _, [ ], @, and © are missing from the glyph set, so they render as question marks. URLs and model names containing these symbols will appear with question marks instead of the original characters. The MIT license text is largely readable because it uses only allowed characters.\n\nThe draw function will drop its extra line and character truncation. The aboutPages array will enforce the six-line limit, so any page that accidentally exceeds it gets clipped silently by the y > h - 8 check. Tests will verify this invariant.\n\nThe draw function keeps its line and character truncation limits as a safety net, with a comment explaining that tests mirror these constraints. Page titles were checked against HUD widths: at 427 pixels the title scales to 216 pixels, and at smaller widths it scales to 108 pixels. Six lines fit vertically on the smallest widget test canvas.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-25890db1-e757-40bc-aa59-578e0b1a03cc-28","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"refresh\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/app.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-25890db1-e757-40bc-aa59-578e0b1a03cc-29","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/app.js","offset":200,"limit":50}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":11390,"output_tokens":2292,"cache_read_input_tokens":81408,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"4a0106f2-dc7a-45af-9548-0e543dd0c1fc"}
