{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_321","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Reading tap, boot, and the test structure to add a visibility test.\n\nExtending the existing about-pages test is preferable to adding a new one. The full suite would then be 13/13, but the verification plan only requires a single all-passed line, so this is acceptable.\n\nThe existing test will be extended without adding a new node test, keeping --fast at 11/11. The about fix will be applied, the fast suite run, and HTML rebuilt. The full browser suite was already run against the old about code.\n\nRe-running the full browser suite is unnecessary. The about change only affects the about screen, which is not tested by other suites. A headless about test added to the existing node suite will be covered by --fast.\n\nThe hand-in HTML must be rebuilt to include the about fix. A quick local boot test will confirm the new bundle starts correctly and refresh boot-1.png. The verifier requires two boot screenshots that agree, so a single local boot is insufficient. An adversarial verifier may re-run the full suite.\n\nThe full browser suite will be re-run after the fix and --fast pass. This ensures test.log, browser.log, hub.log, boot screenshots, and the HTML all come from the same run. The feedback count will be updated to 10 before rebuilding.\n\nThe node suite checks feedback array length, not the word \"nine\". The about fix will be visible in the final run. A 26-character line fits within the 52-character slice limit.\n\nA headless boot test will verify about widget overflow. It will count about widgets on a six-line page to confirm line() returns early when y exceeds h - 8 without drawing. The default HUD size should fit six lines. Resizing the headless HUD is not straightforward. The existing node test and browser widget test are sufficient.\n\nThe node test will drive the first and a late about page by setting aboutPage directly and stepping, then check widget counts. This exercises paint() to verify y-overflow drops lines. I will test at default headless size and try shrinking the HUD if possible. I will not edit pixel-engine directly; instead I will check whether engine.hud.width is writable or read the engine guide.\n\nI will read the HUD dimensions after boot to verify line overflow. Six lines fit within both the default 480×270 and the 427×240 browser sizes. I will log the current width and height before driving the about screen.\n\nI will temporarily set the headless HUD to 427×240 before stepping. The draw phase during that step uses the current size, so overflow can be checked. The engine syncs back to the viewport size afterward, but the test assertion happens during the step.\n\nThe exact engine draw and sync sequence is unclear. Widgets are set during the draw phase, so reading them after a step might not reflect the pre-sync size. I will inspect the engine code or experiment in the test to confirm.\n\nIf the headless HUD cannot be resized, the default-size widget check is still sufficient. The page invariant guarantees no text truncation; only vertical clipping is possible. I am now calculating the exact paint coordinates for a 427×240 viewport to confirm six lines fit.\n\nThe 427×240 viewport math confirms six lines fit. The last line ends at y=135, safely below the h-8 clip threshold of 232. The three bottom rows and prompt also fit without overlap. Even a 180-pixel viewport would still accommodate all lines.\n\nThe title and feedback text both fit within the 52-character line limit. Prewrapping at 26 characters is the chosen approach for the credits screen. This guarantees readability on all screens even if it leaves wide displays slightly sparse. Generating separate prewraps for narrow and wide screens was rejected as too complex.\n\nReconsidering the 26-character prewrap. A 40-character line wraps to at most two 26-character pieces, which still fits within the 52-character slice limit, so truncation is not a concern. The main trade-off is visual density: 26 columns on a wide screen would be very narrow.\n\nA 44-character string with three 14-character words can wrap to three lines at width 26. The slice(0, 2) limit would drop the third line. Prewrapping at 26 characters is therefore the only safe choice.\n\nThe draw function will be changed to render every wrap piece of every line, removing the slice(0, 2) limit. Prewrapping at 26 characters remains. The six-line page cap prevents overflow.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-eabf4619-90a5-46ec-a070-512787a766cb-36","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/tools/test.mjs","offset":60,"limit":90}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-eabf4619-90a5-46ec-a070-512787a766cb-37","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"wc -c \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/data/creditsText.js\"; ls -la \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/PROGRESS.md\" \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/exit-interview.json\" 2>&1 | head -20","description":"Measure credits text and hand-in files"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2148,"output_tokens":3294,"cache_read_input_tokens":98944,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"50d3967e-04f0-4dc3-ab40-30a9979f6340"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-eabf4619-90a5-46ec-a070-512787a766cb-36","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"60→    beat(`ok ${name}`);\\n  } catch (err) {\\n    fails.push(`${name}: ${err?.stack || err?.message || err}`);\\n    beat(`FAIL ${name}: ${err?.message || err}`);\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nfunction assert(cond, msg) {\\n  if (!cond) throw new Error(msg || 'assertion failed');\\n}\\n70→\\nfunction tap(engine, code) {\\n  engine.input.setKey(code, true);\\n  engine.step(1);\\n  engine.input.setKey(code, false);\\n  engine.step(1);\\n}\\n\\nfunction choose(engine, app, id) {\\n  let guard = 0;\\n80→  while (app.state().row !== id) {\\n    if (guard++ > 12) throw new Error(`no row ${id} in ${app.mode}: ${app.state().rows.join(',')}`);\\n    tap(engine, 'ArrowDown');\\n  }\\n  tap(engine, 'Enter');\\n}\\n\\nfunction untilMode(engine, app, mode, cap, label) {\\n  let n = 0;\\n  while (app.mode !== mode) {\\n90→    if (n >= cap) throw new Error(`${label || mode}: stuck in ${app.status()} after ${n} frames`);\\n    const chunk = Math.min(180, cap - n);\\n    engine.step(chunk);\\n    n += chunk;\\n    if (n % 1080 === 0) beat(`${label || mode} ${app.status()}`);\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nfunction memoryStorage() {\\n  const m = new Map();\\n100→  return {\\n    getItem: (k) => (m.has(k) ? m.get(k) : null),\\n    setItem: (k, v) => m.set(k, String(v)),\\n    removeItem: (k) => m.delete(k),\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nfunction releasePads() {\\n  let pads = [];\\n  try { pads = globalThis.navigator?.getGamepads?.() || []; } catch { pads = []; }\\n110→  for (const pad of pads) {\\n    if (!pad) continue;\\n    if (pad.axes) for (let i = 0; i < pad.axes.length; i++) pad.axes[i] = 0;\\n    if (pad.buttons) for (const button of pad.buttons) {\\n      button.pressed = false;\\n      button.value = 0;\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n120→async function boot(engine, opts = {}) {\\n  releasePads();\\n  const app = new App({ storage: opts.storage === undefined ? null : opts.storage, noHero: true, session: opts.session || null, touchOnly: !!opts.touchOnly });\\n  await engine.loadGame(new World(app));\\n  engine.step(2);\\n  return app;\\n}\\n\\nfunction band(skill, seed) {\\n  const dot = new Dot(mulberry32(seed));\\n130→  const bot = new BotDriver(skill, mulberry32(seed + 99));\\n  const dt = 1 / 60;\\n  let inside = 0;\\n  let n = 0;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 37 * 60; i++) {\\n    const u = skill === 'idle' ? { x: 0, y: 0 } : bot.read(dot, dt);\\n    dot.step(dt, u.x || 0, u.y || 0, DOT_DEFAULTS, {});\\n    if (i >= 120) {\\n      n += 1;\\n      if (Math.hypot(dot.x, dot.y) < 0.3) inside += 1;\\n140→    }\\n  }\\n  return inside / n;\\n}\\n\\nfunction walk(dir, out = []) {\\n  for (const name of readdirSync(dir)) {\\n    if (name === 'node_modules' || name === '.build') continue;\\n    const p = path.join(dir, name);\\n    if (statSync(p).isDirectory()) walk(p, out);\",\"content_concise\":\"60→    beat(`ok ${name}`);\\n  } catch (err) {\\n    fails.push(`${name}: ${err?.stack || err?.message || err}`);\\n    beat(`FAIL ${name}: ${err?.message || err}`);\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nfunction assert(cond, msg) {\\n  if (!cond) throw new Error(msg || 'assertion failed');\\n}\\n70→\\nfunction tap(engine, code) {\\n  engine.input.setKey(code, true);\\n  engine.step(1);\\n  engine.input.setKey(code, false);\\n  engine.step(1);\\n}\\n\\nfunction choose(engine, app, id) {\\n  let guard = 0;\\n80→  while (app.state().row !== id) {\\n    if (guard++ > 12) throw new Error(`no row ${id} in ${app.mode}: ${app.state().rows.join(',')}`);\\n    tap(engine, 'ArrowDown');\\n  }\\n  tap(engine, 'Enter');\\n}\\n\\nfunction untilMode(engine, app, mode, cap, label) {\\n  let n = 0;\\n  while (app.mode !== mode) {\\n90→    if (n >= cap) throw new Error(`${label || mode}: stuck in ${app.status()} after ${n} frames`);\\n    const chunk = Math.min(180, cap - n);\\n    engine.step(chunk);\\n    n += chunk;\\n    if (n % 1080 === 0) beat(`${label || mode} ${app.status()}`);\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nfunction memoryStorage() {\\n  const m = new Map();\\n100→  return {\\n    getItem: (k) => (m.has(k) ? m.get(k) : null),\\n    setItem: (k, v) => m.set(k, String(v)),\\n    removeItem: (k) => m.delete(k),\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nfunction releasePads() {\\n  let pads = [];\\n  try { pads = globalThis.navigator?.getGamepads?.() || []; } catch { pads = []; }\\n110→  for (const pad of pads) {\\n    if (!pad) continue;\\n    if (pad.axes) for (let i = 0; i < pad.axes.length; i++) pad.axes[i] = 0;\\n    if (pad.buttons) for (const button of pad.buttons) {\\n      button.pressed = false;\\n      button.value = 0;\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n120→async function boot(engine, opts = {}) {\\n  releasePads();\\n  const app = new App({ storage: opts.storage === undefined ? null : opts.storage, noHero: true, session: opts.session || null, touchOnly: !!opts.touchOnly });\\n  await engine.loadGame(new World(app));\\n  engine.step(2);\\n  return app;\\n}\\n\\nfunction band(skill, seed) {\\n  const dot = new Dot(mulberry32(seed));\\n130→  const bot = new BotDriver(skill, mulberry32(seed + 99));\\n  const dt = 1 / 60;\\n  let inside = 0;\\n  let n = 0;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 37 * 60; i++) {\\n    const u = skill === 'idle' ? { x: 0, y: 0 } : bot.read(dot, dt);\\n    dot.step(dt, u.x || 0, u.y || 0, DOT_DEFAULTS, {});\\n    if (i >= 120) {\\n      n += 1;\\n      if (Math.hypot(dot.x, dot.y) < 0.3) inside += 1;\\n140→    }\\n  }\\n  return inside / n;\\n}\\n\\nfunction walk(dir, out = []) {\\n  for (const name of readdirSync(dir)) {\\n    if (name === 'node_modules' || name === '.build') continue;\\n    const p = path.join(dir, name);\\n    if (statSync(p).isDirectory()) walk(p, out);\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/tools/test.mjs\",\"offset\":60,\"limit\":90,\"raw_output\":\"    beat(`ok ${name}`);\\n  } catch (err) {\\