{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_322","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"creditsText.js is 42KB. Wrapping it once and caching is sufficient.\n\nPage count is roughly 350. No import cycle exists between about.js and font.js. The About screen will keep only the first six lines of source fields, so later fields and long answers will be hidden. The feedback update will be precise.\n\nThe remaining issues failed data checks, voice checks, menus, or the About screen and were fixed before hand-in. The medical disclaimer on the title screen is 39 characters long.\n\nThe medical disclaimer is 45 characters long. It wraps to two lines at narrow widths but fits on one line in the normal HUD. The full sentence will appear on the title screen for all required viewports. The About screen will still display it.\n\nA headless test will step through all 350 About pages to verify no lines are clipped. Navigation will start from the title screen, select About, then tap Next on each page until the final page.\n\nThe headless test will verify Next activation and ArrowRight input. Each About page will be assigned directly to aboutPage for the widget-count sweep. Widgets are named about-i-j, with one widget per wrapped line. Empty lines are filtered out. Some markdown symbols may still register as text length.\n\nSkipped lines will be caught by the widget-count check. Widgets must also stay inside the HUD bounds, so the headless sweep will enforce a 427×240 viewport and verify widget positions. The attract timer is active during About paging because MENU_IDLE includes that state.\n\nStepping 350 frames without input would take about 6 seconds, safely under the 10-second attract timer. Boot and navigation already consume some of those frames.\n\nNavigation consumes roughly 14 frames before the sweep begins. The headless test will reset the idle timer inside the loop to prevent the attract screen from interrupting the 350-page check.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ba337894-21da-4b74-a370-d6ff2a903e06-38","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/app.js","offset":1320,"limit":90}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4483,"output_tokens":1512,"cache_read_input_tokens":100992,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"ff83ec59-f042-409e-b6df-3756428e8570"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-ba337894-21da-4b74-a370-d6ff2a903e06-38","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1320→    const score = this.hubScore || 0;\\n    const win = medleyWindow(Math.max(0, this.medleyT));\\n    try {\\n      this.hub.send({ a: win.index || 0, x: lane?.pos || 0, y: 0, c: 0, t: lane?.sim?.playT || 0, s: score }, { reliable: false });\\n      this.hub.progress({ score, label: 'Medley' });\\n    } catch { /* the round may already be over */ }\\n  }\\n\\n  hubResult() {\\n    if (this.resultSent || !this.hub) return;\\n1330→    this.resultSent = true;\\n    this.hubLive = false;\\n    try {\\n      this.hub.result({\\n        score: this.hubScore || 0,\\n        stats: { events: 3 },\\n        awards: [{ title: 'Stillest', detail: 'You stayed.' }],\\n      });\\n    } catch { /* already sent */ }\\n  }\\n1340→\\n  hubStop() {\\n    this.hubEnded = true;\\n    this.hubLive = false;\\n    if (this._hubTimer) clearInterval(this._hubTimer);\\n    this._hubTimer = null;\\n    try { this.engine?.audio?.stopMusic?.(); } catch { /* quiet */ }\\n  }\\n\\n  widget(id, x, y, w, h) {\\n1350→    this.widgets.push({ id, x, y, w, h });\\n  }\\n\\n  status() {\\n    if (this.mode === 'activity' && this.sim) {\\n      return `activity ${this.activityId} | ${this.sim.phase} | t ${this.sim.playT.toFixed(1)} | score ${Math.round(this.sim.score)}`;\\n    }\\n    if (this.mode === 'medley') return `medley | t ${this.medleyT.toFixed(1)} | score ${Math.round(this.hubScore || 0)}`;\\n    return `${this.mode} | day ${this.guest?.day || 0}`;\\n  }\\n1360→\\n  fingerprint() {\\n    const dot = this.sim?.dot || this.weigh?.dot;\\n    const x = dot ? dot.x.toFixed(4) : '0';\\n    const y = dot ? dot.y.toFixed(4) : '0';\\n    return `${this.mode}|${this.guest?.day || 0}|${Math.round(this.sim?.score || 0)}|${x},${y}`;\\n  }\\n\\n  state() {\\n    const row = this.rows[this.focus];\\n1370→    return {\\n      title: this.title,\\n      mode: this.mode,\\n      focus: this.focus,\\n      row: row?.id || '',\\n      rows: this.rows.map((r) => r.id),\\n      device: this.device.kind,\\n      glyphs: this.settings.glyphs,\\n      glyph: glyphKind(this.device.kind, this.settings.glyphs),\\n      prompt: promptFor(this.device.kind, this.settings.glyphs, this.mode === 'title' ? 'Start' : 'Confirm'),\\n1380→      touchOnly: this.touchOnly,\\n      touchMessage: this.touchOnly ? 'Controller or keyboard required' : '',\\n      music: this.busMusic,\\n      day: this.guest?.day || 0,\\n      week: this.guest?.week || 0,\\n      name: this.guest?.name || '',\\n      drips: this.guest?.drips || 0,\\n      stars: this.lastStars,\\n      score: this.lastScore,\\n      seconds: this.lastSeconds,\\n1390→      lastDrips: this.lastDrips,\\n      lastPrescription: this.lastPrescription,\\n      activity: this.activityId,\\n      confessed: !!this.guest?.confessed,\\n      chart: (this.guest?.chart || []).map((p) => ({ day: p.day, t: p.t, trueAge: p.trueAge, shown: p.shown })),\\n      items: this.guest?.items || [],\\n      tunables: { ...this.tunables },\\n      settings: { ...this.settings },\\n      widgets: this.widgets.map((w) => ({ ...w })),\\n      overlay: this.overlay,\\n1400→      god: this.god,\\n      driver: this.driver,\\n      attract: this.mode === 'attract',\\n      attractId: this.mode === 'attract' ? this.activityId : '',\\n      hideHud: this.hideHud,\\n      frozen: this.frozen,\\n      timeScale: this.engine?.timeScale,\\n      session: !!this.session,\\n      dialogue: this.dialogue,\\n      viewerClip: this.viewerClip,\",\"content_concise\":\"1320→    const score = this.hubScore || 0;\\n    const win = medleyWindow(Math.max(0, this.medleyT));\\n    try {\\n      this.hub.send({ a: win.index || 0, x: lane?.pos || 0, y: 0, c: 0, t: lane?.sim?.playT || 0, s: score }, { reliable: false });\\n      this.hub.progress({ score, label: 'Medley' });\\n    } catch { /* the round may already be over */ }\\n  }\\n\\n  hubResult() {\\n    if (this.resultSent || !this.hub) return;\\n1330→    this.resultSent = true;\\n    this.hubLive = false;\\n    try {\\n      this.hub.result({\\n        score: this.hubScore || 0,\\n        stats: { events: 3 },\\n        awards: [{ title: 'Stillest', detail: 'You stayed.' }],\\n      });\\n    } catch { /* already sent */ }\\n  }\\n1340→\\n  hubStop() {\\n    this.hubEnded = true;\\n    this.hubLive = false;\\n    if (this._hubTimer) clearInterval(this._hubTimer);\\n    this._hubTimer = null;\\n    try { this.engine?.audio?.stopMusic?.(); } catch { /* quiet */ }\\n  }\\n\\n  widget(id, x, y, w, h) {\\n1350→    this.widgets.push({ id, x, y, w, h });\\n  }\\n\\n  status() {\\n    if (this.mode === 'activity' && this.sim) {\\n      return `activity ${this.activityId} | ${this.sim.phase} | t ${this.sim.playT.toFixed(1)} | score ${Math.round(this.sim.score)}`;\\n    }\\n    if (this.mode === 'medley') return `medley | t ${this.medleyT.toFixed(1)} | score ${Math.round(this.hubScore || 0)}`;\\n    return `${this.mode} | day ${this.guest?.day || 0}`;\\n  }\\n1360→\\n  fingerprint() {\\n    const dot = this.sim?.dot || this.weigh?.dot;\\n    const x = dot ? dot.x.toFixed(4) : '0';\\n    const y = dot ? dot.y.toFixed(4) : '0';\\n    return `${this.mode}|${this.guest?.day || 0}|${Math.round(this.sim?.score || 0)}|${x},${y}`;\\n  }\\n\\n  state() {\\n    const row = this.rows[this.focus];\\n1370→    return {\\n      title: this.title,\\n      mode: this.mode,\\n      focus: this.focus,\\n      row: row?.id || '',\\n      rows: this.rows.map((r) => r.id),\\n      device: this.device.kind,\\n      glyphs: this.settings.glyphs,\\n      glyph: glyphKind(this.device.kind, this.settings.glyphs),\\n      prompt: promptFor(this.device.kind, this.settings.glyphs, this.mode === 'title' ? 'Start' : 'Confirm'),\\n1380→      touchOnly: this.touchOnly,\\n      touchMessage: this.touchOnly ? 'Controller or keyboard