{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_323","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Confirmed the aboutPages() call is a one-time operation, so large about pages won't slow the node test.\n\nThe new sweep steps run roughly 350 times. The credits text reconstruction joins characters to match expected output. The shownText function validates page line counts and text wrapping.\n\nThe shownText function returns joined text. Whitespace collapses identically to squash. Markdown and punctuation remain. Empty lines are filtered. The next concern is words longer than 26 characters.\n\nwrapText hard-splits words longer than 26 characters. Joining them with spaces would insert unwanted spaces inside the original word, so includes() would fail. A URL like \"kenney-castle/bridge-straight-pillar\" is 36 characters long and would be split into multiple lines.\n\nJoining wrapped lines with spaces or empty strings is too messy for hard-split words. A simpler approach is to assert against the original source values directly, squashing whitespace on each one.\n\nA simpler assertion is to concatenate all page lines with no separator and compare the whitespace-removed result against the original value. Hard-split words do not add characters, so the character streams match.\n\nThe implementation flattens all page lines into a single string, strips whitespace, and asserts that the result contains every source value, feedback string, and credit text.\n\nThe full credits text is preserved because trimming and whitespace removal on both sides cancel out. wrapText correctly strips leading and trailing spaces while keeping the word intact. The test will also verify that multiple pages exist and that source fields are not all placed on page zero.\n\nThe widget-counting test proves every line receives a widget, so separate page-count assertions are unnecessary. The 350-page estimate yields roughly 2,100 wrapped lines across six columns. Running 350 headless steps should take one to two seconds, which is acceptable. The background island simulation may still run during the menu world.\n\nThirty-five steps is six seconds of game time. If the physics engine slows the full sweep, only a few pages will be spot-checked instead of all three hundred fifty. The line and column limits plus the draw code prove correctness. Widget counts on a few representative pages are enough.\n\nSpot-checking will target five pages: the medical page, a page containing \"Usage\", a feedback page, a license page, and the final page. A helper function locates each target by searching joined lines for the needle. Some phrases may be split across wrapped lines.\n\nJoining wrapped lines with an empty string collapses spaces between words that were split across lines. For example, \"added on\" and \"import\" become \"added onimport\". The assertion must strip all whitespace from the joined text before checking for the original phrase.\n\nThe phrase \"added on import\" is short enough to fit on a single line, so it will be used as the search token for spot-checking pages. The widget test will target the page with six lines and draw it directly. Line lengths will be verified by the test itself.\n\nThe draw code and row layout need updating. Feedback text was checked for banned glyphs. Apostrophes and parentheses are safe because they fall within HUD_EXTRA and AI_HUB ranges. No exotic characters appear in the source text.\n\nUndisplayable glyphs in the full credits text will render as question marks. This is an engine font limit, not a deviation from the plan.\n\nThirty hundred pages would make the Next button tedious to hold down. The plan explicitly requires scrollable full text, so this is acceptable.\n\nArrowRight and Enter use edge-triggered input. They will not repeat unless the engine auto-repeats wasPressed.\n\nNo page number indicator will be added to the title row. The about menu resets to page zero when activated from pause, and pressing Next returns focus to the Next button. A single-page edge case is irrelevant because the credits text spans many pages. The aboutPage index will be clamped if the cached page count changes.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-43ef7c94-cdab-4789-a068-c4e42a43c8ff-39","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/tools/test.mjs","limit":50}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2568,"output_tokens":2236,"cache_read_input_tokens":105472,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"579a34cc-0718-447a-84ba-356960a86b2f"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-43ef7c94-cdab-4789-a068-c4e42a43c8ff-39","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * Drives the shipped game. Prints failures and one \\\"N/N passed\\\" line.\\n * From the dev folder: node tools/test.mjs [--fast]\\n */\\nimport { createHash } from 'node:crypto';\\nimport { execFileSync } from 'node:child_process';\\nimport { appendFileSync, mkdirSync, readFileSync, readdirSync, statSync } from 'node:fs';\\nimport path from 'node:path';\\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\\n10→import {\\n  Engine,\\n  HERO_RIG,\\n  analyzeClip,\\n  checkModel,\\n  compileClips,\\n  parseSong,\\n  validateClip,\\n  validateTexture,\\n} from '../pixel-engine.js';\\n20→import { App, freshGuest } from '../src/app.js';\\nimport { CAMERA, World } from '../src/scenes/world.js';\\nimport { ACTIVITIES, ACTIVITY_BY_ID } from '../src/data/activities.js';\\nimport { DAYS } from '../src/data/week.js';\\nimport { LINES, SAMPLES, allLineStrings, linesFor } from '../src/data/lines.js';\\nimport { SONGS, songLevel } from '../src/audio/songs.js';\\nimport { syllabify } from '../src/audio/voice.js';\\nimport { Dot, DOT_DEFAULTS } from '../src/core/dot.js';\\nimport { BotDriver } from '../src/core/drivers.js';\\nimport { mulberry32 } from '../src/core/rng.js';\\n30→import { dripsFor, milestonesReached, starsFor } from '../src/core/score.js';\\nimport { SAVE_KEY, Save } from '../src/core/save.js';\\nimport { DEFAULT_TUNABLES, TUNABLE_TABS, tabKeys } from '../src/core/tunables.js';\\nimport { missingGlyphs, wrapText } from '../src/ui/font.js';\\nimport { MODELS } from '../src/art/models.js';\\nimport { CLIPS } from '../src/art/clips.js';\\nimport { clinicTile } from '../src/art/textures.js';\\nimport { MEDICAL, SOURCE_INFORMATION, aboutPages, exitInterview } from '../src/data/about.js';\\nimport { CREDITS_TEXT } from '../src/data/creditsText.js';\\nimport { TITLE } from '..