{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_329","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The engine is minified into a few lines.\n\nA focused test will verify HUD size and whether the 6-line page fits. I'll rewrite the first two testing answers to be honest and plain.\n\nThe expert pier jump scored two stars. Pause let the pose clock advance on the button-down frame. Two songs had uneven pattern lengths. A tray board lookup referenced an out-of-scope variable. Several model parts floated. The seagull was spoken as the scale. A dev-tool page could not go back. The prompt could draw past a short screen. The scale voice measured just under the loudness line. Two issues were game-breaking: the pier jump sat under the three-star line until takeoff recentred the dot, and the pose kept playing for one frame after pause.\n\nThe first answer now lists ten issues. The remaining ones failed data, voice, or menu checks and were fixed before hand-in.\n\nThe About screen kept only the first six lines, so later source fields never appeared.\n\nThe About screen issue is confirmed. I will now edit the code: rewrite about.js, update paging and activation, replace simple page checks with stronger assertions, and add a drive.\n\nThe wrapText import in about.js is safe because font.js is standalone. The text-wrapping cache lives in the module, so tests and the game share it. A single call to aboutPages builds the cache, and the game reuses it during draw.\n\nThe page helper splits wrapped text into lines and groups them into pages of about six rows. It also handles empty paragraphs by pushing an empty page.\n\nEmpty credits will skip the empty-page push. The summary page imports CREDITS_SUMMARY from creditsText.js, which is separate from the full credits text that aboutPages receives.\n\nThe About screen will list Credits, Medical, Source Information, Testing, Engine, Prompt, and Kit Credits. The Kit Credits page will show a short summary of licenses followed by the full text.\n\nMedical will appear first in the About screen. Source information and feedback follow. The full license text is placed last so players see acceptance-critical content before the long list of model names. This prioritizes UX over the plan's suggested order.\n\nThe About screen will show five pages: medical note, source, testing/engine/prompt, kit credits summary, and full text. The draw loop will stop slicing lines so all text appears. A page index will be omitted to avoid overflow on narrow screens. Navigation rows are capped at three buttons with Next first, then Previous, then Back. KeyE will not confirm the About screen.\n\nKeyE activates the focused row on the About screen, matching Enter behavior. This is acceptable and not a bug.\n\nPadR1 pages are correctly excluded from the PRESS set. ArrowRight advances exactly one page, whether via the arrow key or the Next button, with no double advance. The refresh after an arrow press ensures the Next row disappears on the final page.\n\nFocus lands on Previous when the last page lacks a Next button. The CREDITS_TEXT import in app.js and the Engine import for the songs test are already present. A new test helper will filter widgets by their about- ID prefix to verify the screen draws.\n\nThe test helper asserts that every drawn widget fits inside the HUD bounds and that the number of rendered widgets matches the page line count. Because each page is capped at twenty-six lines, wrapping produces at most one piece per line, so the lengths align exactly. A clipped widget would reduce the drawn count below the line count and trigger a failure. The next step is to configure a small HUD for this test.\n\nThe test will shrink the HUD to 427 by 240, step once, and assert the About screen draws correctly. It will restore the original size afterward. The assertion will log the actual HUD dimensions. If the engine resets the size before drawing, the test still validates the default layout.\n\nA getter-based HUD resize is too hacky. I will inspect the engine via a quick script instead, then write the code and run a small node snippet to verify the About screen. I also need to kill leftover Chromium processes that are still running at high CPU, since they waste memory and could trigger earlyoom.\n\nI will check the parent process of a lingering Chromium instance while editing. The watcher monitor already reported completion, so I will kill it if it is still running to avoid waking me. I will review the goal plan end to find where to record deviations after tests pass. PROGRESS.md will be a concise log of built features and verification results, kept in the workspace root as required.\n\nI will wait for the final green run before writing PROGRESS.md so the numbers are accurate. I will run --fast first to avoid a long browser suite, then launch the full suite which rebuilds HTML and exit-interview automatically.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e120cc41-c3c4-46bb-bd0b-9bbd10e87bac-47","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/tools/test.mjs","offset":700,"limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":683,"output_tokens":2656,"cache_read_input_tokens":113280,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"26ec318b-6688-4634-9055-50f0ec53e1ca"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-e120cc41-c3c4-46bb-bd0b-9bbd10e87bac-47","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"700→      const empty = new Save(null);\\n      empty.write({ v: 1, slots: [freshGuest('Mem'), null, null], settings: null });\\n      assert(empty.read().slots[0].name === 'Mem', 'null storage');\\n    });\\n\\n    await test('replay fingerprint', async () => {\\n      const app = await boot(host);\\n      host.step(20);\\n      tap(host, 'Enter');\\n      host.step(15);\\n710→      const fp = host.fingerprint();\\n      const rec = host.recording();\\n      assert(rec && rec.frames.length > 10, 'recording');\\n      await host.replay(rec, () => host.loadGame(new World(new App({ storage: null, noHero: true }))));\\n      assert(host.fingerprint() === fp, `replay ${host.fingerprint()} vs ${fp}`);\\n    });\\n  } finally {\\n    host.dispose();\\n  }\\n\\n720→  if (!fast) {\\n    await test('browser, shots, and hub', async () => {\\n      execFileSync(process.execPath, ['tools/build.mjs'], { cwd: devRoot, stdio: ['ignore', 'pipe', 'pipe'] });\\n      const { runBrowser } = await import('./browser.mjs');\\n      const problems = await runBrowser({ devRoot, scratch: SCRATCH });\\n      if (problems.length) throw new Error(problems.join('\\\\n'));\\n    });\\n  }\\n\\n  if (fails.length) {\\n730→    for (const fail of fails) console.log(`FAIL ${fail}`);\\n    console.log(`${total - fails.length}/${total} passed`);\\n    process.exitCode = 1;\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  console.log(`${total}/${total} passed`);\\n}\\n\\nmain().catch((err) => {\\n  console.log(`FAIL runner: ${err?.stack || err}`);\\n740→  console.log(`0/${total} passed`);\\n  process.exitCode = 1;\\n});\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"700→      const empty = new Save(null);\\n      empty.write({ v: 1, slots: [freshGuest('Mem'), null, null], settings: null });\\n      assert(empty.read().slots[0].name === 'Mem', 'null st