{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_330","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Build.mjs pipes stdout rather than inheriting it, so test.log stays on one line.","signature":"1BIWGbQOeSmjnYGZJrIKXvDmOE7HG/PjVvZfKxMd29XUlLVYZ6dWphJ0iL/EZ1p5aCG04+zYAWzEPrvEjSP+xmCD5Hwlu50iBOivGUI+udPD++yLMx4kF9eS8Mcym0lLFVswrUWhQqYhHyUn6QeFcVSK3MjQXBjI1I3D6N0yuQhss91jQHSMHXJzhyPfN86DffA2+b52zyDdTRDJJLjhghaETrPBK5MKauMsPRkr8u12/s+XyqKfwITpu4OdwD+HmA"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9d34f4cc-b8ba-4ad3-8847-1feda5d30f8d-48","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/tools/test.mjs","offset":145,"limit":15}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3138,"output_tokens":129,"cache_read_input_tokens":113920,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"475d16e2-03c0-473e-9601-5c1ea5fd9d01"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-9d34f4cc-b8ba-4ad3-8847-1feda5d30f8d-48","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"145→function walk(dir, out = []) {\\n  for (const name of readdirSync(dir)) {\\n    if (name === 'node_modules' || name === '.build') continue;\\n    const p = path.join(dir, name);\\n    if (statSync(p).isDirectory()) walk(p, out);\\n150→    else if (name.endsWith('.js')) out.push(p);\\n  }\\n  return out;\\n}\\n\\nasync function main() {\\n  console.info = () => {};\\n  await test('dot bands and star thresholds', async () => {\\n    const idle = band('idle', 1);\\n    const average = band('average', 1);\",\"content_concise\":\"145→function walk(dir, out = []) {\\n  for (const name of readdirSync(dir)) {\\n    if (name === 'node_modules' || name === '.build') continue;\\n    const p = path.join(dir, name);\\n    if (statSync(p).isDirectory()) walk(p, out);\\n150→    else if (name.endsWith('.js')) out.push(p);\\n  }\\n  return out;\\n}\\n\\nasync function main() {\\n  console.info = () => {};\\n  await test('dot bands and star thresholds', async () => {\\n    const idle = band('idle', 1);\\n    const average = band('average', 1);\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/tools/test.mjs\",\"offset\":145,\"limit\":15,\"raw_output\":\"function walk(dir, out = []) {\\n  for (const name of readdirSync(dir)) {\\n    if (name === 'node_modules' || name === '.build') continue;\\n    const p = path.join(dir, name);\\n    if (statSync(p).isDirectory()) walk(p, out);\\n    else if (name.endsWith('.js')) out.push(p);\\n  }\\n  return out;\\n}\\n\\nasync function main() {\\n  console.info = () => {};\\n  await test('dot bands and star thresholds', async () => {\\n    const idle = band('idle', 1);\\n    const average = band('average', 1);\\n\",\"total_lines\":742}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"17416547-7808-4d65-9536-3aeba9024a2f"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_331","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Writing the code now. Checking whether `about` mode's ArrowRight conflicts with existing tests.\n\nNo existing tests conflict with the new about screen. Credits mode is separate. I'll import wrapText and CREDITS_SUMMARY into about.js. Circular dependencies are safe.\n\nAdding a one-liner comment to about.js explaining the 26-column pre-wrapping constraint. Confirmed that wrapText at 40 returns identical lines, so bits is always 1. Empty lines are skipped, and long words split across multiple lines.\n\nConfirmed wrapText preserves non-whitespace characters and collapses spaces. The copyright symbol renders as a question mark on screen, but the underlying string data remains intact.\n\nConfirmed page titles fit within the 52-character line limit and center properly on the HUD. The question mark for unknown glyphs is acceptable.\n\nAdding the about screen's button rows. Next and Previous appear only on intermediate pages, with Back always present. The activate handler will intercept next and previous clicks before the grouped back handler.\n\nThe activate handler now advances or retreats the about page index and refreshes the screen. The update method adds keyboard and controller edge detection for ArrowRight, PadR1, ArrowLeft, and PadL1 to navigate pages.\n\nUsing `refresh(false)` for arrow navigation so focus does not jump when pages change. If the Next button disappears, the focused index clamps to the new row set and highlights Previous instead.\n\nArrow navigation will not trigger a refresh when the page index does not change. The test suite needs imports for TESTING_FEEDBACK, ENGINE_FEEDBACK, PROMPT_FEEDBACK, and KIT_CREDITS. The about screen text is safe from glyph crashes because say() replaces unknown characters. The source field contains \"Wii Fit\", which is permitted on this screen.\n\nConfirmed the about screen source field is not scanned for banned names, and the new feedback text contains no prohibited substrings. Now writing the files. For the headless test, the engine constructor already receives a World, but boot() replaces it with a fresh one.\n\nThe headless test will call `boot(engine)` to initialize the engine, then navigate from start to about and assert that the first page shows Next but not Previous.\n\nThe headless test now verifies that the first about page renders widgets. It taps Enter to advance, then uses ArrowLeft and ArrowRight to navigate back and forward. The test also locates the page with the most lines to exercise the densest layout.\n\nThe headless test now loops through the first, densest, and last about pages. It asserts that each page draws exactly as many widgets as its line count. It then iterates over those drawn widgets and other app widgets.\n\nThe headless test now asserts that every drawn widget stays within the HUD bounds. It then shrinks the HUD to 427 by 240, refreshes the densest about page, and captures the resulting widgets.\n\nThe headless test restores the HUD to its original size after the small-screen check. It notes that checking every widget for bounds might fail if existing widgets sit slightly outside, but prompt and row widgets should fit. The \"About\" title at scale 3 on a 427-pixel width is only about 90 pixels, so it fits comfortably. If the engine resets the HUD size before drawing, the small-screen assertion is skipped.\n\nThe browser test forces a viewport size by setting it and stepping twice. Headless mode has no canvas, so the small-screen check might be skipped. I need to verify that the 427×240 HUD is actually applied. I will inspect how HUD dimensions are computed and whether width is writable.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e9383149-eedf-4721-93a3-7de9f2fde5bd-49","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"python3 - << 'PY'\np=\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/pixel-engine.js\"\ntext=open(p,encoding='utf-8',errors='replace').read()\nprint('len', len(text), 'lines', text.count('\\n'))\nfor needle in ['hud.width', '.hud=', 'this.hud', 'syncHud', 'pixelSize']:\n    print(needle, text.find(needle))\n# find width assignment patterns around 'hud'\nidx=0\nc=0\nwhile c<8:\n    i=text.find('hud', idx)\n    if i<0: break\n    snippet=text[max(0,i-40):i+80].replace('\\n',' ')\n    if 'width' in snippet or 'height' in snippet:\n        print('---', i)\n        print(snippet)\n        c+=1\n    idx=i+3\nprint('total hud', text.count('hud'))\nPY","description":"Find how the engine sets HUD size"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":347,"output_tokens":2660,"cache_read_input_tokens":116992,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"9abe6a19-b93d-4aaa-80bd-2731d7d94106"}
