{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_333","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"HUD width and height are getters from this.size.\n\nThe `sync` method always updates `this.size` before checking for a container. This means the HUD dimensions can be set even when no container exists.\n\nThe test sets the HUD size manually before calling step(1). However, step() later resets the HUD to the real viewport dimensions after drawing. The manual override is therefore overwritten.\n\nWidget coordinates from the 427×240 draw remain valid even after the HUD resets to 480×270. The title widget's x-position can verify which size was used: centered on 427 yields 168, while 480 yields 195.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-06e33d9f-c8ee-426e-a8a7-05803aee0f10-51","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"python3 - << 'PY'\np=\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/pixel-engine.js\"\ntext=open(p,encoding='utf-8',errors='replace').read()\ni=text.find('step(e=1)')\nprint('step at', i)\nprint(text[i:i+1800])\nprint('----')\ni=text.find('hud.sync')\nprint('hud.sync', i)\nprint(text[i-200:i+400])\nPY","description":"See when step syncs the HUD"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1404,"output_tokens":801,"cache_read_input_tokens":120064,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"b27f5657-918c-4a93-b43c-8f42f5cac822"}
