{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_336","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Updating the test by replacing about assertions and adding the drive.","signature":"YF9kuHBbo7j9A9mnd87ENAhA+eK/OrWcLVI5suOrRGxet2398owRRjXgIxYL3s+fMDo2Sd5GbD8yuZ0MFpahw9hLtcnwGCVOhuAwYFEsUyIceIOkPBy/K72FHF3x1XD+jZuPOkV+21Ha9BgJy0KS3el5GfSvsGEj5gmJKiL4l3b4UA"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-61477873-cdcd-4932-80dd-167026d8441a-60","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/tools/test.mjs","old_string":"import { MEDICAL, SOURCE_INFORMATION, aboutPages, exitInterview } from '../src/data/about.js';","new_string":"import { ABOUT_COLS, ABOUT_ROWS, ENGINE_FEEDBACK, KIT_CREDITS, MEDICAL, PROMPT_FEEDBACK, SOURCE_INFORMATION, TESTING_FEEDBACK, aboutPages, exitInterview } from '../src/data/about.js';"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-61477873-cdcd-4932-80dd-167026d8441a-61","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/tools/test.mjs","old_string":"    const pages = aboutPages(CREDITS_TEXT).map((p) => `${p.title}\\n${p.lines.join('\\n')}`).join('\\n');\n    assert(pages.includes(MEDICAL), 'medical');\n    for (const key of Object.keys(SOURCE_INFORMATION)) assert(pages.includes(String(SOURCE_INFORMATION[key])), `about ${key}`);\n    assert(pages.includes('Testing Feedback') && pages.includes('Engine Feedback') && pages.includes('Prompt Feedback'), 'feedback');\n    assert(pages.includes('Kenney') && pages.includes('three.js') && pages.includes('Rapier'), 'kit');","new_string":"    const pages = aboutPages(CREDITS_TEXT);\n    const flat = pages.flatMap((p) => p.lines).join('').replace(/\\s+/g, '');\n    const compact = (s) => String(s).replace(/\\s+/g, '');\n    for (const page of pages) {\n      assert(page.lines.length <= ABOUT_ROWS, `${page.title} lines ${page.lines.length}`);\n      for (const text of page.lines) {\n        assert(text.length <= ABOUT_COLS, `about width ${text.length}: ${text}`);\n        assert(wrapText(text, 26).length === 1 && wrapText(text, 40).length === 1, `about rewrap ${text}`);\n      }\n    }\n    assert(flat.includes(compact(MEDICAL)), 'medical');\n    for (const key of Object.keys(SOURCE_INFORMATION)) assert(flat.includes(compact(SOURCE_INFORMATION[key])), `about ${key}`);\n    for (const text of [...TESTING_FEEDBACK, ...ENGINE_FEEDBACK, ...PROMPT_FEEDBACK]) assert(flat.includes(compact(text)), `feedback ${text.slice(0, 24)}`);\n    assert(flat.includes(compact(KIT_CREDITS)) && flat.includes('Kenney') && flat.includes('three.js') && flat.includes('Rapier'), 'kit');\n    assert(flat.includes(compact(CREDITS_TEXT)), 'full credits');\n    const aboutEngine = await Engine.headless(new World(new App({ storage: null, noHero: true })), { camera: CAMERA });\n    try {\n      const app = await boot(aboutEngine);\n      choose(aboutEngine, app, 'start');\n      choose(aboutEngine, app, 'about');\n      assert(app.mode === 'about', app.mode);\n      assert(app.state().rows[0] === 'next' && app.state().rows.includes('back'), app.state().rows.join(','));\n      tap(aboutEngine, 'Enter');\n      assert(app.aboutPage === 1, `next ${app.aboutPage}`);\n      tap(aboutEngine, 'ArrowLeft');\n      assert(app.aboutPage === 0, `left ${app.aboutPage}`);\n      tap(aboutEngine, 'ArrowRight');\n      assert(app.aboutPage === 1, `right ${app.aboutPage}`);\n      const fullest = pages.reduce((best, page, i) => (page.lines.length > pages[best].lines.length ? i : best), 0);\n      const drawPage = (index, width, height) => {\n        aboutEngine.hud.sync({ width, height }, { cssWidth: width, cssHeight: height, offsetX: 0, offsetY: 0 });\n        app.aboutPage = index;\n        app.idle = 0;\n        app.refresh(true);\n        aboutEngine.step(1);\n        const drawn = app.widgets.filter((w) => String(w.id).startsWith('about-'));\n        assert(drawn.length === pages[index].lines.length, `page ${index} drew ${drawn.length}/${pages[index].lines.length} at ${width}x${height}`);\n        for (const w of app.widgets) {\n          assert(w.x >= -0.5 && w.y >= -0.5 && w.x + w.w <= width + 0.5 && w.y + w.h <= height + 0.5, `${w.id} outside ${width}x${height}: ${w.x},${w.y} ${w.w}x${w.h}`);\n        }\n        const title = app.widgets.find((w) => w.id === 'title');\n        const titleW = 5 * 6 * (width < 220 ? 2 : width < 400 ? 3 : 4);\n        const expectedX = Math.max(width < 200 ? 4 : 12, Math.floor((width - titleW) / 2));\n        assert(title && title.x === expectedX, `title x ${title?.x} wanted ${expectedX} at ${width}`);\n      };\n      drawPage(0, 480, 270);\n      drawPage(fullest, 427, 240);\n      drawPage(pages.length - 1, 427, 240);\n      const usagePage = pages.findIndex((p) => p.lines.some((line) => line.includes('added on import')));\n      assert(usagePage > 0, 'usage page');\n      drawPage(usagePage, 427, 240);\n    } finally {\n      aboutEngine.dispose();\n    }"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1892,"output_tokens":1422,"cache_read_input_tokens":124800,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"f167002f-7716-4b46-863d-d8d592bfe08a"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-61477873-cdcd-4932-80dd-167026d8441a-60","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"import { MEDICAL, SOURCE_INFORMATION, aboutPages, exitInterview } from '../src/data/about.js';\",\"new_string\":\"import { ABOUT_COLS, ABOUT_ROWS, ENGINE_FEEDBACK, KIT_CREDITS, MEDICAL, PROMPT_FEEDBACK, SOURCE_INFORMATION, TESTING_FEEDBACK, aboutPages, exitInterview } from '../src/data/about.js';\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/tools/test.mjs has been updated successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/tools/test.mjs has been updated.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/tools/test.mjs\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"import { MEDICAL, SOURCE_INFORMATION, aboutPages, exitInterview } from '../src/data/about.js';\",\"old_line\":37,\"new_string\":\"import { ABOUT_COLS, ABOUT_ROWS, ENGINE_FEEDBACK, KIT_CREDITS, MEDICAL, PROMPT_FEEDBACK, SOURCE_INFORMATION, TESTING_FEEDBACK, aboutPages, exitInterview } from '../src/data/about.js';\",\"new_line\":37,\"context_before\":\"import { MODELS } from '../src/art/models.js';\\nimport { CLIPS } from '../src/art/clips.js';\\nimport { clinicTile } from '../src/art/textures.js';\\n\",\"context_after\":\"import { CREDITS_TEXT } from '../src/data/creditsText.js';\\nimport { TITLE } from '../src/data/title.js';\\n\\n\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-61477873-cdcd-4932-80dd-167026d8441a-61","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"    const pages = aboutPages(CREDITS_TEXT).map((p) => `${p.title}\\\\n${p.lines.join('\\\\n')}`).join('\\\\n');\\n    assert(pages.includes(MEDICAL), 'medical');\\n    for (const key of Object.keys(SOURCE_INFORMATION)) assert(pages.includes(String(SOURCE_INFORMATION[key])), `about ${key}`);\\n    assert(pages.includes('Testing Feedback') && pages.includes('Engine Feedback') && pages.includes('Prompt Feedback'), 'feedback');\\n    assert(pages.includes('Kenney') && pages.includes('three.js') && pages.includes('Rapier'), 'kit');\",\"new_string\":\"    const pages = aboutPages(CREDITS_TEXT);\\n    const flat = pages.flatMap((p) => p.lines).join('').replace(/\\\\s+/g, '');\\n    const compact = (s) => String(s).replace(/\\\\s+/g, '');\\n    for (const page of pages) {\\n      assert(page.lines.length <= ABOUT_ROWS, `${page.title} lines ${page.lines.length}`);\\n      for (const text of page.lines) {\\n        assert(text.length <= ABOUT_COLS, `about width ${text.length}: ${text}`);\\n        assert(wrapText(text, 26).length === 1 && wrapText(text, 40).length === 1, `about rewrap ${text}`);\\n      }\\n    }\\n    assert(flat.includes(compact(MEDICAL)), 'medical');\\n    for (const key of Object.keys(SOURCE_INFORMATION)) assert(flat.includes(compact(SOURCE_INFORMATION[key])), `about ${key}`);\\n    for (const text of [...TESTING_FEEDBACK, ...ENGINE_FEEDBACK, ...PROMPT_FEEDBACK]) assert(flat.includes(compact(text)), `feedback ${text.slice(0, 24)}`);\\n    assert(flat.includes(compact(KIT_CREDITS)) && flat.includes('Kenney') && flat.includes('three.js') && flat.includes('Rapier'), 'kit');\\n    assert(flat.includes(compact(CREDITS_TEXT)), 'full credits');\\n    const aboutEngine = await Engine.headless(new World(new App({ storage: null, noHero: true })), { camera: CAMERA });\\n    try {\\n      const app = await boot(aboutEngine);\\n      choose(aboutEngine, app, 'start');\\n      choose(aboutEngine, app, 'about');\\n      assert(app.mode === 'about', app.mode);\\n      assert(app.state().rows[0] === 'next' && app.state().rows.includes('back'), app.state().rows.join(','));\\n      tap(aboutEngine, 'Enter');\\n      assert(app.aboutPage === 1, `next ${app.aboutPage}`);\\n      tap(aboutEngine, 'ArrowLeft');\\n      assert(app.aboutPage === 0, `left ${app.aboutPage}`);\\n      tap(aboutEngine, 'ArrowRight');\\n      assert(app.aboutPage === 1, `right ${app.aboutPage}`);\\n      const fullest = pages.reduce((best, page, i) => (page.lines.length > pages[best].lines.length ? i : best), 0);\\n      const drawPage = (index, width, height) => {\\n        aboutEngine.hud.sync({ width, height }, { cssWidth: width, cssHeight: height, offsetX: 0, offsetY: 0 });\\n        app.aboutPage = index;\\n        app.idle = 0;\\n        app.refresh(true);\\n        aboutEngine.step(1);\\n        const drawn = app.widgets.filter((w) => String(w.id).startsWith('about-'));\\n        assert(drawn.length === pages[index].lines.length, `page ${index} drew ${drawn.length}/${pages[index].lines.length} at ${width}x${height}`);\\n        for (const w of app.widgets) {\\n          assert(w.x >= -0.5 && w.y >= -0.5 && w.x + w.w <= width + 0.5 && w.y + w.h <= height + 0.5, `${w.id} outside ${width}x${height}: ${w.x},${w.y} ${w.w}x${w.h}`);\\n        }\\n        const title = app.widgets.find((w) => w.id === 'title');\\n        const titleW = 5 * 6 * (width < 220 ? 2 : width < 400 ? 3 : 4);\\n        const expectedX = Math.max(width < 200 ? 4 : 12, Math.floor((width - titleW) / 2));\\n        assert(title && title.x === expectedX, `title x ${title?.x} wanted ${expectedX} at ${width}`);\\n      };\\n      drawPage(0, 480, 270);\\n      drawPage(fullest, 427, 240);\\n      drawPage(pages.length - 1, 427, 240);\\n      const usagePage = pages.findIndex((p) => p.lines.some((line) => line.includes('added on import')));\\n      assert(usagePage > 0, 'usage page');\\n      drawPage(usagePage, 427, 240);\\n    } finally {\\n      aboutEngine.dispose();\\n    }\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/tools/test.mjs has been updated successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/tools/test.mjs has been updated.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/tools/test.mjs\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"    const pages = aboutPages(CREDITS_TEXT).map((p) => `${p.title}\\\\n${p.lines.join('\\\\n')}`).join('\\\\n');\\n    assert(pages.includes(MEDICAL), 'medical');\\n    for (const key of Object.keys(SOURCE_INFORMATION)) assert(pages.includes(String(SOURCE_INFORMATION[key])), `about ${key}`);\\n    assert(pages.includes('Testing Feedback') && pages.includes('Engine Feedback') && pages.includes('Prompt Feedback'), 'feedback');\\n    assert(pages.includes('Kenney') && pages.includes('three.js') && pages.includes('Rapier'), 'kit');\",\"old_line\":210,\"new_string\":\"    const pages = aboutPages(CREDITS_TEXT);\\n    const flat = pages.flatMap((p) => p.lines).join('').replace(/\\\\s+/g, '');\\n    const compact = (s) => String(s).replace(/\\\\s+/g, '');\\n    for (const page of pages) {\\n      assert(page.lines.length <= ABOUT_ROWS, `${page.title} lines ${page.lines.length}`);\\n      for (const text of page.lines) {\\n        assert(text.length <= ABOUT_COLS, `about width ${text.length}: ${text}`);\\n        assert(wrapText(text, 26).length === 1 && wrapText(text, 40).length === 1, `about rewrap ${text}`);\\n      }\\n    }\\n    assert(flat.includes(compact(MEDICAL)), 'medical');\\n    for (const key of Object.keys(SOURCE_INFORMATION)) assert(flat.includes(compact(SOURCE_INFORMATION[key])), `about ${key}`);\\n    for (const text of [...TESTING_FEEDBACK, ...ENGINE_FEEDBACK, ...PROMPT_FEEDBACK]) assert(flat.includes(compact(text)), `feedback ${text.slice(0, 24)}`);\\n    assert(flat.includes(compact(KIT_CREDITS)) && flat.includes('Kenney') && flat.includes('three.js') && flat.includes('Rapier'), 'kit');\\n    assert(flat.includes(compact(CREDITS_TEXT)), 'full credits');\\n    const aboutEngine = await Engine.headless(new World(new App({ storage: null, noHero: true })), { camera: CAMERA });\\n    try {\\n      const app = await boot(aboutEngine);\\n      choose(aboutEngine, app, 'start');\\n      choose(aboutEngine, app, 'about');\\n      assert(app.mode === 'about', app.mode);\\n      assert(app.state().rows[0] === 'next' && app.state().rows.includes('back'), app.state().rows.join(','));\\n      tap(aboutEngine, 'Enter');\\n      assert(app.aboutPage === 1, `next ${app.aboutPage}`);\\n      tap(aboutEngine, 'ArrowLeft');\\n      assert(app.aboutPage === 0, `left ${app.aboutPage}`);\\n      tap(aboutEngine, 'ArrowRight');\\n      assert(app.aboutPage === 1, `right ${app.aboutPage}`);\\n      const fullest = pages.reduce((best, page, i) => (page.lines.length > pages[best].lines.length ? i : best), 0);\\n      const drawPage = (index, width, height) => {\\n        aboutEngine.hud.sync({ width, height }, { cssWidth: width, cssHeight: height, offsetX: 0, offsetY: 0 });\\n        app.aboutPage = index;\\n        app.idle = 0;\\n        app.refresh(true);\\n        aboutEngine.step(1);\\n        const drawn = app.widgets.filter((w) => String(w.id).startsWith('about-'));\\n        assert(drawn.length === pages[index].lines.length, `page ${index} drew ${drawn.length}/${pages[index].lines.length} at ${width}x${height}`);\\n        for (const w of app.widgets) {\\n          assert(w.x >= -0.5 && w.y >= -0.5 && w.x + w.w <= width + 0.5 && w.y + w.h <= height + 0.5, `${w.id} outside ${width}x${height}: ${w.x},${w.y} ${w.w}x${w.h}`);\\n        }\\n        const title = app.widgets.find((w) => w.id === 'title');\\n        const titleW = 5 * 6 * (width < 220 ? 2 : width < 400 ? 3 : 4);\\n        const expectedX = Math.max(width < 200 ? 4 : 12, Math.floor((width - titleW) / 2));\\n        assert(title && title.x === expectedX, `title x ${title?.x} wanted ${expectedX} at ${width}`);\\n      };\\n      drawPage(0, 480, 270);\\n      drawPage(fullest, 427, 240);\\n      drawPage(pages.length - 1, 427, 240);\\n      const usagePage = pages.findIndex((p) => p.lines.some((line) => line.includes('added on import')));\\n      assert(usagePage > 0, 'usage page');\\n      drawPage(usagePage, 427, 240);\\n    } finally {\\n      aboutEngine.dispose();\\n    }\",\"new_line\":210,\"context_before\":\"      assert(!banned.test(def.name), def.name);\\n    }\\n    for (const day of DAYS) assert(!banned.test(`${day.beat} ${day.concern}`), `day ${day.day}`);\\n\",\"context_after\":\"    const interview = exitInterview();\\n    assert(interview.sourceInformation.usage === 'added on import', 'usage');\\n    assert(interview.testingFeedback.length === 4, 'testing feedback');\\n\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"db9726bc-eb31-483a-b83a-2a48d70d38e0"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_337","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Reviewing the title scale logic in paint.\n\nConfirmed the title scale logic and heading() returns 'About' in about mode. Verified the text width calculation for the 5-character title. Now examining the line() function.\n\nThe line() function trims text to 52 characters and centers it with a margin of 4 or 12 pixels. At 427px the title scale is 3, yielding a width of 90px and an x-position of 168. At 480px the scale becomes 4, giving a width of 120px and an x-position of 180.\n\nConfirmed the title scale formula matches paint exactly. Verified widget bounds fit at 427×240, and checked that \"Source Information\" centers properly at scale 2. Now checking whether any Credits page line exceeds the screen width.\n\nConfirmed row labels and Credits lines fit within screen bounds. Verified that held arrow keys are released after tapping, preventing step() from misinterpreting them. Traced the about page navigation flow: Enter advances to the next page, then ArrowLeft and ArrowRight cycle through pages before drawPage sets the index directly. Noted that idle mode advances through four steps without triggering attract mode. Confirmed the title-to-menu-to-about navigation sequence.\n\nConfirmed the about menu item is index 4, requiring four down arrows from the first row. Verified the menu has no more than 12 rows. Noted that console.info is suppressed before tests run, and the about engine test is placed before the shared host in the suite.\n\nSet the test timeout to 180 seconds to accommodate the new engine boot and activity simulations. Confirmed about.js import order is valid, the CREDITS_SUMMARY export exists, and the title widget has no ID collision.\n\nRecalculating widget positions for the 480×270 case with six lines and three rows. The title sits at y=51, the about heading at y=72, and the six lines start at y=144. The row area begins at y=152, leaving a 34-pixel gap before the bottom margin.\n\nConfirmed the 480×270 layout leaves no widget overlap. At 427×240, the three rows end at y=215 and the prompt sits at 219, both safely inside the screen bounds. The title scale stays at 3 for that width. Now running the test.\n\nConfirmed the last body line at y=123 fits within the 240-pixel height limit. The test should pass, though a title x-position mismatch is possible. Checking whether advance() syncs the HUD before draw, since step() later does so. Integer coordinates prevent fractional widget issues. Now examining say() and widget width calculations.\n\nConfirmed the CREDITS_SUMMARY import is safe and free of circular dependencies. The monitor has already completed, so no old watcher needs killing. A GPU process at 99% from 00:25 is present but unrelated to the current test.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-eeae6056-24f9-4863-91b6-2cf6fdc23072-62","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"ps -o pid,ppid,lstart,cmd -p 4172510,4171730,4172528,4103143 2>/dev/null | head -20; echo '--- parents ---'; ps -o pid,ppid,cmd -p 4172508,4171728,4008787 2>/dev/null | head","description":"Identify leftover browser parents"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1684,"output_tokens":1878,"cache_read_input_tokens":126592,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"9e3d3bb6-3523-4fd7-b96f-7fcc06d28f7d"}
