{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_349","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The full test suite passed in 77 seconds.\n\nThe logs look complete and genuine. Timestamps match today's date. Now starting the next steps.\n\nVerifying exit-interview.json rebuild and HTML source fields. Confirming the HTML was built after the about.js change. Next steps include writing PROGRESS.md, updating the goal plan, killing the monitor, and finalizing the reply.\n\nChecking that the HTML and JSON were written during this run. Grepping the built bundle for unique about-page strings. Verifying boot and shot images are painted.\n\nBoot and title images are confirmed painted. The deviations from the original plan are now recorded: instant mode cuts, a single World/App, kinematic Vitamin Tray with three lane-boards, Pier dot recentering at takeoff, and skipped intros for attract, medley, and bot activities.\n\nSession cards use palette stand-ins for the four seat colours. The join press claims a seat without activating the focused menu row on that same frame. Name-screen Backspace edits the name without leaving the screen. Pause freeze is gated in App.fixed when frozen or engine.timeScale is zero, and the pause edge is consumed at the start of fixed() to prevent headless step() from advancing playT.\n\nVerifying the less certain deviations in the source code before recording them. Checking if the monitor is still running to prevent a duplicate DONE signal.\n\nAll eight checklist items will be flipped. The plan file lacks a ## Deviations section, so one will be appended there. Exit interview fields and HTML self-containment will be verified with a quick node check.\n\nPROGRESS.md will be written in the workspace root as the hand-in file. It will record the completed build and verification results concisely. Screenshots will be checked with read_file, and any lingering browsers from this run will be cleared.\n\nThe test suite covers dot bands, activities, week, pause, attract, medley, voice, hash, and About pages. Chromium boots show the title Mint Dial with music 0.1 and zero page errors. Captures are 1281×720 with span 188.8. Boot images agree. Controls, phone gate, widgets at all three sizes, voice RMS, family hour, and WebGPU messages are present. Four hub harness URLs pass on 127.0.0.1:33105. The no-session boot still shows the title. pixel-engine.js is unchanged.\n\nThe About screen contains every source field, the feedback sentence, kit credits, and full credits text. exit-interview.json is built from the same about.js data. The plan will also list honest notes on what was fixed.\n\nThe exit-interview.json schema is being validated against TASK.md. The HTML will be checked for the document title, inlined session.js, and the About-page strings \"Ten issues\", \"added on import\", and \"This is not medical advice\".","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3b02cc30-fec4-4114-bb80-5f7019b8af1f-76","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"SCRATCH=\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/implementer\"\nWORK=\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work\"\nHTML=\"$WORK/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607.html\"\nnode --input-type=module -e '\nimport { readFileSync } from \"node:fs\";\nconst j = JSON.parse(readFileSync(process.argv[1], \"utf8\"));\nconst keys = Object.keys(j).sort().join(\",\");\nif (keys !== \"aiHub,engineFeedback,promptFeedback,sourceInformation,testingFeedback\") throw new Error(\"keys \"+keys);\nconst sk = Object.keys(j.sourceInformation).sort().join(\",\");\nconst want = \"animation,artDirection,audio,date,environment,genre,model,online,perspective,plan,research,source,tech,testing,usage\".split(\",\").sort().join(\",\");\nif (sk !== want) throw new Error(\"source \"+sk);\nif (j.sourceInformation.usage !== \"added on import\") throw new Error(\"usage\");\nif (j.testingFeedback.length !== 4 || j.engineFeedback.length !== 6 || j.promptFeedback.length !== 4) throw new Error(\"feedback lens\");\nfor (const k of [\"name\",\"tagline\",\"description\",\"type\",\"genre\",\"source\",\"series\",\"players\",\"controls\",\"tags\"]) {\n  if (!j.aiHub[k] || (Array.isArray(j.aiHub[k]) && j.aiHub[k].length < 3)) throw new Error(\"aiHub \"+k);\n}\nif (j.aiHub.name !== \"Mint Dial\") throw new Error(\"name\");\nif (j.aiHub.tags.length < 3 || j.aiHub.tags.length > 6) throw new Error(\"tags\");\nconst html = readFileSync(process.argv[2], \"utf8\");\nfor (const s of [\"Mint Dial\",\"added on import\",\"This is not medical advice. Ounce is a scale.\",\"Ten issues\",\"Kenney (CC0)\",\"Wii Fit\",\"Pixel Engine 0.46.0\",\"hub:session\"]) {\n  if (!html.includes(s)) throw new Error(\"html missing \"+s);\n}\nif (/src=[\"\\']https?:/.test(html)) throw new Error(\"external src\");\nconsole.log(\"json ok\", j.aiHub.players, j.aiHub.genre, j.testingFeedback[0].slice(0, 40));\nconsole.log(\"html bytes\", html.length);\n' \"$WORK/exit-interview.json\" \"$HTML\"\necho \"=== mtimes ===\"\nstat -c '%y %n' \"$HTML\" \"$WORK/exit-interview.json\"\necho \"=== browsers ===\"\nps -ef | rg -n \"chrome-headless|firefox|webkit\" | rg -v rg | head -5 || true\n# deviation fingerprints\nDEV=\"$WORK/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src\"\nrg -n \"iris|claimedJoin|nameBuf|pier|timeScale|stand-in|skipIntro|intro\" \"$DEV/app.js\" \"$DEV/core/sims.js\" | head -40\n","description":"Validate exit interview, HTML, and deviation clues"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3b02cc30-fec4-4114-bb80-5f7019b8af1f-77","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/implementer/boot-1.png"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3b02cc30-fec4-4114-bb80-5f7019b8af1f-78","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.bui