{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_368","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Widgets at 1920x1080 now report hudW as 427 instead of 480.\n\nThe widgets test now reports hudW 427 at 1920x1080 and 1280x720 too, not just 640x360. This is a behavior change from the previous run.\n\nThe test still passed with no bad rows or overflow. The smaller HUD at 1920x1080 is unexpected since the game code did not change between runs. This may be non-determinism in the renderer's fill aspect calculation.\n\nThe 427 value matches the 640x360 result, not the expected 480. The widgets test runs before shots on a fresh page, so viewport leakage is unlikely. I will read the widgets function to find the cause.\n\nThe viewport change may not be reaching the renderer. The 427 value matches the small 16:9 HUD size for 640x360, which is odd that all three resolutions report it. Since the rectangles still fit, the smaller HUD is harmless.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9c979458-3bf9-492d-86b8-a29d09076250-108","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"async function widgets|setViewportSize|hudW","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/tools/browser.mjs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1065,"output_tokens":1215,"cache_read_input_tokens":168448,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"2edc46ab-ca9d-4a59-abc7-223a582a0328"}
