{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_371","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The HUD in the boot and title shots uses the exact palette navy color.\n\nPause and Activity HUD colors are correct. HTML and JSON were written at 00:40. The test log shows all 12 tests passed cleanly.\n\nChecking the boot-1 image to confirm the title is visible. Will write PROGRESS.md and update the goal plan checklist and deviations. No leftover monitors remain. The final reply will include source information, testing feedback, engine feedback, prompt feedback, kit credits, and a disclaimer copied exactly from about.js.\n\nWidget 427 is not a failure since the test passed and rectangles fit. PROGRESS.md will note that widget rectangles fit at all three viewports without explaining the HUD pixel size difference. The goal plan checklist items will be marked complete.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-fcfb03c2-21b0-4b3e-97c6-bcdd236800a9-111","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/implementer/boot-1.png"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-fcfb03c2-21b0-4b3e-97c6-bcdd236800a9-112","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/exit-interview.json","limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2531,"output_tokens":1169,"cache_read_input_tokens":171776,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"969dff51-49ee-4d10-a65d-51513bc4106d"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-fcfb03c2-21b0-4b3e-97c6-bcdd236800a9-111","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"ImageContent\":{\"data\":\"\",\"mime_type\":\"image/png\"}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-fcfb03c2-21b0-4b3e-97c6-bcdd236800a9-112","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 22:16:07\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Sports\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"Isometric island, with a fixed camera for each activity\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"Pixel Engine 0.46.0, three.js r186, Rapier 0.20 as bundled, esbuild 0.28.2\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"The engine native pixel look, with new models for the scale, stations, and props\\\",\\n10→    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"Engine ClipDefs compiled onto the hero rig and played with AnimationMixer\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Engine Song and SoundDef data, plus a Web Audio formant voice. Music defaults to 10 percent.\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, own card, 1 to 4 players. Family Hour is local on one screen.\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"node tools/test.mjs, Playwright 1.63 Chromium with the five software WebGPU flags, WebKit and Firefox for the missing-WebGPU path, and the engine headless runner\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"The director plan already included engine and hub research and spikes. I read PLAN.md, the engine guide where the recipes pointed, and the hub README, and I checked the Dot table in code. I did not do extra research on the source beyond that plan.\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n20→    \\\"Ten issues. The expert pier jump scored two stars, pause let the pose clock move on the frame the button went down, two songs had uneven pattern lengths, a tray board lookup named a variable that was not in scope, a few model parts floated, the seagull was spoken as the scale, a dev-tool page could not go back, the prompt could draw past a short screen, the scale's voice measured just under the loudness line, and the About screen kept only the first six lines so later source fields never appeared.\\\",\\n    \\\"Two were game-breaking. The pier jump sat under the three-star line until takeoff recentred the dot, and the pose kept playing for one frame after pause. The others failed a data check, a voice check, a menu, or the About screen, and they were fixed before the hand-in.\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful test was the idle-versus-expert bot pass on every activity. It is what caught the pier jump sitting under the three-star line.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful test was the glyph scan. Every line already used the allowed characters, so it passed on the first run and did not change the game.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"Headless stepping, the pixel HUD, and a real input recorder made a week of play testable without a screen.\\\",\\n    \\\"I guessed wrong about pause. At timeScale 0 the headless stepper still calls fixedUpdate, and that call happens before update reads the pause key, so the pose clock moved unless the sim refused the step. Menu presses do still arrive. The type note reads as if those presses are dropped. Capture also needs all five Vulkan flags or the picture comes back blank.\\\",\\n    \\\"The centre-of-balance itself. The engine will move a character. It will not sway a polite dot, keep a week, or speak in formants.\\\",\\n    \\\"The hardest part was trusting the frame clock. Game time, the press window, and the hub clock are three different clocks, and only one of them is allowed to move a score.\\\",\\n30→    \\\"None. pixel-engine.js is the kit file, byte for byte.\\\",\\n    \\\"I would give the music bus a default of silence until the game sets it, so a shared browser profile cannot leave yesterday volume on today game.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The plan named the mechanics, the sentences, and the tests, so the work was building a game rather than inventing one.\\\",\\n    \\\"The cut list in the plan and the instruction to finish everything on this computer disagree. I followed the instruction and shipped the activities the cut list would drop.\\\",\\n    \\\"The hardest piece was the pier jump star line. The same bot that holds a pose will dive off a dock, and the flight begins wherever the dot was left.\\\",\\n    \\\"I would ask for the pause rule in one sentence: timeScale 0, fixedUpdate silent, update still reads keys. The guide and the type comment do not say the same thing.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n40→    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Mint Dial\\\",\",\"content_concise\":\"1→{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 22:16:07\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Sports\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"Isometric island, with a fixed camera for each activity\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"Pixel Engine 0.46.0, three.js r186, Rapier 0.20 as bundled, esbuild 0.28.2\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"The engine native pixel look, with new models for the scale, stations, and props\\\",\\n10→    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"Engine ClipDefs compiled onto the hero rig and played with AnimationMixer\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Engine Song and SoundDef data, plus a Web Audio formant voice. Music defaults to 10 percent.\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, own card, 1 to 4 players. Family Hour is local on one screen.\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"node tools/test.mjs, Playwright 1.63 Chromium with the five software WebGPU flags, WebKit and Firefox for the missing-WebGPU path, and the engine headless runner\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"The director plan already included engine and hub research and spikes. I read PLAN.md, the engine guide where the recipes pointed, and the hub README, and I checked the Dot table in code. I did not do extra research on the source beyond that plan.\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n20→    \\\"Ten issues. The expert pier jump scored two stars, pause let the pose clock move on the frame the button went down, two songs had uneven pattern lengths, a tray board lookup named a variable that was not in scope, a few model parts floated, the seagull was spoken as the scale, a dev-tool page could not go back, the prompt could draw past a short screen, the scale's voice measured just under the loudness line, and the About screen kept only the first six lines so later source fields never appeared.\\\",\\n    \\\"Two were game-breaking. The pier jump sat under the three-star line until takeoff recentred the dot, and the pose kept playing for one frame after pause. The others failed a data check, a voice check, a menu, or the About screen, and they were fixed before the hand-in.\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful test was the idle-versus-expert bot pass on every activity. It is what caught the pier jump sitting under the three-star line.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful test was the glyph scan. Every line already used the allowed characters, so it passed on the first run and did not change the game.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"Headless stepping, the pixel HUD, and a real input recorder made a week of play testable without a screen.\\\",\\n    \\\"I guessed wrong about pause. At timeScale 0 the headless stepper still calls fixedUpdate, and that call happens before update reads the pause key, so the pose clock moved unless the sim refused the step. Menu presses do still arrive. The type note reads as if those presses are dropped. Capture also needs all five Vulkan flags or the picture comes back blank.\\\",\\n    \\\"The centre-of-balance itself. The engine will move a character. It will not sway a polite dot, keep a week, or speak in formants.\\\",\\n    \\\"The hardest part was trusting the frame clock. Game time, the press window, and the hub clock are three different clocks, and only one of them is allowed to move a score.\\\",\\n30→    \\\"None. pixel-engine.js is the kit file, byte for byte.\\\",\\n    \\\"I would give the music bus a default of silence until the game sets it, so a shared browser profile cannot leave yesterday volume on today game.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The plan named the mechanics, the sentences, and the tests, so the work was building a game rather than inventing one.\\\",\\n    \\\"The cut list in the plan and the instruction to finish everything on this computer disagree. I followed the instruction and shipped the activities the cut list would drop.\\\",\\n    \\\"The hardest piece was the pier jump star line. The same bot that holds a pose will dive off a dock, and the flight begins wherever the dot was left.\\\",\\n    \\\"I would ask for the pause rule in one sentence: timeScale 0, fixedUpdate silent, update still reads keys. The guide and the type comment do not say the same thing.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n40→    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Mint Dial\\\",\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/exit-interview.json\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 22:16:07\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Sports\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"Isometric island, with a fixed camera for each activity\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"Pixel Engine 0.46.0, three.js r186, Rapier 0.20 as bundled, esbuild 0.28.2\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"The engine native pixel look, with new models for the scale, stations, and props\\\",\\n    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"Engine ClipDefs compiled onto the hero rig and played with AnimationMixer\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Engine Song and SoundDef data, plus a Web Audio formant voice. Music defaults to 10 percent.\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, own card, 1 to 4 players. Family Hour is local on one screen.\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"node tools/test.mjs, Playwright 1.63 Chromium with the five software WebGPU flags, WebKit and Firefox for the missing-WebGPU path, and the engine headless runner\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"The director plan already included engine and hub research and spikes. I read PLAN.md, the engine guide where the recipes pointed, and the hub README, and I checked the Dot table in code. I did not do extra research on the source beyond that plan.\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"Ten issues. The expert pier jump scored two stars, pause let the pose clock move on the frame the button went down, two songs had uneven pattern lengths, a tray board lookup named a variable that was not in scope, a few model parts floated, the seagull was spoken as the scale, a dev-tool page could not go back, the prompt could draw past a short screen, the scale's voice measured just under the loudness line, and the About screen kept only the first six lines so later source fields never appeared.\\\",\\n    \\\"Two were game-breaking. The pier jump sat under the three-star line until takeoff recentred the dot, and the pose kept playing for one frame after pause. The others failed a data check, a voice check, a menu, or the About screen, and they were fixed before the hand-in.\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful test was the idle-versus-expert bot pass on every activity. It is what caught the pier jump sitting under the three-star line.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful test was the glyph scan. Every line already used the allowed characters, so it passed on the first run and did not change the game.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"Headless stepping, the pixel HUD, and a real input recorder made a week of play testable without a screen.\\\",\\n    \\\"I guessed wrong about pause. At timeScale 0 the headless stepper still calls fixedUpdate, and that call happens before update reads the pause key, so the pose clock moved unless the sim refused the step. Menu presses do still arrive. The type note reads as if those presses are dropped. Capture also needs all five Vulkan flags or the picture comes back blank.\\\",\\n    \\\"The centre-of-balance itself. The engine will move a character. It will not sway a polite dot, keep a week, or speak in formants.\\\",\\n    \\\"The hardest part was trusting the frame clock. Game time, the press window, and the hub clock are three different clocks, and only one of them is allowed to move a score.\\\",\\n    \\\"None. pixel-engine.js is the kit file, byte for byte.\\\",\\n    \\\"I would give the music bus a default of silence until the game sets it, so a shared browser profile cannot leave yesterday volume on today game.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The plan named the mechanics, the sentences, and the tests, so the work was building a game rather than inventing one.\\\",\\n    \\\"The cut list in the plan and the instruction to finish everything on this computer disagree. I followed the instruction and shipped the activities the cut list would drop.\\\",\\n    \\\"The hardest piece was the pier jump star line. The same bot that holds a pose will dive off a dock, and the flight begins wherever the dot was left.\\\",\\n    \\\"I would ask for the pause rule in one sentence: timeScale 0, fixedUpdate silent, update still reads keys. The guide and the type comment do not say the same thing.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Mint Dial\\\",\\n\",\"total_lines\":58}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"2172b683-83f2-40ed-bd28-48a6153479dc"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_372","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The title screen looks correct.\n\nThe stray \"? Start\" is likely the focus marker \"> \" rendered as a question mark because the font lacks that character.\n\nThe focus marker bug is real and visible on every menu. I will replace it with a character from HUD_EXTRA, such as \"*\" or \"-\".\n\nA small sand rectangle will mark the focused menu row instead of a character. This avoids relying on a missing glyph.\n\nThe boot screenshot confirms the visible bug. I will fix the focus marker and re-run browser boots to verify the screenshot is clean. Widget positions may shift slightly, but the fit tests should still pass.\n\nThe focused row now draws a 6×6 sand rectangle at the left margin instead of a character. Label width is reduced to 26 or 34 characters to keep the text and cursor on screen. The hover test locates rows by position, so widget placement must stay accurate.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c8232b82-1475-4396-8ad6-df2a5cc8eb29-113","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"> ","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/app.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3360,"output_tokens":1353,"cache_read_input_tokens":174208,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"d22f0c79-7c0a-4bb7-aa8d-db2b77b8787a"}
