{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_376","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Waiting for a process to complete. The timeout is set to 180 seconds.\n\nDrafting PROGRESS and plan edits in my head. I will wait for the suite to pass before writing them, since the HTML rebuild runs during testing. I also spotted an eleventh issue: a ? cursor on the boot screenshot.\n\nEditing about.js now would race with the running suite. Node tests may already have imported the old version, and build.mjs could run before or after my edit. The test only checks that feedback strings appear on the pages, not the exact wording, so a mid-run change is risky.\n\nI will let the current suite finish with the original \"Ten issues\" wording. The ? cursor bug was found in a previous screenshot and is being fixed now. Afterward, I will update the feedback to eleven issues and include the cursor. The HTML may still show the old text if the build already ran.\n\nThe node test compares in-memory pages to in-memory constants, so it would pass with either wording. The HTML rebuild is a separate process that reads the file on startup, so saving now risks mismatching the HTML against the test's stale memory.\n\nChecking the HTML file's modification time or the node process to see if build.mjs has started. If it hasn't, I can update the feedback now. If it has, the HTML would still say \"Ten\" while the source says \"Eleven\", requiring another rebuild.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-29285a26-8f6e-44ce-bff7-0f7acbdbb330-117","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"ps -o pid,etime,cmd -C node | head -20; stat -c '%y' \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607.html\"","description":"See if the suite has reached the HTML build yet"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":589,"output_tokens":828,"