{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_378","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Checking test.exit, browser log, and png top.\n\nThe suite passed. I will update feedback to include the cursor, run --fast, and build.mjs. The screenshots still represent the game state since they reflect the tested HTML with the cursor fix. The test.log is from the ten-issues HTML.\n\nThe saved test.log is still 12/12 for nearly identical code. The node test requires the full feedback string to appear in flattened about pages, so a longer sentence still wraps and passes --fast verification. I will run --fast and build.mjs to ensure the hand-in matches. I should not claim the browser log reflects a build containing the eleven-sentence update.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ab207692-8c4d-42f9-8e00-aa83098b25d4-119","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"SCRATCH=\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/implementer\"\necho \"EXIT=$(cat \"$SCRATCH/test.exit\")\"\necho \"=== test.log ===\"\ncat \"$SCRATCH/test.log\"\necho \"=== browser ===\"\nrg -n \"FAIL|boot |drive |phone |widgets |audio |family |shots |webkit |firefox \" \"$SCRATCH/browser.log\"\necho \"=== hub titles ===\"\nrg -n \"pass true|title true|server \" \"$SCRATCH/hub.log\"\npython3 << 'PY'\nimport struct, zlib\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path(\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/implementer/boot-1.png\")\ndata=p.read_bytes(); pos=8; w=h=color=None; idat=b''\nwhile pos < len(data):\n    n,typ=struct.unpack('>I4s', data[pos:pos+8]); chunk=data[pos+8:pos+8+n]; pos+=12+n\n    if typ==b'IHDR':\n        w,h,bit,color,*_=struct.unpack('>IIBBBBB', chunk)\n    elif typ==b'IDAT': idat+=chunk\n    elif typ==b'IEND': break\nraw=zlib.decompress(idat); bpp={6:4,2:3}[color]; stride=w*bpp\nrows=[]; i=0; prev=bytearray(stride)\ndef paeth(a,b,c):\n    p=a+b-c; pa,pb,pc=abs(p-a),abs(p-b),abs(p-c)\n    return a if pa<=pb and pa<=pc else b if pb<=pc else c\nfor y in range(h):\n    f=raw[i]; i+=1; row=bytearray(raw[i:i+stride]); i+=stride\n    if f==1:\n        for x in range(stride):\n            row[x]=(row[x]+(row[x-bpp] if x>=bpp else 0))&255\n    elif f==2:\n        for x in range(stride): row[x]=(row[x]+prev[x])&255\n    elif f==3:\n        for x in range(stride):\n            left=row[x-bpp] if x>=bpp else 0\n            row[x]=(row[x]+((left+prev[x])//2))&255\n    elif f==4:\n        for x in range(stride):\n            a=row[x-bpp] if x>=bpp else 0; b=prev[x]; c=prev[x-bpp] if x>=bpp else 0\n            row[x]=(row[x]+paeth(a,b,c))&255\n    rows.append(bytes(row)); prev=row\n# sample a horizontal run around the Start row. HUD is stretched.\n# Find sand-colored pixels (16764277 -> r,g,b)\n# sand hex: 16764277 = 0xFFCD75? let me compute\nprint('size', w, h)\n# print a coarse map of non-sky pixels in the upper third left side\nsand=0\nfor y in range(80, 280, 2):\n    for x in range(0, 500, 2):\n        r,g,b=rows[y][x*bpp:(x+1)*bpp][:3]\n        if r>180 and g>140 and b<140: sand+=1\nprint('sandish pixels in start area', sand)\nPY","description":"Confirm the focus-marker suite passed"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1305,"output_tokens":1245,"cache_read_input_tokens":183424,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"f2467fc7-f5b0-48d4-a6ca-2fbb2308576a"}
