hort days: morning weigh-in (stillness, lean, or chase, plus one absurd question), a free island of four stations, at least one activity, hammock, evening report, then the next morning. Shown Wobble Age is the true age plus 7 until the confession, which subtracts exactly 7 from every chart point; play then continues into an open Week 2. There is no lose state. Stars are 0–3; Drips are `2 + 3×stars + floor(playSeconds/30)` plus +5 for the day’s prescription; jar milestones unlock locker items; saves are versioned JSON (in-memory fallback if storage is missing) and survive reload. Every PLAN.md §5 activity is playable to a results screen, including hard versions: Holding Still poses, Reps (scrubbed motion, “last one” gag), Hoop Economics, Step Class, Coconut Header, Slackline, Vitamin Tray, Island Jog, Pier Jump, and The Long Stand’s 90 s distraction timeline. An idle bot finishes with 0★ and no throw; an expert bot scores at least 2★ (3★ on easy activities). Player-facing world text uses the short clinical voice, does not use Nintendo names (Wii, Mii, Balance Board, Wii Fit Trainer, Wuhu, Fit Age) except the Source field and the filename, and does not joke about real bodies or make health claims. At least 120 lines exist beyond PLAN.md’s samples, including 0/1/2/3★ lines per activity.\\n4. **10-foot controls, dev mode, attract, audio.** One pixel HUD serves pad, keyboard, and mouse (no DOM menus, no dense data screens). Prompts follow the last device: PlayStation glyphs by default, an Xbox glyph option, keycaps, and mouse buttons. Pause sets `timeScale` to 0 (simulation frozen, menus still read input) and opens Dev Tools with live sliders for the PLAN.md §10 balance, breath/reps, rhythm, games, and economy variables, plus reset-tab and reset-all. After 10 s with no input on the title or any menu, a looping attract demo plays real scenes of every activity family (cheats allowed) until any input returns to the title; it does not start during play, pause, or a hub session. Touch-only devices get no touch controls, the text “Controller or keyboard required”, a settings button, and a running attract loop. All music, SFX, and voices are code (no audio files). Voices are Animalese/Simlish gibberish: the same word always yields the same syllables, a “?” rises in pitch, and an offline render is non-silent with Ounce’s mean pitch above Coach’s. Each song is loud enough that the sum of track volumes × 0.1 × 0.8 is at least 0.03.\\n5. **Local and online Medley.** Family Hour seats up to 4 on one screen (each pad by its own index, plus keyboard-and-mouse); lanes move independently through The Medley — three timed events (a stillness pose, a beat activity, a balance-lean activity), each normalised, then a podium. In an AI Hub session the game skips title, attract, dev mode, and saves; shows its own ready card; plays from the hub clock in ghost mode (progress sent even at score 0, other mats are lerped and never simulated, one result at the end or on time-up); and all four PLAN.md §17 harness URLs (1 player, 2 players, 4 players with latency/jitter/loss, and host-leave) report pass. With no session, the normal title still boots. If WebGPU is missing, the engine’s “Failed to start: WebGPU unavailable” message shows and, in a session, the failure is reported without an uncaught page error.\\n\\n## Verification plan\\n1. **gating:** Add or update real tests that drive the shipped Dot, scoring, Wobble Age, save, voice syllabifier, activity scenes, and menu flow from their real start states (no mocked unit under test, no re-implementation, no hardcoded title). Run `node tools/test.mjs` from the dev folder after the code it covers is in place. Capture stdout/stderr to `{SCRATCH}/test.log`. Pass only if the log ends in a one-line all-passed count, prints no failures, and the assertions cover: Dot bands and 45/70/90 stars; every activity idle 0★ vs expert ≥2★ and correct Drips; a scripted fresh-save week through Day 7, confession −7, and Week 2; save reload, corrupt JSON, and missing storage; pause freeze and resume; every dev slider live plus both resets; attract at 10 s on title and on a menu, no trigger in play, any input exits; medley windows and a ghost lane that does not simulate; stable syllabify and a rising question; `pixel-engine.js` hash equals the kit zip.\\n2. **gating:** Launch the root HTML twice from `file://` with Playwright Chromium and all five flags `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader`. Each run must have zero page errors, a title-screen state that names `{Title}`, and music volume exactly 0.10. Step the engine, composite `renderer.capture()` with the HUD, and save PNGs under `{SCRATCH}/boot-1.png` and `{SCRATCH}/boot-2.png`. The drawing buffer must match the fill-aspect target size and be substantially painted (not a few pixels). A driven confirm or pointer hover must change a recorded UI state (focus or leaving the title prompt). Both runs must agree. If capture throws for an environmental reason, save that log to `{SCRATCH}/capture-error.txt` and pass on the state assertions only. A capture that succeeds and is blank or nearly blank is a failure, not a fallback.\\n3. **gating:** In the same browser suite (included in `node tools/test.mjs`, not a separate unchecked script), on the built HTML: a gamepad stub confirms with Cross and records PlayStation prompts, the Xbox setting switches glyphs, a key switches to keycaps, a mouse move switches to mouse prompts, hover moves focus, and click activates — all readable from game state. A phone profile shows the controller-required message, a settings control, no touch gameplay, and attract running. Two stub pads plus keyboard move three Family Hour lanes independently. After a click, an AnalyserNode reads non-silent music and SFX; an OfflineAudioContext voice render has RMS > 0.02 and Ounce’s mean pitch above Coach’s. Widget rects fit at 1920×1080, 1280×720, and 640×360. WebKit (iPhone profile) and Firefox show the WebGPU-unavailable message and no page error. Write the run log to `{SCRATCH}/browser.log`.\\n4. **gating:** Serve the built game with the hub harness on `127.0.0.1` and an OS-picked port (stop that PID only). Confirm the document title is this game, then run the four harness URLs in criterion 5. Capture results to `{SCRATCH}/hub.log`. Pass only if each reaches `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'` and `window.__hubCheck.pass` is true. Then load the game with no session and confirm the normal title still boots (`{SCRATCH}/nosession.log`).\\n5. **evidence:** `tools/shot.mjs` (or the same step-then-composite path) at 1920×1080 for title, one activity, the island, and pause/dev. Screenshots are for composition only; they do not replace steps 1–4. Save under `{SCRATCH}/shots/`.\\n\\n## Non-goals\\n- FPS targets, GPU optimization, or a performance budget (explicitly deferred).\\n- Real BMI, weight, or health data; Balance Board hardware; Miis; Nintendo names, tunes, or level layouts. Source-faithful mechanics ship only under PLAN.md’s original names and the no-body-shaming rule.\\n- A second authored seven-day story. Week 2 is open-ended continuation, not new daily scripts.\\n- DOM or web-style menus, touch gameplay controls, in-session chat, custom names, `alert`, or navigation.\\n- Editing `pixel-engine.js`. Bundling it into the HTML is not an edit.\\n- A physical pad, a human listener, a second human, a television, or real iOS Safari. Stand-ins in TASK.md are enough.\\n- Proving the silent list of 50 title ideas. Only the RNG-chosen title and the filename pattern are required.\\n\\n## Assumed scope\\n- Workspace root (this folder): the HTML deliverable, `exit-interview.json`, `PROGRESS.md`.\\n- Dev subfolder `{Title}-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/`: game code, tests, vendored kit and hub client.\\n- Download `https://github.com/michaelcrosato/riftlight/releases/latest/download/pixel-engine.zip` (PLAN.md was spiked on kit 0.46.0; if newer, read its changelog from 0.46.0). Copy the zip’s `pixel-engine/` contents into the dev folder. Fetch hub `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js`, and `README.md` from `https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub` into `vendor/hub/`, unmodified.\\n- Tooling already on the machine: Node, esbuild, Playwright 1.63 (do not run `playwright install`). Python only if a static server is required for the harness.\\n- Wii Fit’s defining mechanics (public guides): a centre-of-balance dot kept in a zone; a daily body test that yields one age-like number; yoga holds, strength reps, aerobics, and balance games; a demonstrating trainer; banked time that unlocks activities; star ratings; several players on one console. PLAN.md already remaps these. That remap is the contract, not Nintendo’s names or BMI copy.\\n\\n## Implementation approach\\nKeep designer data (activities, lines, week, medley, songs) separate from scene code, and keep the Dot, drivers, scores, Wobble Age, Drips, and syllable splitter pure so Node can run them with no GPU. Scenes should only apply that state. Expose a small debug state on the running game (scene, score, device, tunables) so browser checks read state instead of pixels. Inline the bundle in the one HTML file so `file://` needs no imports. Do not change `pixel-engine.js`; record its sha256 at unzip time. Follow PLAN.md’s build order and stop after each slice with the tests that cover it green. The cut list in PLAN.md §19 is not a target: those activities can be built here.\\n\\n## Task checklist\\n- [x] Download the kit and hub files, record the engine sha256, scaffold the dev folder and the single-file build, and boot a title scene from `file://`.\\n- [x] Implement the Dot, drivers, actions, device tracking, tunables, pixel HUD (mixed case, glyphs, prompts), settings, pause, and dev sliders; lock the bot ring-time tests.\\n- [x] Ship Holding Still end to end (avatar, coach, results, voice, music) and check the bot star table before adding more activities.\\n- [x] Build the island, weigh-in, seven-day loop, saves, report, sweat jar, and locker unlocks; start the scripted playthrough test.\\n- [x] Add Hoop, Reps, Header, Step, Slackline, Vitamin Tray, Pier Jump, and Island Jog, each with idle-vs-expert bot tests and original lines.\\n- [x] Add The Medley, Family Hour, and the AI Hub ghost card; run all four harness URLs.\\n- [x] Add attract mode, the dev tools tab, the touch-only gate, Hall of Numbers, ferry, daily beats, Long Stand, confession (−7), credits, and the full code-only soundtrack.\\n- [x] Write About/Credits from one data source, emit `exit-interview.json`, update `PROGRESS.md`, and capture `node tools/test.mjs`, two `file://` launches, and the hub log under `{SCRATCH}`.\\n\\n## Risks / Contradictions\\n- PLAN.md §19 allows cutting Pier Jump, Vitamin Tray, Island Jog, and Overhead Mortgage if scope slips. The objective requires everything that can be done on this computer, and those activities can. A cut is not a pass unless `PROGRESS.md` records a concrete environment blocker. Never cut the Dot, Holding Still, Reps, Hoop, Header, Step, Weigh-In, the island, the week, Long Stand, the Medley, attract, dev mode, Settings, or About.\\n- WebGPU screenshots are often blank or `capture()` throws unless all five Vulkan/swiftshader flags are set. A successful blank buffer is an app failure. Only a launcher or capture error that is clearly environmental may fall back to state assertions, and that error must be saved.\\n- WebKit and Firefox on this machine have no `navigator.gpu`, so they can only show the WebGPU-unavailable message. The playable boot is Chromium.\\n- `earlyoom` kills the largest browser under memory pressure. Keep at most two browsers open. Other agents share ports; bind `127.0.0.1` with a port the OS picks, and kill only PIDs this work started.\\n- The required filename stem contains a space (“Wii Fit”) because TASK.md substitutes SOURCE literally. Do not rename the source token.\\n- Player-facing text must avoid Nintendo names, but Source Information and the filename must say Wii Fit. Those two places are the exception.\\n\\n## Deviations\\n- Mode changes cut instantly. There is no screen iris.\\n- Screens share one World and one App.\\n- Vitamin Tray slides vitamins with a tilt formula on three lane boards. It does not use Rapier bodies.\\n- Pier Jump recentres the dot when the flight starts, so the jump is not scored from the crouch.\\n- Attract mode, the medley, and bot-driven activities skip the intro.\\n- The session card uses palette stand-ins for the four seat colours.\\n- A join press that claims a seat does not also activate the focused menu row on that same frame.\\n- On the name screen, Backspace edits the name and does not also leave the screen.\\n- Pause is taken at the start of fixed, before the sim step, because the headless stepper still runs fixedUpdate on the frame timeScale becomes 0.\\n\",\"total_lines\":66}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-920f88f2-5f16-4d28-bee6-f8e83a542519-10","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→Build the game PLAN.md describes. Take your file names and what to hand in from TASK.md, which is filled in for you. Keep your progress in PROGRESS.md, so you can pick up where you were after your context is compacted.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→Build the game PLAN.md describes. Take your file names and what to hand in from TASK.md, which is filled in for you. Keep your progress in PROGRESS.md, so you can pick up where you were after your context is compacted.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/STAGE.md\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"Build the game PLAN.md describes. Take your file names and what to hand in from TASK.md, which is filled in for you. Keep your progress in PROGRESS.md, so you can pick up where you were after your context is compacted.\\n\",\"total_lines\":1}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-920f88f2-5f16-4d28-bee6-f8e83a542519-11","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→# Mint Dial\\n\\nThe hand-in is in this folder: `Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607.html` and `exit-interview.json`. The dev folder uses the same stem. `src/data/about.js` is the only copy of the source fields and the feedback. `tools/build.mjs` writes the HTML and the exit interview from it.\\n\\n## Shipped\\n\\nA week with Ounce the scale. Weigh-in, three guest slots, the ferry, seven days, the island, every planned activity (including Pier Jump, Vitamin Tray, Island Jog, Overhead Mortgage, and The Long Stand), the jar, the confession that subtracts 7, and an open Week 2. Family Hour runs three medley events for up to four players. An AI Hub session uses ghost mode and its own card. Attract mode, dev-tool sliders, and the touch gate are in. Music, effects, and the two voices are code.\\n\\n## Verification\\n10→\\n`node tools/test.mjs` from the dev folder printed `12/12 passed` and no failure lines.\\n\\nTwo `file://` Chromium launches, with the five software WebGPU flags, showed the title Mint Dial, music bus 0.10, and no page errors. Both captures are 1281×720 and painted. The saved frames show the title, the tagline, and the medical line. Prompts follow Cross, Xbox A, Enter, and click. Hover moved the focus from Gentle to More, and the click activated. A phone profile shows “Controller or keyboard required”, a settings control, and attract, and it does not start play from a touch. Widget rects fit at 1920×1080, 1280×720, and 640×360. An analyser read the mix, and an offline voice render was above 0.02 RMS with Ounce’s pitch above Coach’s. Three Family Hour lanes moved. WebKit and Firefox show “Failed to start: WebGPU unavailable” and raise no page error.\\n\\nThe hub harness on `127.0.0.1:38059` passed all four URLs (`players=1`, `players=2`, the lossy four-player case, and host-leave). With no session, the title still boots. JavaScript was served as `text/javascript`.\\n\\n`pixel-engine.js` sha256 is `80408b4c72ef08be3ec628d578f8b008644c1c7e447a4cc8c5979b08212e78aa`, the same as the kit.\\n\\n## About\\n20→\\nThe About screen pages every source field, the three feedback sections, the kit credits, the medical sentence, and the full kit credits text. Next, Previous, and the shoulder buttons move between pages.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→# Mint Dial\\n\\nThe hand-in is in this folder: `Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607.html` and `exit-interview.json`. The dev folder uses the same stem. `src/data/about.js` is the only copy of the source fields and the feedback. `tools/build.mjs` writes the HTML and the exit interview from it.\\n\\n## Shipped\\n\\nA week with Ounce the scale. Weigh-in, three guest slots, the ferry, seven days, the island, every planned activity (including Pier Jump, Vitamin Tray, Island Jog, Overhead Mortgage, and The Long Stand), the jar, the confession that subtracts 7, and an open Week 2. Family Hour runs three medley events for up to four players. An AI Hub session uses ghost mode and its own card. Attract mode, dev-tool sliders, and the touch gate are in. Music, effects, and the two voices are code.\\n\\n## Verification\\n10→\\n`node tools/test.mjs` from the dev folder printed `12/12 passed` and no failure lines.\\n\\nTwo `file://` Chromium launches, with the five software WebGPU flags, showed the title Mint Dial, music bus 0.10, and no page errors. Both captures are 1281×720 and painted. The saved frames show the title, the tagline, and the medical line. Prompts follow Cross, Xbox A, Enter, and click. Hover moved the focus from Gentle to More, and the click activated. A phone profile shows “Controller or keyboard required”, a settings control, and attract, and it does not start play from a touch. Widget rects fit at 1920×1080, 1280×720, and 640×360. An analyser read the mix, and an offline voice render was above 0.02 RMS with Ounce’s pitch above Coach’s. Three Family Hour lanes moved. WebKit and Firefox show “Failed to start: WebGPU unavailable” and raise no page error.\\n\\nThe hub harness on `127.0.0.1:38059` passed all four URLs (`players=1`, `players=2`, the lossy four-player case, and host-leave). With no session, the title still boots. JavaScript was served as `text/javascript`.\\n\\n`pixel-engine.js` sha256 is `80408b4c72ef08be3ec628d578f8b008644c1c7e447a4cc8c5979b08212e78aa`, the same as the kit.\\n\\n## About\\n20→\\nThe About screen pages every source field, the three feedback sections, the kit credits, the medical sentence, and the full kit credits text. Next, Previous, and the shoulder buttons move between pages.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/PROGRESS.md\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"# Mint Dial\\n\\nThe hand-in is in this folder: `Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607.html` and `exit-interview.json`. The dev folder uses the same stem. `src/data/about.js` is the only copy of the source fields and the feedback. `tools/build.mjs` writes the HTML and the exit interview from it.\\n\\n## Shipped\\n\\nA week with Ounce the scale. Weigh-in, three guest slots, the ferry, seven days, the island, every planned activity (including Pier Jump, Vitamin Tray, Island Jog, Overhead Mortgage, and The Long Stand), the jar, the confession that subtracts 7, and an open Week 2. Family Hour runs three medley events for up to four players. An AI Hub session uses ghost mode and its own card. Attract mode, dev-tool sliders, and the touch gate are in. Music, effects, and the two voices are code.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n`node tools/test.mjs` from the dev folder printed `12/12 passed` and no failure lines.\\n\\nTwo `file://` Chromium launches, with the five software WebGPU flags, showed the title Mint Dial, music bus 0.10, and no page errors. Both captures are 1281×720 and painted. The saved frames show the title, the tagline, and the medical line. Prompts follow Cross, Xbox A, Enter, and click. Hover moved the focus from Gentle to More, and the click activated. A phone profile shows “Controller or keyboard required”, a settings control, and attract, and it does not start play from a touch. Widget rects fit at 1920×1080, 1280×720, and 640×360. An analyser read the mix, and an offline voice render was above 0.02 RMS with Ounce’s pitch above Coach’s. Three Family Hour lanes moved. WebKit and Firefox show “Failed to start: WebGPU unavailable” and raise no page error.\\n\\nThe hub harness on `127.0.0.1:38059` passed all four URLs (`players=1`, `players=2`, the lossy four-player case, and host-leave). With no session, the title still boots. JavaScript was served as `text/javascript`.\\n\\n`pixel-engine.js` sha256 is `80408b4c72ef08be3ec628d578f8b008644c1c7e447a4cc8c5979b08212e78aa`, the same as the kit.\\n\\n## About\\n\\nThe About screen pages every source field, the three feedback sections, the kit credits, the medical sentence, and the full kit credits text. Next, Previous, and the shoulder buttons move between pages.\\n\",\"total_lines\":21}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"ee7db8cc-18b9-4625-bf6f-a3b50387221c"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_396","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The hand-in files match the requirements.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The JSON on disk already looks like the About source. I will compare them in code and check that the HTML and the test evidence still match."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8461eff9-4d14-4dd3-8d9e-e070555446ea-12","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"node --input-type=module << 'JS'\nimport { readFileSync, statSync } from 'node:fs';\nimport { exitInterview } from './src/data/about.js';\n\nconst root = '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work';\nconst jsonPath = root + '/exit-interview.json';\nconst htmlPath = root + '/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607.html';\nconst aboutPath = new URL('./src/data/about.js', import.meta.url).pathname;\nconst disk = JSON.parse(readFileSync(jsonPath, 'utf8'));\nconst live = exitInterview();\nconst keys = ['sourceInformation','testingFeedback','engineFeedback','promptFeedback','aiHub'];\nconst srcKeys = ['date','source','plan','genre','perspective','tech','artDirection','animation','audio','online','testing','research','environment','model','usage'];\nconst hubKeys = ['name','tagline','description','type','genre','source','series','players','controls','tags'];\nconst problems = [];\nfor (const k of keys) if (!(k in disk)) problems.push('missing '+k);\nif (JSON.stringify(disk) !== JSON.stringify(live)) {\n  problems.push('JSON differs from exitInterview()');\n  for (const k of keys) {\n    if (JSON.stringify(disk[k]) !== JSON.stringify(live[k])) problems.push('diff '+k);\n  }\n}\nfor (const k of srcKeys) if (!disk.sourceInformation?.[k]) problems.push('empty source '+k);\nif (disk.sourceInformation?.usage !== 'added on import') problems.push('usage');\nif (disk.testingFeedback?.length !== 4) problems.push('testing count');\nif (disk.engineFeedback?.length !== 6) problems.push('engine count');\nif (disk.promptFeedback?.length !== 4) problems.push('prompt count');\nif (!disk.testingFeedback?.[0]?.startsWith('Eleven issues')) problems.push('eleven');\nfor (const k of hubKeys) {\n  const v = disk.aiHub?.[k];\n  if (v == null || v === '' || (Array.isArray(v) && !v.length)) problems.push('empty hub '+k);\n}\nconst html = readFileSync(htmlPath, 'utf8');\nconst needles = [\n  'Eleven issues',\n  'This is not medical advice. Ounce is a scale.',\n  'added on import',\n  'Kenney (CC0), three.js (MIT), Rapier (Apache-2.0), Sweetie 16.',\n  '<title>Mint Dial</title>',\n];\nfor (const n of needles) if (!html.includes(n)) problems.push('html missing: '+n);\nif (/<script[^>]+src=/i.test(html)) problems.push('external script');\nconst mt = (p) => statSync(p).mtime.toISOString();\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify({\n  problems,\n  aboutMtime: mt(aboutPath),\n  jsonMtime: mt(jsonPath),\n  htmlMtime: mt(htmlPath),\n  htmlBytes: html.length,\n  tags: disk.aiHub.tags,\n}, null, 2));\nJS\nstat -c '%y %n' \\\n  \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/implementer/test.log\" \\\n  \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/implementer/test.exit\" \\\n  \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/implementer/browser.log\" \\\n  \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/implementer/hub.log\" \\\n  \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/implementer/nosession.log\" \\\n  \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/implementer/boot-1.png\" \\\n  \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/implementer/boot-2.