record sha256, scaffold dev folder and title\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"Implement Dot, drivers, actions, device, tunables, HUD, pause, dev sliders\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"Ship Holding Still end to end and lock bot star tests\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"Build island, weigh-in, seven-day loop, saves, report, jar, locker\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"Add remaining activities with idle-vs-expert bot tests and lines\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"Fix remaining --fast failures (rng scan, pause freeze, week boot) and get 11/11\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"Fix About HUD so every source field and the full feedback are visible, then rebuild\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"Hand in exit-interview.json, PROGRESS.md, checklist and deviations\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"Confirm exit-interview.json matches about.js and the three hand-in files are in the workspace root\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"Rebuild HTML and exit-interview.json only if they differ from the current About source\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"cancelled\"}],\"state\":{\"todos\":{\"1\":{\"content\":\"Download kit and hub, record sha256, scaffold dev folder and title\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"2\":{\"content\":\"Implement Dot, drivers, actions, device, tunables, HUD, pause, dev sliders\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"3\":{\"content\":\"Ship Holding Still end to end and lock bot star tests\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"4\":{\"content\":\"Build island, weigh-in, seven-day loop, saves, report, jar, locker\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"5\":{\"content\":\"Add remaining activities with idle-vs-expert bot tests and lines\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"6\":{\"content\":\"Fix remaining --fast failures (rng scan, pause freeze, week boot) and get 11/11\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"7\":{\"content\":\"Fix About HUD so every source field and the full feedback are visible, then rebuild\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"8\":{\"content\":\"Hand in exit-interview.json, PROGRESS.md, checklist and deviations\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"confirm-handin\":{\"content\":\"Confirm exit-interview.json matches about.js and the three hand-in files are in the workspace root\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"rebuild-if-stale\":{\"content\":\"Rebuild HTML and exit-interview.json only if they differ from the current About source\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"cancelled\"}}}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"9282ab51-cd70-4e4d-8fc5-286885eb7161"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_399","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The hand-in is confirmed. I am preparing a complete finishing reply that includes all Source Information fields, Testing/Engine/Prompt Feedback, kit credits, and the medical sentence.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The hand-in in this folder matches the current About source. `exit-interview.json` is the same object `exitInterview()` returns, the HTML was built from that source, and `PROGRESS.md` is beside them. Nothing needed a rebuild.\n\n`Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607.html` is the self-contained game. The dev folder uses the same stem. `node tools/test.mjs` printed `12/12 passed`. Two `file://` boots showed the title Mint Dial and a music bus of 0.10, with no page errors. All four hub URLs passed on `127.0.0.1:38059`, and a launch with no session still boots the title. `pixel-engine.js` is unchanged (`80408b4c72ef08be3ec628d578f8b008644c1c7e447a4cc8c5979b08212e78aa`).\n\n## Source Information\n\n- Date: 2026-11-04 22:16:07\n- Source: Wii Fit\n- Plan: PLAN.md\n- Genre: Sports\n- Perspective: Isometric island, with a fixed camera for each activity\n- Tech: Pixel Engine 0.46.0, three.js r186, Rapier 0.20 as bundled, esbuild 0.28.2\n- Art Direction: The engine native pixel look, with new models for the scale, stations, and props\n- Animation: Engine ClipDefs compiled onto the hero rig and played with AnimationMixer\n- Audio: Engine Song and SoundDef data, plus a Web Audio formant voice. Music defaults to 10 percent.\n- Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, own card, 1 to 4 players. Family Hour is local on one screen.\n- Testing: node tools/test.mjs, Playwright 1.63 Chromium with the five software WebGPU flags, WebKit and Firefox for the missing-WebGPU path, and the engine headless runner\n- Research: The director plan already included engine and hub research and spikes. I read PLAN.md, the engine guide where the recipes pointed, and the hub README, and I checked the Dot table in code. I did not do extra research on the source beyond that plan.\n- Environment: Grok CLI (headless); Linux\n- Model: xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\n- Usage: added on import\n\n## Testing Feedback\n\nEleven issues. The expert pier jump scored two stars, pause let the pose clock move on the frame the button went down, two songs had uneven pattern lengths, a tray board lookup named a variable that was not in scope, a few model parts floated, the seagull was spoken as the scale, a dev-tool page could not go back, the prompt could draw past a short screen, the scale's voice measured just under the loudness line, the About screen kept only the first six lines so later source fields never appeared, and the menu cursor was a greater-than sign the font cannot draw, so it showed as a question mark.\n\nTwo were game-breaking. The pier jump sat under the three-star line until takeoff recentred the dot, and the pose kept playing for one frame after pause. The others failed a data check, a voice check, a menu, or the About screen, and they were fixed before the hand-in.\n\nThe most helpful test was the idle-versus-expert bot pass on every activity. It is what caught the pier jump sitting under the three-star line.\n\nThe least helpful test was the glyph scan. Every line already used the allowed characters, so it passed on the first run and did not change the game.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n\nHeadless stepping, the pixel HUD, and a real input recorder made a week of play testable without a screen.\n\nI guessed wrong about pause. At timeScale 0 the headless stepper still calls fixedUpdate, and that call happens before update reads the pause key, so the pose clock moved unless the sim refused the step. Menu presses do still arrive. The type note reads as if those presses are dropped. Capture also needs all five Vulkan flags or the picture comes back blank.\n\nThe centre-of-balance itself. The engine will move a character. It will not sway a polite dot, keep a week, or speak in formants.\n\nThe hardest part was trusting the frame clock. Game time, the press window, and the hub clock are three different clocks, and only one of them is allowed to move a score.\n\nNone. pixel-engine.js is the kit file, byte for byte.\n\nI would give the music bus a default of silence until the game sets it, so a shared browser profile cannot leave yesterday volume on today game.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n\nThe plan named the mechanics, the sentences, and the tests, so the work was building a game rather than inventing one.\n\nThe cut list in the plan and the instruction to finish everything on this computer disagree. I followed the instruction and shipped the activities the cut list would drop.\n\nThe hardest piece was the pier jump star line. The same bot that holds a pose will dive off a dock, and the flight begins wherever the dot was left.\n\nI would ask for the pause rule in one sentence: timeScale 0, fixedUpdate silent, update still reads keys. The guide and the type comment do not say the same thing.\n\nKit credits: Kenney (CC0), three.js (MIT), Rapier (Apache-2.0), Sweetie 16.\n\nThis is not medical advice. Ounce is a scale."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1083,"output_tokens":1337,"cache_read_input_tokens":52864,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"85664e3c-655c-4d16-969d-ec6e06cf272a"}
