ed on import\\\"},\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\\"your answer to each Testing Feedback question, in order\\\"],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\\"your answer to each Engine Feedback question, in order\\\"],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\\"your answer to each Prompt Feedback question, in order\\\"],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"the game's title, as on its title screen\\\",\\n    \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"a few words to go under the title\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"one or two sentences for the catalogue\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game, Tech demo or Tool\\\",\\n120→    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"one of Action, Adventure, Fighting, Flight, Horror, Kids & Learning, Life Sim, Platformer, Puzzle, Racing, RPG, Shooter, Simulation, Sports, Stealth, Strategy\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"the work it's based on, e.g. Moby-Dick\\\",\\n    \\\"series\\\": \\\"its franchise, e.g. Star Fox, or empty\\\",\\n    \\\"players\\\": \\\"how many can play: 1, 1–2 or 1–4\\\",\\n    \\\"controls\\\": \\\"the controls, in one line\\\",\\n    \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"3 to 6 lowercase tags, e.g. 2d, 3d, arcade, story, co-op, versus, first-person, third-person, top-down, side-scrolling, pixel art, low-poly, retro, sci-fi, fantasy, comedy, vehicles, boss fights, exploration\\\"]\\n  }\\n}\\nThe catalogue's model, effort, CLI, date and usage come from the run's record after you finish, so they aren't asked here.\\n\\n130→Testing Feedback\\n\\n- How many issues did testing catch?\\n- How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?\\n- What was the most helpful test you ran?\\n- What was the least helpful test you ran?\\n\\nEngine Feedback\\n\\n- What did you like most about the engine?\\n140→- Did you get stuck or guess wrong?\\n- What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?\\n- What was the hardest part about using the engine?\\n- What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)\\n- If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?\\n\\nPrompt Feedback\\n\\n- What did you like most about this prompt?\\n- What was confusing?\\n150→- What was the hardest thing to do?\\n- What would you change in this prompt?\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/TASK.md\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"SOURCE: Wii Fit\\n\\nGenre: Pick the game genre(s) that best fit the source and would make the best game.\\n\\nPerspective: Pick the camera perspective(s) that best fit the genre and source and would make the best game.\\n\\nGame Title: A playful riff on SOURCE's name. Silently brainstorm 50 titles, then pick one with a real random number generator (e.g., run code).\\n\\nResearch: Whether and how much to research is your choice.\\n\\nPackage: For ease of deployment and sharing provide a single html file [GameTitle-SOURCE-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607].html. Dependencies that can be downloaded do not have to be included in the html file if that is easier.\\n\\nTech Stack: Build on https://github.com/michaelcrosato/riftlight/releases/latest/download/pixel-engine.zip, the riftlight engine kit. Keep the engine (pixel-engine.js) as it ships, as its guide says, and add whatever systems, art assets and animations the game needs on top of it. The rest of the tech stack is your choice.\\n\\nArt Direction: Use the engine’s native style as the base. Make new art assets for whatever makes the game feel like the source; the engine’s asset library is fine for generic props.\\n\\nAnimation: Use the engine’s native animation system as the base. Make new animations for whatever makes the game feel like the source.\\n\\nAudio: All music, sound effects and voices are written in code, with no audio files. Voices are Animalese/Simlish-style gibberish. Music is to be set to 10% volume by default.\\n\\nOnline: https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub\\n\\nWorking Environment and deliverable:\\nCreate a subfolder called [GameTitle-SOURCE-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607] to keep all your dev files in. You can develop separate modules, then bundle into a single file [GameTitle-SOURCE-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607].html in root when you’re done. You may use external CDN dependencies. Do not read files outside what you need: other agents work in the folders beside this one. They share this machine’s ports and processes too. Prefer file:// and the engine’s headless tools. If you need a server (the AI Hub harness does), bind 127.0.0.1 on a port the OS picks (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` prints it) and confirm the page is your game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never pkill, killall, fuser -k, or kill whatever holds a port.\\n\\nPerformance: Treat the performance budget as unlimited. Add as much detail, enemies, effects, lights, and shadows as the scene needs. Out of scope (handled later): FPS targets, optimization.\\n\\nTesting: Test as much as you like with headless tools: scripts that play the game and check its state, including a scripted playthrough of the whole game. Keep them behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count, and rerun it only after changing the code it covers. Use screenshots only for what a script can’t check. Don’t use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\\n\\nEffort: Spend effort however you see fit.\\n\\n## This computer\\nChecked 2026-11-04 20:05 (America/Vancouver) by node check-environment.mjs.\\n\\n- **Computer:** Worki9: 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i9-13900K, 32 cores, 20 GB RAM, 8 GB swap. Ubuntu 26.04.1 LTS on WSL2 (Linux 6.18.33.1-microsoft-standard-WSL2).\\n- **Space:** 850 GB free in the home folder. /tmp: 9.8 GB, in memory (tmpfs), 8.2 GB free when checked.\\n- **Display:** none for runs (they run with DISPLAY unset), so a headed browser needs xvfb-run.\\n- **Browsers:** Playwright 1.63.0 for Python (from playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright), with Chromium 153.0 (WebGL 2, software-rendered; WebGPU, software-rendered, when started with --enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader), Firefox 155.0 (WebGL 2, software-rendered), WebKit 26.6 (WebGL 2) already downloaded. Phone and tablet device profiles are built in.\\n  WebGPU only works on a secure page: file:// or http://127.0.0.1. A WebGPU canvas can come out blank in a headless screenshot, so check the game's state instead.\\n  For Node, `npm install playwright@1.63.0` in your folder uses the browsers already downloaded; another version downloads its own.\\n  Playwright runs here with PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE=ubuntu24.04-x64 (already set for runs): this OS isn't one it supports by name.\\n- **Tools:** node 24.22.1, npm 11.19.1, python3 3.14.8, pip3 26.2.1, git 2.56.0, gh 2.46.0, curl 8.22.0, wget 1.25.0, jq 1.8.1, ffmpeg 9.0.2, ffprobe 9.0.2, sqlite3 3.53.4, zip 3.0, unzip 6.00, rustc 1.99.0, cargo 1.99.0, go 1.27.1, java 27, lighthouse 13.5.0, shot-scraper 1.12, xvfb-run, magick 7.1.2, esbuild 0.28.2, uv 0.12.23, tsc 7.0.2, wasm-bindgen 0.2.129.\\n- **Rust:** rustup's toolchains 1.96.0, 1.98.1, stable; the wasm32-unknown-unknown target on 1.98.1.\\n- **Not installed:** sox, bun, deno.\\n- **Network:** internet works (github.com, registry.npmjs.org).\\n- **Memory:** earlyoom is on: when memory runs out it ends the biggest browser, so \\\"Target closed\\\", \\\"page crashed\\\" or \\\"browser has been closed\\\" means memory ran out, not a bug in your game. Run fewer browsers at once rather than retrying.\\n\\n### What this computer doesn't have\\n\\nNo script can check these, so they're written by hand. Test with the stand-ins; anything that needs the real thing is checked as far as it can be here, never required.\\n\\n- **No physical controller.** Emulate one: replace navigator.getGamepads with a stub that returns a pad in the standard mapping (Playwright's add_init_script / addInitScript).\\n- **No touch device.** Use Playwright's phone and tablet profiles, which have touch, and tap with page.touchscreen.\\n- **Nobody to listen.** Check sound by what Web Audio produces: render it with an OfflineAudioContext, or read levels from an AnalyserNode.\\n- **No second player.** Play multiplayer with two browser pages (or contexts) on this computer.\\n- **No real iPhone or iPad.** WebKit with an iPhone profile is the closest; it isn't iOS Safari.\\n- **No TV.** Judge the 10-foot view from screenshots at 1920×1080.\\n\\n### Sharing this computer\\n\\n- Other agents run here at the same time. Keep one or two browsers open at once, and close them when you're done.\\n- Keep every file you make inside your own folder, not /tmp or a parent folder: /tmp is shared.\\n- The browsers are already downloaded: don't run `playwright install` or `playwright install-deps`.\\n- The system Python has Playwright and nothing else. For one (Pillow, numpy …), use uv: `uv run --with pillow python script.py`, adding `--with playwright==1.63.0` when the script drives a browser too (a newer Playwright can't find the browsers here).\\n\\n## Goal\\n\\nBuild an original game inspired by the source.\\n\\nScope\\n\\nCreate a feature-complete demo. Capture what makes the source distinctive (its world, characters, themes and tone) and turn it into the mechanics, pacing and UX of a great game. The demo must be long enough to show ALL features and gameplay mechanics so a player can clearly understand how the game plays and feels, and what they can and cannot do. Treat the demo as a complete, polished vertical slice. It should contain all the infrastructure, systems, and polish needed so the remainder of the game could later be built out with normal designer tools.\\n\\nInclude a dev mode, reachable from the pause menu, with the standard tools for testing the game quickly. Balance is key, so expose the most important gameplay variables as live sliders, with a reset to defaults.\\n\\nAttract Mode: After 10 seconds without input on the title/menu screen, start a looping AI-played demo or scripted replay (arcade/kiosk style); any input exits it. The AI (or replay) can be simple and may cheat freely (infinite health, ammo, abilities, no clip, etc). Its only job is to show as much of the demo as possible, the attract mode is not meant to balance the game.\\n\\nMultiplayer: Follow https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub for multiplayer integration into ai-hub as well as for the game on its own.\\n\\nNarrative tone: Use a writing style similar to the source’s.\\n\\n## UI & UX: 10-Foot Controller-First Philosophy\\nDesign the game around a PS5 DualSense (or any pad the browser reports in its standard mapping) played on a TV at 10 feet. With keyboard and mouse it's the same game on the same screens, not a separate desktop layout, but they should feel native, not like stand-ins for controller buttons. The keyboard uses the keys PC players expect for the genre. The mouse aims, looks, and clicks menu items and things in the world (hover moves the focus) wherever the genre uses it. On-screen prompts follow the input used last: PlayStation glyphs for the controller (with a Settings option to show Xbox glyphs, A B X Y, instead), keys and mouse buttons for keyboard and mouse.\\n\\nDo not use overly dense, web-style data screens.\\n\\nTouch-only devices: no touch controls; show \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" and the settings button. Let the attract mode run.\\n\\n## Done\\nNo TODOs, placeholders, or stubbed features. The demo is complete.\\n\\n## Source Information\\nCRITICAL: Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen. Write \\\"unknown\\\" for anything you can't confirm.\\n- Date: 2026-11-04 22:16:07\\n- Source: the work it's based on\\n- Plan: the file name of the plan you were given to build from, or none\\n- Genre and Perspective: genre and camera perspective used\\n- Tech: stack, libraries/engines, with versions if applicable\\n- Art Direction: style used\\n- Animation: system used\\n- Audio: music, sound effects and voice used\\n- Online: network features used, or none\\n- Testing: testing parameters allowed\\n- Research: research done, or none\\n- Environment: Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\n- Model: xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\n- Usage: write \\\"added on import\\\". You can't see your own cost, so don't estimate it: the runner records the real cost, tokens and time, and the agent that imports the game into AI Hub puts them on your About/Credits screen.\\n\\nExit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\\\"unknown\\\" for anything you can't confirm). Tools read it (the game's run record and the AI Hub catalogue), so write plain text, and check that the file parses as JSON.\\n{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\\"date\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"plan\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"genre\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"tech\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"animation\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"audio\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"online\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"testing\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"research\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"environment\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"model\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"},\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\\"your answer to each Testing Feedback question, in order\\\"],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\\"your answer to each Engine Feedback question, in order\\\"],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\\"your answer to each Prompt Feedback question, in order\\\"],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"the game's title, as on its title screen\\\",\\n    \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"a few words to go under the title\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"one or two sentences for the catalogue\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game, Tech demo or Tool\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"one of Action, Adventure, Fighting, Flight, Horror, Kids & Learning, Life Sim, Platformer, Puzzle, Racing, RPG, Shooter, Simulation, Sports, Stealth, Strategy\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"the work it's based on, e.g. Moby-Dick\\\",\\n    \\\"series\\\": \\\"its franchise, e.g. Star Fox, or empty\\\",\\n    \\\"players\\\": \\\"how many can play: 1, 1–2 or 1–4\\\",\\n    \\\"controls\\\": \\\"the controls, in one line\\\",\\n    \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"3 to 6 lowercase tags, e.g. 2d, 3d, arcade, story, co-op, versus, first-person, third-person, top-down, side-scrolling, pixel art, low-poly, retro, sci-fi, fantasy, comedy, vehicles, boss fights, exploration\\\"]\\n  }\\n}\\nThe catalogue's model, effort, CLI, date and usage come from the run's record after you finish, so they aren't asked here.\\n\\nTesting Feedback\\n\\n- How many issues did testing catch?\\n- How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?\\n- What was the most helpful test you ran?\\n- What was the least helpful test you ran?\\n\\nEngine Feedback\\n\\n- What did you like most about the engine?\\n- Did you get stuck or guess wrong?\\n- What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?\\n- What was the hardest part about using the engine?\\n- What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)\\n- If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?\\n\\nPrompt Feedback\\n\\n- What did you like most about this prompt?\\n- What was confusing?\\n- What was the hardest thing to do?\\n- What would you change in this prompt?\\n\",\"total_lines\":151}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"312bc73d-ee90-41e4-a73c-a7043ffac7d6"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_401","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a222a508-b00c-4dce-ac55-2fa699baddfc-4","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3%2Fwork/01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469/goal/plan.md"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a222a508-b00c-4dce-ac55-2fa699baddfc-5","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/implementer/test.log","limit":200}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a222a508-b00c-4dce-ac55-2fa699baddfc-6","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/exit-interview.json"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a222a508-b00c-4dce-ac55-2fa699baddfc-7","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/PROGRESS.md","limit":200}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":36561,"output_tokens":353,"cache_read_input_tokens":1792,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"7fb2dfbf-5b9c-4881-a0fc-e946130ff880"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a222a508-b00c-4dce-ac55-2fa699baddfc-4","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→# Plan: Build the Wii Fit-inspired fitness week from PLAN.md and hand in TASK.md’s files\\n\\n## Goal kind\\ncode-change\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n1. **Hand-in and boot.** The workspace root contains `PROGRESS.md`, a valid `exit-interview.json` in the exact TASK.md shape (every value filled, `\\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"`, `aiHub` block included), and one self-contained HTML file whose stem is `{Title}-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607` (`{Title}` is a playful riff on “Wii Fit”, not a Nintendo name, chosen with a real RNG and stored in one constant). A dev folder with that same stem holds the project. The page opens from `file://` with no runtime network fetches, boots on WebGPU with zero page errors, shows that title, and sets the music bus to exactly 0.10 on first run. Shipped `pixel-engine.js` is byte-identical to the downloaded kit. The in-game About/Credits screen shows every TASK.md Source Information field, Testing / Engine / Prompt Feedback, the kit credits, and the sentence “This is not medical advice. Ounce is a scale.” `exit-interview.json` is generated from that same text and re-parses as JSON.\\n2. **The Dot.** Leaning (standard-mapping stick, WASD/arrows with Shift = half lean, mouse offset from the dial as a force) drives an unstable centre-of-balance with lag, sway, noise, overshoot, and velocity impulses — not a 1:1 position map. With PLAN.md’s default tunables, bot time-in-ring over ~35 s (first 2 s ignored) stays in the documented bands: at ring 0.30, idle under 20%, average about 35–65%, good over 80%, expert over 95%. Dot-score stars stay 45 / 70 / 90, so at ring 0.30 idle gets no stars, an average player one, a good player three.\\n3. **Week-long vertical slice.** From a fresh save the real menus reach a named guest (3 slots), a ferry intro, and seven short days: morning weigh-in (stillness, lean, or chase, plus one absurd question), a free island of four stations, at least one activity, hammock, evening report, then the next morning. Shown Wobble Age is the true age plus 7 until the confession, which subtracts exactly 7 from every chart point; play then continues into an open Week 2. There is no lose state. Stars are 0–3; Drips are `2 + 3×stars + floor(playSeconds/30)` plus +5 for the day’s prescription; jar milestones unlock locker items; saves are versioned JSON (in-memory fallback if storage is missing) and survive reload. Every PLAN.md §5 activity is playable to a results screen, including hard versions: Holding Still poses, Reps (scrubbed motion, “last one” gag), Hoop Economics, Step Class, Coconut Header, Slackline, Vitamin Tray, Island Jog, Pier Jump, and The Long Stand’s 90 s distraction timeline. An idle bot finishes with 0★ and no throw; an expert bot scores at least 2★ (3★ on easy activities). Player-facing world text uses the short clinical voice, does not use Nintendo names (Wii, Mii, Balance Board, Wii Fit Trainer, Wuhu, Fit Age) except the Source field and the filename, and does not joke about real bodies or make health claims. At least 120 lines exist beyond PLAN.md’s samples, including 0/1/2/3★ lines per activity.\\n10→4. **10-foot controls, dev mode, attract, audio.** One pixel HUD serves pad, keyboard, and mouse (no DOM menus, no dense data screens). Prompts follow the last device: PlayStation glyphs by default, an Xbox glyph option, keycaps, and mouse buttons. Pause sets `timeScale` to 0 (simulation frozen, menus still read input) and opens Dev Tools with live sliders for the PLAN.md §10 balance, breath/reps, rhythm, games, and economy variables, plus reset-tab and reset-all. After 10 s with no input on the title or any menu, a looping attract demo plays real scenes of every activity family (cheats allowed) until any input returns to the title; it does not start during play, pause, or a hub session. Touch-only devices get no touch controls, the text “Controller or keyboard required”, a settings button, and a running attract loop. All music, SFX, and voices are code (no audio files). Voices are Animalese/Simlish gibberish: the same word always yields the same syllables, a “?” rises in pitch, and an offline render is non-silent with Ounce’s mean pitch above Coach’s. Each song is loud enough that the sum of track volumes × 0.1 × 0.8 is at least 0.03.\\n5. **Local and online Medley.** Family Hour seats up to 4 on one screen (each pad by its own index, plus keyboard-and-mouse); lanes move independently through The Medley — three timed events (a stillness pose, a beat activity, a balance-lean activity), each normalised, then a podium. In an AI Hub session the game skips title, attract, dev mode, and saves; shows its own ready card; plays from the hub clock in ghost mode (progress sent even at score 0, other mats are lerped and never simulated, one result at the end or on time-up); and all four PLAN.md §17 harness URLs (1 player, 2 players, 4 players with latency/jitter/loss, and host-leave) report pass. With no session, the normal title still boots. If WebGPU is missing, the engine’s “Failed to start: WebGPU unavailable” message shows and, in a session, the failure is reported without an uncaught page error.\\n\\n## Verification plan\\n1. **gating:** Add or update real tests that drive the shipped Dot, scoring, Wobble Age, save, voice syllabifier, activity scenes, and menu flow from their real start states (no mocked unit under test, no re-implementation, no hardcoded title). Run `node tools/test.mjs` from the dev folder after the code it covers is in place. Capture stdout/stderr to `{SCRATCH}/test.log`. Pass only if the log ends in a one-line all-passed count, prints no failures, and the assertions cover: Dot bands and 45/70/90 stars; every activity idle 0★ vs expert ≥2★ and correct Drips; a scripted fresh-save week through Day 7, confession −7, and Week 2; save reload, corrupt JSON, and missing storage; pause freeze and resume; every dev slider live plus both resets; attract at 10 s on title and on a menu, no trigger in play, any input exits; medley windows and a ghost lane that does not simulate; stable syllabify and a rising question; `pixel-engine.js` hash equals the kit zip.\\n2. **gating:** Launch the root HTML twice from `file://` with Playwright Chromium and all five flags `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader`. Each run must have zero page errors, a title-screen state that names `{Title}`, and music volume exactly 0.10. Step the engine, composite `renderer.capture()` with the HUD, and save PNGs under `{SCRATCH}/boot-1.png` and `{SCRATCH}/boot-2.png`. The drawing buffer must match the fill-aspect target size and be substantially painted (not a few pixels). A driven confirm or pointer hover must change a recorded UI state (focus or leaving the title prompt). Both runs must agree. If capture throws for an environmental reason, save that log to `{SCRATCH}/capture-error.txt` and pass on the state assertions only. A capture that succeeds and is blank or nearly blank is a failure, not a fallback.\\n3. **gating:** In the same browser suite (included in `node tools/test.mjs`, not a separate unchecked script), on the built HTML: a gamepad stub confirms with Cross and records PlayStation prompts, the Xbox setting switches glyphs, a key switches to keycaps, a mouse move switches to mouse prompts, hover moves focus, and click activates — all readable from game state. A phone profile shows the controller-required message, a settings control, no touch gameplay, and attract running. Two stub pads plus keyboard move three Family Hour lanes independently. After a click, an AnalyserNode reads non-silent music and SFX; an OfflineAudioContext voice render has RMS > 0.02 and Ounce’s mean pitch above Coach’s. Widget rects fit at 1920×1080, 1280×720, and 640×360. WebKit (iPhone profile) and Firefox show the WebGPU-unavailable message and no page error. Write the run log to `{SCRATCH}/browser.log`.\\n4. **gating:** Serve the built game with the hub harness on `127.0.0.1` and an OS-picked port (stop that PID only). Confirm the document title is this game, then run the four harness URLs in criterion 5. Capture results to `{SCRATCH}/hub.log`. Pass only if each reaches `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'` and `window.__hubCheck.pass` is true. Then load the game with no session and confirm the normal title still boots (`{SCRATCH}/nosession.log`).\\n5. **evidence:** `tools/shot.mjs` (or the same step-then-composite path) at 1920×1080 for title, one activity, the island, and pause/dev. Screenshots are for composition only; they do not replace steps 1–4. Save under `{SCRATCH}/shots/`.\\n\\n20→## Non-goals\\n- FPS targets, GPU optimization, or a performance budget (explicitly deferred).\\n- Real BMI, weight, or health data; Balance Board hardware; Miis; Nintendo names, tunes, or level layouts. Source-faithful mechanics ship only under PLAN.md’s original names and the no-body-shaming rule.\\n- A second authored seven-day story. Week 2 is open-ended continuation, not new daily scripts.\\n- DOM or web-style menus, touch gameplay controls, in-session chat, custom names, `alert`, or navigation.\\n- Editing `pixel-engine.js`. Bundling it into the HTML is not an edit.\\n- A physical pad, a human listener, a second human, a television, or real iOS Safari. Stand-ins in TASK.md are enough.\\n- Proving the silent list of 50 title ideas. Only the RNG-chosen title and the filename pattern are required.\\n\\n## Assumed scope\\n30→- Workspace root (this folder): the HTML deliverable, `exit-interview.json`, `PROGRESS.md`.\\n- Dev subfolder `{Title}-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/`: game code, tests, vendored kit and hub client.\\n- Download `https://github.com/michaelcrosato/riftlight/releases/latest/download/pixel-engine.zip` (PLAN.md was spiked on kit 0.46.0; if newer, read its changelog from 0.46.0). Copy the zip’s `pixel-engine/` contents into the dev folder. Fetch hub `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js`, and `README.md` from `https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub` into `vendor/hub/`, unmodified.\\n- Tooling already on the machine: Node, esbuild, Playwright 1.63 (do not run `playwright install`). Python only if a static server is required for the harness.\\n- Wii Fit’s defining mechanics (public guides): a centre-of-balance dot kept in a zone; a daily body test that yields one age-like number; yoga holds, strength reps, aerobics, and balance games; a demonstrating trainer; banked time that unlocks activities; star ratings; several players on one console. PLAN.md already remaps these. That remap is the contract, not Nintendo’s names or BMI copy.\\n\\n## Implementation approach\\nKeep designer data (activities, lines, week, medley, songs) separate from scene code, and keep the Dot, drivers, scores, Wobble Age, Drips, and syllable splitter pure so Node can run them with no GPU. Scenes should only apply that state. Expose a small debug state on the running game (scene, score, device, tunables) so browser checks read state instead of pixels. Inline the bundle in the one HTML file so `file://` needs no imports. Do not change `pixel-engine.js`; record its sha256 at unzip time. Follow PLAN.md’s build order and stop after each slice with the tests that cover it green. The cut list in PLAN.md §19 is not a target: those activities can be built here.\\n\\n## Task checklist\\n40→- [x] Download the kit and hub files, record the engine sha256, scaffold the dev folder and the single-file build, and boot a title scene from `file://`.\\n- [x] Implement the Dot, drivers, actions, device tracking, tunables, pixel HUD (mixed case, glyphs, prompts), settings, pause, and dev sliders; lock the bot ring-time tests.\\n- [x] Ship Holding Still end to end (avatar, coach, results, voice, music) and check the bot star table before adding more activities.\\n- [x] Build the island, weigh-in, seven-day loop, saves, report, sweat jar, and locker unlocks; start the scripted playthrough test.\\n- [x] Add Hoop, Reps, Header, Step, Slackline, Vitamin Tray, Pier Jump, and Island Jog, each with idle-vs-expert bot tests and original lines.\\n- [x] Add The Medley, Family Hour, and the AI Hub ghost card; run all four harness URLs.\\n- [x] Add attract mode, the dev tools tab, the touch-only gate, Hall of Numbers, ferry, daily beats, Long Stand, confession (−7), credits, and the full code-only soundtrack.\\n- [x] Write About/Credits from one data source, emit `exit-interview.json`, update `PROGRESS.md`, and capture `node tools/test.mjs`, two `file://` launches, and the hub log under `{SCRATCH}`.\\n\\n## Risks / Contradictions\\n50→- PLAN.md §19 allows cutting Pier Jump, Vitamin Tray, Island Jog, and Overhead Mortgage if scope slips. The objective requires everything that can be done on this computer, and those activities can. A cut is not a pass unless `PROGRESS.md` records a concrete environment blocker. Never cut the Dot, Holding Still, Reps, Hoop, Header, Step, Weigh-In, the island, the week, Long Stand, the Medley, attract, dev mode, Settings, or About.\\n- WebGPU screenshots are often blank or `capture()` throws unless all five Vulkan/swiftshader flags are set. A successful blank buffer is an app failure. Only a launcher or capture error that is clearly environmental may fall back to state assertions, and that error must be saved.\\n- WebKit and Firefox on this machine have no `navigator.gpu`, so they can only show the WebGPU-unavailable message. The playable boot is Chromium.\\n- `earlyoom` kills the largest browser under memory pressure. Keep at most two browsers open. Other agents share ports; bind `127.0.0.1` with a port the OS picks, and kill only PIDs this work started.\\n- The required filename stem contains a space (“Wii Fit”) because TASK.md substitutes SOURCE literally. Do not rename the source token.\\n- Player-facing text must avoid Nintendo names, but Source Information and the filename must say Wii Fit. Those two places are the exception.\\n\\n## Deviations\\n- Mode changes cut instantly. There is no screen iris.\\n- Screens share one World and one App.\\n60→- Vitamin Tray slides vitamins with a tilt formula on three lane boards. It does not use Rapier bodies.\\n- Pier Jump recentres the dot when the flight starts, so the jump is not scored from the crouch.\\n- Attract mode, the medley, and bot-driven activities skip the intro.\\n- The session card uses palette stand-ins for the four seat colours.\\n- A join press that claims a seat does not also activate the focused menu row on that same frame.\\n- On the name screen, Backspace edits the name and does not also leave the screen.\\n- Pause is taken at the start of fixed, before the sim step, because the headless stepper still runs fixedUpdate on the frame timeScale becomes 0.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→# Plan: Build the Wii Fit-inspired fitness week from PLAN.md and hand in TASK.md’s files\\n\\n## Goal kind\\ncode-change\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n1. **Hand-in and boot.** The workspace root contains `PROGRESS.md`, a valid `exit-interview.json` in the exact TASK.md shape (every value filled, `\\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"`, `aiHub` block included), and one self-contained HTML file whose stem is `{Title}-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607` (`{Title}` is a playful riff on “Wii Fit”, not a Nintendo name, chosen with a real RNG and stored in one constant). A dev folder with that same stem holds the project. The page opens from `file://` with no runtime network fetches, boots on WebGPU with zero page errors, shows that title, and sets the music bus to exactly 0.10 on first run. Shipped `pixel-engine.js` is byte-identical to the downloaded kit. The in-game About/Credits screen shows every TASK.md Source Information field, Testing / Engine / Prompt Feedback, the kit credits, and the sentence “This is not medical advice. Ounce is a scale.” `exit-interview.json` is generated from that same text and re-parses as JSON.\\n2. **The Dot.** Leaning (standard-mapping stick, WASD/arrows with Shift = half lean, mouse offset from the dial as a force) drives an unstable centre-of-balance with lag, sway, noise, overshoot, and velocity impulses — not a 1:1 position map. With PLAN.md’s default tunables, bot time-in-ring over ~35 s (first 2 s ignored) stays in the documented bands: at ring 0.30, idle under 20%, average about 35–65%, good over 80%, expert over 95%. Dot-score stars stay 45 / 70 / 90, so at ring 0.30 idle gets no stars, an average player one, a good player three.\\n3. **Week-long vertical slice.** From a fresh save the real menus reach a named guest (3 slots), a ferry intro, and seven short days: morning weigh-in (stillness, lean, or chase, plus one absurd question), a free island of four stations, at least one activity, hammock, evening report, then the next morning. Shown Wobble Age is the true age plus 7 until the confession, which subtracts exactly 7 from every chart point; play then continues into an open Week 2. There is no lose state. Stars are 0–3; Drips are `2 + 3×stars + floor(playSeconds/30)` plus +5 for the day’s prescription; jar milestones unlock locker items; saves are versioned JSON (in-memory fallback if storage is missing) and survive reload. Every PLAN.md §5 activity is playable to a results screen, including hard versions: Holding Still poses, Reps (scrubbed motion, “last one” gag), Hoop Economics, Step Class, Coconut Header, Slackline, Vitamin Tray, Island Jog, Pier Jump, and The Long Stand’s 90 s distraction timeline. An idle bot finishes with 0★ and no throw; an expert bot scores at least 2★ (3★ on easy activities). Player-facing world text uses the short clinical voice, does not use Nintendo names (Wii, Mii, Balance Board, Wii Fit Trainer, Wuhu, Fit Age) except the Source field and the filename, and does not joke about real bodies or make health claims. At least 120 lines exist beyond PLAN.md’s samples, including 0/1/2/3★ lines per activity.\\n10→4. **10-foot controls, dev mode, attract, audio.** One pixel HUD serves pad, keyboard, and mouse (no DOM menus, no dense data screens). Prompts follow the last device: PlayStation glyphs by default, an Xbox glyph option, keycaps, and mouse buttons. Pause sets `timeScale` to 0 (simulation frozen, menus still read input) and opens Dev Tools with live sliders for the PLAN.md §10 balance, breath/reps, rhythm, games, and economy variables, plus reset-tab and reset-all. After 10 s with no input on the title or any menu, a looping attract demo plays real scenes of every activity family (cheats allowed) until any input returns to the title; it does not start during play, pause, or a hub session. Touch-only devices get no touch controls, the text “Controller or keyboard required”, a settings button, and a running attract loop. All music, SFX, and voices are code (no audio files). Voices are Animalese/Simlish gibberish: the same word always yields the same syllables, a “?” rises in pitch, and an offline render is non-silent with Ounce’s mean pitch above Coach’s. Each song is loud enough that the sum of track volumes × 0.1 × 0.8 is at least 0.03.\\n5. **Local and online Medley.** Family Hour seats up to 4 on one screen (each pad by its own index, plus keyboard-and-mouse); lanes move independently through The Medley — three timed events (a stillness pose, a beat activity, a balance-lean activity), each normalised, then a podium. In an AI Hub session the game skips title, attract, dev mode, and saves; shows its own ready card; plays from the hub clock in ghost mode (progress sent even at score 0, other mats are lerped and never simulated, one result at the end or on time-up); and all four PLAN.md §17 harness URLs (1 player, 2 players, 4 players with latency/jitter/loss, and host-leave) report pass. With no session, the normal title still boots. If WebGPU is missing, the engine’s “Failed to start: WebGPU unavailable” message shows and, in a session, the failure is reported without an uncaught page error.\\n\\n## Verification plan\\n1. **gating:** Add or update real tests that drive the shipped Dot, scoring, Wobble Age, save, voice syllabifier, activity scenes, and menu flow from their real start states (no mocked unit under test, no re-implementation, no hardcoded title). Run `node tools/test.mjs` from the dev folder after the code it covers is in place. Capture stdout/stderr to `{SCRATCH}/test.log`. Pass only if the log ends in a one-line all-passed count, prints no failures, and the assertions cover: Dot bands and 45/70/90 stars; every activity idle 0★ vs expert ≥2★ and correct Drips; a scripted fresh-save week through Day 7, confession −7, and Week 2; save reload, corrupt JSON, and missing storage; pause freeze and resume; every dev slider live plus both resets; attract at 10 s on title and on a menu, no trigger in play, any input exits; medley windows and a ghost lane that does not simulate; stable syllabify and a rising question; `pixel-engine.js` hash equals the kit zip.\\n2. **gating:** Launch the root HTML twice from `file://` with Playwright Chromium and all five flags `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader`. Each run must have zero page errors, a title-screen state that names `{Title}`, and music volume exactly 0.10. Step the engine, composite `renderer.capture()` with the HUD, and save PNGs under `{SCRATCH}/boot-1.png` and `{SCRATCH}/boot-2.png`. The drawing buffer must match the fill-aspect target size and be substantially painted (not a few pixels). A driven confirm or pointer hover must change a recorded UI state (focus or leaving the title prompt). Both runs must agree. If capture throws for an environmental reason, save that log to `{SCRATCH}/capture-error.txt` and pass on the state assertions only. A capture that succeeds and is blank or nearly blank is a failure, not a fallback.\\n3. **gating:** In the same browser suite (included in `node tools/test.mjs`, not a separate unchecked script), on the built HTML: a gamepad stub confirms with Cross and records PlayStation prompts, the Xbox setting switches glyphs, a key switches to keycaps, a mouse move switches to mouse prompts, hover moves focus, and click activates — all readable from game state. A phone profile shows the controller-required message, a settings control, no touch gameplay, and attract running. Two stub pads plus keyboard move three Family Hour lanes independently. After a click, an AnalyserNode reads non-silent music and SFX; an OfflineAudioContext voice render has RMS > 0.02 and Ounce’s mean pitch above Coach’s. Widget rects fit at 1920×1080, 1280×720, and 640×360. WebKit (iPhone profile) and Firefox show the WebGPU-unavailable message and no page error. Write the run log to `{SCRATCH}/browser.log`.\\n4. **gating:** Serve the built game with the hub harness on `127.0.0.1` and an OS-picked port (stop that PID only). Confirm the document title is this game, then run the four harness URLs in criterion 5. Capture results to `{SCRATCH}/hub.log`. Pass only if each reaches `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'` and `window.__hubCheck.pass` is true. Then load the game with no session and confirm the normal title still boots (`{SCRATCH}/nosession.log`).\\n5. **evidence:** `tools/shot.mjs` (or the same step-then-composite path) at 1920×1080 for title, one activity, the island, and pause/dev. Screenshots are for composition only; they do not replace steps 1–4. Save under `{SCRATCH}/shots/`.\\n\\n20→## Non-goals\\n- FPS targets, GPU optimization, or a performance budget (explicitly deferred).\\n- Real BMI, weight, or health data; Balance Board hardware; Miis; Nintendo names, tunes, or level layouts. Source-faithful mechanics ship only under PLAN.md’s original names and the no-body-shaming rule.\\n- A second authored seven-day story. Week 2 is open-ended continuation, not new daily scripts.\\n- DOM or web-style menus, touch gameplay controls, in-session chat, custom names, `alert`, or navigation.\\n- Editing `pixel-engine.js`. Bundling it into the HTML is not an edit.\\n- A physical pad, a human listener, a second human, a television, or real iOS Safari. Stand-ins in TASK.md are enough.\\n- Proving the silent list of 50 title ideas. Only the RNG-chosen title and the filename pattern are required.\\n\\n## Assumed scope\\n30→- Workspace root (this folder): the HTML deliverable, `exit-interview.json`, `PROGRESS.md`.\\n- Dev subfolder `{Title}-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/`: game code, tests, vendored kit and hub client.\\n- Download `https://github.com/michaelcrosato/riftlight/releases/latest/download/pixel-engine.zip` (PLAN.md was spiked on kit 0.46.0; if newer, read its changelog from 0.46.0). Copy the zip’s `pixel-engine/` contents into the dev folder. Fetch hub `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js`, and `README.md` from `https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub` into `vendor/hub/`, unmodified.\\n- Tooling already on the machine: Node, esbuild, Playwright 1.63 (do not run `playwright install`). Python only if a static server is required for the harness.\\n- Wii Fit’s defining mechanics (public guides): a centre-of-balance dot kept in a zone; a daily body test that yields one age-like number; yoga holds, strength reps, aerobics, and balance games; a demonstrating trainer; banked time that unlocks activities; star ratings; several players on one console. PLAN.md already remaps these. That remap is the contract, not Nintendo’s names or BMI copy.\\n\\n## Implementation approach\\nKeep designer data (activities, lines, week, medley, songs) separate from scene code, and keep the Dot, drivers, scores, Wobble Age, Drips, and syllable splitter pure so Node can run them with no GPU. Scenes should only apply that state. Expose a small debug state on the running game (scene, score, device, tunables) so browser checks read state instead of pixels. Inline the bundle in the one HTML file so `file://` needs no imports. Do not change `pixel-engine.js`; record its sha256 at unzip time. Follow PLAN.md’s build order and stop after each slice with the tests that cover it green. The cut list in PLAN.md §19 is not a target: those activities can be built here.\\n\\n## Task checklist\\n40→- [x] Download the kit and hub files, record the engine sha256, scaffold the dev folder and the single-file build, and boot a title scene from `file://`.\\n- [x] Implement the Dot, drivers, actions, device tracking, tunables, pixel HUD (mixed case, glyphs, prompts), settings, pause, and dev sliders; lock the bot ring-time tests.\\n- [x] Ship Holding Still end to end (avatar, coach, results, voice, music) and check the bot star table before adding more activities.\\n- [x] Build the island, weigh-in, seven-day loop, saves, report, sweat jar, and locker unlocks; start the scripted playthrough test.\\n- [x] Add Hoop, Reps, Header, Step, Slackline, Vitamin Tray, Pier Jump, and Island Jog, each with idle-vs-expert bot tests and original lines.\\n- [x] Add The Medley, Family Hour, and the AI Hub ghost card; run all four harness URLs.\\n- [x] Add attract mode, the dev tools tab, the touch-only gate, Hall of Numbers, ferry, daily beats, Long Stand, confession (−7), credits, and the full code-only soundtrack.\\n- [x] Write About/Credits from one data source, emit `exit-interview.json`, update `PROGRESS.md`, and capture `node tools/test.mjs`, two `file://` launches, and the hub log under `{SCRATCH}`.\\n\\n## Risks / Contradictions\\n50→- PLAN.md §19 allows cutting Pier Jump, Vitamin Tray, Island Jog, and Overhead Mortgage if scope slips. The objective requires everything that can be done on this computer, and those activities can. A cut is not a pass unless `PROGRESS.md` records a concrete environment blocker. Never cut the Dot, Holding Still, Reps, Hoop, Header, Step, Weigh-In, the island, the week, Long Stand, the Medley, attract, dev mode, Settings, or About.\\n- WebGPU screenshots are often blank or `capture()` throws unless all five Vulkan/swiftshader flags are set. A successful blank buffer is an app failure. Only a launcher or capture error that is clearly environmental may fall back to state assertions, and that error must be saved.\\n- WebKit and Firefox on this machine have no `navigator.gpu`, so they can only show the WebGPU-unavailable message. The playable boot is Chromium.\\n- `earlyoom` kills the largest browser under memory pressure. Keep at most two browsers open. Other agents share ports; bind `127.0.0.1` with a port the OS picks, and kill only PIDs this work started.\\n- The required filename stem contains a space (“Wii Fit”) because TASK.md substitutes SOURCE literally. Do not rename the source token.\\n- Player-facing text must avoid Nintendo names, but Source Information and the filename must say Wii Fit. Those two places are the exception.\\n\\n## Deviations\\n- Mode changes cut instantly. There is no screen iris.\\n- Screens share one World and one App.\\n60→- Vitamin Tray slides vitamins with a tilt formula on three lane boards. It does not use Rapier bodies.\\n- Pier Jump recentres the dot when the flight starts, so the jump is not scored from the crouch.\\n- Attract mode, the medley, and bot-driven activities skip the intro.\\n- The session card uses palette stand-ins for the four seat colours.\\n- A join press that claims a seat does not also activate the focused menu row on that same frame.\\n- On the name screen, Backspace edits the name and does not also leave the screen.\\n- Pause is taken at the start of fixed, before the sim step, because the headless stepper still runs fixedUpdate on the frame timeScale becomes 0.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3%2Fwork/01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469/goal/plan.md\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"# Plan: Build the Wii Fit-inspired fitness week from PLAN.md and hand in TASK.md’s files\\n\\n## Goal kind\\ncode-change\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n1. **Hand-in and boot.** The workspace root contains `PROGRESS.md`, a valid `exit-interview.json` in the exact TASK.md shape (every value filled, `\\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"`, `aiHub` block included), and one self-contained HTML file whose stem is `{Title}-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607` (`{Title}` is a playful riff on “Wii Fit”, not a Nintendo name, chosen with a real RNG and stored in one constant). A dev folder with that same stem holds the project. The page opens from `file://` with no runtime network fetches, boots on WebGPU with zero page errors, shows that title, and sets the music bus to exactly 0.10 on first run. Shipped `pixel-engine.js` is byte-identical to the downloaded kit. The in-game About/Credits screen shows every TASK.md Source Information field, Testing / Engine / Prompt Feedback, the kit credits, and the sentence “This is not medical advice. Ounce is a scale.” `exit-interview.json` is generated from that same text and re-parses as JSON.\\n2. **The Dot.** Leaning (standard-mapping stick, WASD/arrows with Shift = half lean, mouse offset from the dial as a force) drives an unstable centre-of-balance with lag, sway, noise, overshoot, and velocity impulses — not a 1:1 position map. With PLAN.md’s default tunables, bot time-in-ring over ~35 s (first 2 s ignored) stays in the documented bands: at ring 0.30, idle under 20%, average about 35–65%, good over 80%, expert over 95%. Dot-score stars stay 45 / 70 / 90, so at ring 0.30 idle gets no stars, an average player one, a good player three.\\n3. **Week-long vertical slice.** From a fresh save the real menus reach a named guest (3 slots), a ferry intro, and seven short days: morning weigh-in (stillness, lean, or chase, plus one absurd question), a free island of four stations, at least one activity, hammock, evening report, then the next morning. Shown Wobble Age is the true age plus 7 until the confession, which subtracts exactly 7 from every chart point; play then continues into an open Week 2. There is no lose state. Stars are 0–3; Drips are `2 + 3×stars + floor(playSeconds/30)` plus +5 for the day’s prescription; jar milestones unlock locker items; saves are versioned JSON (in-memory fallback if storage is missing) and survive reload. Every PLAN.md §5 activity is playable to a results screen, including hard versions: Holding Still poses, Reps (scrubbed motion, “last one” gag), Hoop Economics, Step Class, Coconut Header, Slackline, Vitamin Tray, Island Jog, Pier Jump, and The Long Stand’s 90 s distraction timeline. An idle bot finishes with 0★ and no throw; an expert bot scores at least 2★ (3★ on easy activities). Player-facing world text uses the short clinical voice, does not use Nintendo names (Wii, Mii, Balance Board, Wii Fit Trainer, Wuhu, Fit Age) except the Source field and the filename, and does not joke about real bodies or make health claims. At least 120 lines exist beyond PLAN.md’s samples, including 0/1/2/3★ lines per activity.\\n4. **10-foot controls, dev mode, attract, audio.** One pixel HUD serves pad, keyboard, and mouse (no DOM menus, no dense data screens). Prompts follow the last device: PlayStation glyphs by default, an Xbox glyph option, keycaps, and mouse buttons. Pause sets `timeScale` to 0 (simulation frozen, menus still read input) and opens Dev Tools with live sliders for the PLAN.md §10 balance, breath/reps, rhythm, games, and economy variables, plus reset-tab and reset-all. After 10 s with no input on the title or any menu, a looping attract demo plays real scenes of every activity family (cheats allowed) until any input returns to the title; it does not start during play, pause, or a hub session. Touch-only devices get no touch controls, the text “Controller or keyboard required”, a settings button, and a running attract loop. All music, SFX, and voices are code (no audio files). Voices are Animalese/Simlish gibberish: the same word always yields the same syllables, a “?” rises in pitch, and an offline render is non-silent with Ounce’s mean pitch above Coach’s. Each song is loud enough that the sum of track volumes × 0.1 × 0.8 is at least 0.03.\\n5. **Local and online Medley.** Family Hour seats up to 4 on one screen (each pad by its own index, plus keyboard-and-mouse); lanes move independently through The Medley — three timed events (a stillness pose, a beat activity, a balance-lean activity), each normalised, then a podium. In an AI Hub session the game skips title, attract, dev mode, and saves; shows its own ready card; plays from the hub clock in ghost mode (progress sent even at score 0, other mats are lerped and never simulated, one result at the end or on time-up); and all four PLAN.md §17 harness URLs (1 player, 2 players, 4 players with latency/jitter/loss, and host-leave) report pass. With no session, the normal title still boots. If WebGPU is missing, the engine’s “Failed to start: WebGPU unavailable” message shows and, in a session, the failure is reported without an uncaught page error.\\n\\n## Verification plan\\n1. **gating:** Add or update real tests that drive the shipped Dot, scoring, Wobble Age, save, voice syllabifier, activity scenes, and menu flow from their real start states (no mocked unit under test, no re-implementation, no hardcoded title). Run `node tools/test.mjs` from the dev folder after the code it covers is in place. Capture stdout/stderr to `{SCRATCH}/test.log`. Pass only if the log ends in a one-line all-passed count, prints no failures, and the assertions cover: Dot bands and 45/70/90 stars; every activity idle 0★ vs expert ≥2★ and correct Drips; a scripted fresh-save week through Day 7, confession −7, and Week 2; save reload, corrupt JSON, and missing storage; pause freeze and resume; every dev slider live plus both resets; attract at 10 s on title and on a menu, no trigger in play, any input exits; medley windows and a ghost lane that does not simulate; stable syllabify and a rising question; `pixel-engine.js` hash equals the kit zip.\\n2. **gating:** Launch the root HTML twice from `file://` with Playwright Chromium and all five flags `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader`. Each run must have zero page errors, a title-screen state that names `{Title}`, and music volume exactly 0.10. Step the engine, composite `renderer.capture()` with the HUD, and save PNGs under `{SCRATCH}/boot-1.png` and `{SCRATCH}/boot-2.png`. The drawing buffer must match the fill-aspect target size and be substantially painted (not a few pixels). A driven confirm or pointer hover must change a recorded UI state (focus or leaving the title prompt). Both runs must agree. If capture throws for an environmental reason, save that log to `{SCRATCH}/capture-error.txt` and pass on the state assertions only. A capture that succeeds and is blank or nearly blank is a failure, not a fallback.\\n3. **gating:** In the same browser suite (included in `node tools/test.mjs`, not a separate unchecked script), on the built HTML: a gamepad stub confirms with Cross and records PlayStation prompts, the Xbox setting switches glyphs, a key switches to keycaps, a mouse move switches to mouse prompts, hover moves focus, and click activates — all readable from game state. A phone profile shows the controller-required message, a settings control, no touch gameplay, and attract running. Two stub pads plus keyboard move three Family Hour lanes independently. After a click, an AnalyserNode reads non-silent music and SFX; an OfflineAudioContext voice render has RMS > 0.02 and Ounce’s mean pitch above Coach’s. Widget rects fit at 1920×1080, 1280×720, and 640×360. WebKit (iPhone profile) and Firefox show the WebGPU-unavailable message and no page error. Write the run log to `{SCRATCH}/browser.log`.\\n4. **gating:** Serve the built game with the hub harness on `127.0.0.1` and an OS-picked port (stop that PID only). Confirm the document title is this game, then run the four harness URLs in criterion 5. Capture results to `{SCRATCH}/hub.log`. Pass only if each reaches `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'` and `window.__hubCheck.pass` is true. Then load the game with no session and confirm the normal title still boots (`{SCRATCH}/nosession.log`).\\n5. **evidence:** `tools/shot.mjs` (or the same step-then-composite path) at 1920×1080 for title, one activity, the island, and pause/dev. Screenshots are for composition only; they do not replace steps 1–4. Save under `{SCRATCH}/shots/`.\\n\\n## Non-goals\\n- FPS targets, GPU optimization, or a performance budget (explicitly deferred).\\n- Real BMI, weight, or health data; Balance Board hardware; Miis; Nintendo names, tunes, or level layouts. Source-faithful mechanics ship only under PLAN.md’s original names and the no-body-shaming rule.\\n- A second authored seven-day story. Week 2 is open-ended continuation, not new daily scripts.\\n- DOM or web-style menus, touch gameplay controls, in-session chat, custom names, `alert`, or navigation.\\n- Editing `pixel-engine.js`. Bundling it into the HTML is not an edit.\\n- A physical pad, a human listener, a second human, a television, or real iOS Safari. Stand-ins in TASK.md are enough.\\n- Proving the silent list of 50 title ideas. Only the RNG-chosen title and the filename pattern are required.\\n\\n## Assumed scope\\n- Workspace root (this folder): the HTML deliverable, `exit-interview.json`, `PROGRESS.md`.\\n- Dev subfolder `{Title}-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/`: game code, tests, vendored kit and hub client.\\n- Download `https://github.com/michaelcrosato/riftlight/releases/latest/download/pixel-engine.zip` (PLAN.md was spiked on kit 0.46.0; if newer, read its changelog from 0.46.0). Copy the zip’s `pixel-engine/` contents into the dev folder. Fetch hub `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js`, and `README.md` from `https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub` into `vendor/hub/`, unmodified.\\n- Tooling already on the machine: Node, esbuild, Playwright 1.63 (do not run `playwright install`). Python only if a static server is required for the harness.\\n- Wii Fit’s defining mechanics (public guides): a centre-of-balance dot kept in a zone; a daily body test that yields one age-like number; yoga holds, strength reps, aerobics, and balance games; a demonstrating trainer; banked time that unlocks activities; star ratings; several players on one console. PLAN.md already remaps these. That remap is the contract, not Nintendo’s names or BMI copy.\\n\\n## Implementation approach\\nKeep designer data (activities, lines, week, medley, songs) separate from scene code, and keep the Dot, drivers, scores, Wobble Age, Drips, and syllable splitter pure so Node can run them with no GPU. Scenes should only apply that state. Expose a small debug state on the running game (scene, score, device, tunables) so browser checks read state instead of pixels. Inline the bundle in the one HTML file so `file://` needs no imports. Do not change `pixel-engine.js`; record its sha256 at unzip time. Follow PLAN.md’s build order and stop after each slice with the tests that cover it green. The cut list in PLAN.md §19 is not a target: those activities can be built here.\\n\\n## Task checklist\\n- [x] Download the kit and hub files, record the engine sha256, scaffold the dev folder and the single-file build, and boot a title scene from `file://`.\\n- [x] Implement the Dot, drivers, actions, device tracking, tunables, pixel HUD (mixed case, glyphs, prompts), settings, pause, and dev sliders; lock the bot ring-time tests.\\n- [x] Ship Holding Still end to end (avatar, coach, results, voice, music) and check the bot star table before adding more activities.\\n- [x] Build the island, weigh-in, seven-day loop, saves, report, sweat jar, and locker unlocks; start the scripted playthrough test.\\n- [x] Add Hoop, Reps, Header, Step, Slackline, Vitamin Tray, Pier Jump, and Island Jog, each with idle-vs-expert bot tests and original lines.\\n- [x] Add The Medley, Family Hour, and the AI Hub ghost card; run all four harness URLs.\\n- [x] Add attract mode, the dev tools tab, the touch-only gate, Hall of Numbers, ferry, daily beats, Long Stand, confession (−7), credits, and the full code-only soundtrack.\\n- [x] Write About/Credits from one data source, emit `exit-interview.json`, update `PROGRESS.md`, and capture `node tools/test.mjs`, two `file://` launches, and the hub log under `{SCRATCH}`.\\n\\n## Risks / Contradictions\\n- PLAN.md §19 allows cutting Pier Jump, Vitamin Tray, Island Jog, and Overhead Mortgage if scope slips. The objective requires everything that can be done on this computer, and those activities can. A cut is not a pass unless `PROGRESS.md` records a concrete environment blocker. Never cut the Dot, Holding Still, Reps, Hoop, Header, Step, Weigh-In, the island, the week, Long Stand, the Medley, attract, dev mode, Settings, or About.\\n- WebGPU screenshots are often blank or `capture()` throws unless all five Vulkan/swiftshader flags are set. A successful blank buffer is an app failure. Only a launcher or capture error that is clearly environmental may fall back to state assertions, and that error must be saved.\\n- WebKit and Firefox on this machine have no `navigator.gpu`, so they can only show the WebGPU-unavailable message. The playable boot is Chromium.\\n- `earlyoom` kills the largest browser under memory pressure. Keep at most two browsers open. Other agents share ports; bind `127.0.0.1` with a port the OS picks, and kill only PIDs this work started.\\n- The required filename stem contains a space (“Wii Fit”) because TASK.md substitutes SOURCE literally. Do not rename the source token.\\n- Player-facing text must avoid Nintendo names, but Source Information and the filename must say Wii Fit. Those two places are the exception.\\n\\n## Deviations\\n- Mode changes cut instantly. There is no screen iris.\\n- Screens share one World and one App.\\n- Vitamin Tray slides vitamins with a tilt formula on three lane boards. It does not use Rapier bodies.\\n- Pier Jump recentres the dot when the flight starts, so the jump is not scored from the crouch.\\n- Attract mode, the medley, and bot-driven activities skip the intro.\\n- The session card uses palette stand-ins for the four seat colours.\\n- A join press that claims a seat does not also activate the focused menu row on that same frame.\\n- On the name screen, Backspace edits the name and does not also leave the screen.\\n- Pause is taken at the start of fixed, before the sim step, because the headless stepper still runs fixedUpdate on the frame timeScale becomes 0.\\n\",\"total_lines\":66}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a222a508-b00c-4dce-ac55-2fa699baddfc-5","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→12/12 passed\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→12/12 passed\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/implementer/test.log\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":200,\"raw_output\":\"12/12 passed\\n\",\"total_lines\":1}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a222a508-b00c-4dce-ac55-2fa699baddfc-6","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 22:16:07\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Sports\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"Isometric island, with a fixed camera for each activity\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"Pixel Engine 0.46.0, three.js r186, Rapier 0.20 as bundled, esbuild 0.28.2\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"The engine native pixel look, with new models for the scale, stations, and props\\\",\\n10→    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"Engine ClipDefs compiled onto the hero rig and played with AnimationMixer\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Engine Song and SoundDef data, plus a Web Audio formant voice. Music defaults to 10 percent.\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, own card, 1 to 4 players. Family Hour is local on one screen.\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"node tools/test.mjs, Playwright 1.63 Chromium with the five software WebGPU flags, WebKit and Firefox for the missing-WebGPU path, and the engine headless runner\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"The director plan already included engine and hub research and spikes. I read PLAN.md, the engine guide where the recipes pointed, and the hub README, and I checked the Dot table in code. I did not do extra research on the source beyond that plan.\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n20→    \\\"Eleven issues. The expert pier jump scored two stars, pause let the pose clock move on the frame the button went down, two songs had uneven pattern lengths, a tray board lookup named a variable that was not in scope, a few model parts floated, the seagull was spoken as the scale, a dev-tool page could not go back, the prompt could draw past a short screen, the scale's voice measured just under the loudness line, the About screen kept only the first six lines so later source fields never appeared, and the menu cursor was a greater-than sign the font cannot draw, so it showed as a question mark.\\\",\\n    \\\"Two were game-breaking. The pier jump sat under the three-star line until takeoff recentred the dot, and the pose kept playing for one frame after pause. The others failed a data check, a voice check, a menu, or the About screen, and they were fixed before the hand-in.\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful test was the idle-versus-expert bot pass on every activity. It is what caught the pier jump sitting under the three-star line.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful test was the glyph scan. Every line already used the allowed characters, so it passed on the first run and did not change the game.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"Headless stepping, the pixel HUD, and a real input recorder made a week of play testable without a screen.\\\",\\n    \\\"I guessed wrong about pause. At timeScale 0 the headless stepper still calls fixedUpdate, and that call happens before update reads the pause key, so the pose clock moved unless the sim refused the step. Menu presses do still arrive. The type note reads as if those presses are dropped. Capture also needs all five Vulkan flags or the picture comes back blank.\\\",\\n    \\\"The centre-of-balance itself. The engine will move a character. It will not sway a polite dot, keep a week, or speak in formants.\\\",\\n    \\\"The hardest part was trusting the frame clock. Game time, the press window, and the hub clock are three different clocks, and only one of them is allowed to move a score.\\\",\\n30→    \\\"None. pixel-engine.js is the kit file, byte for byte.\\\",\\n    \\\"I would give the music bus a default of silence until the game sets it, so a shared browser profile cannot leave yesterday volume on today game.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The plan named the mechanics, the sentences, and the tests, so the work was building a game rather than inventing one.\\\",\\n    \\\"The cut list in the plan and the instruction to finish everything on this computer disagree. I followed the instruction and shipped the activities the cut list would drop.\\\",\\n    \\\"The hardest piece was the pier jump star line. The same bot that holds a pose will dive off a dock, and the flight begins wherever the dot was left.\\\",\\n    \\\"I would ask for the pause rule in one sentence: timeScale 0, fixedUpdate silent, update still reads keys. The guide and the type comment do not say the same thing.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n40→    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Mint Dial\\\",\\n    \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"Keep the dot in the circle.\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"A week on a small island with a polite scale. Hold still, keep time, and try not to believe the number.\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Sports\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"series\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"players\\\": \\\"1–4\\\",\\n    \\\"controls\\\": \\\"Left stick, WASD or mouse: lean. R2, Space or click: breathe. L1/R1, F/J or mouse buttons: step.\\\",\\n    \\\"tags\\\": [\\n50→      \\\"pixel art\\\",\\n      \\\"comedy\\\",\\n      \\\"versus\\\",\\n      \\\"arcade\\\",\\n      \\\"3d\\\",\\n      \\\"story\\\"\\n    ]\\n  }\\n}\",\"content_concise\":\"1→{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 22:16:07\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Sports\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"Isometric island, with a fixed camera for each activity\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"Pixel Engine 0.46.0, three.js r186, Rapier 0.20 as bundled, esbuild 0.28.2\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"The engine native pixel look, with new models for the scale, stations, and props\\\",\\n10→    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"Engine ClipDefs compiled onto the hero rig and played with AnimationMixer\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Engine Song and SoundDef data, plus a Web Audio formant voice. Music defaults to 10 percent.\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, own card, 1 to 4 players. Family Hour is local on one screen.\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"node tools/test.mjs, Playwright 1.63 Chromium with the five software WebGPU flags, WebKit and Firefox for the missing-WebGPU path, and the engine headless runner\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"The director plan already included engine and hub research and spikes. I read PLAN.md, the engine guide where the recipes pointed, and the hub README, and I checked the Dot table in code. I did not do extra research on the source beyond that plan.\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n20→    \\\"Eleven issues. The expert pier jump scored two stars, pause let the pose clock move on the frame the button went down, two songs had uneven pattern lengths, a tray board lookup named a variable that was not in scope, a few model parts floated, the seagull was spoken as the scale, a dev-tool page could not go back, the prompt could draw past a short screen, the scale's voice measured just under the loudness line, the About screen kept only the first six lines so later source fields never appeared, and the menu cursor was a greater-than sign the font cannot draw, so it showed as a question mark.\\\",\\n    \\\"Two were game-breaking. The pier jump sat under the three-star line until takeoff recentred the dot, and the pose kept playing for one frame after pause. The others failed a data check, a voice check, a menu, or the About screen, and they were fixed before the hand-in.\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful test was the idle-versus-expert bot pass on every activity. It is what caught the pier jump sitting under the three-star line.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful test was the glyph scan. Every line already used the allowed characters, so it passed on the first run and did not change the game.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"Headless stepping, the pixel HUD, and a real input recorder made a week of play testable without a screen.\\\",\\n    \\\"I guessed wrong about pause. At timeScale 0 the headless stepper still calls fixedUpdate, and that call happens before update reads the pause key, so the pose clock moved unless the sim refused the step. Menu presses do still arrive. The type note reads as if those presses are dropped. Capture also needs all five Vulkan flags or the picture comes back blank.\\\",\\n    \\\"The centre-of-balance itself. The engine will move a character. It will not sway a polite dot, keep a week, or speak in formants.\\\",\\n    \\\"The hardest part was trusting the frame clock. Game time, the press window, and the hub clock are three different clocks, and only one of them is allowed to move a score.\\\",\\n30→    \\\"None. pixel-engine.js is the kit file, byte for byte.\\\",\\n    \\\"I would give the music bus a default of silence until the game sets it, so a shared browser profile cannot leave yesterday volume on today game.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The plan named the mechanics, the sentences, and the tests, so the work was building a game rather than inventing one.\\\",\\n    \\\"The cut list in the plan and the instruction to finish everything on this computer disagree. I followed the instruction and shipped the activities the cut list would drop.\\\",\\n    \\\"The hardest piece was the pier jump star line. The same bot that holds a pose will dive off a dock, and the flight begins wherever the dot was left.\\\",\\n    \\\"I would ask for the pause rule in one sentence: timeScale 0, fixedUpdate silent, update still reads keys. The guide and the type comment do not say the same thing.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n40→    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Mint Dial\\\",\\n    \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"Keep the dot in the circle.\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"A week on a small island with a polite scale. Hold still, keep time, and try not to believe the number.\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Sports\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"series\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"players\\\": \\\"1–4\\\",\\n    \\\"controls\\\": \\\"Left stick, WASD or mouse: lean. R2, Space or click: breathe. L1/R1, F/J or mouse buttons: step.\\\",\\n    \\\"tags\\\": [\\n50→      \\\"pixel art\\\",\\n      \\\"comedy\\\",\\n      \\\"versus\\\",\\n      \\\"arcade\\\",\\n      \\\"3d\\\",\\n      \\\"story\\\"\\n    ]\\n  }\\n}\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/exit-interview.json\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 22:16:07\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Sports\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"Isometric island, with a fixed camera for each activity\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"Pixel Engine 0.46.0, three.js r186, Rapier 0.20 as bundled, esbuild 0.28.2\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"The engine native pixel look, with new models for the scale, stations, and props\\\",\\n    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"Engine ClipDefs compiled onto the hero rig and played with AnimationMixer\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Engine Song and SoundDef data, plus a Web Audio formant voice. Music defaults to 10 percent.\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, own card, 1 to 4 players. Family Hour is local on one screen.\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"node tools/test.mjs, Playwright 1.63 Chromium with the five software WebGPU flags, WebKit and Firefox for the missing-WebGPU path, and the engine headless runner\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"The director plan already included engine and hub research and spikes. I read PLAN.md, the engine guide where the recipes pointed, and the hub README, and I checked the Dot table in code. I did not do extra research on the source beyond that plan.\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"Eleven issues. The expert pier jump scored two stars, pause let the pose clock move on the frame the button went down, two songs had uneven pattern lengths, a tray board lookup named a variable that was not in scope, a few model parts floated, the seagull was spoken as the scale, a dev-tool page could not go back, the prompt could draw past a short screen, the scale's voice measured just under the loudness line, the About screen kept only the first six lines so later source fields never appeared, and the menu cursor was a greater-than sign the font cannot draw, so it showed as a question mark.\\\",\\n    \\\"Two were game-breaking. The pier jump sat under the three-star line until takeoff recentred the dot, and the pose kept playing for one frame after pause. The others failed a data check, a voice check, a menu, or the About screen, and they were fixed before the hand-in.\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful test was the idle-versus-expert bot pass on every activity. It is what caught the pier jump sitting under the three-star line.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful test was the glyph scan. Every line already used the allowed characters, so it passed on the first run and did not change the game.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"Headless stepping, the pixel HUD, and a real input recorder made a week of play testable without a screen.\\\",\\n    \\\"I guessed wrong about pause. At timeScale 0 the headless stepper still calls fixedUpdate, and that call happens before update reads the pause key, so the pose clock moved unless the sim refused the step. Menu presses do still arrive. The type note reads as if those presses are dropped. Capture also needs all five Vulkan flags or the picture comes back blank.\\\",\\n    \\\"The centre-of-balance itself. The engine will move a character. It will not sway a polite dot, keep a week, or speak in formants.\\\",\\n    \\\"The hardest part was trusting the frame clock. Game time, the press window, and the hub clock are three different clocks, and only one of them is allowed to move a score.\\\",\\n    \\\"None. pixel-engine.js is the kit file, byte for byte.\\\",\\n    \\\"I would give the music bus a default of silence until the game sets it, so a shared browser profile cannot leave yesterday volume on today game.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The plan named the mechanics, the sentences, and the tests, so the work was building a game rather than inventing one.\\\",\\n    \\\"The cut list in the plan and the instruction to finish everything on this computer disagree. I followed the instruction and shipped the activities the cut list would drop.\\\",\\n    \\\"The hardest piece was the pier jump star line. The same bot that holds a pose will dive off a dock, and the flight begins wherever the dot was left.\\\",\\n    \\\"I would ask for the pause rule in one sentence: timeScale 0, fixedUpdate silent, update still reads keys. The guide and the type comment do not say the same thing.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Mint Dial\\\",\\n    \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"Keep the dot in the circle.\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"A week on a small island with a polite scale. Hold still, keep time, and try not to believe the number.\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Sports\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"series\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"players\\\": \\\"1–4\\\",\\n    \\\"controls\\\": \\\"Left stick, WASD or mouse: lean. R2, Space or click: breathe. L1/R1, F/J or mouse buttons: step.\\\",\\n    \\\"tags\\\": [\\n      \\\"pixel art\\\",\\n      \\\"comedy\\\",\\n      \\\"versus\\\",\\n      \\\"arcade\\\",\\n      \\\"3d\\\",\\n      \\\"story\\\"\\n    ]\\n  }\\n}\",\"total_lines\":58}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a222a508-b00c-4dce-ac55-2fa699baddfc-7","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→# Mint Dial\\n\\nThe hand-in is in this folder: `Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607.html` and `exit-interview.json`. The dev folder uses the same stem. `src/data/about.js` is the only copy of the source fields and the feedback. `tools/build.mjs` writes the HTML and the exit interview from it.\\n\\n## Shipped\\n\\nA week with Ounce the scale. Weigh-in, three guest slots, the ferry, seven days, the island, every planned activity (including Pier Jump, Vitamin Tray, Island Jog, Overhead Mortgage, and The Long Stand), the jar, the confession that subtracts 7, and an open Week 2. Family Hour runs three medley events for up to four players. An AI Hub session uses ghost mode and its own card. Attract mode, dev-tool sliders, and the touch gate are in. Music, effects, and the two voices are code.\\n\\n## Verification\\n10→\\n`node tools/test.mjs` from the dev folder printed `12/12 passed` and no failure lines.\\n\\nTwo `file://` Chromium launches, with the five software WebGPU flags, showed the title Mint Dial, music bus 0.10, and no page errors. Both captures are 1281×720 and painted. The saved frames show the title, the tagline, and the medical line. Prompts follow Cross, Xbox A, Enter, and click. Hover moved the focus from Gentle to More, and the click activated. A phone profile shows “Controller or keyboard required”, a settings control, and attract, and it does not start play from a touch. Widget rects fit at 1920×1080, 1280×720, and 640×360. An analyser read the mix, and an offline voice render was above 0.02 RMS with Ounce’s pitch above Coach’s. Three Family Hour lanes moved. WebKit and Firefox show “Failed to start: WebGPU unavailable” and raise no page error.\\n\\nThe hub harness on `127.0.0.1:38059` passed all four URLs (`players=1`, `players=2`, the lossy four-player case, and host-leave). With no session, the title still boots. JavaScript was served as `text/javascript`.\\n\\n`pixel-engine.js` sha256 is `80408b4c72ef08be3ec628d578f8b008644c1c7e447a4cc8c5979b08212e78aa`, the same as the kit.\\n\\n## About\\n20→\\nThe About screen pages every source field, the three feedback sections, the kit credits, the medical sentence, and the full kit credits text. Next, Previous, and the shoulder buttons move between pages.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→# Mint Dial\\n\\nThe hand-in is in this folder: `Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607.html` and `exit-interview.json`. The dev folder uses the same stem. `src/data/about.js` is the only copy of the source fields and the feedback. `tools/build.mjs` writes the HTML and the exit interview from it.\\n\\n## Shipped\\n\\nA week with Ounce the scale. Weigh-in, three guest slots, the ferry, seven days, the island, every planned activity (including Pier Jump, Vitamin Tray, Island Jog, Overhead Mortgage, and The Long Stand), the jar, the confession that subtracts 7, and an open Week 2. Family Hour runs three medley events for up to four players. An AI Hub session uses ghost mode and its own card. Attract mode, dev-tool sliders, and the touch gate are in. Music, effects, and the two voices are code.\\n\\n## Verification\\n10→\\n`node tools/test.mjs` from the dev folder printed `12/12 passed` and no failure lines.\\n\\nTwo `file://` Chromium launches, with the five software WebGPU flags, showed the title Mint Dial, music bus 0.10, and no page errors. Both captures are 1281×720 and painted. The saved frames show the title, the tagline, and the medical line. Prompts follow Cross, Xbox A, Enter, and click. Hover moved the focus from Gentle to More, and the click activated. A phone profile shows “Controller or keyboard required”, a settings control, and attract, and it does not start play from a touch. Widget rects fit at 1920×1080, 1280×720, and 640×360. An analyser read the mix, and an offline voice render was above 0.02 RMS with Ounce’s pitch above Coach’s. Three Family Hour lanes moved. WebKit and Firefox show “Failed to start: WebGPU unavailable” and raise no page error.\\n\\nThe hub harness on `127.0.0.1:38059` passed all four URLs (`players=1`, `players=2`, the lossy four-player case, and host-leave). With no session, the title still boots. JavaScript was served as `text/javascript`.\\n\\n`pixel-engine.js` sha256 is `80408b4c72ef08be3ec628d578f8b008644c1c7e447a4cc8c5979b08212e78aa`, the same as the kit.\\n\\n## About\\n20→\\nThe About screen pages every source field, the three feedback sections, the kit credits, the medical sentence, and the full kit credits text. Next, Previous, and the shoulder buttons move between pages.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/PROGRESS.md\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":200,\"raw_output\":\"# Mint Dial\\n\\nThe hand-in is in this folder: `Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607.html` and `exit-interview.json`. The dev folder uses the same stem. `src/data/about.js` is the only copy of the source fields and the feedback. `tools/build.mjs` writes the HTML and the exit interview from it.\\n\\n## Shipped\\n\\nA week with Ounce the scale. Weigh-in, three guest slots, the ferry, seven days, the island, every planned activity (including Pier Jump, Vitamin Tray, Island Jog, Overhead Mortgage, and The Long Stand), the jar, the confession that subtracts 7, and an open Week 2. Family Hour runs three medley events for up to four players. An AI Hub session uses ghost mode and its own card. Attract mode, dev-tool sliders, and the touch gate are in. Music, effects, and the two voices are code.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n`node tools/test.mjs` from the dev folder printed `12/12 passed` and no failure lines.\\n\\nTwo `file://` Chromium launches, with the five software WebGPU flags, showed the title Mint Dial, music bus 0.10, and no page errors. Both captures are 1281×720 and painted. The saved frames show the title, the tagline, and the medical line. Prompts follow Cross, Xbox A, Enter, and click. Hover moved the focus from Gentle to More, and the click activated. A phone profile shows “Controller or keyboard required”, a settings control, and attract, and it does not start play from a touch. Widget rects fit at 1920×1080, 1280×720, and 640×360. An analyser read the mix, and an offline voice render was above 0.02 RMS with Ounce’s pitch above Coach’s. Three Family Hour lanes moved. WebKit and Firefox show “Failed to start: WebGPU unavailable” and raise no page error.\\n\\nThe hub harness on `127.0.0.1:38059` passed all four URLs (`players=1`, `players=2`, the lossy four-player case, and host-leave). With no session, the title still boots. JavaScript was served as `text/javascript`.\\n\\n`pixel-engine.js` sha256 is `80408b4c72ef08be3ec628d578f8b008644c1c7e447a4cc8c5979b08212e78aa`, the same as the kit.\\n\\n## About\\n\\nThe About screen pages every source field, the three feedback sections, the kit credits, the medical sentence, and the full kit credits text. Next, Previous, and the shoulder buttons move between pages.\\n\",\"total_lines\":21}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"550fd7b6-78d9-44ac-a5be-754c0800db12"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_402","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The hand-in claims 12/12 tests and hub passes. I'll read the test harness and the captured logs before judging whether those checks actually drive the game."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4d35bf02-63f2-4d97-a669-1e34114de2d1-8","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/tools/test.mjs","limit":250}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4d35bf02-63f2-4d97-a669-1e34114de2d1-9","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/implementer/hub.log"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4d35bf02-63f2-4d97-a669-1e34114de2d1-10","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/implementer/nosession.log"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4d35bf02-63f2-4d97-a669-1e34114de2d1-11","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/implementer/browser.log","limit":200}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4d35bf02-63f2-4d97-a669-1e34114de2d1-12","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"^function |^export |^async function |^const tests|describe\\(|it\\(|test\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/tools/test.mjs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5963,"output_tokens":656,"cache_read_input_tokens":38272,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"43c5148f-ee88-407d-b9bf-0ad1a6fdda68"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-4d35bf02-63f2-4d97-a669-1e34114de2d1-8","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * Drives the shipped game. Prints failures and one \\\"N/N passed\\\" line.\\n * From the dev folder: node tools/test.mjs [--fast]\\n */\\nimport { createHash } from 'node:crypto';\\nimport { execFileSync } from 'node:child_process';\\nimport { appendFileSync, mkdirSync, readFileSync, readdirSync, statSync } from 'node:fs';\\nimport path from 'node:path';\\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\\n10→import {\\n  Engine,\\n  HERO_RIG,\\n  analyzeClip,\\n  checkModel,\\n  compileClips,\\n  parseSong,\\n  validateClip,\\n  validateTexture,\\n} from '../pixel-engine.js';\\n20→import { App, freshGuest } from '../src/app.js';\\nimport { CAMERA, World } from '../src/scenes/world.js';\\nimport { ACTIVITIES, ACTIVITY_BY_ID } from '../src/data/activities.js';\\nimport { DAYS } from '../src/data/week.js';\\nimport { LINES, SAMPLES, allLineStrings, linesFor } from '../src/data/lines.js';\\nimport { SONGS, songLevel } from '../src/audio/songs.js';\\nimport { syllabify } from '../src/audio/voice.js';\\nimport { Dot, DOT_DEFAULTS } from '../src/core/dot.js';\\nimport { BotDriver } from '../src/core/drivers.js';\\nimport { mulberry32 } from '../src/core/rng.js';\\n30→import { dripsFor, milestonesReached, starsFor } from '../src/core/score.js';\\nimport { SAVE_KEY, Save } from '../src/core/save.js';\\nimport { DEFAULT_TUNABLES, TUNABLE_TABS, tabKeys } from '../src/core/tunables.js';\\nimport { missingGlyphs, wrapText } from '../src/ui/font.js';\\nimport { MODELS } from '../src/art/models.js';\\nimport { CLIPS } from '../src/art/clips.js';\\nimport { clinicTile } from '../src/art/textures.js';\\nimport { ABOUT_COLS, ABOUT_ROWS, ENGINE_FEEDBACK, KIT_CREDITS, MEDICAL, PROMPT_FEEDBACK, SOURCE_INFORMATION, TESTING_FEEDBACK, aboutPages, exitInterview } from '../src/data/about.js';\\nimport { CREDITS_TEXT } from '../src/data/creditsText.js';\\nimport { TITLE } from '../src/data/title.js';\\n40→\\nconst here = path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url));\\nconst devRoot = path.resolve(here, '..');\\nconst SCRATCH = '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/implementer';\\nconst fast = process.argv.includes('--fast');\\nmkdirSync(SCRATCH, { recursive: true });\\nconst BEAT = path.join(SCRATCH, 'beat.log');\\n\\nconst fails = [];\\nlet total = 0;\\n50→\\nfunction beat(msg) {\\n  try { appendFileSync(BEAT, `${new Date().toISOString()} ${msg}\\\\n`); } catch { /* scratch only */ }\\n}\\n\\nasync function test(name, fn) {\\n  total += 1;\\n  beat(`start ${name}`);\\n  try {\\n    await fn();\\n60→    beat(`ok ${name}`);\\n  } catch (err) {\\n    fails.push(`${name}: ${err?.stack || err?.message || err}`);\\n    beat(`FAIL ${name}: ${err?.message || err}`);\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nfunction assert(cond, msg) {\\n  if (!cond) throw new Error(msg || 'assertion failed');\\n}\\n70→\\nfunction tap(engine, code) {\\n  engine.input.setKey(code, true);\\n  engine.step(1);\\n  engine.input.setKey(code, false);\\n  engine.step(1);\\n}\\n\\nfunction choose(engine, app, id) {\\n  let guard = 0;\\n80→  while (app.state().row !== id) {\\n    if (guard++ > 12) throw new Error(`no row ${id} in ${app.mode}: ${app.state().rows.join(',')}`);\\n    tap(engine, 'ArrowDown');\\n  }\\n  tap(engine, 'Enter');\\n}\\n\\nfunction untilMode(engine, app, mode, cap, label) {\\n  let n = 0;\\n  while (app.mode !== mode) {\\n90→    if (n >= cap) throw new Error(`${label || mode}: stuck in ${app.status()} after ${n} frames`);\\n    const chunk = Math.min(180, cap - n);\\n    engine.step(chunk);\\n    n += chunk;\\n    if (n % 1080 === 0) beat(`${label || mode} ${app.status()}`);\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nfunction memoryStorage() {\\n  const m = new Map();\\n100→  return {\\n    getItem: (k) => (m.has(k) ? m.get(k) : null),\\n    setItem: (k, v) => m.set(k, String(v)),\\n    removeItem: (k) => m.delete(k),\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nfunction releasePads() {\\n  let pads = [];\\n  try { pads = globalThis.navigator?.getGamepads?.() || []; } catch { pads = []; }\\n110→  for (const pad of pads) {\\n    if (!pad) continue;\\n    if (pad.axes) for (let i = 0; i < pad.axes.length; i++) pad.axes[i] = 0;\\n    if (pad.buttons) for (const button of pad.buttons) {\\n      button.pressed = false;\\n      button.value = 0;\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n120→async function boot(engine, opts = {}) {\\n  releasePads();\\n  const app = new App({ storage: opts.storage === undefined ? null : opts.storage, noHero: true, session: opts.session || null, touchOnly: !!opts.touchOnly });\\n  await engine.loadGame(new World(app));\\n  engine.step(2);\\n  return app;\\n}\\n\\nfunction band(skill, seed) {\\n  const dot = new Dot(mulberry32(seed));\\n130→  const bot = new BotDriver(skill, mulberry32(seed + 99));\\n  const dt = 1 / 60;\\n  let inside = 0;\\n  let n = 0;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 37 * 60; i++) {\\n    const u = skill === 'idle' ? { x: 0, y: 0 } : bot.read(dot, dt);\\n    dot.step(dt, u.x || 0, u.y || 0, DOT_DEFAULTS, {});\\n    if (i >= 120) {\\n      n += 1;\\n      if (Math.hypot(dot.x, dot.y) < 0.3) inside += 1;\\n140→    }\\n  }\\n  return inside / n;\\n}\\n\\nfunction walk(dir, out = []) {\\n  for (const name of readdirSync(dir)) {\\n    if (name === 'node_modules' || name === '.build') continue;\\n    const p = path.join(dir, name);\\n    if (statSync(p).isDirectory()) walk(p, out);\\n150→    else if (name.endsWith('.js')) out.push(p);\\n  }\\n  return out;\\n}\\n\\nasync function main() {\\n  console.info = () => {};\\n  await test('dot bands and star thresholds', async () => {\\n    const idle = band('idle', 1);\\n    const average = band('average', 1);\\n160→    const good = band('good', 1);\\n    const expert = band('expert', 1);\\n    assert(idle < 0.2, `idle ${idle}`);\\n    assert(average > 0.35 && average < 0.65, `average ${average}`);\\n    assert(good > 0.8, `good ${good}`);\\n    assert(expert > 0.95, `expert ${expert}`);\\n    assert(starsFor(idle * 100, [45, 70, 90]) === 0, 'idle stars');\\n    assert(starsFor(good * 100, [45, 70, 90]) === 3, 'good stars');\\n    assert(starsFor(44, [45, 70, 90]) === 0, 'below one');\\n    assert(starsFor(45, [45, 70, 90]) === 1, 'one');\\n170→    assert(starsFor(70, [45, 70, 90]) === 2, 'two');\\n    assert(starsFor(90, [45, 70, 90]) === 3, 'three');\\n    assert(DOT_DEFAULTS.dotInstability === 0.6 && DOT_DEFAULTS.dotLag === 0.08, 'defaults');\\n  });\\n\\n  await test('songs, lines, models, hash, about', async () => {\\n    for (const [name, song] of Object.entries(SONGS)) {\\n      parseSong(song);\\n      const level = songLevel(song);\\n      assert(level >= 0.03, `${name} level ${level}`);\\n180→    }\\n    assert(SONGS.step.bpm === 104, 'step bpm');\\n    const hash = createHash('sha256').update(readFileSync(path.join(devRoot, 'pixel-engine.js'))).digest('hex');\\n    const expected = readFileSync(path.join(devRoot, 'vendor/pixel-engine.sha256'), 'utf8').trim().split(/\\\\s+/)[0];\\n    assert(hash === expected, `hash ${hash}`);\\n    for (const model of MODELS) {\\n      const report = checkModel(model);\\n      assert(report.problems.length === 0, `${model.id || model.name} ${report.problems.join(';')}`);\\n    }\\n    const tex = validateTexture(clinicTile);\\n190→    assert(tex.problems.length === 0, `texture ${tex.problems.join(';')}`);\\n    assert(LINES.length >= 120, `lines ${LINES.length}`);\\n    const banned = /\\\\b(Wii|Mii|Wuhu)\\\\b|Balance Board|Wii Fit Trainer|Fit Age/;\\n    for (const text of allLineStrings()) {\\n      const bad = missingGlyphs(text);\\n      assert(bad.length === 0, `glyph ${bad.join('')} in ${text}`);\\n      for (const piece of wrapText(text, 52)) assert(piece.length <= 52, `wrap width ${piece}`);\\n      assert(wrapText(text, 52).length <= 3, `wrap lines ${text}`);\\n      assert(!banned.test(text), `banned ${text}`);\\n    }\\n200→    for (const def of ACTIVITIES) {\\n      for (const stars of [0, 1, 2, 3]) {\\n        for (const repeat of [false, true]) {\\n          const found = linesFor(def.id, stars, repeat);\\n          assert(found.length >= 1, `missing ${def.id} ${stars} ${repeat}`);\\n        }\\n      }\\n      assert(!banned.test(def.name), def.name);\\n    }\\n    for (const day of DAYS) assert(!banned.test(`${day.beat} ${day.concern}`), `day ${day.day}`);\\n210→    const pages = aboutPages(CREDITS_TEXT);\\n    const flat = pages.flatMap((p) => p.lines).join('').replace(/\\\\s+/g, '');\\n    const compact = (s) => String(s).replace(/\\\\s+/g, '');\\n    for (const page of pages) {\\n      assert(page.lines.length <= ABOUT_ROWS, `${page.title} lines ${page.lines.length}`);\\n      for (const text of page.lines) {\\n        assert(text.length <= ABOUT_COLS, `about width ${text.length}: ${text}`);\\n        assert(wrapText(text, 26).length === 1 && wrapText(text, 40).length === 1, `about rewrap ${text}`);\\n      }\\n    }\\n220→    assert(flat.includes(compact(MEDICAL)), 'medical');\\n    for (const key of Object.keys(SOURCE_INFORMATION)) assert(flat.includes(compact(SOURCE_INFORMATION[key])), `about ${key}`);\\n    for (const text of [...TESTING_FEEDBACK, ...ENGINE_FEEDBACK, ...PROMPT_FEEDBACK]) assert(flat.includes(compact(text)), `feedback ${text.slice(0, 24)}`);\\n    assert(flat.includes(compact(KIT_CREDITS)) && flat.includes('Kenney') && flat.includes('three.js') && flat.includes('Rapier'), 'kit');\\n    assert(flat.includes(compact(CREDITS_TEXT)), 'full credits');\\n    const aboutEngine = await Engine.headless(new World(new App({ storage: null, noHero: true })), { camera: CAMERA });\\n    try {\\n      const app = await boot(aboutEngine);\\n      choose(aboutEngine, app, 'start');\\n      choose(aboutEngine, app, 'about');\\n230→      assert(app.mode === 'about', app.mode);\\n      assert(app.state().rows[0] === 'next' && app.state().rows.includes('back'), app.state().rows.join(','));\\n      tap(aboutEngine, 'Enter');\\n      assert(app.aboutPage === 1, `next ${app.aboutPage}`);\\n      tap(aboutEngine, 'ArrowLeft');\\n      assert(app.aboutPage === 0, `left ${app.aboutPage}`);\\n      tap(aboutEngine, 'ArrowRight');\\n      assert(app.aboutPage === 1, `right ${app.aboutPage}`);\\n      const fullest = pages.reduce((best, page, i) => (page.lines.length > pages[best].lines.length ? i : best), 0);\\n      const drawPage = (index, width, height) => {\\n240→        aboutEngine.hud.sync({ width, height }, { cssWidth: width, cssHeight: height, offsetX: 0, offsetY: 0 });\\n        app.aboutPage = index;\\n        app.idle = 0;\\n        app.refresh(true);\\n        aboutEngine.step(1);\\n        const drawn = app.widgets.filter((w) => /^about-\\\\d/.test(w.id));\\n        assert(drawn.length === pages[index].lines.length, `page ${index} drew ${drawn.length}/${pages[index].lines.length} at ${width}x${height}`);\\n        for (const w of app.widgets) {\\n          assert(w.x >= -0.5 && w.y >= -0.5 && w.x + w.w <= width + 0.5 && w.y + w.h <= height + 0.5, `${w.id} outside ${width}x${height}: ${w.x},${w.y} ${w.w}x${w.h}`);\\n        }\\n250→        const head = app.widgets.find((w) => w.id === 'head');\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * Drives the shipped game. Prints failures and one \\\"N/N passed\\\" line.\\n * From the dev folder: node tools/test.mjs [--fast]\\n */\\nimport { createHash } from 'node:crypto';\\nimport { execFileSync } from 'node:child_process';\\nimport { appendFileSync, mkdirSync, readFileSync, readdirSync, statSync } from 'node:fs';\\nimport path from 'node:path';\\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\\n10→import {\\n  Engine,\\n  HERO_RIG,\\n  analyzeClip,\\n  checkModel,\\n  compileClips,\\n  parseSong,\\n  validateClip,\\n  validateTexture,\\n} from '../pixel-engine.js';\\n20→import { App, freshGuest } from '../src/app.js';\\nimport { CAMERA, World } from '../src/scenes/world.js';\\nimport { ACTIVITIES, ACTIVITY_BY_ID } from '../src/data/activities.js';\\nimport { DAYS } from '../src/data/week.js';\\nimport { LINES, SAMPLES, allLineStrings, linesFor } from '../src/data/lines.js';\\nimport { SONGS, songLevel } from '../src/audio/songs.js';\\nimport { syllabify } from '../src/audio/voice.js';\\nimport { Dot, DOT_DEFAULTS } from '../src/core/dot.js';\\nimport { BotDriver } from '../src/core/drivers.js';\\nimport { mulberry32 } from '../src/core/rng.js';\\n30→import { dripsFor, milestonesReached, starsFor } from '../src/core/score.js';\\nimport { SAVE_KEY, Save } from '../src/core/save.js';\\nimport { DEFAULT_TUNABLES, TUNABLE_TABS, tabKeys } from '../src/core/tunables.js';\\nimport { missingGlyphs, wrapText } from '../src/ui/font.js';\\nimport { MODELS } from '../src/art/models.js';\\nimport { CLIPS } from '../src/art/clips.js';\\nimport { clinicTile } from '../src/art/textures.js';\\nimport { ABOUT_COLS, ABOUT_ROWS, ENGINE_FEEDBACK, KIT_CREDITS, MEDICAL, PROMPT_FEEDBACK, SOURCE_INFORMATION, TESTING_FEEDBACK, aboutPages, exitInterview } from '../src/data/about.js';\\nimport { CREDITS_TEXT } from '../src/data/creditsText.js';\\nimport { TITLE } from '../src/data/title.js';\\n40→\\nconst here = path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url));\\nconst devRoot = path.resolve(here, '..');\\nconst SCRATCH = '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/implementer';\\nconst fast = process.argv.includes('--fast');\\nmkdirSync(SCRATCH, { recursive: true });\\nconst BEAT = path.join(SCRATCH, 'beat.log');\\n\\nconst fails = [];\\nlet total = 0;\\n50→\\nfunction beat(msg) {\\n  try { appendFileSync(BEAT, `${new Date().toISOString()} ${msg}\\\\n`); } catch { /* scratch only */ }\\n}\\n\\nasync function test(name, fn) {\\n  total += 1;\\n  beat(`start ${name}`);\\n  try {\\n    await fn();\\n60→    beat(`ok ${name}`);\\n  } catch (err) {\\n    fails.push(`${name}: ${err?.stack || err?.message || err}`);\\n    beat(`FAIL ${name}: ${err?.message || err}`);\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nfunction assert(cond, msg) {\\n  if (!cond) throw new Error(msg || 'assertion failed');\\n}\\n70→\\nfunction tap(engine, code) {\\n  engine.input.setKey(code, true);\\n  engine.step(1);\\n  engine.input.setKey(code, false);\\n  engine.step(1);\\n}\\n\\nfunction choose(engine, app, id) {\\n  let guard = 0;\\n80→  while (app.state().row !== id) {\\n    if (guard++ > 12) throw new Error(`no row ${id} in ${app.mode}: ${app.state().rows.join(',')}`);\\n    tap(engine, 'ArrowDown');\\n  }\\n  tap(engine, 'Enter');\\n}\\n\\nfunction untilMode(engine, app, mode, cap, label) {\\n  let n = 0;\\n  while (app.mode !== mode) {\\n90→    if (n >= cap) throw new Error(`${label || mode}: stuck in ${app.status()} after ${n} frames`);\\n    const chunk = Math.min(180, cap - n);\\n    engine.step(chunk);\\n    n += chunk;\\n    if (n % 1080 === 0) beat(`${label || mode} ${app.status()}`);\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nfunction memoryStorage() {\\n  const m = new Map();\\n100→  return {\\n    getItem: (k) => (m.has(k) ? m.get(k) : null),\\n    setItem: (k, v) => m.set(k, String(v)),\\n    removeItem: (k) => m.delete(k),\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nfunction releasePads() {\\n  let pads = [];\\n  try { pads = globalThis.navigator?.getGamepads?.() || []; } catch { pads = []; }\\n110→  for (const pad of pads) {\\n    if (!pad) continue;\\n    if (pad.axes) for (let i = 0; i < pad.axes.length; i++) pad.axes[i] = 0;\\n    if (pad.buttons) for (const button of pad.buttons) {\\n      button.pressed = false;\\n      button.value = 0;\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n120→async function boot(engine, opts = {}) {\\n  releasePads();\\n  const app = new App({ storage: opts.storage === undefined ? null : opts.storage, noHero: true, session: opts.session || null, touchOnly: !!opts.touchOnly });\\n  await engine.loadGame(new World(app));\\n  engine.step(2);\\n  return app;\\n}\\n\\nfunction band(skill, seed) {\\n  const dot = new Dot(mulberry32(seed));\\n130→  const bot = new BotDriver(skill, mulberry32(seed + 99));\\n  const dt = 1 / 60;\\n  let inside = 0;\\n  let n = 0;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 37 * 60; i++) {\\n    const u = skill === 'idle' ? { x: 0, y: 0 } : bot.read(dot, dt);\\n    dot.step(dt, u.x || 0, u.y || 0, DOT_DEFAULTS, {});\\n    if (i >= 120) {\\n      n += 1;\\n      if (Math.hypot(dot.x, dot.y) < 0.3) inside += 1;\\n140→    }\\n  }\\n  return inside / n;\\n}\\n\\nfunction walk(dir, out = []) {\\n  for (const name of readdirSync(dir)) {\\n    if (name === 'node_modules' || name === '.build') continue;\\n    const p = path.join(dir, name);\\n    if (statSync(p).isDirectory()) walk(p, out);\\n150→    else if (name.endsWith('.js')) out.push(p);\\n  }\\n  return out;\\n}\\n\\nasync function main() {\\n  console.info = () => {};\\n  await test('dot bands and star thresholds', async () => {\\n    const idle = band('idle', 1);\\n    const average = band('average', 1);\\n160→    const good = band('good', 1);\\n    const expert = band('expert', 1);\\n    assert(idle < 0.2, `idle ${idle}`);\\n    assert(average > 0.35 && average < 0.65, `average ${average}`);\\n    assert(good > 0.8, `good ${good}`);\\n    assert(expert > 0.95, `expert ${expert}`);\\n    assert(starsFor(idle * 100, [45, 70, 90]) === 0, 'idle stars');\\n    assert(starsFor(good * 100, [45, 70, 90]) === 3, 'good stars');\\n    assert(starsFor(44, [45, 70, 90]) === 0, 'below one');\\n    assert(starsFor(45, [45, 70, 90]) === 1, 'one');\\n170→    assert(starsFor(70, [45, 70, 90]) === 2, 'two');\\n    assert(starsFor(90, [45, 70, 90]) === 3, 'three');\\n    assert(DOT_DEFAULTS.dotInstability === 0.6 && DOT_DEFAULTS.dotLag === 0.08, 'defaults');\\n  });\\n\\n  await test('songs, lines, models, hash, about', async () => {\\n    for (const [name, song] of Object.entries(SONGS)) {\\n      parseSong(song);\\n      const level = songLevel(song);\\n      assert(level >= 0.03, `${name} level ${level}`);\\n180→    }\\n    assert(SONGS.step.bpm === 104, 'step bpm');\\n    const hash = createHash('sha256').update(readFileSync(path.join(devRoot, 'pixel-engine.js'))).digest('hex');\\n    const expected = readFileSync(path.join(devRoot, 'vendor/pixel-engine.sha256'), 'utf8').trim().split(/\\\\s+/)[0];\\n    assert(hash === expected, `hash ${hash}`);\\n    for (const model of MODELS) {\\n      const report = checkModel(model);\\n      assert(report.problems.length === 0, `${model.id || model.name} ${report.problems.join(';')}`);\\n    }\\n    const tex = validateTexture(clinicTile);\\n190→    assert(tex.problems.length === 0, `texture ${tex.problems.join(';')}`);\\n    assert(LINES.length >= 120, `lines ${LINES.length}`);\\n    const banned = /\\\\b(Wii|Mii|Wuhu)\\\\b|Balance Board|Wii Fit Trainer|Fit Age/;\\n    for (const text of allLineStrings()) {\\n      const bad = missingGlyphs(text);\\n      assert(bad.length === 0, `glyph ${bad.join('')} in ${text}`);\\n      for (const piece of wrapText(text, 52)) assert(piece.length <= 52, `wrap width ${piece}`);\\n      assert(wrapText(text, 52).length <= 3, `wrap lines ${text}`);\\n      assert(!banned.test(text), `banned ${text}`);\\n    }\\n200→    for (const def of ACTIVITIES) {\\n      for (const stars of [0, 1, 2, 3]) {\\n        for (const repeat of [false, true]) {\\n          const found = linesFor(def.id, stars, repeat);\\n          assert(found.length >= 1, `missing ${def.id} ${stars} ${repeat}`);\\n        }\\n      }\\n      assert(!banned.test(def.name), def.name);\\n    }\\n    for (const day of DAYS) assert(!banned.test(`${day.beat} ${day.concern}`), `day ${day.day}`);\\n210→    const pages = aboutPages(CREDITS_TEXT);\\n    const flat = pages.flatMap((p) => p.lines).join('').replace(/\\\\s+/g, '');\\n    const compact = (s) => String(s).replace(/\\\\s+/g, '');\\n    for (const page of pages) {\\n      assert(page.lines.length <= ABOUT_ROWS, `${page.title} lines ${page.lines.length}`);\\n      for (const text of page.lines) {\\n        assert(text.length <= ABOUT_COLS, `about width