05,111,110,39,41,32,114,101,116,117,114,110,32,39,79,110,101,32,113,117,101,115,116,105,111,110,39,59,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":30,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/app.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":4,\"content\":\"import { questionFor } from './data/questions.js';\"},{\"line_number\":23,\"content\":\"  'title', 'menu', 'slots', 'name', 'settings', 'about', 'howto', 'dropin',\"},{\"line_number\":24,\"content\":\"  'station', 'ferry', 'join', 'results', 'reveal', 'question', 'report',\"},{\"line_number\":78,\"content\":\"    felt: '',\"},{\"line_number\":126,\"content\":\"    this.drop = false;\"},{\"line_number\":146,\"content\":\"    this.question = null;\"},{\"line_number\":176,\"content\":\"    this.dropRecords = {};\"},{\"line_number\":204,\"content\":\"      this.drop = false;\"},{\"line_number\":232,\"content\":\"          { id: 'dropin', label: 'Drop-In' },\"},{\"line_number\":246,\"content\":\"      case 'question':\"},{\"line_number\":247,\"content\":\"        return (this.question?.answers || []).map((label, i) => ({ id: `a${i}`, label }));\"},{\"line_number\":314,\"content\":\"      case 'dropin':\"},{\"line_number\":341,\"content\":\"    if ((this.guest && (this.guest.day >= 6 || this.guest.unlockAll)) || this.drop) {\"},{\"line_number\":417,\"content\":\"    if (this.drop || this.guest?.unlockAll) return true;\"},{\"line_number\":462,\"content\":\"    if (!g || this.drop) return false;\"},{\"line_number\":487,\"content\":\"    if (this.guest && !this.drop) {\"},{\"line_number\":510,\"content\":\"      const rec = this.dropRecords[id] || { bestStars: 0, plays: 0 };\"},{\"line_number\":513,\"content\":\"      this.dropRecords[id] = rec;\"},{\"line_number\":524,\"content\":\"    if (this.guest && !this.drop) {\"},{\"line_number\":531,\"content\":\"    this.question = questionFor(this.guest?.day || 1);\"},{\"line_number\":532,\"content\":\"    this.mode = 'question';\"},{\"line_number\":557,\"content\":\"    if (this.guest && this.slot != null && !this.drop) data.slots[this.slot] = this.guest;\"},{\"line_number\":570,\"content\":\"      if (id === 'week') { this.drop = false; this.mode = 'slots'; }\"},{\"line_number\":571,\"content\":\"      else if (id === 'dropin') { this.drop = true; this.guest = freshGuest('Drop In'); this.guest.unlockAll = true; this.mode = 'island'; }\"},{\"line_number\":609,\"content\":\"    if (this.mode === 'question' && id.startsWith('a')) {\"},{\"line_number\":611,\"content\":\"      if (this.guest) this.guest.felt = this.question?.remarks?.[this.answer] || '';\"},{\"line_number\":658,\"content\":\"    if (this.mode === 'dropin' && id === 'play') { this.mode = 'island'; this.refresh(true); }\"},{\"line_number\":1271,\"content\":\"    else if (this.mode === 'confession') { line = 'I have been adding seven. It felt like kindness. It was not.'; }\"},{\"line_number\":1518,\"content\":\"    y = line(view, 'felt', wrapText(app.guest.felt || 'Noted.', 40)[0], y, 1, 'sand');\"},{\"line_number\":1625,\"content\":\"  if (app.mode === 'question') return 'One question';\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"1d261146-8d4c-48c7-ad73-1360f17f9796"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_409","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The latest full test run passed, including browser and hub at 07:47.\n\nThe 12/12 test log matches the previous run. I am now hunting for real bugs that tests miss. The guest felt age is saved to slots, but the plan says it should be used once and never saved. I need to verify whether a number picker exists for this age question.\n\nDrop-in guests bypass prescriptions but may still receive drips. I need to verify that drops only record visits and never award drips.\n\nThe jog score formula is correct despite messy dead code. A jog cadence bug is also being investigated.\n\nThe jog cadence line is a no-op and does not affect the final calculation.\n\nA same-side stumble bug was found. The initial side defaults to 'L', so the first left step counts as a stumble. The badSide counter persists forever, reducing speed by 0.5 on every subsequent left step.\n\nThe plan specifies a 0.5-second penalty for same-side stumbles, not a permanent speed reduction. This confirms the Island Jog bug.\n\nThe expert bot alternates sides, so the first left step is a false stumble. After that, side is R when the next left edge arrives, so the speed penalty never triggers again.\n\nThe speed penalty is only a temporary dip of 0.5 m/s per left step, not a persistent multiplier. The expert bot still scored well enough to pass tests.\n\nThe speed penalty is only about 0.008 meters per left step, not the planned 0.5 seconds. This is effectively a no-op. I am weighing whether this core bug is severe enough to warrant refutation.\n\nThe jog is playable and the expert can still earn three stars. The same-side stumble bug is a real but minor defect. It is quantitatively wrong yet too small to serve as a decisive adversarial refutation.\n\nThe same-side stumble is a minor mechanic. It is not central to the core Island Jog design, which focuses on foot alternation and cup collection.\n\nThe same-side stumble is a borderline no-op. I am now hunting for clearer bugs. I will search for the age number picker, check if hard versions have a UI toggle, and look into the ferry intro dot, last-one gag, long stand timeline events, attract hub walk, session pause freezing, HTML structure, and pixel-engine hash versus zip.\n\nMusic volume is confirmed at exactly 0.10 in the browser log.\n\nA widget fit discrepancy was spotted: widgets render at 640x360 but the HUD remains fixed at 480x270. If the engine does not update HUD dimensions when the window resizes, the fit test could be dishonest. I need to read browser.mjs to verify whether the page actually resizes.\n\nThe boot capture resolution is 1281x720, which conflicts with the plan's fill aspect requirement.\n\nThe 1281x720 boot capture is acceptable. The buffer matches the fill-aspect target size.\n\nThe hoop score stays at zero during play. I need to check whether rotations accumulate in the onStep handler or only update at finish.\n\nThe tray board mechanic is a dead code bug. The wrong-cup penalty path is unreachable because `this.bad` is never incremented. Rail gaps are also missing. Vitamins are locked to their own lane, so cross-lane tilting is impossible. The activity is simplified to independent 1D lanes.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5a26442c-66aa-4741-8b75-4fab4c8b6c15-35","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"How old|feltAge|picker|last one|Last one|lied|hard","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src","glob":"*.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5a26442c-66aa-4741-8b75-4fab4c8b6c15-36","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"ATTRACT|playlist|hub walk|iris|attracting","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/app.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5a26442c-66aa-4741-8b75-4fab4c8b6c15-37","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/core/sims.js","offset":190,"limit":320}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5a26442c-66aa-4741-8b75-4fab4c8b6c15-38","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/core/sims.js","offset":890,"limit":250}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6397,"output_tokens":2597,"cache_read_input_tokens":95488,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"76a44ca4-d122-4ca4-bc5c-ecd3322d448c"}
