{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_418","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Custom clips in clips.js are validated in tests but never compiled onto the running hero or played.\n\nThe hero only receives kit clips via attachModel, and only in island mode. Activity pose clips are dead code. The about text falsely claims gameplay uses AnimationMixer. The task is to use the engine's native animation system as the base.\n\nThe animations were created but never wired to gameplay. The code-correctness floor requires refuting features that serve no core purpose. For a Wii Fit-style game, animation is essential because the experience centers on holding balance poses while watching an avatar demonstrate them. Without the avatar performing the pose and without a readable dial, the activity screen becomes a static diorama.\n\nThe heading omits the activity name, making activities indistinguishable. RepSim only tracks downward lean and ignores left-right stick input for Apology Lunges and stick-up input for Overhead Mortgage. Keyboard rate control is never set, so bots pass by writing depth directly while players score near zero.\n\n`world.js` never compiles `CLIPS` or sets `action.time` from rep scrub. The camera stays locked on the title shot during activities. Mouse lean is measured from screen center rather than a dial.\n\nThe \"keep the dot in the circle\" readout is a ground ring beneath the yoga mat, not the specified HUD dial. This hides the activity state from players.\n\nMissing coach and classmates are polish, so they fall outside the core floor.\n\nThe ground ring may satisfy the \"You are a dot\" pillar if it is visible and leaning moves the dot.\n\nThe ground ring is 1.6 meters in radius and sits at the origin, directly in front of the camera. It should be clearly visible in the activity screenshot, so the earlier assumption that it was hidden or missed may be wrong.\n\nMost tests use `noHero: true`, so they never notice missing animation. The activity screenshot shows the idle hero, confirming the defect in play. The dev anim viewer sets `viewerClip` but never plays it; its test only asserts the string is truthy.\n\nLean body language after mixer.update is absent. This is dead specified behavior.\n\nThe paint function contains no HUD circle or dot. No 2D dial was missed.\n\nThe title is Mint Dial. This satisfies the non-goal requirement.\n\nExit interview matches the about text.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3fc18083-a2e5-45ff-af69-4564fbfff538-65","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"openPause|session","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/app.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3fc18083-a2e5-45ff-af69-4564fbfff538-66","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/app.js","offset":800,"limit":140}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4096,"output_tokens":1268,"cache_read_input_tokens":144256,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"61a9eb92-4e01-4a7e-ba10-6b78ef381796"}
