s been created.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/goal-verdict-46b978a86300-1-0.json has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/goal-verdict-46b978a86300-1-0.json\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"{\\n  \\\"refuted\\\": true,\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"bug\\\",\\n      \\\"location\\\": \\\"Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/core/sims.js:253\\\",\\n      \\\"detail\\\": \\\"Reps only follow u.depth, and LocalDriver sets depth to downward lean only (drivers.js:103) and never sets useRate. Stick-right lunges and stick-up presses leave r at 0; keyboard rate control is dead. Bots pass because auto() writes depth itself. Drive RepSim with LocalDriver-shaped input (right, up, and a key rate) and assert r tracks that axis.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"bug\\\",\\n      \\\"location\\\": \\\"Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/scenes/world.js:162\\\",\\n      \\\"detail\\\": \\\"Pose/rep clips are never compiled or played; hero.fixedUpdate runs only on the island menu; the camera stays the title shot; paint() draws no balance dial and labels play mode \\\\\\\"activity\\\\\\\". shots/activity.png is the same diorama with \\\\\\\"play 1s\\\\\\\". Play the activity clip (scrub reps with action.time), draw the dial the lean is measured from, and show the activity name. Recapture an activity frame that shows that.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"tools/test.mjs bots score via Sim.auto(); shots/activity.png and world.js:170-184 show clips and the dial are not on the play path. Latest beat.log ends ok browser at 07:47.\\\",\\n  \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n  \\\"blocking\\\": \\\"none\\\",\\n  \\\"details_md\\\": \\\"See the classifier markdown for the writeup.\\\"\\n}\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-b6fe3c47-facb-4f66-ac98-86573098756d-70","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"# Verdict: Refuted\\n\\nThe hand-in boots, the week state machine scores, and the last captured `node tools/test.mjs` run ends `12/12 passed` (`beat.log` through `ok browser, shots, and hub` at 07:47:20). Those tests drive `BotDriver` / `Sim.auto()`, not the player input path and not the picture. Two shipped behaviors are wrong on the path a player actually uses.\\n\\n## 1. Reps ignore the input the activity asks for\\n\\n`RepSim.onStep` scrubs only `u.depth` (`src/core/sims.js` around the `u.depth` / `useRate` branch). `LocalDriver.readFrom` sets `depth` to `Math.max(0, -y)` and never sets `useRate` or `rate` (`src/core/drivers.js`).\\n\\n- Apology Lunges are specified as stick left/right. A full right stick `{x: 1, y: 0}` yields `depth: 0`, so `r` stays 0 and the rep scores as a miss.\\n- Overhead Mortgage is specified as stick up. `{y: 1}` also yields `depth: 0`.\\n- Keyboard rate control (W/S move `r`, no key holds it) is a branch nothing calls.\\n\\nExpert bots still 3-star because `RepSim.auto()` writes `depth` itself. The idle/expert test never builds a `LocalDriver` sample. Fix the axis (down = downward lean, side = horizontal, up = upward) and the keyboard rate path, and assert it with `LocalDriver`-shaped input into `RepSim.step`, not `auto()`.\\n\\n## 2. Activities do not show the pose, the dial, or their name\\n\\n`src/art/clips.js` is validated in the test by compiling clips onto a throwaway model. `World.loadHero` compiles only `HERO_CLIPS` and `fixedUpdate` moves the hero only when `mode === 'island'` (`src/scenes/world.js`). Nothing sets a mixer clip from the activity, and nothing sets `action.time = r * duration` for reps. `cameraTarget()` always looks at the origin. `paint()` has no dial, no crosshair, and `heading()` falls through to the mode string, so play is titled \\\"activity\\\".\\n\\n`implementer/shots/activity.png` is the same island as the title and the menu, with the lines \\\"activity\\\" and \\\"play 1s\\\", an idle hero, and no readable circle. Lean is measured from the screen centre (`app.js` `readFrom` dial argument), not from a drawn dial. A player cannot see which activity is running or what the pose is doing.\\n\\nWire the activity clip onto the hero (scrub reps from `r`), draw the balance dial the mouse/stick is judged against, and put the activity name on that screen. Recapture the activity shot so it shows that, not another copy of the island menu.\\n\\n## What held\\n\\n`exit-interview.json` matches the TASK shape. The HTML is one file, title Mint Dial, music bus 0.10 on two `file://` boots, hub four URLs passed on `127.0.0.1:38059`, and the dot/week/save/voice tests exercise real modules. Those do not cover the two bugs above.\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/goal-classifier-46b978a86300-1-skeptic-0.md has been created.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/goal-classifier-46b978a86300-1-skeptic-0.md has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/goal-classifier-46b978a86300-1-skeptic-0.md\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"# Verdict: Refuted\\n\\nThe hand-in boots, the week state machine scores, and the last captured `node tools/test.mjs` run ends `12/12 passed` (`beat.log` through `ok browser, shots, and hub` at 07:47:20). Those tests drive `BotDriver` / `Sim.auto()`, not the player input path and not the picture. Two shipped behaviors are wrong on the path a player actually uses.\\n\\n## 1. Reps ignore the input the activity asks for\\n\\n`RepSim.onStep` scrubs only `u.depth` (`src/core/sims.js` around the `u.depth` / `useRate` branch). `LocalDriver.readFrom` sets `depth` to `Math.max(0, -y)` and never sets `useRate` or `rate` (`src/core/drivers.js`).\\n\\n- Apology Lunges are specified as stick left/right. A full right stick `{x: 1, y: 0}` yields `depth: 0`, so `r` stays 0 and the rep scores as a miss.\\n- Overhead Mortgage is specified as stick up. `{y: 1}` also yields `depth: 0`.\\n- Keyboard rate control (W/S move `r`, no key holds it) is a branch nothing calls.\\n\\nExpert bots still 3-star because `RepSim.auto()` writes `depth` itself. The idle/expert test never builds a `LocalDriver` sample. Fix the axis (down = downward lean, side = horizontal, up = upward) and the keyboard rate path, and assert it with `LocalDriver`-shaped input into `RepSim.step`, not `auto()`.\\n\\n## 2. Activities do not show the pose, the dial, or their name\\n\\n`src/art/clips.js` is validated in the test by compiling clips onto a throwaway model. `World.loadHero` compiles only `HERO_CLIPS` and `fixedUpdate` moves the hero only when `mode === 'island'` (`src/scenes/world.js`). Nothing sets a mixer clip from the activity, and nothing sets `action.time = r * duration` for reps. `cameraTarget()` always looks at the origin. `paint()` has no dial, no crosshair, and `heading()` falls through to the mode string, so play is titled \\\"activity\\\".\\n\\n`implementer/shots/activity.png` is the same island as the title and the menu, with the lines \\\"activity\\\" and \\\"play 1s\\\", an idle hero, and no readable circle. Lean is measured from the screen centre (`app.js` `readFrom` dial argument), not from a drawn dial. A player cannot see which activity is running or what the pose is doing.\\n\\nWire the activity clip onto the hero (scrub reps from `r`), draw the balance dial the mouse/stick is judged against, and put the activity name on that screen. Recapture the activity shot so it shows that, not another copy of the island menu.\\n\\n## What held\\n\\n`exit-interview.json` matches the TASK shape. The HTML is one file, title Mint Dial, music bus 0.10 on two `file://` boots, hub four URLs passed on `127.0.0.1:38059`, and the dot/week/save/voice tests exercise real modules. Those do not cover the two bugs above.\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"83e9c7f9-053b-4fce-82ba-850209f51fd9"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_421","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The JSON details_md field should contain the markdown content directly. If omitted, the aggregator falls back to the details file.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The verdict JSON should carry the same writeup as the markdown file. I'll put that text into `details_md`."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a87388a0-ae21-47e0-a199-a11f9654a9a4-71","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/goal-verdict-46b978a86300-1-0.json","content":"{\n  \"refuted\": true,\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"bug\",\n      \"location\": \"Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/core/sims.js:253\",\n      \"detail\": \"Reps only follow u.depth, and LocalDriver sets depth to downward lean only (drivers.js:103) and never sets useRate. Stick-right lunges and stick-up presses leave r at 0; keyboard rate control is dead. Bots pass because auto() writes depth itself. Drive RepSim with LocalDriver-shaped input (right, up, and a key rate) and assert r tracks that axis.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"bug\",\n      \"location\": \"Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/scenes/world.js:162\",\n      \"detail\": \"Pose/rep clips are never compiled or played; hero.fixedUpdate runs only on the island menu; the camera stays the title shot; paint() draws no balance dial and labels play mode \\\"activity\\\". shots/activity.png is the same diorama with \\\"play 1s\\\". Play the activity clip (scrub reps with action.time), draw the dial the lean is measured from, and show the activity name. Recapture an activity frame that shows that.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"evidence\": \"tools/test.mjs bots score via Sim.auto(); shots/activity.png and world.js:170-184 show clips and the dial are not on the play path. Latest beat.log ends ok browser at 07:47.\",\n  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n  \"blocking\": \"none\",\n  \"details_md\": \"# Verdict: Refuted\\n\\nThe hand-in boots, the week state machine scores, and the last captured `node tools/test.mjs` run ends `12/12 passed` (`beat.log` through `ok browser, shots, and hub` at 07:47:20). Those tests drive `BotDriver` / `Sim.auto()`, not the player input path and not the picture. Two shipped behaviors are wrong on the path a player actually uses.\\n\\n## 1. Reps ignore the input the activity asks for\\n\\n`RepSim.onStep` scrubs only `u.depth` (`src/core/sims.js` around the `u.depth` / `useRate` branch). `LocalDriver.readFrom` sets `depth` to `Math.max(0, -y)` and never sets `useRate` or `rate` (`src/core/drivers.js`).\\n\\n- Apology Lunges are specified as stick left/right. A full right stick `{x: 1, y: 0}` yields `depth: 0`, so `r` stays 0 and the rep scores as a miss.\\n- Overhead Mortgage is specified as stick up. `{y: 1}` also yields `depth: 0`.\\n- Keyboard rate control (W/S move `r`, no key holds it) is a branch nothing calls.\\n\\nExpert bots still 3-star because `RepSim.auto()` writes `depth` itself. The idle/expert test never builds a `LocalDriver` sample. Fix the axis (down = downward lean, side = horizontal, up = upward) and the keyboard rate path, and assert it with `LocalDriver`-shaped input into `RepSim.step`, not `auto()`.\\n\\n## 2. Activities do not show the pose, the dial, or their name\\n\\n`src/art/clips.js` is validated in the test by compiling clips onto a throwaway model. `World.loadHero` compiles only `HERO_CLIPS` and `fixedUpdate` moves the hero only when `mode === 'island'` (`src/scenes/world.js`). Nothing sets a mixer clip from the activity, and nothing sets `action.time = r * duration` for reps. `cameraTarget()` always looks at the origin. `paint()` has no dial, no crosshair, and `heading()` falls through to the mode string, so play is titled \\\"activity\\\".\\n\\n`implementer/shots/activity.png` is the same island as the title and the menu, with the lines \\\"activity\\\" and \\\"play 1s\\\", an idle hero, and no readable circle. Lean is measured from the screen centre (`app.js` `readFrom` dial argument), not from a drawn dial. A player cannot see which activity is running or what the pose is doing.\\n\\nWire the activity clip onto the hero (scrub reps from `r`), draw the balance dial the mouse/stick is judged against, and put the activity name on that screen. Recapture the activity shot so it shows that, not another copy of the island menu.\\n\\n## What held\\n\\n`exit-interview.json` matches the TASK shape. The HTML is one file, title Mint Dial, music bus 0.10 on two `file://` boots, hub four URLs passed on `127.0.0.1:38059`, and the dot/week/save/voice tests exercise real modules. Those do not cover the two bugs above.\\n\"\n}\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3613,"output_tokens":1366,"cache_read_input_tokens":152832,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"d16acea2-b0b1-43f7-a169-038254d54399"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a87388a0-ae21-47e0-a199-a11f9654a9a4-71","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"{\\n  \\\"refuted\\\": true,\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"bug\\\",\\n      \\\"location\\\": \\\"Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/core/sims.js:253\\\",\\n      \\\"detail\\\": \\\"Reps only follow u.depth, and LocalDriver sets depth to downward lean only (drivers.js:103) and never sets useRate. Stick-right lunges and stick-up presses leave r at 0; keyboard rate control is dead. Bots pass because auto() writes depth itself. Drive RepSim with LocalDriver-shaped input (right, up, and a key rate) and assert r tracks that axis.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"bug\\\",\\n      \\\"location\\\": \\\"Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/scenes/world.js:162\\\",\\n      \\\"detail\\\": \\\"Pose/rep clips are never compiled or played; hero.fixedUpdate runs only on the island menu; the camera stays the title shot; paint() draws no balance dial and labels play mode \\\\\\\"activity\\\\\\\". shots/activity.png is the same diorama with \\\\\\\"play 1s\\\\\\\". Play the activity clip (scrub reps with action.time), draw the dial the lean is measured from, and show the activity name. Recapture an activity frame that shows that.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"tools/test.mjs bots score via Sim.auto(); shots/activity.png and world.js:170-184 show clips and the dial are not on the play path. Latest beat.log ends ok browser at 07:47.\\\",\\n  \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n  \\\"blocking\\\": \\\"none\\\",\\n  \\\"details_md\\\": \\\"See the classifier markdown for the writeup.\\\"\\n}\\n\",\"new_string\":\"{\\n  \\\"refuted\\\": true,\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"bug\\\",\\n      \\\"location\\\": \\\"Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/core/sims.js:253\\\",\\n      \\\"detail\\\": \\\"Reps only follow u.depth, and LocalDriver sets depth to downward lean only (drivers.js:103) and never sets useRate. Stick-right lunges and stick-up presses leave r at 0; keyboard rate control is dead. Bots pass because auto() writes depth itself. Drive RepSim with LocalDriver-shaped input (right, up, and a key rate) and assert r tracks that axis.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"bug\\\",\\n      \\\"location\\\": \\\"Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/scenes/world.js:162\\\",\\n      \\\"detail\\\": \\\"Pose/rep clips are never compiled or played; hero.fixedUpdate runs only on the island menu; the camera stays the title shot; paint() draws no balance dial and labels play mode \\\\\\\"activity\\\\\\\". shots/activity.png is the same diorama with \\\\\\\"play 1s\\\\\\\". Play the activity clip (scrub reps with action.time), draw the dial the lean is measured from, and show the activity name. Recapture an activity frame that shows that.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"tools/test.mjs bots score via Sim.auto(); shots/activity.png and world.js:170-184 show clips and the dial are not on the play path. Latest beat.log ends ok browser at 07:47.\\\",\\n  \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n  \\\"blocking\\\": \\\"none\\\",\\n  \\\"details_md\\\": \\\"# Verdict: Refuted\\\\n\\\\nThe hand-in boots, the week state machine scores, and the last captured `node tools/test.mjs` run ends `12/12 passed` (`beat.log` through `ok browser, shots, and hub` at 07:47:20). Those tests drive `BotDriver` / `Sim.auto()`, not the player input path and not the picture. Two shipped behaviors are wrong on the path a player actually uses.\\\\n\\\\n## 1. Reps ignore the input the activity asks for\\\\n\\\\n`RepSim.onStep` scrubs only `u.depth` (`src/core/sims.js` around the `u.depth` / `useRate` branch). `LocalDriver.readFrom` sets `depth` to `Math.max(0, -y)` and never sets `useRate` or `rate` (`src/core/drivers.js`).\\\\n\\\\n- Apology Lunges are specified as stick left/right. A full right stick `{x: 1, y: 0}` yields `depth: 0`, so `r` stays 0 and the rep scores as a miss.\\\\n- Overhead Mortgage is specified as stick up. `{y: 1}` also yields `depth: 0`.\\\\n- Keyboard rate control (W/S move `r`, no key holds it) is a branch nothing calls.\\\\n\\\\nExpert bots still 3-star because `RepSim.auto()` writes `depth` itself. The idle/expert test never builds a `LocalDriver` sample. Fix the axis (down = downward lean, side = horizontal, up = upward) and the keyboard rate path, and assert it with `LocalDriver`-shaped input into `RepSim.step`, not `auto()`.\\\\n\\\\n## 2. Activities do not show the pose, the dial, or their name\\\\n\\\\n`src/art/clips.js` is validated in the test by compiling clips onto a throwaway model. `World.loadHero` compiles only `HERO_CLIPS` and `fixedUpdate` moves the hero only when `mode === 'island'` (`src/scenes/world.js`). Nothing sets a mixer clip from the activity, and nothing sets `action.time = r * duration` for reps. `cameraTarget()` always looks at the origin. `paint()` has no dial, no crosshair, and `heading()` falls through to the mode string, so play is titled \\\\\\\"activity\\\\\\\".\\\\n\\\\n`implementer/shots/activity.png` is the same island as the title and the menu, with the lines \\\\\\\"activity\\\\\\\" and \\\\\\\"play 1s\\\\\\\", an idle hero, and no readable circle. Lean is measured from the screen centre (`app.js` `readFrom` dial argument), not from a drawn dial. A player cannot see which activity is running or what the pose is doing.\\\\n\\\\nWire the activity clip onto the hero (scrub reps from `r`), draw the balance dial the mouse/stick is judged against, and put the activity name on that screen. Recapture the activity shot so it shows that, not another copy of the island menu.\\\\n\\\\n## What held\\\\n\\\\n`exit-interview.json` matches the TASK shape. The HTML is one file, title Mint Dial, music bus 0.10 on two `file://` boots, hub four URLs passed on `127.0.0.1:38059`, and the dot/week/save/voice tests exercise real modules. Those do not cover the two bugs above.\\\\n\\\"\\n}\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"Wrote file successfully to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/goal-verdict-46b978a86300-1-0.json.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"Wrote file successfully to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/goal-verdict-46b978a86300-1-0.json.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/goal-verdict-46b978a86300-1-0.json\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"{\\n  \\\"refuted\\\": true,\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"bug\\\",\\n      \\\"location\\\": \\\"Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/core/sims.js:253\\\",\\n      \\\"detail\\\": \\\"Reps only follow u.depth, and LocalDriver sets depth to downward lean only (drivers.js:103) and never sets useRate. Stick-right lunges and stick-up presses leave r at 0; keyboard rate control is dead. Bots pass because auto() writes depth itself. Drive RepSim with LocalDriver-shaped input (right, up, and a key rate) and assert r tracks that axis.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"bug\\\",\\n      \\\"location\\\": \\\"Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/scenes/world.js:162\\\",\\n      \\\"detail\\\": \\\"Pose/rep clips are never compiled or played; hero.fixedUpdate runs only on the island menu; the camera stays the title shot; paint() draws no balance dial and labels play mode \\\\\\\"activity\\\\\\\". shots/activity.png is the same diorama with \\\\\\\"play 1s\\\\\\\". Play the activity clip (scrub reps with action.time), draw the dial the lean is measured from, and show the activity name. Recapture an activity frame that shows that.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \