res, and the last captured `node tools/test.mjs` run ends `12/12 passed` (`beat.log` through `ok browser, shots, and hub` at 07:47:20). Those tests drive `BotDriver` / `Sim.auto()`, not the player input path and not the picture. Two shipped behaviors are wrong on the path a player actually uses.\\\\n\\\\n## 1. Reps ignore the input the activity asks for\\\\n\\\\n`RepSim.onStep` scrubs only `u.depth` (`src/core/sims.js` around the `u.depth` / `useRate` branch). `LocalDriver.readFrom` sets `depth` to `Math.max(0, -y)` and never sets `useRate` or `rate` (`src/core/drivers.js`).\\\\n\\\\n- Apology Lunges are specified as stick left/right. A full right stick `{x: 1, y: 0}` yields `depth: 0`, so `r` stays 0 and the rep scores as a miss.\\\\n- Overhead Mortgage is specified as stick up. `{y: 1}` also yields `depth: 0`.\\\\n- Keyboard rate control (W/S move `r`, no key holds it) is a branch nothing calls.\\\\n\\\\nExpert bots still 3-star because `RepSim.auto()` writes `depth` itself. The idle/expert test never builds a `LocalDriver` sample. Fix the axis (down = downward lean, side = horizontal, up = upward) and the keyboard rate path, and assert it with `LocalDriver`-shaped input into `RepSim.step`, not `auto()`.\\\\n\\\\n## 2. Activities do not show the pose, the dial, or their name\\\\n\\\\n`src/art/clips.js` is validated in the test by compiling clips onto a throwaway model. `World.loadHero` compiles only `HERO_CLIPS` and `fixedUpdate` moves the hero only when `mode === 'island'` (`src/scenes/world.js`). Nothing sets a mixer clip from the activity, and nothing sets `action.time = r * duration` for reps. `cameraTarget()` always looks at the origin. `paint()` has no dial, no crosshair, and `heading()` falls through to the mode string, so play is titled \\\\\\\"activity\\\\\\\".\\\\n\\\\n`implementer/shots/activity.png` is the same island as the title and the menu, with the lines \\\\\\\"activity\\\\\\\" and \\\\\\\"play 1s\\\\\\\", an idle hero, and no readable circle. Lean is measured from the screen centre (`app.js` `readFrom` dial argument), not from a drawn dial. A player cannot see which activity is running or what the pose is doing.\\\\n\\\\nWire the activity clip onto the hero (scrub reps from `r`), draw the balance dial the mouse/stick is judged against, and put the activity name on that screen. Recapture the activity shot so it shows that, not another copy of the island menu.\\\\n\\\\n## What held\\\\n\\\\n`exit-interview.json` matches the TASK shape. The HTML is one file, title Mint Dial, music bus 0.10 on two `file://` boots, hub four URLs passed on `127.0.0.1:38059`, and the dot/week/save/voice tests exercise real modules. Those do not cover the two bugs above.\\\\n\\\"\\n}\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"b10fcd29-8079-44cb-af0b-9d85d1f70c53"}
