{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_436","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I am examining the play() test around line 450 to understand how activities are driven. I will also check for rep score tests that might break if depth reading changes.\n\nBots using auto() will still work correctly with derived depth. Keyboard inputs stay on the lag path. I must preserve existing expert bot star scores and avoid changing the lag formula for the depth path. I am now drafting the axisDepth function for side-axis stick input.\n\nThe side-axis depth formula alternates stick-right between 1 and 0 across even and odd reps. A brief test stays in rep 0, so the depth tracks correctly without dropping. RepSim starts in an intro phase unless skipIntro is used.\n\nThe test will use `skipIntro: true` to bypass the intro phase and enter play immediately. The constructor confirms that `skipIntro` replaces the queue entirely, so practice is skipped.\n\nI am drafting a `fakeInput` helper that returns LocalDriver-shaped objects with axis values. This will let me drive the real code path and verify that the driver sets `useRate`.\n\nThe `fakeInput` helper now includes `isDown` and `wasPressed` methods. I am testing the pad path with stick-right input and verifying that keyboard input sets `useRate` to true. The next step is to feed these inputs into RepSim.\n\nLocalDriver will treat keyboard input as a non-pad, non-mouse device. It computes rate from KeyS/ArrowDown and KeyW/ArrowUp presses, setting useRate to true for keyboard devices.\n\nI will flip the up-axis rate sign in the simulation so keyboard S and W control the press direction correctly. When useRate is true for all keyboard input, the rate no longer follows depth position; instead it holds steady or moves at target speed. This prevents position-slamming during squats when no keys are held.\n\nThe up-axis rate sign is negated so keyboard W increases the rep counter. Stick up still follows the non-rate depth path. ArrowUp and ArrowDown will also set rate for squats since they are in the lean wishY. Mouse input does not use rate.\n\nMouse y negative is depth for squats, positive for press, and x is lunges. PadDriver does not set useRate; RepSim reads x and y directly. The family key lane uses LocalDriver. If a device is both pad and keys, the pad branch wins and useRate stays false.\n\nThe onStep depth logic now branches on useRate. When active, it clamps the rep counter using rate multiplied by speed and delta time.\n\nThe non-rate path now uses `depthOf` to compute depth from the input axis and smoothly interpolates the rep counter toward that value. The `depthOf` helper returns `u.depth` for down-axis, clamped `u.y` for up-axis, side-axis depth with alternating stick-right, and a fallback derived from `u.y`. Bot auto logic already sets both `depth` and `y` to match the axis, so the simulation reads them correctly.\n\nFatigue still applies at rep 0 because amplitude is zero, so early test frames are unaffected. I am drafting a `drive` helper that steps the simulation for a fixed duration using a constant input.\n\nI am writing the test assertions. Pad stick-right drives a lunge and stick-up drives a press, both asserting the rep counter rises above 0.45. Keyboard S drives a squat with useRate set and rate positive, asserting the rep counter exceeds 0.3. I will also verify that a negative stick input on a squat does not raise the rep counter.\n\nI added a negative control test: a right stick on a squat must not raise the rep counter. Stick-down still drives the squat correctly. I calculated the lag interpolation math to confirm the rep counter reaches its target within the test duration. Keyboard rate speed is 0.78125 reps per second.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-665d5639-d44d-46b6-9ebd-c823f4af50eb-59","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"Torso|Pelvis","glob":"**/hero/rig.d.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-665d5639-d44d-46b6-9ebd-c823f4af50eb-60","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/app.js","offset":410,"limit":50}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-665d5639-d44d-46b6-9ebd-c823f4af50eb-61","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"export \\{[^}]*AnimationMixer|AnimationMixer","glob":"**/pixel-engine.d.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-665d5639-d44d-46b6-9ebd-c823f4af50eb-62","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/tools/test.mjs","offset":430,"limit":90}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2233,"output_tokens":2853,"cache_read_input_tokens":114048,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"06aa776b-1948-4c35-9576-6937cd8b2646"}
