bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"fda97f3a-c06c-48c1-a048-b7508157e137"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_438","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Dial geometry will be centralized in one function used by both paint and readFrom. The lean will then be measured from the drawn dial.\n\nThe dial will be centered at (W/2, 56) with radius 44. The mouse force radius is 70. Moving the lean measurement point from the HUD centre to this drawn dial would change mouse lean values. Existing tests might not cover mouse position during play.\n\nThe `dialLayout` function will compute the dial center and radius dynamically based on screen dimensions. It will only render during activity, weigh, attract, and medley modes.\n\nThe dial centre will be fixed at (W/2, 56) for all modes where readFrom runs. Mouse clicks on menus will no longer affect lean measurement. A mouse at screen centre will now register as a downward lean from the dial. The drive test relies on gamepad stubs and keys rather than mouse input.\n\nThe dial will be drawn as a 2px ring using 28 white rectangles. Hovering over the title or settings screen is safe because readFrom is not called during those states.\n\nThe dial will also render an inner target ring scaled to the activity zone. The lean indicator dot will be drawn as a red rectangle at the offset position, with HUD Y coordinates inverted so upward lean points upward. A widget wrapper will be added around the dial for input handling. I need to verify whether StillSim exposes its ring property or if I should fall back to a default value.\n\nThe heading will display the activity name during activity and attract modes. Long names like \"The Chair Nobody Asked For\" are 26 characters, which at scale 2 requires 312 pixels—well within both 480 and 427 pixel widths. The heading uses scale 2 rather than titleScale, so it will not overflow on smaller screens.\n\nThe camera will switch to a close fixed shot during gameplay. Hero pose playback will be implemented in world.js. A concern remains about two mixers: the character's updateVisual also runs the kit animator, which writes bones.\n\nThe kit animator inside updateVisual overwrites the pose on every frame. The custom mixer must run after it so its pose wins. Otherwise the kit mixer would restore idle pose the next frame.\n\nSkipping updateVisual during activity is safer than overwriting the kit animator. The hero will not walk. fixedUpdate should not receive move input. The hero can stay at spawn if the pose is applied directly to the model transform rather than the physics body. This avoids foot IK root movement and keeps physics in sync.\n\nSkipping updateVisual would leave the hero model at its last island position, possibly off-screen from the activity camera. The hero must be explicitly placed at the mat before pose playback begins.\n\nThe hero model will be locked to the origin during pose playback, and updateVisual will be skipped so the kit animator cannot overwrite the custom pose. Returning to the island will resume normal physics updates. The camera will use a 28-degree field of view aimed at [0, 1.05, 0] from [2.4, 1.7, 3.4]. The viewerClip from the dev animation tool will also be played when set.\n\nThe camera will sit close and front-right to frame the hero body. The raised leg in the tree pose should be visible.\n\nLean offsets will be applied after the mixer writes its pose each frame. Torso rotation will use dot.x scaled by 0.18 and dot.y scaled by 0.12. Pelvis position will shift horizontally by dot.x scaled by 0.05. These offsets stack on top of the clip pose.\n\nScrubbing will pause the action, set its time to the clamp of the ring value against duration, and then call poseMixer.update(0) to refresh the pose. The playActivityClip method will select the clip from viewerClip or the activity definition, and it will stop any other active actions before starting the new one.\n\nThe new action is reset, looped indefinitely, and clamped when finished. Repetition activities pause the clip at a time scaled by the activity ring value and refresh the pose mixer; other activities play normally.\n\nStill poses are held clips that freeze the pose at frame zero. The tree shot will use the Tree clip with the activity name on the HUD and the dial drawn. The viewerClip from dev tools will only play during dev mode or explicit viewing to avoid overriding normal gameplay.\n\nThe camera update will return early when freeCam is active, preventing it from overriding the dev camera test. An empty viewerClip will not block activity clips; the code falls back to the activity definition's clip name.\n\nCamera switching will be limited to mode changes rather than running every frame. The PLAY_CAMERA object must be a fresh instance so tests that spread CAMERA are not mutated.\n\nThe close camera will also apply to the weigh-in screen, showing the dial and heading even when no activity clip exists. The hero will be grounded via fixedUpdate during activities, attract, and medley while remaining visually locked at the mat.\n\nDuring the play shot, fixedUpdate will be skipped so the hero stays at spawn. Only the visual root will move to the mat. On exit, updateVisual will snap the model back to the physics body. The skeptic cited fixedUpdate-only-on-island as a bug description, not a requirement for rep activities.\n\nThe hero will stay at spawn [0,0,3.2] during activities. Calling updateVisual would snap the mesh to the physics body and overwrite the pose mixer. The camera will target that spawn point so the close-up frames the hero.\n\nThe hero will run a zero-move fixedUpdate during activities to stay grounded without island movement. Then updateVisual will handle grounding and interpolation, followed by the custom pose mixer overwriting the clip pose. The concern is whether updateVisual's internal mixer update will fight the custom mixer and leave bones blended.\n\nThe custom mixer runs after updateVisual, so its tracks overwrite the kit animator's idle pose. The activity clips target Pelvis, Torso, arms, and legs, which should fully mask any leftover idle animation.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-23fe7133-c293-4d7c-9bd2-26a7017fba28-66","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"noHero|compileClips|HERO_MODEL|clips","glob":"**/test.mjs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-23fe7133-c293-4d7c-9bd2-26a7017fba28-67","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/main.js","limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":931,"output_tokens":3590,"cache_read_input_tokens":120960,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"62eea5af-4f6d-4ed5-bbb2-81e7ee9f6d5d"}
