{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-535660ca-0856-40d4-aa73-f065dc7e6790-124","content":"{\"type\":\"Bash\",\"output\":[49,50,47,49,50,32,112,97,115,115,101,100,10,69,88,73,84,58,48,10],\"output_for_prompt\":\"exit: 0\\n12/12 passed\\nEXIT:0\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"command\":\"cd \\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607\\\" && env -u NO_COLOR -u FORCE_COLOR node tools/test.mjs --fast > \\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/implementer/fast.log\\\" 2>&1; echo EXIT:$? >> \\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/implementer/fast.log\\\"; tail -20 \\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/implementer/fast.log\\\"\",\"truncated\":false,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Re-run node tests after the pose assertion fix\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3%2Fwork/01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469/terminal/call-535660ca-0856-40d4-aa73-f065dc7e6790-124.log\",\"total_bytes\":20}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"69a144f9-a8b0-45bd-9637-052b0391bf00"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_470","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All 12 tests passed in fast mode. The browser test was skipped.\n\nNode tests passed. I will update about.js feedback to include the two new issues before rebuilding HTML with browser shots. The activity PNG also needs review.\n\nThe missing pose was a screen bug that made the activity look like the title. Three issues were game-breaking: pier, pause, and reps that ignored every lean except down. The menu cursor was a greater-than sign the font cannot draw, so it showed as a question mark.\n\nThe about.js feedback draft now includes the pier jump sitting under the three-star line until takeoff recentres the dot, the pose playing for one frame after pause, and lunges or presses failing to move when the stick does. The remaining issues were fixed before hand-in.\n\nThe \"most helpful test\" comment needs revision. The idle-versus-expert bots wrote depth themselves, so they never caught the rep input bug. The glyph scan comment can stay.\n\nI will update about.js and run the full suite into test.log. PROGRESS.md will be updated after the suite completes. The scratch pose-check.mjs file will be deleted once it is no longer needed. I should verify that no browsers remain running before the full test begins. A widget track overflow during the browser widget test would appear on the title screen rather than the squat activity.\n\nThe activity shot is 1920 pixels wide. The dial widget sits at y=12 on a 480x270 screen, so the head remains below it. The browser widget test only checks pose and does not verify widget overflow, meaning a track that extends past the HUD would go unnoticed there. The node test only checks the dial box, so an overflowing track would also evade detection in that suite.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f91f1caa-2ad0-47ae-bd44-f44af59200c3-125","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/data/about.js","old_string":"  'Eleven issues. The expert pier jump scored two stars, pause let the pose clock move on the frame the button went down, two songs had uneven pattern lengths, a tray board lookup named a variable that was not in scope, a few model parts floated, the seagull was spoken as the scale, a dev-tool page could not go back, the prompt could draw past a short screen, the scale\\'s voice measured just under the loudness line, the About screen kept only the first six lines so later source fields never appeared, and the menu cursor was a greater-than sign the font cannot draw, so it showed as a question mark.',\n  'Two were game-breaking. The pier jump sat under the three-star line until takeoff recentred the dot, and the pose kept playing for one frame after pause. The others failed a data check, a voice check, a menu, or the About screen, and they were fixed before the hand-in.',\n  'The most helpful test was the idle-versus-expert bot pass on every activity. It is what caught the pier jump sitting under the three-star line.',","new_string":"  'Thirteen issues. The expert pier jump scored two stars, pause let the pose clock move on the frame the button went down, two songs had uneven pattern lengths, a tray board lookup named a variable that was not in scope, a few model parts floated, the seagull was spoken as the scale, a dev-tool page could not go back, the prompt could draw past a short screen, the scale\\'s voice measured just under the loudness line, the About screen kept only the first six lines so later source fields never appeared, the menu cursor was a greater-than sign the font cannot draw, so it showed as a question mark, reps listened only to a downward lean so a sideways lunge and an upward press did nothing, and an activity kept the title camera, never played its pose, and labelled the screen activity.',\n  'Three were game-breaking. The pier jump sat under the three-star line until takeoff recentred the dot, the pose kept playing for one frame after pause, and a lunge or a press did not move when the stick did. The others failed a data check, a voice check, a menu, or the picture of the exercise, and they were fixed before the hand-in.',\n  'The most helpful test was driving a rep with the input the stick and the keys actually produce. The idle-versus-expert bots wrote the depth themselves, so they still scored while a sideways lunge stayed at zero. That same bot pass is what caught the pier jump.',"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":493,"output_tokens":1495,"cache_read_input_tokens":178944,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"58c8577f-3fac-4b21-b33c-eb95266bb631"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f91f1caa-2ad0-47ae-bd44-f44af59200c3-125","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"  'Eleven issues. The expert pier jump scored two stars, pause let the pose clock move on the frame the button went down, two songs had uneven pattern lengths, a tray board lookup named a variable that was not in scope, a few model parts floated, the seagull was spoken as the scale, a dev-tool page could not go back, the prompt could draw past a short screen, the scale\\\\'s voice measured just under the loudness line, the About screen kept only the first six lines so later source fields never appeared, and the menu cursor was a greater-than sign the font cannot draw, so it showed as a question mark.',\\n  'Two were game-breaking. The pier jump sat under the three-star line until takeoff recentred the dot, and the pose kept playing for one frame after pause. The others failed a data check, a voice check, a menu, or the About screen, and they were fixed before the hand-in.',\\n  'The most helpful test was the idle-versus-expert bot pass on every activity. It is what caught the pier jump sitting under the three-star line.',\",\"new_string\":\"  'Thirteen issues. The expert pier jump scored two stars, pause let the pose clock move on the frame the button went down, two songs had uneven pattern lengths, a tray board lookup named a variable that was not in scope, a few model parts floated, the seagull was spoken as the scale, a dev-tool page could not go back, the prompt could draw past a short screen, the scale\\\\'s voice measured just under the loudness line, the About screen kept only the first six lines so later source fields never appeared, the menu cursor was a greater-than sign the font cannot draw, so it showed as a question mark, reps listened only to a downward lean so a sideways lunge and an upward press did nothing, and an activity kept the title camera, never played its pose, and labelled the screen activity.',\\n  'Three were game-breaking. The pier jump sat under the three-star line until takeoff recentred the dot, the pose kept playing for one frame after pause, and a lunge or a press did not move when the stick did. The others failed a data check, a voice check, a menu, or the picture of the exercise, and they were fixed before the hand-in.',\\n  'The most helpful test was driving a rep with the input the stick and the keys actually produce. The idle-versus-expert bots wrote the depth themselves, so they still scored while a sideways lunge stayed at zero. That same bot pass is what caught the pier jump.',\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/data/about.js has been updated successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/data/about.js has been updated.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/data/about.js\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"  'Eleven issues. The expert pier jump scored two stars, pause let the pose clock move on the frame the button went down, two songs had uneven pattern lengths, a tray board lookup named a variable that was not in scope, a few model parts floated, the seagull was spoken as the scale, a dev-tool page could not go back, the prompt could draw past a short screen, the scale\\\\'s voice measured just under the loudness line, the About screen kept only the first six lines so later source fields never appeared, and the menu cursor was a greater-than sign the font cannot draw, so it showed as a question mark.',\\n  'Two were game-breaking. The pier jump sat under the three-star line until takeoff recentred the dot, and the pose kept playing for one frame after pause. The others failed a data check, a voice check, a menu, or the About screen, and they were fixed before the hand-in.',\\n  'The most helpful test was the idle-versus-expert bot pass on every activity. It is what caught the pier jump sitting under the three-star line.',\",\"old_line\":27,\"new_string\":\"  'Thirteen issues. The expert pier jump scored two stars, pause let the pose clock move on the frame the button went down, two songs had uneven pattern lengths, a tray board lookup named a variable that was not in scope, a few model parts floated, the seagull was spoken as the scale, a dev-tool page could not go back, the prompt could draw past a short screen, the scale\\\\'s voice measured just under the loudness line, the About screen kept only the first six lines so later source fields never appeared, the menu cursor was a greater-than sign the font cannot draw, so it showed as a question mark, reps listened only to a downward lean so a sideways lunge and an upward press did nothing, and an activity kept the title camera, never played its pose, and labelled the screen activity.',\\n  'Three were game-breaking. The pier jump sat under the three-star line until takeoff recentred the dot, the pose kept playing for one frame after pause, and a lunge or a press did not move when the stick did. The others failed a data check, a voice check, a menu, or the picture of the exercise, and they were fixed before the hand-in.',\\n  'The most helpful test was driving a rep with the input the stick and the keys actually produce. The idle-versus-expert bots wrote the depth themselves, so they still scored while a sideways lunge stayed at zero. That same bot pass is what caught the pier jump.',\",\"new_line\":27,\"context_before\":\"};\\n\\nexport const TESTING_FEEDBACK = [\\n\",\"context_after\":\"  'The least helpful test was the glyph scan. Every line already used the allowed characters, so it passed on the first run and did not change the game.',\\n];\\n\\n\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"cf233a6b-4476-4fb4-ad58-8f3abc590ebf"}
