{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_482","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The HTML build timestamp is 01:15:22. The app.js file was last modified at 01:14:57, before the build.\n\nThe suite finished at 01:16:41. PROGRESS.md was updated after the build but does not affect the game. The evidence is current and matches the sources. The skeptic cited stale line numbers from an older snapshot. The evaluator requires a rebuild and recapture.\n\nRebuilding without source changes will recapture the shot. The flagged gaps are already fixed in code, so re-running the full suite is redundant. The evaluator's request for confirmation is satisfied by the existing files.\n\nThe rejection likely predates the fixes and was written as a template. The next step asks to run the plan's verification steps. I will check whether the activity shot actually fails the skeptic's visual bar.\n\nThe new activity shot shows the dial and title but still displays \"play 1s\" as the phase line. The character may look unchanged because the skinned mesh does not follow the animation mixer. I will compare a standing frame and a deep squat frame to verify whether the pose actually shifts visually.\n\nThe animation mixer and model share the same loaded scene, so the bones should be driven correctly. The latest image shows the hero standing with arms forward and body filling the lower half.\n\nThe camera frames the hero from a slight forward angle. A standing figure places its head around y=1.6, which sits above the look target and explains why the head appears centered with sky visible. A deep squat would drop the head toward y=1.2. I will capture the start and forced deep squat frames to see if the pose actually changes.\n\nI will write a short Playwright script to open the existing HTML, step through the squat animation at both r=0 and r=1, capture the frames, and compare them. If the images differ, the clip is visible; if not, I need to fix playback. The evaluator still requires a recapture.\n\nI will run the diagnostic capture first to avoid recapturing a still-wrong frame. I checked whether `hero.updateVisual` is skipped and the skinned mesh needs manual bone matrix updates. The AnimationMixer should update transforms automatically on the next render, so `updateVisual` is not required. The scene model and mixer are correctly linked.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-55506f91-0535-4baa-8cfa-1671b0bcfac1-142","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"capture\\(","glob":"**/*.{d.ts,mjs}","head_limit":20}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-55506f91-0535-4baa-8cfa-1671b0bcfac1-143","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/implementer/browser.log","limit":20}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-55506f91-0535-4baa-8cfa-1671b0bcfac1-144","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/implementer/hub.log","limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3225,"output_tokens":1358,"cache_read_input_tokens":199680,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"60893b72-83d6-4c7a-ae58-f1ce48839b9a"}
