{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_495","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The suite passed. PROGRESS.md still names the old hub port, so I am updating that line to the run that just finished."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-60435af7-6d5a-446a-a466-1a558ee1b43c-34","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/PROGRESS.md","old_string":"The hub harness on `127.0.0.1:38059` passed all four URLs (`players=1`, `players=2`, the lossy four-player case, and host-leave). With no session, the title still boots. JavaScript was served as `text/javascript`.","new_string":"The hub harness on `127.0.0.1:37259` passed all four URLs (`players=1`, `players=2`, the lossy four-player case, and host-leave). With no session, the title still boots. JavaScript was served as `text/javascript`. The activity frame is a close shot of Squats of Regret: the pose is on the body, the balance dial and the rep track are on screen, and the exercise name sits below the face."}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-60435af7-6d5a-446a-a466-1a558ee1b43c-35","name":"todo_write","input":{"todos":[{"id":"rebuild-evidence","content":"Rebuild HTML and exit-interview, recapture activity shot, fresh suite logs","status":"completed"}],"merge":true}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1170,"output_tokens":397,"cache_read_input_tokens":67712,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"385e25dd-0040-4873-a4a4-3307a19b28fd"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-60435af7-6d5a-446a-a466-1a558ee1b43c-34","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"The hub harness on `127.0.0.1:38059` passed all four URLs (`players=1`, `players=2`, the lossy four-player case, and host-leave). With no session, the title still boots. JavaScript was served as `text/javascript`.\",\"new_string\":\"The hub harness on `127.0.0.1:37259` passed all four URLs (`players=1`, `players=2`, the lossy four-player case, and host-leave). With no session, the title still boots. JavaScript was served as `text/javascript`. The activity frame is a close shot of Squats of Regret: the pose is on the body, the balance dial and the rep track are on screen, and the exercise name sits below the face.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/PROGRESS.md has been updated successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/PROGRESS.md has been updated.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/PROGRESS.md\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"The hub harness on `127.0.0.1:38059` passed all four URLs (`players=1`, `players=2`, the lossy four-player case, and host-leave). With no session, the title still boots. JavaScript was served as `text/javascript`.\",\"old_line\":15,\"new_string\":\"The hub harness on `127.0.0.1:37259` passed all four URLs (`players=1`, `players=2`, the lossy four-player case, and host-leave). With no session, the title still boots. JavaScript was served as `text/javascript`. The activity frame is a close shot of Squats of Regret: the pose is on the body, the balance dial and the rep track are on screen, and the exercise name sits below the face.\",\"new_line\":15,\"context_before\":\"\\nTwo `file://` Chromium launches, with the five software WebGPU flags, showed the title Mint Dial, music bus 0.10, and no page errors. Both captures are 1281×720 and painted. The saved frames show the title, the tagline, and the medical line. Prompts follow Cross, Xbox A, Enter, and click. Hover moved the focus from Gentle to More, and the click activated. A phone profile shows “Controller or keyboard required”, a settings control, and attract, and it does not start play from a touch. Widget rects fit at 1920×1080, 1280×720, and 640×360. An analyser read the mix, and an offline voice render was above 0.02 RMS with Ounce’s pitch above Coach’s. Three Family Hour lanes moved. WebKit and Firefox show “Failed to start: WebGPU unavailable” and raise no page error.\\n\\n\",\"context_after\":\"\\n`pixel-engine.js` sha256 is `80408b4c72ef08be3ec628d578f8b008644c1c7e447a4cc8c5979b08212e78aa`, the same as the kit.\\n\\n\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-60435af7-6d5a-446a-a466-1a558ee1b43c-35","content":"{\"type\":\"Todo\",\"TodosUpdated\":{\"summary_for_prompt\":\"- [completed] 1: Download kit and hub, record sha256, scaffold dev folder and title\\n- [completed] 2: Implement Dot, drivers, actions, device, tunables, HUD, pause, dev sliders\\n- [completed] 3: Ship Holding Still end to end and lock bot star tests\\n- [completed] 4: Build island, weigh-in, seven-day loop, saves, report, jar, locker\\n- [completed] 5: Add remaining activities with idle-vs-expert bot tests and lines\\n- [completed] 6: Fix remaining --fast failures (rng scan, pause freeze, week boot) and get 11/11\\n- [completed] 7: Fix About HUD so every source field and the full feedback are visible, then rebuild\\n- [completed] 8: Hand in exit-interview.json, PROGRESS.md, checklist and deviations\\n- [completed] confirm-handin: Confirm exit-interview.json matches about.js and the three hand-in files are in the workspace root\\n- [cancelled] rebuild-if-stale: Rebuild HTML and exit-interview.json only if they differ from the current About source\\n- [completed] reps-input: Drive RepSim from LocalDriver right/up lean and key rate, with a real-path test\\n- [completed] activity-scene: Play activity clips, draw the balance dial, show the activity name, recapture the activity frame\\n- [completed] reverify: Re-run the suite and confirm the activity shot shows the clip, dial, and name\\n- [completed] verify-reps: Confirm RepSim follows stick axes and keyboard rate via LocalDriver\\n- [completed] verify-pose: Confirm activity clips, close camera, dial, and exercise name\\n- [completed] rebuild-evidence: Rebuild HTML and exit-interview, recapture activity shot, fresh suite logs\\n\",\"todos\":[{\"content\":\"Download kit and hub, record sha256, scaffold dev folder and title\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"Implement Dot, drivers, actions, device, tunables, HUD, pause, dev sliders\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"Ship Holding Still end to end and lock bot star tests\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"Build island, weigh-in, seven-day loop, saves, report, jar, locker\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"Add remaining activities with idle-vs-expert bot tests and lines\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"Fix remaining --fast failures (rng scan, pause freeze, week boot) and get 11/11\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"Fix About HUD so every source field and the full feedback are visible, then rebuild\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"Hand in exit-interview.json, PROGRESS.md, checklist and deviations\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"Confirm exit-interview.json matches about.js and the three hand-in files are in the workspace root\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"Rebuild HTML and exit-interview.json only if they differ from the current About source\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"cancelled\"},{\"content\":\"Drive RepSim from LocalDriver right/up lean and key rate, with a real-path test\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"Play activity clips, draw the balance dial, show the activity name, recapture the activity frame\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"Re-run the suite and confirm the activity shot shows the clip, dial, and name\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"Confirm RepSim follows stick axes and keyboard rate via LocalDriver\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"Confirm activity clips, close camera, dial, and exercise name\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"Rebuild HTML and exit-interview, recapture activity shot, fresh suite logs\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"}],\"state\":{\"todos\":{\"1\":{\"content\":\"Download kit and hub, record sha256, scaffold dev folder and title\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"2\":{\"content\":\"Implement Dot, drivers, actions, device, tunables, HUD, pause, dev sliders\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"3\":{\"content\":\"Ship Holding Still end to end and lock bot star tests\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"4\":{\"content\":\"Build island, weigh-in, seven-day loop, saves, report, jar, locker\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"5\":{\"content\":\"Add remaining activities with idle-vs-expert bot tests and lines\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"6\":{\"content\":\"Fix remaining --fast failures (rng scan, pause freeze, week boot) and get 11/11\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"7\":{\"content\":\"Fix About HUD so every source field and the full feedback are visible, then rebuild\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"8\":{\"content\":\"Hand in exit-interview.json, PROGRESS.md, checklist and deviations\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"confirm-handin\":{\"content\":\"Confirm exit-interview.json matches about.js and the three hand-in files are in the workspace root\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"rebuild-if-stale\":{\"content\":\"Rebuild HTML and exit-interview.json only if they differ from the current About source\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"cancelled\"},\"reps-input\":{\"content\":\"Drive RepSim from LocalDriver right/up lean and key rate, with a real-path test\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"activity-scene\":{\"content\":\"Play activity clips, draw the balance dial, show the activity name, recapture the activity frame\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"reverify\":{\"content\":\"Re-run the suite and confirm the activity shot shows the clip, dial, and name\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"verify-reps\":{\"content\":\"Confirm RepSim follows stick axes and keyboard rate via LocalDriver\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"verify-pose\":{\"content\":\"Confirm activity clips, close camera, dial, and exercise name\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"rebuild-evidence\":{\"content\":\"Rebuild HTML and exit-interview, recapture activity shot, fresh suite logs\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"}}}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"1b0df6d5-92d5-4fde-a6b9-45f83ecea1a5"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_496","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The final reply must include all Source Information fields, Testing/Engine/Prompt Feedback, kit credits, and the exact sentence \"This is not medical advice.\"\n\nSource Information fields are being compiled from about.js. The scale is a Wii Fit activity. The plan is PLAN.md. The genre is Sports. The perspective is an isometric island with a fixed camera. The tech stack is Pixel Engine 0.46.0, three.js r186, Rapier 0.20, and esbuild 0.28.2. Art direction uses the engine's native pixel look with new models for the scale, stations, and props. Animations use ClipDefs compiled onto the hero rig and played with AnimationMixer.\n\nAudio uses engine Song and SoundDef data plus a Web Audio formant voice. Music defaults to 10 percent. Online features include AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, own card, and one to four players. Family Hour is local on one screen. Testing runs node tools/test.mjs with Playwright 1.63 Chromium using five software WebGPU flags. WebKit and Firefox cover the missing-WebGPU path. The engine headless runner is also used. Research covered the director plan, engine guide, hub README, and the Dot table in code.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The hand-in is rebuilt from the current sources, and `node tools/test.mjs` printed `13/13 passed`.\n\nReps follow the stick for that exercise and the keyboard moves them by rate. A sideways lunge and an upward press both raise the rep, and holding S does the same. Squats of Regret plays the `SquatRep` clip on a close camera, draws the balance dial and the rep track, and shows the exercise name below the face. The fresh activity frame matches that.\n\nThe single-file HTML and `exit-interview.json` were written by `tools/build.mjs` at 01:23. The JSON matches `exitInterview()` from `src/data/about.js`. Usage is `added on import`. The document title is Mint Dial. Two `file://` boots showed that title, music bus 0.10, and no page errors. The hub on `127.0.0.1:37259` passed all four harness URLs, and a page with no session still opens the title.\n\nThis is not medical advice. Ounce is a scale.\n\n**Source Information**\n\n- Date: 2026-11-04 22:16:07\n- Source: Wii Fit\n- Plan: PLAN.md\n- Genre: Sports\n- Perspective: Isometric island, with a fixed camera for each activity\n- Tech: Pixel Engine 0.46.0, three.js r186, Rapier 0.20 as bundled, esbuild 0.28.2\n- Art Direction: The engine native pixel look, with new models for the scale, stations, and props\n- Animation: Engine ClipDefs compiled onto the hero rig and played with AnimationMixer\n- Audio: Engine Song and SoundDef data, plus a Web Audio formant voice. Music defaults to 10 percent.\n- Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, own card, 1 to 4 players. Family Hour is local on one screen.\n- Testing: node tools/test.mjs, Playwright 1.63 Chromium with the five software WebGPU flags, WebKit and Firefox for the missing-WebGPU path, and the engine headless runner\n- Research: The director plan already included engine and hub research and spikes. I read PLAN.md, the engine guide where the recipes pointed, and the hub README, and I checked the Dot table in code. I did not do extra research on the source beyond that plan.\n- Environment: Grok CLI (headless); Linux\n- Model: xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\n- Usage: added on import\n\n**Testing Feedback**\n\n1. Thirteen issues. The expert pier jump scored two stars, pause let the pose clock move on the frame the button went down, two songs had uneven pattern lengths, a tray board lookup named a variable that was not in scope, a few model parts floated, the seagull was spoken as the scale, a dev-tool page could not go back, the prompt could draw past a short screen, the scale's voice measured just under the loudness line, the About screen kept only the first six lines so later source fields never appeared, the menu cursor was a greater-than sign the font cannot draw, so it showed as a question mark, reps listened only to a downward lean so a sideways lunge and an upward press did nothing, and an activity kept the title camera, never played its pose, and labelled the screen activity.\n2. Three were game-breaking. The pier jump sat under the three-star line until takeoff recentred the dot, the pose kept playing for one frame after pause, and a lunge or a press did not move when the stick did. The others failed a data check, a voice check, a menu, or the picture of the exercise, and they were fixed before the hand-in.\n3. The most helpful test was driving a rep with the input the stick and the keys actually produce. The idle-versus-expert bots wrote the depth themselves, so they still scored while a sideways lunge stayed at zero. That same bot pass is what caught the pier jump.\n4. The least helpful test was the glyph scan. Every line already used the allowed characters, so it passed on the first run and did not change the game.\n\n**Engine Feedback**\n\n1. Headless stepping, the pixel HUD, and a real input recorder made a week of play testable without a screen.\n2. I guessed wrong about pause. At timeScale 0 the headless stepper still calls fixedUpdate, and that call happens before update reads the pause key, so the pose clock moved unless the sim refused the step. Menu presses do still arrive. The type note reads as if those presses are dropped. Capture also needs all five Vulkan flags or the picture comes back blank.\n3. The centre-of-balance itself. The engine will move a character. It will not sway a polite dot, keep a week, or speak in formants.\n4. The hardest part was trusting the frame clock. Game time, the press window, and the hub clock are three different clocks, and only one of them is allowed to move a score.\n5. None. pixel-engine.js is the kit file, byte for byte.\n6. I would give the music bus a default of silence until the game sets it, so a shared browser profile cannot leave yesterday volume on today game.\n\n**Prompt Feedback**\n\n1. The plan named the mechanics, the sentences, and the tests, so the work was building a game rather than inventing one.\n2. The cut list in the plan and the instruction to finish everything on this computer disagree. I followed the instruction and shipped the activities the cut list would drop.\n3. The hardest piece was the pier jump star line. The same bot that holds a pose will dive off a dock, and the flight begins wherever the dot was left.\n4. I would ask for the pause rule in one sentence: timeScale 0, fixedUpdate silent, update still reads keys. The guide and the type comment do not say the same thing.\n\nKit credits: Kenney (CC0), three.js (MIT), Rapier (Apache-2.0), Sweetie 16."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":876,"output_tokens":1911,"cache_read_input_tokens":68864,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"cf14201b-e30b-404d-887e-cc3f22e44024"}
