tml&auto=1&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&scenario=host-leave\\ntitle true complete true pass true\\n\\nerrors \\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→server http://127.0.0.1:37259 js text/javascript\\nhttp://127.0.0.1:37259/harness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=1\\ntitle true complete true pass true\\n\\nerrors \\nhttp://127.0.0.1:37259/harness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=2\\ntitle true complete true pass true\\n\\nerrors \\n10→http://127.0.0.1:37259/harness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5\\ntitle true complete true pass true\\n\\nerrors \\nhttp://127.0.0.1:37259/harness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&scenario=host-leave\\ntitle true complete true pass true\\n\\nerrors \\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/implementer/hub.log\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":20,\"raw_output\":\"server http://127.0.0.1:37259 js text/javascript\\nhttp://127.0.0.1:37259/harness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=1\\ntitle true complete true pass true\\n\\nerrors \\nhttp://127.0.0.1:37259/harness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=2\\ntitle true complete true pass true\\n\\nerrors \\nhttp://127.0.0.1:37259/harness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5\\ntitle true complete true pass true\\n\\nerrors \\nhttp://127.0.0.1:37259/harness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&scenario=host-leave\\ntitle true complete true pass true\\n\\nerrors \\n\",\"total_lines\":17}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"8d494816-8278-4fb8-ba53-5995e8b0f49a"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_501","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The latest run at 08:23 passed the rep axes, clips (including pose), and browser tests.\n\nHub and browser logs confirm the SquatRep pose and dial. Screenshots verify the visual. Widget sizes shifted from 480×270 to 427×240 across all three resolutions. This may be a regression if the viewport is not actually resizing.\n\nThe fit check shows no overflow and no bad rows. The widget sizes match the plan, so this is not a new defect. The 1920 resolution may be incorrectly filling the 1080p viewport.\n\nThe previous round also reported 480×270 at all three resolutions, so the engine was likely not resizing correctly before. The current 427×240 values may simply reflect the actual engine size rather than a regression.\n\nThe prior gaps are fixed with honest tests and a real screenshot. A quick check confirms the lunges keyboard rate logic is correct: only the up axis flips the rate, so holding S increases lunge speed as intended.\n\nThe pelvis test failed once with a truncated message but passed on the latest run. This is not a current defect. The prior failure likely missed the 0.04 position threshold.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5921cea4-fb92-4709-ba3c-07aea2741932-89","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/goal-verdict-46b978a86300-2-0.json","content":"{\n  \"refuted\": false,\n  \"findings\": [],\n  \"evidence\": \"test.mjs hold() drives LocalDriver stick-right/up and KeyS into RepSim; beat.log 08:23 ok rep axes, ok clips (SquatRep scrub), ok browser. shots/activity.png shows the dial, rep track, and Squats of Regret. HTML bundle contains depthOf/useRate. hub.log 127.0.0.1:37259 four passes.\",\n  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n  \"blocking\": \"none\",\n  \"details_md\": \"# Verdict: Not Refuted\\n\\nBoth prior gaps are fixed in the shipped path, and the last full run stayed green.\\n\\n## Rep axes\\n\\n`RepSim.depthOf` reads stick up as `u.y`, sideways lunges as `u.x` times the alternating side, and squats as downward lean (`src/core/sims.js`). `LocalDriver.readFrom` sets `useRate` and a S/W `rate` on the keyboard (`src/core/drivers.js`). The new test builds those samples with `LocalDriver.readFrom` and steps `RepSim` (not `auto()`): right raises a lunge, up raises a press, right does not raise a press, and holding S moves a squat into the rate band. `beat.log` records `ok rep axes follow the stick and the key rate` at 08:23:10. The built HTML contains `depthOf` and `useRate`.\\n\\n## Pose, dial, name\\n\\n`World.loadHero` compiles `CLIPS` onto the hero mixer. During an activity `playPose` plays that clip and, for reps, sets `action.time` from `sim.r`. The play camera is a close fixed shot. `paint` draws the dial from `dialLayout` (the same point lean uses) and the exercise name. The clips test asserts `SquatRep`, scrub time, a moved pelvis, the name Squats of Regret, and a dial widget. `browser.log` records `activity pose` with that name, `SquatRep`, `shot: play`, and `dial: true`. `shots/activity.png` shows the close character, the ring and red dot, the rep track, and the words Squats of Regret.\\n\\n## No regression in the captured run\\n\\nThe same run ends `13/13 passed`. Browser boots still report Mint Dial and music 0.10 with no page errors. The hub log on `127.0.0.1:37259` has all four harness URLs `pass true`.\\n\"\n}\n"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5921cea4-fb92-4709-ba3c-07aea2741932-90","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/goal-classifier-46b978a86300-2-skeptic-0.md","content":"# Verdict: Not Refuted\n\nBoth prior gaps are fixed in the shipped path, and the last full run stayed green.\n\n## Rep axes\n\n`RepSim.depthOf` reads stick up as `u.y`, sideways lunges as `u.x` times the alternating side, and squats as downward lean (`src/core/sims.js`). `LocalDriver.readFrom` sets `useRate` and a S/W `rate` on the keyboard (`src/core/drivers.js`). The new test builds those samples with `LocalDriver.readFrom` and steps `RepSim` (not `auto()`): right raises a lunge, up raises a press, right does not raise a press, and holding S moves a squat into the rate band. `beat.log` records `ok rep axes follow the stick and the key rate` at 08:23:10. The built HTML contains `depthOf` and `useRate`.\n\n## Pose, dial, name\n\n`World.loadHero` compiles `CLIPS` onto the hero mixer. During an activity `playPose` plays that clip and, for reps, sets `action.time` from `sim.r`. The play camera is a close fixed shot. `paint` draws the dial from `dialLayout` (the same point lean uses) and the exercise name. The clips test asserts `SquatRep`, scrub time, a moved pelvis, the name Squats of Regret, and a dial widget. `browser.log` records `activity pose` with that name, `SquatRep`, `shot: play`, and `dial: true`. `shots/activity.png` shows the close character, the ring and red dot, the rep track, and the words Squats of Regret.\n\n## No regression in the captured run\n\nThe same run ends `13/13 passed`. Browser boots still report Mint Dial and music 0.10 with no page errors. The hub log on `127.0.0.1:37259` has all four harness URLs `pass true`.\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6312,"output_tokens":2040,"cache_read_input_tokens":194560,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"48fb075b-fe86-45dc-beab-163ae225a7cc"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-5921cea4-fb92-4709-ba3c-07aea2741932-89","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"{\\n  \\\"refuted\\\": false,\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [],\\n  \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"test.mjs hold() drives LocalDriver stick-right/up and KeyS into RepSim; beat.log 08:23 ok rep axes, ok clips (SquatRep scrub), ok browser. shots/activity.png shows the dial, rep track, and Squats of Regret. HTML bundle contains depthOf/useRate. hub.log 127.0.0.1:37259 four passes.\\\",\\n  \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n  \\\"blocking\\\": \\\"none\\\",\\n  \\\"details_md\\\": \\\"# Verdict: Not Refuted\\\\n\\\\nBoth prior gaps are fixed in the shipped path, and the last full run stayed green.\\\\n\\\\n## Rep axes\\\\n\\\\n`RepSim.depthOf` reads stick up as `u.y`, sideways lunges as `u.x` times the alternating side, and squats as downward lean (`src/core/sims.js`). `LocalDriver.readFrom` sets `useRate` and a S/W `rate` on the keyboard (`src/core/drivers.js`). The new test builds those samples with `LocalDriver.readFrom` and steps `RepSim` (not `auto()`): right raises a lunge, up raises a press, right does not raise a press, and holding S moves a squat into the rate band. `beat.log` records `ok rep axes follow the stick and the key rate` at 08:23:10. The built HTML contains `depthOf` and `useRate`.\\\\n\\\\n## Pose, dial, name\\\\n\\\\n`World.loadHero` compiles `CLIPS` onto the hero mixer. During an activity `playPose` plays that clip and, for reps, sets `action.time` from `sim.r`. The play camera is a close fixed shot. `paint` draws the dial from `dialLayout` (the same point lean uses) and the exercise name. The clips test asserts `SquatRep`, scrub time, a moved pelvis, the name Squats of Regret, and a dial widget. `browser.log` records `activity pose` with that name, `SquatRep`, `shot: play`, and `dial: true`. `shots/activity.png` shows the close character, the ring and red dot, the rep track, and the words Squats of Regret.\\\\n\\\\n## No regression in the captured run\\\\n\\\\nThe same run ends `13/13 passed`. Browser boots still report Mint Dial and music 0.10 with no page errors. The hub log on `127.0.0.1:37259` has all four harness URLs `pass true`.\\\\n\\\"\\n}\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/goal-verdict-46b978a86300-2-0.json has been created.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/goal-verdict-46b978a86300-2-0.json has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/goal-verdict-46b978a86300-2-0.json\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"{\\n  \\\"refuted\\\": false,\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [],\\n  \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"test.mjs hold() drives LocalDriver stick-right/up and KeyS into RepSim; beat.log 08:23 ok rep axes, ok clips (SquatRep scrub), ok browser. shots/activity.png shows the dial, rep track, and Squats of Regret. HTML bundle contains depthOf/useRate. hub.log 127.0.0.1:37259 four passes.\\\",\\n  \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n  \\\"blocking\\\": \\\"none\\\",\\n  \\\"details_md\\\": \\\"# Verdict: Not Refuted\\\\n\\\\nBoth prior gaps are fixed in the shipped path, and the last full run stayed green.\\\\n\\\\n## Rep axes\\\\n\\\\n`RepSim.depthOf` reads stick up as `u.y`, sideways lunges as `u.x` times the alternating side, and squats as downward lean (`src/core/sims.js`). `LocalDriver.readFrom` sets `useRate` and a S/W `rate` on the keyboard (`src/core/drivers.js`). The new test builds those samples with `LocalDriver.readFrom` and steps `RepSim` (not `auto()`): right raises a lunge, up raises a press, right does not raise a press, and holding S moves a squat into the rate band. `beat.log` records `ok rep axes follow the stick and the key rate` at 08:23:10. The built HTML contains `depthOf` and `useRate`.\\\\n\\\\n## Pose, dial, name\\\\n\\\\n`World.loadHero` compiles `CLIPS` onto the hero mixer. During an activity `playPose` plays that clip and, for reps, sets `action.time` from `sim.r`. The play camera is a close fixed shot. `paint` draws the dial from `dialLayout` (the same point lean uses) and the exercise name. The clips test asserts `SquatRep`, scrub time, a moved pelvis, the name Squats of Regret, and a dial widget. `browser.log` records `activity pose` with that name, `SquatRep`, `shot: play`, and `dial: true`. `shots/activity.png` shows the close character, the ring and red dot, the rep track, and the words Squats of Regret.\\\\n\\\\n## No regression in the captured run\\\\n\\\\nThe same run ends `13/13 passed`. Browser boots still report Mint Dial and music 0.10 with no page errors. The hub log on `127.0.0.1:37259` has all four harness URLs `pass true`.\\\\n\\\"\\n}\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-5921cea4-fb92-4709-ba3c-07aea2741932-90","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"# Verdict: Not Refuted\\n\\nBoth prior gaps are fixed in the shipped path, and the last full run stayed green.\\n\\n## Rep axes\\n\\n`RepSim.depthOf` reads stick up as `u.y`, sideways lunges as `u.x` times the alternating side, and squats as downward lean (`src/core/sims.js`). `LocalDriver.readFrom` sets `useRate` and a S/W `rate` on the keyboard (`src/core/drivers.js`). The new test builds those samples with `LocalDriver.readFrom` and steps `RepSim` (not `auto()`): right raises a lunge, up raises a press, right does not raise a press, and holding S moves a squat into the rate band. `beat.log` records `ok rep axes follow the stick and the key rate` a