with `LocalDriver.readFrom` and steps `RepSim` (not `auto()`): right raises a lunge, up raises a press, right does not raise a press, and holding S moves a squat into the rate band. `beat.log` records `ok rep axes follow the stick and the key rate` at 08:23:10. The built HTML contains `depthOf` and `useRate`.\\n\\n## Pose, dial, name\\n\\n`World.loadHero` compiles `CLIPS` onto the hero mixer. During an activity `playPose` plays that clip and, for reps, sets `action.time` from `sim.r`. The play camera is a close fixed shot. `paint` draws the dial from `dialLayout` (the same point lean uses) and the exercise name. The clips test asserts `SquatRep`, scrub time, a moved pelvis, the name Squats of Regret, and a dial widget. `browser.log` records `activity pose` with that name, `SquatRep`, `shot: play`, and `dial: true`. `shots/activity.png` shows the close character, the ring and red dot, the rep track, and the words Squats of Regret.\\n\\n## No regression in the captured run\\n\\nThe same run ends `13/13 passed`. Browser boots still report Mint Dial and music 0.10 with no page errors. The hub log on `127.0.0.1:37259` has all four harness URLs `pass true`.\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"b00a8849-3b94-4ff1-bde7-aa5b943eaeab"}
