{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_509","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Reviewing prior gaps.Checking if the rep tracking is correct for LocalDriver-shaped input.\n\nLocalDriver was missing keyboard rate control. Reps only followed depth and never used rate. The fix adds useRate and rate to LocalDriver and updates\n\nTracing the physics: RepSim.depthOf to handle LocalDriver maps stick up, side, and down  directions to depthaxes. Need to verify and rate flags, while this logic and check if tests cover LocalDriver-shaped RepSim integrates those input. Also hunting inputs into rotation a potential bug with speed. keyboard rate on the up axis.\n\nThe keyboard rate logic is correct. LocalDriver maps S to +1 and W to -1, so holding S increases r for downward exercises and upward presses invert the rate to increase r.\n\nThe non-rate path integrates depth directly into rotation. The prior bug was that reps only followed depth, while LocalDriver never set useRate.\n\nThe side-axis depth logic is correct. Stick-right lunges alternate sides properly: even reps yield 1, odd reps yield 0.\n\nStick-right lunges and stick-up presses now correctly drive rotation toward 1. Keyboard rate control is restored for squat. Verifying the keyed squat math.\n\nThe prior gap only required r to track the axis, not to alternate sides. Stick-right lunges returning 0 on odd reps may be a bug. Stick-up presses should correctly use u.y.\n\nThe keyed squat math checks out: at tempo 3.2, rotation gains roughly 0.39 over half a second, landing between\n\nKeyboard rate integration the test bounds.\n\nFatigue adds a sine-wave oscillation is a concern. Holding to rotation based on S drives r to 1 and the repFatigue tunable. keeps it there, while\n\nOne potential issue: the target drops. This keyboard devices may would score poorly. report useRate as true even when no keys are The prior gap asked pressed, which would for keyboard rate control still apply rate integration to be functional. with a zero value.\n\nKeyboard input is now fully rate-driven. LocalDriver sets useRate to true for WASD, so holding D or A leaves rate at zero and rotation stays at zero. The prior test used a pad\n\nKeyboard rate integration device for stick input, is correct. Holding which explains why  S drives r to 1 at the bug went unnoticed.the target slope during the down phase. This matches the repTarget curve exactly. The prior concern about poor scoring was unfounded.\n\nChecking PLAN.md to confirm whether keyboard input should control lunges via stick axes or only via S/W rate. Also investigating a potential bug in the side axis logic.\n\nThe keyboard up rate is slightly slower than the target's return slope, but this should still score fine and is not a prior gap issue. Fatigue jitter is harmless when repFatigue defaults to zero. Side-axis fallback to depth for near-zero x inputs is acceptable.\n\nThe side axis logic intentionally flips direction each rep. Holding stick right on the first rep drives","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3878,"output_tokens":1452,"cache_read_input_tokens":40448,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"f9fb2b9b-a8d8-4365-a96a-0d2a1c28d931"}
