{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_514","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I am examining the activity screenshot.\n\nThe prior gap explicitly identified stick-right lunges leaving r at zero as the bug. The fix tracks the axis so that stick-right raises r on even-numbered reps. Since rep 0 is even, holding stick-right for 0.5 seconds from the start correctly raises r. The test tempo of 1.6 seconds means this half-second hold still falls within rep 0, so the test passes.\n\nExpert bots use auto() to set depth and movement vectors directly, so they never rely on useRate. For lunges, auto sets x to side times depth, and depthOf computes depth from that x value. For presses, auto sets y to depth, which depthOf returns directly. For squats, auto sets y to negative depth while keeping depth, and depthOf \n\nThe activity showsuses the maximum of  a balance dial withdepth and negative y. a yellow inner ring and red dot, a vertical rep track, and the name \"Squats of Regret.\" The character appears to be in a squatting pose with arms at sides. The lag path is therefore not skipped for expert bots.\n\nI should verify whether the activity screenshot was recaptured this round and inspect the test.log for 13/13 results. The painted dial must match the driver's dialLayout coordinates: x=240, y=56, radius=44.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e0bbc881-36b7-4304-a6e6-adc969ad1a88-12","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function paint|id: 'dial'|activityName|dialLayout|widgets\\.push|head","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src","glob":"**/*.{js,mjs}"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e0bbc881-36b7-4304-a6e6-adc969ad1a88-13","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"axis:","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src