tent\":\"## Acceptance criteria\"},{\"line_number\":10,\"content\":\"4. **10-foot controls, dev mode, attract, audio.** One pixel HUD serves pad, keyboard, and mouse (no DOM menus, no dense data screens). Prompts follow the last device: PlayStation glyphs by default, an Xbox glyph option, keycaps, and mouse buttons. Pause sets `timeScale` to 0 (simulation frozen, menus still read input) and opens Dev Tools with live sliders for the PLAN.md §10 balance, breath/reps, rhythm, games, and economy variables, plus reset-tab and reset-all. After 10 s with no input on the title or any menu, a looping attract demo plays real scenes of every activity family (cheats allowed) until any input returns to the title; it does not start during play, pause, or a hub session. Touch-only devices get no touch controls, the text “Controller or keyboard required”, a settings button, and a running attract loop. All music, SFX, and voices are code (no audio files). Voices are Animalese/Simlish gibberish: the same word always yields the same syllables, a “?” rises in pitch, and an [... truncated (1031 chars total)]\"},{\"line_number\":14,\"content\":\"1. **gating:** Add or update real tests that drive the shipped Dot, scoring, Wobble Age, save, voice syllabifier, activity scenes, and menu flow from their real start states (no mocked unit under test, no re-implementation, no hardcoded title). Run `node tools/test.mjs` from the dev folder after the code it covers is in place. Capture stdout/stderr to `{SCRATCH}/test.log`. Pass only if the log ends in a one-line all-passed count, prints no failures, and the assertions cover: Dot bands and 45/70/90 stars; every activity idle 0★ vs expert ≥2★ and correct Drips; a scripted fresh-save week through Day 7, confession −7, and Week 2; save reload, corrupt JSON, and missing storage; pause freeze and resume; every dev slider live plus both resets; attract at 10 s on title and on a menu, no trigger in play, any input exits; medley windows and a ghost lane that does not simulate; stable syllabify and a rising question; `pixel-engine.js` hash equals the kit zip.\"},{\"line_number\":15,\"content\":\"2. **gating:** Launch the root HTML twice from `file://` with Playwright Chromium and all five flags `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader`. Each run must have zero page errors, a title-screen state that names `{Title}`, and music volume exactly 0.10. Step the engine, composite `renderer.capture()` with the HUD, and save PNGs under `{SCRATCH}/boot-1.png` and `{SCRATCH}/boot-2.png`. The drawing buffer must match the fill-aspect target size and be substantially painted (not a few pixels). A driven confirm or pointer hover must change a recorded UI state (focus or leaving the title prompt). Both runs must agree. If capture throws for an environmental reason, save that log to `{SCRATCH}/capture-error.txt` and pass on the state assertions only. A capture that succeeds and is blank or nearly blank is a failure, not a fallback.\"},{\"line_number\":16,\"content\":\"3. **gating:** In the same browser suite (included in `node tools/test.mjs`, not a separate unchecked script), on the built HTML: a gamepad stub confirms with Cross and records PlayStation prompts, the Xbox setting switches glyphs, a key switches to keycaps, a mouse move switches to mouse prompts, hover moves focus, and click activates — all readable from game state. A phone profile shows the controller-required message, a settings control, no touch gameplay, and attract running. Two stub pads plus keyboard move three Family Hour lanes independently. After a click, an AnalyserNode reads non-silent music and SFX; an OfflineAudioContext voice render has RMS > 0.02 and Ounce’s mean pitch above Coach’s. Widget rects fit at 1920×1080, 1280×720, and 640×360. WebKit (iPhone profile) and Firefox show the WebGPU-unavailable message and no page error. Write the run log to `{SCRATCH}/browser.log`.\"},{\"line_number\":17,\"content\":\"4. **gating:** Serve the built game with the hub harness on `127.0.0.1` and an OS-picked port (stop that PID only). Confirm the document title is this game, then run the four harness URLs in criterion 5. Capture results to `{SCRATCH}/hub.log`. Pass only if each reaches `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'` and `window.__hubCheck.pass` is true. Then load the game with no session and confirm the normal title still boots (`{SCRATCH}/nosession.log`).\"},{\"line_number\":34,\"content\":\"- Wii Fit’s defining mechanics (public guides): a centre-of-balance dot kept in a zone; a daily body test that yields one age-like number; yoga holds, strength reps, aerobics, and balance games; a demonstrating trainer; banked time that unlocks activities; star ratings; several players on one console. PLAN.md already remaps these. That remap is the contract, not Nintendo’s names or BMI copy.\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-82d85359-afa4-431b-8193-79f15ce5c4de-21","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→13/13 passed\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→13/13 passed\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/implementer/test.log\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"13/13 passed\\n\",\"total_lines\":1}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-82d85359-afa4-431b-8193-79f15ce5c4de-22","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→boot 1 {\\\"title\\\":\\\"Mint Dial\\\",\\\"stateTitle\\\":\\\"Mint Dial\\\",\\\"mode\\\":\\\"title\\\",\\\"music\\\":0.1,\\\"bus\\\":0.1}\\nboot 1 shot 1281x720 span 188.8 title start\\nboot 2 {\\\"title\\\":\\\"Mint Dial\\\",\\\"stateTitle\\\":\\\"Mint Dial\\\",\\\"mode\\\":\\\"title\\\",\\\"music\\\":0.1,\\\"bus\\\":0.1}\\nboot 2 shot 1281x720 span 188.8 title start\\ndrive {\\\"cross\\\":\\\"Cross Confirm\\\",\\\"xbox\\\":\\