{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_523","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"\n\nThe close-up image likely hides the legs, so a deep squat can still appear upright with arms at the sides. The squat animation actually places arms forward-down, not at the sides. At partial depth the arm pose interpolates between these endpoints. The one-second play call with tempo 3.2 yieldsEvidence is newer than a step size of roughly 0.31. the source.\n\nChecking hub.log and\n\nThe one-second play a possible rep-side-alternation call with tempo 3.2 should reach roughly bug. A quick node script will verify the rate 80–100% depth, placing arms forward. If the screenshot still shows math. The depthOf logic arms at the sides,  for side lunges is the browser capture likely fails to applycorrect. the pose visually even though the headless test confirms the pelvis moved.\n\nI will inspect the browser.mjs capture code and read the image file directly, since the description may be an imperfect model caption. I also need to check if the character\n\nKeyboard useRate inverts on press, but LocalDriver rate uses keys rather than stick. Pad testing animator's pose mixer is overriding the activity pose on the rendered mesh. avoids this mismatch. The side depthOf clamp is sound. Stick magnitude stays clamped to 1.\n\nChecking whether the HTML bundle includes the new depthOf and\n\nThe headless test  useRate code. The browser test succeeded, so reads pelvis positionthe bundle was rebuilt. immediately after step(), Bundle timestamps are before any separate being compared against source files to confirm render pass. This means freshness. A stale  the browser capture path is the only place where a post-update render could reset the pose bones to idle and hide the squat.bundle would cause the browser test to fail.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6923d22b-da01-4f2d-9d0e-adf19fc07bbd-24","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/tools/browser.mjs","offset":440,"limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6923d22b-da01-4f2d-9d0e-adf19fc07bbd-25","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"updateVisual|mixer\\.update|clipAction","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/pixel-engine.js","head_limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6923d22b-da01-4f2d-9d0e-adf19fc07bbd-26","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/implementer/clips.txt","limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2909,"output_tokens":2664,"cache_read_input_tokens":65024,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"cb99358e-ca62-4366-889e-bd02da917e89"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-6923d22b-da01-4f2d-9d0e-adf19fc07bbd-24","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"440→    };\\n    const choose = (id) => {\\n      let guard = 0;\\n      while (app.state().row !== id && guard++ < 12) tap('ArrowDown');\\n      tap('Enter');\\n    };\\n    if (app.mode !== 'title') {\\n      app.go('title');\\n      engine.step(1);\\n    }\\n450→    if (app.mode === 'title') choose('start');\\n    choose('family');\\n    pads[0] = make(0.85, true);\\n    engine.step(1);\\n    pads[1] = make(-0.85, true);\\n    engine.step(1);\\n    tap('Enter');\\n    choose('start');\\n    engine.input.setKey('ArrowRight', true);\\n    engine.step(90);\\n460→    engine.input.setKey('ArrowRight', false);\\n    engine.step(1);\\n    return { mode: app.mode, pos: app.lanes.map((lane) => lane.pos), seats: app.state().seats };\\n  });\\n  log(browserLog, `family ${JSON.stringify(lanes)}`);\\n  if (lanes.mode !== 'medley' || lanes.pos.length < 3) bad(`family lanes ${JSON.stringify(lanes)}`);\\n  if (new Set(lanes.pos.map((n) => Number(n).toFixed(3))).size < 3) bad(`family positions ${lanes.pos.join(',')}`);\\n  if (errors.length) bad(`widget page errors ${errors.join(' | ')}`);\\n  await page.close();\\n}\\n470→\\nasync function shots(browser, fileUrl, scratch, browserLog) {\\n  const page = await browser.newPage({ viewport: { width: 1920, height: 1080 } });\\n  await page.goto(fileUrl);\\n  await waitGame(page);\\n  const dir = path.join(scratch, 'shots');\\n  const title = await grab(page);\\n  if (title.url) writePng(path.join(dir, 'title.png'), title.url);\\n  await page.evaluate(() => {\\n    const app = window.__GAME__;\\n480→    const engine = window.__PIXEL_ENGINE__;\\n    app.setDriver('expert');\\n    app.go('activity', 'squat');\\n    engine.step(50);\\n  });\\n  const activity = await grab(page);\\n  if (activity.url) writePng(path.join(dir, 'activity.png'), activity.url);\\n  const pose = await page.evaluate(() => {\\n    const app = window.__GAME__;\\n    const world = window.__PIXEL_ENGINE__.game;\\n490→    const state = app.state();\\n    return {\\n      mode: state.mode,\\n      name: state.activityName,\\n      pose: world?.poseName || '',\\n      time: world?.poseTime || 0,\\n      shot: world?.shot || '',\\n      dial: state.widgets.some((w) => w.id === 'dial'),\\n      head: state.widgets.some((w) => w.id === 'head'),\\n    };\\n500→  });\\n  log(browserLog, `activity pose ${JSON.stringify(pose)}`);\\n  if (pose.name !== 'Squats of Regret') bad(`activity name ${pose.name}`);\\n  if (pose.pose !== 'SquatRep' || pose.time <= 0.05) bad(`activity clip ${pose.pose} ${pose.time}`);\\n  if (!pose.dial || !pose.head) bad(`activity hud dial ${pose.dial} head ${pose.head}`);\\n  if (pose.shot !== 'play') bad(`activity camera ${pose.shot}`);\\n  await page.evaluate(() => {\\n    const app = window.__GAME__;\\n    window.__PIXEL_ENGINE__.step(1);\\n    app.go('island');\\n510→    window.__PIXEL_ENGINE__.step(2);\\n  });\\n  const island = await grab(page);\\n  if (island.url) writePng(path.join(dir, 'island.png'), island.url);\\n  await page.evaluate(() => {\\n    const app = window.__GAME__;\\n    const engine = window.__PIXEL_ENGINE__;\\n    app.setDriver('expert');\\n    app.go('activity', 'hoop');\\n    engine.step(5);\\n520→    engine.input.setKey('KeyP', true);\\n    engine.step(1);\\n    engine.input.setKey('KeyP', false);\\n    engine.step(1);\\n    const tap = (code) => {\\n      engine.input.setKey(code, true);\\n      engine.step(1);\\n      engine.input.setKey(code, false);\\n      engine.step(1);\\n    };\\n530→    let guard = 0;\\n    while (app.state().row !== 'dev' && guard++ < 10) tap('ArrowDown');\\n    tap('Enter');\\n  });\\n  const dev = await grab(page);\\n  if (dev.url) writePng(path.join(dir, 'pause.png'), dev.url);\\n  log(browserLog, `shots title ${title.mode} activity ${activity.mode} island ${island.mode} dev ${dev.mode}`);\\n  await page.close();\\n}\\n\\n540→async function missingGpu(launcher, name, fileUrl, problems, browserLog) {\\n  let browser;\\n  try {\\n    browser = await launcher.launch({ headless: true });\\n    const errors = [];\\n    const page = await browser.newPage({ viewport: { width: 390, height: 844 } });\\n    page.on('pageerror', (err) => errors.push(String(err)));\\n    await page.goto(fileUrl);\\n    await page.waitForTimeout(2500);\\n    const text = await page.evaluate(() => document.body ? document.body.innerText : '');\\n550→    log(browserLog, `${name} ${text.slice(0, 240)} pageerrors ${errors.join(' | ')}`);\\n    if (!text.includes('Failed to start: WebGPU unavailable')) problems.push(`${name} missing WebGPU message`);\\n    if (errors.length) problems.push(`${name} pageerror ${errors.join(' | ')}`);\\n    await page.close();\\n  } catch (err) {\\n    problems.push(`${name} ${err?.message || err}`);\\n  } finally {\\n    if (browser) await browser.close();\\n  }\\n}\",\"content_concise\":\"440→    };\\n    const choose = (id) => {\\n      let guard = 0;\\n      while (app.state().row !== id && guard++ < 12) tap('ArrowDown');\\n      tap('Enter');\\n    };\\n    if (app.mode !== 'title') {\\n      app.go('title');\\n      engine.step(1);\\n    }\\n450→    if (app.mode === 'title') choose('start');\\n    choose('family');\\n    pads[0] = make(0.85, true);\\n    engine.step(1);\\n    pads[1] = make(-0.85, true);\\n    engine.step(1);\\n    tap('Enter');\\n    choose('start');\\n    engine.input.setKey('ArrowRight', true);\\n    engine.step(90);\\n460→    engine.input.setKey('ArrowRight', false);\\n    engine.step(1);\\n    return { mode: app.mode, pos: app.lanes.map((lane) => lane.pos), seats: app.state().seats };\\n  });\\n  log(browserLog, `family ${JSON.stringify(lanes)}`);\\n  if (lanes.mode !== 'medley' || lanes.pos.length < 3) bad(`family lanes ${JSON.stringify(lanes)}`);\\n  if (new Set(lanes.pos.map((n) => Number(n).toFi