{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_527","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The browser log confirmsThe HTML contains the new code. A grep of the SquatRep pose. bundle.js returned no results.\n\nThe pose time of 0.91 indicates the character should be near the bottom of a deep squat. The vision model instead\n\nThe build directory is gitignored, so grep sees a standing figure. This suggests a visual bug where the mixer time is set but the mesh does not reflect the pose. skipped it. Browser tests passed against the HTML file:// URL.\n\nVision models often I am now inspecting misread pixel art.  the rep step in theThe description likely conflates a low-angle shipped HTML to verify squat with a standing it matches the source pose. The orange shapes and checking a potential at the bottom are probably bug in the side-axis arms held forward, not feet. The 26-degree clamp logic. pitch keeps the torso upright.\n\nThe prior gap described a diorama shot. The new shot is a close-up with the Squats of Regret activity and a dial. This confirms the visual gap is fixed.\n\nThe side-axis logic I will now hunt for a real bug in the rep is consistent between logic that the test might miss. the bot auto and depthOf. The keyboard rate does\n\nThe keyboard rate  not alternate sidesinversion for the 'up' axis was examined.  for lunges; it scrubsS increases squat depth and W decreases it, a single lunge direction matching the coach's by r. The plan mentions target wave. The speed values are close enough mirroring the left-side to the target slope. This is not a real  clip on odd reps, butbug. the code may not implement this yet.\n\nThe overhead press keyboard mapping is correct. W raises the arms and S lowers them.\n\nThe side lunge logic holds S to increase depth regardless of which side the rep targets. The visual clip does not alternate sides between reps. The side flip only affects the input axis for scoring, not the\n\nA code comment at  animation.line 708 documents left-side mirroring. The prior acceptance criteria only required playing the activity clip, so this may be a pre-existing defect rather than a new regression.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7fb180c1-2a61-4218-8493-933ea0a93514-33","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"repTempoScale|repLag|repFatigue","glob":"**/tunables.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7fb180c1-2a61-4218-8493-933ea0a93514-34","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607.html","offset":45720,"limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":549,"output_tokens":1710,"cache_read_input_tokens":85504,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"b49bb002-e5a6-456f-bdf3-a6726d6a7b68"}
