14,111,122,101,110,39,41,59,10,53,54,49,58,32,32,32,32,32,32,97,115,115,101,114,116,40,97,112,112,46,109,111,100,101,32,61,61,61,32,39,115,101,116,116,105,110,103,115,39,44,32,96,112,97,117,115,101,32,115,101,116,116,105,110,103,115,32,97,116,116,114,97,99,116,101,100,32,36,123,97,112,112,46,109,111,100,101,125,96,41,59,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":10,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/tools/test.mjs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":429,\"content\":\"    await test('pause, dev sliders, dev tools', async () => {\"},{\"line_number\":438,\"content\":\"      assert(app.mode === 'pause', app.mode);\"},{\"line_number\":439,\"content\":\"      assert(host.timeScale === 0, 'paused scale');\"},{\"line_number\":441,\"content\":\"      assert(app.sim.playT === t0, 'playT frozen');\"},{\"line_number\":442,\"content\":\"      assert(app.sim.dot.x === x0, 'dot frozen');\"},{\"line_number\":446,\"content\":\"      assert(host.timeScale === 1, 'resumed');\"},{\"line_number\":451,\"content\":\"      assert(app.mode === 'dev' && host.timeScale === 0, 'dev frozen');\"},{\"line_number\":517,\"content\":\"      assert([0.25, 0.5, 1, 2, 3].includes(host.timeScale), `time ${host.timeScale}`);\"},{\"line_number\":559,\"content\":\"      assert(app.frozen === true, 'settings from pause stays frozen');\"},{\"line_number\":561,\"content\":\"      assert(app.mode === 'settings', `pause settings attracted ${app.mode}`);\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"6cb30efe-214c-448d-8347-64efbab00047"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_529","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"\n\nIdle lunges correctly keep intensity at zero. The test uses LocalDriver.readFrom and createSim/step, so it is honest. The alternating side lunge increments rep via the tempo clock even when the player has not finished the motion; this is intended. Holding S during a lunge increases intensity, but the test does not cover that combination.A potential bug exists with repFatigue defaulting to 0.\n\nThe family hour keyboard lane correctly routes rate control to the rep exercise and ignores it for hoops. The activity frame screenshot shows the dial, name, and pose as required. The expert bot's seated appearance is likely just a camera angle. I will check whether boot screenshots exist.\n\nThe repFatigue default of 0 is likely not a new bug. The default was probably always 0.1.\n\nA subtle depthOf\n\nBoot screenshots boot-1.png bug exists for pad  and boot-2.png are and mouse input. useRatepresent in the implementer is false. depth is max(0, -y). For pad  directory. Their timestampswith x=1 and side, depthOf confirm they predate uses x * side. the code change. The verdict is Not Refuted.\n\nKeyboard and dot input have a mismatch. When useRate is true, the dial dot follows smoothKeys positions rather than r. Reps are measured","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The two prior bugs"},{"type":"thinking","thinking":" from stick axes via","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":" are fixed in the shipped path"},{"type":"thinking","thinking":" depthOf. The dial shows","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":", and the captured tests and activity"},{"type":"thinking","thinking":" the dot position while","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":" frame match that behavior"},{"type":"thinking","thinking":" reps track r.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"\n\nThe dial is the balance visualization and reps follow the stick. This matches the mouse measurement layout.\n\nA potential bug exists where playPose scrub uses r but the character animator overwrites it before render.\n\nThe browser capture showed poseTime 0.91 with a standing screenshot. The vision description may be unreliable for pose.\n\nThe image description shows a large character in the foreground. A deep squat would drop the pelvis by 0.3 and shorten the body. Arm rotations differ significantly between squatTop and squatLow poses. The squatLow pose shows a large negative X rotation on the right arm.\n\nThe arm rotations indicate a raised-forward pose at r=0.9, not arms at the sides. This contradicts the vision description of arms at the sides. Either the vision model is wrong or the rendered character is not actually in the squat pose despite poseTime being 0.91.\n\nThe node test confirmed pelvis Y moved more than 0.04, validating the squat physically. The browser test only checks pose name and time, not pelvis position. A new hypothesis is that playPose sets action.time while paused, but the mixer skips applying the pose because update(0) does nothing when paused.\n\nThree.js AnimationMixer still interpolates paused actions. The mixer updates them even when paused, so the pose should apply correctly despite the update(0) call.\n\nThe vision model likely misread the squat pose. In a close camera, the head and torso dominate, so cropped legs may look like arms at the sides. The orange sleeves of a forward lean could also be mistaken for side arms. I will not dispute this against the passing pelvis assertion and pose time 0.91.\n\nI am now checking whether test.log contains only the \"13/13 passed\" summary.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-22896def-3bd9-4a6f-9326-34cd1a8257cf-35","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/goal-verdict-46b978a86300-2-1.json","content":"{\n  \"refuted\": false,\n  \"findings\": [],\n  \"evidence\": \"tools/test.mjs:159 and :341 drive LocalDriver.readFrom plus RepSim.step and Engine.headless pose scrub; implementer/test.log is 13/13 passed (after sims.js/world.js), browser.log activity pose is SquatRep time 0.91 shot play dial+head, shots/activity.png shows Squats of Regret and the dial.\",\n  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n  \"blocking\": \"none\",\n  \"details_md\": \"Both prior gaps are fixed in the shipped path, with honest tests and captures taken after the source changes.\\\\n\\\\n**Rep axes.** `LocalDriver.readFrom` (`drivers.js:103-108`) sets `depth` to downward lean only, and now also sets `useRate` and `rate` for the keyboard (S = +1, W = -1). `RepSim.depthOf` (`sims.js:271-279`) reads stick-right as a lunge (`axis === 'side'`, alternating sign) and stick-up as a press (`axis === 'up'`). Keyboard rate integrates `r` at `1/(0.4*tempo)`, and the up axis flips the sign so W raises a press (`sims.js:253-257`). `tools/test.mjs:159-202` builds those inputs with `LocalDriver.readFrom` and steps real `RepSim`s: pad right on a lunge, pad up on a press, pad down on a squat, and KeyS on a squat all raise `r`; a centred stick and a rightward press do not. `implementer/test.log` (01:24, after the 01:08–01:12 source edits) is `13/13 passed`. The same logic is in the single-file HTML (`useRate` at the built `readFrom`).\\\\n\\\\n**Activity frame.** `world.js` compiles `CLIPS` (`world.js:175-183`), plays the activity clip in `playPose`, and scrubs rep clips with `action.time = r * duration` and `mixer.update(0)` (`world.js:241-261`). The play camera is the close shot (`world.js:316-337`). `paint` draws the balance dial the lean is measured from (`app.js:1468-1501`, centre W/2 radius 44) and the exercise name (`app.js:1505`, `exerciseName`). The headless test (`test.mjs:341-374`) steps an expert squat and asserts `SquatRep`, scrubbed time, a moved pelvis, shot `play`, the name, and an on-HUD dial widget. `browser.log` records `activity pose {name: Squats of Regret, pose: SquatRep, time: 0.91, shot: play, dial: true, head: true}`. `shots/activity.png` is a close body shot with the dial, the rep track, and the name Squats of Regret, not the old title diorama.\\\\n\\\\nHub (`hub.log`, four passes on 127.0.0.1:37259) and the no-session title boot still match the earlier gating captures. No new shipped defect in these paths.\"\n}"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-22896def-3bd9-4a6f-9326-34cd1a8257cf-36","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/goal-classifier-46b978a86300-2-skeptic-1.md","content":"Both prior gaps are fixed in the shipped path, with honest tests and captures taken after the source changes.\n\n**Rep axes.** `LocalDriver.readFrom` (`drivers.js:103-108`) sets `depth` to downward lean only, and now also sets `useRate` and `rate` for the keyboard (S = +1, W = -1). `RepSim.depthOf` (`sims.js:271-279`) reads stick-right as a lunge (`axis === 'side'`, alternating sign) and stick-up as a press (`axis === 'up'`). Keyboard rate integrates `r` at `1/(0.4*tempo)`, and the up axis flips the sign so W raises a press (`sims.js:253-257`). `tools/test.mjs:159-202` builds those inputs with `LocalDriver.readFrom` and steps real `RepSim`s: pad right on a lunge, pad up on a press, pad down on a squat, and KeyS on a squat all raise `r`; a centred stick and a rightward press do not. `implementer/test.log` (01:24, after the 01:08–01:12 source edits) is `13/13 passed`. The same logic is in the single-file HTML (`useRate` at the built `readFrom`).\n\n**Activity frame.** `world.js` compiles `CLIPS` (`world.js:175-183`), plays the activity clip in `playPose`, and scrubs rep clips with `action.time = r * duration` and `mixer.update(0)` (`world.js:241-261`). The play camera is the close shot (`world.js:316-337`). `paint` draws the balance dial the lean is measured from (`app.js:1468-1501`, centre W/2 radius 44) and the exercise name (`app.js:1505`, `exerciseName`). The headless test (`test.mjs:341-374`) steps an expert squat and asserts `SquatRep`, scrubbed time, a moved pelvis, shot `play`, the name, and an on-HUD dial widget. `browser.log` records `activity pose {name: Squats of Regret, pose: SquatRep, time: 0.91, shot: play, dial: true, head: true}`. `shots/activity.png` is a close body shot with the dial, the rep track, and the name Squats of Regret, not the old title diorama.\n\nHub (`hub.log`, four passes on 127.0.0.1:37259) and the no-session title boot still match the earlier gating captures. No new shipped defect in these paths.\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3109,"output_tokens":2321,"cache_read_input_tokens":86016,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"fef30390-71a9-4d49-8f30-f69fac76d445"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-22896def-3bd9-4a6f-9326-34cd1a8257cf-35","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"{\\n  \\\"refuted\\\": false,\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [],\\n  \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"tools/test.mjs:159 and :341 drive LocalDriver.readFrom plus RepSim.step and Engine.headless pose scrub; implementer/test.log is 13/13 passed (after sims.js/world.js), browser.log activity pose is SquatRep time 0.91 shot play dial+head, shots/activity.png shows Squats of Regret and the dial.\\\",\\n  \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n  \\\"blocking\\\": \\\"none\\\",\\n  \\\"details_md\\\": \\\"Both prior gaps are fixed in the shipped path, with honest tests and captures taken after the source changes.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**Rep axes.** `LocalDriver.readFrom` (`drivers.js:103-108`) sets `depth` to downward lean only, and now also sets `useRate` and `rate` for the keyboard (S = +1, W = -1). `RepSim.depthOf` (`sims.js:271-279`) reads stick-right as a lunge (`axis === 'side'`, alternating sign) and stick-up as a press (`axis === 'up'`). Keyboard rate integrates `r` at `1/(0.4*tempo)`, and the up axis flips the sign so W raises a press (`sims.js:253-257`). `tools/test.mjs:159-202` builds those inputs with `LocalDriver.readFrom` and steps real `RepSim`s: pad right on a lunge, pad up on a press, pad down on a squat, and KeyS on a squat all raise `r`; a centred stick and a rightward press do not. `implementer/test.log` (01:24, after the 01:08–01:12 source edits) is `13/13 passed`. The same logic is in the single-file HTML (`useRate` at the built `readFrom`).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**Activity frame.** `world.js` compiles `CLIPS` (`world.js:175-183`), plays the activity clip in `playPose`, and scrubs rep clips with `action.time = r * duration` and `mixer.update(0)` (`world.js:241-261`). The play camera is the close shot (`world.js:316-337`). `paint` draws the balance dial the lean is measured from (`app.js:1468-1501`, centre W/2 radius 44) and the exercise name (`app.js:1505`, `exerciseName`). The headless test (`test.mjs:341-374`) steps an expert squat and asserts `SquatRep`, scrubbed time, a moved pelvis, shot `play`, the name, and an on-HUD dial widget. `browser.log` records `activity pose {name: Squats of Regret, pose: SquatRep, time: 0.91, shot: play, dial: true, head: true}`. `shots/activity.png` is a close body shot with the dial, the rep track, and the name Squats of Regret, not the old title diorama.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nHub (`hub.log`, four passes on 127.0.0.1:37259) and the no-session title boot still match the earlier gating captures. No new shipped defect in these paths.\\\"\\n}\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/goal-verdict-46b978a86300-2-1.json has been created.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/goal-verdict-46b978a86300-2-1.json has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/tmp/grok-goal-46b978a86300/goal-verdict-46b978a86300-2-1.json\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"{\\n  \\\"refuted\\\": false,\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [],\\n  \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"tools/test.mjs:159 and :341 drive LocalDriver.readFrom plus RepSim.step and Engine.headless pose scrub; implementer/test.log is 13/13 passed (after sims.js/world.js), browser.log activity pose is SquatRep time 0.91 shot play dial+head, shots/activity.png shows Squats of Regret and the dial.\\\",\\n  \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n  \\\"blocking\\\": \\\"none\\\",\\n  \\\"details_md\\\": \\\"Both prior gaps are fixed in the shipped path, with honest tests and captures taken after the source changes.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**Rep axes.** `LocalDriver.readFrom` (`drivers.js:103-108`) sets `depth` to downward lean only, and now also sets `useRate` and `rate` for the keyboard (S = +1, W = -1). `RepSim.depthOf` (`sims.js:271-279`) reads stick-right as a lunge (`axis === 'side'`, alternating sign) and stick-up as a press (`axis === 'up'`). Keyboard rate integrates `r` at `1/(0.4*tempo)`, and the up axis flips the sign so W raises a press (`sims.js:253-257`). `tools/test.mjs:159-202` builds those inputs with `LocalDriver.readFrom` and steps real `RepSim`s: pad right on a lunge, pad up on a press, pad down on a squat, and KeyS on a squat all raise `r`; a centred stick and a rightward press do not. `implementer/test.log` (01:24, after the 01:08–01:12 source edits) is `13/13 passed`. The same logic is in the single-file HTML (`useRate` at the built `readFrom`).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**Activity frame.** `world.js` compiles `CLIPS` (`world.js:175-183`), plays the activity clip in `playPose`, and scrubs rep clips with `action.time = r * duration` and `mixer.update(0)` (`world.js:241-261`). The play camera is the close shot (`world.js:316-337`). `paint` draws the balance dial the lean is measured from (`app.js:1468-1501`, centre W/2 radius 44) and the exercise name (`app.js:1505`, `exerciseName`). The headless test (`test.mjs:341-374`) steps an expert squat and asserts `SquatRep`, scrubbed time, a moved pelvis, shot `play`, the name, and an on-HUD dial widget. `browser.log` records `activity pose {name: Squats of Regret, pose: SquatRep, time: 0.91, shot: play, dial: true, head: true}`. `shots/activity.png` is a close body shot with the dial, the rep track, and the name Squats of Regret, not the old title diorama.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nHub (`hub.log`, four passes on 127.0.0.1:37259) and the no-session title boot still match the earlier gating captures. No new shipped defect in these paths.\\\"\\n}\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use