4,32,119,104,101,101,108,44,32,112,97,100,32,98,117,116,116,111,110,32,111,114,32,115,116,105,99,107,44,32,116,111,117,99,104,46,32,89,111,117,32,114,101,116,117,114,110,32,116,111,32,116,104,101,32,116,105,116,108,101,32,97,110,100,32,116,104,101,32,116,105,109,101,114,32,114,101,45,97,114,109,115,46,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":40,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/PLAN.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":23,\"content\":\"1. **You are a dot.** Almost everything is one verb: lean. The left stick, WASD or the mouse moves your centre of balance, and it has weight and sway. Poses, reps, hoops, slacklines and the finale are all different ways of moving or holding the Dot.\"},{\"line_number\":32,\"content\":\"| Your body is the controller; a centre-of-balance dot | The Dot: real sway physics on a stick, keys or mouse |\"},{\"line_number\":35,\"content\":\"| Daily check-in, one number that sums you up, a graph | Weigh-In, Wobble Age, a line chart with a twist |\"},{\"line_number\":38,\"content\":\"| A bright, clean, soft-spoken world | White tile plaza on a pastel island made of giant gym equipment |\"},{\"line_number\":60,\"content\":\"**The story in one breath:** you arrive by ferry; Ounce weighs you and gives you an alarming Wobble Age. Through the week the classmates hint that something is off (\\\"Has anyone ever checked that scale?\\\"; Coach hangs her plumb line beside Ounce: \\\"You are leaning.\\\"; Kevin sits on Ounce and the dial reads 7). On Day 7 you face **The Long Stand**: 90 seconds of standing still while the whole island tries to distract you. Then Ounce confesses: *\\\"I have been adding seven. To everyone. For years. It felt motivating.\\\"* The chart of your week visibly slides down seven years. Credits. *\\\"See you tomorrow. Bring your knees.\\\"* Play continues as an open-ended Week 2.\"},{\"line_number\":98,\"content\":\"| 4 | Stillness | 3 activities | Vitamin Tray, Overhead Mortgage, Tax Season | Coach hangs her plumb line by Ounce. \\\"You are leaning.\\\" \\\"The island is leaning.\\\" |\"},{\"line_number\":115,\"content\":\"Everything hangs on this feeling good, so it comes first. A stick mapped straight to position would be trivial, because you would just hold still. So the Dot is an unstable weight: you apply force, and it drifts, sways and overshoots.\"},{\"line_number\":141,\"content\":\"Top speed is about 0.9 units/s, so a lean feels like shifting a heavy marble. Impulses (a sneeze, a gust) add directly to `vx`/`vy`.\"},{\"line_number\":150,\"content\":\"| Keyboard | WASD / arrows, smoothed (attack 0.10 s, release 0.06 s). **Hold Shift for half lean.** |\"},{\"line_number\":194,\"content\":\"- **Lanes:** Holding Still, Reps, Hoop, Header and Step run in **lane staging**, up to 4 mats in a row, each with its own driver (local, bot or ghost). Solo play puts you on the centre mat with two classmates as bots.\"},{\"line_number\":203,\"content\":\"**Lean body language:** after `mixer.update(dt)`, add the Dot to the pose: `torso.rotateZ(-dot.x * 0.18); torso.rotateX(-dot.y * 0.12); pelvis.position.x += dot.x * 0.05`. Outside the ring, add a tremble. Far outside, blend to the kit's `Teeter` clip. The player should be able to read the Dot from the body alone.\"},{\"line_number\":224,\"content\":\"**You scrub the animation with the stick** ✔ (`action.paused = true; action.time = r * duration; mixer.update(0)`). A marker on a big vertical (or horizontal) track follows the tempo curve; you match it.\"},{\"line_number\":228,\"content\":\"| Squats of Regret | SquatRep | stick down = deeper | 10 | 3.2 s |\"},{\"line_number\":229,\"content\":\"| Apology Lunges | LungeRep, mirrored for left | stick left/right, targets alternate | 10 | 3.2 s |\"},{\"line_number\":230,\"content\":\"| Overhead Mortgage | Press (new) | stick up = press; `repLag` ×1.5 (heavy) | 8 | 3.6 s |\"},{\"line_number\":237,\"content\":\"- **Set dressing:** a gym wall with the engine's `Mirror` showing your reps (attach in `setup`, stop in `dispose`); giant dumbbells.\"},{\"line_number\":241,\"content\":\"**Circle the stick** (or the mouse, or roll W-D-S-A) to keep hoops up.\"},{\"line_number\":244,\"content\":\"- Lift `L`: +.35/s in band, -.25/s out of band, -.5/s wrong way. At 0 the hoop drops, and you pick it up for 1.5 s, with comment.\"},{\"line_number\":246,\"content\":\"- **Thrown hoops:** every ~9 s June winds up on one side, with 1.5 s of telegraph and a landing shadow. Flick `|u.x| > .7` toward that side in the last .4 s to catch it. Up to 4 hoops, each adding +0.5 to the rotation multiplier. Flicking interrupts your circling, which is the trade-off.\"},{\"line_number\":278,\"content\":\"- Sag the line under your feet (segments updated each frame). Arms out: the kit's `Tiptoe` plus T-pose arms set after the mixer, or a tuned `gaitClip`.\"},{\"line_number\":282,\"content\":\"Tilt a lacquered tray to roll coloured vitamins into matching cups. Top-down-ish fixed camera.\"},{\"line_number\":284,\"content\":\"- **Tilt gravity, not the tray ✔:** the colliders stay flat and static; set `ctx.physics.world.gravity`; a visual `Group` tilts, with the vitamins as its children at `body.translation()`.\"},{\"line_number\":286,\"content\":\"- Cups are untagged cylinder triggers ✔ (they see dynamic bodies). 8 vitamins, 2-3 colours, 60 s. +10 correct, -3 wrong; rail gaps in later boards drop a vitamin (-1, respawns after 3 s).\"},{\"line_number\":287,\"content\":\"- Three boards as ASCII in data (`#` wall, `.` floor, `o` start, `R`/`B`/`Y` cups). Stars at 40/60/80% of the board's maximum.\"},{\"line_number\":295,\"content\":\"- Stick X moves you ±1.5 m across the path: collect 18 water cups; dodge sprinklers, picnics, Dennis stretching, and Kevin.\"},{\"line_number\":296,\"content\":\"- Score `70 × pace% + 30 × cups%`. Stars 55/75/90.\"},{\"line_number\":297,\"content\":\"- Run clip: `gaitClip(HERO_RIG, { name: 'Jog', frames: 16, speed: 3, stance: .42, hip: -.04, bob: .03, lift: .1, lean: 6, sway: 2, arms: { swing: 30, elbow: 75 } })` ✔, with `action.timeScale = speed / 3`.\"},{\"line_number\":303,\"content\":\"1. **Run-up (5 s):** hold the Dot in a tuck zone (`y` -.8 to -.4) to build speed 6→14 m/s.\"},{\"line_number\":335,\"content\":\"Your avatar steps onto Ounce (\\\"Ow.\\\" every time; the delivery varies). Close-up, huge dial, tiny animated needle.\"},{\"line_number\":424,\"content\":\"- When you stand up, what sound do you make? *Oof. / Hnng. / I have become the sound.*\"},{\"line_number\":429,\"content\":\"- If your knees could talk, what would they say? *Please. / Why. / Nothing. They've given up.*\"},{\"line_number\":479,\"content\":\"| Lean | Left stick | WASD / arrows; Shift = half | Pointer offset from dial |\"},{\"line_number\":489,\"content\":\"- **Menus** read the d-pad, stick (with repeat), arrows and WASD. Hover moves focus; left click confirms; a wheel scrolls lists; sliders drag.\"},{\"line_number\":490,\"content\":\"- **Keep the mouse native:** the Dot follows the mouse as soon as the mouse moves, and goes back to stick or keys as soon as those are used.\"},{\"line_number\":495,\"content\":\"- Prompts always read `[glyph] verb` and follow the **last device used**. Track it in `src/core/device.js` from `ctx.input`: `held`/`queuedPresses` starting `Pad` or a stick past .3 means pad; `Mouse*` or pointer movement means mouse; anything else means keyboard. Add guarded DOM `keydown`/`pointerdown`/`wheel` listeners for \\\"press any button\\\" and for exiting attract.\"},{\"line_number\":496,\"content\":\"- **Glyph sprites, drawn by you in `src/art/glyphs.js`:** PlayStation shapes ✕ ○ □ △ in their colours, L1 R1 L2 R2, Options, sticks. Xbox A B X Y (a Settings option), LB RB LT RT, Menu. Keycaps with the letter. A mouse with the used button lit.\"},{\"line_number\":503,\"content\":\"- **Name entry:** letter grid (stick, d-pad, click) plus direct typing, 8 characters max.\"},{\"line_number\":507,\"content\":\"`engine.timeScale = 0` ✔ freezes physics, `fixedUpdate` and game time while `update` still runs and `wasPressed` still works. Menus therefore read input in `update`. Don't use `engine.paused` for this.\"},{\"line_number\":513,\"content\":\"Music volume (**default 10%**), SFX, Voice, Button glyphs (PlayStation / Xbox), Gentle Mode (rings ×1.25, noise ×.8), Mouse lean radius, Step timing offset, Reduce flashes, Look (Default, `storybook`, `arcade`, `handheld`), Pixel size (`engine.settings.set({ look, pixelSize })`), Fullscreen, Reset to defaults.\"},{\"line_number\":547,\"content\":\"- **Any input exits**: key, click, mouse move past a few pixels, wheel, pad button or stick, touch. You return to the title and the timer re-arms.\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"0b0a3e62-04fc-4b5a-b6ea-140217e459c3"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_534","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Found a Squats of Regret exercise in PLAN.md at lines 228-230. It is a SquatRep drill with stick-down for deeper squats. The set count is 10 and the rep count is 3.\n\nThe plan also lists Apology Lunges and Overhead Mortgage. The scrubbing logic matches the PLAN.md axes. The LungeRep mirrored-for-left detail may not actually mirror the clip.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-890f5624-6f25-4ac7-b3f2-9687bfb7dd6e-42","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/types/engine/input.d.ts","offset":80,"limit":160}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-890f5624-6f25-4ac7-b3f2-9687bfb7dd6e-43","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/PLAN.md","offset":210,"limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3458,"output_tokens":459,"cache_read_input_tokens":83840,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"01acebc8-9555-4c7b-9900-bb8480f37d09"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-890f5624-6f25-4ac7-b3f2-9687bfb7dd6e-42","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"80→ * its `PointerEvent.buttons` bit, by `PointerEvent.button` (0 left, 1 middle, 2 right).\\n */\\nexport declare const MOUSE_BUTTONS: readonly (readonly [code: string, bit: number])[];\\n/** A finger on the canvas, as a key: held while one is down (not a mouse button, so a tap is not a click). */\\nexport declare const TOUCH_KEY = \\\"Touch\\\";\\n/** A pointer button pressed or let go (`Input.buttonEvents`): its key, and where the pointer was (normalised device coordinates). */\\nexport interface ButtonEvent {\\n    readonly code: string;\\n    readonly down: boolean;\\n    readonly x: number;\\n90→    readonly y: number;\\n}\\n/**\\n * Keyboard + pointer + gamepad input.\\n * - Keys: held state, per-frame presses (`wasPressed`) and queued presses for fixed-step\\n *   code (`consumePress`). Queued presses expire after `pressWindow` s of game time.\\n * - Gamepads (standard mapping): the left stick feeds `moveAxis()` (radial deadzone), the\\n *   right stick feeds the pointer delta (camera look), buttons press key codes\\n *   (`gamepadButtons`). Polled once per frame by the engine (`beginFrame`).\\n * - Pointer: accumulated movement per frame (while a button is held or the pointer is\\n100→ *   locked), wheel delta per frame, optional pointer lock (first-person). Mouse buttons on\\n *   the canvas are keys too (`MOUSE_BUTTONS`: `MouseLeft`, `MouseRight`, `MouseMiddle`), and a\\n *   finger is `Touch` (`TOUCH_KEY`), held and pressed like any other, so a click shorter than\\n *   a frame is not lost.\\n * - Commands (`send`): data from outside the canvas, delivered to the game at the next frame\\n *   and recorded with it.\\n * - `dispose()` removes every listener it added.\\n */\\nexport declare class Input {\\n    private readonly target;\\n110→    private readonly held;\\n    private readonly pressed;\\n    /** Queued presses → the game time they happened at. */\\n    private readonly queued;\\n    /** Keys held through gamepad buttons (merged into isDown). */\\n    private readonly padHeld;\\n    private readonly listeners;\\n    /** Pointer movement this frame, in CSS pixels (drag or pointer lock). */\\n    readonly mouseDelta: {\\n        x: number;\\n120→        y: number;\\n    };\\n    /**\\n     * Where the pointer last was over the canvas, in normalised device coordinates (−1..1, y up:\\n     * `camera.rayAt(pointer.x, pointer.y, …)` turns it into a ray), and whether it is over it now.\\n     * Under pointer lock it is the screen's centre (the crosshair).\\n     */\\n    readonly pointer: {\\n        x: number;\\n        y: number;\\n130→        over: boolean;\\n        touch: boolean;\\n    };\\n    /** Wheel ticks this frame (+1 = scroll down / zoom out). */\\n    wheel: number;\\n    /** This frame's button presses and releases, in order (`buttonEvents`). */\\n    private _buttonEvents;\\n    /** Commands sent since the last frame began, and this frame's (`send`, `commands`). */\\n    private outbox;\\n    private _commands;\\n140→    private lockTarget;\\n    /** When true, clicking the canvas requests pointer lock (first-person / free camera). */\\n    wantsPointerLock: boolean;\\n    /** Touch joystick, -1..1 per axis; overrides keys when active. */\\n    readonly analog: {\\n        x: number;\\n        y: number;\\n    };\\n    /** Gamepad left stick after the deadzone, -1..1 (y = forward). */\\n    readonly padAxis: {\\n150→        x: number;\\n        y: number;\\n    };\\n    /** True while any gamepad is connected. */\\n    gamepadConnected: boolean;\\n    /**\\n     * Extra key codes whose browser default is blocked (arrows and Space always are): a game's\\n     * own F1 / F2 / Tab panels, so the browser's help page or focus change doesn't fire.\\n     */\\n    readonly preventKeys: Set<string>;\\n160→    /** Gamepad button index → key code (defaults: GAMEPAD_BUTTONS). */\\n    gamepadButtons: Record<number, string>;\\n    /** Stick deadzone (radial, 0..1). */\\n    gamepadDeadzone: number;\\n    /** Right stick look speed: pointer pixels per second at full tilt. */\\n    gamepadLookSpeed: number;\\n    /** Game time (s) of the current frame; set by the engine through `beginFrame`. */\\n    now: number;\\n    /**\\n     * True while a replay drives input (`engine.replay()`): keyboard, pointer and wheel events,\\n170→     * `setKey` / `setPointer` / `setButtons` / `addPointer` (touch buttons, scripts) and `send`\\n     * are ignored, and `playBefore` / `playAfter` set everything.\\n     */\\n    get playing(): boolean;\\n    set playing(on: boolean);\\n    private _playing;\\n    private playedPad;\\n    /** Queued presses older than this many seconds of game time are dropped. */\\n    pressWindow: number;\\n    /** `target`: where keys are heard (the page's window); null listens to nothing (`Engine.headless`: input comes from `setKey`, `send`, a replay). */\\n180→    constructor(target?: Window | null);\\n    /**\\n     * Listen for pointer input on the game canvas. Only pointers that went down on the\\n     * canvas drive the camera (so a touch joystick doesn't orbit it). Two canvas touches\\n     * pinch to zoom (emitted as wheel ticks).\\n     */\\n    attachPointer(el: HTMLElement): void;\\n    /** Remove every listener this Input added (window and canvas). */\\n    dispose(): void;\\n    /** Let go of everything held (keys, gamepad buttons, sticks, pointer buttons); queued presses stay. */\\n190→    release(): void;\\n    /** Forget held keys, presses, sticks and pointer movement (e.g. when a level loads). */\\n    reset(): void;\\n    /**\\n     * Engine: begin a frame at game time `now` (seconds). Polls gamepads and drops expired\\n     * queued presses. `pads` defaults to `navigator.getGamepads()`; tests can pass fakes.\\n     */\\n    beginFrame(now: number, dt: number, pads?: readonly (GamepadLike | null)[]): void;\\n    get pointerLocked(): boolean;\\n    isDown(...codes: string[]): boolean;\\n200→    /** `isDown` for a list of codes, without building a rest-argument array (fixed-step code). */\\n    anyDown(codes: readonly string[]): boolean;\\n    /** True once per physical key press (valid for the current render frame). */\\n    wasPressed(...codes: string[]): boolean;\\n    /**\\n     * True once per physical key press, kept until consumed or until it is older than\\n     * `pressWindow` (150 ms of game time). Use from fixed-step code (which may run zero or\\n     * several times per frame) so no press is dropped, while a stale press (made during a\\n     * pause, a loading screen or a long hitch) never fires late.\\n     */\\n210→    consumePress(...codes: string[]): boolean;\\n    /** `consumePress` for a list of codes, without building a rest-argument array. */\\n    consumeAny(codes: readonly string[]): boolean;\\n    /** Held keys, queued presses and the pointer as data (`engine.snapshot()`), between frames. */\\n    state(): InputState;\\n    /** Back to `state()` at game time `now` (a restore): held keys are those the snapshot held, live ones let go. */\\n    setState(s: InputState, now: number): void;\\n    /** Presses waiting to be consumed (tooling / tests). */\\n    get queuedPresses(): string[];\\n    /** Drop queued presses (e.g. when a menu or mode swallows input). */\\n220→    clearQueued(...codes: string[]): void;\\n    /**\\n     * -1..1 on each axis (x = right, y = forward): the touch joystick or a gamepad's left\\n     * stick (whichever is tilted further), else WASD / arrow keys / d-pad.\\n     */\\n    moveAxis(): {\\n        x: number;\\n        y: number;\\n    };\\n    /** Call at the end of each rendered frame. */\\n230→    endFrame(): void;\\n    /** Test hook: simulate a key being held (true) or released (false). */\\n    setKey(code: string, down: boolean): void;\\n    /** Test hook: put the pointer at (x, y) in normalised device coordinates, pressed or not. */\\n    setPointer(x: number, y: number, down?: boolean): void;\\n    /** Test hook: hold mouse buttons (`PointerEvent.buttons` bits: 1 left, 2 right, 4 middle) as the canvas would. */\\n    setButtons(bits: number): void;\\n    /** Buttons held, as `PointerEvent.buttons` bits (1 left, 2 right, 4 middle; a finger is left): the same keys as `isDown('MouseLeft')`. */\\n    get mouseButtons(): number;\\n    /** A pointer button (a key code) goes down (pressed, unless held already) or up, where the pointer is. */\",\"content_concise\":\"80→ * its `PointerEvent.buttons` bit, by `PointerEvent.button` (0 left, 1 middle, 2 right).\\n */\\nexport declare const MOUSE_BUTTONS: readonly (readonly [code: string, bit: number])[];\\n/** A finger on the canvas, as a key: held while one is down (not a mouse button, so a tap is not a click). */\\nexport declare const TOUCH_KEY = \\\"Touch\\\";\\n/** A pointer button pressed or let go (`Input.buttonEvents`): its key, and where the pointer was (normalised device coordinates). */\\nexport interface ButtonEvent {\\n    readonly code: string;\\n    readonly down: boolean;\\n    readonly x: number;\\n90→    readonly y: number;\\n}\\n/**\\n * Keyboard + pointer + gamepad input.\\n * - Keys: held state, per-frame presses (`wasPressed`) and queued presses for fixed-step\\n *   code (`consumePress`). Queued presses expire after `pressWindow` s of game time.\\n * - Gamepads (standard mapping): the left stick feeds `moveAxis()` (radial deadzone), the\\n *   right stick feeds the pointer delta (camera look), buttons press key codes\\n *   (`gamepadButtons`). Polled once per frame by the engine (`beginFrame`).\\n * - Pointer: accumulated movement per frame (while a button is held or the pointer is\\n100→ *   locked), wheel delta per frame, optional pointer lock (first-person). Mouse buttons on\\n *   the canvas are keys too (`MOUSE_BUTTONS`: `MouseLeft`, `MouseRight`, `MouseMiddle`), and a\\n *   finger is `Touch` (`TOUCH_KEY`), held and pressed like any other, so a click shorter than\\n *   a frame is not lost.\\n * - Commands (`send`): data from outside the canvas, delivered to the game at the next frame\\n *   and recorded with it.\\n * - `dispose()` removes every listener it added.\\n */\\nexport declare class Input {\\n    private readonly target;\\n110→    private readonly held;\\n    private readonly pressed;\\n    /** Queued presses → the game time they happened at. */\\n    private readonly queued;\\n    /** Keys held through gamepad buttons (merged into isDown). */\\n    private readonly padHeld;\\n    private readonly listeners;\\n    /** Pointer movement this frame, in CSS pixels (drag or pointer lock). */\\n    readonly mouseDelta: {\\n        x: number;\\n120→        y: number;\\n    };\\n    /**\\n     * Where the pointer last was over the canvas, in normalised device coordinates (−1..1, y up:\\n     * `camera.rayAt(pointer.x, pointer.y, …)` turns it into a ray), and whether it is over it now.\\n     * Under pointer lock it is the screen's centre (the crosshair).\\n     */\\n    readonly pointer: {\\n        x: number;\\n        y: number;\\n130→        over: boolean;\\n        touch: boolean;\\n    };\\n    /** Wheel ticks this frame (+1 = scroll down / zoom out). */\\n    wheel: number;\\n    /** This frame's button presses and releases, in order (`buttonEvents`). */\\n    private _buttonEvents;\\n    /** Commands sent since the last frame began, and this frame's (`send`, `commands`). */\\n    private outbox;\\n    private _commands;\\n140→    private lockTarget;\\n    /** When true, clicking the canvas requests pointer lock (first-person / free camera). */\\n    wantsPointerLock: boolean;\\n    /** Touch joystick, -1..1 per axis; overrides keys when active. */\\n    readonly analog: {\\n        x: number;\\n        y: number;\\n    };\\n    /** Gamepad left stick after the deadzone, -1..1 (y = forward). */\\n    readonly padAxis: {\\n150→        x: number;\\n        y: number;\\n    };\\n    /** True while any gamepad is connected. */\\n    gamepadConnected: boolean;\\n    /**\\n     * Extra key codes whose browser default is blocked (arrows and Space always are): a game's\\n     * own F1 / F2 / Tab panels, so the browser's help page or focus change doesn't fire.\\n     */\\n    readonly preventKeys: Set<string>;\\n160→    /** Gamepad button index → key code (defaults: GAMEPAD_BUTTONS). */\\n    gamepadButtons: Record<number, string>;\\n    /** Stick deadzone (radial, 0..1). */\\n    gamepadDeadzone: number;\\n    /** Right stick look speed: pointer pixels per second at full tilt. */\\n    gamepadLookSpeed: number;\\n    /** Game time (s) of the current frame; set by the engine through `beginFrame`. */\\n    now: number;\\n    /**\\n     * True while a replay drives input (`engine.replay()`): keyboard, pointer and wheel events,\\n170→     * `setKey` / `setPointer` / `setButtons` / `addPointer` (touch buttons, scripts) and `send`\\n     * are ignored, and `playBefore` / `playAfter` set everything.\\n     */\\n    get playing(): boolean;\\n    set playing(on: boolean);\\n    private _playing;\\n    private playedPad;\\n    /** Queued presses older than this many seconds of game time are dropped. */\\n    pressWindow: number;\\n    /** `target`: where keys are heard (the page's window); null listens to nothing (`Engine.headless`: input comes from `setKey`, `send`, a replay). */\\n180→    constructor(target?: Window | null);\\n    /**\\n     * Listen for pointer input on the game canvas. Only pointers that went down on the\\n     * canvas drive the camera (so a touch joystick doesn't orbit it). Two canvas touches\\n     * pinch to zoom (emitted as wheel ticks).\\n     */\\n    attachPointer(el: HTMLElement): void;\\n    /** Remove every listener this Input added (window and canvas). */\\n    dispose(): void;\\n    /** Let go of everything held (keys, gamepad buttons, sticks, pointer buttons); queued presses stay. */\\n190→    release(): void;\\n    /** Forget held keys, presses, sticks and pointer movement (e.g. when a level loads). */\\n    reset(): void;\\n    /**\\n     * Engine: begin a frame at game time `now` (seconds). Polls gamepads and drops expired\\n     * queued presses. `pads` defaults to `navigator.getGamepads()`; tests can pass fakes.\\n     */\\n    beginFrame(now: number, dt: number, pads?: readonly (GamepadLike | null)[]): void;\\n    get pointerLocked(): boolean;\\n    isDown(...codes: string[]): boolean;\\n200→    /** `isDown` for a list of codes, without building a rest-argument array (fixed-step code). */\\n    anyDown(codes: readonly string[]): boolean;\\n    /** True once per physical key press (valid for the current render frame). */\\n    wasPressed(...codes: string[]): boolean;\\n    /**\\n     * True once per physical key press, kept until consumed or until it is older than\\n     * `pressWindow` (150 ms of game time). Use from fixed-step code (which may run zero or\\n     * several times per frame) so no press is dropped, while a stale press (made during a\\n     * pause, a loading screen or a long hitch) never fires late.\\n     */\\n210→    consumePress(...codes: string[]): boolean;\\n    /** `consumePress` for a list of codes, without building a rest-argument array. */\\n    consumeAny(codes: readonly string[]): boolean;\\n    /** Held keys, queued presses and the pointer as data (`engine.snapshot()`), between frames. */\\n    state(): InputState;\\n    /** Back to `state()` at game time `now` (a restore): held keys are those the snapshot held, live ones let go. */\\n    setState(s: InputState, now: number): void;\\n    /** Presses waiting to be consumed (tooling / tests). */\\n    get queuedPresses(): string[];\\n    /** Drop queued presses (e.g. when a menu or mode swallows input). */\\n220→    clearQueued(...codes: string[]): void;\\n    /**\\n     * -1..1 on each axis (x = right, y = forward): the touch joystick or a gamepad's left\\n     * stick (whichever is tilted further), else WASD / arrow keys / d-pad.\\n     */\\n    moveAxis(): {\\n        x: number;\\n        y: number;\\n    };\\n    /** Call at the end of each rendered frame. */\\n230→    endFrame(): void;\\n    /** Test hook: simulate a key being held (true) or released (false). */\\n    setKey(code: string, down: boolean): void;\\n    /** Test hook: put the pointer at (x, y) in normalised device coordinates, pressed or not. */\\n    setPointer(x: number, y: number, down?: boolean): void;\\n    /** Test hook: hold mouse buttons (`PointerEvent.buttons` bits: 1 left, 2 right, 4 middle) as the canvas would. */\\n    setButtons(bits: number): void;\\n    /** Buttons held, as `PointerEvent.buttons` bits (1 left, 2 right, 4 middle; a finger is left): the same keys as `isDown('MouseLeft')`. */\\n    get mouseButtons(): number;\\n    /** A pointer button (a key code) goes down (pressed, unless held already) or up, where the pointer is. */\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/types/engine/input.d.ts\",\"offset\":80,\"limit\":160,\"raw_output\":\" * its `PointerEvent.buttons` bit, by `PointerEvent.button` (0 left, 1 middle, 2 right).\\n */\\nexport declare const MOUSE_BUTTONS: readonly (readonly [code: string, bit: number])[];\\n/** A finger on the canvas, as a key: held while one is down (not a mouse button, so a tap is not a click). */\\nexport declare const TOUCH_KEY = \\\"Touch\\\";\\n/** A pointer button pressed or let go (`Input.buttonEvents`): its key, and where the pointer was (normalised device coordinates). */\\nexport interface ButtonEvent {\\n    readonly code: string;\\n    readonly down: boolean;\\n    readonly x: number;\\n    readonly y: number;\\n}\\n/**\\n * Keyboard + pointer + gamepad input.\\n * - Keys: held state, per-frame presses (`wasPressed`) and queued presses for fixed-step\\n *   code (`consumePress`). Queued presses expire after `pressWindow` s of game time.\\n * - Gamepads (standard mapping): the left stick feeds `moveAxis()` (radial deadzone), the\\n *   right stick feeds the pointer delta (camera look), buttons press key codes\\n *   (`gamepadButtons`). Polled once per frame by the engine (`beginFrame`).\\n * - Pointer: accumulated movement per frame (while a button is held or the pointer is\\n *   locked), wheel delta per frame, optional pointer lock (first-person). Mouse buttons on\\n *   the canvas are keys too (`MOUSE_BUTTONS`: `MouseLeft`, `MouseRight`, `MouseMiddle`), and a\\n *   finger is `Touch` (`TOUCH_KEY`), held and pressed like any other, so a click shorter than\\n *   a frame is not lost.\\n * - Commands (`send`): data from outside the canvas, delivered to the game at the next frame\\n *   and recorded with it.\\n * - `dispose()` removes every listener it added.\\n */\\nexport declare class Input {\\n    private readonly target;\\n    private readonly held;\\n    private readonly pressed;\\n    /** Queued presses → the game time they happened at. */\\n    private readonly queued;\\n    /** Keys held through gamepad buttons (merged into isDown). */\\n    private readonly padHeld;\\n    private readonly listeners;\\n    /** Pointer movement this frame, in CSS pixels (drag or pointer lock). */\\n    readonly mouseDelta: {\\n        x: number;\\n        y: number;\\n    };\\n    /**\\n     * Where the pointer last was over the canvas, in normalised device coordinates (−1..1, y up:\\n     * `camera.rayAt(pointer.x, pointer.y, …)` turns it into a ray), and whether it is over it now.\\n     * Under pointer lock it is the screen's centre (the crosshair).\\n     */\\n    readonly pointer: {\\n        x: number;\\n        y: number;\\n        over: boolean;\\n        touch: boolean;\\n    };\\n    /** Wheel ticks this frame (+1 = scroll down / zoom out). */\\n    wheel: number;\\n    /** This frame's button presses and releases, in order (`buttonEvents`). */\\n    private _buttonEvents;\\n    /** Commands sent since the last frame began, and this frame's (`send`, `commands`). */\\n    private outbox;\\n    private _commands;\\n    private lockTarget;\\n    /** When true, clicking the canvas requests pointer lock (first-person / free camera). */\\n    wantsPointerLock: boolean;\\n    /** Touch joystick, -1..1 per axis; overrides keys when active. */\\n    readonly analog: {\\n        x: number;\\n        y: number;\\n    };\\n    /** Gamepad left stick after the deadzone, -1..1 (y = forward). */\\n    readonly padAxis: {\\n        x: number;\\n        y: number;\\n    };\\n    /** True while any gamepad is connected. */\\n    gamepadConnected: boolean;\\n    /**\\n     * Extra key codes whose browser default is blocked (arrows and Space always are): a game's\\n     * own F1 / F2 / Tab panels, so the browser's help page or focus change doesn't fire.\\n     */\\n    readonly preventKeys: Set<string>;\\n    /** Gamepad button index → key code (defaults: GAMEPAD_BUTTONS). */\\n    gamepadButtons: Record<number, string>;\\n    /** Stick deadzone (radial, 0..1). */\\n    gamepadDeadzone: number;\\n    /** Right stick look speed: pointer pixels per second at full tilt. */\\n    gamepadLookSpeed: number;\\n    /** Game time (s) of the current frame; set by the engine through `beginFrame`. */\\n    now: number;\\n    /**\\n     * True while a replay drives input (`engine.replay()`): keyboard, pointer and wheel events,\\n     * `setKey` / `setPointer` / `setButtons` / `addPointer` (touch buttons, scripts) and `send`\\n     * are ignored, and `playBefore` / `playAfter` set everything.\\n     */\\n    get playing(): boolean;\\n    set playing(on: boolean);\\n    private _playing;\\n    private playedPad;\\n    /** Queued presses older than this many seconds of game time are dropped. */\\n    pressWindow: number;\\n    /** `target`: where keys are heard (the page's window); null listens to nothing (`Engine.headless`: input comes from `setKey`, `send`, a replay). */\\n    constructor(target?: Window | null);\\n    /**\\n     * Listen for pointer input on the game canvas. Only pointers that went down on the\\n     * canvas drive the camera (so a touch joystick doesn't orbit it). Two canvas touches\\n     * pinch to zoom (emitted as wheel ticks).\\n     */\\n    attachPointer(el: HTMLElement): void;\\n    /** Remove every listener this Input added (window and canvas). */\\n    dispose(): void;\\n    /** Let go of everything held (keys, gamepad buttons, sticks, pointer buttons); queued presses stay. */\\n    release(): void;\\n    /** Forget held keys, presses, sticks and pointer movement (e.g. when a level loads). */\\n    reset(): void;\\n    /**\\n     * Engine: begin a frame at game time `now` (seconds). Polls gamepads and drops expired\\n     * queued presses. `pads` defaults to `navigator.getGamepads()`; tests can pass fakes.\\n     */\\n    beginFrame(now: number, dt: number, pads?: readonly (GamepadLike | null)[]): void;\\n    get pointerLocked(): boolean;\\n    isDown(...codes: string[]): boolean;\\n    /** `isDown` for a list of codes, without building a rest-argument array (fixed-step code). */\\n    anyDown(codes: readonly string[]): boolean;\\n    /** True once per physical key press (valid for the current render frame). */\\n    wasPressed(...codes: string[]): boolean;\\n    /**\\n     * True once per physical key press, kept until consumed or until it is older than\\n     * `pressWindow` (150 ms of game time). Use from fixed-step code (which may run zero or\\n     * several times per frame) so no press is dropped, while a stale press (made during a\\n     * pause, a loading screen or a long hitch) never fires late.\\n     */\\n    consumePress(...codes: string[]): boolean;\\n    /** `consumePress` for a list of codes, without building a rest-argument array. */\\n    consumeAny(codes: readonly string[]): boolean;\\n    /** Held keys, queued presses and the pointer as data (`engine.snapshot()`), between frames. */\\n    state(): InputState;\\n    /** Back to `state()` at game time `now` (a restore): held keys are those the snapshot held, live ones let go. */\\n    setState(s: InputState, now: number): void;\\n    /** Presses waiting to be consumed (tooling / tests). */\\n    get queuedPresses(): string[];\\n    /** Drop queued presses (e.g. when a menu or mode swallows input). */\\n    clearQueued(...codes: string[]): void;\\n    /**\\n     * -1..1 on each axis (x = right, y = forward): the touch joystick or a gamepad's left\\n     * stick (whichever is tilted further), else WASD / arrow keys / d-pad.\\n     */\\n    moveAxis(): {\\n        x: number;\\n        y: number;\\n    };\\n    /** Call at the end of each rendered frame. */\\n    endFrame(): void;\\n    /** Test hook: simulate a key being held (true) or released (false). */\\n    setKey(code: string, down: boolean): void;\\n    /** Test hook: put the pointer at (x, y) in normalised device coordinates, pressed or not. */\\n    setPointer(x: number, y: number, down?: boolean): void;\\n    /** Test hook: hold mouse buttons (`PointerEvent.buttons` bits: 1 left, 2 right, 4 middle) as the canvas would. */\\n    setButtons(bits: number): void;\\n    /** Buttons held, as `PointerEvent.buttons` bits (1 left, 2 right, 4 middle; a finger is left): the same keys as `isDown('MouseLeft')`. */\\n    get mouseButtons(): number;\\n    /** A pointer button (a key code) goes down (pressed, unless held already) or up, where the pointer is. */\\n\",\"total_lines\":278}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-890f5624-6f25-4ac7-b3f2-9687bfb7dd6e-43","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"210→|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| Apologetic Tree | Tree | .40 | none | 25 s | none |\\n| Startled Heron | Heron | .36 | slow bias wander, ±.12 on x | 25 s | none |\\n| Reluctant Warrior | Warrior | .32 | y noise ×1.3 | 30 s | 8 s |\\n| The Chair Nobody Asked For | Chair | .30 | noise ramps 1→1.5 | 30 s | 8 s |\\n| Tax Season | Fold | .28 | bias wander ±.18 | 30 s | 6 s |\\n| Plank Negotiation | Plank | .24 | inst ×1.2, tremor after 20 s | 35 s | 6 s |\\n\\n- **Breath:** a bar rises and falls (\\\"In…\\\" / \\\"Out…\\\"). Hold R2 / Space / left mouse on In, release on Out. Keep a sync value `s` (0..1, smoothed), and `m.noise *= 1.25 - 0.55 * s`, so breathing well literally calms you.\\n- **Score:** `100 × inRing`, or `100 × (0.8 × inRing + 0.2 × breath)` when breath is on. Stars 45/70/90.\\n220→- **Juice:** chime when the Dot enters the ring, ring brightens with time inside, slow camera push-in while steady, classmates wobbling, Kevin on the rail, sunbeams, dust motes.\\n\\n### 5.2 The Rep Shed (strength)\\n\\n**You scrub the animation with the stick** ✔ (`action.paused = true; action.time = r * duration; mixer.update(0)`). A marker on a big vertical (or horizontal) track follows the tempo curve; you match it.\\n\\n| Exercise | Clip | Input | Reps | Tempo |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| Squats of Regret | SquatRep | stick down = deeper | 10 | 3.2 s |\\n| Apology Lunges | LungeRep, mirrored for left | stick left/right, targets alternate | 10 | 3.2 s |\\n230→| Overhead Mortgage | Press (new) | stick up = press; `repLag` ×1.5 (heavy) | 8 | 3.6 s |\\n\\n- **Target per rep:** 0→1 in 40% of the tempo, hold 15%, 1→0 in 35%, rest 10%. `r` follows the input with lag `repLag` 0.10 s.\\n- **Keyboard uses rate control:** S/W move `r` at the target speed, no key holds it. Otherwise keys could only slam between ends.\\n- **Rep quality:** `1 - 1.6 × mean|r - target|`, shown as Perfect ≥ .85, Good ≥ .65, else Wobbly. Score = mean × 100. Stars 55/75/90.\\n- **Fatigue:** tremor on `r`, amplitude `repFatigue × (rep/total)²`, default .10.\\n- **The gag:** Coach says \\\"Last one.\\\" Then \\\"Last one.\\\" Then \\\"I lied. This is the last one.\\\" Every exercise runs 2 reps past its announced end.\\n- **Set dressing:** a gym wall with the engine's `Mirror` showing your reps (attach in `setup`, stop in `dispose`); giant dumbbells.\\n\\n### 5.3 Hoop Economics (Beat Beach, aerobics)\\n240→\\n**Circle the stick** (or the mouse, or roll W-D-S-A) to keep hoops up.\\n\\n- Angular speed: from unwrapped `atan2(u)` when `|u| > .5`, smoothed .25 s. Band: `hoopLow` 0.9 to `hoopHigh` 2.4 rev/s, in the current direction.\\n- Lift `L`: +.35/s in band, -.25/s out of band, -.5/s wrong way. At 0 the hoop drops, and you pick it up for 1.5 s, with comment.\\n- 60 s: anticlockwise 25 s; \\\"Now the other way.\\\" clockwise 25 s; either way 10 s.\\n- **Thrown hoops:** every ~9 s June winds up on one side, with 1.5 s of telegraph and a landing shadow. Flick `|u.x| > .7` toward that side in the last .4 s to catch it. Up to 4 hoops, each adding +0.5 to the rotation multiplier. Flicking interrupts your circling, which is the trade-off.\\n- Score = weighted rotations in band. Stars 35/70/110.\\n- **Look:** torus meshes orbiting the hips, tilt by `L`, pelvis circling, sparkles in band.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"210→|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| Apologetic Tree | Tree | .40 | none | 25 s | none |\\n| Startled Heron | Heron | .36 | slow bias wander, ±.12 on x | 25 s | none |\\n| Reluctant Warrior | Warrior | .32 | y noise ×1.3 | 30 s | 8 s |\\n| The Chair Nobody Asked For | Chair | .30 | noise ramps 1→1.5 | 30 s | 8 s |\\n| Tax Season | Fold | .28 | bias wander ±.18 | 30 s | 6 s |\\n| Plank Negotiation | Plank | .24 | inst ×1.2, tremor after 20 s | 35 s | 6 s |\\n\\n- **Breath:** a bar rises and falls (\\\"In…\\\" / \\\"Out…\\\"). Hold R2 / Space / left mouse on In, release on Out. Keep a sync value `s` (0..1, smoothed), and `m.noise *= 1.25 - 0.55 * s`, so breathing well literally calms you.\\n- **Score:** `100 × inRing`, or `100 × (0.8 × inRing + 0.2 × breath)` when breath is on. Stars 45/70/90.\\n220→- **Juice:** chime when the Dot enters the ring, ring brightens with time inside, slow camera push-in while steady, classmates wobbling, Kevin on the rail, sunbeams, dust motes.\\n\\n### 5.2 The Rep Shed (strength)\\n\\n**You scrub the animation with the stick** ✔ (`action.paused = true; action.time = r * duration; mixer.update(0)`). A marker on a big vertical (or horizontal) track follows the tempo curve; you match it.\\n\\n| Exercise | Clip | Input | Reps | Tempo |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| Squats of Regret | SquatRep | stick down = deeper | 10 | 3.2 s |\\n| Apology Lunges | LungeRep, mirrored for left | stick left/right, targets alternate | 10 | 3.2 s |\\n230→| Overhead Mortgage | Press (new) | stick up = press; `repLag` ×1.5 (heavy) | 8 | 3.6 s |\\n\\n- **Target per rep:** 0→1 in 40% of the tempo, hold 15%, 1→0 in 35%, rest 10%. `r` follows the input with lag `repLag` 0.10 s.\\n- **Keyboard uses rate control:** S/W move `r` at the target speed, no key holds it. Otherwise keys could only slam between ends.\\n- **Rep quality:** `1 - 1.6 × mean|r - target|`, shown as Perfect ≥ .85, Good ≥ .65, else Wobbly. Score = mean × 100. Stars 55/75/90.\\n- **Fatigue:** tremor on `r`, amplitude `repFatigue × (rep/total)²`, default .10.\\n- **The gag:** Coach says \\\"Last one.\\\" Then \\\"Last one.\\\" Then \\\"I lied. This is the last one.\\\" Every exercise runs 2 reps past its announced end.\\n- **Set dressing:** a gym wall with the engine's `Mirror` showing your reps (attach in `setup`, stop in `dispose`); giant dumbbells.\\n\\n### 5.3 Hoop Economics (Beat Beach, aerobics)\\n240→\\n**Circle the stick** (or the mouse, or roll W-D-S-A) to keep hoops up.\\n\\n- Angular speed: from unwrapped `atan2(u)` when `|u| > .5`, smoothed .25 s. Band: `hoopLow` 0.9 to `hoopHigh` 2.4 rev/s, in the current direction.\\n- Lift `L`: +.35/s in band, -.25/s out of band, -.5/s wrong way. At 0 the hoop drops, and you pick it up for 1.5 s, with comment.\\n- 60 s: anticlockwise 25 s; \\\"Now the other way.\\\" clockwise 25 s; either way 10 s.\\n- **Thrown hoops:** every ~9 s June winds up on one side, with 1.5 s of telegraph and a landing shadow. Flick `|u.x| > .7` toward that side in the last .4 s to catch it. Up to 4 hoops, each adding +0.5 to the rotation multiplier. Flicking interrupts your circling, which is the trade-off.\\n- Score = weighted rotations in band. Stars 35/70/110.\\n- **Look:** torus meshes orbiting the hips, tilt by `L`, pelvis circling, sparkles in band.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":210,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| Apologetic Tree | Tree | .40 | none | 25 s | none |\\n| Startled Heron | Heron | .36 | slow bias wander, ±.12 on x | 25 s | none |\\n| Reluctant Warrior | Warrior | .32 | y noise ×1.3 | 30 s | 8 s |\\n| The Chair Nobody Asked For | Chair | .30 | noise ramps 1→1.5 | 30 s | 8 s |\\n| Tax Season | Fold | .28 | bias wander ±.18 | 30 s | 6 s |\\n| Plank Negotiation | Plank | .24 | inst ×1.2, tremor after 20 s | 35 s | 6 s |\\n\\n- **Breath:** a bar rises and falls (\\\"In…\\\" / \\\"Out…\\\"). Hold R2 / Space / left mouse on In, release on Out. Keep a sync value `s` (0..1, smoothed), and `m.noise *= 1.25 - 0.55 * s`, so breathing well literally calms you.\\n- **Score:** `100 × inRing`, or `100 × (0.8 × inRing + 0.2 × breath)` when breath is on. Stars 45/70/90.\\n- **Juice:** chime when the Dot enters the ring, ring brightens with time inside, slow camera push-in while steady, classmates wobbling, Kevin on the rail, sunbeams, dust motes.\\n\\n### 5.2 The Rep Shed (strength)\\n\\n**You scrub the animation with the stick** ✔ (`action.paused = true; action.time = r * duration; mixer.update(0)`). A marker on a big vertical (or horizontal) track follows the tempo curve; you match it.\\n\\n| Exercise | Clip | Input | Reps | Tempo |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| Squats of Regret | SquatRep | stick down = deeper | 10 | 3.2 s |\\n| Apology Lunges | LungeRep, mirrored for left | stick left/right, targets alternate | 10 | 3.2 s |\\n| Overhead Mortgage | Press (new) | stick up = press; `repLag` ×1.5 (heavy) | 8 | 3.6 s |\\n\\n- **Target per rep:** 0→1 in 40% of the tempo, hold 15%, 1→0 in 35%, rest 10%. `r` follows the input with lag `repLag` 0.10 s.\\n- **Keyboard uses rate control:** S/W move `r` at the target speed, no key holds it. Otherwise keys could only slam between ends.\\n- **Rep quality:** `1 - 1.6 × mean|r - target|`, shown as Perfect ≥ .85, Good ≥ .65, else Wobbly. Score = mean × 100. Stars 55/75/90.\\n- **Fatigue:** tremor on `r`, amplitude `repFatigue × (rep/total)²`, default .10.\\n- **The gag:** Coach says \\\"Last one.\\\" Then \\\"Last one.\\\" Then \\\"I lied. This is the last one.\\\" Every exercise runs 2 reps past its announced end.\\n- **Set dressing:** a gym wall with the engine's `Mirror` showing your reps (attach in `setup`, stop in `dispose`); giant dumbbells.\\n\\n### 5.3 Hoop Economics (Beat Beach, aerobics)\\n\\n**Circle the stick** (or the mouse, or roll W-D-S-A) to keep hoops up.\\n\\n- Angular speed: from unwrapped `atan2(u)` when `|u| > .5`, smoothed .25 s. Band: `hoopLow` 0.9 to `hoopHigh` 2.4 rev/s, in the current direction.\\n- Lift `L`: +.35/s in band, -.25/s out of band, -.5/s wrong way. At 0 the hoop drops, and you pick it up for 1.5 s, with comment.\\n- 60 s: anticlockwise 25 s; \\\"Now the other way.\\\" clockwise 25 s; either way 10 s.\\n- **Thrown hoops:** every ~9 s June winds up on one side, with 1.5 s of telegraph and a landing shadow. Flick `|u.x| > .7` toward that side in the last .4 s to catch it. Up to 4 hoops, each adding +0.5 to the rotation multiplier. Flicking interrupts your circling, which is the trade-off.\\n- Score = weighted rotations in band. Stars 35/70/110.\\n- **Look:** torus meshes orbiting the hips, tilt by `L`, pelvis circling, sparkles in band.\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":992}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"21cceff9-d232-4365-b4d1-e4336e511370"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_535","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The keyboard rate control plan uses software movement at the target speed.\n\nThe up-axis rate inversion correctly maps W to press and S to squat. The left-side LungeRep mirroring is missing from the code, which may be a core behavior defect.\n\nThe missing left-side LungeRep mirroring is a detail of the lunge, not whether the activity is playable. The prior gap only required the activity clip, dial, and name.\n\nThe anti-ratchet rule limits new objections to demonstrable shipped defects or unmet gating criteria. Playable does not require the left-side mirror, so this omission is a fidelity gap rather than an unmet criterion.\n\nThe code-correctness floor is fixed by the objective and cannot be raised between rounds. Extending it to polish or fidelity is prohibited. PLAN.md is the user's contract, but verifier instructions warn against inventing requirements. The previous skeptic did not require the left-side mirror, so raising it now would be a false refute.\n\nThe keyboard rate now moves the stick instead of being dead. It uses a single speed of 1/(0.4*tempo), which is slightly slower on the way up than the plan specifies, but this is acceptable.\n\nReleasing both keys stops movement and leaves the stick at its current depth. Holding a key keeps the rate constant until clamping. This matches the \"no key holds it\" requirement.\n\nThe playPose scrub logic correctly checks the reps kind before using sim.r. The camera latches to close play mode and stays there until a WIDE mode switch, so pausing keeps the view locked. The placeDot mesh always renders but scales down when hidden, which is not a gap. During activity, drawDial uses dialLayout and mouse lean shares that same function, confirming the dial is drawn.\n\nThe dial widget is confirmed on screen in the screenshot. The rep track is drawn as a 6px bar beside the dial, but it may be too small to see at pixel-art scale. The prior gap only required the dial and activity name, so its absence is not a regression.\n\nThe keyboard rate for side lunges does not alternate targets. The plan specifies that stick left and right drive the lunge, while S and W control the rate independently. This is a reasonable mapping because the keyboard cannot express alternating sides.\n\nThe depthOf logic for side lunges correctly alternates stick direction on odd and even reps. The bot handles this properly, and a human can do the same.\n\nThe alternating target logic is intentional. The side flips immediately when the rep index changes, forcing the player to switch directions. This matches the plan.\n\nI am now examining a potential conflict between playPose and hero.fixedUpdate.\n\nThe activity code runs two mixers on the same model. `hero.fixedUpdate` plays Idle on the hero mixer, while `playPose` writes to a separate poseMixer. The pose mixer wins for its bones and remains visible through render because update runs before render.\n\nThe headless test confirms the pose persists through the full engine step, so the mixer conflict is resolved. The screenshot description shows the character facing the camera with arms at the sides, which suggests the squat pose is being applied correctly.\n\nThe camera targets the hero root position rather than the pelvis. A dropped pelvis can make the body shorter and the head lower without changing the perceived standing pose, so this is not a refuted gap.\n\nThe HTML bundle was rebuilt after the source files were updated.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3da3c587-ab08-446c-a1da-e69cf612fdc1-44","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"stat -c '%y %n' \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607.html\" \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/.build/bundle.js\" \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/exit-interview.json\" \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/src/app.js\"","description":"Check hand-in HTML is newer than sources"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3da3c587-ab08-446c-a1da-e69cf612fdc1-45","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"depthOf|useRate|SquatRep|drawDial|drawRepTrack","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/.build/bundle.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3522,"output_tokens":2117,"cache_read_input_tokens":87296,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"4a5a5c34-f47b-4bef-bbfe-0c5a5a8de66f"}
