,116,104,101,105,114,32,99,111,108,111,117,114,44,32,97,110,100,32,119,104,105,99,104,32,111,102,32,116,104,101,109,32,97,114,101,32,114,101,97,100,121,59,10,49,53,51,58,45,32,104,111,119,32,116,111,32,119,105,110,32,116,104,101,32,114,111,117,110,100,59,10,49,53,52,58,45,32,116,104,101,32,99,111,110,116,114,111,108,115,32,116,104,105,115,32,112,108,97,121,101,114,32,119,105,108,108,32,117,115,101,59,10,49,53,55,58,65,110,100,32,105,116,32,116,97,107,101,115,32,116,119,111,32,97,110,115,119,101,114,115,44,32,102,114,111,109,32,116,104,101,32,107,101,121,98,111,97,114,100,44,32,97,32,99,111,110,116,114,111,108,108,101,114,44,32,111,114,32,97,32,116,97,112,32,111,114,32,99,108,105,99,107,10,49,54,54,58,99,104,111,105,99,101,115,44,32,97,110,100,32,112,108,97,121,32,98,101,103,105,110,115,32,111,110,108,121,32,97,116,32,96,115,116,97,114,116,96,46,32,73,110,32,112,97,114,97,108,108,101,108,32,97,110,100,32,103,104,111,115,116,32,105,116,32,100,114,97,119,115,32,110,111,10,49,55,53,58,124,32,96,112,97,117,115,101,100,96,32,124,32,96,116,114,117,101,96,32,119,104,105,108,101,32,109,111,115,116,32,112,108,97,121,101,114,115,32,97,115,107,101,100,32,102,111,114,32,109,111,114,101,32,116,105,109,101,32,124,10,49,55,55,58,124,32,96,114,101,97,100,121,96,32,124,32,116,104,101,32,105,100,115,32,111,102,32,116,104,101,32,112,108,97,121,101,114,115,32,119,104,111,32,97,114,101,32,114,101,97,100,121,32,124,10,49,55,56,58,124,32,96,97,115,107,105,110,103,96,32,124,32,104,111,119,32,109,97,110,121,32,112,108,97,121,101,114,115,32,97,115,107,101,100,32,102,111,114,32,109,111,114,101,32,116,105,109,101,32,40,110,101,118,101,114,32,119,104,111,41,32,124,10,49,55,57,58,124,32,96,97,115,107,101,100,96,32,124,32,96,116,114,117,101,96,32,119,104,101,110,32,116,104,105,115,32,112,108,97,121,101,114,32,97,115,107,101,100,32,102,111,114,32,109,111,114,101,32,116,105,109,101,32,124,10,49,57,48,58,45,32,96,65,73,72,117,98,46,112,114,111,103,114,101,115,115,40,123,32,115,99,111,114,101,44,32,108,97,98,101,108,32,125,41,96,44,32,105,110,32,112,97,114,97,108,108,101,108,32,97,110,100,32,103,104,111,115,116,58,32,116,104,101,32,112,108,97,121,101,114,39,115,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":40,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/PROGRESS.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":7,\"content\":\"A week with Ounce the scale. Weigh-in, three guest slots, the ferry, seven days, the island, every planned activity (including Pier Jump, Vitamin Tray, Island Jog, Overhead Mortgage, and The Long Stand), the jar, the confession that subtracts 7, and an open Week 2. Family Hour runs three medley events for up to four players. An AI Hub session uses ghost mode and its own card. Attract mode, dev-tool sliders, and the touch gate are in. Music, effects, and the two voices are code.\"},{\"line_number\":11,\"content\":\"`node tools/test.mjs` from the dev folder printed `13/13 passed` and no failure lines. Reps follow the stick for that exercise (down, sideways, or up) and the keyboard moves them by rate. An activity plays its clip, frames the body, draws the balance dial, and shows the exercise name.\"},{\"line_number\":13,\"content\":\"Two `file://` Chromium launches, with the five software WebGPU flags, showed the title Mint Dial, music bus 0.10, and no page errors. Both captures are 1281×720 and painted. The saved frames show the title, the tagline, and the medical line. Prompts follow Cross, Xbox A, Enter, and click. Hover moved the focus from Gentle to More, and the click activated. A phone profile shows “Controller or keyboard required”, a settings control, and attract, and it does not start play from a touch. Widget rects fit at 1920×1080, 1280×720, and 640×360. An analyser read the mix, and an offline voice render was above 0.02 RMS with Ounce’s pitch above Coach’s. Three Family Hour lanes moved. WebKit and Firefox show “Failed to start: WebGPU unavailable” and raise no page error.\"},{\"line_number\":15,\"content\":\"The hub harness on `127.0.0.1:37259` passed all four URLs (`players=1`, `players=2`, the lossy four-player case, and host-leave). With no session, the title still boots. JavaScript was served as `text/javascript`. The activity frame is a close shot of Squats of Regret: the pose is on the body, the balance dial and the rep track are on screen, and the exercise name sits below the face.\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/vendor/hub/README.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":3,\"content\":\"An **AI Hub session** is up to four players, each on their own device,\"},{\"line_number\":4,\"content\":\"playing rounds of games one after another. The hub runs everything around a\"},{\"line_number\":32,\"content\":\"| `ghost` | its own copy of the round | each copy's own player: where it is and what it is doing |\"},{\"line_number\":33,\"content\":\"| `shared-world` | one world for all players, run by the host's copy | what each player does, to the host; the world, from the host |\"},{\"line_number\":35,\"content\":\"- **Parallel**: every player plays their own copy of the round, from the same\"},{\"line_number\":37,\"content\":\"- **Ghost**: as parallel, and each copy also shows the other players'\"},{\"line_number\":40,\"content\":\"- **Shared world**: all players play in one world. The host's copy runs that\"},{\"line_number\":41,\"content\":\"  world; the other copies send it what their own player does, and show the\"},{\"line_number\":44,\"content\":\"Games tagged with the older modes keep working: `race` is played as ghost,\"},{\"line_number\":51,\"content\":\"1. The hub loads the game on every player's device, and the players get 10\"},{\"line_number\":52,\"content\":\"   to 30 seconds with the game's card: what the game is, how to win, the\"},{\"line_number\":58,\"content\":\"5. The round ends when every player has a result, when the host of a shared\"},{\"line_number\":68,\"content\":\"<meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"MIN-MAX\\\">\"},{\"line_number\":74,\"content\":\"- `hub:session-players`: the smallest and largest number of players the game\"},{\"line_number\":75,\"content\":\"  takes in a session. The hub deals the game only when the number of players\"},{\"line_number\":78,\"content\":\"- `hub:session-goal` and `hub:session-howto`: how to win and the game's\"},{\"line_number\":85,\"content\":\"- `hub:webgpu` with `required`: the game cannot run without WebGPU. The hub\"},{\"line_number\":86,\"content\":\"  then deals it only when every player's browser has WebGPU.\"},{\"line_number\":115,\"content\":\"  start, with no key press: the players answer the card.\"},{\"line_number\":116,\"content\":\"- The round starts when the card's countdown ends or every player pressed\"},{\"line_number\":118,\"content\":\"  20 more seconds; after that its player sits the round out.\"},{\"line_number\":124,\"content\":\"| `me` | this copy's player id |\"},{\"line_number\":125,\"content\":\"| `players` | `[{ id, name, color }]`, ids `0..N-1` in seat order |\"},{\"line_number\":127,\"content\":\"| `server` | `true` only on a copy that hosts a shared world with no player of its own |\"},{\"line_number\":136,\"content\":\"Before every round the players get 10 to 30 seconds to learn what comes\"},{\"line_number\":146,\"content\":\"title, its music, its world, the players lining up. Introduce the game the way\"},{\"line_number\":152,\"content\":\"- the players, each in their colour, and which of them are ready;\"},{\"line_number\":153,\"content\":\"- how to win the round;\"},{\"line_number\":154,\"content\":\"- the controls this player will use;\"},{\"line_number\":157,\"content\":\"And it takes two answers, from the keyboard, a controller, or a tap or click\"},{\"line_number\":166,\"content\":\"choices, and play begins only at `start`. In parallel and ghost it draws no\"},{\"line_number\":175,\"content\":\"| `paused` | `true` while most players asked for more time |\"},{\"line_number\":177,\"content\":\"| `ready` | the ids of the players who are ready |\"},{\"line_number\":178,\"content\":\"| `asking` | how many players asked for more time (never who) |\"},{\"line_number\":179,\"content\":\"| `asked` | `true` when this player asked for more time |\"},{\"line_number\":190,\"content\":\"- `AIHub.progress({ score, label })`, in parallel and ghost: the player's\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-31fd8ac0-5e01-45be-be18-2bf2861633fe-5","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→{\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"mint-dial\\\",\\n  \\\"private\\\": true,\\n  \\\"type\\\": \\\"module\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"1.0.0\\\",\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Mint Dial, a fitness week about a polite scale.\\\"\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→{\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"mint-dial\\\",\\n  \\\"private\\\": true,\\n  \\\"type\\\": \\\"module\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"1.0.0\\\",\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Mint Dial, a fitness week about a polite scale.\\\"\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/Mint Dial-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-221607/package.json\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"{\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"mint-dial\\\",\\n  \\\"private\\\": true,\\n  \\\"type\\\": \\\"module\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"1.0.0\\\",\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Mint Dial, a fitness week about a polite scale.\\\"\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":7}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"12c4e92c-cb48-49b7-bda2-b146f330d0c2"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_541","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to write a very short summary of how to play.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6a90525e-0098-47bd-92d3-97ca07296f97-6","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/exit-interview.json","limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6a90525e-0098-47bd-92d3-97ca07296f97-7","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"controls|Enter|Cross|WASD|title screen|Play","glob":"**/src/data/{title,about,creditsText}.js","head_limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5049,"output_tokens":313,"cache_read_input_tokens":15744,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa22-c3bd-7423-a5f1-ddadc552f469","uuid":"26c0b3bb-fa9f-4dcb-9705-00ecf16a0f9c"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-6a90525e-0098-47bd-92d3-97ca07296f97-6","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 22:16:07\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Sports\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"Isometric island, with a fixed camera for each activity\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"Pixel Engine 0.46.0, three.js r186, Rapier 0.20 as bundled, esbuild 0.28.2\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"The engine native pixel look, with new models for the scale, stations, and props\\\",\\n10→    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"Engine ClipDefs compiled onto the hero rig and played with AnimationMixer\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Engine Song and SoundDef data, plus a Web Audio formant voice. Music defaults to 10 percent.\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, own card, 1 to 4 players. Family Hour is local on one screen.\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"node tools/test.mjs, Playwright 1.63 Chromium with the five software WebGPU flags, WebKit and Firefox for the missing-WebGPU path, and the engine headless runner\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"The director plan already included engine and hub research and spikes. I read PLAN.md, the engine guide where the recipes pointed, and the hub README, and I checked the Dot table in code. I did not do extra research on the source beyond that plan.\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n20→    \\\"Thirteen issues. The expert pier jump scored two stars, pause let the pose clock move on the frame the button went down, two songs had uneven pattern lengths, a tray board lookup named a variable that was not in scope, a few model parts floated, the seagull was spoken as the scale, a dev-tool page could not go back, the prompt could draw past a short screen, the scale's voice measured just under the loudness line, the About screen kept only the first six lines so later source fields never appeared, the menu cursor was a greater-than sign the font cannot draw, so it showed as a question mark, reps listened only to a downward lean so a sideways lunge and an upward press did nothing, and an activity kept the title camera, never played its pose, and labelled the screen activity.\\\",\\n    \\\"Three were game-breaking. The pier jump sat under the three-star line until takeoff recentred the dot, the pose kept playing for one frame after pause, and a lunge or a press did not move when the stick did. The others failed a data check, a voice check, a menu, or the picture of the exercise, and they were fixed before the hand-in.\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful test was driving a rep with the input the stick and the keys actually produce. The idle-versus-expert bots wrote the depth themselves, so they still scored while a sideways lunge stayed at zero. That same bot pass is what caught the pier jump.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful test was the glyph scan. Every line already used the allowed characters, so it passed on the first run and did not change the game.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"Headless stepping, the pixel HUD, and a real input recorder made a week of play testable without a screen.\\\",\\n    \\\"I guessed wrong about pause. At timeScale 0 the headless stepper still calls fixedUpdate, and that call happens before update reads the pause key, so the pose clock moved unless the sim refused the step. Menu presses do still arrive. The type note reads as if those presses are dropped. Capture also needs all five Vulkan flags or the picture comes back blank.\\\",\\n    \\\"The centre-of-balance itself. The engine will move a character. It will not sway a polite dot, keep a week, or speak in formants.\\\",\\n    \\\"The hardest part was trusting the frame clock. Game time, the press window, and the hub clock are three different clocks, and only one of them is allowed to move a score.\\\",\\n30→    \\\"None. pixel-engine.js is the kit file, byte for byte.\\\",\\n    \\\"I would give the music bus a default of silence until the game sets it, so a shared browser profile cannot leave yesterday volume on today game.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The plan named the mechanics, the sentences, and the tests, so the work was building a game rather than inventing one.\\\",\\n    \\\"The cut list in the plan and the instruction to finish everything on this computer disagree. I followed the instruction and shipped the activities the cut list would drop.\\\",\\n    \\\"The hardest piece was the pier jump star line. The same bot that holds a pose will dive off a dock, and the flight begins wherever the dot was left.\\\",\\n    \\\"I would ask for the pause rule in one sentence: timeScale 0, fixedUpdate silent, update still reads keys. The guide and the type comment do not say the same thing.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n40→    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Mint Dial\\\",\",\"content_concise\":\"1→{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 22:16:07\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Sports\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"Isometric island, with a fixed camera for each activity\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"Pixel Engine 0.46.0, three.js r186, Rapier 0.20 as bundled, esbuild 0.28.2\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"The engine native pixel look, with new models for the scale, stations, and props\\\",\\n10→    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"Engine ClipDefs compiled onto the hero rig and played with AnimationMixer\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Engine Song and SoundDef data, plus a Web Audio formant voice. Music defaults to 10 percent.\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, own card, 1 to 4 players. Family Hour is local on one screen.\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"node tools/test.mjs, Playwright 1.63 Chromium with the five software WebGPU flags, WebKit and Firefox for the missing-WebGPU path, and the engine headless runner\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"The director plan already included engine and hub research and spikes. I read PLAN.md, the engine guide where the recipes pointed, and the hub README, and I checked the Dot table in code. I did not do extra research on the source beyond that plan.\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n20→    \\\"Thirteen issues. The expert pier jump scored two stars, pause let the pose clock move on the frame the button went down, two songs had uneven pattern lengths, a tray board lookup named a variable that was not in scope, a few model parts floated, the seagull was spoken as the scale, a dev-tool page could not go back, the prompt could draw past a short screen, the scale's voice measured just under the loudness line, the About screen kept only the first six lines so later source fields never appeared, the menu cursor was a greater-than sign the font cannot draw, so it showed as a question mark, reps listened only to a downward lean so a sideways lunge and an upward press did nothing, and an activity kept the title camera, never played its pose, and labelled the screen activity.\\\",\\n    \\\"Three were game-breaking. The pier jump sat under the three-star line until takeoff recentred the dot, the pose kept playing for one frame after pause, and a lunge or a press did not move when the stick did. The others failed a data check, a voice check, a menu, or the picture of the exercise, and they were fixed before the hand-in.\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful test was driving a rep with the input the stick and the keys actually produce. The idle-versus-expert bots wrote the depth themselves, so they still scored while a sideways lunge stayed at zero. That same bot pass is what caught the pier jump.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful test was the glyph scan. Every line already used the allowed characters, so it passed on the first run and did not change the game.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"Headless stepping, the pixel HUD, and a real input recorder made a week of play testable without a screen.\\\",\\n    \\\"I guessed wrong about pause. At timeScale 0 the headless stepper still calls fixedUpdate, and that call happens before update reads the pause key, so the pose clock moved unless the sim refused the step. Menu presses do still arrive. The type note reads as if those presses are dropped. Capture also needs all five Vulkan flags or the picture comes back blank.\\\",\\n    \\\"The centre-of-balance itself. The engine will move a character. It will not sway a polite dot, keep a week, or speak in formants.\\\",\\n    \\\"The hardest part was trusting the frame clock. Game time, the press window, and the hub clock are three different clocks, and only one of them is allowed to move a score.\\\",\\n30→    \\\"None. pixel-engine.js is the kit file, byte for byte.\\\",\\n    \\\"I would give the music bus a default of silence until the game sets it, so a shared browser profile cannot leave yesterday volume on today game.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The plan named the mechanics, the sentences, and the tests, so the work was building a game rather than inventing one.\\\",\\n    \\\"The cut list in the plan and the instruction to finish everything on this computer disagree. I followed the instruction and shipped the activities the cut list would drop.\\\",\\n    \\\"The hardest piece was the pier jump star line. The same bot that holds a pose will dive off a dock, and the flight begins wherever the dot was left.\\\",\\n    \\\"I would ask for the pause rule in one sentence: timeScale 0, fixedUpdate silent, update still reads keys. The guide and the type comment do not say the same thing.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n40→    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Mint Dial\\\",\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-221607__x6981e3/work/exit-interview.json\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 22:16:07\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Sports\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"Isometric island, with a fixed camera for each activity\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"Pixel Engine 0.46.0, three.js r186, Rapier 0.20 as bundled, esbuild 0.28.2\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"The engine native pixel look, with new models for the scale, stations, and props\\\",\\n    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"Engine ClipDefs compiled onto the hero rig and played with AnimationMixer\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Engine Song and SoundDef data, plus a Web Audio formant voice. Music defaults to 10 percent.\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, own card, 1 to 4 players. Family Hour is local on one screen.\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"node tools/test.mjs, Playwright 1.63 Chromium with the five software WebGPU flags, WebKit and Firefox for the missing-WebGPU path, and the engine headless runner\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"The director plan already included engine and hub research and spikes. I read PLAN.md, the engine guide where the recipes pointed, and the hub README, and I checked the Dot table in code. I did not do extra research on the source beyond that plan.\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testi